msgstr "Velocidade alvo para o motor nos eixos."

#: doc/classes/Generic6DOFJoint3D.xml doc/classes/PhysicsServer3D.xml
msgid "Maximum acceleration for the motor at the axes."
msgstr "Aceleração máxima para o motor nos eixos."

#: doc/classes/Generic6DOFJoint3D.xml
msgid "If enabled, linear motion is possible within the given limits."
msgstr "Se ativado, o movimento linear é possível dentro dos limites dados."

#: doc/classes/Generic6DOFJoint3D.xml
msgid "If enabled, rotational motion is possible within the given limits."
msgstr ""
"Se ativado, o movimento rotacional é possível dentro dos limites dados."

#: doc/classes/Generic6DOFJoint3D.xml
msgid "If enabled, there is a rotational motor across these axes."
msgstr "Se ativado, há um motor rotacional nesses eixos."

#: doc/classes/Generic6DOFJoint3D.xml
msgid "If enabled, there is a linear motor across these axes."
msgstr "Se ativado, há um motor linear através desses eixos."

#: doc/classes/Generic6DOFJoint3D.xml doc/classes/HingeJoint3D.xml
msgid "Represents the size of the [enum Flag] enum."
msgstr "Representa o tamanho da enumeração [enum Flag]."

#: doc/classes/Geometry2D.xml
msgid "Provides methods for some common 2D geometric operations."
msgstr "Fornece métodos para algumas operações geométricas 2D comuns."

#: doc/classes/Geometry2D.xml
msgid ""
"Provides a set of helper functions to create geometric shapes, compute "
"intersections between shapes, and process various other geometric operations "
"in 2D."
msgstr ""
"Fornece um conjunto de funções auxiliares para criar formas geométricas, "
"calcular interseções entre formas e processar várias outras operações "
"geométricas em 2D."

#: doc/classes/Geometry2D.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the [url=https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/"
"Bresenham%27s_line_algorithm]Bresenham line[/url] between the [param from] "
"and [param to] points. A Bresenham line is a series of pixels that draws a "
"line and is always 1-pixel thick on every row and column of the drawing "
"(never more, never less).\n"
"Example code to draw a line between two [Marker2D] nodes using a series of "
"[method CanvasItem.draw_rect] calls:\n"
"[codeblock]\n"
"func _draw():\n"
"\tfor pixel in Geometry2D.bresenham_line($MarkerA.position, "
"$MarkerB.position):\n"
"\t\tdraw_rect(Rect2(pixel, Vector2.ONE), Color.WHITE)\n"
"[/codeblock]"
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Geometry2D.xml
msgid ""
"Clips [param polygon_a] against [param polygon_b] and returns an array of "
"clipped polygons. This performs [constant OPERATION_DIFFERENCE] between "
"polygons. Returns an empty array if [param polygon_b] completely overlaps "
"[param polygon_a].\n"
"If [param polygon_b] is enclosed by [param polygon_a], returns an outer "
"polygon (boundary) and inner polygon (hole) which could be distinguished by "
"calling [method is_polygon_clockwise]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Geometry2D.xml
msgid ""
"Clips [param polyline] against [param polygon] and returns an array of "
"clipped polylines. This performs [constant OPERATION_DIFFERENCE] between the "
"polyline and the polygon. This operation can be thought of as cutting a line "
"with a closed shape."
msgstr ""
"Corta [param polyline] em relação a [param polygon] e retorna uma matriz de "
"polilinhas cortadas. Isso executa [constant OPERATION_DIFFERENCE] entre a "
"polilinha e o polígono. Esta operação pode ser pensada como cortar uma linha "
"com uma forma fechada."

#: doc/classes/Geometry2D.xml
msgid ""
"Given an array of [Vector2]s, returns the convex hull as a list of points in "
"counterclockwise order. The last point is the same as the first one."
msgstr ""
"Dado um array de [Vector2]s, retorna o envoltório convexo como uma lista de "
"pontos em sentido anti-horário. O último ponto é o mesmo que o primeiro."

#: doc/classes/Geometry2D.xml
msgid ""
"Decomposes the [param polygon] into multiple convex hulls and returns an "
"array of [PackedVector2Array]."
msgstr ""
"Decompõe o [param polygon] em múltiplos cascos convexos e retorna um array "
"de [PackedVector2Array]."

#: doc/classes/Geometry2D.xml
msgid ""
"Mutually excludes common area defined by intersection of [param polygon_a] "
"and [param polygon_b] (see [method intersect_polygons]) and returns an array "
"of excluded polygons. This performs [constant OPERATION_XOR] between "
"polygons. In other words, returns all but common area between polygons.\n"
"The operation may result in an outer polygon (boundary) and inner polygon "
"(hole) produced which could be distinguished by calling [method "
"is_polygon_clockwise]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Geometry2D.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the 2D point on the 2D segment ([param s1], [param s2]) that is "
"closest to [param point]. The returned point will always be inside the "
"specified segment."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o ponto 2D no segmento 2D ([param s1], [param s2]) que está mais "
"próximo de [param point]. O ponto retornado estará sempre dentro do segmento "
"especificado."

#: doc/classes/Geometry2D.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the 2D point on the 2D line defined by ([param s1], [param s2]) that "
"is closest to [param point]. The returned point can be inside the segment "
"([param s1], [param s2]) or outside of it, i.e. somewhere on the line "
"extending from the segment."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o ponto 2D na linha 2D definida por ([param s1], [param s2]) que "
"está mais próximo de [param point]. O ponto retornado pode estar dentro do "
"segmento ([param s1], [param s2]) ou fora dele, ou seja, em algum lugar na "
"linha que se estende a partir do segmento."

#: doc/classes/Geometry2D.xml
msgid ""
"Given the two 2D segments ([param p1], [param q1]) and ([param p2], [param "
"q2]), finds those two points on the two segments that are closest to each "
"other. Returns a [PackedVector2Array] that contains this point on ([param "
"p1], [param q1]) as well the accompanying point on ([param p2], [param q2])."
msgstr ""
"Dados os dois segmentos 2D ([param p1], [param q1]) e ([param p2], [param "
"q2]), encontra os dois pontos nesses dois segmentos que estão mais próximos "
"um do outro. Retorna um [PackedVector2Array] que contém este ponto em "
"([param p1], [param q1]) bem como o ponto correspondente em ([param p2], "
"[param q2])."

#: doc/classes/Geometry2D.xml
msgid ""
"Intersects [param polygon_a] with [param polygon_b] and returns an array of "
"intersected polygons. This performs [constant OPERATION_INTERSECTION] "
"between polygons. In other words, returns common area shared by polygons. "
"Returns an empty array if no intersection occurs.\n"
"The operation may result in an outer polygon (boundary) and inner polygon "
"(hole) produced which could be distinguished by calling [method "
"is_polygon_clockwise]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Geometry2D.xml
msgid ""
"Intersects [param polyline] with [param polygon] and returns an array of "
"intersected polylines. This performs [constant OPERATION_INTERSECTION] "
"between the polyline and the polygon. This operation can be thought of as "
"chopping a line with a closed shape."
msgstr ""
"Faz a interseção de [param polyline] com [param polygon] e retorna uma "
"matriz de polilinhas intersectadas. Isso executa [constant "
"OPERATION_INTERSECTION] entre a polilinha e o polígono. Esta operação pode "
"ser pensada como cortar uma linha com uma forma fechada."

#: doc/classes/Geometry2D.xml
msgid ""
"Returns [code]true[/code] if [param point] is inside the circle or if it's "
"located exactly [i]on[/i] the circle's boundary, otherwise returns "
"[code]false[/code]."
msgstr ""
"Retorna [code]true[/code] se [param point] estiver dentro do círculo ou se "
"estiver localizado exatamente [i]no[/i] limite do círculo, caso contrário, "
"retorna [code]false[/code]."

#: doc/classes/Geometry2D.xml
msgid ""
"Returns [code]true[/code] if [param point] is inside [param polygon] or if "
"it's located exactly [i]on[/i] polygon's boundary, otherwise returns "
"[code]false[/code]."
msgstr ""
"Retorna [code]true[/code] se [param point] estiver dentro de [param polygon] "
"ou se estiver localizado exatamente [i]no[/i] limite do polígono, caso "
"contrário, retorna [code]false[/code]."

#: doc/classes/Geometry2D.xml
msgid ""
"Returns [code]true[/code] if [param polygon]'s vertices are ordered in "
"clockwise order, otherwise returns [code]false[/code].\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Assumes a Cartesian coordinate system where [code]+x[/code] is "
"right and [code]+y[/code] is up. If using screen coordinates ([code]+y[/"
"code] is down), the result will need to be flipped (i.e. a [code]true[/code] "
"result will indicate counter-clockwise)."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Geometry2D.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the point of intersection between the two lines ([param from_a], "
"[param dir_a]) and ([param from_b], [param dir_b]). Returns a [Vector2], or "
"[code]null[/code] if the lines are parallel.\n"
"[code]from[/code] and [code]dir[/code] are [i]not[/i] endpoints of a line "
"segment or ray but the slope ([code]dir[/code]) and a known point "
"([code]from[/code]) on that line. To get the intersection between two line "
"segments, use [method segment_intersects_segment].\n"
"[codeblocks]\n"
"[gdscript]\n"
"var from_a = Vector2.ZERO\n"
"var dir_a = Vector2.RIGHT\n"
"var from_b = Vector2.DOWN\n"
"\n"
"# Returns Vector2(1, 0)\n"
"Geometry2D.line_intersects_line(from_a, dir_a, from_b, Vector2(1, -1))\n"
"# Returns Vector2(-1, 0)\n"
"Geometry2D.line_intersects_line(from_a, dir_a, from_b, Vector2(-1, -1))\n"
"# Returns null\n"
"Geometry2D.line_intersects_line(from_a, dir_a, from_b, Vector2.RIGHT)\n"
"[/gdscript]\n"
"[csharp]\n"
"var fromA = Vector2.Zero;\n"
"var dirA = Vector2.Right;\n"
"var fromB = Vector2.Down;\n"
"\n"
"// Returns new Vector2(1, 0)\n"
"Geometry2D.LineIntersectsLine(fromA, dirA, fromB, new Vector2(1, -1));\n"
"// Returns new Vector2(-1, 0)\n"
"Geometry2D.LineIntersectsLine(fromA, dirA, fromB, new Vector2(-1, -1));\n"
"// Returns null\n"
"Geometry2D.LineIntersectsLine(fromA, dirA, fromB, Vector2.Right);\n"
"[/csharp]\n"
"[/codeblocks]"
msgstr ""
"Retorna o ponto de intersecção entre as duas linhas ([param from_a], [param "
"dir_a]) e ([param from_b], [param dir_b]). Retorna um [Vector2], ou "
"[code]null[/code] se as linhas forem paralelas.\n"
"[code]from[/code] e [code]dir[/code] [i]não[/i] são extremidades de um "
"segmento de reta ou raio, mas sim a inclinação ([code]dir[/code]) e um ponto "
"conhecido ([code]from[/code]) nessa linha. Para obter a intersecção entre "
"dois segmentos de reta, use [method segment_intersects_segment].\n"
"[codeblocks]\n"
"[gdscript]\n"
"var from_a = Vector2.ZERO\n"
"var dir_a = Vector2.RIGHT\n"
"var from_b = Vector2.DOWN\n"
"\n"
"# Retorna Vector2(1, 0)\n"
"Geometry2D.line_intersects_line(from_a, dir_a, from_b, Vector2(1, -1))\n"
"# Retorna Vector2(-1, 0)\n"
"Geometry2D.line_intersects_line(from_a, dir_a, from_b, Vector2(-1, -1))\n"
"# Retorna null\n"
"Geometry2D.line_intersects_line(from_a, dir_a, from_b, Vector2.RIGHT)\n"
"[/gdscript]\n"
"[csharp]\n"
"var fromA = Vector2.Zero;\n"
"var dirA = Vector2.Right;\n"
"var fromB = Vector2.Down;\n"
"\n"
"// Retorna new Vector2(1, 0)\n"
"Geometry2D.LineIntersectsLine(fromA, dirA, fromB, new Vector2(1, -1));\n"
"// Retorna new Vector2(-1, 0)\n"
"Geometry2D.LineIntersectsLine(fromA, dirA, fromB, new Vector2(-1, -1));\n"
"// Retorna null\n"
"Geometry2D.LineIntersectsLine(fromA, dirA, fromB, Vector2.Right);\n"
"[/csharp]\n"
"[/codeblocks]"

#: doc/classes/Geometry2D.xml
msgid ""
"Given an array of [Vector2]s representing tiles, builds an atlas. The "
"returned dictionary has two keys: [code]points[/code] is a "
"[PackedVector2Array] that specifies the positions of each tile, [code]size[/"
"code] contains the overall size of the whole atlas as [Vector2i]."
msgstr ""
"Dado um array de [Vector2]s representando tiles, constrói um atlas. O "
"dicionário retornado tem duas chaves: [code]points[/code] é um "
"[PackedVector2Array] que especifica as posições de cada tile, [code]size[/"
"code] contém o tamanho geral de todo o atlas como [Vector2i]."

#: doc/classes/Geometry2D.xml
msgid ""
"Merges (combines) [param polygon_a] and [param polygon_b] and returns an "
"array of merged polygons. This performs [constant OPERATION_UNION] between "
"polygons.\n"
"The operation may result in an outer polygon (boundary) and multiple inner "
"polygons (holes) produced which could be distinguished by calling [method "
"is_polygon_clockwise]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Geometry2D.xml
msgid ""
"Inflates or deflates [param polygon] by [param delta] units (pixels). If "
"[param delta] is positive, makes the polygon grow outward. If [param delta] "
"is negative, shrinks the polygon inward. Returns an array of polygons "
"because inflating/deflating may result in multiple discrete polygons. "
"Returns an empty array if [param delta] is negative and the absolute value "
"of it approximately exceeds the minimum bounding rectangle dimensions of the "
"polygon.\n"
"Each polygon's vertices will be rounded as determined by [param join_type].\n"
"The operation may result in an outer polygon (boundary) and inner polygon "
"(hole) produced which could be distinguished by calling [method "
"is_polygon_clockwise].\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] To translate the polygon's vertices specifically, multiply them "
"to a [Transform2D]:\n"
"[codeblocks]\n"
"[gdscript]\n"
"var polygon = PackedVector2Array([Vector2(0, 0), Vector2(100, 0), "
"Vector2(100, 100), Vector2(0, 100)])\n"
"var offset = Vector2(50, 50)\n"
"polygon = Transform2D(0, offset) * polygon\n"
"print(polygon) # Prints [(50.0, 50.0), (150.0, 50.0), (150.0, 150.0), (50.0, "
"150.0)]\n"
"[/gdscript]\n"
"[csharp]\n"
"Vector2[] polygon = [new Vector2(0, 0), new Vector2(100, 0), new "
"Vector2(100, 100), new Vector2(0, 100)];\n"
"var offset = new Vector2(50, 50);\n"
"polygon = new Transform2D(0, offset) * polygon;\n"
"GD.Print((Variant)polygon); // Prints [(50, 50), (150, 50), (150, 150), (50, "
"150)]\n"
"[/csharp]\n"
"[/codeblocks]"
msgstr ""
"Infla ou desinfla o [param polygon] em [param delta] unidades (píxeis). Se "
"[param delta] for positivo, faz o polígono crescer para fora. Se [param "
"delta] for negativo, encolhe o polígono para dentro. Retorna uma matriz de "
"polígonos porque inflar/desinflar pode resultar em múltiplos polígonos "
"discretos. Retorna uma matriz vazia se [param delta] for negativo e seu "
"valor absoluto exceder aproximadamente as dimensões mínimas do retângulo "
"delimitador do polígono.\n"
"Os vértices de cada polígono serão arredondados conforme determinado por "
"[param join_type].\n"
"A operação pode resultar em um polígono externo (limite) e um polígono "
"interno (furo) produzidos, que podem ser distinguidos chamando [method "
"is_polygon_clockwise].\n"
"[b]Nota:[/b] Para transladar os vértices do polígono especificamente, "
"multiplique-os por um [Transform2D]:\n"
"[codeblocks]\n"
"[gdscript]\n"
"var polygon = PackedVector2Array([Vector2(0, 0), Vector2(100, 0), "
"Vector2(100, 100), Vector2(0, 100)])\n"
"var offset = Vector2(50, 50)\n"
"polygon = Transform2D(0, offset) * polygon\n"
"print(polygon) # Imprime [(50.0, 50.0), (150.0, 50.0), (150.0, 150.0), "
"(50.0, 150.0)]\n"
"[/gdscript]\n"
"[csharp]\n"
"Vector2[] polygon = [new Vector2(0, 0), new Vector2(100, 0), new "
"Vector2(100, 100), new Vector2(0, 100)];\n"
"var offset = new Vector2(50, 50);\n"
"polygon = new Transform2D(0, offset) * polygon;\n"
"GD.Print((Variant)polygon); // Imprime [(50, 50), (150, 50), (150, 150), "
"(50, 150)]\n"
"[/csharp]\n"
"[/codeblocks]"

#: doc/classes/Geometry2D.xml
msgid ""
"Inflates or deflates [param polyline] by [param delta] units (pixels), "
"producing polygons. If [param delta] is positive, makes the polyline grow "
"outward. Returns an array of polygons because inflating/deflating may result "
"in multiple discrete polygons. If [param delta] is negative, returns an "
"empty array.\n"
"Each polygon's vertices will be rounded as determined by [param join_type].\n"
"Each polygon's endpoints will be rounded as determined by [param end_type].\n"
"The operation may result in an outer polygon (boundary) and inner polygon "
"(hole) produced which could be distinguished by calling [method "
"is_polygon_clockwise]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Geometry2D.xml
msgid ""
"Returns if [param point] is inside the triangle specified by [param a], "
"[param b] and [param c]."
msgstr ""
"Retorna se [param point] está dentro do triângulo especificado por [param "
"a], [param b] e [param c]."

#: doc/classes/Geometry2D.xml
msgid ""
"Given the 2D segment ([param segment_from], [param segment_to]), returns the "
"position on the segment (as a number between 0 and 1) at which the segment "
"hits the circle that is located at position [param circle_position] and has "
"radius [param circle_radius]. If the segment does not intersect the circle, "
"-1 is returned (this is also the case if the line extending the segment "
"would intersect the circle, but the segment does not)."
msgstr ""
"Dado o segmento 2D ([param segment_from], [param segment_to]), retorna a "
"posição no segmento (como um número entre 0 e 1) em que o segmento atinge o "
"círculo localizado na posição [param circle_position] e com raio [param "
"circle_radius]. Se o segmento não intersectar o círculo, -1 será retornado "
"(esse também é o caso se a linha que estende o segmento intersectasse o "
"círculo, mas o segmento não)."

#: doc/classes/Geometry2D.xml
msgid ""
"Checks if two line segments intersect, with line [code]a[/code] between "
"[param from_a] and [param to_a] and line [code]b[/code] between [param "
"from_b] and [param to_b]. If the line segments intersect, the point of "
"intersection is returned as a [Vector2]. If no intersection takes place, "
"[code]null[/code] is returned."
msgstr ""
"Verifica se dois segmentos de linha se interceptam, com a linha [code]a[/"
"code] entre [param from_a] e [param to_a] e a linha [code]b[/code] entre "
"[param from_b] e [param to_b]. Se os segmentos de linha se interceptarem, o "
"ponto de interseção é retornado como um [Vector2]. Se nenhuma interseção "
"ocorrer, [code]null[/code] será retornado."

#: doc/classes/Geometry2D.xml
msgid ""
"Triangulates the area specified by discrete set of [param points] such that "
"no point is inside the circumcircle of any resulting triangle. Returns a "
"[PackedInt32Array] where each triangle consists of three consecutive point "
"indices into [param points] (i.e. the returned array will have [code]n * 3[/"
"code] elements, with [code]n[/code] being the number of found triangles). If "
"the triangulation did not succeed, an empty [PackedInt32Array] is returned."
msgstr ""
"Triangula a área especificada por um conjunto discreto de [param points] de "
"modo que nenhum ponto esteja dentro da circuncircunferência de nenhum "
"triângulo resultante. Retorna um [PackedInt32Array] onde cada triângulo "
"consiste em três índices de pontos consecutivos em [param points] (ou seja, "
"o array retornado terá elementos [code]n * 3[/code], sendo [code]n[/code] o "
"número de triângulos encontrados). Se a triangulação não for bem-sucedida, "
"um [PackedInt32Array] vazio será retornado."

#: doc/classes/Geometry2D.xml
msgid ""
"Triangulates the polygon specified by the points in [param polygon]. Returns "
"a [PackedInt32Array] where each triangle consists of three consecutive point "
"indices into [param polygon] (i.e. the returned array will have [code]n * 3[/"
"code] elements, with [code]n[/code] being the number of found triangles). "
"Output triangles will always be counter clockwise, and the contour will be "
"flipped if it's clockwise. If the triangulation did not succeed, an empty "
"[PackedInt32Array] is returned."
msgstr ""
"Triangula o polígono especificado pelos pontos em [param polygon]. Retorna "
"um [PackedInt32Array] onde cada triângulo consiste em três índices de pontos "
"consecutivos em [param polygon] (ou seja, o array retornado terá elementos "
"[code]n * 3[/code], sendo [code]n[/code] o número de triângulos "
"encontrados). Os triângulos de saída serão sempre no sentido anti-horário, e "
"o contorno será invertido se estiver no sentido horário. Se a triangulação "
"não for bem-sucedida, um [PackedInt32Array] vazio será retornado."

#: doc/classes/Geometry2D.xml
msgid ""
"Create regions where either subject or clip polygons (or both) are filled."
msgstr ""
"Cria regiões onde polígonos de assunto ou de recorte (ou ambos) são "
"preenchidos."

#: doc/classes/Geometry2D.xml
msgid ""
"Create regions where subject polygons are filled except where clip polygons "
"are filled."
msgstr ""
"Cria regiões onde os polígonos sujeitos são preenchidos, exceto onde os "
"polígonos de corte são preenchidos."

#: doc/classes/Geometry2D.xml
msgid "Create regions where both subject and clip polygons are filled."
msgstr ""
"Cria regiões onde tanto os polígonos de assunto quanto os de recorte são "
"preenchidos."

#: doc/classes/Geometry2D.xml
msgid ""
"Create regions where either subject or clip polygons are filled but not "
"where both are filled."
msgstr ""
"Cria regiões onde os polígonos de assunto ou de recorte são preenchidos, mas "
"não onde ambos são preenchidos."

#: doc/classes/Geometry2D.xml
msgid ""
"Squaring is applied uniformally at all convex edge joins at [code]1 * delta[/"
"code]."
msgstr ""
"O esquadrejamento é aplicado uniformemente em todas as junções de arestas "
"convexas em [code]1 * delta[/code]."

#: doc/classes/Geometry2D.xml
msgid ""
"While flattened paths can never perfectly trace an arc, they are "
"approximated by a series of arc chords."
msgstr ""
"Embora caminhos achatados nunca possam traçar um arco perfeitamente, eles "
"são aproximados por uma série de cordas de arco."

#: doc/classes/Geometry2D.xml
msgid ""
"There's a necessary limit to mitered joins since offsetting edges that join "
"at very acute angles will produce excessively long and narrow \"spikes\". "
"For any given edge join, when miter offsetting would exceed that maximum "
"distance, \"square\" joining is applied."
msgstr ""
"Há um limite necessário para junções em mitre, uma vez que o deslocamento de "
"arestas que se unem em ângulos muito agudos produzirá \"pontas\" "
"excessivamente longas e estreitas. Para qualquer junção de aresta "
"especificada, quando o deslocamento em mitre exceder essa distância máxima, "
"a junção \"quadrada\" é aplicada."

#: doc/classes/Geometry2D.xml
msgid ""
"Endpoints are joined using the [enum PolyJoinType] value and the path filled "
"as a polygon."
msgstr ""
"Os pontos de extremidade são unidos usando o valor [enum PolyJoinType] e o "
"caminho é preenchido como um polígono."

#: doc/classes/Geometry2D.xml
msgid ""
"Endpoints are joined using the [enum PolyJoinType] value and the path filled "
"as a polyline."
msgstr ""
"Os pontos de extremidade são unidos usando o valor [enum PolyJoinType] e o "
"caminho é preenchido como uma polilinha."

#: doc/classes/Geometry2D.xml
msgid "Endpoints are squared off with no extension."
msgstr "As extremidades são cortadas em linha reta, sem extensão."

#: doc/classes/Geometry2D.xml
msgid "Endpoints are squared off and extended by [code]delta[/code] units."
msgstr ""
"As extremidades são cortadas em ângulo reto e estendidas por unidades de "
"[code]delta[/code]."

#: doc/classes/Geometry2D.xml
msgid "Endpoints are rounded off and extended by [code]delta[/code] units."
msgstr ""
"As extremidades são arredondadas e estendidas por unidades de [code]delta[/"
"code]."

#: doc/classes/Geometry3D.xml
msgid "Provides methods for some common 3D geometric operations."
msgstr "Fornece métodos para algumas operações geométricas 3D comuns."

#: doc/classes/Geometry3D.xml
msgid ""
"Provides a set of helper functions to create geometric shapes, compute "
"intersections between shapes, and process various other geometric operations "
"in 3D."
msgstr ""
"Fornece um conjunto de funções auxiliares para criar formas geométricas, "
"calcular interseções entre formas e processar várias outras operações "
"geométricas em 3D."

#: doc/classes/Geometry3D.xml
msgid ""
"Returns an array with 6 [Plane]s that describe the sides of a box centered "
"at the origin. The box size is defined by [param extents], which represents "
"one (positive) corner of the box (i.e. half its actual size)."
msgstr ""
"Retorna um array com 6 [Plane]s que descrevem os lados de uma caixa "
"centralizada na origem. O tamanho da caixa é definido por [param extents], "
"que representa um canto (positivo) da caixa (ou seja, metade do seu tamanho "
"real)."

#: doc/classes/Geometry3D.xml
msgid ""
"Returns an array of [Plane]s closely bounding a faceted capsule centered at "
"the origin with radius [param radius] and height [param height]. The "
"parameter [param sides] defines how many planes will be generated for the "
"side part of the capsule, whereas [param lats] gives the number of "
"latitudinal steps at the bottom and top of the capsule. The parameter [param "
"axis] describes the axis along which the capsule is oriented (0 for X, 1 for "
"Y, 2 for Z)."
msgstr ""
"Retorna um array de [Plane]s que delimitam rigidamente uma cápsula facetada "
"centralizada na origem com raio [param radius] e altura [param height]. O "
"parâmetro [param sides] define quantos planos serão gerados para a parte "
"lateral da cápsula, enquanto [param lats] fornece o número de etapas "
"latitudinais na parte inferior e superior da cápsula. O parâmetro [param "
"axis] descreve o eixo ao longo do qual a cápsula está orientada (0 para X, 1 "
"para Y, 2 para Z)."

#: doc/classes/Geometry3D.xml
msgid ""
"Returns an array of [Plane]s closely bounding a faceted cylinder centered at "
"the origin with radius [param radius] and height [param height]. The "
"parameter [param sides] defines how many planes will be generated for the "
"round part of the cylinder. The parameter [param axis] describes the axis "
"along which the cylinder is oriented (0 for X, 1 for Y, 2 for Z)."
msgstr ""
"Retorna um array de [Plane]s que delimitam rigidamente um cilindro facetado "
"centrado na origem com raio [param radius] e altura [param height]. O "
"parâmetro [param sides] define quantos planos serão gerados para a parte "
"redonda do cilindro. O parâmetro [param axis] descreve o eixo ao longo do "
"qual o cilindro está orientado (0 para X, 1 para Y, 2 para Z)."

#: doc/classes/Geometry3D.xml
msgid ""
"Clips the polygon defined by the points in [param points] against the [param "
"plane] and returns the points of the clipped polygon."
msgstr ""
"Recorta o polígono definido pelos pontos em [param points] em relação ao "
"[param plane] e retorna os pontos do polígono recortado."

#: doc/classes/Geometry3D.xml
msgid ""
"Calculates and returns all the vertex points of a convex shape defined by an "
"array of [param planes]."
msgstr ""
"Calcula e retorna todos os pontos de vértice de uma forma convexa definida "
"por um array de [param planes]."

#: doc/classes/Geometry3D.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the 3D point on the 3D segment ([param s1], [param s2]) that is "
"closest to [param point]. The returned point will always be inside the "
"specified segment."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o ponto 3D no segmento 3D ([param s1], [param s2]) que está mais "
"próximo de [param point]. O ponto retornado estará sempre dentro do segmento "
"especificado."

#: doc/classes/Geometry3D.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the 3D point on the 3D line defined by ([param s1], [param s2]) that "
"is closest to [param point]. The returned point can be inside the segment "
"([param s1], [param s2]) or outside of it, i.e. somewhere on the line "
"extending from the segment."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o ponto 3D na linha 3D definida por ([param s1], [param s2]) que "
"está mais próximo de [param point]. O ponto retornado pode estar dentro do "
"segmento ([param s1], [param s2]) ou fora dele, ou seja, em algum lugar na "
"linha que se estende a partir do segmento."

#: doc/classes/Geometry3D.xml
msgid ""
"Given the two 3D segments ([param p1], [param p2]) and ([param q1], [param "
"q2]), finds those two points on the two segments that are closest to each "
"other. Returns a [PackedVector3Array] that contains this point on ([param "
"p1], [param p2]) as well the accompanying point on ([param q1], [param q2])."
msgstr ""
"Dados os dois segmentos 3D ([param p1], [param p2]) e ([param q1], [param "
"q2]), encontra os dois pontos nesses dois segmentos que estão mais próximos "
"um do outro. Retorna um [PackedVector3Array] que contém este ponto em "
"([param p1], [param p2]) bem como o ponto correspondente em ([param q1], "
"[param q2])."

#: doc/classes/Geometry3D.xml
msgid ""
"Returns a [Vector3] containing weights based on how close a 3D position "
"([param point]) is to a triangle's different vertices ([param a], [param b] "
"and [param c]). This is useful for interpolating between the data of "
"different vertices in a triangle. One example use case is using this to "
"smoothly rotate over a mesh instead of relying solely on face normals.\n"
"[url=https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Barycentric_coordinate_system]Here is a "
"more detailed explanation of barycentric coordinates.[/url]"
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Geometry3D.xml
msgid ""
"Tests if the 3D ray starting at [param from] with the direction of [param "
"dir] intersects the triangle specified by [param a], [param b] and [param "
"c]. If yes, returns the point of intersection as [Vector3]. If no "
"intersection takes place, returns [code]null[/code]."
msgstr ""
"Testa se o raio 3D começando em [param from] com a direção de [param dir] "
"intercepta o triângulo especificado por [param a], [param b] e [param c]. Se "
"sim, retorna o ponto de interseção como [Vector3]. Se nenhuma interseção "
"ocorrer, retorna [code]null[/code]."

#: doc/classes/Geometry3D.xml
msgid ""
"Given a convex hull defined though the [Plane]s in the array [param planes], "
"tests if the segment ([param from], [param to]) intersects with that hull. "
"If an intersection is found, returns a [PackedVector3Array] containing the "
"point the intersection and the hull's normal. Otherwise, returns an empty "
"array."
msgstr ""
"Dado um casco convexo definido através dos [Plane]s no array [param planes], "
"testa se o segmento ([param from], [param to]) intercepta esse casco. Se uma "
"interseção for encontrada, retorna um [PackedVector3Array] contendo o ponto "
"de interseção e a normal do casco. Caso contrário, retorna um array vazio."

#: doc/classes/Geometry3D.xml
msgid ""
"Checks if the segment ([param from], [param to]) intersects the cylinder "
"with height [param height] that is centered at the origin and has radius "
"[param radius]. If no, returns an empty [PackedVector3Array]. If an "
"intersection takes place, the returned array contains the point of "
"intersection and the cylinder's normal at the point of intersection."
msgstr ""
"Verifica se o segmento ([param from], [param to]) intercepta o cilindro com "
"altura [param height] centralizado na origem e com raio [param radius]. Caso "
"contrário, retorna um [PackedVector3Array] vazio. Se ocorrer uma interseção, "
"o array retornado contém o ponto de interseção e a normal do cilindro no "
"ponto de interseção."

#: doc/classes/Geometry3D.xml
msgid ""
"Checks if the segment ([param from], [param to]) intersects the sphere that "
"is located at [param sphere_position] and has radius [param sphere_radius]. "
"If no, returns an empty [PackedVector3Array]. If yes, returns a "
"[PackedVector3Array] containing the point of intersection and the sphere's "
"normal at the point of intersection."
msgstr ""
"Verifica se o segmento ([param from], [param to]) intercepta a esfera "
"localizada em [param sphere_position] e que possui o raio [param "
"sphere_radius]. Se não, retorna um [PackedVector3Array] vazio. Se sim, "
"retorna um [PackedVector3Array] contendo o ponto de interseção e a normal da "
"esfera no ponto de interseção."

#: doc/classes/Geometry3D.xml
msgid ""
"Tests if the segment ([param from], [param to]) intersects the triangle "
"[param a], [param b], [param c]. If yes, returns the point of intersection "
"as [Vector3]. If no intersection takes place, returns [code]null[/code]."
msgstr ""
"Testa se o segmento ([param from], [param to]) intercepta o triângulo [param "
"a], [param b], [param c]. Em caso afirmativo, retorna o ponto de intersecção "
"como [Vector3]. Se nenhuma intersecção ocorrer, retorna [code]null[/code]."

#: doc/classes/Geometry3D.xml
msgid ""
"Tetrahedralizes the volume specified by a discrete set of [param points] in "
"3D space, ensuring that no point lies within the circumsphere of any "
"resulting tetrahedron. The method returns a [PackedInt32Array] where each "
"tetrahedron consists of four consecutive point indices into the [param "
"points] array (resulting in an array with [code]n * 4[/code] elements, where "
"[code]n[/code] is the number of tetrahedra found). If the tetrahedralization "
"is unsuccessful, an empty [PackedInt32Array] is returned."
msgstr ""
"Cria uma tetrahedralização do volume especificado por um conjunto discreto "
"de [param points] em espaço 3D, garantindo que nenhum ponto esteja dentro da "
"circunsufera de nenhum tetraedro resultante. O método retorna um "
"[PackedInt32Array] onde cada tetraedro consiste em quatro índices de pontos "
"consecutivos no array [param points] (resultando em um array com elementos "
"[code]n * 4[/code], onde [code]n[/code] é o número de tetraedros "
"encontrados). Se a tetrahedralização não for bem-sucedida, um "
"[PackedInt32Array] vazio será retornado."

#: doc/classes/GeometryInstance3D.xml
msgid "Base node for geometry-based visual instances."
msgstr "Nó base para instâncias visuais baseadas em geometria."

#: doc/classes/GeometryInstance3D.xml
msgid ""
"Base node for geometry-based visual instances. Shares some common "
"functionality like visibility and custom materials."
msgstr ""
"Nó base para instâncias visuais baseadas em geometria. Compartilha algumas "
"funcionalidades comuns, como visibilidade e materiais personalizados."

#: doc/classes/GeometryInstance3D.xml
msgid "Visibility ranges (HLOD)"
msgstr "Intervalos de visibilidade (HLOD)"

#: doc/classes/GeometryInstance3D.xml
msgid ""
"Set the value of a shader uniform for this instance only ([url=$DOCS_URL/"
"tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.html#per-instance-"
"uniforms]per-instance uniform[/url]). See also [method "
"ShaderMaterial.set_shader_parameter] to assign a uniform on all instances "
"using the same [ShaderMaterial].\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] For a shader uniform to be assignable on a per-instance basis, "
"it [i]must[/i] be defined with [code]instance uniform ...[/code] rather than "
"[code]uniform ...[/code] in the shader code.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] [param name] is case-sensitive and must match the name of the "
"uniform in the code exactly (not the capitalized name in the inspector).\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Per-instance shader uniforms are only available in Spatial and "
"CanvasItem shaders, but not for Fog, Sky, or Particles shaders."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/GeometryInstance3D.xml
msgid "The mode used to cast shadows from this instance."
msgstr "O modo usado para projetar sombras a partir desta instância."

#: doc/classes/GeometryInstance3D.xml
msgid ""
"Overrides the bounding box of this node with a custom one. This can be used "
"to avoid the expensive [AABB] recalculation that happens when a skeleton is "
"used with a [MeshInstance3D] or to have precise control over the "
"[MeshInstance3D]'s bounding box. To use the default AABB, set value to an "
"[AABB] with all fields set to [code]0.0[/code]. To avoid frustum culling, "
"set [member custom_aabb] to a very large AABB that covers your entire game "
"world such as [code]AABB(-10000, -10000, -10000, 20000, 20000, 20000)[/"
"code]. To disable all forms of culling (including occlusion and layer "
"culling), call [method RenderingServer.instance_set_ignore_culling] on the "
"[GeometryInstance3D]'s [RID]."
msgstr ""
"Substitui a caixa delimitadora deste nó por uma personalizada. Isso pode ser "
"usado para evitar o recálculo custoso de [AABB] que ocorre quando um "
"esqueleto é usado com um [MeshInstance3D] ou para ter controle preciso sobre "
"a caixa delimitadora do [MeshInstance3D]. Para usar o AABB padrão, defina o "
"valor para um [AABB] com todos os campos definidos como [code]0.0[/code]. "
"Para evitar o descarte por frustum, defina [member custom_aabb] para um AABB "
"muito grande que cubra todo o seu mundo de jogo, como [code]AABB(-10000, "
"-10000, -10000, 20000, 20000, 20000)[/code]. Para desativar todas as formas "
"de descarte (incluindo oclusão e descarte de camadas), chame [method "
"RenderingServer.instance_set_ignore_culling] no [RID] do "
"[GeometryInstance3D]."

#: doc/classes/GeometryInstance3D.xml
msgid ""
"The extra distance added to the GeometryInstance3D's bounding box ([AABB]) "
"to increase its cull box."
msgstr ""
"A distância extra adicionada à caixa delimitadora do GeometryInstance3D "
"([AABB]) para aumentar sua caixa de corte."

#: doc/classes/GeometryInstance3D.xml
msgid "Use [member gi_lightmap_texel_scale] instead."
msgstr "Use [member gi_lightmap_texel_scale] em vez disso."

#: doc/classes/GeometryInstance3D.xml
msgid "The texel density to use for lightmapping in [LightmapGI]."
msgstr ""
"A densidade de texels a ser usada para mapeamento de luz em [LightmapGI]."

#: doc/classes/GeometryInstance3D.xml
msgid ""
"The texel density to use for lightmapping in [LightmapGI]. Greater scale "
"values provide higher resolution in the lightmap, which can result in "
"sharper shadows for lights that have both direct and indirect light baked. "
"However, greater scale values will also increase the space taken by the mesh "
"in the lightmap texture, which increases the memory, storage, and bake time "
"requirements. When using a single mesh at different scales, consider "
"adjusting this value to keep the lightmap texel density consistent across "
"meshes.\n"
"For example, doubling [member gi_lightmap_texel_scale] doubles the lightmap "
"texture resolution for this object [i]on each axis[/i], so it will "
"[i]quadruple[/i] the texel count."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/GeometryInstance3D.xml
msgid ""
"The global illumination mode to use for the whole geometry. To avoid "
"inconsistent results, use a mode that matches the purpose of the mesh during "
"gameplay (static/dynamic).\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Lights' bake mode will also affect the global illumination "
"rendering. See [member Light3D.light_bake_mode]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/GeometryInstance3D.xml
msgid ""
"If [code]true[/code], disables occlusion culling for this instance. Useful "
"for gizmos that must be rendered even when occlusion culling is in use.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] [member ignore_occlusion_culling] does not affect frustum "
"culling (which is what happens when an object is not visible given the "
"camera's angle). To avoid frustum culling, set [member custom_aabb] to a "
"very large AABB that covers your entire game world such as "
"[code]AABB(-10000, -10000, -10000, 20000, 20000, 20000)[/code]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/GeometryInstance3D.xml
msgid ""
"Changes how quickly the mesh transitions to a lower level of detail. A value "
"of 0 will force the mesh to its lowest level of detail, a value of 1 will "
"use the default settings, and larger values will keep the mesh in a higher "
"level of detail at farther distances.\n"
"Useful for testing level of detail transitions in the editor."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/GeometryInstance3D.xml
msgid ""
"The material overlay for the whole geometry.\n"
"If a material is assigned to this property, it will be rendered on top of "
"any other active material for all the surfaces."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/GeometryInstance3D.xml
msgid ""
"The material override for the whole geometry.\n"
"If a material is assigned to this property, it will be used instead of any "
"material set in any material slot of the mesh."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/GeometryInstance3D.xml
msgid ""
"The transparency applied to the whole geometry (as a multiplier of the "
"materials' existing transparency). [code]0.0[/code] is fully opaque, while "
"[code]1.0[/code] is fully transparent. Values greater than [code]0.0[/code] "
"(exclusive) will force the geometry's materials to go through the "
"transparent pipeline, which is slower to render and can exhibit rendering "
"issues due to incorrect transparency sorting. However, unlike using a "
"transparent material, setting [member transparency] to a value greater than "
"[code]0.0[/code] (exclusive) will [i]not[/i] disable shadow rendering.\n"
"In spatial shaders, [code]1.0 - transparency[/code] is set as the default "
"value of the [code]ALPHA[/code] built-in.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] [member transparency] is clamped between [code]0.0[/code] and "
"[code]1.0[/code], so this property cannot be used to make transparent "
"materials more opaque than they originally are.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Only supported when using the Forward+ rendering method. When "
"using the Mobile or Compatibility rendering method, [member transparency] is "
"ignored and is considered as always being [code]0.0[/code]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/GeometryInstance3D.xml
msgid ""
"Starting distance from which the GeometryInstance3D will be visible, taking "
"[member visibility_range_begin_margin] into account as well. The default "
"value of 0 is used to disable the range check."
msgstr ""
"Distância inicial a partir da qual o GeometryInstance3D ficará visível, "
"levando em conta também [member visibility_range_begin_margin]. O valor "
"padrão 0 é usado para desativar a verificação de intervalo."

#: doc/classes/GeometryInstance3D.xml
msgid ""
"Margin for the [member visibility_range_begin] threshold. The "
"GeometryInstance3D will only change its visibility state when it goes over "
"or under the [member visibility_range_begin] threshold by this amount.\n"
"If [member visibility_range_fade_mode] is [constant "
"VISIBILITY_RANGE_FADE_DISABLED], this acts as a hysteresis distance. If "
"[member visibility_range_fade_mode] is [constant VISIBILITY_RANGE_FADE_SELF] "
"or [constant VISIBILITY_RANGE_FADE_DEPENDENCIES], this acts as a fade "
"transition distance and must be set to a value greater than [code]0.0[/code] "
"for the effect to be noticeable."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/GeometryInstance3D.xml
msgid ""
"Distance from which the GeometryInstance3D will be hidden, taking [member "
"visibility_range_end_margin] into account as well. The default value of 0 is "
"used to disable the range check."
msgstr ""
"Distância a partir da qual o GeometryInstance3D será ocultado, levando "
"também em conta [member visibility_range_end_margin]. O valor padrão 0 é "
"usado para desativar a verificação de intervalo."

#: doc/classes/GeometryInstance3D.xml
msgid ""
"Margin for the [member visibility_range_end] threshold. The "
"GeometryInstance3D will only change its visibility state when it goes over "
"or under the [member visibility_range_end] threshold by this amount.\n"
"If [member visibility_range_fade_mode] is [constant "
"VISIBILITY_RANGE_FADE_DISABLED], this acts as a hysteresis distance. If "
"[member visibility_range_fade_mode] is [constant VISIBILITY_RANGE_FADE_SELF] "
"or [constant VISIBILITY_RANGE_FADE_DEPENDENCIES], this acts as a fade "
"transition distance and must be set to a value greater than [code]0.0[/code] "
"for the effect to be noticeable."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/GeometryInstance3D.xml
msgid ""
"Controls which instances will be faded when approaching the limits of the "
"visibility range."
msgstr ""
"Controla quais instâncias serão esmaecidas ao se aproximarem dos limites do "
"alcance de visibilidade."

#: doc/classes/GeometryInstance3D.xml
msgid ""
"Will not cast any shadows. Use this to improve performance for small "
"geometry that is unlikely to cast noticeable shadows (such as debris)."
msgstr ""
"Não projetará sombras. Use isso para melhorar o desempenho de geometrias "
"pequenas que provavelmente não projetarão sombras perceptíveis (como "
"detritos)."

#: doc/classes/GeometryInstance3D.xml
msgid ""
"Will cast shadows from all visible faces in the GeometryInstance3D.\n"
"Will take culling into account, so faces not being rendered will not be "
"taken into account when shadow casting."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/GeometryInstance3D.xml
msgid ""
"Will cast shadows from all visible faces in the GeometryInstance3D.\n"
"Will not take culling into account, so all faces will be taken into account "
"when shadow casting."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/GeometryInstance3D.xml
msgid ""
"Will only show the shadows casted from this object.\n"
"In other words, the actual mesh will not be visible, only the shadows casted "
"from the mesh will be."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/GeometryInstance3D.xml
msgid ""
"Disabled global illumination mode. Use for dynamic objects that do not "
"contribute to global illumination (such as characters). When using [VoxelGI] "
"and SDFGI, the geometry will [i]receive[/i] indirect lighting and "
"reflections but the geometry will not be considered in GI baking."
msgstr ""
"Modo de iluminação global desativado. Use para objetos dinâmicos que não "
"contribuem para a iluminação global (como personagens). Ao usar [VoxelGI] e "
"SDFGI, a geometria irá [i]receber[/i] iluminação indireta e reflexos, mas a "
"geometria não será considerada no bake de GI."

#: doc/classes/GeometryInstance3D.xml
msgid ""
"Baked global illumination mode. Use for static objects that contribute to "
"global illumination (such as level geometry). This GI mode is effective when "
"using [VoxelGI], SDFGI and [LightmapGI]."
msgstr ""
"Modo de iluminação global baked. Use para objetos estáticos que contribuem "
"para a iluminação global (como a geometria do nível). Este modo de GI é "
"eficaz ao usar [VoxelGI], SDFGI e [LightmapGI]."

#: doc/classes/GeometryInstance3D.xml
msgid ""
"Dynamic global illumination mode. Use for dynamic objects that contribute to "
"global illumination. This GI mode is only effective when using [VoxelGI], "
"but it has a higher performance impact than [constant GI_MODE_STATIC]. When "
"using other GI methods, this will act the same as [constant "
"GI_MODE_DISABLED]. When using [LightmapGI], the object will receive indirect "
"lighting using lightmap probes instead of using the baked lightmap texture."
msgstr ""
"Modo de iluminação global dinâmica. Use para objetos dinâmicos que "
"contribuem para a iluminação global. Este modo GI só é eficaz ao usar "
"[VoxelGI], mas tem um impacto de desempenho maior do que [constant "
"GI_MODE_STATIC]. Ao usar outros métodos GI, isso agirá da mesma forma que "
"[constant GI_MODE_DISABLED]. Ao usar [LightmapGI], o objeto receberá "
"iluminação indireta usando sondas de lightmap em vez de usar a textura de "
"lightmap bakeada."

#: doc/classes/GeometryInstance3D.xml
msgid "The standard texel density for lightmapping with [LightmapGI]."
msgstr "A densidade de texels padrão para mapeamento de luz com [LightmapGI]."

#: doc/classes/GeometryInstance3D.xml
msgid ""
"Multiplies texel density by 2× for lightmapping with [LightmapGI]. To ensure "
"consistency in texel density, use this when scaling a mesh by a factor "
"between 1.5 and 3.0."
msgstr ""
"Multiplica a densidade de texels por 2× para mapeamento de luz com "
"[LightmapGI]. Para garantir consistência na densidade de texels, use isso ao "
"redimensionar uma malha por um fator entre 1.5 e 3.0."

#: doc/classes/GeometryInstance3D.xml
msgid ""
"Multiplies texel density by 4× for lightmapping with [LightmapGI]. To ensure "
"consistency in texel density, use this when scaling a mesh by a factor "
"between 3.0 and 6.0."
msgstr ""
"Multiplica a densidade de texels por 4× para mapeamento de luz com "
"[LightmapGI]. Para garantir consistência na densidade de texels, use isso ao "
"redimensionar uma malha por um fator entre 3.0 e 6.0."

#: doc/classes/GeometryInstance3D.xml
msgid ""
"Multiplies texel density by 8× for lightmapping with [LightmapGI]. To ensure "
"consistency in texel density, use this when scaling a mesh by a factor "
"greater than 6.0."
msgstr ""
"Multiplica a densidade de texels por 8× para mapeamento de luz com "
"[LightmapGI]. Para garantir consistência na densidade de texels, use isso ao "
"dimensionar uma malha por um fator maior que 6.0."

#: doc/classes/GeometryInstance3D.xml
msgid "Represents the size of the [enum LightmapScale] enum."
msgstr "Representa o tamanho da enumeração [enum LightmapScale]."

#: doc/classes/GeometryInstance3D.xml
msgid ""
"Will not fade itself nor its visibility dependencies, hysteresis will be "
"used instead. This is the fastest approach to manual LOD, but it can result "
"in noticeable LOD transitions depending on how the LOD meshes are authored. "
"See [member visibility_range_begin] and [member Node3D.visibility_parent] "
"for more information."
msgstr ""
"Não desvanecerá a si mesmo nem às suas dependências de visibilidade; em vez "
"disso, será usada histerese. Esta é a abordagem mais rápida para LOD manual, "
"mas pode resultar em transições de LOD perceptíveis, dependendo de como as "
"malhas de LOD foram criadas. Veja [member visibility_range_begin] e [member "
"Node3D.visibility_parent] para mais informações."

#: doc/classes/GeometryInstance3D.xml
msgid ""
"Will fade-out itself when reaching the limits of its own visibility range. "
"This is slower than [constant VISIBILITY_RANGE_FADE_DISABLED], but it can "
"provide smoother transitions. The fading range is determined by [member "
"visibility_range_begin_margin] and [member visibility_range_end_margin].\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Only supported when using the Forward+ rendering method. When "
"using the Mobile or Compatibility rendering method, this mode acts like "
"[constant VISIBILITY_RANGE_FADE_DISABLED] but with hysteresis disabled."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/GeometryInstance3D.xml
msgid ""
"Will fade-in its visibility dependencies (see [member "
"Node3D.visibility_parent]) when reaching the limits of its own visibility "
"range. This is slower than [constant VISIBILITY_RANGE_FADE_DISABLED], but it "
"can provide smoother transitions. The fading range is determined by [member "
"visibility_range_begin_margin] and [member visibility_range_end_margin].\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Only supported when using the Forward+ rendering method. When "
"using the Mobile or Compatibility rendering method, this mode acts like "
"[constant VISIBILITY_RANGE_FADE_DISABLED] but with hysteresis disabled."
msgstr ""

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFAccessor.xml
msgid "Represents a glTF accessor."
msgstr "Representa um acessor glTF."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFAccessor.xml
msgid ""
"GLTFAccessor is a data structure representing a glTF [code]accessor[/code] "
"that would be found in the [code]\"accessors\"[/code] array. A buffer is a "
"blob of binary data. A buffer view is a slice of a buffer. An accessor is a "
"typed interpretation of the data in a buffer view.\n"
"Most custom data stored in glTF does not need accessors, only buffer views "
"(see [GLTFBufferView]). Accessors are for more advanced use cases such as "
"interleaved mesh data encoded for the GPU."
msgstr ""

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFAccessor.xml
#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFBufferView.xml
msgid "Buffers, BufferViews, and Accessors in Khronos glTF specification"
msgstr "Buffers, BufferViews e Accessors na especificação glTF da Khronos"

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFAccessor.xml
msgid "Creates a new GLTFAccessor instance by parsing the given [Dictionary]."
msgstr ""
"Cria uma nova instância de GLTFAccessor analisando o [Dictionary] fornecido."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFAccessor.xml
msgid "Serializes this GLTFAccessor instance into a [Dictionary]."
msgstr "Serializa esta instância GLTFAccessor em um [Dictionary]."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFAccessor.xml
msgid "The glTF accessor type, as an enum."
msgstr "O tipo de acessor glTF, como uma enumeração."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFAccessor.xml
msgid ""
"The index of the buffer view this accessor is referencing. If [code]-1[/"
"code], this accessor is not referencing any buffer view."
msgstr ""
"O índice da visualização de buffer que este acessor está referenciando. Se "
"[code]-1[/code], este acessor não está referenciando nenhuma visualização de "
"buffer."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFAccessor.xml
msgid "The offset relative to the start of the buffer view in bytes."
msgstr "O deslocamento relativo ao início do buffer view em bytes."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFAccessor.xml
msgid ""
"The glTF component type as an enum. See [enum GLTFComponentType] for "
"possible values. Within the core glTF specification, a value of 5125 or "
"\"UNSIGNED_INT\" must not be used for any accessor that is not referenced by "
"mesh.primitive.indices."
msgstr ""
"O tipo de componente glTF como um enum. Consulte [enum GLTFComponentType] "
"para valores possíveis. Dentro da especificação principal do glTF, um valor "
"de 5125 ou \"UNSIGNED_INT\" não deve ser usado para nenhum acessador que não "
"seja referenciado por mesh.primitive.indices."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFAccessor.xml
msgid "The number of elements referenced by this accessor."
msgstr "O número de elementos referenciados por este acessor."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFAccessor.xml
msgid "Maximum value of each component in this accessor."
msgstr "Valor máximo de cada componente neste acessor."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFAccessor.xml
msgid "Minimum value of each component in this accessor."
msgstr "Valor mínimo de cada componente neste acessor."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFAccessor.xml
msgid "Specifies whether integer data values are normalized before usage."
msgstr ""
"Especifica se os valores de dados inteiros são normalizados antes do uso."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFAccessor.xml
msgid "Number of deviating accessor values stored in the sparse array."
msgstr ""
"Número de valores de acessório divergentes armazenados na matriz esparsa."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFAccessor.xml
msgid ""
"The index of the buffer view with sparse indices. The referenced buffer view "
"MUST NOT have its target or byteStride properties defined. The buffer view "
"and the optional byteOffset MUST be aligned to the componentType byte length."
msgstr ""
"O índice da visualização de buffer com índices esparsos. A visualização de "
"buffer referenciada NÃO DEVE ter suas propriedades target ou byteStride "
"definidas. A visualização de buffer e o byteOffset opcional DEVEM estar "
"alinhados ao comprimento em bytes do componentType."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFAccessor.xml
msgid ""
"The indices component data type as an enum. Possible values are 5121 for "
"\"UNSIGNED_BYTE\", 5123 for \"UNSIGNED_SHORT\", and 5125 for "
"\"UNSIGNED_INT\"."
msgstr ""
"O tipo de dados do componente de índices como um enum. Os valores possíveis "
"são 5121 para \"UNSIGNED_BYTE\", 5123 para \"UNSIGNED_SHORT\" e 5125 para "
"\"UNSIGNED_INT\"."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFAccessor.xml
msgid ""
"The index of the bufferView with sparse values. The referenced buffer view "
"MUST NOT have its target or byteStride properties defined."
msgstr ""
"O índice do bufferView com valores esparsos. A visualização de buffer "
"referenciada NÃO DEVE ter suas propriedades target ou byteStride definidas."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFAccessor.xml
msgid "The offset relative to the start of the bufferView in bytes."
msgstr "O deslocamento relativo ao início do bufferView em bytes."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFAccessor.xml
msgid "Use [member accessor_type] instead."
msgstr "Use [member accessor_type] em vez disso."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFAccessor.xml
msgid ""
"The glTF accessor type, as an [int]. Possible values are [code]0[/code] for "
"\"SCALAR\", [code]1[/code] for \"VEC2\", [code]2[/code] for \"VEC3\", "
"[code]3[/code] for \"VEC4\", [code]4[/code] for \"MAT2\", [code]5[/code] for "
"\"MAT3\", and [code]6[/code] for \"MAT4\"."
msgstr ""
"O tipo de acessor glTF, como um [int]. Os valores possíveis são [code]0[/"
"code] para \"SCALAR\", [code]1[/code] para \"VEC2\", [code]2[/code] para "
"\"VEC3\", [code]3[/code] para \"VEC4\", [code]4[/code] para \"MAT2\", "
"[code]5[/code] para \"MAT3\" e [code]6[/code] para \"MAT4\"."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFAccessor.xml
msgid ""
"Accessor type \"SCALAR\". For the glTF object model, this can be used to map "
"to a single float, int, or bool value, or a float array."
msgstr ""
"Tipo de acessor \"SCALAR\". Para o modelo de objeto glTF, isso pode ser "
"usado para mapear para um único valor float, int ou bool, ou uma matriz "
"float."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFAccessor.xml
msgid ""
"Accessor type \"VEC2\". For the glTF object model, this maps to \"float2\", "
"represented in the glTF JSON as an array of two floats."
msgstr ""
"Tipo de acessor \"VEC2\". Para o modelo de objeto glTF, isso mapeia para "
"\"float2\", representado no JSON glTF como uma matriz de dois números de "
"ponto flutuante."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFAccessor.xml
msgid ""
"Accessor type \"VEC3\". For the glTF object model, this maps to \"float3\", "
"represented in the glTF JSON as an array of three floats."
msgstr ""
"Tipo de acessor \"VEC3\". Para o modelo de objeto glTF, isso mapeia para "
"\"float3\", representado no JSON glTF como uma matriz de três números de "
"ponto flutuante."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFAccessor.xml
msgid ""
"Accessor type \"VEC4\". For the glTF object model, this maps to \"float4\", "
"represented in the glTF JSON as an array of four floats."
msgstr ""
"Tipo de acessor \"VEC4\". Para o modelo de objeto glTF, isso mapeia para "
"\"float4\", representado no JSON glTF como uma matriz de quatro números de "
"ponto flutuante."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFAccessor.xml
msgid ""
"Accessor type \"MAT2\". For the glTF object model, this maps to "
"\"float2x2\", represented in the glTF JSON as an array of four floats."
msgstr ""
"Tipo de acessor \"MAT2\". Para o modelo de objeto glTF, isso mapeia para "
"\"float2x2\", representado no JSON glTF como uma matriz de quatro números de "
"ponto flutuante."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFAccessor.xml
msgid ""
"Accessor type \"MAT3\". For the glTF object model, this maps to "
"\"float3x3\", represented in the glTF JSON as an array of nine floats."
msgstr ""
"Tipo de acessor \"MAT3\". Para o modelo de objeto glTF, isso mapeia para "
"\"float3x3\", representado no JSON glTF como uma matriz de nove números de "
"ponto flutuante."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFAccessor.xml
msgid ""
"Accessor type \"MAT4\". For the glTF object model, this maps to "
"\"float4x4\", represented in the glTF JSON as an array of sixteen floats."
msgstr ""
"Tipo de acessor \"MAT4\". Para o modelo de objeto glTF, isso mapeia para "
"\"float4x4\", representado no JSON glTF como uma matriz de dezesseis números "
"de ponto flutuante."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFAccessor.xml
msgid ""
"Component type \"NONE\". This is not a valid component type, and is used to "
"indicate that the component type is not set."
msgstr ""
"Tipo de componente \"NONE\". Este não é um tipo de componente válido e é "
"usado para indicar que o tipo de componente não está definido."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFAccessor.xml
msgid ""
"Component type \"BYTE\". The value is [code]0x1400[/code] which comes from "
"OpenGL. This indicates data is stored in 1-byte or 8-bit signed integers. "
"This is a core part of the glTF specification."
msgstr ""
"Tipo de componente \"BYTE\". O valor é [code]0x1400[/code], que vem do "
"OpenGL. Isso indica que os dados são armazenados em inteiros com sinal de 1 "
"byte ou 8 bits. Esta é uma parte central da especificação glTF."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFAccessor.xml
msgid ""
"Component type \"UNSIGNED_BYTE\". The value is [code]0x1401[/code] which "
"comes from OpenGL. This indicates data is stored in 1-byte or 8-bit unsigned "
"integers. This is a core part of the glTF specification."
msgstr ""
"Tipo de componente \"UNSIGNED_BYTE\". O valor é [code]0x1401[/code], que vem "
"do OpenGL. Isso indica que os dados são armazenados em inteiros sem sinal de "
"1 byte ou 8 bits. Esta é uma parte central da especificação glTF."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFAccessor.xml
msgid ""
"Component type \"SHORT\". The value is [code]0x1402[/code] which comes from "
"OpenGL. This indicates data is stored in 2-byte or 16-bit signed integers. "
"This is a core part of the glTF specification."
msgstr ""
"Tipo de componente \"SHORT\". O valor é [code]0x1402[/code], que vem do "
"OpenGL. Isso indica que os dados são armazenados em inteiros com sinal de 2 "
"bytes ou 16 bits. Esta é uma parte central da especificação glTF."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFAccessor.xml
msgid ""
"Component type \"UNSIGNED_SHORT\". The value is [code]0x1403[/code] which "
"comes from OpenGL. This indicates data is stored in 2-byte or 16-bit "
"unsigned integers. This is a core part of the glTF specification."
msgstr ""
"Tipo de componente \"UNSIGNED_SHORT\". O valor é [code]0x1403[/code], que "
"vem do OpenGL. Isso indica que os dados são armazenados em inteiros sem "
"sinal de 2 bytes ou 16 bits. Esta é uma parte central da especificação glTF."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFAccessor.xml
msgid ""
"Component type \"INT\". The value is [code]0x1404[/code] which comes from "
"OpenGL. This indicates data is stored in 4-byte or 32-bit signed integers. "
"This is NOT a core part of the glTF specification, and may not be supported "
"by all glTF importers. May be used by some extensions including "
"[code]KHR_interactivity[/code]."
msgstr ""
"Tipo de componente \"INT\". O valor é [code]0x1404[/code], que vem do "
"OpenGL. Isso indica que os dados são armazenados em inteiros com sinal de 4 "
"bytes ou 32 bits. Esta NÃO é uma parte central da especificação glTF e pode "
"não ser suportada por todos os importadores glTF. Pode ser usado por algumas "
"extensões, incluindo [code]KHR_interactivity[/code]."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFAccessor.xml
msgid ""
"Component type \"UNSIGNED_INT\". The value is [code]0x1405[/code] which "
"comes from OpenGL. This indicates data is stored in 4-byte or 32-bit "
"unsigned integers. This is a core part of the glTF specification."
msgstr ""
"Tipo de componente \"UNSIGNED_INT\". O valor é [code]0x1405[/code], que vem "
"do OpenGL. Isso indica que os dados são armazenados em inteiros sem sinal de "
"4 bytes ou 32 bits. Esta é uma parte central da especificação glTF."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFAccessor.xml
msgid ""
"Component type \"FLOAT\". The value is [code]0x1406[/code] which comes from "
"OpenGL. This indicates data is stored in 4-byte or 32-bit floating-point "
"numbers. This is a core part of the glTF specification."
msgstr ""
"Tipo de componente \"FLOAT\". O valor é [code]0x1406[/code], que vem do "
"OpenGL. Isso indica que os dados são armazenados em números de ponto "
"flutuante de 4 bytes ou 32 bits. Esta é uma parte central da especificação "
"glTF."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFAccessor.xml
msgid ""
"Component type \"DOUBLE\". The value is [code]0x140A[/code] which comes from "
"OpenGL. This indicates data is stored in 8-byte or 64-bit floating-point "
"numbers. This is NOT a core part of the glTF specification, and may not be "
"supported by all glTF importers. May be used by some extensions including "
"[code]KHR_interactivity[/code]."
msgstr ""
"Tipo de componente \"DOUBLE\". O valor é [code]0x140A[/code], que vem do "
"OpenGL. Isso indica que os dados são armazenados em números de ponto "
"flutuante de 8 bytes ou 64 bits. Esta NÃO é uma parte central da "
"especificação glTF e pode não ser suportada por todos os importadores glTF. "
"Pode ser usado por algumas extensões, incluindo [code]KHR_interactivity[/"
"code]."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFAccessor.xml
msgid ""
"Component type \"HALF_FLOAT\". The value is [code]0x140B[/code] which comes "
"from OpenGL. This indicates data is stored in 2-byte or 16-bit floating-"
"point numbers. This is NOT a core part of the glTF specification, and may "
"not be supported by all glTF importers. May be used by some extensions "
"including [code]KHR_interactivity[/code]."
msgstr ""
"Tipo de componente \"HALF_FLOAT\". O valor é [code]0x140B[/code] que vem do "
"OpenGL. Isso indica que os dados são armazenados em números de ponto "
"flutuante de 2 bytes ou 16 bits. Esta NÃO é uma parte central da "
"especificação glTF e pode não ser suportada por todos os importadores glTF. "
"Pode ser usado por algumas extensões, incluindo [code]KHR_interactivity[/"
"code]."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFAccessor.xml
msgid ""
"Component type \"LONG\". The value is [code]0x140E[/code] which comes from "
"OpenGL. This indicates data is stored in 8-byte or 64-bit signed integers. "
"This is NOT a core part of the glTF specification, and may not be supported "
"by all glTF importers. May be used by some extensions including "
"[code]KHR_interactivity[/code]."
msgstr ""
"Tipo de componente \"LONG\". O valor é [code]0x140E[/code], que vem do "
"OpenGL. Isso indica que os dados são armazenados em inteiros com sinal de 8 "
"bytes ou 64 bits. Esta NÃO é uma parte central da especificação glTF e pode "
"não ser suportada por todos os importadores glTF. Pode ser usado por algumas "
"extensões, incluindo [code]KHR_interactivity[/code]."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFAccessor.xml
msgid ""
"Component type \"UNSIGNED_LONG\". The value is [code]0x140F[/code] which "
"comes from OpenGL. This indicates data is stored in 8-byte or 64-bit "
"unsigned integers. This is NOT a core part of the glTF specification, and "
"may not be supported by all glTF importers. May be used by some extensions "
"including [code]KHR_interactivity[/code]."
msgstr ""
"Tipo de componente \"UNSIGNED_LONG\". O valor é [code]0x140F[/code], que vem "
"do OpenGL. Isso indica que os dados são armazenados em inteiros sem sinal de "
"8 bytes ou 64 bits. Esta NÃO é uma parte central da especificação glTF e "
"pode não ser suportada por todos os importadores glTF. Pode ser usado por "
"algumas extensões, incluindo [code]KHR_interactivity[/code]."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFAnimation.xml
msgid ""
"Gets additional arbitrary data in this [GLTFAnimation] instance. This can be "
"used to keep per-node state data in [GLTFDocumentExtension] classes, which "
"is important because they are stateless.\n"
"The argument should be the [GLTFDocumentExtension] name (does not have to "
"match the extension name in the glTF file), and the return value can be "
"anything you set. If nothing was set, the return value is [code]null[/code]."
msgstr ""

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFAnimation.xml
msgid ""
"Sets additional arbitrary data in this [GLTFAnimation] instance. This can be "
"used to keep per-node state data in [GLTFDocumentExtension] classes, which "
"is important because they are stateless.\n"
"The first argument should be the [GLTFDocumentExtension] name (does not have "
"to match the extension name in the glTF file), and the second argument can "
"be anything you want."
msgstr ""

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFAnimation.xml
msgid "The original name of the animation."
msgstr "O nome original da animação."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFBufferView.xml
msgid "Represents a glTF buffer view."
msgstr "Representa uma visualização de buffer glTF."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFBufferView.xml
msgid ""
"GLTFBufferView is a data structure representing a glTF [code]bufferView[/"
"code] that would be found in the [code]\"bufferViews\"[/code] array. A "
"buffer is a blob of binary data. A buffer view is a slice of a buffer that "
"can be used to identify and extract data from the buffer.\n"
"Most custom uses of buffers only need to use the [member buffer], [member "
"byte_length], and [member byte_offset]. The [member byte_stride] and [member "
"indices] properties are for more advanced use cases such as interleaved mesh "
"data encoded for the GPU."
msgstr ""

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFBufferView.xml
msgid ""
"Creates a new GLTFBufferView instance by parsing the given [Dictionary]."
msgstr ""
"Cria uma nova instância de GLTFBufferView analisando o [Dictionary] "
"fornecido."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFBufferView.xml
msgid ""
"Loads the buffer view data from the buffer referenced by this buffer view in "
"the given [GLTFState]. Interleaved data with a byte stride is not yet "
"supported by this method. The data is returned as a [PackedByteArray]."
msgstr ""
"Carrega os dados da visualização de buffer do buffer referenciado por esta "
"visualização de buffer no [GLTFState] fornecido. Dados intercalados com um "
"espaçamento de bytes ainda não são suportados por este método. Os dados são "
"retornados como um [PackedByteArray]."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFBufferView.xml
msgid "Serializes this GLTFBufferView instance into a [Dictionary]."
msgstr "Serializa esta instância GLTFBufferView em um [Dictionary]."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFBufferView.xml
msgid ""
"The index of the buffer this buffer view is referencing. If [code]-1[/code], "
"this buffer view is not referencing any buffer."
msgstr ""
"O índice do buffer ao qual esta visualização de buffer se refere. Se "
"[code]-1[/code], esta visualização de buffer não se refere a nenhum buffer."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFBufferView.xml
msgid ""
"The length, in bytes, of this buffer view. If [code]0[/code], this buffer "
"view is empty."
msgstr ""
"O comprimento, em bytes, desta visualização de buffer. Se [code]0[/code], "
"esta visualização de buffer estará vazia."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFBufferView.xml
msgid ""
"The offset, in bytes, from the start of the buffer to the start of this "
"buffer view."
msgstr ""
"O deslocamento, em bytes, desde o início do buffer até o início desta "
"visualização de buffer."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFBufferView.xml
msgid ""
"The stride, in bytes, between interleaved data. If [code]-1[/code], this "
"buffer view is not interleaved."
msgstr ""
"O espaçamento, em bytes, entre dados entrelaçados. Se [code]-1[/code], esta "
"visualização de buffer não está entrelaçada."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFBufferView.xml
msgid ""
"[code]true[/code] if the GLTFBufferView's OpenGL GPU buffer type is an "
"[code]ELEMENT_ARRAY_BUFFER[/code] used for vertex indices (integer constant "
"[code]34963[/code]). [code]false[/code] if the buffer type is any other "
"value. See [url=https://github.com/KhronosGroup/glTF-Tutorials/blob/master/"
"gltfTutorial/gltfTutorial_005_BuffersBufferViewsAccessors.md]Buffers, "
"BufferViews, and Accessors[/url] for possible values. This property is set "
"on import and used on export."
msgstr ""
"[code]true[/code] se o tipo de buffer OpenGL da GPU do GLTFBufferView for um "
"[code]ELEMENT_ARRAY_BUFFER[/code] usado para índices de vértices (constante "
"inteira [code]34963[/code]). [code]false[/code] se o tipo de buffer for "
"qualquer outro valor. Veja [url=https://github.com/KhronosGroup/glTF-"
"Tutorials/blob/master/gltfTutorial/"
"gltfTutorial_005_BuffersBufferViewsAccessors.md]Buffers, BufferViews, e "
"Accessors[/url] para valores possíveis. Esta propriedade é definida na "
"importação e usada na exportação."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFBufferView.xml
msgid ""
"[code]true[/code] if the GLTFBufferView's OpenGL GPU buffer type is an "
"[code]ARRAY_BUFFER[/code] used for vertex attributes (integer constant "
"[code]34962[/code]). [code]false[/code] if the buffer type is any other "
"value. See [url=https://github.com/KhronosGroup/glTF-Tutorials/blob/master/"
"gltfTutorial/gltfTutorial_005_BuffersBufferViewsAccessors.md]Buffers, "
"BufferViews, and Accessors[/url] for possible values. This property is set "
"on import and used on export."
msgstr ""
"[code]true[/code] se o tipo de buffer OpenGL da GPU do GLTFBufferView for um "
"[code]ARRAY_BUFFER[/code] usado para atributos de vértices (constante "
"inteira [code]34962[/code]). [code]false[/code] se o tipo de buffer for "
"qualquer outro valor. Veja [url=https://github.com/KhronosGroup/glTF-"
"Tutorials/blob/master/gltfTutorial/"
"gltfTutorial_005_BuffersBufferViewsAccessors.md]Buffers, BufferViews, e "
"Accessors[/url] para valores possíveis. Esta propriedade é definida na "
"importação e usada na exportação."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFCamera.xml
msgid "Represents a glTF camera."
msgstr "Representa uma câmera glTF."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFCamera.xml
msgid "Represents a camera as defined by the base glTF spec."
msgstr ""
"Representa uma câmera conforme definida pela especificação base do glTF."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFCamera.xml
msgid "glTF camera detailed specification"
msgstr "Especificação detalhada da câmera glTF"

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFCamera.xml
msgid "glTF camera spec and example file"
msgstr "Especificação de câmera glTF e arquivo de exemplo"

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFCamera.xml
msgid "Creates a new GLTFCamera instance by parsing the given [Dictionary]."
msgstr ""
"Cria uma nova instância GLTFCamera analisando o [Dictionary] fornecido."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFCamera.xml
msgid "Create a new GLTFCamera instance from the given Godot [Camera3D] node."
msgstr ""
"Cria uma nova instância de GLTFCamera a partir do nó [Camera3D] do Godot "
"fornecido."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFCamera.xml
msgid "Serializes this GLTFCamera instance into a [Dictionary]."
msgstr "Serializa esta instância GLTFCamera em um [Dictionary]."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFCamera.xml
msgid "Converts this GLTFCamera instance into a Godot [Camera3D] node."
msgstr "Converte esta instância GLTFCamera em um nó [Camera3D] do Godot."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFCamera.xml
msgid ""
"The distance to the far culling boundary for this camera relative to its "
"local Z axis, in meters. This maps to glTF's [code]zfar[/code] property."
msgstr ""
"A distância até o limite de corte distante para esta câmera em relação ao "
"seu eixo Z local, em metros. Isso mapeia para a propriedade [code]zfar[/"
"code] do glTF."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFCamera.xml
msgid ""
"The distance to the near culling boundary for this camera relative to its "
"local Z axis, in meters. This maps to glTF's [code]znear[/code] property."
msgstr ""
"A distância até o limite de corte próximo para esta câmera em relação ao seu "
"eixo Z local, em metros. Isso mapeia para a propriedade [code]znear[/code] "
"do glTF."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFCamera.xml
msgid ""
"The FOV of the camera. This class and glTF define the camera FOV in radians, "
"while Godot uses degrees. This maps to glTF's [code]yfov[/code] property. "
"This value is only used for perspective cameras, when [member perspective] "
"is [code]true[/code]."
msgstr ""
"O FOV da câmera. Esta classe e o glTF definem o FOV da câmera em radianos, "
"enquanto o Godot usa graus. Isso mapeia para a propriedade [code]yfov[/code] "
"do glTF. Este valor é usado apenas para câmeras em perspectiva, quando "
"[member perspective] é [code]true[/code]."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFCamera.xml
msgid ""
"If [code]true[/code], the camera is in perspective mode. Otherwise, the "
"camera is in orthographic/orthogonal mode. This maps to glTF's camera "
"[code]type[/code] property. See [member Camera3D.projection] and the glTF "
"spec for more information."
msgstr ""
"Se [code]true[/code], a câmera está no modo perspectiva. Caso contrário, a "
"câmera está no modo ortográfico/ortogonal. Isso mapeia para a propriedade "
"[code]type[/code] da câmera do glTF. Consulte [member Camera3D.projection] e "
"a especificação do glTF para obter mais informações."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFCamera.xml
msgid ""
"The size of the camera. This class and glTF define the camera size magnitude "
"as a radius in meters, while Godot defines it as a diameter in meters. This "
"maps to glTF's [code]ymag[/code] property. This value is only used for "
"orthographic/orthogonal cameras, when [member perspective] is [code]false[/"
"code]."
msgstr ""
"O tamanho da câmera. Esta classe e o glTF definem a magnitude do tamanho da "
"câmera como um raio em metros, enquanto o Godot a define como um diâmetro em "
"metros. Isso corresponde à propriedade [code]ymag[/code] do glTF. Este valor "
"é usado apenas para câmeras ortográficas/ortogonais, quando [member "
"perspective] é [code]false[/code]."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFDocument.xml
msgid "Class for importing and exporting glTF files in and out of Godot."
msgstr ""
"Classe para importar e exportar arquivos glTF para dentro e fora do Godot."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFDocument.xml
msgid ""
"GLTFDocument supports reading data from a glTF file, buffer, or Godot scene. "
"This data can then be written to the filesystem, buffer, or used to create a "
"Godot scene.\n"
"All of the data in a glTF scene is stored in the [GLTFState] class. "
"GLTFDocument processes state objects, but does not contain any scene data "
"itself. GLTFDocument has member variables to store export configuration "
"settings such as the image format, but is otherwise stateless. Multiple "
"scenes can be processed with the same settings using the same GLTFDocument "
"object and different [GLTFState] objects.\n"
"GLTFDocument can be extended with arbitrary functionality by extending the "
"[GLTFDocumentExtension] class and registering it with GLTFDocument via "
"[method register_gltf_document_extension]. This allows for custom data to be "
"imported and exported."
msgstr ""

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFDocument.xml
msgid "glTF 'What the duck?' guide"
msgstr "Guia glTF 'What the duck?'"

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFDocument.xml
msgid "Khronos glTF specification"
msgstr "Especificação Khronos glTF"

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFDocument.xml
msgid ""
"Takes a [PackedByteArray] defining a glTF and imports the data to the given "
"[GLTFState] object through the [param state] parameter.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] The [param base_path] tells [method append_from_buffer] where "
"to find dependencies and can be empty."
msgstr ""

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFDocument.xml
msgid ""
"Takes a path to a glTF file and imports the data at that file path to the "
"given [GLTFState] object through the [param state] parameter.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] The [param base_path] tells [method append_from_file] where to "
"find dependencies and can be empty."
msgstr ""

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFDocument.xml
msgid ""
"Takes a Godot Engine scene node and exports it and its descendants to the "
"given [GLTFState] object through the [param state] parameter."
msgstr ""
"Pega um nó de cena da Godot Engine e exporta ele e seus descendentes para o "
"objeto [GLTFAstate] fornecido através do parâmetro [param state]."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFDocument.xml
msgid ""
"Determines a mapping between the given Godot [param node_path] and the "
"corresponding glTF Object Model JSON pointer(s) in the generated glTF file. "
"The details of this mapping are returned in a [GLTFObjectModelProperty] "
"object. Additional mappings can be supplied via the [method "
"GLTFDocumentExtension._import_object_model_property] callback method."
msgstr ""
"Determina um mapeamento entre o [param node_path] do Godot fornecido e o(s) "
"ponteiro(s) JSON do Modelo de Objeto glTF correspondente(s) no arquivo glTF "
"gerado. Os detalhes deste mapeamento são retornados em um objeto "
"[GLTFObjectModelProperty]. Mapeamentos adicionais podem ser fornecidos por "
"meio do método de retorno de chamada [method "
"GLTFDocumentExtension._import_object_model_property]."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFDocument.xml
msgid ""
"Takes a [GLTFState] object through the [param state] parameter and returns a "
"glTF [PackedByteArray]."
msgstr ""
"Leva um objeto [GLTFState] através do parâmetro [param state] e retorna um "
"[PackedByteArray] glTF."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFDocument.xml
msgid ""
"Takes a [GLTFState] object through the [param state] parameter and returns a "
"Godot Engine scene node.\n"
"The [param bake_fps] parameter overrides the bake_fps in [param state]."
msgstr ""

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFDocument.xml
msgid ""
"Returns a list of all support glTF extensions, including extensions "
"supported directly by the engine, and extensions supported by user plugins "
"registering [GLTFDocumentExtension] classes.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] If this method is run before a GLTFDocumentExtension is "
"registered, its extensions won't be included in the list. Be sure to only "
"run this method after all extensions are registered. If you run this when "
"the engine starts, consider waiting a frame before calling this method to "
"ensure all extensions are registered."
msgstr ""

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFDocument.xml
msgid ""
"Determines a mapping between the given glTF Object Model [param "
"json_pointer] and the corresponding Godot node path(s) in the generated "
"Godot scene. The details of this mapping are returned in a "
"[GLTFObjectModelProperty] object. Additional mappings can be supplied via "
"the [method GLTFDocumentExtension._export_object_model_property] callback "
"method."
msgstr ""
"Determina um mapeamento entre o [param json_pointer] do Modelo de Objeto "
"glTF fornecido e o(s) caminho(s) correspondente(s) do nó Godot na cena Godot "
"gerada. Os detalhes deste mapeamento são retornados em um objeto "
"[GLTFObjectModelProperty]. Mapeamentos adicionais podem ser fornecidos por "
"meio do método de retorno de chamada [method "
"GLTFDocumentExtension._export_object_model_property]."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFDocument.xml
msgid ""
"Registers the given [GLTFDocumentExtension] instance with GLTFDocument. If "
"[param first_priority] is [code]true[/code], this extension will be run "
"first. Otherwise, it will be run last.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Like GLTFDocument itself, all GLTFDocumentExtension classes "
"must be stateless in order to function properly. If you need to store data, "
"use the [code]set_additional_data[/code] and [code]get_additional_data[/"
"code] methods in [GLTFState] or [GLTFNode]."
msgstr ""

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFDocument.xml
msgid "Unregisters the given [GLTFDocumentExtension] instance."
msgstr "Desregistra a instância de [GLTFDocumentExtension] fornecida."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFDocument.xml
msgid ""
"Takes a [GLTFState] object through the [param state] parameter and writes a "
"glTF file to the filesystem.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] The extension of the glTF file determines if it is a .glb "
"binary file or a .gltf text file."
msgstr ""

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFDocument.xml
msgid ""
"The user-friendly name of the fallback image format. This is used when "
"exporting the glTF file, including writing to a file and writing to a byte "
"array.\n"
"This property may only be one of \"None\", \"PNG\", or \"JPEG\", and is only "
"used when the [member image_format] is not one of \"None\", \"PNG\", or "
"\"JPEG\". If having multiple extension image formats is desired, that can be "
"done using a [GLTFDocumentExtension] class - this property only covers the "
"use case of providing a base glTF fallback image when using a custom image "
"format."
msgstr ""

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFDocument.xml
msgid ""
"The quality of the fallback image, if any. For PNG files, this downscales "
"the image on both dimensions by this factor. For JPEG files, this is the "
"lossy quality of the image. A low value is recommended, since including "
"multiple high quality images in a glTF file defeats the file size gains of "
"using a more efficient image format."
msgstr ""
"A qualidade da imagem de fallback, se houver. Para arquivos PNG, isso reduz "
"a escala da imagem em ambas as dimensões por este fator. Para arquivos JPEG, "
"esta é a qualidade com perda da imagem. Um valor baixo é recomendado, uma "
"vez que incluir várias imagens de alta qualidade em um arquivo glTF anula os "
"ganhos de tamanho de arquivo obtidos com o uso de um formato de imagem mais "
"eficiente."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFDocument.xml
msgid ""
"The user-friendly name of the export image format. This is used when "
"exporting the glTF file, including writing to a file and writing to a byte "
"array.\n"
"By default, Godot allows the following options: \"None\", \"PNG\", \"JPEG\", "
"\"Lossless WebP\", and \"Lossy WebP\". Support for more image formats can be "
"added in [GLTFDocumentExtension] classes. A single extension class can "
"provide multiple options for the specific format to use, or even an option "
"that uses multiple formats at once."
msgstr ""

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFDocument.xml
msgid ""
"If [member image_format] is a lossy image format, this determines the lossy "
"quality of the image. On a range of [code]0.0[/code] to [code]1.0[/code], "
"where [code]0.0[/code] is the lowest quality and [code]1.0[/code] is the "
"highest quality. A lossy quality of [code]1.0[/code] is not the same as "
"lossless."
msgstr ""
"Se [member image_format] for um formato de imagem com perdas, isso determina "
"a qualidade com perdas da imagem. Em um intervalo de [code]0.0[/code] a "
"[code]1.0[/code], onde [code]0.0[/code] é a qualidade mais baixa e "
"[code]1.0[/code] é a qualidade mais alta. Uma qualidade com perdas de "
"[code]1.0[/code] não é a mesma coisa que sem perdas."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFDocument.xml
msgid ""
"How to process the root node during export. The default and recommended "
"value is [constant ROOT_NODE_MODE_SINGLE_ROOT].\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Regardless of how the glTF file is exported, when importing, "
"the root node type and name can be overridden in the scene import settings "
"tab."
msgstr ""

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFDocument.xml
msgid ""
"How to handle texture maps during import. The default and recommended value "
"is [constant TEXTURE_MAP_MODE_REMAP_TO_STANDARD_MATERIAL], which "
"automatically remaps from glTF's flexible texture map system to the more "
"specific texture map slots in Godot's [StandardMaterial3D] class. "
"Alternatively, [constant TEXTURE_MAP_MODE_DO_NOT_REMAP] can be used to "
"preserve the original texture maps from the glTF file, which may be "
"desirable if using the glTF file with custom shaders, but may not display "
"correctly with Godot's built-in materials."
msgstr ""
"Como lidar com mapas de textura durante a importação. O valor padrão e "
"recomendado é [constant TEXTURE_MAP_MODE_REMAP_TO_STANDARD_MATERIAL], que "
"remapeia automaticamente do sistema flexível de mapa de textura do glTF para "
"os slots de mapa de textura mais específicos na classe [StandardMaterial3D] "
"do Godot. Como alternativa, [constant TEXTURE_MAP_MODE_DO_NOT_REMAP] pode "
"ser usado para preservar os mapas de textura originais do arquivo glTF, o "
"que pode ser desejável se estiver usando o arquivo glTF com shaders "
"personalizados, mas pode não ser exibido corretamente com os materiais "
"integrados do Godot."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFDocument.xml
msgid ""
"How to deal with node visibility during export. This setting does nothing if "
"all nodes are visible. The default and recommended value is [constant "
"VISIBILITY_MODE_INCLUDE_REQUIRED], which uses the [code]KHR_node_visibility[/"
"code] extension."
msgstr ""
"Como lidar com a visibilidade de nós durante a exportação. Esta configuração "
"não faz nada se todos os nós estiverem visíveis. O valor padrão e "
"recomendado é [constant VISIBILITY_MODE_INCLUDE_REQUIRED], que usa a "
"extensão [code]KHR_node_visibility[/code]."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFDocument.xml
msgid ""
"Treat the Godot scene's root node as the root node of the glTF file, and "
"mark it as the single root node via the [code]GODOT_single_root[/code] glTF "
"extension. This will be parsed the same as [constant "
"ROOT_NODE_MODE_KEEP_ROOT] if the implementation does not support "
"[code]GODOT_single_root[/code]."
msgstr ""
"Trata o nó raiz da cena do Godot como o nó raiz do arquivo glTF e o marca "
"como o único nó raiz por meio da extensão glTF [code]GODOT_single_root[/"
"code]. Isso será analisado da mesma forma que [constant "
"ROOT_NODE_MODE_KEEP_ROOT] se a implementação não suportar "
"[code]GODOT_single_root[/code]."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFDocument.xml
msgid ""
"Treat the Godot scene's root node as the root node of the glTF file, but do "
"not mark it as anything special. An extra root node will be generated when "
"importing into Godot. This uses only vanilla glTF features. This is "
"equivalent to the behavior in Godot 4.1 and earlier."
msgstr ""
"Trata o nó raiz da cena do Godot como o nó raiz do arquivo glTF, mas não o "
"marca como nada de especial. Um nó raiz extra será gerado ao importar para o "
"Godot. Isso usa apenas recursos padrão de glTF. Isso é equivalente ao "
"comportamento no Godot 4.1 e anteriores."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFDocument.xml
msgid ""
"Treat the Godot scene's root node as the name of the glTF scene, and add all "
"of its children as root nodes of the glTF file. This uses only vanilla glTF "
"features. This avoids an extra root node, but only the name of the Godot "
"scene's root node will be preserved, as it will not be saved as a node."
msgstr ""
"Trata o nó raiz da cena do Godot como o nome da cena glTF e adiciona todos "
"os seus filhos como nós raiz do arquivo glTF. Isso usa apenas recursos "
"nativos do glTF. Isso evita um nó raiz extra, mas apenas o nome do nó raiz "
"da cena do Godot será preservado, pois ele não será salvo como um nó."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFDocument.xml
msgid ""
"Import the texture maps in the glTF file as they are, without trying to fit "
"them into specific texture slots suitable for Godot's built-in materials. "
"This may be desirable if using the glTF file with custom shaders, but may "
"not display correctly with Godot's built-in materials. This is equivalent to "
"the behavior in Godot 4.6 and earlier."
msgstr ""
"Importa os mapas de textura no arquivo glTF como estão, sem tentar encaixá-"
"los em slots de textura específicos adequados para os materiais integrados "
"do Godot. Isso pode ser desejável ao usar o arquivo glTF com shaders "
"personalizados, mas pode não ser exibido corretamente com os materiais "
"integrados do Godot. Isso é equivalente ao comportamento no Godot 4.6 e "
"anteriores."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFDocument.xml
msgid ""
"Import the texture maps in the glTF file remapped to the most suitable "
"texture slots based on Godot's [StandardMaterial3D] class. This is the "
"default behavior."
msgstr ""
"Importa os mapas de textura no arquivo glTF remapeados para os slots de "
"textura mais adequados com base na classe [StandardMaterial3D] do Godot. "
"Este é o comportamento padrão."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFDocument.xml
msgid ""
"If the scene contains any non-visible nodes, include them, mark them as non-"
"visible with [code]KHR_node_visibility[/code], and require that importers "
"respect their non-visibility. Downside: If the importer does not support "
"[code]KHR_node_visibility[/code], the file cannot be imported."
msgstr ""
"Se a cena contiver nós não visíveis, inclua-os, marque-os como não visíveis "
"com [code]KHR_node_visibility[/code] e exija que os importadores respeitem "
"sua não visibilidade. Desvantagem: Se o importador não suportar "
"[code]KHR_node_visibility[/code], o arquivo não poderá ser importado."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFDocument.xml
msgid ""
"If the scene contains any non-visible nodes, include them, mark them as non-"
"visible with [code]KHR_node_visibility[/code], and do not impose any "
"requirements on importers. Downside: If the importer does not support "
"[code]KHR_node_visibility[/code], invisible objects will be visible."
msgstr ""
"Se a cena contiver nós não visíveis, inclua-os, marque-os como não visíveis "
"com [code]KHR_node_visibility[/code] e não impõe nenhum requisito aos "
"importadores. Desvantagem: Se o importador não suportar "
"[code]KHR_node_visibility[/code], objetos invisíveis ficarão visíveis."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFDocument.xml
msgid ""
"If the scene contains any non-visible nodes, do not include them in the "
"export. This is the same as the behavior in Godot 4.4 and earlier. Downside: "
"Invisible nodes will not exist in the exported file."
msgstr ""
"Se a cena contiver algum nó não visível, não os inclua na exportação. Este é "
"o mesmo comportamento do Godot 4.4 e anteriores. Desvantagem: Nós invisíveis "
"não existirão no arquivo exportado."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFDocumentExtension.xml
msgid "[GLTFDocument] extension class."
msgstr "Classe de extensão [GLTFDocument]."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFDocumentExtension.xml
msgid ""
"Extends the functionality of the [GLTFDocument] class by allowing you to run "
"arbitrary code at various stages of glTF import or export.\n"
"To use, make a new class extending GLTFDocumentExtension, override any "
"methods you need, make an instance of your class, and register it using "
"[method GLTFDocument.register_gltf_document_extension].\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] All GLTFDocumentExtension classes are duplicated when beginning "
"the import or export process. Except for configuration values, these classes "
"must be stateless in order to function properly. If you need to store data, "
"use the [code]set_additional_data[/code] and [code]get_additional_data[/"
"code] methods in [GLTFState] or [GLTFNode]."
msgstr ""

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFDocumentExtension.xml
msgid ""
"Part of the export process. This method is run after [method "
"_export_preflight] and before [method _export_post_convert].\n"
"Runs when converting the data from a Godot scene node. This method can be "
"used to process the Godot scene node data into a format that can be used by "
"[method _export_node]."
msgstr ""

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFDocumentExtension.xml
msgid ""
"Runs prior to the export process. This method is run before [method "
"_export_preflight] when exporting a scene from the editor, or it may not be "
"run at all in other situations.\n"
"Unlike the rest of the export methods, this does not run when calling a "
"[GLTFDocument]'s export methods in sequence with everything else, but rather "
"runs before that entire process occurs, allowing configuration to occur "
"beforehand, potentially minutes or hours in advance of [method "
"_export_preflight]. This allows extensions to decide which properties to "
"show in the editor export settings dialog based on the contents of the "
"scene, hiding any settings that are not relevant for that scene. The [param "
"root_node] parameter may be [code]null[/code], in which case all properties "
"should be shown."
msgstr ""

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFDocumentExtension.xml
msgid ""
"Part of the export process. This method is run after [method "
"_get_saveable_image_formats] and before [method _export_post]. If this "
"[GLTFDocumentExtension] is used for exporting images, this runs after "
"[method _serialize_texture_json].\n"
"This method can be used to modify the final JSON of each node. Data should "
"be primarily stored in [param gltf_node] prior to serializing the JSON, but "
"the original Godot [Node] is also provided if available. [param node] may be "
"[code]null[/code] if not available, such as when exporting glTF data not "
"generated from a Godot scene."
msgstr ""

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFDocumentExtension.xml
msgid ""
"Part of the export process. Allows GLTFDocumentExtension classes to provide "
"mappings for properties of nodes in the Godot scene tree, to JSON pointers "
"to glTF properties, as defined by the glTF object model.\n"
"Returns a [GLTFObjectModelProperty] instance that defines how the property "
"should be mapped. If your extension can't handle the property, return "
"[code]null[/code] or an instance without any JSON pointers (see [method "
"GLTFObjectModelProperty.has_json_pointers]). You should use [method "
"GLTFObjectModelProperty.set_types] to set the types, and set the JSON "
"pointer(s) using the [member GLTFObjectModelProperty.json_pointers] "
"property.\n"
"The parameters provide context for the property, including the NodePath, the "
"Godot node, the GLTF node index, and the target object. The [param "
"target_object] will be equal to [param godot_node] if no sub-object can be "
"found, otherwise it will point to a sub-object. For example, if the path is "
"[code]^\"A/B/C/MeshInstance3D:mesh:surface_0/material:emission_intensity\"[/"
"code], it will get the node, then the mesh, and then the material, so [param "
"target_object] will be the [Material] resource, and [param target_depth] "
"will be 2 because 2 levels were traversed to get to the target."
msgstr ""

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFDocumentExtension.xml
msgid ""
"Part of the export process. This method is run last, after all other parts "
"of the export process.\n"
"This method can be used to modify the final JSON of the generated glTF file."
msgstr ""

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFDocumentExtension.xml
msgid ""
"Part of the export process. This method is run after [method "
"_convert_scene_node] and before [method _export_preserialize].\n"
"This method can be used to modify the converted node data structures before "
"serialization with any additional data from the scene tree."
msgstr ""

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFDocumentExtension.xml
msgid ""
"Part of the export process. This method is run first, before all other parts "
"of the export process.\n"
"The return value is used to determine if this [GLTFDocumentExtension] "
"instance should be used for exporting a given glTF file. If [constant OK], "
"the export will use this [GLTFDocumentExtension] instance. If not "
"overridden, [constant OK] is returned."
msgstr ""

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFDocumentExtension.xml
msgid ""
"Part of the export process. This method is run after [method "
"_export_post_convert] and before [method _get_saveable_image_formats].\n"
"This method can be used to alter the state before performing serialization. "
"It runs every time when generating a buffer with [method "
"GLTFDocument.generate_buffer] or writing to the file system with [method "
"GLTFDocument.write_to_filesystem]."
msgstr ""

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFDocumentExtension.xml
msgid ""
"Part of the import process. This method is run after [method "
"_import_pre_generate] and before [method _import_node].\n"
"Runs when generating a Godot scene node from a GLTFNode. The returned node "
"will be added to the scene tree. Multiple nodes can be generated in this "
"step if they are added as a child of the returned node.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] The [param scene_parent] parameter may be [code]null[/code] if "
"this is the single root node."
msgstr ""

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFDocumentExtension.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the file extension to use for saving image data into, for example, "
"[code]\".png\"[/code]. If defined, when this extension is used to handle "
"images, and the images are saved to a separate file, the image bytes will be "
"copied to a file with this extension. If this is set, there should be a "
"[ResourceImporter] class able to import the file. If not defined or empty, "
"Godot will save the image into a PNG file."
msgstr ""
"Retorna a extensão de arquivo a ser usada para salvar dados de imagem, por "
"exemplo, [code]\".png\"[/code]. Se definida, quando esta extensão for usada "
"para manipular imagens, e as imagens forem salvas em um arquivo separado, os "
"bytes da imagem serão copiados para um arquivo com esta extensão. Se isso "
"estiver definido, deve haver uma classe [ResourceImporter] capaz de importar "
"o arquivo. Se não estiver definida ou vazia, o Godot salvará a imagem em um "
"arquivo PNG."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFDocumentExtension.xml
msgid ""
"Part of the export process. This method is run after [method "
"_convert_scene_node] and before [method _export_node].\n"
"Returns an array of the image formats that can be saved/exported by this "
"extension. This extension will only be selected as the image exporter if the "
"[GLTFDocument]'s [member GLTFDocument.image_format] is in this array. If "
"this [GLTFDocumentExtension] is selected as the image exporter, one of the "
"[method _save_image_at_path] or [method _serialize_image_to_bytes] methods "
"will run next, otherwise [method _export_node] will run next. If the format "
"name contains [code]\"Lossy\"[/code], the lossy quality slider will be "
"displayed."
msgstr ""

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFDocumentExtension.xml
msgid ""
"Part of the import process. This method is run after [method "
"_import_preflight] and before [method _parse_node_extensions].\n"
"Returns an array of the glTF extensions supported by this "
"GLTFDocumentExtension class. This is used to validate if a glTF file with "
"required extensions can be loaded."
msgstr ""

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFDocumentExtension.xml
msgid ""
"Part of the import process. This method is run after [method "
"_generate_scene_node] and before [method _import_post].\n"
"This method can be used to make modifications to each of the generated Godot "
"scene nodes."
msgstr ""

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFDocumentExtension.xml
msgid ""
"Part of the import process. Allows GLTFDocumentExtension classes to provide "
"mappings for JSON pointers to glTF properties, as defined by the glTF object "
"model, to properties of nodes in the Godot scene tree.\n"
"Returns a [GLTFObjectModelProperty] instance that defines how the property "
"should be mapped. If your extension can't handle the property, return "
"[code]null[/code] or an instance without any NodePaths (see [method "
"GLTFObjectModelProperty.has_node_paths]). You should use [method "
"GLTFObjectModelProperty.set_types] to set the types, and [method "
"GLTFObjectModelProperty.append_path_to_property] function is useful for most "
"simple cases.\n"
"In many cases, [param partial_paths] will contain the start of a path, "
"allowing the extension to complete the path. For example, for [code]/nodes/3/"
"extensions/MY_ext/prop[/code], Godot will pass you a NodePath that leads to "
"node 3, so the GLTFDocumentExtension class only needs to resolve the last "
"[code]MY_ext/prop[/code] part of the path. In this example, the extension "
"should check [code]split.size() > 4 and split[0] == \"nodes\" and split[2] "
"== \"extensions\" and split[3] == \"MY_ext\"[/code] at the start of the "
"function to check if this JSON pointer applies to it, then it can use [param "
"partial_paths] and handle [code]split[4][/code]."
msgstr ""

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFDocumentExtension.xml
msgid ""
"Part of the import process. This method is run last, after all other parts "
"of the import process.\n"
"This method can be used to modify the final Godot scene generated by the "
"import process."
msgstr ""

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFDocumentExtension.xml
msgid ""
"Part of the import process. This method is run after [method "
"_parse_node_extensions] and before [method _import_pre_generate].\n"
"This method can be used to modify any of the data imported so far after "
"parsing each node, but before generating the scene or any of its nodes."
msgstr ""

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFDocumentExtension.xml
msgid ""
"Part of the import process. This method is run after [method "
"_import_post_parse] and before [method _generate_scene_node].\n"
"This method can be used to modify or read from any of the processed data "
"structures, before generating the nodes and then running the final per-node "
"import step."
msgstr ""

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFDocumentExtension.xml
msgid ""
"Part of the import process. This method is run first, before all other parts "
"of the import process.\n"
"The return value is used to determine if this [GLTFDocumentExtension] "
"instance should be used for importing a given glTF file. If [constant OK], "
"the import will use this [GLTFDocumentExtension] instance. If not "
"overridden, [constant OK] is returned."
msgstr ""

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFDocumentExtension.xml
msgid ""
"Part of the import process. This method is run after [method "
"_parse_node_extensions] and before [method _parse_texture_json].\n"
"Runs when parsing image data from a glTF file. The data could be sourced "
"from a separate file, a URI, or a buffer, and then is passed as a byte array."
msgstr ""

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFDocumentExtension.xml
msgid ""
"Part of the import process. This method is run after [method "
"_get_supported_extensions] and before [method _import_post_parse].\n"
"Runs when parsing the node extensions of a GLTFNode. This method can be used "
"to process the extension JSON data into a format that can be used by [method "
"_generate_scene_node]. The return value should be a member of the [enum "
"Error] enum."
msgstr ""

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFDocumentExtension.xml
msgid ""
"Part of the import process. This method is run after [method "
"_parse_image_data] and before [method _generate_scene_node].\n"
"Runs when parsing the texture JSON from the glTF textures array. This can be "
"used to set the source image index to use as the texture."
msgstr ""

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFDocumentExtension.xml
msgid ""
"Part of the export process. This method is run after [method "
"_get_saveable_image_formats] and before [method _serialize_texture_json].\n"
"This method is run when saving images separately from the glTF file. When "
"images are embedded, [method _serialize_image_to_bytes] runs instead. Note "
"that these methods only run when this [GLTFDocumentExtension] is selected as "
"the image exporter."
msgstr ""

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFDocumentExtension.xml
msgid ""
"Part of the export process. This method is run after [method "
"_get_saveable_image_formats] and before [method _serialize_texture_json].\n"
"This method is run when embedding images in the glTF file. When images are "
"saved separately, [method _save_image_at_path] runs instead. Note that these "
"methods only run when this [GLTFDocumentExtension] is selected as the image "
"exporter.\n"
"This method must set the image MIME type in the [param image_dict] with the "
"[code]\"mimeType\"[/code] key. For example, for a PNG image, it would be set "
"to [code]\"image/png\"[/code]. The return value must be a [PackedByteArray] "
"containing the image data."
msgstr ""

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFDocumentExtension.xml
msgid ""
"Part of the export process. This method is run after [method "
"_save_image_at_path] or [method _serialize_image_to_bytes], and before "
"[method _export_node]. Note that this method only runs when this "
"[GLTFDocumentExtension] is selected as the image exporter.\n"
"This method can be used to set up the extensions for the texture JSON by "
"editing [param texture_json]. The extension must also be added as used "
"extension with [method GLTFState.add_used_extension], be sure to set "
"[code]required[/code] to [code]true[/code] if you are not providing a "
"fallback."
msgstr ""

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFLight.xml
msgid "Represents a glTF light."
msgstr "Representa uma luz glTF."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFLight.xml
msgid ""
"Represents a light as defined by the [code]KHR_lights_punctual[/code] glTF "
"extension."
msgstr ""
"Representa uma luz conforme definida pela extensão glTF "
"[code]KHR_lights_punctual[/code]."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFLight.xml
msgid "KHR_lights_punctual glTF extension spec"
msgstr "Especificação da extensão glTF KHR_lights_punctual"

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFLight.xml
msgid "Creates a new GLTFLight instance by parsing the given [Dictionary]."
msgstr "Cria uma nova instância GLTFLight analisando o [Dictionary] fornecido."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFLight.xml
msgid "Create a new GLTFLight instance from the given Godot [Light3D] node."
msgstr ""
"Cria uma nova instância GLTFLight a partir do nó [Light3D] do Godot "
"fornecido."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFLight.xml
msgid "Serializes this GLTFLight instance into a [Dictionary]."
msgstr "Serializa esta instância GLTFLight em um [Dictionary]."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFLight.xml
msgid "Converts this GLTFLight instance into a Godot [Light3D] node."
msgstr "Converte esta instância GLTFLight em um nó [Light3D] do Godot."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFLight.xml
msgid ""
"The [Color] of the light in linear space. Defaults to white. A black color "
"causes the light to have no effect.\n"
"This value is linear to match glTF, but will be converted to nonlinear sRGB "
"when creating a Godot [Light3D] node upon import, or converted to linear "
"when exporting a Godot [Light3D] to glTF."
msgstr ""

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFLight.xml
msgid ""
"The inner angle of the cone in a spotlight. Must be less than or equal to "
"the outer cone angle.\n"
"Within this angle, the light is at full brightness. Between the inner and "
"outer cone angles, there is a transition from full brightness to zero "
"brightness. When creating a Godot [SpotLight3D], the ratio between the inner "
"and outer cone angles is used to calculate the attenuation of the light."
msgstr ""

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFLight.xml
msgid ""
"The intensity of the light. This is expressed in candelas (lumens per "
"steradian) for point and spot lights, and lux (lumens per m²) for "
"directional lights. When creating a Godot light, this value is converted to "
"a unitless multiplier."
msgstr ""
"A intensidade da luz. Isso é expresso em candelas (lúmens por esterradiano) "
"para luzes pontuais e de facho, e lux (lúmens por m²) para luzes "
"direcionais. Ao criar uma luz no Godot, esse valor é convertido em um "
"multiplicador sem unidade."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFLight.xml
msgid ""
"The type of the light. The values accepted by Godot are \"point\", \"spot\", "
"and \"directional\", which correspond to Godot's [OmniLight3D], "
"[SpotLight3D], and [DirectionalLight3D] respectively."
msgstr ""
"O tipo da luz. Os valores aceitos pelo Godot são \"point\", \"spot\" e "
"\"directional\", que correspondem a [OmniLight3D], [SpotLight3D] e "
"[DirectionalLight3D] do Godot, respectivamente."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFLight.xml
msgid ""
"The outer angle of the cone in a spotlight. Must be greater than or equal to "
"the inner angle.\n"
"At this angle, the light drops off to zero brightness. Between the inner and "
"outer cone angles, there is a transition from full brightness to zero "
"brightness. If this angle is a half turn, then the spotlight emits in all "
"directions. When creating a Godot [SpotLight3D], the outer cone angle is "
"used as the angle of the spotlight."
msgstr ""

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFLight.xml
msgid ""
"The range of the light, beyond which the light has no effect. glTF lights "
"with no range defined behave like physical lights (which have infinite "
"range). When creating a Godot light, the range is clamped to [code]4096.0[/"
"code]."
msgstr ""
"O alcance da luz, além do qual a luz não tem efeito. Luzes glTF sem alcance "
"definido se comportam como luzes físicas (que têm alcance infinito). Ao "
"criar uma luz do Godot, o alcance é limitado a [code]4096.0[/code]."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFMesh.xml
msgid "GLTFMesh represents a glTF mesh."
msgstr "GLTFMesh representa uma malha glTF."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFMesh.xml
msgid ""
"GLTFMesh handles 3D mesh data imported from glTF files. It includes "
"properties for blend channels, blend weights, instance materials, and the "
"mesh itself."
msgstr ""
"O GLTFMesh lida com dados de malha 3D importados de arquivos glTF. Ele "
"inclui propriedades para canais de mistura, pesos de mistura, materiais de "
"instância e a própria malha."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFMesh.xml
msgid ""
"Gets additional arbitrary data in this [GLTFMesh] instance. This can be used "
"to keep per-node state data in [GLTFDocumentExtension] classes, which is "
"important because they are stateless.\n"
"The argument should be the [GLTFDocumentExtension] name (does not have to "
"match the extension name in the glTF file), and the return value can be "
"anything you set. If nothing was set, the return value is [code]null[/code]."
msgstr ""

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFMesh.xml
msgid ""
"Sets additional arbitrary data in this [GLTFMesh] instance. This can be used "
"to keep per-node state data in [GLTFDocumentExtension] classes, which is "
"important because they are stateless.\n"
"The first argument should be the [GLTFDocumentExtension] name (does not have "
"to match the extension name in the glTF file), and the second argument can "
"be anything you want."
msgstr ""

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFMesh.xml
msgid "An array of floats representing the blend weights of the mesh."
msgstr "Uma matriz de floats representando os pesos de mesclagem da malha."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFMesh.xml
msgid ""
"An array of Material objects representing the materials used in the mesh."
msgstr ""
"Um array de objetos Material representando os materiais usados na malha."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFMesh.xml
msgid "The [ImporterMesh] object representing the mesh itself."
msgstr "O objeto [ImporterMesh] representando a própria malha."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFMesh.xml
msgid "The original name of the mesh."
msgstr "O nome original da malha."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFNode.xml
msgid "glTF node class."
msgstr "Classe de nó glTF."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFNode.xml
msgid ""
"Represents a glTF node. glTF nodes may have names, transforms, children "
"(other glTF nodes), and more specialized properties (represented by their "
"own classes).\n"
"glTF nodes generally exist inside of [GLTFState] which represents all data "
"of a glTF file. Most of GLTFNode's properties are indices of other data in "
"the glTF file. You can extend a glTF node with additional properties by "
"using [method get_additional_data] and [method set_additional_data]."
msgstr ""

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFNode.xml
msgid "glTF scene and node spec"
msgstr "Especificação de cena e nó glTF"

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFNode.xml
msgid "Appends the given child node index to the [member children] array."
msgstr "Anexa o índice do nó filho fornecido ao array [member children]."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFNode.xml
msgid ""
"Gets additional arbitrary data in this [GLTFNode] instance. This can be used "
"to keep per-node state data in [GLTFDocumentExtension] classes, which is "
"important because they are stateless.\n"
"The argument should be the [GLTFDocumentExtension] name (does not have to "
"match the extension name in the glTF file), and the return value can be "
"anything you set. If nothing was set, the return value is [code]null[/code]."
msgstr ""

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFNode.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the [NodePath] that this GLTF node will have in the Godot scene tree "
"after being imported. This is useful when importing glTF object model "
"pointers with [GLTFObjectModelProperty], for handling extensions such as "
"[code]KHR_animation_pointer[/code] or [code]KHR_interactivity[/code].\n"
"If [param handle_skeletons] is [code]true[/code], paths to skeleton bone "
"glTF nodes will be resolved properly. For example, a path that would be "
"[code]^\"A/B/C/Bone1/Bone2/Bone3\"[/code] if [code]false[/code] will become "
"[code]^\"A/B/C/Skeleton3D:Bone3\"[/code]."
msgstr ""

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFNode.xml
msgid ""
"Sets additional arbitrary data in this [GLTFNode] instance. This can be used "
"to keep per-node state data in [GLTFDocumentExtension] classes, which is "
"important because they are stateless.\n"
"The first argument should be the [GLTFDocumentExtension] name (does not have "
"to match the extension name in the glTF file), and the second argument can "
"be anything you want."
msgstr ""

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFNode.xml
msgid ""
"If this glTF node is a camera, the index of the [GLTFCamera] in the "
"[GLTFState] that describes the camera's properties. If [code]-1[/code], this "
"node is not a camera."
msgstr ""
"Se este nó glTF for uma câmera, o índice do [GLTFCamera] no [GLTFState] que "
"descreve as propriedades da câmera. Se [code]-1[/code], este nó não é uma "
"câmera."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFNode.xml
msgid ""
"The indices of the child nodes in the [GLTFState]. If this glTF node has no "
"children, this will be an empty array."
msgstr ""
"Os índices dos nós filhos no [GLTFState]. Se este nó glTF não tiver filhos, "
"este será um array vazio."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFNode.xml
msgid ""
"How deep into the node hierarchy this node is. A root node will have a "
"height of 0, its children will have a height of 1, and so on. If -1, the "
"height has not been calculated."
msgstr ""
"A profundidade em que este nó está na hierarquia de nós. Um nó raiz terá "
"altura 0, seus filhos terão altura 1 e assim por diante. Se -1, a altura não "
"foi calculada."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFNode.xml
msgid ""
"If this glTF node is a light, the index of the [GLTFLight] in the "
"[GLTFState] that describes the light's properties. If -1, this node is not a "
"light."
msgstr ""
"Se este nó glTF for uma luz, o índice do [GLTFLight] no [GLTFState] que "
"descreve as propriedades da luz. Se for -1, este nó não é uma luz."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFNode.xml
msgid ""
"If this glTF node is a mesh, the index of the [GLTFMesh] in the [GLTFState] "
"that describes the mesh's properties. If -1, this node is not a mesh."
msgstr ""
"Se este nó glTF for uma malha, o índice do [GLTFMesh] no [GLTFState] que "
"descreve as propriedades da malha. Se for -1, este nó não é uma malha."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFNode.xml
msgid "The original name of the node."
msgstr "O nome original do nó."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFNode.xml
msgid ""
"The index of the parent node in the [GLTFState]. If -1, this node is a root "
"node."
msgstr "O índice do nó pai no [GLTFState]. Se -1, este nó é um nó raiz."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFNode.xml
msgid "The position of the glTF node relative to its parent."
msgstr "A posição do nó glTF em relação ao seu pai."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFNode.xml
msgid "The rotation of the glTF node relative to its parent."
msgstr "A rotação do nó glTF em relação ao seu pai."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFNode.xml
msgid "The scale of the glTF node relative to its parent."
msgstr "A escala do nó glTF em relação ao seu pai."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFNode.xml
msgid ""
"If this glTF node has a skeleton, the index of the [GLTFSkeleton] in the "
"[GLTFState] that describes the skeleton's properties. If -1, this node does "
"not have a skeleton."
msgstr ""
"Se este nó glTF tiver um esqueleto, o índice do [GLTFSkeleton] no "
"[GLTFState] que descreve as propriedades do esqueleto. Se -1, este nó não "
"tem esqueleto."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFNode.xml
msgid ""
"If this glTF node has a skin, the index of the [GLTFSkin] in the [GLTFState] "
"that describes the skin's properties. If -1, this node does not have a skin."
msgstr ""
"Se este nó glTF tiver uma skin, o índice do [GLTFSkin] no [GLTFState] que "
"descreve as propriedades da skin. Se for -1, este nó não tem skin."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFNode.xml
msgid ""
"If [code]true[/code], the GLTF node is visible. If [code]false[/code], the "
"GLTF node is not visible. This is converted to the [member Node3D.visible] "
"property in the Godot scene, and is exported to [code]KHR_node_visibility[/"
"code] when [code]false[/code]."
msgstr ""
"Se [code]true[/code], o nó GLTF fica visível. Se [code]false[/code], o nó "
"GLTF não fica visível. Isso é convertido para a propriedade [member "
"Node3D.visible] na cena do Godot e é exportado para "
"[code]KHR_node_visibility[/code] quando [code]false[/code]."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFNode.xml
msgid ""
"The transform of the glTF node relative to its parent. This property is "
"usually unused since the position, rotation, and scale properties are "
"preferred."
msgstr ""
"A transformação do nó glTF em relação ao seu pai. Esta propriedade "
"geralmente não é usada, pois as propriedades de posição, rotação e escala "
"são preferidas."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFObjectModelProperty.xml
msgid "Describes how to access a property as defined in the glTF object model."
msgstr ""
"Descreve como acessar uma propriedade conforme definido no modelo de objeto "
"glTF."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFObjectModelProperty.xml
msgid ""
"GLTFObjectModelProperty defines a mapping between a property in the glTF "
"object model and a NodePath in the Godot scene tree. This can be used to "
"animate properties in a glTF file using the [code]KHR_animation_pointer[/"
"code] extension, or to access them through an engine-agnostic script such as "
"a behavior graph as defined by the [code]KHR_interactivity[/code] "
"extension.\n"
"The glTF property is identified by JSON pointer(s) stored in [member "
"json_pointers], while the Godot property it maps to is defined by [member "
"node_paths]. In most cases [member json_pointers] and [member node_paths] "
"will each only have one item, but in some cases a single glTF JSON pointer "
"will map to multiple Godot properties, or a single Godot property will be "
"mapped to multiple glTF JSON pointers, or it might be a many-to-many "
"relationship.\n"
"[Expression] objects can be used to define conversions between the data, "
"such as when glTF defines an angle in radians and Godot uses degrees. The "
"[member object_model_type] property defines the type of data stored in the "
"glTF file as defined by the object model, see [enum GLTFObjectModelType] for "
"possible values."
msgstr ""

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFObjectModelProperty.xml
msgid "GLTF Object Model"
msgstr "Modelo de Objeto GLTF"

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFObjectModelProperty.xml
msgid "KHR_animation_pointer GLTF extension"
msgstr "Extensão GLTF KHR_animation_pointer"

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFObjectModelProperty.xml
msgid ""
"Appends a [NodePath] to [member node_paths]. This can be used by "
"[GLTFDocumentExtension] classes to define how a glTF object model property "
"maps to a Godot property, or multiple Godot properties. Prefer using [method "
"append_path_to_property] for simple cases. Be sure to also call [method "
"set_types] once (the order does not matter)."
msgstr ""
"Adiciona um [NodePath] a [member node_paths]. Isso pode ser usado por "
"classes [GLTFDocumentExtension] para definir como uma propriedade do modelo "
"de objeto glTF mapeia para uma propriedade do Godot, ou múltiplas "
"propriedades do Godot. Prefira usar [method append_path_to_property] para "
"casos simples. Certifique-se de também chamar [method set_types] uma vez (a "
"ordem não importa)."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFObjectModelProperty.xml
msgid ""
"High-level wrapper over [method append_node_path] that handles the most "
"common cases. It constructs a new [NodePath] using [param node_path] as a "
"base and appends [param prop_name] to the subpath. Be sure to also call "
"[method set_types] once (the order does not matter)."
msgstr ""
"Wrapper de alto nível sobre [method append_node_path] que lida com os casos "
"mais comuns. Ele constrói um novo [NodePath] usando [param node_path] como "
"base e anexa [param prop_name] ao subcaminho. Certifique-se de também chamar "
"[method set_types] uma vez (a ordem não importa)."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFObjectModelProperty.xml
msgid ""
"The GLTF accessor type associated with this property's [member "
"object_model_type]. See [member GLTFAccessor.accessor_type] for possible "
"values, and see [enum GLTFObjectModelType] for how the object model type "
"maps to accessor types."
msgstr ""
"O tipo de acessório GLTF associado a este [member object_model_type] da "
"propriedade. Veja [member GLTFAccessor.accessor_type] para valores possíveis "
"e veja [enum GLTFObjectModelType] para saber como o tipo de modelo de objeto "
"é mapeado para tipos de acessório."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFObjectModelProperty.xml
msgid ""
"Returns [code]true[/code] if [member json_pointers] is not empty. This is "
"used during export to determine if a [GLTFObjectModelProperty] can handle "
"converting a Godot property to a glTF object model property."
msgstr ""
"Retorna [code]true[/code] se [member json_pointers] não estiver vazio. Isso "
"é usado durante a exportação para determinar se um [GLTFObjectModelProperty] "
"pode lidar com a conversão de uma propriedade do Godot em uma propriedade de "
"modelo de objeto glTF."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFObjectModelProperty.xml
msgid ""
"Returns [code]true[/code] if [member node_paths] is not empty. This is used "
"during import to determine if a [GLTFObjectModelProperty] can handle "
"converting a glTF object model property to a Godot property."
msgstr ""
"Retorna [code]true[/code] se [member node_paths] não estiver vazio. Isso é "
"usado durante a importação para determinar se um [GLTFObjectModelProperty] "
"pode lidar com a conversão de uma propriedade de modelo de objeto glTF em "
"uma propriedade do Godot."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFObjectModelProperty.xml
msgid ""
"Sets the [member variant_type] and [member object_model_type] properties. "
"This is a convenience method to set both properties at once, since they are "
"almost always known at the same time. This method should be called once. "
"Calling it again with the same values will have no effect."
msgstr ""
"Define as propriedades [member variant_type] e [member object_model_type]. "
"Este é um método de conveniência para definir ambas as propriedades de uma "
"só vez, já que elas são quase sempre conhecidas ao mesmo tempo. Este método "
"deve ser chamado uma vez. Chamá-lo novamente com os mesmos valores não terá "
"efeito."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFObjectModelProperty.xml
msgid ""
"If set, this [Expression] will be used to convert the property value from "
"the glTF object model to the value expected by the Godot property. This is "
"useful when the glTF object model uses a different unit system, or when the "
"data needs to be transformed in some way. If [code]null[/code], the value "
"will be copied as-is."
msgstr ""
"Se definido, esta [Expression] será usada para converter o valor da "
"propriedade do modelo de objeto glTF para o valor esperado pela propriedade "
"do Godot. Isso é útil quando o modelo de objeto glTF usa um sistema de "
"unidades diferente ou quando os dados precisam ser transformados de alguma "
"forma. Se [code]null[/code], o valor será copiado como está."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFObjectModelProperty.xml
msgid ""
"If set, this [Expression] will be used to convert the property value from "
"the Godot property to the value expected by the glTF object model. This is "
"useful when the glTF object model uses a different unit system, or when the "
"data needs to be transformed in some way. If [code]null[/code], the value "
"will be copied as-is."
msgstr ""
"Se definido, esta [Expression] será usada para converter o valor da "
"propriedade do Godot para o valor esperado pelo modelo de objeto glTF. Isso "
"é útil quando o modelo de objeto glTF usa um sistema de unidades diferente "
"ou quando os dados precisam ser transformados de alguma forma. Se "
"[code]null[/code], o valor será copiado como está."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFObjectModelProperty.xml
msgid ""
"The glTF object model JSON pointers used to identify the property in the "
"glTF object model. In most cases, there will be only one item in this array, "
"but specific cases may require multiple pointers. The items are themselves "
"arrays which represent the JSON pointer split into its components."
msgstr ""
"Os ponteiros JSON do modelo de objeto glTF usados para identificar a "
"propriedade no modelo de objeto glTF. Na maioria dos casos, haverá apenas um "
"item neste array, mas casos específicos podem exigir múltiplos ponteiros. Os "
"itens são em si arrays que representam o ponteiro JSON dividido em seus "
"componentes."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFObjectModelProperty.xml
msgid ""
"An array of [NodePath]s that point to a property, or multiple properties, in "
"the Godot scene tree. On import, this will either be set by [GLTFDocument], "
"or by a [GLTFDocumentExtension] class. For simple cases, use [method "
"append_path_to_property] to add properties to this array.\n"
"In most cases [member node_paths] will only have one item, but in some cases "
"a single glTF JSON pointer will map to multiple Godot properties. For "
"example, a [GLTFCamera] or [GLTFLight] used on multiple glTF nodes will be "
"represented by multiple Godot nodes."
msgstr ""

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFObjectModelProperty.xml
msgid ""
"The type of data stored in the glTF file as defined by the object model. "
"This is a superset of the available accessor types, and determines the "
"accessor type."
msgstr ""
"O tipo de dados armazenados no arquivo glTF conforme definido pelo modelo de "
"objeto. Este é um superconjunto dos tipos de acessor disponíveis e determina "
"o tipo de acessor."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFObjectModelProperty.xml
msgid ""
"The type of data stored in the Godot property. This is the type of the "
"property that the [member node_paths] point to."
msgstr ""
"O tipo de dado armazenado na propriedade do Godot. Este é o tipo da "
"propriedade para a qual os [member node_paths] apontam."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFObjectModelProperty.xml
msgid ""
"Unknown or not set object model type. If the object model type is set to "
"this value, the real type still needs to be determined."
msgstr ""
"Tipo de modelo de objeto desconhecido ou não definido. Se o tipo de modelo "
"de objeto for definido como este valor, o tipo real ainda precisa ser "
"determinado."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFObjectModelProperty.xml
msgid ""
"Object model type \"bool\". Represented in the glTF JSON as a boolean, and "
"encoded in a [GLTFAccessor] as \"SCALAR\". When encoded in an accessor, a "
"value of [code]0[/code] is [code]false[/code], and any other value is "
"[code]true[/code]."
msgstr ""
"Tipo de modelo de objeto \"bool\". Representado no JSON do glTF como um "
"booleano e codificado em um [GLTFAccessor] como \"SCALAR\". Quando "
"codificado em um acessador, um valor de [code]0[/code] é [code]false[/code], "
"e qualquer outro valor é [code]true[/code]."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFObjectModelProperty.xml
msgid ""
"Object model type \"float\". Represented in the glTF JSON as a number, and "
"encoded in a [GLTFAccessor] as \"SCALAR\"."
msgstr ""
"Tipo de modelo de objeto \"float\". Representado no JSON do glTF como um "
"número e codificado em um [GLTFAccessor] como \"SCALAR\"."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFObjectModelProperty.xml
msgid ""
"Object model type \"float[lb][rb]\". Represented in the glTF JSON as an "
"array of numbers, and encoded in a [GLTFAccessor] as \"SCALAR\"."
msgstr ""
"Tipo de modelo de objeto \"float[lb][rb]\". Representado no JSON glTF como "
"uma matriz de números e codificado em um [GLTFAccessor] como \"SCALAR\"."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFObjectModelProperty.xml
msgid ""
"Object model type \"float2\". Represented in the glTF JSON as an array of "
"two numbers, and encoded in a [GLTFAccessor] as \"VEC2\"."
msgstr ""
"Tipo de modelo de objeto \"float2\". Representado no JSON glTF como uma "
"matriz de dois números e codificado em um [GLTFAccessor] como \"VEC2\"."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFObjectModelProperty.xml
msgid ""
"Object model type \"float3\". Represented in the glTF JSON as an array of "
"three numbers, and encoded in a [GLTFAccessor] as \"VEC3\"."
msgstr ""
"Tipo de modelo de objeto \"float3\". Representado no JSON glTF como uma "
"matriz de três números e codificado em um [GLTFAccessor] como \"VEC3\"."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFObjectModelProperty.xml
msgid ""
"Object model type \"float4\". Represented in the glTF JSON as an array of "
"four numbers, and encoded in a [GLTFAccessor] as \"VEC4\"."
msgstr ""
"Tipo de modelo de objeto \"float4\". Representado no JSON glTF como uma "
"matriz de quatro números e codificado em um [GLTFAccessor] como \"VEC4\"."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFObjectModelProperty.xml
msgid ""
"Object model type \"float2x2\". Represented in the glTF JSON as an array of "
"four numbers, and encoded in a [GLTFAccessor] as \"MAT2\"."
msgstr ""
"Tipo de modelo de objeto \"float2x2\". Representado no JSON glTF como uma "
"matriz de quatro números e codificado em um [GLTFAccessor] como \"MAT2\"."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFObjectModelProperty.xml
msgid ""
"Object model type \"float3x3\". Represented in the glTF JSON as an array of "
"nine numbers, and encoded in a [GLTFAccessor] as \"MAT3\"."
msgstr ""
"Tipo de modelo de objeto \"float3x3\". Representado no JSON glTF como uma "
"matriz de nove números e codificado em um [GLTFAccessor] como \"MAT3\"."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFObjectModelProperty.xml
msgid ""
"Object model type \"float4x4\". Represented in the glTF JSON as an array of "
"sixteen numbers, and encoded in a [GLTFAccessor] as \"MAT4\"."
msgstr ""
"Tipo de modelo de objeto \"float4x4\". Representado no JSON glTF como uma "
"matriz de dezesseis números e codificado em um [GLTFAccessor] como \"MAT4\"."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFObjectModelProperty.xml
msgid ""
"Object model type \"int\". Represented in the glTF JSON as a number, and "
"encoded in a [GLTFAccessor] as \"SCALAR\". The range of values is limited to "
"signed integers. For [code]KHR_interactivity[/code], only 32-bit integers "
"are supported."
msgstr ""
"Tipo de modelo de objeto \"int\". Representado no JSON do glTF como um "
"número e codificado em um [GLTFAccessor] como \"SCALAR\". O intervalo de "
"valores é limitado a inteiros com sinal. Para [code]KHR_interactivity[/"
"code], apenas inteiros de 32 bits são suportados."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFPhysicsBody.xml
msgid "Represents a glTF physics body."
msgstr "Representa um corpo de física glTF."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFPhysicsBody.xml
msgid ""
"Represents a physics body as an intermediary between the "
"[code]OMI_physics_body[/code] glTF data and Godot's nodes, and it's "
"abstracted in a way that allows adding support for different glTF physics "
"extensions in the future."
msgstr ""
"Representa um corpo físico como um intermediário entre os dados de glTF do "
"[code]OMI_physics_body[/code] e os nós do Godot, sendo abstraído de forma a "
"permitir adicionar suporte a diferentes extensões de física glTF no futuro."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFPhysicsBody.xml
msgid "OMI_physics_body glTF extension"
msgstr "Extensão glTF OMI_physics_body"

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFPhysicsBody.xml
msgid ""
"Creates a new GLTFPhysicsBody instance by parsing the given [Dictionary] in "
"the [code]OMI_physics_body[/code] glTF extension format."
msgstr ""
"Cria uma nova instância GLTFPhysicsBody analisando o [Dictionary] fornecido "
"no formato de extensão glTF [code]OMI_physics_body[/code]."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFPhysicsBody.xml
msgid ""
"Creates a new GLTFPhysicsBody instance from the given Godot "
"[CollisionObject3D] node."
msgstr ""
"Cria uma nova instância GLTFPhysicsBody a partir do nó [CollisionObject3D] "
"do Godot fornecido."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFPhysicsBody.xml
msgid ""
"Serializes this GLTFPhysicsBody instance into a [Dictionary]. It will be in "
"the format expected by the [code]OMI_physics_body[/code] glTF extension."
msgstr ""
"Serializa esta instância GLTFPhysicsBody em um [Dictionary]. Estará no "
"formato esperado pela extensão glTF [code]OMI_physics_body[/code]."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFPhysicsBody.xml
msgid ""
"Converts this GLTFPhysicsBody instance into a Godot [CollisionObject3D] node."
msgstr ""
"Converte esta instância de GLTFPhysicsBody em um nó [CollisionObject3D] do "
"Godot."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFPhysicsBody.xml
msgid ""
"The angular velocity of the physics body, in radians per second. This is "
"only used when the body type is \"rigid\" or \"vehicle\"."
msgstr ""
"A velocidade angular do corpo físico, em radianos por segundo. Isto é usado "
"apenas quando o tipo de corpo é \"rigid\" ou \"vehicle\"."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFPhysicsBody.xml
msgid ""
"The type of the body.\n"
"When importing, this controls what type of [CollisionObject3D] node Godot "
"should generate. Valid values are [code]\"static\"[/code], [code]"
"\"animatable\"[/code], [code]\"character\"[/code], [code]\"rigid\"[/code], "
"[code]\"vehicle\"[/code], and [code]\"trigger\"[/code].\n"
"When exporting, this will be squashed down to one of [code]\"static\"[/"
"code], [code]\"kinematic\"[/code], or [code]\"dynamic\"[/code] motion types, "
"or the [code]\"trigger\"[/code] property."
msgstr ""

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFPhysicsBody.xml
msgid ""
"The center of mass of the body, in meters. This is in local space relative "
"to the body. By default, the center of the mass is the body's origin."
msgstr ""
"O centro de massa do corpo, em metros. Isso está no espaço local em relação "
"ao corpo. Por padrão, o centro de massa é a origem do corpo."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFPhysicsBody.xml
msgid ""
"The inertia strength of the physics body, in kilogram meter squared (kg⋅m²). "
"This represents the inertia around the principle axes, the diagonal of the "
"inertia tensor matrix. This is only used when the body type is \"rigid\" or "
"\"vehicle\".\n"
"When converted to a Godot [RigidBody3D] node, if this value is zero, then "
"the inertia will be calculated automatically."
msgstr ""

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFPhysicsBody.xml
msgid ""
"The inertia orientation of the physics body. This defines the rotation of "
"the inertia's principle axes relative to the object's local axes. This is "
"only used when the body type is \"rigid\" or \"vehicle\" and [member "
"inertia_diagonal] is set to a non-zero value."
msgstr ""
"A orientação de inércia do corpo físico. Isso define a rotação dos eixos "
"principais da inércia em relação aos eixos locais do objeto. Isso só é usado "
"quando o tipo de corpo é \"rigid\" ou \"vehicle\" e [member "
"inertia_diagonal] é definido como um valor diferente de zero."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFPhysicsBody.xml
msgid ""
"The inertia tensor of the physics body, in kilogram meter squared (kg⋅m²). "
"This is only used when the body type is \"rigid\" or \"vehicle\".\n"
"When converted to a Godot [RigidBody3D] node, if this value is zero, then "
"the inertia will be calculated automatically."
msgstr ""

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFPhysicsBody.xml
msgid ""
"The linear velocity of the physics body, in meters per second. This is only "
"used when the body type is \"rigid\" or \"vehicle\"."
msgstr ""
"A velocidade linear do corpo físico, em metros por segundo. Isto é usado "
"apenas quando o tipo de corpo é \"rigid\" ou \"vehicle\"."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFPhysicsBody.xml
msgid ""
"The mass of the physics body, in kilograms. This is only used when the body "
"type is \"rigid\" or \"vehicle\"."
msgstr ""
"A massa do corpo físico, em quilogramas. Isso só é usado quando o tipo de "
"corpo é \"rigid\" ou \"vehicle\"."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFPhysicsShape.xml
msgid "Represents a glTF physics shape."
msgstr "Representa uma forma de física glTF."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFPhysicsShape.xml
msgid ""
"Represents a physics shape as defined by the [code]OMI_physics_shape[/code] "
"or [code]OMI_collider[/code] glTF extensions. This class is an intermediary "
"between the glTF data and Godot's nodes, and it's abstracted in a way that "
"allows adding support for different glTF physics extensions in the future."
msgstr ""
"Representa uma forma de física conforme definida pelas extensões glTF "
"[code]OMI_physics_shape[/code] ou [code]OMI_collider[/code]. Esta classe é "
"uma intermediária entre os dados glTF e os nós do Godot, e é abstraída de "
"forma a permitir a adição de suporte para diferentes extensões de física "
"glTF no futuro."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFPhysicsShape.xml
msgid "OMI_physics_shape glTF extension"
msgstr "Extensão glTF OMI_physics_shape"

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFPhysicsShape.xml
msgid "OMI_collider glTF extension"
msgstr "Extensão glTF OMI_collider"

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFPhysicsShape.xml
msgid ""
"Creates a new GLTFPhysicsShape instance by parsing the given [Dictionary]."
msgstr ""
"Cria uma nova instância de GLTFPhysicsShape analisando o [Dictionary] "
"fornecido."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFPhysicsShape.xml
msgid ""
"Creates a new GLTFPhysicsShape instance from the given Godot "
"[CollisionShape3D] node."
msgstr ""
"Cria uma nova instância GLTFPhysicsShape a partir do nó [CollisionShape3D] "
"do Godot fornecido."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFPhysicsShape.xml
msgid ""
"Creates a new GLTFPhysicsShape instance from the given Godot [Shape3D] "
"resource."
msgstr ""
"Cria uma nova instância de GLTFPhysicsShape a partir do recurso [Shape3D] "
"fornecido do Godot."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFPhysicsShape.xml
msgid ""
"Serializes this GLTFPhysicsShape instance into a [Dictionary] in the format "
"defined by [code]OMI_physics_shape[/code]."
msgstr ""
"Serializa esta instância GLTFPhysicsShape em um [Dictionary] no formato "
"definido por [code]OMI_physics_shape[/code]."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFPhysicsShape.xml
msgid ""
"Converts this GLTFPhysicsShape instance into a Godot [CollisionShape3D] node."
msgstr ""
"Converte esta instância de GLTFPhysicsShape em um nó [CollisionShape3D] do "
"Godot."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFPhysicsShape.xml
msgid ""
"Converts this GLTFPhysicsShape instance into a Godot [Shape3D] resource."
msgstr ""
"Converte esta instância de GLTFPhysicsShape em um recurso [Shape3D] do Godot."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFPhysicsShape.xml
msgid ""
"The height of the shape, in meters. This is only used when the shape type is "
"[code]\"capsule\"[/code] or [code]\"cylinder\"[/code]. This value should not "
"be negative, and for [code]\"capsule\"[/code] it should be at least twice "
"the radius."
msgstr ""
"A altura da forma, em metros. Isso só é usado quando o tipo de forma é [code]"
"\"capsule\"[/code] ou [code]\"cylinder\"[/code]. Este valor não deve ser "
"negativo e, para [code]\"capsule\"[/code], deve ser pelo menos o dobro do "
"raio."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFPhysicsShape.xml
msgid ""
"The [ImporterMesh] resource of the shape. This is only used when the shape "
"type is [code]\"hull\"[/code] (convex hull) or [code]\"trimesh\"[/code] "
"(concave trimesh)."
msgstr ""
"O recurso [ImporterMesh] da forma. Isso só é usado quando o tipo de forma é "
"[code]\"hull\"[/code] (casco convexo) ou [code]\"trimesh\"[/code] (trimesh "
"côncavo)."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFPhysicsShape.xml
msgid ""
"If [code]true[/code], indicates that this shape is a trigger. For Godot, "
"this means that the shape should be a child of an [Area3D] node.\n"
"This is the only variable not used in the [method to_node] method, it's "
"intended to be used alongside when deciding where to add the generated node "
"as a child."
msgstr ""

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFPhysicsShape.xml
msgid ""
"The index of the shape's mesh in the glTF file. This is only used when the "
"shape type is [code]\"hull\"[/code] (convex hull) or [code]\"trimesh\"[/"
"code] (concave trimesh)."
msgstr ""
"O índice da malha da forma no arquivo glTF. Isso só é usado quando o tipo de "
"forma é [code]\"hull\"[/code] (casco convexo) ou [code]\"trimesh\"[/code] "
"(trimesh côncavo)."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFPhysicsShape.xml
msgid ""
"The radius of the shape, in meters. This is only used when the shape type is "
"[code]\"capsule\"[/code], [code]\"cylinder\"[/code], or [code]\"sphere\"[/"
"code]. This value should not be negative."
msgstr ""
"O raio da forma, em metros. Isso é usado apenas quando o tipo de forma é "
"[code]\"capsule\"[/code], [code]\"cylinder\"[/code] ou [code]\"sphere\"[/"
"code]. Este valor não deve ser negativo."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFPhysicsShape.xml
msgid ""
"The type of shape this shape represents. Valid values are [code]\"box\"[/"
"code], [code]\"capsule\"[/code], [code]\"cylinder\"[/code], [code]"
"\"sphere\"[/code], [code]\"hull\"[/code], and [code]\"trimesh\"[/code]."
msgstr ""
"O tipo de forma que esta forma representa. Os valores válidos são [code]"
"\"box\"[/code], [code]\"capsule\"[/code], [code]\"cylinder\"[/code], [code]"
"\"sphere\"[/code], [code]\"hull\"[/code] e [code]\"trimesh\"[/code]."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFPhysicsShape.xml
msgid ""
"The size of the shape, in meters. This is only used when the shape type is "
"[code]\"box\"[/code], and it represents the [code]\"diameter\"[/code] of the "
"box. This value should not be negative."
msgstr ""
"O tamanho da forma, em metros. Isso é usado apenas quando o tipo de forma é "
"[code]\"box\"[/code] e representa o [code]\"diameter\"[/code] da caixa. Este "
"valor não deve ser negativo."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFSkeleton.xml
msgid ""
"Returns a [Dictionary] that maps skeleton bone indices to the indices of "
"glTF nodes. This property is unused during import, and only set during "
"export. In a glTF file, a bone is a node, so Godot converts skeleton bones "
"to glTF nodes."
msgstr ""
"Retorna um [Dictionary] que mapeia índices de ossos de esqueleto para os "
"índices de nós glTF. Esta propriedade não é usada durante a importação e é "
"definida apenas durante a exportação. Em um arquivo glTF, um osso é um nó, "
"então o Godot converte ossos de esqueleto em nós glTF."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFSkeleton.xml
msgid ""
"Sets a [Dictionary] that maps skeleton bone indices to the indices of glTF "
"nodes. This property is unused during import, and only set during export. In "
"a glTF file, a bone is a node, so Godot converts skeleton bones to glTF "
"nodes."
msgstr ""
"Define um [Dictionary] que mapeia índices de ossos de esqueletos para os "
"índices de nós glTF. Esta propriedade não é usada durante a importação e é "
"definida apenas durante a exportação. Em um arquivo glTF, um osso é um nó, "
"então o Godot converte ossos de esqueleto em nós glTF."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFSpecGloss.xml
msgid "Archived glTF extension for specular/glossy materials."
msgstr "Extensão glTF arquivada para materiais especulares/brilhantes."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFSpecGloss.xml
msgid ""
"KHR_materials_pbrSpecularGlossiness is an archived glTF extension. This "
"means that it is deprecated and not recommended for new files. However, it "
"is still supported for loading old files."
msgstr ""
"KHR_materials_pbrSpecularGlossiness é uma extensão glTF arquivada. Isso "
"significa que ela está obsoleta e não é recomendada para novos arquivos. No "
"entanto, ela ainda é suportada para carregar arquivos antigos."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFSpecGloss.xml
msgid "KHR_materials_pbrSpecularGlossiness glTF extension spec"
msgstr "Especificação da extensão glTF KHR_materials_pbrSpecularGlossiness"

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFSpecGloss.xml
msgid "The reflected diffuse factor of the material."
msgstr "O fator difuso refletido do material."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFSpecGloss.xml
msgid "The diffuse texture."
msgstr "A textura difusa."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFSpecGloss.xml
msgid "The glossiness or smoothness of the material."
msgstr "O brilho ou suavidade do material."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFSpecGloss.xml
msgid "The specular-glossiness texture."
msgstr "A textura de brilho especular."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFSpecGloss.xml
msgid "The specular RGB color of the material. The alpha channel is unused."
msgstr "A cor RGB especular do material. O canal alfa não é usado."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFState.xml
msgid "Represents all data of a glTF file."
msgstr "Representa todos os dados de um arquivo glTF."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFState.xml
msgid ""
"Contains all nodes and resources of a glTF file. This is used by "
"[GLTFDocument] as data storage, which allows [GLTFDocument] and all "
"[GLTFDocumentExtension] classes to remain stateless.\n"
"GLTFState can be populated by [GLTFDocument] reading a file or by converting "
"a Godot scene. Then the data can either be used to create a Godot scene or "
"save to a glTF file. The code that converts to/from a Godot scene can be "
"intercepted at arbitrary points by [GLTFDocumentExtension] classes. This "
"allows for custom data to be stored in the glTF file or for custom data to "
"be converted to/from Godot nodes."
msgstr ""

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFState.xml
msgid "glTF asset header schema"
msgstr "Esquema de cabeçalho de ativo glTF"

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFState.xml
msgid ""
"Appends an extension to the list of extensions used by this glTF file during "
"serialization. If [param required] is [code]true[/code], the extension will "
"also be added to the list of required extensions. Do not run this in [method "
"GLTFDocumentExtension._export_post], as that stage is too late to add "
"extensions. The final list is sorted alphabetically."
msgstr ""
"Adiciona uma extensão à lista de extensões usadas por este arquivo glTF "
"durante a serialização. Se [param required] for [code]true[/code], a "
"extensão também será adicionada à lista de extensões obrigatórias. Não "
"execute isso em [method GLTFDocumentExtension._export_post], pois esse "
"estágio é tarde demais para adicionar extensões. A lista final é ordenada "
"alfabeticamente."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFState.xml
msgid ""
"Appends the given byte array [param data] to the buffers and creates a "
"[GLTFBufferView] for it. The index of the destination [GLTFBufferView] is "
"returned. If [param deduplication] is [code]true[/code], the buffers are "
"first searched for duplicate data, otherwise new bytes are always appended."
msgstr ""
"Anexa o array de bytes [param data] fornecido aos buffers e cria um "
"[GLTFBufferView] para ele. O índice do [GLTFBufferView] de destino é "
"retornado. Se [param deduplication] for [code]true[/code], os buffers são "
"pesquisados primeiro por dados duplicados, caso contrário, novos bytes são "
"sempre anexados."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFState.xml
msgid ""
"Appends the given [GLTFNode] to the state, and returns its new index. This "
"can be used to export one Godot node as multiple glTF nodes, or inject new "
"glTF nodes at import time. On import, this must be called before [method "
"GLTFDocumentExtension._generate_scene_node] finishes for the parent node. On "
"export, this must be called before [method "
"GLTFDocumentExtension._export_node] runs for the parent node.\n"
"The [param godot_scene_node] parameter is the Godot scene node that "
"corresponds to this glTF node. This is highly recommended to be set to a "
"valid node, but may be [code]null[/code] if there is no corresponding Godot "
"scene node. One Godot scene node may be used for multiple glTF nodes, so if "
"exporting multiple glTF nodes for one Godot scene node, use the same Godot "
"scene node for each.\n"
"The [param parent_node_index] parameter is the index of the parent "
"[GLTFNode] in the state. If [code]-1[/code], the node will be a root node, "
"otherwise the new node will be added to the parent's list of children. The "
"index will also be written to the [member GLTFNode.parent] property of the "
"new node."
msgstr ""

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFState.xml
msgid ""
"Gets additional arbitrary data in this [GLTFState] instance. This can be "
"used to keep per-file state data in [GLTFDocumentExtension] classes, which "
"is important because they are stateless.\n"
"The argument should be the [GLTFDocumentExtension] name (does not have to "
"match the extension name in the glTF file), and the return value can be "
"anything you set. If nothing was set, the return value is [code]null[/code]."
msgstr ""

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFState.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the [AnimationPlayer] node with the given index. These nodes are "
"only used during the export process when converting Godot [AnimationPlayer] "
"nodes to glTF animations."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o nó [AnimationPlayer] com o índice fornecido. Esses nós são usados "
"apenas durante o processo de exportação ao converter nós [AnimationPlayer] "
"do Godot em animações glTF."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFState.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the number of [AnimationPlayer] nodes in this [GLTFState]. These "
"nodes are only used during the export process when converting Godot "
"[AnimationPlayer] nodes to glTF animations."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o número de nós [AnimationPlayer] neste [GLTFState]. Esses nós são "
"usados apenas durante o processo de exportação ao converter nós "
"[AnimationPlayer] do Godot em animações glTF."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFState.xml
msgid ""
"Returns an array of all [GLTFAnimation]s in the glTF file. When importing, "
"these will be generated as animations in an [AnimationPlayer] node. When "
"exporting, these will be generated from Godot [AnimationPlayer] nodes."
msgstr ""
"Retorna um array de todos os [GLTFAnimation]s no arquivo glTF. Ao importar, "
"estes serão gerados como animações em um nó [AnimationPlayer]. Ao exportar, "
"estes serão gerados a partir de nós [AnimationPlayer] do Godot."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFState.xml
msgid ""
"Returns an array of all [GLTFCamera]s in the glTF file. These are the "
"cameras that the [member GLTFNode.camera] index refers to."
msgstr ""
"Retorna uma matriz de todos os [GLTFCamera]s no arquivo glTF. Estas são as "
"câmeras a que o índice [member GLTFNode.camera] se refere."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFState.xml
msgid "Use [member handle_binary_image_mode] instead."
msgstr "Use [member handle_binary_image_mode] em vez disso."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFState.xml
msgid ""
"Deprecated untyped alias for [member handle_binary_image_mode]. When "
"importing a glTF file with unimported raw binary images embedded inside of "
"binary blob buffers, in data URIs, or separate files not imported by Godot, "
"this controls how the images are handled."
msgstr ""
"Alias descontinuado e não tipado para [member handle_binary_image_mode]. Ao "
"importar um arquivo glTF com imagens binárias brutas não importadas "
"incorporadas dentro de buffers de blob binário, em URIs de dados ou arquivos "
"separados não importados pelo Godot, isso controla como as imagens são "
"tratadas."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFState.xml
msgid ""
"Gets the images of the glTF file as an array of [Texture2D]s. These are the "
"images that the [member GLTFTexture.src_image] index refers to."
msgstr ""
"Obtém as imagens do arquivo glTF como um array de [Texture2D]s. Estas são as "
"imagens a que o índice [member GLTFTexture.src_image] se refere."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFState.xml
msgid ""
"Returns an array of all [GLTFLight]s in the glTF file. These are the lights "
"that the [member GLTFNode.light] index refers to."
msgstr ""
"Retorna uma matriz de todas as [GLTFLight]s no arquivo glTF. Estas são as "
"luzes às quais o índice [member GLTFNode.light] se refere."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFState.xml
msgid ""
"Returns an array of all [GLTFMesh]es in the glTF file. These are the meshes "
"that the [member GLTFNode.mesh] index refers to."
msgstr ""
"Retorna uma matriz de todos os [GLTFMesh]es no glTF file. Estas são as "
"malhas às quais o índice [member GLTFNode.mesh] se refere."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFState.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the index of the [GLTFNode] corresponding to this Godot scene node. "
"This is the inverse of [method get_scene_node]. Useful during the export "
"process.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Not every Godot scene node will have a corresponding "
"[GLTFNode], and not every [GLTFNode] will have a scene node generated. If "
"there is no [GLTFNode] index for this scene node, [code]-1[/code] is "
"returned."
msgstr ""

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFState.xml
msgid ""
"Returns an array of all [GLTFNode]s in the glTF file. These are the nodes "
"that [member GLTFNode.children] and [member root_nodes] refer to. This "
"includes nodes that may not be generated in the Godot scene, or nodes that "
"may generate multiple Godot scene nodes."
msgstr ""
"Retorna uma matriz de todos os [GLTFNode]s no arquivo glTF. Estes são os nós "
"aos quais [member GLTFNode.children] e [member root_nodes] se referem. Isso "
"inclui nós que podem não ser gerados na cena do Godot ou nós que podem gerar "
"múltiplos nós de cena do Godot."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFState.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the Godot scene node that corresponds to the same index as the "
"[GLTFNode] it was generated from. This is the inverse of [method "
"get_node_index]. Useful during the import process.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Not every [GLTFNode] will have a scene node generated, and not "
"every generated scene node will have a corresponding [GLTFNode]. If there is "
"no scene node for this [GLTFNode] index, [code]null[/code] is returned."
msgstr ""

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFState.xml
msgid ""
"Returns an array of all [GLTFSkeleton]s in the glTF file. These are the "
"skeletons that the [member GLTFNode.skeleton] index refers to."
msgstr ""
"Retorna uma matriz de todos os [GLTFSkeletons] no arquivo glTF. Estes são os "
"esqueletos aos quais o índice [member GLTFNode.skeleton] se refere."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFState.xml
msgid ""
"Returns an array of all [GLTFSkin]s in the glTF file. These are the skins "
"that the [member GLTFNode.skin] index refers to."
msgstr ""
"Retorna uma matriz de todos os [GLTFSkin]s no arquivo glTF. Estas são as "
"skins às quais o índice [member GLTFNode.skin] se refere."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFState.xml
msgid ""
"Retrieves the array of texture samplers that are used by the textures "
"contained in the glTF."
msgstr ""
"Recupera a matriz de amostradores de textura que são usados pelas texturas "
"contidas no glTF."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFState.xml
msgid ""
"Returns an array of unique animation names. This is only used during the "
"import process."
msgstr ""
"Retorna um array de nomes de animação exclusivos. Isso é usado apenas "
"durante o processo de importação."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFState.xml
msgid ""
"Returns an array of unique node names. This is used in both the import "
"process and export process."
msgstr ""
"Retorna um matriz de nomes de nós exclusivos. Isso é usado tanto no processo "
"de importação quanto no processo de exportação."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFState.xml
msgid ""
"Sets additional arbitrary data in this [GLTFState] instance. This can be "
"used to keep per-file state data in [GLTFDocumentExtension] classes, which "
"is important because they are stateless.\n"
"The first argument should be the [GLTFDocumentExtension] name (does not have "
"to match the extension name in the glTF file), and the second argument can "
"be anything you want."
msgstr ""

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFState.xml
msgid ""
"Sets the [GLTFAnimation]s in the state. When importing, these will be "
"generated as animations in an [AnimationPlayer] node. When exporting, these "
"will be generated from Godot [AnimationPlayer] nodes."
msgstr ""
"Define as [GLTFAnimation]s no estado. Ao importar, elas serão geradas como "
"animações em um nó [AnimationPlayer]. Ao exportar, elas serão geradas a "
"partir de nós [AnimationPlayer] do Godot."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFState.xml
msgid ""
"Sets the [GLTFCamera]s in the state. These are the cameras that the [member "
"GLTFNode.camera] index refers to."
msgstr ""
"Define as [GLTFCamera]s no estado. Essas são as câmeras às quais o índice "
"[member GLTFNode.camera] se refere."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFState.xml
msgid ""
"Sets the images in the state stored as an array of [Texture2D]s. This can be "
"used during export. These are the images that the [member "
"GLTFTexture.src_image] index refers to."
msgstr ""
"Define as imagens no estado armazenado como um array de [Texture2D]s. Isso "
"pode ser usado durante a exportação. Estas são as imagens a que o índice "
"[member GLTFTexture.src_image] se refere."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFState.xml
msgid ""
"Sets the [GLTFLight]s in the state. These are the lights that the [member "
"GLTFNode.light] index refers to."
msgstr ""
"Define os [GLTFLight]s no estado. Estas são as luzes às quais o índice "
"[member GLTFNode.light] se refere."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFState.xml
msgid ""
"Sets the [GLTFMesh]es in the state. These are the meshes that the [member "
"GLTFNode.mesh] index refers to."
msgstr ""
"Define as [GLTFSkin]es no estado. Estas são as malhas às quais o índice "
"[member GLTFNode.mesh] se refere."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFState.xml
msgid ""
"Sets the [GLTFNode]s in the state. These are the nodes that [member "
"GLTFNode.children] and [member root_nodes] refer to. Some of the nodes set "
"here may not be generated in the Godot scene, or may generate multiple Godot "
"scene nodes."
msgstr ""
"Define os [GLTFNode]s no estado. Estes são os nós aos quais [member "
"GLTFNode.children] e [root_nodes] se referem. Alguns dos nós definidos aqui "
"podem não ser gerados na cena do Godot ou podem gerar vários nós de cena do "
"Godot."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFState.xml
msgid ""
"Sets the [GLTFSkeleton]s in the state. These are the skeletons that the "
"[member GLTFNode.skeleton] index refers to."
msgstr ""
"Define os [GLTFSkeleton]s no estado. Estes são os esqueletos aos quais o "
"índice [member GLTFNode.skeleton] se refere."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFState.xml
msgid ""
"Sets the [GLTFSkin]s in the state. These are the skins that the [member "
"GLTFNode.skin] index refers to."
msgstr ""
"Define os [GLTFSkin]s no estado. Estas são as skins às quais o índice "
"[member GLTFNode.skin] se refere."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFState.xml
msgid ""
"Sets the array of texture samplers that are used by the textures contained "
"in the glTF."
msgstr ""
"Define o array de amostradores de textura que são usados pelas texturas "
"contidas no glTF."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFState.xml
msgid ""
"Sets the unique animation names in the state. This is only used during the "
"import process."
msgstr ""
"Define os nomes de animação exclusivos no estado. Isso é usado apenas "
"durante o processo de importação."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFState.xml
msgid ""
"Sets the unique node names in the state. This is used in both the import "
"process and export process."
msgstr ""
"Define os nomes de nós exclusivos no estado. Isso é usado tanto no processo "
"de importação quanto no de exportação."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFState.xml
msgid "The baking fps of the animation for either import or export."
msgstr "Os fps de cozimento da animação para importação ou exportação."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFState.xml
msgid ""
"The folder path associated with this glTF data. This is used to find other "
"files the glTF file references, like images or binary buffers. This will be "
"set during import when appending from a file, and will be set during export "
"when writing to a file."
msgstr ""
"O caminho da pasta associado a estes dados glTF. Isso é usado para encontrar "
"outros arquivos referenciados pelo arquivo glTF, como imagens ou buffers "
"binários. Isso será definido durante a importação ao anexar de um arquivo e "
"será definido durante a exportação ao gravar em um arquivo."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFState.xml
msgid ""
"The copyright string in the asset header of the glTF file. This is set "
"during import if present and export if non-empty. See the glTF asset header "
"documentation for more information."
msgstr ""
"A string de direitos autorais no cabeçalho de ativos do arquivo glTF. Isso é "
"definido durante a importação, se presente, e a exportação, se não estiver "
"vazio. Consulte a documentação do cabeçalho de ativos glTF para obter mais "
"informações."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFState.xml
msgid ""
"The file name associated with this glTF data. If it ends with [code].gltf[/"
"code], this is text-based glTF, otherwise this is binary GLB. This will be "
"set during import when appending from a file, and will be set during export "
"when writing to a file. If writing to a buffer, this will be an empty string."
msgstr ""
"O nome de arquivo associado a estes dados glTF. Se terminar com [code].gltf[/"
"code], trata-se de glTF baseado em texto; caso contrário, é um GLB binário. "
"Isso será definido durante a importação ao anexar de um arquivo e será "
"definido durante a exportação ao gravar em um arquivo. Se for gravado em um "
"buffer, esta será uma string vazia."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFState.xml
msgid "The binary buffer attached to a .glb file."
msgstr "O buffer binário anexado a um arquivo .glb."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFState.xml
msgid ""
"When importing a glTF file with unimported raw binary images embedded inside "
"of binary blob buffers, in data URIs, or separate files not imported by "
"Godot, this controls how the images are handled. Images can be discarded, "
"saved as separate files, or embedded in the scene lossily or losslessly. See "
"[enum HandleBinaryImageMode] for options.\n"
"This property does nothing for image files in the [code]res://[/code] folder "
"imported by Godot, as those are handled by Godot's image importer directly, "
"and then the Godot scene generated from the glTF file will use the images as "
"Godot imported them."
msgstr ""

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFState.xml
msgid ""
"If [code]true[/code], forces all GLTFNodes in the document to be bones of a "
"single [Skeleton3D] Godot node."
msgstr ""
"Se [code]true[/code], força todos os GLTFNodes no documento a serem ossos de "
"um único nó [Skeleton3D] do Godot."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFState.xml
msgid "The original raw JSON document corresponding to this GLTFState."
msgstr "O documento JSON bruto original correspondente a este GLTFState."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFState.xml
msgid ""
"The root nodes of the glTF file. Typically, a glTF file will only have one "
"scene, and therefore one root node. However, a glTF file may have multiple "
"scenes and therefore multiple root nodes, which will be generated as "
"siblings of each other and as children of the root node of the generated "
"Godot scene."
msgstr ""
"Os nós raiz do arquivo glTF. Tipicamente, um arquivo glTF terá apenas uma "
"cena e, portanto, um único nó raiz. No entanto, um arquivo glTF pode ter "
"várias cenas e, portanto, vários nós raiz, que serão gerados como irmãos "
"entre si e como filhos do nó raiz da cena do Godot gerada."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFState.xml
msgid ""
"The name of the scene. When importing, if not specified, this will be the "
"file name. When exporting, if specified, the scene name will be saved to the "
"glTF file."
msgstr ""
"O nome da cena. Ao importar, se não especificado, este será o nome do "
"arquivo. Ao exportar, se especificado, o nome da cena será salvo no arquivo "
"glTF."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFState.xml
msgid ""
"When importing a glTF file with embedded binary images, discards all images "
"and uses untextured materials in their place. Images stored as separate "
"files in the [code]res://[/code] folder are not affected by this; those will "
"be used as Godot imported them."
msgstr ""
"Ao importar um arquivo glTF com imagens binárias embutidas, descarta todas "
"as imagens e usa materiais sem textura em seu lugar. Imagens armazenadas "
"como arquivos separados na pasta [code]res://[/code] não são afetadas por "
"isso; elas serão usadas da maneira como o Godot as importou."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFState.xml
msgid ""
"When importing a glTF file with embedded binary images, extracts them and "
"saves them to their own files. This allows the image to be imported by "
"Godot's image importer, which can then have their import options customized "
"by the user, including optionally compressing the image to VRAM texture "
"formats.\n"
"This will save the images's bytes exactly as-is, without recompression. For "
"image formats supplied by glTF extensions, the file will have a filename "
"ending with the file extension supplied by [method "
"GLTFDocumentExtension._get_image_file_extension] of the extension class.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] This option is editor-only. At runtime, this acts the same as "
"[constant HANDLE_BINARY_IMAGE_MODE_EMBED_AS_UNCOMPRESSED]."
msgstr ""

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFState.xml
msgid ""
"When importing a glTF file with embedded binary images, embeds textures VRAM "
"compressed with Basis Universal into the generated scene. Images stored as "
"separate files in the [code]res://[/code] folder are not affected by this; "
"those will be used as Godot imported them."
msgstr ""
"Ao importar um arquivo glTF com imagens binárias embutidas, incorpora "
"texturas compactadas em VRAM com Basis Universal na cena gerada. Imagens "
"armazenadas como arquivos separados na pasta [code]res://[/code] não são "
"afetadas por isso; elas serão usadas da maneira como o Godot as importou."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFState.xml
msgid ""
"When importing a glTF file with embedded binary images, embeds textures "
"compressed losslessly into the generated scene. Images stored as separate "
"files in the [code]res://[/code] folder are not affected by this; those will "
"be used as Godot imported them."
msgstr ""
"Ao importar um arquivo glTF com imagens binárias embutidas, embutir texturas "
"compactadas sem perdas na cena gerada. Imagens armazenadas como arquivos "
"separados na pasta [code]res://[/code] não são afetadas por isso; essas "
"serão usadas como o Godot as importou."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFState.xml
msgid "Use [constant HANDLE_BINARY_IMAGE_MODE_DISCARD_TEXTURES] instead."
msgstr ""
"Em vez disso, use [constant HANDLE_BINARY_IMAGE_MODE_DISCARD_TEXTURES]."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFState.xml
msgid "Discards all embedded textures and uses untextured materials."
msgstr "Descartar todas as texturas embutidas e usar materiais sem textura."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFState.xml
msgid "Use [constant HANDLE_BINARY_IMAGE_MODE_EXTRACT_TEXTURES] instead."
msgstr ""
"Em vez disso, use [constant HANDLE_BINARY_IMAGE_MODE_EXTRACT_TEXTURES]."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFState.xml
msgid ""
"Extracts embedded textures to be reimported and compressed. Editor only. "
"Acts as uncompressed at runtime."
msgstr ""
"Extrai texturas embutidas para serem reimportadas e compactadas. Apenas para "
"o editor. Atua como descompactado em tempo de execução."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFState.xml
msgid "Use [constant HANDLE_BINARY_IMAGE_MODE_EMBED_AS_BASISU] instead."
msgstr "Em vez disso, use [constant HANDLE_BINARY_IMAGE_MODE_EMBED_AS_BASISU]."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFState.xml
msgid ""
"Embeds textures VRAM compressed with Basis Universal into the generated "
"scene."
msgstr "Embarca texturas VRAM compactadas com Basis Universal na cena gerada."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFState.xml
msgid "Use [constant HANDLE_BINARY_IMAGE_MODE_EMBED_AS_UNCOMPRESSED] instead."
msgstr ""
"Use [constant HANDLE_BINARY_IMAGE_MODE_EMBED_AS_UNCOMPRESSED] em vez disso."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFState.xml
msgid ""
"Embeds textures compressed losslessly into the generated scene, matching old "
"behavior."
msgstr ""
"Incorpora texturas compactadas sem perdas na cena gerada, correspondendo ao "
"comportamento antigo."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFTexture.xml
msgid "GLTFTexture represents a texture in a glTF file."
msgstr "GLTFTexture representa a textura em um arquivo glTF."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFTexture.xml
msgid ""
"ID of the texture sampler to use when sampling the image. If -1, then the "
"default texture sampler is used (linear filtering, and repeat wrapping in "
"both axes)."
msgstr ""
"ID do amostrador de textura a ser usado ao fazer a amostragem da imagem. Se "
"-1, o amostrador de textura padrão é usado (filtragem linear e repetição de "
"wrap em ambos os eixos)."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFTexture.xml
msgid ""
"The index of the image associated with this texture, see [method "
"GLTFState.get_images]. If -1, then this texture does not have an image "
"assigned."
msgstr ""
"O índice da imagem associada a esta textura, consulte [method "
"GLTFState.get_images]. Se -1, então esta textura não tem uma imagem "
"atribuída."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFTextureSampler.xml
msgid "Represents a glTF texture sampler"
msgstr "Representa um amostrador de textura glTF"

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFTextureSampler.xml
msgid ""
"Represents a texture sampler as defined by the base glTF spec. Texture "
"samplers in glTF specify how to sample data from the texture's base image, "
"when rendering the texture on an object."
msgstr ""
"Representa um amostrador de textura conforme definido pela especificação "
"base do glTF. Os amostradores de textura no glTF especificam como amostrar "
"dados da imagem base da textura ao renderizar a textura em um objeto."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFTextureSampler.xml
msgid ""
"Texture's magnification filter, used when texture appears larger on screen "
"than the source image."
msgstr ""
"Filtro de magnificação da textura, usado quando a textura aparece maior na "
"tela do que a imagem de origem."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFTextureSampler.xml
msgid ""
"Texture's minification filter, used when the texture appears smaller on "
"screen than the source image."
msgstr ""
"Filtro de minificação da textura, usado quando a textura aparece menor na "
"tela do que a imagem de origem."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFTextureSampler.xml
msgid "Wrapping mode to use for S-axis (horizontal) texture coordinates."
msgstr ""
"Modo de repetição a ser usado para as coordenadas de textura do eixo S "
"(horizontal)."

#: modules/gltf/doc_classes/GLTFTextureSampler.xml
msgid "Wrapping mode to use for T-axis (vertical) texture coordinates."
msgstr ""
"Modo de repetição a ser usado para as coordenadas de textura do eixo T "
"(vertical)."

#: doc/classes/GodotInstance.xml
msgid "Provides access to an embedded Godot instance."
msgstr "Fornece acesso a uma instância embutida do Godot."

#: doc/classes/GodotInstance.xml
msgid ""
"GodotInstance represents a running Godot instance that is controlled from an "
"outside codebase, without a perpetual main loop. It is created by the C API "
"[code]libgodot_create_godot_instance[/code]. Only one may be created per "
"process."
msgstr ""
"GodotInstance representa uma instância em execução do Godot que é controlada "
"a partir de uma base de código externa, sem um loop principal perpétuo. É "
"criada pela API C [code]libgodot_create_godot_instance[/code]. Apenas uma "
"pode ser criada por processo."

#: doc/classes/GodotInstance.xml
msgid "Notifies the instance that it is now in focus."
msgstr "Notifica a instância de que ela está agora em foco."

#: doc/classes/GodotInstance.xml
msgid "Notifies the instance that it is now not in focus."
msgstr "Notifica a instância de que ela agora não está em foco."

#: doc/classes/GodotInstance.xml
msgid "Returns [code]true[/code] if this instance has been fully started."
msgstr "Retorna [code]true[/code] se esta instância foi totalmente iniciada."

#: doc/classes/GodotInstance.xml
msgid ""
"Runs a single iteration of the main loop. Returns [code]true[/code] if the "
"engine is attempting to quit."
msgstr ""
"Executa uma única iteração do loop principal. Retorna [code]true[/code] se o "
"motor estiver tentando fechar."

#: doc/classes/GodotInstance.xml
msgid "Notifies the instance that it is going to be paused."
msgstr "Notifica a instância de que ela será pausada."

#: doc/classes/GodotInstance.xml
msgid "Notifies the instance that it is being resumed."
msgstr "Notifica a instância de que ela está sendo retomada."

#: doc/classes/GodotInstance.xml
msgid ""
"Finishes this instance's startup sequence. Returns [code]true[/code] on "
"success."
msgstr ""
"Finaliza a sequência de inicialização desta instância. Retorna [code]true[/"
"code] em caso de sucesso."

#: doc/classes/GPUParticles2D.xml
msgid "A 2D particle emitter."
msgstr "Um emissor de partículas 2D."

#: doc/classes/GPUParticles2D.xml
msgid ""
"2D particle node used to create a variety of particle systems and effects. "
"[GPUParticles2D] features an emitter that generates some number of particles "
"at a given rate.\n"
"Use the [member process_material] property to add a "
"[ParticleProcessMaterial] to configure particle appearance and behavior. "
"Alternatively, you can add a [ShaderMaterial] which will be applied to all "
"particles.\n"
"2D particles can optionally collide with [LightOccluder2D], but they don't "
"collide with [PhysicsBody2D] nodes."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/GPUParticles2D.xml
msgid "2D Particles Demo"
msgstr "Demonstração de Partículas 2D"

#: doc/classes/GPUParticles2D.xml
msgid ""
"2D Dodge The Creeps Demo (uses GPUParticles2D for the trail behind the "
"player)"
msgstr ""
"Demonstração 2D de desviar dos monstros (usa GPUParticles2D para o rastro "
"atrás do jogador)"

#: doc/classes/GPUParticles2D.xml
msgid ""
"Returns a rectangle containing the positions of all existing particles.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] When using threaded rendering this method synchronizes the "
"rendering thread. Calling it often may have a negative impact on performance."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/GPUParticles2D.xml
msgid "Sets this node's properties to match a given [CPUParticles2D] node."
msgstr ""
"Define as propriedades deste nó para corresponder a um dado nó "
"[CPUParticles2D]."

#: doc/classes/GPUParticles2D.xml doc/classes/GPUParticles3D.xml
msgid ""
"Emits a single particle. Whether [param xform], [param velocity], [param "
"color] and [param custom] are applied depends on the value of [param flags]. "
"See [enum EmitFlags].\n"
"The default ParticleProcessMaterial will overwrite [param color] and use the "
"contents of [param custom] as [code](rotation, age, animation, lifetime)[/"
"code].\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] [method emit_particle] is only supported on the Forward+ and "
"Mobile rendering methods, not Compatibility."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/GPUParticles2D.xml doc/classes/GPUParticles3D.xml
msgid ""
"Restarts the particle emission cycle, clearing existing particles. To avoid "
"particles vanishing from the viewport, wait for the [signal finished] signal "
"before calling.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] The [signal finished] signal is only emitted by [member "
"one_shot] emitters.\n"
"If [param keep_seed] is [code]true[/code], the current random seed will be "
"preserved. Useful for seeking and playback."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/GPUParticles2D.xml doc/classes/GPUParticles3D.xml
msgid ""
"The number of particles to emit in one emission cycle. The effective "
"emission rate is [code](amount * amount_ratio) / lifetime[/code] particles "
"per second. Higher values will increase GPU requirements, even if not all "
"particles are visible at a given time or if [member amount_ratio] is "
"decreased.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Changing this value will cause the particle system to restart. "
"To avoid this, change [member amount_ratio] instead."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/GPUParticles2D.xml doc/classes/GPUParticles3D.xml
msgid ""
"The ratio of particles that should actually be emitted. If set to a value "
"lower than [code]1.0[/code], this will set the amount of emitted particles "
"throughout the lifetime to [code]amount * amount_ratio[/code]. Unlike "
"changing [member amount], changing [member amount_ratio] while emitting does "
"not affect already-emitted particles and doesn't cause the particle system "
"to restart. [member amount_ratio] can be used to create effects that make "
"the number of emitted particles vary over time.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Reducing the [member amount_ratio] has no performance benefit, "
"since resources need to be allocated and processed for the total [member "
"amount] of particles regardless of the [member amount_ratio]. If you don't "
"intend to change the number of particles emitted while the particles are "
"emitting, make sure [member amount_ratio] is set to [code]1[/code] and "
"change [member amount] to your liking instead."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/GPUParticles2D.xml
msgid ""
"Multiplier for particle's collision radius. [code]1.0[/code] corresponds to "
"the size of the sprite. If particles appear to sink into the ground when "
"colliding, increase this value. If particles appear to float when colliding, "
"decrease this value. Only effective if [member "
"ParticleProcessMaterial.collision_mode] is [constant "
"ParticleProcessMaterial.COLLISION_RIGID] or [constant "
"ParticleProcessMaterial.COLLISION_HIDE_ON_CONTACT].\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Particles always have a spherical collision shape."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/GPUParticles2D.xml doc/classes/GPUParticles3D.xml
msgid ""
"If [code]true[/code], particles are being emitted. [member emitting] can be "
"used to start and stop particles from emitting. However, if [member "
"one_shot] is [code]true[/code] setting [member emitting] to [code]true[/"
"code] will not restart the emission cycle unless all active particles have "
"finished processing. Use the [signal finished] signal to be notified once "
"all active particles finish processing.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] For [member one_shot] emitters, due to the particles being "
"computed on the GPU, there may be a short period after receiving the [signal "
"finished] signal during which setting this to [code]true[/code] will not "
"restart the emission cycle.\n"
"[b]Tip:[/b] If your [member one_shot] emitter needs to immediately restart "
"emitting particles once [signal finished] signal is received, consider "
"calling [method restart] instead of setting [member emitting]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/GPUParticles2D.xml doc/classes/GPUParticles3D.xml
msgid ""
"Causes all the particles in this node to interpolate towards the end of "
"their lifetime.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] This only works when used with a [ParticleProcessMaterial]. It "
"needs to be manually implemented for custom process shaders."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/GPUParticles2D.xml doc/classes/GPUParticles3D.xml
msgid ""
"Enables particle interpolation, which makes the particle movement smoother "
"when their [member fixed_fps] is lower than the screen refresh rate."
msgstr ""
"Ativa a interpolação de partículas, o que torna o movimento das partículas "
"mais suave quando seu [member fixed_fps] é menor que a taxa de atualização "
"da tela."

#: doc/classes/GPUParticles2D.xml doc/classes/GPUParticles3D.xml
msgid ""
"The amount of time each particle will exist (in seconds). The effective "
"emission rate is [code](amount * amount_ratio) / lifetime[/code] particles "
"per second."
msgstr ""
"A quantidade de tempo que cada partícula existirá (em segundos). A taxa de "
"emissão efetiva é de [code](amount * amount_ratio) / lifetime[/code] "
"partículas por segundo."

#: doc/classes/GPUParticles2D.xml
msgid ""
"If [code]true[/code], particles use the parent node's coordinate space "
"(known as local coordinates). This will cause particles to move and rotate "
"along the [GPUParticles2D] node (and its parents) when it is moved or "
"rotated. If [code]false[/code], particles use global coordinates; they will "
"not move or rotate along the [GPUParticles2D] node (and its parents) when it "
"is moved or rotated."
msgstr ""
"Se [code]true[/code], as partículas usam o espaço de coordenadas do nó pai "
"(conhecido como coordenadas locais). Isso fará com que as partículas se "
"movam e girem junto com o nó [GPUParticles2D] (e seus pais) quando ele for "
"movido ou girado. Se [code]false[/code], as partículas usam coordenadas "
"globais; elas não se moverão ou girarão junto com o nó [GPUParticles2D] (e "
"seus pais) quando ele for movido ou girado."

#: doc/classes/GPUParticles2D.xml
msgid ""
"Particle system starts as if it had already run for this many seconds.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] This can be very expensive if set to a high number as it "
"requires running the particle shader a number of times equal to the [member "
"fixed_fps] (or 30, if [member fixed_fps] is 0) for every second. In extreme "
"cases it can even lead to a GPU crash due to the volume of work done in a "
"single frame."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/GPUParticles2D.xml doc/classes/GPUParticles3D.xml
msgid ""
"[Material] for processing particles. Can be a [ParticleProcessMaterial] or a "
"[ShaderMaterial]."
msgstr ""
"[Material] para processamento de partículas. Pode ser um "
"[ParticleProcessMaterial] ou um [ShaderMaterial]."

#: doc/classes/GPUParticles2D.xml
msgid ""
"Path to another [GPUParticles2D] node that will be used as a subemitter (see "
"[member ParticleProcessMaterial.sub_emitter_mode]). Subemitters can be used "
"to achieve effects such as fireworks, sparks on collision, bubbles popping "
"into water drops, and more.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] When [member sub_emitter] is set, the target [GPUParticles2D] "
"node will no longer emit particles on its own."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/GPUParticles2D.xml
msgid ""
"Particle texture. If [code]null[/code], particles will be squares with a "
"size of 1×1 pixels.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] To use a flipbook texture, assign a new [CanvasItemMaterial] to "
"the [GPUParticles2D]'s [member CanvasItem.material] property, then enable "
"[member CanvasItemMaterial.particles_animation] and set [member "
"CanvasItemMaterial.particles_anim_h_frames], [member "
"CanvasItemMaterial.particles_anim_v_frames], and [member "
"CanvasItemMaterial.particles_anim_loop] to match the flipbook texture."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/GPUParticles2D.xml
msgid ""
"If [code]true[/code], enables particle trails using a mesh skinning system.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Unlike [GPUParticles3D], the number of trail sections and "
"subdivisions is set with the [member trail_sections] and [member "
"trail_section_subdivisions] properties."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/GPUParticles2D.xml doc/classes/GPUParticles3D.xml
msgid ""
"The amount of time the particle's trail should represent (in seconds). Only "
"effective if [member trail_enabled] is [code]true[/code]."
msgstr ""
"A quantidade de tempo que a trilha da partícula deve representar (em "
"segundos). Só é eficaz se [member trail_enabled] for [code]true[/code]."

#: doc/classes/GPUParticles2D.xml
msgid ""
"The number of subdivisions to use for the particle trail rendering. Higher "
"values can result in smoother trail curves, at the cost of performance due "
"to increased mesh complexity. See also [member trail_sections]. Only "
"effective if [member trail_enabled] is [code]true[/code]."
msgstr ""
"O número de subdivisões a serem usadas para a renderização da trilha de "
"partículas. Valores mais altos podem resultar em curvas de trilha mais "
"suaves, ao custo de desempenho devido ao aumento da complexidade da malha. "
"Veja também [member trail_sections]. Eficaz apenas se [member trail_enabled] "
"for [code]true[/code]."

#: doc/classes/GPUParticles2D.xml
msgid ""
"The number of sections to use for the particle trail rendering. Higher "
"values can result in smoother trail curves, at the cost of performance due "
"to increased mesh complexity. See also [member trail_section_subdivisions]. "
"Only effective if [member trail_enabled] is [code]true[/code]."
msgstr ""
"O número de seções a serem usadas para a renderização da trilha de "
"partículas. Valores mais altos podem resultar em curvas de trilha mais "
"suaves, ao custo de desempenho devido ao aumento da complexidade da malha. "
"Veja também [member trail_section_subdivisions]. Só é eficaz se [member "
"trail_enabled] for [code]true[/code]."

#: doc/classes/GPUParticles2D.xml
msgid ""
"The [Rect2] that determines the node's region which needs to be visible on "
"screen for the particle system to be active.\n"
"Grow the rect if particles suddenly appear/disappear when the node enters/"
"exits the screen. The [Rect2] can be grown via code or with the [b]Particles "
"→ Generate Visibility Rect[/b] editor tool."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/GPUParticles2D.xml doc/classes/GPUParticles3D.xml
msgid ""
"Emitted when all active particles have finished processing. To immediately "
"restart the emission cycle, call [method restart].\n"
"This signal is never emitted when [member one_shot] is disabled, as "
"particles will be emitted and processed continuously.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] For [member one_shot] emitters, due to the particles being "
"computed on the GPU, there may be a short period after receiving the signal "
"during which setting [member emitting] to [code]true[/code] will not restart "
"the emission cycle. This delay is avoided by instead calling [method "
"restart]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/GPUParticles2D.xml doc/classes/GPUParticles3D.xml
msgid ""
"Particles are drawn in reverse order of remaining lifetime. In other words, "
"the particle with the lowest lifetime is drawn at the front."
msgstr ""
"As partículas são desenhadas em ordem inversa de tempo de vida restante. Em "
"outras palavras, a partícula com o menor tempo de vida é desenhada na frente."

#: doc/classes/GPUParticles2D.xml doc/classes/GPUParticles3D.xml
#: doc/classes/RenderingServer.xml
msgid "Particle starts at the specified position."
msgstr "A partícula começa na posição especificada."

#: doc/classes/GPUParticles2D.xml doc/classes/GPUParticles3D.xml
#: doc/classes/RenderingServer.xml
msgid "Particle starts with specified rotation and scale."
msgstr "A partícula começa com a rotação e a escala especificadas."

#: doc/classes/GPUParticles2D.xml doc/classes/GPUParticles3D.xml
#: doc/classes/RenderingServer.xml
msgid ""
"Particle starts with the specified velocity vector, which defines the "
"emission direction and speed."
msgstr ""
"A partícula começa com o vetor de velocidade especificado, que define a "
"direção e a velocidade da emissão."

#: doc/classes/GPUParticles2D.xml doc/classes/GPUParticles3D.xml
#: doc/classes/RenderingServer.xml
msgid "Particle starts with specified color."
msgstr "A partícula começa com a cor especificada."

#: doc/classes/GPUParticles2D.xml doc/classes/GPUParticles3D.xml
#: doc/classes/RenderingServer.xml
msgid "Particle starts with specified [code]CUSTOM[/code] data."
msgstr "A partícula começa com os dados [code]CUSTOM[/code] especificados."

#: doc/classes/GPUParticles3D.xml
msgid "A 3D particle emitter."
msgstr "Um emissor de partículas 3D."

#: doc/classes/GPUParticles3D.xml
msgid ""
"3D particle node used to create a variety of particle systems and effects. "
"[GPUParticles3D] features an emitter that generates some number of particles "
"at a given rate.\n"
"Use [member process_material] to add a [ParticleProcessMaterial] to "
"configure particle appearance and behavior. Alternatively, you can add a "
"[ShaderMaterial] which will be applied to all particles."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/GPUParticles3D.xml
msgid "Controlling thousands of fish with Particles"
msgstr "Controlando milhares de peixes com Partículas"

#: doc/classes/GPUParticles3D.xml
msgid "Sets this node's properties to match a given [CPUParticles3D] node."
msgstr ""
"Define as propriedades deste nó para corresponder a um dado nó "
"[CPUParticles3D]."

#: doc/classes/GPUParticles3D.xml
msgid "Returns the [Mesh] that is drawn at index [param pass]."
msgstr "Retorna o [Mesh] que é desenhado no índice [param pass]."

#: doc/classes/GPUParticles3D.xml
msgid "Sets the [Mesh] that is drawn at index [param pass]."
msgstr "Define o [Mesh] que é desenhado no índice [param pass]."

#: doc/classes/GPUParticles3D.xml
msgid ""
"The base diameter for particle collision in meters. If particles appear to "
"sink into the ground when colliding, increase this value. If particles "
"appear to float when colliding, decrease this value. Only effective if "
"[member ParticleProcessMaterial.collision_mode] is [constant "
"ParticleProcessMaterial.COLLISION_RIGID] or [constant "
"ParticleProcessMaterial.COLLISION_HIDE_ON_CONTACT].\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Particles always have a spherical collision shape."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/GPUParticles3D.xml
msgid ""
"Particle draw order.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] [constant DRAW_ORDER_INDEX] is the only option that supports "
"motion vectors for effects like TAA. It is suggested to use this draw order "
"if the particles are opaque to fix ghosting artifacts."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/GPUParticles3D.xml
msgid "[Mesh] that is drawn for the first draw pass."
msgstr "[Mesh] que é desenhado para a primeira passada de desenho."

#: doc/classes/GPUParticles3D.xml
msgid "[Mesh] that is drawn for the second draw pass."
msgstr "[Mesh] que é desenhado para a segunda passada de desenho."

#: doc/classes/GPUParticles3D.xml
msgid "[Mesh] that is drawn for the third draw pass."
msgstr "[Mesh] que é desenhado para a terceira passada de desenho."

#: doc/classes/GPUParticles3D.xml
msgid "[Mesh] that is drawn for the fourth draw pass."
msgstr "[Mesh] que é desenhado para a quarta passada de desenho."

#: doc/classes/GPUParticles3D.xml
msgid "The number of draw passes when rendering particles."
msgstr "O número de passagens de desenho ao renderizar partículas."

#: doc/classes/GPUParticles3D.xml
msgid ""
"Time ratio between each emission. If [code]0[/code], particles are emitted "
"continuously. If [code]1[/code], all particles are emitted simultaneously."
msgstr ""
"Proporção de tempo entre cada emissão. Se [code]0[/code], as partículas são "
"emitidas continuamente. Se [code]1[/code], todas as partículas são emitidas "
"simultaneamente."

#: doc/classes/GPUParticles3D.xml
msgid ""
"If [code]true[/code], particles use the parent node's coordinate space "
"(known as local coordinates). This will cause particles to move and rotate "
"along the [GPUParticles3D] node (and its parents) when it is moved or "
"rotated. If [code]false[/code], particles use global coordinates; they will "
"not move or rotate along the [GPUParticles3D] node (and its parents) when it "
"is moved or rotated."
msgstr ""
"Se [code]true[/code], as partículas usam o espaço de coordenadas do nó pai "
"(conhecido como coordenadas locais). Isso fará com que as partículas se "
"movam e girem junto com o nó [GPUParticles3D] (e seus pais) quando ele for "
"movido ou girado. Se [code]false[/code], as partículas usam coordenadas "
"globais; elas não se moverão ou girarão junto com o nó [GPUParticles3D] (e "
"seus pais) quando ele for movido ou girado."

#: doc/classes/GPUParticles3D.xml
msgid ""
"If [code]true[/code], only the number of particles equal to [member amount] "
"will be emitted."
msgstr ""
"Se [code]true[/code], apenas o número de partículas igual a [member amount] "
"será emitido."

#: doc/classes/GPUParticles3D.xml
msgid ""
"Amount of time to preprocess the particles before animation starts. Lets you "
"start the animation some time after particles have started emitting.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] This can be very expensive if set to a high number as it "
"requires running the particle shader a number of times equal to the [member "
"fixed_fps] (or 30, if [member fixed_fps] is 0) for every second. In extreme "
"cases it can even lead to a GPU crash due to the volume of work done in a "
"single frame."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/GPUParticles3D.xml
msgid "Emission randomness ratio."
msgstr "Razão de aleatoriedade de emissão."

#: doc/classes/GPUParticles3D.xml
msgid ""
"Speed scaling ratio. A value of [code]0[/code] can be used to pause the "
"particles."
msgstr ""
"Taxa de escala de velocidade. Um valor de [code]0[/code] pode ser usado para "
"pausar as partículas."

#: doc/classes/GPUParticles3D.xml
msgid ""
"Path to another [GPUParticles3D] node that will be used as a subemitter (see "
"[member ParticleProcessMaterial.sub_emitter_mode]). Subemitters can be used "
"to achieve effects such as fireworks, sparks on collision, bubbles popping "
"into water drops, and more.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] When [member sub_emitter] is set, the target [GPUParticles3D] "
"node will no longer emit particles on its own."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/GPUParticles3D.xml
msgid ""
"If [code]true[/code], enables particle trails using a mesh skinning system. "
"Designed to work with [RibbonTrailMesh] and [TubeTrailMesh].\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] [member BaseMaterial3D.use_particle_trails] must also be "
"enabled on the particle mesh's material. Otherwise, setting [member "
"trail_enabled] to [code]true[/code] will have no effect.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Unlike [GPUParticles2D], the number of trail sections and "
"subdivisions is set in the [RibbonTrailMesh] or the [TubeTrailMesh]'s "
"properties."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/GPUParticles3D.xml
msgid ""
"The alignment of particles. Use this for billboarding and aligning to "
"velocity."
msgstr ""
"O alinhamento das partículas. Use isto para \"billboarding\" e alinhamento à "
"velocidade."

#: doc/classes/GPUParticles3D.xml
msgid ""
"When using transform align local billboard, which axis to use for the "
"billboarding. Supports only X or Y."
msgstr ""
"Ao usar o alinhamento de transformação de billboard local, qual eixo usar "
"para o billboard. Suporta apenas X ou Y."

#: doc/classes/GPUParticles3D.xml
msgid ""
"In the case of billboarded particles, which custom channel to read from to "
"calculate their angle."
msgstr ""
"No caso de partículas com billboard, de qual canal personalizado ler para "
"calcular o ângulo delas."

#: doc/classes/GPUParticles3D.xml
msgid ""
"The [AABB] that determines the node's region which needs to be visible on "
"screen for the particle system to be active. [member "
"GeometryInstance3D.extra_cull_margin] is added on each of the AABB's axes. "
"Particle collisions and attraction will only occur within this area.\n"
"Grow the box if particles suddenly appear/disappear when the node enters/"
"exits the screen. The [AABB] can be grown via code or with the [b]Particles "
"→ Generate AABB[/b] editor tool.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] [member visibility_aabb] is overridden by [member "
"GeometryInstance3D.custom_aabb] if that property is set to a non-default "
"value."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/GPUParticles3D.xml
msgid "Maximum number of draw passes supported."
msgstr "Número máximo de passagens de desenho suportadas."

#: doc/classes/GPUParticles3D.xml doc/classes/RenderingServer.xml
msgid "Do not align particle transforms relative to the camera or velocity."
msgstr ""
"Não alinhe as transformações de partículas em relação à câmera ou à "
"velocidade."

#: doc/classes/GPUParticles3D.xml doc/classes/RenderingServer.xml
msgid "Align each particle's Z axis to face the camera."
msgstr "Alinha o eixo Z de cada partícula para ficar voltado para a câmera."

#: doc/classes/GPUParticles3D.xml doc/classes/RenderingServer.xml
msgid "Align each particle's Y axis to the velocity vector."
msgstr "Alinha o eixo Y de cada partícula ao vetor de velocidade."

#: doc/classes/GPUParticles3D.xml doc/classes/RenderingServer.xml
msgid ""
"Align each particle's Z axis to face the camera and Y axis to the velocity "
"vector."
msgstr ""
"Alinha o eixo Z de cada partícula para encarar a câmera e o eixo Y para o "
"vetor de velocidade."

#: doc/classes/GPUParticles3D.xml
msgid ""
"Align each particle's Z axis to face the camera, while preserving a given "
"axis (X or Y)."
msgstr ""
"Alinha o eixo Z de cada partícula para encarar a câmera, preservando um "
"determinado eixo (X ou Y)."

#: doc/classes/GPUParticlesAttractor3D.xml
msgid "Abstract base class for 3D particle attractors."
msgstr "Classe base abstrata para atratores de partículas 3D."

#: doc/classes/GPUParticlesAttractor3D.xml
msgid ""
"Particle attractors can be used to attract particles towards the attractor's "
"origin, or to push them away from the attractor's origin.\n"
"Particle attractors work in real-time and can be moved, rotated and scaled "
"during gameplay. Unlike collision shapes, non-uniform scaling of attractors "
"is also supported.\n"
"Attractors can be temporarily disabled by hiding them, or by setting their "
"[member strength] to [code]0.0[/code].\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Particle attractors only affect [GPUParticles3D], not "
"[CPUParticles3D]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/GPUParticlesAttractor3D.xml
msgid ""
"The particle attractor's attenuation. Higher values result in more gradual "
"pushing of particles as they come closer to the attractor's origin. Zero or "
"negative values will cause particles to be pushed very fast as soon as the "
"touch the attractor's edges."
msgstr ""
"A atenuação do atrator de partículas. Valores mais altos resultam em um "
"empurrão mais gradual das partículas à medida que se aproximam da origem do "
"atrator. Valores zero ou negativos farão com que as partículas sejam "
"empurradas muito rápido assim que atingirem as bordas do atrator."

#: doc/classes/GPUParticlesAttractor3D.xml
msgid ""
"The particle rendering layers ([member VisualInstance3D.layers]) that will "
"be affected by the attractor. By default, all particles are affected by an "
"attractor.\n"
"After configuring particle nodes accordingly, specific layers can be "
"unchecked to prevent certain particles from being affected by attractors. "
"For example, this can be used if you're using an attractor as part of a "
"spell effect but don't want the attractor to affect unrelated weather "
"particles at the same position.\n"
"Particle attraction can also be disabled on a per-process material basis by "
"setting [member ParticleProcessMaterial.attractor_interaction_enabled] on "
"the [GPUParticles3D] node."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/GPUParticlesAttractor3D.xml
msgid ""
"Adjusts how directional the attractor is. At [code]0.0[/code], the attractor "
"is not directional at all: it will attract particles towards its center. At "
"[code]1.0[/code], the attractor is fully directional: particles will always "
"be pushed towards local -Z (or +Z if [member strength] is negative).\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] If [member directionality] is greater than [code]0.0[/code], "
"the direction in which particles are pushed can be changed by rotating the "
"[GPUParticlesAttractor3D] node."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/GPUParticlesAttractor3D.xml
msgid ""
"Adjusts the strength of the attractor. If [member strength] is negative, "
"particles will be pushed in the opposite direction. Particles will be pushed "
"[i]away[/i] from the attractor's origin if [member directionality] is "
"[code]0.0[/code], or towards local +Z if [member directionality] is greater "
"than [code]0.0[/code]."
msgstr ""
"Ajusta a força do atrator. Se [member strength] for negativo, as partículas "
"serão empurradas na direção oposta. As partículas serão empurradas [i]para "
"longe[/i] da origem do atrator se [member directionality] for [code]0.0[/"
"code], ou em direção ao +Z local se [member directionality] for maior que "
"[code]0.0[/code]."

#: doc/classes/GPUParticlesAttractorBox3D.xml
msgid ""
"A box-shaped attractor that influences particles from [GPUParticles3D] nodes."
msgstr ""
"Um atrator em formato de caixa que influencia partículas de nós "
"[GPUParticles3D]."

#: doc/classes/GPUParticlesAttractorBox3D.xml
msgid ""
"A box-shaped attractor that influences particles from [GPUParticles3D] "
"nodes. Can be used to attract particles towards its origin, or to push them "
"away from its origin.\n"
"Particle attractors work in real-time and can be moved, rotated and scaled "
"during gameplay. Unlike collision shapes, non-uniform scaling of attractors "
"is also supported.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Particle attractors only affect [GPUParticles3D], not "
"[CPUParticles3D]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/GPUParticlesAttractorBox3D.xml
msgid "The attractor box's size in 3D units."
msgstr "O tamanho da caixa do atrator em unidades 3D."

#: doc/classes/GPUParticlesAttractorSphere3D.xml
msgid ""
"A spheroid-shaped attractor that influences particles from [GPUParticles3D] "
"nodes."
msgstr ""
"Um atrator em formato de esferoide que influencia partículas de nós "
"[GPUParticles3D]."

#: doc/classes/GPUParticlesAttractorSphere3D.xml
msgid ""
"A spheroid-shaped attractor that influences particles from [GPUParticles3D] "
"nodes. Can be used to attract particles towards its origin, or to push them "
"away from its origin.\n"
"Particle attractors work in real-time and can be moved, rotated and scaled "
"during gameplay. Unlike collision shapes, non-uniform scaling of attractors "
"is also supported.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Particle attractors only affect [GPUParticles3D], not "
"[CPUParticles3D]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/GPUParticlesAttractorSphere3D.xml
msgid ""
"The attractor sphere's radius in 3D units.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Stretched ellipses can be obtained by using non-uniform scaling "
"on the [GPUParticlesAttractorSphere3D] node."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/GPUParticlesAttractorVectorField3D.xml
msgid ""
"A box-shaped attractor with varying directions and strengths defined in it "
"that influences particles from [GPUParticles3D] nodes."
msgstr ""
"Um atrator em forma de caixa com direções e intensidades variadas definidas "
"nele que influencia partículas de nós [GPUParticles3D]."

#: doc/classes/GPUParticlesAttractorVectorField3D.xml
msgid ""
"A box-shaped attractor with varying directions and strengths defined in it "
"that influences particles from [GPUParticles3D] nodes.\n"
"Unlike [GPUParticlesAttractorBox3D], [GPUParticlesAttractorVectorField3D] "
"uses a [member texture] to affect attraction strength within the box. This "
"can be used to create complex attraction scenarios where particles travel in "
"different directions depending on their location. This can be useful for "
"weather effects such as sandstorms.\n"
"Particle attractors work in real-time and can be moved, rotated and scaled "
"during gameplay. Unlike collision shapes, non-uniform scaling of attractors "
"is also supported.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Particle attractors only affect [GPUParticles3D], not "
"[CPUParticles3D]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/GPUParticlesAttractorVectorField3D.xml
msgid "The size of the vector field box in 3D units."
msgstr "O tamanho da caixa do campo vetorial em unidades 3D."

#: doc/classes/GPUParticlesAttractorVectorField3D.xml
msgid ""
"The 3D texture to be used. Values are linearly interpolated between the "
"texture's pixels.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] To get better performance, the 3D texture's resolution should "
"reflect the [member size] of the attractor. Since particle attraction is "
"usually low-frequency data, the texture can be kept at a low resolution such "
"as 64×64×64."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/GPUParticlesCollision3D.xml
msgid ""
"Abstract base class for 3D particle collision shapes affecting "
"[GPUParticles3D] nodes."
msgstr ""
"Classe base abstrata para formas de colisão de partículas 3D que afetam nós "
"[GPUParticles3D]."

#: doc/classes/GPUParticlesCollision3D.xml
msgid ""
"Particle collision shapes can be used to make particles stop or bounce "
"against them.\n"
"Particle collision shapes work in real-time and can be moved, rotated and "
"scaled during gameplay. Unlike attractors, non-uniform scaling of collision "
"shapes is [i]not[/i] supported.\n"
"Particle collision shapes can be temporarily disabled by hiding them.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] [member ParticleProcessMaterial.collision_mode] must be "
"[constant ParticleProcessMaterial.COLLISION_RIGID] or [constant "
"ParticleProcessMaterial.COLLISION_HIDE_ON_CONTACT] on the [GPUParticles3D]'s "
"process material for collision to work.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Particle collision only affects [GPUParticles3D], not "
"[CPUParticles3D].\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Particles pushed by a collider that is being moved will not be "
"interpolated, which can result in visible stuttering. This can be alleviated "
"by setting [member GPUParticles3D.fixed_fps] to [code]0[/code] or a value "
"that matches or exceeds the target framerate."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/GPUParticlesCollision3D.xml
msgid ""
"The particle rendering layers ([member VisualInstance3D.layers]) that will "
"be affected by the collision shape. By default, all particles that have "
"[member ParticleProcessMaterial.collision_mode] set to [constant "
"ParticleProcessMaterial.COLLISION_RIGID] or [constant "
"ParticleProcessMaterial.COLLISION_HIDE_ON_CONTACT] will be affected by a "
"collision shape.\n"
"After configuring particle nodes accordingly, specific layers can be "
"unchecked to prevent certain particles from being affected by colliders. For "
"example, this can be used if you're using a collider as part of a spell "
"effect but don't want the collider to affect unrelated weather particles at "
"the same position.\n"
"Particle collision can also be disabled on a per-process material basis by "
"setting [member ParticleProcessMaterial.collision_mode] on the "
"[GPUParticles3D] node."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/GPUParticlesCollisionBox3D.xml
msgid ""
"A box-shaped 3D particle collision shape affecting [GPUParticles3D] nodes."
msgstr ""
"Uma forma de colisão de partículas 3D em formato de caixa afetando nós "
"[GPUParticles3D]."

#: doc/classes/GPUParticlesCollisionBox3D.xml
msgid ""
"A box-shaped 3D particle collision shape affecting [GPUParticles3D] nodes.\n"
"Particle collision shapes work in real-time and can be moved, rotated and "
"scaled during gameplay. Unlike attractors, non-uniform scaling of collision "
"shapes is [i]not[/i] supported.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] [member ParticleProcessMaterial.collision_mode] must be "
"[constant ParticleProcessMaterial.COLLISION_RIGID] or [constant "
"ParticleProcessMaterial.COLLISION_HIDE_ON_CONTACT] on the [GPUParticles3D]'s "
"process material for collision to work.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Particle collision only affects [GPUParticles3D], not "
"[CPUParticles3D]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/GPUParticlesCollisionBox3D.xml
msgid "The collision box's size in 3D units."
msgstr "O tamanho da caixa de colisão em unidades 3D."

#: doc/classes/GPUParticlesCollisionHeightField3D.xml
msgid ""
"A real-time heightmap-shaped 3D particle collision shape affecting "
"[GPUParticles3D] nodes."
msgstr ""
"Uma forma de colisão de partículas 3D em formato de mapa de altura em tempo "
"real que afeta nós [GPUParticles3D]."

#: doc/classes/GPUParticlesCollisionHeightField3D.xml
msgid ""
"A real-time heightmap-shaped 3D particle collision shape affecting "
"[GPUParticles3D] nodes.\n"
"Heightmap shapes allow for efficiently representing collisions for convex "
"and concave objects with a single \"floor\" (such as terrain). This is less "
"flexible than [GPUParticlesCollisionSDF3D], but it doesn't require a baking "
"step.\n"
"[GPUParticlesCollisionHeightField3D] can also be regenerated in real-time "
"when it is moved, when the camera moves, or even continuously. This makes "
"[GPUParticlesCollisionHeightField3D] a good choice for weather effects such "
"as rain and snow and games with highly dynamic geometry. However, this class "
"is limited since heightmaps cannot represent overhangs (e.g. indoors or "
"caves).\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] [member ParticleProcessMaterial.collision_mode] must be "
"[code]true[/code] on the [GPUParticles3D]'s process material for collision "
"to work.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Particle collision only affects [GPUParticles3D], not "
"[CPUParticles3D]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/GPUParticlesCollisionHeightField3D.xml
msgid ""
"Returns [code]true[/code] if the specified layer of the [member "
"heightfield_mask] is enabled, given a [param layer_number] between [code]1[/"
"code] and [code]20[/code], inclusive."
msgstr ""
"Retorna [code]true[/code] se a camada especificada da [member "
"heightfield_mask] estiver ativada, dado um [param layer_number] entre "
"[code]1[/code] e [code]20[/code], inclusive."

#: doc/classes/GPUParticlesCollisionHeightField3D.xml
msgid ""
"Based on [param value], enables or disables the specified layer in the "
"[member heightfield_mask], given a [param layer_number] between [code]1[/"
"code] and [code]20[/code], inclusive."
msgstr ""
"Com base no [param value], ativa ou desativa a camada especificada na "
"[member heightfield_mask], dado um [param layer_number] entre [code]1[/code] "
"e [code]20[/code], inclusive."

#: doc/classes/GPUParticlesCollisionHeightField3D.xml
msgid ""
"If [code]true[/code], the [GPUParticlesCollisionHeightField3D] will follow "
"the current camera in global space. The [GPUParticlesCollisionHeightField3D] "
"does not need to be a child of the [Camera3D] node for this to work.\n"
"Following the camera has a performance cost, as it will force the heightmap "
"to update whenever the camera moves. Consider lowering [member resolution] "
"to improve performance if [member follow_camera_enabled] is [code]true[/"
"code]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/GPUParticlesCollisionHeightField3D.xml
msgid ""
"The visual layers to account for when updating the heightmap. Only "
"[MeshInstance3D]s whose [member VisualInstance3D.layers] match with this "
"[member heightfield_mask] will be included in the heightmap collision "
"update. By default, all 20 user-visible layers are taken into account for "
"updating the heightmap collision.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Since the [member heightfield_mask] allows for 32 layers to be "
"stored in total, there are an additional 12 layers that are only used "
"internally by the engine and aren't exposed in the editor. Setting [member "
"heightfield_mask] using a script allows you to toggle those reserved layers, "
"which can be useful for editor plugins.\n"
"To adjust [member heightfield_mask] more easily using a script, use [method "
"get_heightfield_mask_value] and [method set_heightfield_mask_value]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/GPUParticlesCollisionHeightField3D.xml
msgid ""
"Higher resolutions can represent small details more accurately in large "
"scenes, at the cost of lower performance. If [member update_mode] is "
"[constant UPDATE_MODE_ALWAYS], consider using the lowest resolution possible."
msgstr ""
"Resoluções mais altas podem representar pequenos detalhes com mais precisão "
"em grandes cenas, ao custo de menor desempenho. Se [member update_mode] for "
"[constant UPDATE_MODE_ALWAYS], considere usar a menor resolução possível."

#: doc/classes/GPUParticlesCollisionHeightField3D.xml
msgid ""
"The collision heightmap's size in 3D units. To improve heightmap quality, "
"[member size] should be set as small as possible while covering the parts of "
"the scene you need."
msgstr ""
"O tamanho do mapa de altura de colisão em unidades 3D. Para melhorar a "
"qualidade do mapa de altura, [member size] deve ser definido o menor "
"possível enquanto cobre as partes da cena de que você precisa."

#: doc/classes/GPUParticlesCollisionHeightField3D.xml
msgid "The update policy to use for the generated heightmap."
msgstr "A política de atualização a ser usada para o heightmap gerado."

#: doc/classes/GPUParticlesCollisionHeightField3D.xml
msgid ""
"Generate a 256×256 heightmap. Intended for small-scale scenes, or larger "
"scenes with no distant particles."
msgstr ""
"Gera um heightmap de 256×256. Destinado a cenas de pequena escala ou cenas "
"maiores sem partículas distantes."

#: doc/classes/GPUParticlesCollisionHeightField3D.xml
msgid ""
"Generate a 512×512 heightmap. Intended for medium-scale scenes, or larger "
"scenes with no distant particles."
msgstr ""
"Gera um heightmap de 512×512. Destinado a cenas de média escala ou cenas "
"maiores sem partículas distantes."

#: doc/classes/GPUParticlesCollisionHeightField3D.xml
msgid ""
"Generate a 1024×1024 heightmap. Intended for large scenes with distant "
"particles."
msgstr ""
"Gera um mapa de altura de 1024×1024. Destinado a cenas grandes com "
"partículas distantes."

#: doc/classes/GPUParticlesCollisionHeightField3D.xml
msgid ""
"Generate a 2048×2048 heightmap. Intended for very large scenes with distant "
"particles."
msgstr ""
"Gera um mapa de altura 2048×2048. Destinado a cenas muito grandes com "
"partículas distantes."

#: doc/classes/GPUParticlesCollisionHeightField3D.xml
msgid ""
"Generate a 4096×4096 heightmap. Intended for huge scenes with distant "
"particles."
msgstr ""
"Gera um mapa de altura de 4096×4096. Destinado a cenas enormes com "
"partículas distantes."

#: doc/classes/GPUParticlesCollisionHeightField3D.xml
msgid ""
"Generate a 8192×8192 heightmap. Intended for gigantic scenes with distant "
"particles."
msgstr ""
"Gera um mapa de altura 8192×8192. Destinado a cenas gigantescas com "
"partículas distantes."

#: doc/classes/GPUParticlesCollisionHeightField3D.xml
#: doc/classes/GPUParticlesCollisionSDF3D.xml
msgid "Represents the size of the [enum Resolution] enum."
msgstr "Representa o tamanho da enumeração [enum Resolution]."

#: doc/classes/GPUParticlesCollisionHeightField3D.xml
msgid ""
"Only update the heightmap when the [GPUParticlesCollisionHeightField3D] node "
"is moved, or when the camera moves if [member follow_camera_enabled] is "
"[code]true[/code]. An update can be forced by slightly moving the "
"[GPUParticlesCollisionHeightField3D] in any direction, or by calling [method "
"RenderingServer.particles_collision_height_field_update]."
msgstr ""
"Atualiza o mapa de altura apenas quando o nó "
"[GPUParticlesCollisionHeightField3D] é movido ou quando a câmera se move, se "
"[member follow_camera_enabled] for [code]true[/code]. Uma atualização pode "
"ser forçada movendo ligeiramente o [GPUParticlesCollisionHeightField3D] em "
"qualquer direção ou chamando [method "
"RenderingServer.particles_collision_height_field_update]."

#: doc/classes/GPUParticlesCollisionHeightField3D.xml
msgid ""
"Update the heightmap every frame. This has a significant performance cost. "
"This update should only be used when geometry that particles can collide "
"with changes significantly during gameplay."
msgstr ""
"Atualiza o mapa de altura a cada quadro. Isso tem um custo de desempenho "
"significativo. Esta atualização só deve ser usada quando a geometria com a "
"qual as partículas podem colidir mudar significativamente durante a "
"jogabilidade."

#: doc/classes/GPUParticlesCollisionSDF3D.xml
msgid ""
"A baked signed distance field 3D particle collision shape affecting "
"[GPUParticles3D] nodes."
msgstr ""
"Uma forma de colisão de partículas 3D em formato de campo de distância com "
"sinal bakeado que afeta nós [GPUParticles3D]."

#: doc/classes/GPUParticlesCollisionSDF3D.xml
msgid ""
"A baked signed distance field 3D particle collision shape affecting "
"[GPUParticles3D] nodes.\n"
"Signed distance fields (SDF) allow for efficiently representing approximate "
"collision shapes for convex and concave objects of any shape. This is more "
"flexible than [GPUParticlesCollisionHeightField3D], but it requires a baking "
"step.\n"
"[b]Baking:[/b] The signed distance field texture can be baked by selecting "
"the [GPUParticlesCollisionSDF3D] node in the editor, then clicking [b]Bake "
"SDF[/b] at the top of the 3D viewport. Any [i]visible[/i] [MeshInstance3D]s "
"within the [member size] will be taken into account for baking, regardless "
"of their [member GeometryInstance3D.gi_mode].\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Baking a [GPUParticlesCollisionSDF3D]'s [member texture] is "
"only possible within the editor, as there is no bake method exposed for use "
"in exported projects. However, it's still possible to load pre-baked "
"[Texture3D]s into its [member texture] property in an exported project.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] [member ParticleProcessMaterial.collision_mode] must be "
"[constant ParticleProcessMaterial.COLLISION_RIGID] or [constant "
"ParticleProcessMaterial.COLLISION_HIDE_ON_CONTACT] on the [GPUParticles3D]'s "
"process material for collision to work.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Particle collision only affects [GPUParticles3D], not "
"[CPUParticles3D]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/GPUParticlesCollisionSDF3D.xml
#: doc/classes/OccluderInstance3D.xml
msgid ""
"Returns whether or not the specified layer of the [member bake_mask] is "
"enabled, given a [param layer_number] between 1 and 32."
msgstr ""
"Retorna se a camada especificada do [member bake_mask] está ativada ou não, "
"dado um [param layer_number] entre 1 e 32."

#: doc/classes/GPUParticlesCollisionSDF3D.xml
#: doc/classes/OccluderInstance3D.xml
msgid ""
"Based on [param value], enables or disables the specified layer in the "
"[member bake_mask], given a [param layer_number] between 1 and 32."
msgstr ""
"Com base em [param value], ativa ou desativa a camada especificada em "
"[member bake_mask], dado um [param layer_number] entre 1 e 32."

#: doc/classes/GPUParticlesCollisionSDF3D.xml
msgid ""
"The visual layers to account for when baking the particle collision SDF. "
"Only [MeshInstance3D]s whose [member VisualInstance3D.layers] match with "
"this [member bake_mask] will be included in the generated particle collision "
"SDF. By default, all objects are taken into account for the particle "
"collision SDF baking."
msgstr ""
"As camadas visuais a serem consideradas ao criar o SDF de colisão de "
"partículas. Apenas [MeshInstance3D] cujos [member VisualInstance3D.layers] "
"correspondem a este [member bake_mask] serão incluídos no SDF de colisão de "
"partículas gerado. Por padrão, todos os objetos são levados em consideração "
"para a criação do SDF de colisão de partículas."

#: doc/classes/GPUParticlesCollisionSDF3D.xml
msgid ""
"The bake resolution to use for the signed distance field [member texture]. "
"The texture must be baked again for changes to the [member resolution] "
"property to be effective. Higher resolutions have a greater performance cost "
"and take more time to bake. Higher resolutions also result in larger baked "
"textures, leading to increased VRAM and storage space requirements. To "
"improve performance and reduce bake times, use the lowest resolution "
"possible for the object you're representing the collision of."
msgstr ""
"A resolução de bake a ser usada para a [member texture] de campo de "
"distância assinada. A textura deve ser feita em bake novamente para que as "
"alterações na propriedade [member resolution] tenham efeito. Resoluções mais "
"altas têm um custo de desempenho maior e levam mais tempo para o bake. "
"Resoluções mais altas também resultam em texturas maiores geradas por bake, "
"levando a requisitos aumentados de VRAM e espaço de armazenamento. Para "
"melhorar o desempenho e reduzir os tempos de bake, use a menor resolução "
"possível para o objeto cuja colisão você está representando."

#: doc/classes/GPUParticlesCollisionSDF3D.xml
msgid ""
"The collision SDF's size in 3D units. To improve SDF quality, the [member "
"size] should be set as small as possible while covering the parts of the "
"scene you need."
msgstr ""
"O tamanho do SDF de colisão em unidades 3D. Para melhorar a qualidade do "
"SDF, o [member size] deve ser definido o menor possível, cobrindo as partes "
"da cena de que você precisa."

#: doc/classes/GPUParticlesCollisionSDF3D.xml
msgid "The 3D texture representing the signed distance field."
msgstr "A textura 3D representando o campo de distância assinado."

#: doc/classes/GPUParticlesCollisionSDF3D.xml
msgid ""
"The collision shape's thickness. Unlike other particle colliders, "
"[GPUParticlesCollisionSDF3D] is actually hollow on the inside. [member "
"thickness] can be increased to prevent particles from tunneling through the "
"collision shape at high speeds, or when the [GPUParticlesCollisionSDF3D] is "
"moved."
msgstr ""
"A espessura da forma de colisão. Ao contrário de outros colisores de "
"partículas, o [GPUParticlesCollisionSDF3D] é na verdade oco por dentro. "
"[member thickness] pode ser aumentado para evitar que as partículas "
"atravessem a forma de colisão em altas velocidades ou quando o "
"[GPUParticlesCollisionSDF3D] for movido."

#: doc/classes/GPUParticlesCollisionSDF3D.xml
msgid ""
"Bake a 16×16×16 signed distance field. This is the fastest option, but also "
"the least precise."
msgstr ""
"Faz o bake de um campo de distância sinalizada 16×16×16. Esta é a opção mais "
"rápida, mas também a menos precisa."

#: doc/classes/GPUParticlesCollisionSDF3D.xml
msgid "Bake a 32×32×32 signed distance field."
msgstr "Criar um campo de distância assinado 32×32×32."

#: doc/classes/GPUParticlesCollisionSDF3D.xml
msgid "Bake a 64×64×64 signed distance field."
msgstr "Criar um campo de distância assinado 64×64×64."

#: doc/classes/GPUParticlesCollisionSDF3D.xml
msgid "Bake a 128×128×128 signed distance field."
msgstr "Criar um campo de distância assinado 128×128×128."

#: doc/classes/GPUParticlesCollisionSDF3D.xml
msgid "Bake a 256×256×256 signed distance field."
msgstr "Criar um campo de distância assinado 256×256×256."

#: doc/classes/GPUParticlesCollisionSDF3D.xml
msgid ""
"Bake a 512×512×512 signed distance field. This is the slowest option, but "
"also the most precise."
msgstr ""
"Faz o bake de um campo de distância sinalizada 512×512×512. Esta é a opção "
"mais lenta, mas também a mais precisa."

#: doc/classes/GPUParticlesCollisionSphere3D.xml
msgid ""
"A sphere-shaped 3D particle collision shape affecting [GPUParticles3D] nodes."
msgstr ""
"Uma forma de colisão de partículas 3D em formato de esfera afetando nós "
"[GPUParticles3D]."

#: doc/classes/GPUParticlesCollisionSphere3D.xml
msgid ""
"A sphere-shaped 3D particle collision shape affecting [GPUParticles3D] "
"nodes.\n"
"Particle collision shapes work in real-time and can be moved, rotated and "
"scaled during gameplay. Unlike attractors, non-uniform scaling of collision "
"shapes is [i]not[/i] supported.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] [member ParticleProcessMaterial.collision_mode] must be "
"[constant ParticleProcessMaterial.COLLISION_RIGID] or [constant "
"ParticleProcessMaterial.COLLISION_HIDE_ON_CONTACT] on the [GPUParticles3D]'s "
"process material for collision to work.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Particle collision only affects [GPUParticles3D], not "
"[CPUParticles3D]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/GPUParticlesCollisionSphere3D.xml
msgid "The collision sphere's radius in 3D units."
msgstr "O raio da esfera de colisão em unidades 3D."

#: doc/classes/Gradient.xml
msgid "A color transition."
msgstr "Uma transição de cor."

#: doc/classes/Gradient.xml
msgid ""
"This resource describes a color transition by defining a set of colored "
"points and how to interpolate between them.\n"
"See also [Curve] which supports more complex easing methods, but does not "
"support colors."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Gradient.xml
msgid "Adds the specified color to the gradient, with the specified offset."
msgstr ""
"Adiciona a cor especificada ao gradiente, com o deslocamento especificado."

#: doc/classes/Gradient.xml
msgid "Returns the color of the gradient color at index [param point]."
msgstr "Retorna a cor do gradiente de cor no índice [param point]."

#: doc/classes/Gradient.xml
msgid "Returns the offset of the gradient color at index [param point]."
msgstr "Retorna o deslocamento do gradiente de cor no índice [param point]."

#: doc/classes/Gradient.xml
msgid "Returns the number of colors in the gradient."
msgstr "Retorna o número de cores no gradiente."

#: doc/classes/Gradient.xml
msgid "Removes the color at index [param point]."
msgstr "Remove a cor no índice [param point]."

#: doc/classes/Gradient.xml
msgid ""
"Reverses/mirrors the gradient.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] This method mirrors all points around the middle of the "
"gradient, which may produce unexpected results when [member "
"interpolation_mode] is set to [constant GRADIENT_INTERPOLATE_CONSTANT]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Gradient.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the interpolated color specified by [param offset]. [param offset] "
"should be between [code]0.0[/code] and [code]1.0[/code] (inclusive). Using a "
"value lower than [code]0.0[/code] will return the same color as [code]0.0[/"
"code], and using a value higher than [code]1.0[/code] will return the same "
"color as [code]1.0[/code]. If your input value is not within this range, "
"consider using [method @GlobalScope.remap] on the input value with output "
"values set to [code]0.0[/code] and [code]1.0[/code]."
msgstr ""
"Retorna a cor interpolada especificada por [param offset]. [param offset] "
"deve estar entre [code]0.0[/code] e [code]1.0[/code] (inclusive). Usar um "
"valor inferior a [code]0.0[/code] retornará a mesma cor que [code]0.0[/"
"code], e usar um valor superior a [code]1.0[/code] retornará a mesma cor que "
"[code]1.0[/code]. Se o seu valor de entrada não estiver dentro deste "
"intervalo, considere usar [method @GlobalScope.remap] no valor de entrada "
"com valores de saída definidos como [code]0.0[/code] e [code]1.0[/code]."

#: doc/classes/Gradient.xml
msgid "Sets the color of the gradient color at index [param point]."
msgstr "Define a cor do gradiente no índice [param point]."

#: doc/classes/Gradient.xml
msgid "Sets the offset for the gradient color at index [param point]."
msgstr "Define o deslocamento para a cor do gradiente no índice [param point]."

#: doc/classes/Gradient.xml
msgid ""
"Gradient's colors as a [PackedColorArray].\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Setting this property updates all colors at once. To update any "
"color individually use [method set_color]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Gradient.xml
msgid ""
"The color space used to interpolate between points of the gradient. It does "
"not affect the returned colors, which will always use nonlinear sRGB "
"encoding.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] This setting has no effect when [member interpolation_mode] is "
"set to [constant GRADIENT_INTERPOLATE_CONSTANT]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Gradient.xml
msgid "The algorithm used to interpolate between points of the gradient."
msgstr "O algoritmo usado para interpolar entre os pontos do gradiente."

#: doc/classes/Gradient.xml
msgid ""
"Gradient's offsets as a [PackedFloat32Array].\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Setting this property updates all offsets at once. To update "
"any offset individually use [method set_offset]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Gradient.xml
msgid ""
"Constant interpolation, color changes abruptly at each point and stays "
"uniform between. This might cause visible aliasing when used for a gradient "
"texture in some cases."
msgstr ""
"Interpolação constante, a cor muda abruptamente em cada ponto e permanece "
"uniforme entre eles. Isso pode causar serrilhamento visível quando usado "
"para uma textura de gradiente em alguns casos."

#: doc/classes/Gradient.xml
msgid "Cubic interpolation."
msgstr "Interpolação cúbica."

#: doc/classes/Gradient.xml
msgid "sRGB color space."
msgstr "Espaço de cores sRGB."

#: doc/classes/Gradient.xml
msgid "Linear sRGB color space."
msgstr "Espaço de cores sRGB linear."

#: doc/classes/Gradient.xml
msgid ""
"[url=https://bottosson.github.io/posts/oklab/]Oklab[/url] color space. This "
"color space provides a smooth and uniform-looking transition between colors."
msgstr ""
"Espaço de cores [url=https://bottosson.github.io/posts/oklab/]Oklab[/url]. "
"Este espaço de cores fornece uma transição suave e com aparência uniforme "
"entre as cores."

#: doc/classes/GradientTexture1D.xml
msgid "A 1D texture that uses colors obtained from a [Gradient]."
msgstr "Uma textura 1D que usa cores obtidas de um [Gradient]."

#: doc/classes/GradientTexture1D.xml
msgid ""
"A 1D texture that obtains colors from a [Gradient] to fill the texture data. "
"The texture is filled by sampling the gradient for each pixel. Therefore, "
"the texture does not necessarily represent an exact copy of the gradient, as "
"it may miss some colors if there are not enough pixels. See also "
"[GradientTexture2D], [CurveTexture] and [CurveXYZTexture]."
msgstr ""
"Uma textura 1D que obtém cores de um [Gradient] para preencher os dados da "
"textura. A textura é preenchida amostrando o gradiente para cada pixel. "
"Portanto, a textura não representa necessariamente uma cópia exata do "
"gradiente, pois pode perder algumas cores se não houver pixels suficientes. "
"Veja também [GradientTexture2D], [CurveTexture] e [CurveXYZTexture]."

#: doc/classes/GradientTexture1D.xml doc/classes/GradientTexture2D.xml
msgid "The [Gradient] used to fill the texture."
msgstr "O [Gradient] usado para preencher a textura."

#: doc/classes/GradientTexture1D.xml doc/classes/GradientTexture2D.xml
msgid ""
"If [code]true[/code], the generated texture will support high dynamic range "
"([constant Image.FORMAT_RGBAF] format). This allows for glow effects to work "
"if [member Environment.glow_enabled] is [code]true[/code]. If [code]false[/"
"code], the generated texture will use low dynamic range; overbright colors "
"will be clamped ([constant Image.FORMAT_RGBA8] format)."
msgstr ""
"Se [code]true[/code], a textura gerada suportará alto alcance dinâmico "
"(formato [constant Image.FORMAT_RGBAF]). Isso permite que os efeitos de "
"brilho funcionem se [member Environment.glow_enabled] for [code]true[/code]. "
"Se [code]false[/code], a textura gerada usará baixo alcance dinâmico; cores "
"excessivamente brilhantes serão limitadas (formato [constant "
"Image.FORMAT_RGBA8])."

#: doc/classes/GradientTexture1D.xml
msgid "The number of color samples that will be obtained from the [Gradient]."
msgstr "O número de amostras de cores que serão obtidas de [Gradient]."

#: doc/classes/GradientTexture2D.xml
msgid ""
"A 2D texture that creates a pattern with colors obtained from a [Gradient]."
msgstr "Uma textura 2D que cria um padrão com cores obtidas de um [Gradient]."

#: doc/classes/GradientTexture2D.xml
msgid ""
"A 2D texture that obtains colors from a [Gradient] to fill the texture data. "
"This texture is able to transform a color transition into different patterns "
"such as a linear or a radial gradient. The texture is filled by "
"interpolating colors starting from [member fill_from] to [member fill_to] "
"offsets by default, but the gradient fill can be repeated to cover the "
"entire texture.\n"
"The gradient is sampled individually for each pixel so it does not "
"necessarily represent an exact copy of the gradient (see [member width] and "
"[member height]). See also [GradientTexture1D], [CurveTexture] and "
"[CurveXYZTexture]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/GradientTexture2D.xml
msgid "The gradient's fill type."
msgstr "O tipo de preenchimento do gradiente."

#: doc/classes/GradientTexture2D.xml
msgid ""
"The initial offset used to fill the texture specified in UV coordinates."
msgstr ""
"O deslocamento inicial usado para preencher a textura especificada em "
"coordenadas UV."

#: doc/classes/GradientTexture2D.xml
msgid "The final offset used to fill the texture specified in UV coordinates."
msgstr ""
"O deslocamento final usado para preencher a textura especificada em "
"coordenadas UV."

#: doc/classes/GradientTexture2D.xml
msgid ""
"The number of vertical color samples that will be obtained from the "
"[Gradient], which also represents the texture's height."
msgstr ""
"O número de amostras de cor verticais que serão obtidas do [Gradient], o que "
"também representa a altura da textura."

#: doc/classes/GradientTexture2D.xml
msgid "The gradient's repeat type."
msgstr "O tipo de repetição do gradiente."

#: doc/classes/GradientTexture2D.xml
msgid ""
"The number of horizontal color samples that will be obtained from the "
"[Gradient], which also represents the texture's width."
msgstr ""
"O número de amostras de cor horizontais que serão obtidas do [Gradient], o "
"que também representa a largura da textura."

#: doc/classes/GradientTexture2D.xml
msgid "The colors are linearly interpolated in a straight line."
msgstr "As cores são interpoladas linearmente em uma linha reta."

#: doc/classes/GradientTexture2D.xml
msgid "The colors are linearly interpolated in a circular pattern."
msgstr "As cores são interpoladas linearmente em um padrão circular."

#: doc/classes/GradientTexture2D.xml
msgid "The colors are linearly interpolated in a square pattern."
msgstr "As cores são interpoladas linearmente em um padrão quadrado."

#: doc/classes/GradientTexture2D.xml
msgid "The colors are linearly interpolated in a cone pattern."
msgstr "As cores são interpoladas linearmente em um padrão de cone."

#: doc/classes/GradientTexture2D.xml
msgid ""
"The gradient fill is restricted to the range defined by [member fill_from] "
"to [member fill_to] offsets."
msgstr ""
"O preenchimento de gradiente é restrito ao intervalo definido pelos "
"deslocamentos [member fill_from] a [member fill_to]."

#: doc/classes/GradientTexture2D.xml
msgid ""
"The texture is filled starting from [member fill_from] to [member fill_to] "
"offsets, repeating the same pattern in both directions."
msgstr ""
"A textura é preenchida começando de [member fill_from] até os deslocamentos "
"[member fill_to], repetindo o mesmo padrão em ambas as direções."

#: doc/classes/GradientTexture2D.xml
msgid ""
"The texture is filled starting from [member fill_from] to [member fill_to] "
"offsets, mirroring the pattern in both directions."
msgstr ""
"A textura é preenchida a partir dos deslocamentos [member fill_from] até "
"[member fill_to], espelhando o padrão em ambas as direções."

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid "An editor for graph-like structures, using [GraphNode]s."
msgstr "Um editor para estruturas em formato de grafo, usando [GraphNode]s."

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid ""
"[GraphEdit] provides tools for creation, manipulation, and display of "
"various graphs. Its main purpose in the engine is to power the visual "
"programming systems, such as visual shaders, but it is also available for "
"use in user projects.\n"
"[GraphEdit] by itself is only an empty container, representing an infinite "
"grid where [GraphNode]s can be placed. Each [GraphNode] represents a node in "
"the graph, a single unit of data in the connected scheme. [GraphEdit], in "
"turn, helps to control various interactions with nodes and between nodes. "
"When the user attempts to connect, disconnect, or delete a [GraphNode], a "
"signal is emitted in the [GraphEdit], but no action is taken by default. It "
"is the responsibility of the programmer utilizing this control to implement "
"the necessary logic to determine how each request should be handled.\n"
"[b]Performance:[/b] It is greatly advised to enable low-processor usage mode "
"(see [member OS.low_processor_usage_mode]) when using GraphEdits.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Keep in mind that [method Node.get_children] will also return "
"the connection layer node named [code]_connection_layer[/code] due to "
"technical limitations. This behavior may change in future releases."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid ""
"Virtual method which can be overridden to customize how connections are "
"drawn."
msgstr ""
"Método virtual que pode ser substituído para personalizar como as conexões "
"são desenhadas."

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid ""
"Returns whether the [param mouse_position] is in the input hot zone.\n"
"By default, a hot zone is a [Rect2] positioned such that its center is at "
"[param in_node].[method GraphNode.get_input_port_position]([param in_port]) "
"(For output's case, call [method GraphNode.get_output_port_position] "
"instead). The hot zone's width is twice the Theme Property "
"[code]port_grab_distance_horizontal[/code], and its height is twice the "
"[code]port_grab_distance_vertical[/code].\n"
"Below is a sample code to help get started:\n"
"[codeblock]\n"
"func _is_in_input_hotzone(in_node, in_port, mouse_position):\n"
"\tvar port_size = "
"Vector2(get_theme_constant(\"port_grab_distance_horizontal\"), "
"get_theme_constant(\"port_grab_distance_vertical\"))\n"
"\tvar port_pos = in_node.get_position() + "
"in_node.get_input_port_position(in_port) - port_size / 2\n"
"\tvar rect = Rect2(port_pos, port_size)\n"
"\n"
"\treturn rect.has_point(mouse_position)\n"
"[/codeblock]"
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid ""
"Returns whether the [param mouse_position] is in the output hot zone. For "
"more information on hot zones, see [method _is_in_input_hotzone].\n"
"Below is a sample code to help get started:\n"
"[codeblock]\n"
"func _is_in_output_hotzone(in_node, in_port, mouse_position):\n"
"\tvar port_size = "
"Vector2(get_theme_constant(\"port_grab_distance_horizontal\"), "
"get_theme_constant(\"port_grab_distance_vertical\"))\n"
"\tvar port_pos = in_node.get_position() + "
"in_node.get_output_port_position(in_port) - port_size / 2\n"
"\tvar rect = Rect2(port_pos, port_size)\n"
"\n"
"\treturn rect.has_point(mouse_position)\n"
"[/codeblock]"
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid ""
"This virtual method can be used to insert additional error detection while "
"the user is dragging a connection over a valid port.\n"
"Return [code]true[/code] if the connection is indeed valid or return "
"[code]false[/code] if the connection is impossible. If the connection is "
"impossible, no snapping to the port and thus no connection request to that "
"port will happen.\n"
"In this example a connection to same node is suppressed:\n"
"[codeblocks]\n"
"[gdscript]\n"
"func _is_node_hover_valid(from, from_port, to, to_port):\n"
"\treturn from != to\n"
"[/gdscript]\n"
"[csharp]\n"
"public override bool _IsNodeHoverValid(StringName fromNode, int fromPort, "
"StringName toNode, int toPort)\n"
"{\n"
"\treturn fromNode != toNode;\n"
"}\n"
"[/csharp]\n"
"[/codeblocks]"
msgstr ""
"Este método virtual pode ser usado para inserir detecção de erros adicional "
"enquanto o usuário arrasta uma conexão sobre uma porta válida.\n"
"Retorne [code]true[/code] se a conexão for realmente válida ou retorne "
"[code]false[/code] se a conexão for impossível. Se a conexão for impossível, "
"nenhum encaixe na porta e, portanto, nenhuma solicitação de conexão para "
"essa porta ocorrerá.\n"
"Neste exemplo, uma conexão para o mesmo nó é suprimida:\n"
"[codeblocks]\n"
"[gdscript]\n"
"func _is_node_hover_valid(from, from_port, to, to_port):\n"
"\treturn from != to\n"
"[/gdscript]\n"
"[csharp]\n"
"public override bool _IsNodeHoverValid(StringName fromNode, int fromPort, "
"StringName toNode, int toPort)\n"
"{\n"
"\treturn fromNode != toNode;\n"
"}\n"
"[/csharp]\n"
"[/codeblocks]"

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid ""
"Allows the connection between two different port types. The port type is "
"defined individually for the left and the right port of each slot with the "
"[method GraphNode.set_slot] method.\n"
"See also [method is_valid_connection_type] and [method "
"remove_valid_connection_type]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid ""
"Allows to disconnect nodes when dragging from the left port of the "
"[GraphNode]'s slot if it has the specified type. See also [method "
"remove_valid_left_disconnect_type]."
msgstr ""
"Permite desconectar nós ao arrastar a partir da porta esquerda do slot do "
"[GraphNode] se ele tiver o tipo especificado. Veja também [method "
"remove_valid_left_disconnect_type]."

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid ""
"Allows to disconnect nodes when dragging from the right port of the "
"[GraphNode]'s slot if it has the specified type. See also [method "
"remove_valid_right_disconnect_type]."
msgstr ""
"Permite desconectar nós ao arrastar a partir da porta direita do slot do "
"[GraphNode] se ele tiver o tipo especificado. Veja também [method "
"remove_valid_right_disconnect_type]."

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid ""
"Rearranges selected nodes in a layout with minimum crossings between "
"connections and uniform horizontal and vertical gap between nodes."
msgstr ""
"Reorganiza nós selecionados em um layout com cruzamentos mínimos entre "
"conexões e espaçamento horizontal e vertical uniforme entre os nós."

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid ""
"Attaches the [param element] [GraphElement] to the [param frame] "
"[GraphFrame]."
msgstr ""
"Anexa o [GraphElement] de [param element] ao [GraphFrame] de [param frame]."

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid "Removes all connections between nodes."
msgstr "Remove todas as conexões entre nós."

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid ""
"Create a connection between the [param from_port] of the [param from_node] "
"[GraphNode] and the [param to_port] of the [param to_node] [GraphNode]. If "
"the connection already exists, no connection is created.\n"
"Connections with [param keep_alive] set to [code]false[/code] may be deleted "
"automatically if invalid during a redraw."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid ""
"Detaches the [param element] [GraphElement] from the [GraphFrame] it is "
"currently attached to."
msgstr ""
"Desconecta o [GraphElement] [param element] do [GraphFrame] ao qual ele está "
"conectado no momento."

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid ""
"Removes the connection between the [param from_port] of the [param "
"from_node] [GraphNode] and the [param to_port] of the [param to_node] "
"[GraphNode]. If the connection does not exist, no connection is removed."
msgstr ""
"Remove a conexão entre a [param from_port] do [GraphNode] [param from_node] "
"e a [param to_port] do [GraphNode] [param to_node]. Se a conexão não "
"existir, nenhuma conexão será removida."

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid ""
"Ends the creation of the current connection. In other words, if you are "
"dragging a connection you can use this method to abort the process and "
"remove the line that followed your cursor.\n"
"This is best used together with [signal connection_drag_started] and [signal "
"connection_drag_ended] to add custom behavior like node addition through "
"shortcuts.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] This method suppresses any other connection request signals "
"apart from [signal connection_drag_ended]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid ""
"Returns an array of node names that are attached to the [GraphFrame] with "
"the given name."
msgstr ""
"Retorna um array de nomes de nós que estão anexados ao [GraphFrame] com o "
"nome fornecido."

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the closest connection to the given point in screen space. If no "
"connection is found within [param max_distance] pixels, an empty "
"[Dictionary] is returned.\n"
"A connection is represented as a [Dictionary] in the form of:\n"
"[codeblock]\n"
"{\n"
"\tfrom_node: StringName,\n"
"\tfrom_port: int,\n"
"\tto_node: StringName,\n"
"\tto_port: int,\n"
"\tkeep_alive: bool\n"
"}\n"
"[/codeblock]\n"
"For example, getting a connection at a given mouse position can be achieved "
"like this:\n"
"[codeblocks]\n"
"[gdscript]\n"
"var connection = "
"get_closest_connection_at_point(mouse_event.get_position())\n"
"[/gdscript]\n"
"[/codeblocks]"
msgstr ""
"Retorna a conexão mais próxima do ponto fornecido no espaço de tela. Se "
"nenhuma conexão for encontrada dentro de [param max_distance] píxeis, um "
"[Dictionary] vazio será retornado.\n"
"Uma conexão é representada como um [Dictionary] na forma de:\n"
"[codeblock]\n"
"{\n"
"\tfrom_node: StringName,\n"
"\tfrom_port: int,\n"
"\tto_node: StringName,\n"
"\tto_port: int,\n"
"\tkeep_alive: bool\n"
"}\n"
"[/codeblock]\n"
"Por exemplo, obter uma conexão em uma determinada posição do mouse pode ser "
"feito assim:\n"
"[codeblocks]\n"
"[gdscript]\n"
"var connection = "
"get_closest_connection_at_point(mouse_event.get_position())\n"
"[/gdscript]\n"
"[/codeblocks]"

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the number of connections from [param from_port] of [param "
"from_node]."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o número de conexões a partir de [param from_port] de [param "
"from_node]."

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the points which would make up a connection between [param "
"from_node] and [param to_node]."
msgstr ""
"Retorna os pontos que formariam uma conexão entre [param from_node] e [param "
"to_node]."

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid ""
"Returns an [Array] containing a list of all connections for [param node].\n"
"A connection is represented as a [Dictionary] in the form of:\n"
"[codeblock]\n"
"{\n"
"\tfrom_node: StringName,\n"
"\tfrom_port: int,\n"
"\tto_node: StringName,\n"
"\tto_port: int,\n"
"\tkeep_alive: bool\n"
"}\n"
"[/codeblock]\n"
"[b]Example:[/b] Get all connections on a specific port:\n"
"[codeblock]\n"
"func get_connection_list_from_port(node, port):\n"
"\tvar connections = get_connection_list_from_node(node)\n"
"\tvar result = []\n"
"\tfor connection in connections:\n"
"\t\tvar dict = {}\n"
"\t\tif connection[\"from_node\"] == node and connection[\"from_port\"] == "
"port:\n"
"\t\t\tdict[\"node\"] = connection[\"to_node\"]\n"
"\t\t\tdict[\"port\"] = connection[\"to_port\"]\n"
"\t\t\tdict[\"type\"] = \"left\"\n"
"\t\t\tresult.push_back(dict)\n"
"\t\telif connection[\"to_node\"] == node and connection[\"to_port\"] == "
"port:\n"
"\t\t\tdict[\"node\"] = connection[\"from_node\"]\n"
"\t\t\tdict[\"port\"] = connection[\"from_port\"]\n"
"\t\t\tdict[\"type\"] = \"right\"\n"
"\t\t\tresult.push_back(dict)\n"
"\treturn result\n"
"[/codeblock]"
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid ""
"Returns an [Array] containing the list of connections that intersect with "
"the given [Rect2].\n"
"A connection is represented as a [Dictionary] in the form of:\n"
"[codeblock]\n"
"{\n"
"\tfrom_node: StringName,\n"
"\tfrom_port: int,\n"
"\tto_node: StringName,\n"
"\tto_port: int,\n"
"\tkeep_alive: bool\n"
"}\n"
"[/codeblock]"
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the [GraphFrame] that contains the [GraphElement] with the given "
"name."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o [GraphFrame] que contém o [GraphElement] com o nome fornecido."

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid ""
"Gets the [HBoxContainer] that contains the zooming and grid snap controls in "
"the top left of the graph. You can use this method to reposition the toolbar "
"or to add your own custom controls to it.\n"
"[b]Warning:[/b] This is a required internal node, removing and freeing it "
"may cause a crash. If you wish to hide it or any of its children, use their "
"[member CanvasItem.visible] property."
msgstr ""
"Obtém o [HBoxContainer] que contém os controles de zoom e de atração pela "
"grade no canto superior esquerdo do grafo. Você pode usar este método para "
"reposicionar a barra de ferramentas ou para adicionar seus próprios "
"controles personalizados a ela.\n"
"[b]Aviso:[/b] Este é um nó interno obrigatório. Removê-lo e liberá-lo pode "
"causar uma falha. Se deseja ocultá-lo ou algum dos seus filhos, use a "
"propriedade [member CanvasItem.visible] deles."

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid ""
"Returns [code]true[/code] if the [param from_port] of the [param from_node] "
"[GraphNode] is connected to the [param to_port] of the [param to_node] "
"[GraphNode]."
msgstr ""
"Retorna [code]true[/code] se o [param from_port] do [GraphNode] [param "
"from_node] estiver conectado ao [param to_port] do [GraphNode] [param "
"to_node]."

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid ""
"Returns whether it's possible to make a connection between two different "
"port types. The port type is defined individually for the left and the right "
"port of each slot with the [method GraphNode.set_slot] method.\n"
"See also [method add_valid_connection_type] and [method "
"remove_valid_connection_type]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid ""
"Disallows the connection between two different port types previously allowed "
"by [method add_valid_connection_type]. The port type is defined individually "
"for the left and the right port of each slot with the [method "
"GraphNode.set_slot] method.\n"
"See also [method is_valid_connection_type]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid ""
"Disallows to disconnect nodes when dragging from the left port of the "
"[GraphNode]'s slot if it has the specified type. Use this to disable a "
"disconnection previously allowed with [method "
"add_valid_left_disconnect_type]."
msgstr ""
"Proíbe desconectar nós ao arrastar a partir da porta esquerda do slot do "
"[GraphNode] se ele tiver o tipo especificado. Use isto para desativar uma "
"desconexão previamente permitida com [method add_valid_left_disconnect_type]."

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid ""
"Disallows to disconnect nodes when dragging from the right port of the "
"[GraphNode]'s slot if it has the specified type. Use this to disable a "
"disconnection previously allowed with [method "
"add_valid_right_disconnect_type]."
msgstr ""
"Proíbe desconectar nós ao arrastar a partir da porta direita do slot do "
"[GraphNode] se ele tiver o tipo especificado. Use isto para desativar uma "
"desconexão previamente permitida com [method "
"add_valid_right_disconnect_type]."

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid ""
"Sets the coloration of the connection between [param from_node]'s [param "
"from_port] and [param to_node]'s [param to_port] with the color provided in "
"the [theme_item activity] theme property. The color is linearly interpolated "
"between the connection color and the activity color using [param amount] as "
"weight."
msgstr ""
"Define a coloração da conexão entre o [param from_port] de [param from_node] "
"e o [param to_port] de [param to_node] com a cor fornecida na propriedade de "
"tema [theme_item activity]. A cor é interpolada linearmente entre a cor da "
"conexão e a cor da atividade usando [param amount] como peso."

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid "Sets the specified [param node] as the one selected."
msgstr "Define o [param node] especificado como o selecionado."

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid "If [code]true[/code], the lines between nodes will use antialiasing."
msgstr "Se [code]true[/code], as linhas entre os nós usarão antialiasing."

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid ""
"The curvature of the lines between the nodes. 0 results in straight lines."
msgstr "A curvatura das linhas entre os nós. 0 resulta em linhas retas."

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid "The thickness of the lines between the nodes."
msgstr "A espessura das linhas entre os nós."

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid ""
"The connections between [GraphNode]s.\n"
"A connection is represented as a [Dictionary] in the form of:\n"
"[codeblock]\n"
"{\n"
"\tfrom_node: StringName,\n"
"\tfrom_port: int,\n"
"\tto_node: StringName,\n"
"\tto_port: int,\n"
"\tkeep_alive: bool\n"
"}\n"
"[/codeblock]\n"
"Connections with [code]keep_alive[/code] set to [code]false[/code] may be "
"deleted automatically if invalid during a redraw."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid "The pattern used for drawing the grid."
msgstr "O padrão usado para desenhar a grade."

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid "If [code]true[/code], the minimap is visible."
msgstr "Se [code]true[/code], o minimapa está visível."

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid "The opacity of the minimap rectangle."
msgstr "A opacidade do retângulo do minimapa."

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid ""
"The size of the minimap rectangle. The map itself is based on the size of "
"the grid area and is scaled to fit this rectangle."
msgstr ""
"O tamanho do retângulo do minimapa. O mapa em si é baseado no tamanho da "
"área da grade e é dimensionado para caber neste retângulo."

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid "Defines the control scheme for panning with mouse wheel."
msgstr ""
"Define o esquema de controle para movimentação panorâmica com a roda do "
"mouse."

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid ""
"If [code]true[/code], enables disconnection of existing connections in the "
"GraphEdit by dragging the right end."
msgstr ""
"Se [code]true[/code], ativa a desconexão de conexões existentes no GraphEdit "
"arrastando a extremidade direita."

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid "The scroll offset."
msgstr "O deslocamento de rolagem."

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid ""
"If [code]true[/code], the button to automatically arrange graph nodes is "
"visible."
msgstr ""
"Se [code]true[/code], o botão para organizar nós de grafos automaticamente "
"fica visível."

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid "If [code]true[/code], the grid is visible."
msgstr "Se [code]true[/code], a grade estará visível."

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid ""
"If [code]true[/code], buttons that allow to configure grid and snapping "
"options are visible."
msgstr ""
"Se [code]true[/code], os botões que permitem configurar as opções de grade e "
"alinhamento (snapping) ficam visíveis."

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid "If [code]true[/code], the menu toolbar is visible."
msgstr "Se [code]true[/code], a barra de ferramentas do menu estará visível."

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid "If [code]true[/code], the button to toggle the minimap is visible."
msgstr "Se [code]true[/code], o botão para alternar o minimapa fica visível."

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid ""
"If [code]true[/code], buttons that allow to change and reset the zoom level "
"are visible."
msgstr ""
"Se [code]true[/code], os botões que permitem alterar e redefinir o nível de "
"zoom ficam visíveis."

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid ""
"If [code]true[/code], the label with the current zoom level is visible. The "
"zoom level is displayed in percents."
msgstr ""
"Se [code]true[/code], o rótulo com o nível de zoom atual estará visível. O "
"nível de zoom é exibido em porcentagens."

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid ""
"The snapping distance in pixels, also determines the grid line distance."
msgstr ""
"A distância de ajuste em pixels, também determina a distância da linha da "
"grade."

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid "If [code]true[/code], enables snapping."
msgstr "Se [code]true[/code], ativa o ajuste (snapping)."

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid "[Dictionary] of human-readable port type names."
msgstr "[Dictionary] de nomes de tipos de porta legíveis por humanos."

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid "The current zoom value."
msgstr "O valor atual de zoom."

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid "The upper zoom limit."
msgstr "O limite superior de zoom."

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid "The lower zoom limit."
msgstr "O limite inferior de zoom."

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid "The step of each zoom level."
msgstr "O passo de cada nível de zoom."

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid "Emitted at the beginning of a [GraphElement]'s movement."
msgstr "Emitido no início do movimento de um [GraphElement]."

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid "Emitted at the end of a connection drag."
msgstr "Emitido no final de um arrasto de conexão."

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid "Emitted at the beginning of a connection drag."
msgstr "Emitido no início de um arraste de conexão."

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid ""
"Emitted when user drags a connection from an input port into the empty space "
"of the graph."
msgstr ""
"Emitido quando o usuário arrasta uma conexão de uma porta de entrada para o "
"espaço vazio do grafo."

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid ""
"Emitted to the GraphEdit when the connection between the [param from_port] "
"of the [param from_node] [GraphNode] and the [param to_port] of the [param "
"to_node] [GraphNode] is attempted to be created."
msgstr ""
"Emitido para o GraphEdit quando a conexão entre a [param from_port] do "
"[GraphNode] [param from_node] e a [param to_port] do [GraphNode] [param "
"to_node] é tentada ser criada."

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid ""
"Emitted when user drags a connection from an output port into the empty "
"space of the graph."
msgstr ""
"Emitido quando o usuário arrasta uma conexão de uma porta de saída para o "
"espaço vazio do grafo."

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid ""
"Emitted when this [GraphEdit] captures a [code]ui_copy[/code] action "
"([kbd]Ctrl + C[/kbd] by default). In general, this signal indicates that the "
"selected [GraphElement]s should be copied."
msgstr ""
"Emitido quando este [GraphEdit] captura uma ação [code]ui_copy[/code] "
"([kbd]Ctrl + C[/kbd] por padrão). Em geral, este sinal indica que os "
"[GraphElement]s selecionados devem ser copiados."

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid ""
"Emitted when this [GraphEdit] captures a [code]ui_cut[/code] action "
"([kbd]Ctrl + X[/kbd] by default). In general, this signal indicates that the "
"selected [GraphElement]s should be cut."
msgstr ""
"Emitido quando este [GraphEdit] captura uma ação [code]ui_cut[/code] "
"([kbd]Ctrl + X[/kbd] por padrão). Em geral, este sinal indica que os "
"[GraphElement]s selecionados devem ser cortados."

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid ""
"Emitted when this [GraphEdit] captures a [code]ui_graph_delete[/code] action "
"([kbd]Delete[/kbd] by default).\n"
"[param nodes] is an array of node names that should be removed. These "
"usually include all selected nodes."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid ""
"Emitted to the GraphEdit when the connection between [param from_port] of "
"[param from_node] [GraphNode] and [param to_port] of [param to_node] "
"[GraphNode] is attempted to be removed."
msgstr ""
"Emitido para o GraphEdit quando se tenta remover a conexão entre o [param "
"from_port] de [param from_node] [GraphNode] e o [param to_port] de [param "
"to_node] [GraphNode]."

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid ""
"Emitted when this [GraphEdit] captures a [code]ui_graph_duplicate[/code] "
"action ([kbd]Ctrl + D[/kbd] by default). In general, this signal indicates "
"that the selected [GraphElement]s should be duplicated."
msgstr ""
"Emitido quando este [GraphEdit] captura uma ação [code]ui_graph_duplicate[/"
"code] ([kbd]Ctrl + D[/kbd] por padrão). Em geral, este sinal indica que os "
"[GraphElement]s selecionados devem ser duplicados."

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid "Emitted at the end of a [GraphElement]'s movement."
msgstr "Emitido no final do movimento de um [GraphElement]."

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid ""
"Emitted when the [GraphFrame] [param frame] is resized to [param new_rect]."
msgstr ""
"Emitido quando o [GraphFrame] [param frame] é redimensionado para [param "
"new_rect]."

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid ""
"Emitted when one or more [GraphElement]s are dropped onto the [GraphFrame] "
"named [param frame], when they were not previously attached to any other "
"one.\n"
"[param elements] is an array of [GraphElement]s to be attached."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid "Emitted when the given [GraphElement] node is deselected."
msgstr "Emitido quando o nó [GraphElement] fornecido é desmarcado."

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid "Emitted when the given [GraphElement] node is selected."
msgstr "Emitido quando o nó [GraphElement] fornecido é selecionado."

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid ""
"Emitted when this [GraphEdit] captures a [code]ui_paste[/code] action "
"([kbd]Ctrl + V[/kbd] by default). In general, this signal indicates that "
"previously copied [GraphElement]s should be pasted."
msgstr ""
"Emitido quando este [GraphEdit] captura uma ação [code]ui_paste[/code] "
"([kbd]Ctrl + V[/kbd] por padrão). Em geral, este sinal indica que os "
"[GraphElement]s copiados anteriormente devem ser colados."

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid ""
"Emitted when a popup is requested. Happens on right-clicking in the "
"GraphEdit. [param at_position] is the position of the mouse pointer when the "
"signal is sent."
msgstr ""
"Emitido quando um pop-up é solicitado. Ocorre ao clicar com o botão direito "
"no GraphEdit. [param at_position] é a posição do ponteiro do mouse quando o "
"sinal é enviado."

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid ""
"Emitted when the scroll offset is changed by the user. It will not be "
"emitted when changed in code."
msgstr ""
"Emitido quando o deslocamento da rolagem é alterado pelo usuário. Não será "
"emitido quando alterado via código."

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid ""
"[kbd]Mouse Wheel[/kbd] will zoom, [kbd]Ctrl + Mouse Wheel[/kbd] will move "
"the view."
msgstr ""
"[kbd]Roda do Mouse[/kbd] aplicará zoom, [kbd]Ctrl + Roda do Mouse[/kbd] "
"moverá a visão."

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid ""
"[kbd]Mouse Wheel[/kbd] will move the view, [kbd]Ctrl + Mouse Wheel[/kbd] "
"will zoom."
msgstr ""
"[kbd]Roda do Mouse[/kbd] moverá a visão, [kbd]Ctrl + Roda do Mouse[/kbd] "
"aplicará zoom."

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid "Draw the grid using solid lines."
msgstr "Desenhar a grade usando linhas sólidas."

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid "Draw the grid using dots."
msgstr "Desenhar a grade usando pontos."

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid ""
"Color the connection line is interpolated to based on the activity value of "
"a connection (see [method set_connection_activity])."
msgstr ""
"Cor para a qual a linha de conexão é interpolada com base no valor de "
"atividade de uma conexão (veja [method set_connection_activity])."

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid ""
"Color which is blended with the connection line when the mouse is hovering "
"over it."
msgstr ""
"Cor que é misturada com a linha de conexão quando o mouse passa por cima "
"dela."

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid ""
"Color of the rim around each connection line used for making intersecting "
"lines more distinguishable."
msgstr ""
"Cor da borda ao redor de cada linha de conexão usada para tornar linhas "
"interceptantes mais distinguíveis."

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid ""
"Color which is blended with the connection line when the currently dragged "
"connection is hovering over a valid target port."
msgstr ""
"Cor que é misturada com a linha de conexão quando a conexão arrastada no "
"momento está sobre uma porta de destino válida."

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid "Color of major grid lines/dots."
msgstr "Cor das linhas/pontos da grade principal."

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid "Color of minor grid lines/dots."
msgstr "Cor das linhas/pontos da grade secundária."

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid "The fill color of the selection rectangle."
msgstr "A cor de preenchimento do retângulo de seleção."

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid "The outline color of the selection rectangle."
msgstr "A cor da borda do retângulo de seleção."

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid ""
"Widens the line of a connection when the mouse is hovering over it by a "
"percentage factor. A value of [code]0[/code] disables the highlight. A value "
"of [code]100[/code] doubles the line width."
msgstr ""
"Alarga a linha de uma conexão quando o mouse passa sobre ela por um fator "
"percentual. Um valor de [code]0[/code] desativa o destaque. Um valor de "
"[code]100[/code] dobra a largura da linha."

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid "The horizontal range within which a port can be grabbed (inner side)."
msgstr ""
"O intervalo horizontal dentro do qual uma porta pode ser agarrada (lado "
"interno)."

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid "The horizontal range within which a port can be grabbed (outer side)."
msgstr ""
"O intervalo horizontal dentro do qual uma porta pode ser agarrada (lado "
"externo)."

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid "The icon for the grid toggle button."
msgstr "O ícone para o botão de alternância da grade."

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid "The icon for the layout button for auto-arranging the graph."
msgstr "O ícone para o botão de layout para auto-organização do grafo."

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid "The icon for the minimap toggle button."
msgstr "O ícone para o botão de alternância do minimapa."

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid "The icon for the snapping toggle button."
msgstr "O ícone para o botão de alternância de ajuste."

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid "The icon for the zoom in button."
msgstr "O ícone para o botão de zoom in."

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid "The icon for the zoom out button."
msgstr "O ícone para o botão de zoom out."

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid "The icon for the zoom reset button."
msgstr "O ícone para o botão de redefinição de zoom."

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid "The background drawn under the grid."
msgstr "O fundo desenhado sob a grade."

#: doc/classes/GraphEdit.xml
msgid ""
"[StyleBox] used when the [GraphEdit] is focused (when used with assistive "
"apps)."
msgstr ""
"[StyleBox] usado quando o [GraphEdit] está focado (quando usado com "
"aplicativos assistivos)."

#: doc/classes/GraphElement.xml
msgid ""
"A container that represents a basic element that can be placed inside a "
"[GraphEdit] control."
msgstr ""
"Um contêiner que representa um elemento básico que pode ser colocado dentro "
"de um controle [GraphEdit]."

#: doc/classes/GraphElement.xml
msgid ""
"[GraphElement] allows to create custom elements for a [GraphEdit] graph. By "
"default such elements can be selected, resized, and repositioned, but they "
"cannot be connected. For a graph element that allows for connections see "
"[GraphNode]."
msgstr ""
"[GraphElement] permite criar elementos personalizados para um gráfico "
"[GraphEdit]. Por padrão, esses elementos podem ser selecionados, "
"redimensionados e reposicionados, mas não podem ser conectados. Para um "
"elemento de gráfico que permite conexões, consulte [GraphNode]."

#: doc/classes/GraphElement.xml
msgid "If [code]true[/code], the user can drag the GraphElement."
msgstr "Se [code]true[/code], o usuário pode arrastar o GraphElement."

#: doc/classes/GraphElement.xml
msgid ""
"The offset of the GraphElement, relative to the scroll offset of the "
"[GraphEdit]."
msgstr ""
"O deslocamento (offset) do GraphElement, relativo ao deslocamento de rolagem "
"do [GraphEdit]."

#: doc/classes/GraphElement.xml
msgid ""
"If [code]true[/code], the user can resize the GraphElement.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Dragging the handle will only emit the [signal resize_request] "
"and [signal resize_end] signals, the GraphElement needs to be resized "
"manually."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/GraphElement.xml
msgid ""
"If [code]true[/code], [PopupMenu]s that are descendants of the GraphElement "
"are scaled with the [GraphEdit] zoom."
msgstr ""
"Se [code]true[/code], os [PopupMenu]s que são descendentes do GraphElement "
"são dimensionados com o zoom do [GraphEdit]."

#: doc/classes/GraphElement.xml
msgid "If [code]true[/code], the user can select the GraphElement."
msgstr "Se [code]true[/code], o usuário pode selecionar o GraphElement."

#: doc/classes/GraphElement.xml
msgid "If [code]true[/code], the GraphElement is selected."
msgstr "Se [code]true[/code], o GraphElement está selecionado."

#: doc/classes/GraphElement.xml
msgid "Emitted when removing the GraphElement is requested."
msgstr "Emitido quando a remoção do GraphElement é solicitada."

#: doc/classes/GraphElement.xml
msgid "Emitted when the GraphElement is dragged."
msgstr "Emitido quando o GraphElement é arrastado."

#: doc/classes/GraphElement.xml
msgid "Emitted when the GraphElement is deselected."
msgstr "Emitido quando o GraphElement é desselecionado."

#: doc/classes/GraphElement.xml
msgid "Emitted when the GraphElement is selected."
msgstr "Emitido quando o GraphElement é selecionado."

#: doc/classes/GraphElement.xml
msgid "Emitted when the GraphElement is moved."
msgstr "Emitido quando o GraphElement é movido."

#: doc/classes/GraphElement.xml
msgid ""
"Emitted when displaying the GraphElement over other ones is requested. "
"Happens on focusing (clicking into) the GraphElement."
msgstr ""
"Emitido quando é solicitada a exibição do GraphElement sobre outros. Ocorre "
"ao focar (clicar dentro) no GraphElement."

#: doc/classes/GraphElement.xml
msgid ""
"Emitted when releasing the mouse button after dragging the resizer handle "
"(see [member resizable])."
msgstr ""
"Emitido ao soltar o botão do mouse após arrastar a alça de redimensionamento "
"(veja [member resizable])."

#: doc/classes/GraphElement.xml
msgid ""
"Emitted when resizing the GraphElement is requested. Happens on dragging the "
"resizer handle (see [member resizable])."
msgstr ""
"Emitido quando o redimensionamento do GraphElement é solicitado. Ocorre ao "
"arrastar a alça de redimensionamento (veja [member resizable])."

#: doc/classes/GraphElement.xml
msgid ""
"The icon used for the resizer, visible when [member resizable] is enabled."
msgstr ""
"O ícone usado para o redimensionador, visível quando [member resizable] está "
"ativado."

#: doc/classes/GraphFrame.xml
msgid ""
"GraphFrame is a special [GraphElement] that can be used to organize other "
"[GraphElement]s inside a [GraphEdit]."
msgstr ""
"GraphFrame é um [GraphElement] especial que pode ser usado para organizar "
"outros [GraphElement]s dentro de um [GraphEdit]."

#: doc/classes/GraphFrame.xml
msgid ""
"GraphFrame is a special [GraphElement] to which other [GraphElement]s can be "
"attached. It can be configured to automatically resize to enclose all "
"attached [GraphElement]s. If the frame is moved, all the attached "
"[GraphElement]s inside it will be moved as well.\n"
"A GraphFrame is always kept behind the connection layer and other "
"[GraphElement]s inside a [GraphEdit]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/GraphFrame.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the [HBoxContainer] used for the title bar, only containing a "
"[Label] for displaying the title by default.\n"
"This can be used to add custom controls to the title bar such as option or "
"close buttons."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/GraphFrame.xml
msgid ""
"If [code]true[/code], the frame's rect will be adjusted automatically to "
"enclose all attached [GraphElement]s."
msgstr ""
"Se [code]true[/code], o retângulo do quadro será ajustado automaticamente "
"para envolver todos os [GraphElement]s anexados."

#: doc/classes/GraphFrame.xml
msgid ""
"The margin around the attached nodes that is used to calculate the size of "
"the frame when [member autoshrink_enabled] is [code]true[/code]."
msgstr ""
"A margem ao redor dos nós anexados que é usada para calcular o tamanho do "
"quadro quando [member autoshrink_enabled] é [code]true[/code]."

#: doc/classes/GraphFrame.xml
msgid "The margin inside the frame that can be used to drag the frame."
msgstr "A margem dentro do quadro que pode ser usada para arrastar o quadro."

#: doc/classes/GraphFrame.xml
#: modules/visual_shader/doc_classes/VisualShaderNodeFrame.xml
msgid ""
"The color of the frame when [member tint_color_enabled] is [code]true[/code]."
msgstr ""
"A cor da moldura quando [member tint_color_enabled] é [code]true[/code]."

#: doc/classes/GraphFrame.xml
msgid "If [code]true[/code], the tint color will be used to tint the frame."
msgstr ""
"Se [code]true[/code], a cor de tonalidade será usada para tingir o quadro."

#: doc/classes/GraphFrame.xml
msgid "Title of the frame."
msgstr "Título do quadro."

#: doc/classes/GraphFrame.xml
msgid ""
"Emitted when [member autoshrink_enabled] or [member autoshrink_margin] "
"changes."
msgstr ""
"Emitido quando [member autoshrink_enabled] ou [member autoshrink_margin] é "
"alterado."

#: doc/classes/GraphFrame.xml doc/classes/GraphNode.xml
msgid "The color modulation applied to the resizer icon."
msgstr "A modulação de cor aplicada ao ícone do redimensionador."

#: doc/classes/GraphFrame.xml
msgid "The default [StyleBox] used for the background of the [GraphFrame]."
msgstr "O [StyleBox] padrão usado para o fundo do [GraphFrame]."

#: doc/classes/GraphFrame.xml
msgid ""
"The [StyleBox] used for the background of the [GraphFrame] when it is "
"selected."
msgstr ""
"O [StyleBox] usado para o fundo do [GraphFrame] quando ele está selecionado."

#: doc/classes/GraphFrame.xml
msgid "The [StyleBox] used for the title bar of the [GraphFrame]."
msgstr "O [StyleBox] usado para a barra de título do [GraphFrame]."

#: doc/classes/GraphFrame.xml
msgid ""
"The [StyleBox] used for the title bar of the [GraphFrame] when it is "
"selected."
msgstr ""
"O [StyleBox] usado para a barra de título do [GraphFrame] quando ele está "
"selecionado."

#: doc/classes/GraphNode.xml
msgid ""
"A container with connection ports, representing a node in a [GraphEdit]."
msgstr ""
"Um contêiner com portas de conexão, representando um nó em um [GraphEdit]."

#: doc/classes/GraphNode.xml
msgid ""
"[GraphNode] allows to create nodes for a [GraphEdit] graph with customizable "
"content based on its child controls. [GraphNode] is derived from [Container] "
"and it is responsible for placing its children on screen. This works similar "
"to [VBoxContainer]. Children, in turn, provide [GraphNode] with so-called "
"slots, each of which can have a connection port on either side.\n"
"Each [GraphNode] slot is defined by its index and can provide the node with "
"up to two ports: one on the left, and one on the right. By convention the "
"left port is also referred to as the [b]input port[/b] and the right port is "
"referred to as the [b]output port[/b]. Each port can be enabled and "
"configured individually, using different type and color. The type is an "
"arbitrary value that you can define using your own considerations. The "
"parent [GraphEdit] will receive this information on each connect and "
"disconnect request.\n"
"Slots can be configured in the Inspector dock once you add at least one "
"child [Control]. The properties are grouped by each slot's index in the "
"\"Slot\" section.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] While GraphNode is set up using slots and slot indices, "
"connections are made between the ports which are enabled. Because of that "
"[GraphEdit] uses the port's index and not the slot's index. You can use "
"[method get_input_port_slot] and [method get_output_port_slot] to get the "
"slot index from the port index."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/GraphNode.xml
msgid ""
"Disables all slots of the GraphNode. This will remove all input/output ports "
"from the GraphNode."
msgstr ""
"Desativa todos os slots do GraphNode. Isso removerá todas as portas de "
"entrada/saída do GraphNode."

#: doc/classes/GraphNode.xml
msgid ""
"Disables the slot with the given [param slot_index]. This will remove the "
"corresponding input and output port from the GraphNode."
msgstr ""
"Desativa o slot com o [param slot_index] fornecido. Isso removerá a porta de "
"entrada e saída correspondente do GraphNode."

#: doc/classes/GraphNode.xml
msgid "Returns the [Color] of the input port with the given [param port_idx]."
msgstr "Retorna a [Color] da porta de entrada com o [param port_idx] dado."

#: doc/classes/GraphNode.xml
msgid "Returns the number of slots with an enabled input port."
msgstr "Retorna o número de slots com uma porta de entrada ativada."

#: doc/classes/GraphNode.xml
msgid "Returns the position of the input port with the given [param port_idx]."
msgstr "Retorna a posição da porta de entrada com o [param port_idx] dado."

#: doc/classes/GraphNode.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the corresponding slot index of the input port with the given [param "
"port_idx]."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o índice de slot correspondente da porta de entrada com o [param "
"port_idx] dado."

#: doc/classes/GraphNode.xml
msgid "Returns the type of the input port with the given [param port_idx]."
msgstr "Retorna o tipo da porta de entrada com o [param port_idx] dado."

#: doc/classes/GraphNode.xml
msgid "Returns the [Color] of the output port with the given [param port_idx]."
msgstr "Retorna a [Color] da porta de saída com o [param port_idx] dado."

#: doc/classes/GraphNode.xml
msgid "Returns the number of slots with an enabled output port."
msgstr "Retorna o número de slots com uma porta de saída ativada."

#: doc/classes/GraphNode.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the position of the output port with the given [param port_idx]."
msgstr "Retorna a posição da porta de saída com o [param port_idx] dado."

#: doc/classes/GraphNode.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the corresponding slot index of the output port with the given "
"[param port_idx]."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o índice de slot correspondente da porta de saída com o [param "
"port_idx] dado."

#: doc/classes/GraphNode.xml
msgid "Returns the type of the output port with the given [param port_idx]."
msgstr "Retorna o tipo da porta de saída com o [param port_idx] dado."

#: doc/classes/GraphNode.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the left (input) [Color] of the slot with the given [param "
"slot_index]."
msgstr ""
"Retorna a [Color] esquerda (entrada) do slot com o [param slot_index] dado."

#: doc/classes/GraphNode.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the right (output) [Color] of the slot with the given [param "
"slot_index]."
msgstr ""
"Retorna a [Color] direita (saída) do slot com o [param slot_index] dado."

#: doc/classes/GraphNode.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the left (input) custom [Texture2D] of the slot with the given "
"[param slot_index]."
msgstr ""
"Retorna a [Texture2D] personalizada esquerda (entrada) do slot com o [param "
"slot_index] dado."

#: doc/classes/GraphNode.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the right (output) custom [Texture2D] of the slot with the given "
"[param slot_index]."
msgstr ""
"Retorna a [Texture2D] personalizada direita (saída) do slot com o [param "
"slot_index] dado."

#: doc/classes/GraphNode.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the left (input) metadata of the slot with the given [param "
"slot_index]."
msgstr ""
"Retorna os metadados esquerdos (entrada) do slot com o [param slot_index] "
"dado."

#: doc/classes/GraphNode.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the right (output) metadata of the slot with the given [param "
"slot_index]."
msgstr ""
"Retorna os metadados direitos (saída) do slot com o [param slot_index] dado."

#: doc/classes/GraphNode.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the left (input) type of the slot with the given [param slot_index]."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o tipo esquerdo (entrada) do slot com o [param slot_index] dado."

#: doc/classes/GraphNode.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the right (output) type of the slot with the given [param "
"slot_index]."
msgstr "Retorna o tipo direito (saída) do slot com o [param slot_index] dado."

#: doc/classes/GraphNode.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the [HBoxContainer] used for the title bar, only containing a "
"[Label] for displaying the title by default. This can be used to add custom "
"controls to the title bar such as option or close buttons."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o [HBoxContainer] usado para a barra de título, contendo apenas um "
"[Label] para exibir o título por padrão. Isso pode ser usado para adicionar "
"controles personalizados à barra de título, como botões de opção ou de "
"fechar."

#: doc/classes/GraphNode.xml
msgid ""
"Returns [code]true[/code] if the background [StyleBox] of the slot with the "
"given [param slot_index] is drawn."
msgstr ""
"Retorna [code]true[/code] se o [StyleBox] de fundo do slot com o [param "
"slot_index] fornecido for desenhado."

#: doc/classes/GraphNode.xml
msgid ""
"Returns [code]true[/code] if left (input) side of the slot with the given "
"[param slot_index] is enabled."
msgstr ""
"Retorna [code]true[/code] se o lado esquerdo (entrada) do slot com o [param "
"slot_index] dado estiver ativado."

#: doc/classes/GraphNode.xml
msgid ""
"Returns [code]true[/code] if right (output) side of the slot with the given "
"[param slot_index] is enabled."
msgstr ""
"Retorna [code]true[/code] se o lado direito (saída) do slot com o [param "
"slot_index] dado estiver ativado."

#: doc/classes/GraphNode.xml
msgid ""
"Sets properties of the slot with the given [param slot_index].\n"
"If [param enable_left_port]/[param enable_right_port] is [code]true[/code], "
"a port will appear and the slot will be able to be connected from this "
"side.\n"
"With [param type_left]/[param type_right] an arbitrary type can be assigned "
"to each port. Two ports can be connected if they share the same type, or if "
"the connection between their types is allowed in the parent [GraphEdit] (see "
"[method GraphEdit.add_valid_connection_type]). Keep in mind that the "
"[GraphEdit] has the final say in accepting the connection. Type "
"compatibility simply allows the [signal GraphEdit.connection_request] signal "
"to be emitted.\n"
"Ports can be further customized using [param color_left]/[param color_right] "
"and [param custom_icon_left]/[param custom_icon_right]. The color parameter "
"adds a tint to the icon. The custom icon can be used to override the default "
"port dot.\n"
"Additionally, [param draw_stylebox] can be used to enable or disable drawing "
"of the background stylebox for each slot. See [theme_item slot].\n"
"Individual properties can also be set using one of the [code]set_slot_*[/"
"code] methods.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] This method only sets properties of the slot. To create the "
"slot itself, add a [Control]-derived child to the GraphNode."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/GraphNode.xml
msgid ""
"Sets the [Color] of the left (input) side of the slot with the given [param "
"slot_index] to [param color]."
msgstr ""
"Define a [Color] do lado esquerdo (entrada) do slot com o [param slot_index] "
"dado para [param color]."

#: doc/classes/GraphNode.xml
msgid ""
"Sets the [Color] of the right (output) side of the slot with the given "
"[param slot_index] to [param color]."
msgstr ""
"Define a [Color] do lado direito (saída) do slot com o [param slot_index] "
"dado para [param color]."

#: doc/classes/GraphNode.xml
msgid ""
"Sets the custom [Texture2D] of the left (input) side of the slot with the "
"given [param slot_index] to [param custom_icon]."
msgstr ""
"Define a [Texture2D] personalizada do lado esquerdo (entrada) do slot com o "
"[param slot_index] dado para [param custom_icon]."

#: doc/classes/GraphNode.xml
msgid ""
"Sets the custom [Texture2D] of the right (output) side of the slot with the "
"given [param slot_index] to [param custom_icon]."
msgstr ""
"Define a [Texture2D] personalizada do lado direito (saída) do slot com o "
"[param slot_index] dado para [param custom_icon]."

#: doc/classes/GraphNode.xml
msgid ""
"Toggles the background [StyleBox] of the slot with the given [param "
"slot_index]."
msgstr "Alterna o [StyleBox] de fundo do slot com o [param slot_index] dado."

#: doc/classes/GraphNode.xml
msgid ""
"Toggles the left (input) side of the slot with the given [param slot_index]. "
"If [param enable] is [code]true[/code], a port will appear on the left side "
"and the slot will be able to be connected from this side."
msgstr ""
"Alterna o lado esquerdo (entrada) do slot com o [param slot_index] "
"fornecido. Se [param enable] for [code]true[/code], uma porta aparecerá no "
"lado esquerdo e o slot poderá ser conectado a partir deste lado."

#: doc/classes/GraphNode.xml
msgid ""
"Toggles the right (output) side of the slot with the given [param "
"slot_index]. If [param enable] is [code]true[/code], a port will appear on "
"the right side and the slot will be able to be connected from this side."
msgstr ""
"Alterna o lado direito (saída) do slot com o [param slot_index] fornecido. "
"Se [param enable] for [code]true[/code], uma porta aparecerá no lado direito "
"e o slot poderá ser conectado por este lado."

#: doc/classes/GraphNode.xml
msgid ""
"Sets the custom metadata for the left (input) side of the slot with the "
"given [param slot_index] to [param value]."
msgstr ""
"Define os metadados personalizados para o lado esquerdo (entrada) do slot "
"com o [param slot_index] dado para [param value]."

#: doc/classes/GraphNode.xml
msgid ""
"Sets the custom metadata for the right (output) side of the slot with the "
"given [param slot_index] to [param value]."
msgstr ""
"Define os metadados personalizados para o lado direito (saída) do slot com o "
"[param slot_index] dado para [param value]."

#: doc/classes/GraphNode.xml
msgid ""
"Sets the left (input) type of the slot with the given [param slot_index] to "
"[param type]. If the value is negative, all connections will be disallowed "
"to be created via user inputs."
msgstr ""
"Define o tipo esquerdo (entrada) do slot com o [param slot_index] fornecido "
"para [param type]. Se o valor for negativo, todas as conexões não poderão "
"ser criadas por meio de entradas do usuário."

#: doc/classes/GraphNode.xml
msgid ""
"Sets the right (output) type of the slot with the given [param slot_index] "
"to [param type]. If the value is negative, all connections will be "
"disallowed to be created via user inputs."
msgstr ""
"Define o tipo direito (saída) do slot com o [param slot_index] fornecido "
"para [param type]. Se o valor for negativo, todas as conexões não poderão "
"ser criadas por meio de entradas do usuário."

#: doc/classes/GraphNode.xml
msgid ""
"If [code]true[/code], you can connect ports with different types, even if "
"the connection was not explicitly allowed in the parent [GraphEdit]."
msgstr ""
"Se [code]true[/code], você pode conectar portas com tipos diferentes, mesmo "
"que a conexão não tenha sido explicitamente permitida no [GraphEdit] pai."

#: doc/classes/GraphNode.xml
msgid ""
"Determines how connection slots can be focused.\n"
"- If set to [constant Control.FOCUS_CLICK], connections can only be made "
"with the mouse.\n"
"- If set to [constant Control.FOCUS_ALL], slots can also be focused using "
"the [member ProjectSettings.input/ui_up] and [member ProjectSettings.input/"
"ui_down] and connected using [member ProjectSettings.input/ui_left] and "
"[member ProjectSettings.input/ui_right] input actions.\n"
"- If set to [constant Control.FOCUS_ACCESSIBILITY], slot input actions are "
"only enabled when the screen reader is active."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/GraphNode.xml
msgid "The text displayed in the GraphNode's title bar."
msgstr "O texto exibido na barra de título do GraphNode."

#: doc/classes/GraphNode.xml
msgid "Emitted when any slot's size might have changed."
msgstr "Emitido quando o tamanho de qualquer slot pode ter mudado."

#: doc/classes/GraphNode.xml
msgid "Emitted when any GraphNode's slot is updated."
msgstr "Emitido quando o slot de qualquer GraphNode é atualizado."

#: doc/classes/GraphNode.xml
msgid "Horizontal offset for the ports."
msgstr "Deslocamento horizontal para as portas."

#: doc/classes/GraphNode.xml
msgid "The vertical distance between ports."
msgstr "A distância vertical entre as portas."

#: doc/classes/GraphNode.xml
msgid "The icon used for representing ports."
msgstr "O ícone usado para representar portas."

#: doc/classes/GraphNode.xml
msgid "The default background for the slot area of the [GraphNode]."
msgstr "O fundo padrão para a área de slot do [GraphNode]."

#: doc/classes/GraphNode.xml
msgid ""
"[StyleBox] used when the [GraphNode] is focused (when used with assistive "
"apps)."
msgstr ""
"[StyleBox] usado quando o [GraphNode] está focado (quando usado com "
"aplicativos assistivos)."

#: doc/classes/GraphNode.xml
msgid "The [StyleBox] used for the slot area when selected."
msgstr "O [StyleBox] usado para a área do slot quando selecionado."

#: doc/classes/GraphNode.xml
msgid "The [StyleBox] used for each slot of the [GraphNode]."
msgstr "O [StyleBox] usado para cada slot do [GraphNode]."

#: doc/classes/GraphNode.xml
msgid ""
"[StyleBox] used when the slot is focused (when used with assistive apps)."
msgstr ""
"[StyleBox] usado quando o slot está focado (quando usado com aplicativos "
"assistivos)."

#: doc/classes/GraphNode.xml
msgid "The [StyleBox] used for the title bar of the [GraphNode]."
msgstr "O [StyleBox] usado para a barra de título do [GraphNode]."

#: doc/classes/GraphNode.xml
msgid ""
"The [StyleBox] used for the title bar of the [GraphNode] when it is selected."
msgstr ""
"O [StyleBox] usado para a barra de título do [GraphNode] quando ele está "
"selecionado."

#: doc/classes/GridContainer.xml
msgid "A container that arranges its child controls in a grid layout."
msgstr "Um contêiner que organiza seus controles filhos em um layout de grade."

#: doc/classes/GridContainer.xml
msgid ""
"[GridContainer] arranges its child controls in a grid layout. The number of "
"columns is specified by the [member columns] property, whereas the number of "
"rows depends on how many are needed for the child controls. The number of "
"rows and columns is preserved for every size of the container.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] [GridContainer] only works with child nodes inheriting from "
"[Control]. It won't rearrange child nodes inheriting from [Node2D]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/GridContainer.xml
msgid ""
"The number of columns in the [GridContainer]. If modified, [GridContainer] "
"reorders its Control-derived children to accommodate the new layout."
msgstr ""
"O número de colunas no [GridContainer]. Se modificado, o [GridContainer] "
"reordena seus filhos derivados de Control para acomodar o novo layout."

#: modules/gridmap/doc_classes/GridMap.xml
msgid "Node for 3D tile-based maps."
msgstr "Nó para mapas 3D baseados em mosaicos."

#: modules/gridmap/doc_classes/GridMap.xml
msgid ""
"GridMap lets you place meshes on a grid interactively. It works both from "
"the editor and from scripts, which can help you create in-game level "
"editors.\n"
"GridMaps use a [MeshLibrary] which contains a list of tiles. Each tile is a "
"mesh with materials plus optional collision and navigation shapes.\n"
"A GridMap contains a collection of cells. Each grid cell refers to a tile in "
"the [MeshLibrary]. All cells in the map have the same dimensions.\n"
"Internally, a GridMap is split into a sparse collection of octants for "
"efficient rendering and physics processing. Every octant has the same "
"dimensions and can contain several cells.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] GridMap doesn't extend [VisualInstance3D] and therefore can't "
"be hidden or cull masked based on [member VisualInstance3D.layers]. If you "
"make a light not affect the first layer, the whole GridMap won't be lit by "
"the light in question."
msgstr ""

#: modules/gridmap/doc_classes/GridMap.xml
msgid "Using gridmaps"
msgstr "Usando mapas de malha"

#: modules/gridmap/doc_classes/GridMap.xml
msgid "Clear all cells."
msgstr "Limpar todas as células."

#: modules/gridmap/doc_classes/GridMap.xml
msgid "Clears all baked meshes. See [method make_baked_meshes]."
msgstr "Limpa todas as malhas geradas. Veja [method make_baked_meshes]."

#: modules/gridmap/doc_classes/GridMap.xml
msgid "Returns [RID] of a baked mesh with the given [param idx]."
msgstr "Retorna o [RID] de uma malha gerada com o [param idx] fornecido."

#: modules/gridmap/doc_classes/GridMap.xml
msgid ""
"Returns an array of [ArrayMesh]es and [Transform3D] references of all bake "
"meshes that exist within the current GridMap. Even indices contain "
"[ArrayMesh]es, while odd indices contain [Transform3D]s that are always "
"equal to [constant Transform3D.IDENTITY].\n"
"This method relies on the output of [method make_baked_meshes], which will "
"be called with [code]gen_lightmap_uv[/code] set to [code]true[/code] and "
"[code]lightmap_uv_texel_size[/code] set to [code]0.1[/code] if it hasn't "
"been called yet."
msgstr ""

#: modules/gridmap/doc_classes/GridMap.xml
msgid ""
"Returns one of 24 possible rotations that lie along the vectors (x,y,z) with "
"each component being either -1, 0, or 1. For further details, refer to the "
"Godot source code."
msgstr ""
"Retorna uma das 24 rotações possíveis que se encontram ao longo dos vetores "
"(x,y,z) com cada componente sendo -1, 0 ou 1. Para mais detalhes, consulte o "
"código-fonte do Godot."

#: modules/gridmap/doc_classes/GridMap.xml
msgid ""
"The [MeshLibrary] item index located at the given grid coordinates. If the "
"cell is empty, [constant INVALID_CELL_ITEM] will be returned."
msgstr ""
"O índice de item do [MeshLibrary] localizado nas coordenadas de grade "
"fornecidas. Se a célula estiver vazia, [constant INVALID_CELL_ITEM] será "
"retornado."

#: modules/gridmap/doc_classes/GridMap.xml
msgid "Returns the basis that gives the specified cell its orientation."
msgstr "Retorna a base que dá à célula especificada sua orientação."

#: modules/gridmap/doc_classes/GridMap.xml
msgid ""
"The orientation of the cell at the given grid coordinates. [code]-1[/code] "
"is returned if the cell is empty."
msgstr ""
"A orientação da célula nas coordenadas de grade dadas. [code]-1[/code] é "
"retornado se a célula estiver vazia."

#: modules/gridmap/doc_classes/GridMap.xml
msgid ""
"Returns an array of [Transform3D] and [Mesh] references corresponding to the "
"non-empty cells in the grid. The transforms are specified in local space. "
"Even indices contain [Transform3D]s, while odd indices contain [Mesh]es "
"related to the [Transform3D] in the index preceding it."
msgstr ""
"Retorna um array de referências a [Transform3D] e [Mesh] correspondentes às "
"células não vazias na grade. As transformações são especificadas no espaço "
"local. Índices pares contêm [Transform3D]s, enquanto índices ímpares contêm "
"[Mesh]es relacionados ao [Transform3D] no índice que o antecede."

#: modules/gridmap/doc_classes/GridMap.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the [RID] of the navigation map this GridMap node uses for its cell "
"baked navigation meshes.\n"
"This function returns always the map set on the GridMap node and not the map "
"on the NavigationServer. If the map is changed directly with the "
"NavigationServer API the GridMap node will not be aware of the map change."
msgstr ""

#: modules/gridmap/doc_classes/GridMap.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the [Vector3i] octant coordinates of the octant that the cell at "
"[param cell_coords] belongs to."
msgstr ""
"Retorna as coordenadas de octante [Vector3i] do octante ao qual a célula em "
"[param cell_coords] pertence."

#: modules/gridmap/doc_classes/GridMap.xml
msgid ""
"Returns an array of [Vector3i] octant coordinates that are inside the given "
"[param bounds], including octants that have no cells in use."
msgstr ""
"Retorna uma matriz de coordenadas de octante [Vector3i] que estão dentro dos "
"[param bounds] fornecidos, incluindo octantes que não possuem células em uso."

#: modules/gridmap/doc_classes/GridMap.xml
msgid ""
"This function considers a discretization of rotations into 24 points on unit "
"sphere, lying along the vectors (x,y,z) with each component being either -1, "
"0, or 1, and returns the index (in the range from 0 to 23) of the point best "
"representing the orientation of the object. For further details, refer to "
"the Godot source code."
msgstr ""
"Esta função considera uma discretização de rotações em 24 pontos na esfera "
"unitária, localizados ao longo dos vetores (x,y,z) com cada componente sendo "
"-1, 0 ou 1, e retorna o índice (no intervalo de 0 a 23) do ponto que melhor "
"representa a orientação do objeto. Para mais detalhes, consulte o código-"
"fonte do Godot."

#: modules/gridmap/doc_classes/GridMap.xml
msgid ""
"Returns an array of [Vector3] with the non-empty cell coordinates in the "
"grid map."
msgstr ""
"Retorna uma matriz de [Vector3] com as coordenadas de célula não vazias no "
"mapa de grade."

#: modules/gridmap/doc_classes/GridMap.xml
msgid ""
"Returns an array of all cells with the given item index specified in [param "
"item]."
msgstr ""
"Retorna uma matriz de todas as células com o índice de item dado "
"especificado em [param item]."

#: modules/gridmap/doc_classes/GridMap.xml
msgid ""
"Returns an array of [Vector3i]s with the cell coordinates of non-empty cells "
"inside the octant at [param octant_coords]."
msgstr ""
"Retorna um array de [Vector3i] com as coordenadas de célula de células não "
"vazias dentro do octante em [param octant_coords]."

#: modules/gridmap/doc_classes/GridMap.xml
msgid ""
"Returns an array of [Vector3i]s with the cell coordinates of cells inside "
"the octant at [param octant_coords] that use the specified cell [param item]."
msgstr ""
"Retorna um array de [Vector3i]s com as coordenadas de célula das células "
"dentro do octante em [param octant_coords] que usam o [param item] de célula "
"especificado."

#: modules/gridmap/doc_classes/GridMap.xml
msgid ""
"Returns an array of [Vector3i]s with the octant coordinates of the non-empty "
"octants in the grid map."
msgstr ""
"Retorna um array de [Vector3i] com as coordenadas de octante dos octantes "
"não vazios no mapa de grade."

#: modules/gridmap/doc_classes/GridMap.xml
msgid ""
"Returns an array of [Vector3i]s with the octant coordinates of the octants "
"that use the specified [param item] in the grid map."
msgstr ""
"Retorna uma matriz de [Vector3i] com as coordenadas de octante dos octantes "
"que usam o [param item] especificado no mapa de grade."

#: modules/gridmap/doc_classes/GridMap.xml
msgid ""
"Returns an array of [Vector3i]s with the octant coordinates of non-empty "
"octants that are inside the local [param bounds]."
msgstr ""
"Retorna uma matriz de [Vector3i]s com as coordenadas de octantes de octantes "
"não vazios que estão dentro do [param bounds] local."

#: modules/gridmap/doc_classes/GridMap.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the map coordinates of the cell containing the given [param "
"local_position]. If [param local_position] is in global coordinates, "
"consider using [method Node3D.to_local] before passing it to this method. "
"See also [method map_to_local]."
msgstr ""
"Retorna as coordenadas do mapa da célula que contém o [param local_position] "
"fornecido. Se [param local_position] estiver em coordenadas globais, "
"considere usar [method Node3D.to_local] antes de passá-lo para este método. "
"Consulte também [method map_to_local]."

#: modules/gridmap/doc_classes/GridMap.xml
msgid ""
"Generates a baked mesh that represents all meshes in the assigned "
"[MeshLibrary] for use with [LightmapGI]. If [param gen_lightmap_uv] is "
"[code]true[/code], UV2 data will be generated for each mesh currently used "
"in the [GridMap]. Otherwise, only meshes that already have UV2 data present "
"will be able to use baked lightmaps. When generating UV2, [param "
"lightmap_uv_texel_size] controls the texel density for lightmaps, with lower "
"values resulting in more detailed lightmaps. [param lightmap_uv_texel_size] "
"is ignored if [param gen_lightmap_uv] is [code]false[/code]. See also "
"[method get_bake_meshes], which relies on the output of this method.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Calling this method will not actually bake lightmaps, as "
"lightmap baking is performed using the [LightmapGI] node."
msgstr ""

#: modules/gridmap/doc_classes/GridMap.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the position of a grid cell in the GridMap's local coordinate space. "
"To convert the returned value into global coordinates, use [method "
"Node3D.to_global]. See also [method local_to_map]."
msgstr ""
"Retorna a posição de uma célula da grade no espaço de coordenadas locais do "
"GridMap. Para converter o valor retornado em coordenadas globais, use "
"[method Node3D.to_global]. Veja também [method local_to_map]."

#: modules/gridmap/doc_classes/GridMap.xml
msgid ""
"Sets the mesh index for the cell referenced by its grid coordinates.\n"
"A negative item index such as [constant INVALID_CELL_ITEM] will clear the "
"cell.\n"
"Optionally, the item's orientation can be passed. For valid orientation "
"values, see [method get_orthogonal_index_from_basis]."
msgstr ""

#: modules/gridmap/doc_classes/GridMap.xml
msgid ""
"Sets the [RID] of the navigation map this GridMap node should use for its "
"cell baked navigation meshes."
msgstr ""
"Define o [RID] do mapa de navegação que este nó GridMap deve usar para suas "
"malhas de navegação geradas por célula."

#: modules/gridmap/doc_classes/GridMap.xml
msgid ""
"If [code]true[/code], this GridMap creates a navigation region for each cell "
"that uses a [member mesh_library] item with a navigation mesh. The created "
"navigation region will use the navigation layers bitmask assigned to the "
"[MeshLibrary]'s item."
msgstr ""
"Se [code]true[/code], este GridMap cria uma região de navegação para cada "
"célula que usa um item [member mesh_library] com uma malha de navegação. A "
"região de navegação criada usará a máscara de bits de camadas de navegação "
"atribuída ao item do [MeshLibrary]."

#: modules/gridmap/doc_classes/GridMap.xml
msgid "If [code]true[/code], grid items are centered on the X axis."
msgstr "Se [code]true[/code], os itens da grade são centralizados no eixo X."

#: modules/gridmap/doc_classes/GridMap.xml
msgid "If [code]true[/code], grid items are centered on the Y axis."
msgstr "Se [code]true[/code], os itens da grade são centralizados no eixo Y."

#: modules/gridmap/doc_classes/GridMap.xml
msgid "If [code]true[/code], grid items are centered on the Z axis."
msgstr "Se [code]true[/code], os itens da grade são centralizados no eixo Z."

#: modules/gridmap/doc_classes/GridMap.xml
msgid ""
"The size of each octant measured in number of cells. This applies to all "
"three axis."
msgstr ""
"O tamanho de cada octante medido em número de células. Isso se aplica a "
"todos os três eixos."

#: modules/gridmap/doc_classes/GridMap.xml
msgid ""
"The scale of the cell items.\n"
"This does not affect the size of the grid cells themselves, only the items "
"in them. This can be used to make cell items overlap their neighbors."
msgstr ""

#: modules/gridmap/doc_classes/GridMap.xml
msgid ""
"The dimensions of the grid's cells.\n"
"This does not affect the size of the meshes. See [member cell_scale]."
msgstr ""

#: modules/gridmap/doc_classes/GridMap.xml
msgid ""
"The physics layers this GridMap is in.\n"
"GridMaps act as static bodies, meaning they aren't affected by gravity or "
"other forces. They only affect other physics bodies that collide with them."
msgstr ""

#: modules/gridmap/doc_classes/GridMap.xml
msgid ""
"The physics layers this GridMap detects collisions in. See [url=$DOCS_URL/"
"tutorials/physics/physics_introduction.html#collision-layers-and-"
"masks]Collision layers and masks[/url] in the documentation for more "
"information."
msgstr ""
"As camadas de física em que este GridMap detecta colisões. Veja "
"[url=$DOCS_URL/tutorials/physics/physics_introduction.html#collision-layers-"
"and-masks]Collision layers and masks[/url] na documentação para obter mais "
"informações."

#: modules/gridmap/doc_classes/GridMap.xml
msgid ""
"Show or hide the [GridMap]'s collision shapes. If set to [constant "
"DEBUG_VISIBILITY_MODE_DEFAULT], this depends on the show collision debug "
"settings."
msgstr ""
"Mostra ou oculta as formas de colisão do [GridMap]. Se definido como "
"[constant DEBUG_VISIBILITY_MODE_DEFAULT], isso depende das configurações de "
"depuração de colisão de exibição."

#: modules/gridmap/doc_classes/GridMap.xml
msgid "The assigned [MeshLibrary]."
msgstr "O [MeshLibrary] atribuído."

#: modules/gridmap/doc_classes/GridMap.xml
msgid ""
"Overrides the default friction and bounce physics properties for the whole "
"[GridMap]."
msgstr ""
"Substitui as propriedades físicas padrão de atrito e ressalto para todo o "
"[GridMap]."

#: modules/gridmap/doc_classes/GridMap.xml
msgid "Emitted when [member cell_size] changes."
msgstr "Emitido quando [member cell_size] muda."

#: modules/gridmap/doc_classes/GridMap.xml
msgid "Emitted when the [MeshLibrary] of this GridMap changes."
msgstr "Emitido quando o [MeshLibrary] deste GridMap muda."

#: modules/gridmap/doc_classes/GridMap.xml
msgid ""
"Invalid cell item that can be used in [method set_cell_item] to clear cells "
"(or represent an empty cell in [method get_cell_item])."
msgstr ""
"Item de célula inválido que pode ser usado em [method set_cell_item] para "
"limpar células (ou representar uma célula vazia em [method get_cell_item])."

#: modules/gridmap/doc_classes/GridMap.xml
msgid ""
"Hide the collisions debug shapes in the editor, and use the debug settings "
"to determine their visibility in game (i.e. [member "
"SceneTree.debug_collisions_hint] or [member "
"SceneTree.debug_navigation_hint])."
msgstr ""
"Oculta as formas de depuração de colisões no editor e usa as configurações "
"de depuração para determinar sua visibilidade no jogo (ou seja, [member "
"SceneTree.debug_collisions_hint] ou [member "
"SceneTree.debug_navigation_hint])."

#: modules/gridmap/doc_classes/GridMap.xml
msgid "Always show the collisions debug shapes."
msgstr "Sempre mostrar as formas de depuração de colisões."

#: modules/gridmap/doc_classes/GridMap.xml
msgid "Always hide the collisions debug shapes."
msgstr "Sempre ocultar as formas de depuração de colisões."

#: modules/gridmap/doc_classes/GridMapEditorPlugin.xml
msgid "Editor for [GridMap] nodes."
msgstr "Editor para nós [GridMap]."

#: modules/gridmap/doc_classes/GridMapEditorPlugin.xml
msgid ""
"GridMapEditorPlugin provides access to the [GridMap] editor functionality."
msgstr ""
"O GridMapEditorPlugin fornece acesso à funcionalidade do editor [GridMap]."

#: modules/gridmap/doc_classes/GridMapEditorPlugin.xml
msgid "Deselects any currently selected cells."
msgstr "Desseleciona quaisquer células selecionadas no momento."

#: modules/gridmap/doc_classes/GridMapEditorPlugin.xml
msgid "Returns the [GridMap] node currently edited by the grid map editor."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o nó [GridMap] atualmente editado pelo editor de mapas de grade."

#: modules/gridmap/doc_classes/GridMapEditorPlugin.xml
msgid "Returns an array of [Vector3i]s with the selected cells' coordinates."
msgstr ""
"Retorna um array de [Vector3i] com as coordenadas das células selecionadas."

#: modules/gridmap/doc_classes/GridMapEditorPlugin.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the index of the selected [MeshLibrary] item in the grid map "
"editor's palette or [code]-1[/code] if no item is selected.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] The indices might not be in the same order as they appear in "
"the editor's interface."
msgstr ""

#: modules/gridmap/doc_classes/GridMapEditorPlugin.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the cell coordinate bounds of the current selection. Use [method "
"has_selection] to check if there is an active selection."
msgstr ""
"Retorna os limites de coordenadas de célula da seleção atual. Use [method "
"has_selection] para verificar se há uma seleção ativa."

#: modules/gridmap/doc_classes/GridMapEditorPlugin.xml
msgid "Returns [code]true[/code] if there are selected cells."
msgstr "Retorna [code]true[/code] se houver células selecionadas."

#: modules/gridmap/doc_classes/GridMapEditorPlugin.xml
msgid ""
"Selects the [MeshLibrary] item with the given index in the grid map editor's "
"palette. If a negative index is given, no item will be selected. If a value "
"greater than the last index is given, the last item will be selected.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] The indices might not be in the same order as they appear in "
"the editor's interface."
msgstr ""

#: modules/gridmap/doc_classes/GridMapEditorPlugin.xml
msgid ""
"Selects the cells inside the given bounds from [param begin] to [param end]."
msgstr ""
"Seleciona as células dentro dos limites dados de [param begin] a [param end]."

#: doc/classes/GrooveJoint2D.xml
