msgstr "Concavidade máxima. Varia de [code]0.0[/code] a [code]1.0[/code]."

#: doc/classes/MeshConvexDecompositionSettings.xml
msgid "The maximum number of convex hulls to produce from the merge operation."
msgstr ""
"O número máximo de cascos convexos a serem produzidos a partir da operação "
"de mesclagem."

#: doc/classes/MeshConvexDecompositionSettings.xml
msgid ""
"Controls the maximum number of triangles per convex-hull. Ranges from "
"[code]4[/code] to [code]1024[/code]."
msgstr ""
"Controla o número máximo de triângulos por casco convexo. Varia de [code]4[/"
"code] a [code]1024[/code]."

#: doc/classes/MeshConvexDecompositionSettings.xml
msgid ""
"Controls the adaptive sampling of the generated convex-hulls. Ranges from "
"[code]0.0[/code] to [code]0.01[/code]."
msgstr ""
"Controla a amostragem adaptativa dos cascos convexos gerados. Varia de "
"[code]0.0[/code] a [code]0.01[/code]."

#: doc/classes/MeshConvexDecompositionSettings.xml
msgid "Mode for the approximate convex decomposition."
msgstr "Modo para a decomposição convexa aproximada."

#: doc/classes/MeshConvexDecompositionSettings.xml
msgid ""
"If [code]true[/code], normalizes the mesh before applying the convex "
"decomposition."
msgstr ""
"Se [code]true[/code], normaliza a malha antes de aplicar a decomposição "
"convexa."

#: doc/classes/MeshConvexDecompositionSettings.xml
msgid ""
"Controls the granularity of the search for the \"best\" clipping plane. "
"Ranges from [code]1[/code] to [code]16[/code]."
msgstr ""
"Controla a granularidade da busca pelo \"melhor\" plano de corte. Varia de "
"[code]1[/code] a [code]16[/code]."

#: doc/classes/MeshConvexDecompositionSettings.xml
msgid ""
"If [code]true[/code], projects output convex hull vertices onto the original "
"source mesh to increase floating-point accuracy of the results."
msgstr ""
"Se [code]true[/code], projeta os vértices do casco convexo de saída na malha "
"de origem original para aumentar a precisão de ponto flutuante dos "
"resultados."

#: doc/classes/MeshConvexDecompositionSettings.xml
msgid "Maximum number of voxels generated during the voxelization stage."
msgstr "Número máximo de voxels gerados durante o estágio de voxelização."

#: doc/classes/MeshConvexDecompositionSettings.xml
msgid ""
"Controls the bias toward clipping along revolution axes. Ranges from "
"[code]0.0[/code] to [code]1.0[/code]."
msgstr ""
"Controla o viés em direção ao corte ao longo dos eixos de revolução. Varia "
"de [code]0.0[/code] a [code]1.0[/code]."

#: doc/classes/MeshConvexDecompositionSettings.xml
msgid ""
"Controls the bias toward clipping along symmetry planes. Ranges from "
"[code]0.0[/code] to [code]1.0[/code]."
msgstr ""
"Controla o viés em direção ao corte ao longo dos planos de simetria. Varia "
"de [code]0.0[/code] a [code]1.0[/code]."

#: doc/classes/MeshConvexDecompositionSettings.xml
msgid "Constant for voxel-based approximate convex decomposition."
msgstr "Constante para decomposição convexa aproximada baseada em voxels."

#: doc/classes/MeshConvexDecompositionSettings.xml
msgid "Constant for tetrahedron-based approximate convex decomposition."
msgstr "Constante para decomposição convexa aproximada baseada em tetraedros."

#: doc/classes/MeshDataTool.xml
msgid "Helper tool to access and edit [Mesh] data."
msgstr "Ferramenta auxiliar para acessar e editar dados de [Mesh]."

#: doc/classes/MeshDataTool.xml
msgid ""
"MeshDataTool provides access to individual vertices in a [Mesh]. It allows "
"users to read and edit vertex data of meshes. It also creates an array of "
"faces and edges.\n"
"To use MeshDataTool, load a mesh with [method create_from_surface]. When you "
"are finished editing the data commit the data to a mesh with [method "
"commit_to_surface].\n"
"Below is an example of how MeshDataTool may be used.\n"
"[codeblocks]\n"
"[gdscript]\n"
"var mesh = ArrayMesh.new()\n"
"mesh.add_surface_from_arrays(Mesh.PRIMITIVE_TRIANGLES, "
"BoxMesh.new().get_mesh_arrays())\n"
"var mdt = MeshDataTool.new()\n"
"mdt.create_from_surface(mesh, 0)\n"
"for i in range(mdt.get_vertex_count()):\n"
"\tvar vertex = mdt.get_vertex(i)\n"
"\t# In this example we extend the mesh by one unit, which results in "
"separated faces as it is flat shaded.\n"
"\tvertex += mdt.get_vertex_normal(i)\n"
"\t# Save your change.\n"
"\tmdt.set_vertex(i, vertex)\n"
"mesh.clear_surfaces()\n"
"mdt.commit_to_surface(mesh)\n"
"var mi = MeshInstance.new()\n"
"mi.mesh = mesh\n"
"add_child(mi)\n"
"[/gdscript]\n"
"[csharp]\n"
"var mesh = new ArrayMesh();\n"
"mesh.AddSurfaceFromArrays(Mesh.PrimitiveType.Triangles, new "
"BoxMesh().GetMeshArrays());\n"
"var mdt = new MeshDataTool();\n"
"mdt.CreateFromSurface(mesh, 0);\n"
"for (var i = 0; i < mdt.GetVertexCount(); i++)\n"
"{\n"
"\tVector3 vertex = mdt.GetVertex(i);\n"
"\t// In this example we extend the mesh by one unit, which results in "
"separated faces as it is flat shaded.\n"
"\tvertex += mdt.GetVertexNormal(i);\n"
"\t// Save your change.\n"
"\tmdt.SetVertex(i, vertex);\n"
"}\n"
"mesh.ClearSurfaces();\n"
"mdt.CommitToSurface(mesh);\n"
"var mi = new MeshInstance();\n"
"mi.Mesh = mesh;\n"
"AddChild(mi);\n"
"[/csharp]\n"
"[/codeblocks]\n"
"See also [ArrayMesh], [ImmediateMesh] and [SurfaceTool] for procedural "
"geometry generation.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Godot uses clockwise [url=https://learnopengl.com/Advanced-"
"OpenGL/Face-culling]winding order[/url] for front faces of triangle "
"primitive modes."
msgstr ""
"O MeshDataTool fornece acesso a vértices individuais em um [Mesh]. Ele "
"permite que os usuários leiam e editem dados de vértices de malhas. Ele "
"também cria um array de faces e arestas.\n"
"Para usar o MeshDataTool, carregue uma malha com [method "
"create_from_surface]. Quando terminar de editar os dados, confirme os dados "
"em uma malha com [method commit_to_surface].\n"
"Abaixo está um exemplo de como o MeshDataTool pode ser usado.\n"
"[codeblocks]\n"
"[gdscript]\n"
"var mesh = ArrayMesh.new()\n"
"mesh.add_surface_from_arrays(Mesh.PRIMITIVE_TRIANGLES, "
"BoxMesh.new().get_mesh_arrays())\n"
"var mdt = MeshDataTool.new()\n"
"mdt.create_from_surface(mesh, 0)\n"
"for i in range(mdt.get_vertex_count()):\n"
"\tvar vertex = mdt.get_vertex(i)\n"
"\t# Neste exemplo, estendemos a malha em uma unidade, o que resulta em faces "
"separadas, pois ela usa sombreamento plano.\n"
"\tvertex += mdt.get_vertex_normal(i)\n"
"\t# Salve sua alteração.\n"
"\tmdt.set_vertex(i, vertex)\n"
"mesh.clear_surfaces()\n"
"mdt.commit_to_surface(mesh)\n"
"var mi = MeshInstance.new()\n"
"mi.mesh = mesh\n"
"add_child(mi)\n"
"[/gdscript]\n"
"[csharp]\n"
"var mesh = new ArrayMesh();\n"
"mesh.AddSurfaceFromArrays(Mesh.PrimitiveType.Triangles, new "
"BoxMesh().GetMeshArrays());\n"
"var mdt = new MeshDataTool();\n"
"mdt.CreateFromSurface(mesh, 0);\n"
"for (var i = 0; i < mdt.GetVertexCount(); i++)\n"
"{\n"
"\tVector3 vertex = mdt.GetVertex(i);\n"
"\t// Neste exemplo, estendemos a malha em uma unidade, o que resulta em "
"faces separadas, pois ela usa sombreamento plano.\n"
"\tvertex += mdt.GetVertexNormal(i);\n"
"\t// Salve sua alteração.\n"
"\tmdt.SetVertex(i, vertex);\n"
"}\n"
"mesh.ClearSurfaces();\n"
"mdt.CommitToSurface(mesh);\n"
"var mi = new MeshInstance();\n"
"mi.Mesh = mesh;\n"
"AddChild(mi);\n"
"[/csharp]\n"
"[/codeblocks]\n"
"Veja também [ArrayMesh], [ImmediateMesh] e [SurfaceTool] para geração de "
"geometria procedural.\n"
"[b]Nota:[/b] O Godot usa a [url=https://learnopengl.com/Advanced-OpenGL/Face-"
"culling]ordem de enrolamento[/url] no sentido horário para as faces frontais "
"dos modos primitivos de triângulo."

#: doc/classes/MeshDataTool.xml
msgid "Using the MeshDataTool"
msgstr "Usando o MeshDataTool"

#: doc/classes/MeshDataTool.xml
msgid "Clears all data currently in MeshDataTool."
msgstr "Limpa todos os dados atualmente no MeshDataTool."

#: doc/classes/MeshDataTool.xml
msgid "Adds a new surface to specified [Mesh] with edited data."
msgstr ""
"Adiciona uma nova superfície ao [Mesh] especificado com dados editados."

#: doc/classes/MeshDataTool.xml
msgid ""
"Uses specified surface of given [Mesh] to populate data for MeshDataTool.\n"
"Requires [Mesh] with primitive type [constant Mesh.PRIMITIVE_TRIANGLES]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/MeshDataTool.xml
msgid "Returns the number of edges in this [Mesh]."
msgstr "Retorna o número de arestas neste [Mesh]."

#: doc/classes/MeshDataTool.xml
msgid "Returns array of faces that touch given edge."
msgstr "Retorna a matriz de faces que tocam a aresta fornecida."

#: doc/classes/MeshDataTool.xml
msgid "Returns meta information assigned to given edge."
msgstr "Retorna informações de metadados atribuídas à aresta fornecida."

#: doc/classes/MeshDataTool.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the index of the specified [param vertex] connected to the edge at "
"index [param idx].\n"
"[param vertex] can only be [code]0[/code] or [code]1[/code], as edges are "
"composed of two vertices."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/MeshDataTool.xml
msgid "Returns the number of faces in this [Mesh]."
msgstr "Retorna o número de faces neste [Mesh]."

#: doc/classes/MeshDataTool.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the edge associated with the face at index [param idx].\n"
"[param edge] argument must be either [code]0[/code], [code]1[/code], or "
"[code]2[/code] because a face only has three edges."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/MeshDataTool.xml
msgid "Returns the metadata associated with the given face."
msgstr "Retorna os metadados associados à face fornecida."

#: doc/classes/MeshDataTool.xml
msgid "Calculates and returns the face normal of the given face."
msgstr "Calcula e retorna a normal da face da face dada."

#: doc/classes/MeshDataTool.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the specified vertex index of the given face.\n"
"[param vertex] must be either [code]0[/code], [code]1[/code], or [code]2[/"
"code] because faces contain three vertices.\n"
"[codeblocks]\n"
"[gdscript]\n"
"var index = mesh_data_tool.get_face_vertex(0, 1) # Gets the index of the "
"second vertex of the first face.\n"
"var position = mesh_data_tool.get_vertex(index)\n"
"var normal = mesh_data_tool.get_vertex_normal(index)\n"
"[/gdscript]\n"
"[csharp]\n"
"int index = meshDataTool.GetFaceVertex(0, 1); // Gets the index of the "
"second vertex of the first face.\n"
"Vector3 position = meshDataTool.GetVertex(index);\n"
"Vector3 normal = meshDataTool.GetVertexNormal(index);\n"
"[/csharp]\n"
"[/codeblocks]"
msgstr ""
"Retorna o índice de vértice especificado da face fornecida.\n"
"[param vertex] deve ser [code]0[/code], [code]1[/code] ou [code]2[/code], "
"pois as faces contêm três vértices.\n"
"[codeblocks]\n"
"[gdscript]\n"
"var index = mesh_data_tool.get_face_vertex(0, 1) # Obtém o índice do segundo "
"vértice da primeira face.\n"
"var position = mesh_data_tool.get_vertex(index)\n"
"var normal = mesh_data_tool.get_vertex_normal(index)\n"
"[/gdscript]\n"
"[csharp]\n"
"int index = meshDataTool.GetFaceVertex(0, 1); // Obtém o índice do segundo "
"vértice da primeira face.\n"
"Vector3 position = meshDataTool.GetVertex(index);\n"
"Vector3 normal = meshDataTool.GetVertexNormal(index);\n"
"[/csharp]\n"
"[/codeblocks]"

#: doc/classes/MeshDataTool.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the [Mesh]'s format as a combination of the [enum Mesh.ArrayFormat] "
"flags. For example, a mesh containing both vertices and normals would return "
"a format of [code]3[/code] because [constant Mesh.ARRAY_FORMAT_VERTEX] is "
"[code]1[/code] and [constant Mesh.ARRAY_FORMAT_NORMAL] is [code]2[/code]."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o formato do [Mesh] como uma combinação das flags do [enum "
"Mesh.ArrayFormat]. Por exemplo, uma malha contendo vértices e normais "
"retornaria um formato de [code]3[/code] porque [constant "
"Mesh.ARRAY_FORMAT_VERTEX] é [code]1[/code] e [constant "
"Mesh.ARRAY_FORMAT_NORMAL] é [code]2[/code]."

#: doc/classes/MeshDataTool.xml
msgid "Returns the material assigned to the [Mesh]."
msgstr "Retorna o material atribuído ao [Mesh]."

#: doc/classes/MeshDataTool.xml
msgid "Returns the position of the given vertex."
msgstr "Retorna a posição do vértice fornecido."

#: doc/classes/MeshDataTool.xml
msgid "Returns the bones of the given vertex."
msgstr "Retorna os ossos do vértice fornecido."

#: doc/classes/MeshDataTool.xml
msgid "Returns the color of the given vertex."
msgstr "Retorna a cor do vértice fornecido."

#: doc/classes/MeshDataTool.xml
msgid "Returns the total number of vertices in [Mesh]."
msgstr "Retorna o número total de vértices no [Mesh]."

#: doc/classes/MeshDataTool.xml
msgid "Returns an array of edges that share the given vertex."
msgstr "Retorna um array de arestas que compartilham o vértice fornecido."

#: doc/classes/MeshDataTool.xml
msgid "Returns an array of faces that share the given vertex."
msgstr "Retorna um array de faces que compartilham o vértice fornecido."

#: doc/classes/MeshDataTool.xml
msgid "Returns the metadata associated with the given vertex."
msgstr "Retorna os metadados associados ao vértice fornecido."

#: doc/classes/MeshDataTool.xml
msgid "Returns the normal of the given vertex."
msgstr "Retorna a normal do vértice fornecido."

#: doc/classes/MeshDataTool.xml
msgid "Returns the tangent of the given vertex."
msgstr "Retorna a tangente do vértice fornecido."

#: doc/classes/MeshDataTool.xml
msgid "Returns the UV of the given vertex."
msgstr "Retorna a UV do vértice fornecido."

#: doc/classes/MeshDataTool.xml
msgid "Returns the UV2 of the given vertex."
msgstr "Retorna o UV2 do vértice fornecido."

#: doc/classes/MeshDataTool.xml
msgid "Returns bone weights of the given vertex."
msgstr "Retorna os pesos dos ossos do vértice fornecido."

#: doc/classes/MeshDataTool.xml
msgid "Sets the metadata of the given edge."
msgstr "Define os metadados da aresta fornecida."

#: doc/classes/MeshDataTool.xml
msgid "Sets the metadata of the given face."
msgstr "Define os metadados da face fornecida."

#: doc/classes/MeshDataTool.xml
msgid "Sets the material to be used by newly-constructed [Mesh]."
msgstr "Define o material a ser usado por [Mesh] recém-construídos."

#: doc/classes/MeshDataTool.xml
msgid "Sets the position of the given vertex."
msgstr "Define a posição do vértice fornecido."

#: doc/classes/MeshDataTool.xml
msgid "Sets the bones of the given vertex."
msgstr "Define os ossos do vértice fornecido."

#: doc/classes/MeshDataTool.xml
msgid "Sets the color of the given vertex."
msgstr "Define a cor do vértice fornecido."

#: doc/classes/MeshDataTool.xml
msgid "Sets the metadata associated with the given vertex."
msgstr "Define os metadados associados ao vértice fornecido."

#: doc/classes/MeshDataTool.xml
msgid "Sets the normal of the given vertex."
msgstr "Define a normal do vértice fornecido."

#: doc/classes/MeshDataTool.xml
msgid ""
"Sets the tangent of the given vertex.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Even though [param tangent] is a [Plane], it does not directly "
"represent the tangent plane. Its [member Plane.x], [member Plane.y], and "
"[member Plane.z] represent the tangent vector and [member Plane.d] should be "
"either [code]-1[/code] or [code]1[/code]. See also [constant "
"Mesh.ARRAY_TANGENT]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/MeshDataTool.xml
msgid "Sets the UV of the given vertex."
msgstr "Define as UV do vértice fornecido."

#: doc/classes/MeshDataTool.xml
msgid "Sets the UV2 of the given vertex."
msgstr "Define a UV2 do vértice fornecido."

#: doc/classes/MeshDataTool.xml
msgid "Sets the bone weights of the given vertex."
msgstr "Define os pesos dos ossos do vértice fornecido."

#: doc/classes/MeshInstance2D.xml
msgid "Node used for displaying a [Mesh] in 2D."
msgstr "Nó usado para exibir um [Mesh] em 2D."

#: doc/classes/MeshInstance2D.xml
msgid ""
"Node used for displaying a [Mesh] in 2D. This can be faster to render "
"compared to displaying a [Sprite2D] node with large transparent areas, "
"especially if the node takes up a lot of space on screen at high viewport "
"resolutions. This is because using a mesh designed to fit the sprite's "
"opaque areas will reduce GPU fill rate utilization (at the cost of increased "
"vertex processing utilization).\n"
"When a [Mesh] has to be instantiated more than thousands of times close to "
"each other, consider using a [MultiMesh] in a [MultiMeshInstance2D] "
"instead.\n"
"A [MeshInstance2D] can be created from an existing [Sprite2D] via a tool in "
"the editor toolbar. Select the [Sprite2D] node, then choose [b]Sprite2D > "
"Convert to MeshInstance2D[/b] at the top of the 2D editor viewport."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/MeshInstance2D.xml
msgid "2D meshes"
msgstr "Malhas 2D"

#: doc/classes/MeshInstance2D.xml
msgid "The [Mesh] that will be drawn by the [MeshInstance2D]."
msgstr "O [Mesh] que será desenhado pelo [MeshInstance2D]."

#: doc/classes/MeshInstance2D.xml doc/classes/MultiMeshInstance2D.xml
msgid ""
"The [Texture2D] that will be used if using the default [CanvasItemMaterial]. "
"Can be accessed as [code]TEXTURE[/code] in CanvasItem shader."
msgstr ""
"O [Texture2D] que será usado ao usar o [CanvasItemMaterial] padrão. Pode ser "
"acessado como [code]TEXTURE[/code] no shader do CanvasItem."

#: doc/classes/MeshInstance2D.xml doc/classes/MultiMeshInstance2D.xml
msgid "Emitted when the [member texture] is changed."
msgstr "Emitido quando a [member texture] muda."

#: doc/classes/MeshInstance3D.xml
msgid "Node that instances meshes into a scenario."
msgstr "Nó que instancia malhas em um cenário."

#: doc/classes/MeshInstance3D.xml
msgid ""
"MeshInstance3D is a node that takes a [Mesh] resource and adds it to the "
"current scenario by creating an instance of it. This is the class most often "
"used to render 3D geometry and can be used to instance a single [Mesh] in "
"many places. This allows reusing geometry, which can save on resources. When "
"a [Mesh] has to be instantiated more than thousands of times at close "
"proximity, consider using a [MultiMesh] in a [MultiMeshInstance3D] instead."
msgstr ""
"MeshInstance3D é um nó que pega um recurso [Mesh] e o adiciona ao cenário "
"atual criando uma instância dele. Esta é a classe mais usada para renderizar "
"geometria 3D e pode ser usada para instanciar um único [Mesh] em vários "
"lugares. Isso permite reutilizar a geometria, o que pode economizar "
"recursos. Quando um [Mesh] precisa ser instanciado mais de milhares de vezes "
"em proximidade, considere usar um [MultiMesh] em um [MultiMeshInstance3D] em "
"vez disso."

#: doc/classes/MeshInstance3D.xml
msgid ""
"Takes a snapshot from the current [ArrayMesh] with all blend shapes applied "
"according to their current weights and bakes it to the provided [param "
"existing] mesh. If no [param existing] mesh is provided a new [ArrayMesh] is "
"created, baked and returned. Mesh surface materials are not copied.\n"
"[b]Performance:[/b] [Mesh] data needs to be received from the GPU, stalling "
"the [RenderingServer] in the process."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/MeshInstance3D.xml
msgid ""
"Takes a snapshot of the current animated skeleton pose of the skinned mesh "
"and bakes it to the provided [param existing] mesh. If no [param existing] "
"mesh is provided a new [ArrayMesh] is created, baked, and returned. Requires "
"a skeleton with a registered skin to work. Blendshapes are ignored. Mesh "
"surface materials are not copied.\n"
"[b]Performance:[/b] [Mesh] data needs to be retrieved from the GPU, stalling "
"the [RenderingServer] in the process."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/MeshInstance3D.xml
msgid ""
"This helper creates a [StaticBody3D] child node with a "
"[ConvexPolygonShape3D] collision shape calculated from the mesh geometry. "
"It's mainly used for testing.\n"
"If [param clean] is [code]true[/code] (default), duplicate and interior "
"vertices are removed automatically. You can set it to [code]false[/code] to "
"make the process faster if not needed.\n"
"If [param simplify] is [code]true[/code], the geometry can be further "
"simplified to reduce the number of vertices. Disabled by default."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/MeshInstance3D.xml
msgid ""
"This helper creates a [MeshInstance3D] child node with gizmos at every "
"vertex calculated from the mesh geometry. It's mainly used for testing."
msgstr ""
"Este auxiliar cria um nó filho [MeshInstance3D] com gizmos em cada vértice "
"calculado a partir da geometria da malha. É usado principalmente para testes."

#: doc/classes/MeshInstance3D.xml
msgid ""
"This helper creates a [StaticBody3D] child node with multiple "
"[ConvexPolygonShape3D] collision shapes calculated from the mesh geometry "
"via convex decomposition. The convex decomposition operation can be "
"controlled with parameters from the optional [param settings]."
msgstr ""
"Este auxiliar cria um nó filho [StaticBody3D] com várias formas de colisão "
"[ConvexPolygonShape2D] calculadas a partir da geometria da malha por meio de "
"decomposição convexa. A operação de decomposição convexa pode ser controlada "
"com parâmetros de [param settings] opcional."

#: doc/classes/MeshInstance3D.xml
msgid ""
"This helper creates a [StaticBody3D] child node with a "
"[ConcavePolygonShape3D] collision shape calculated from the mesh geometry. "
"It's mainly used for testing."
msgstr ""
"Este auxiliar cria um nó filho [StaticBody3D] com uma forma de colisão "
"[ConcavePolygonShape3D] calculada a partir da geometria da malha. É usado "
"principalmente para testes."

#: doc/classes/MeshInstance3D.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the index of the blend shape with the given [param name]. Returns "
"[code]-1[/code] if no blend shape with this name exists, including when "
"[member mesh] is [code]null[/code]."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o índice da forma de mesclagem com o [param name] fornecido. Retorna "
"[code]-1[/code] se nenhuma forma de mesclagem com este nome existir, "
"inclusive quando [member mesh] for [code]null[/code]."

#: doc/classes/MeshInstance3D.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the [Material] that will be used by the [Mesh] when drawing. This "
"can return the [member GeometryInstance3D.material_override], the surface "
"override [Material] defined in this [MeshInstance3D], or the surface "
"[Material] defined in the [member mesh]. For example, if [member "
"GeometryInstance3D.material_override] is used, all surfaces will return the "
"override material.\n"
"Returns [code]null[/code] if no material is active, including when [member "
"mesh] is [code]null[/code]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/MeshInstance3D.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the number of blend shapes available. Produces an error if [member "
"mesh] is [code]null[/code]."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o número de formas de mesclagem disponíveis. Produz um erro se "
"[member mesh] for [code]null[/code]."

#: doc/classes/MeshInstance3D.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the value of the blend shape at the given [param blend_shape_idx]. "
"Returns [code]0.0[/code] and produces an error if [member mesh] is "
"[code]null[/code] or doesn't have a blend shape at that index."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o valor da forma de mesclagem no [param blend_shape_idx] dado. "
"Retorna [code]0.0[/code] e produz um erro se [member mesh] for [code]null[/"
"code] ou não tiver uma forma de mesclagem nesse índice."

#: doc/classes/MeshInstance3D.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the internal [SkinReference] containing the skeleton's [RID] "
"attached to this RID. See also [method Resource.get_rid], [method "
"SkinReference.get_skeleton], and [method "
"RenderingServer.instance_attach_skeleton]."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o [SkinReference] interno contendo o [RID] do esqueleto anexado a "
"este RID. Veja também [method Resource.get_rid], [method "
"SkinReference.get_skeleton] e [method "
"RenderingServer.instance_attach_skeleton]."

#: doc/classes/MeshInstance3D.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the override [Material] for the specified [param surface] of the "
"[Mesh] resource. See also [method get_surface_override_material_count].\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] This returns the [Material] associated to the "
"[MeshInstance3D]'s Surface Material Override properties, not the material "
"within the [Mesh] resource. To get the material within the [Mesh] resource, "
"use [method Mesh.surface_get_material] instead."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/MeshInstance3D.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the number of surface override materials. This is equivalent to "
"[method Mesh.get_surface_count]. See also [method "
"get_surface_override_material]."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o número de materiais de substituição de superfície. Isso é "
"equivalente a [method Mesh.get_surface_count]. Veja também [method "
"get_surface_override_material]."

#: doc/classes/MeshInstance3D.xml
msgid ""
"Sets the value of the blend shape at [param blend_shape_idx] to [param "
"value]. Produces an error if [member mesh] is [code]null[/code] or doesn't "
"have a blend shape at that index."
msgstr ""
"Define o valor da forma de mesclagem em [param blend_shape_idx] para [param "
"value]. Produz um erro se [member mesh] for [code]null[/code] ou não tiver "
"uma forma de mesclagem nesse índice."

#: doc/classes/MeshInstance3D.xml
msgid ""
"Sets the override [param material] for the specified [param surface] of the "
"[Mesh] resource. This material is associated with this [MeshInstance3D] "
"rather than with [member mesh].\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] This assigns the [Material] associated to the "
"[MeshInstance3D]'s Surface Material Override properties, not the material "
"within the [Mesh] resource. To set the material within the [Mesh] resource, "
"use [method Mesh.surface_set_material] instead."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/MeshInstance3D.xml
msgid "The [Mesh] resource for the instance."
msgstr "O recurso [Mesh] para a instância."

#: doc/classes/MeshInstance3D.xml
msgid ""
"[NodePath] to the [Skeleton3D] associated with the instance.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] The default value of this property has changed in Godot 4.6. "
"Enable [member ProjectSettings.animation/compatibility/"
"default_parent_skeleton_in_mesh_instance_3d] if the old behavior is needed "
"for compatibility."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/MeshInstance3D.xml
msgid "The [Skin] to be used by this instance."
msgstr "O [Skin] a ser usado por esta instância."

#: doc/classes/MeshLibrary.xml
msgid "Library of meshes."
msgstr "Biblioteca de malhas."

#: doc/classes/MeshLibrary.xml
msgid ""
"A library of meshes. Contains a list of [Mesh] resources, each with a name "
"and ID. Each item can also include collision and navigation shapes. This "
"resource is used in [GridMap]."
msgstr ""
"Uma biblioteca de malhas. Contém uma lista de recursos [Mesh], cada um com "
"um nome e ID. Cada item também pode incluir formas de colisão e navegação. "
"Este recurso é usado em [GridMap]."

#: doc/classes/MeshLibrary.xml
msgid "Clears the library."
msgstr "Limpa a biblioteca."

#: doc/classes/MeshLibrary.xml
msgid ""
"Creates a new item in the library with the given ID.\n"
"You can get an unused ID from [method get_last_unused_item_id]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/MeshLibrary.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the first item with the given name, or [code]-1[/code] if no item is "
"found."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o primeiro item com o nome fornecido, ou [code]-1[/code] se nenhum "
"item for encontrado."

#: doc/classes/MeshLibrary.xml
msgid "Returns the number of items present in the library."
msgstr "Retorna o número de itens presentes na biblioteca."

#: doc/classes/MeshLibrary.xml
msgid "Returns the list of item IDs in use."
msgstr "Retorna a lista de IDs de itens em uso."

#: doc/classes/MeshLibrary.xml
msgid "Returns the item's mesh."
msgstr "Retorna a malha do item."

#: doc/classes/MeshLibrary.xml
msgid "Returns the item's shadow casting mode."
msgstr "Retorna o modo de projeção de sombra do item."

#: doc/classes/MeshLibrary.xml
msgid "Returns the transform applied to the item's mesh."
msgstr "Retorna a transformação aplicada à malha do item."

#: doc/classes/MeshLibrary.xml
msgid "Returns the item's name."
msgstr "Retorna o nome do item."

#: doc/classes/MeshLibrary.xml
msgid "Returns the item's navigation layers bitmask."
msgstr "Retorna a máscara de bits das camadas de navegação do item."

#: doc/classes/MeshLibrary.xml
msgid "Returns the item's navigation mesh."
msgstr "Retorna a malha de navegação do item."

#: doc/classes/MeshLibrary.xml
msgid "Returns the transform applied to the item's navigation mesh."
msgstr "Retorna a transformação aplicada à malha de navegação do item."

#: doc/classes/MeshLibrary.xml
msgid ""
"When running in the editor, returns a generated item preview (a 3D rendering "
"in isometric perspective). When used in a running project, returns the "
"manually-defined item preview which can be set using [method "
"set_item_preview]. Returns an empty [Texture2D] if no preview was manually "
"set in a running project."
msgstr ""
"Ao rodar no editor, retorna uma pré-visualização de item gerada (uma "
"renderização 3D em perspectiva isométrica). Quando usado em um projeto em "
"execução, retorna a pré-visualização de item definida manualmente, que pode "
"ser configurada usando [method set_item_preview]. Retorna um [Texture2D] "
"vazio se nenhuma pré-visualização foi definida manualmente em um projeto em "
"execução."

#: doc/classes/MeshLibrary.xml
msgid ""
"Returns an item's collision shapes.\n"
"The array consists of each [Shape3D] followed by its [Transform3D]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/MeshLibrary.xml
msgid "Gets an unused ID for a new item."
msgstr "Obtém um ID não utilizado para um novo item."

#: doc/classes/MeshLibrary.xml
msgid "Removes the item."
msgstr "Remove o item."

#: doc/classes/MeshLibrary.xml
msgid "Sets the item's mesh."
msgstr "Define a malha do item."

#: doc/classes/MeshLibrary.xml
msgid "Sets the item's shadow casting mode to [param shadow_casting_setting]."
msgstr ""
"Define o modo de projeção de sombra do item como [param "
"shadow_casting_setting]."

#: doc/classes/MeshLibrary.xml
msgid "Sets the transform to apply to the item's mesh."
msgstr "Define a transformação a ser aplicada à malha do item."

#: doc/classes/MeshLibrary.xml
msgid ""
"Sets the item's name.\n"
"This name is shown in the editor. It can also be used to look up the item "
"later using [method find_item_by_name]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/MeshLibrary.xml
msgid "Sets the item's navigation layers bitmask."
msgstr "Define a máscara de bits das camadas de navegação do item."

#: doc/classes/MeshLibrary.xml
msgid "Sets the item's navigation mesh."
msgstr "Define a malha de navegação do item."

#: doc/classes/MeshLibrary.xml
msgid "Sets the transform to apply to the item's navigation mesh."
msgstr "Define a transformação a ser aplicada à malha de navegação do item."

#: doc/classes/MeshLibrary.xml
msgid "Sets a texture to use as the item's preview icon in the editor."
msgstr ""
"Define uma textura para ser usada como o ícone de visualização do item no "
"editor."

#: doc/classes/MeshLibrary.xml
msgid ""
"Sets an item's collision shapes.\n"
"The array should consist of [Shape3D] objects, each followed by a "
"[Transform3D] that will be applied to it. For shapes that should not have a "
"transform, use [constant Transform3D.IDENTITY]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/MeshTexture.xml
msgid "Simple texture that uses a mesh to draw itself."
msgstr "Textura simples que usa uma malha para se desenhar."

#: doc/classes/MeshTexture.xml
msgid ""
"Simple texture that uses a mesh to draw itself. It's limited because flags "
"can't be changed and region drawing is not supported."
msgstr ""
"Textura simples que usa uma malha para se desenhar. É limitada porque os "
"andares não podem ser alterados e o desenho de região não é compatível."

#: doc/classes/MeshTexture.xml
msgid "Sets the base texture that the Mesh will use to draw."
msgstr "Define a textura base que o Mesh usará para desenhar."

#: doc/classes/MeshTexture.xml
msgid "Sets the size of the image, needed for reference."
msgstr "Define o tamanho da imagem, necessário para referência."

#: doc/classes/MeshTexture.xml
msgid "Sets the mesh used to draw. It must be a mesh using 2D vertices."
msgstr ""
"Define a malha usada para desenhar. Ela deve ser uma malha usando vértices "
"2D."

#: doc/classes/MethodTweener.xml
msgid ""
"Interpolates an abstract value and supplies it to a method called over time."
msgstr ""
"Interpola um valor abstrato e o fornece a um método chamado ao longo do "
"tempo."

#: doc/classes/MethodTweener.xml
msgid ""
"[MethodTweener] is similar to a combination of [CallbackTweener] and "
"[PropertyTweener]. It calls a method providing an interpolated value as a "
"parameter. See [method Tween.tween_method] for more usage information.\n"
"The tweener will finish automatically if the callback's target object is "
"freed.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] [method Tween.tween_method] is the only correct way to create "
"[MethodTweener]. Any [MethodTweener] created manually will not function "
"correctly."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/MethodTweener.xml
msgid ""
"Sets the time in seconds after which the [MethodTweener] will start "
"interpolating. By default there's no delay."
msgstr ""
"Define o tempo em segundos após o qual o [MethodTweener] começará a "
"interpolar. Por padrão, não há atraso."

#: doc/classes/MethodTweener.xml doc/classes/PropertyTweener.xml
msgid ""
"Sets the type of used easing from [enum Tween.EaseType]. If not set, the "
"default easing is used from the [Tween] that contains this Tweener."
msgstr ""
"Define o tipo de atenuação usado a partir de [enum Tween.EaseType]. Se não "
"for definido, a atenuação padrão do [Tween] que contém este Tweener será "
"usada."

#: doc/classes/MethodTweener.xml doc/classes/PropertyTweener.xml
msgid ""
"Sets the type of used transition from [enum Tween.TransitionType]. If not "
"set, the default transition is used from the [Tween] that contains this "
"Tweener."
msgstr ""
"Define o tipo de transição usada a partir de [enum Tween.TransitionType]. Se "
"não for definida, a transição padrão será usada a partir do [Tween] que "
"contém este Tweener."

#: doc/classes/MissingNode.xml
msgid ""
"An internal editor class intended for keeping the data of unrecognized nodes."
msgstr ""
"Uma classe de editor interna destinada a manter os dados de nós não "
"reconhecidos."

#: doc/classes/MissingNode.xml
msgid ""
"This is an internal editor class intended for keeping data of nodes of "
"unknown type (most likely this type was supplied by an extension that is no "
"longer loaded). It can't be manually instantiated or placed in a scene.\n"
"[b]Warning:[/b] Ignore missing nodes unless you know what you are doing. "
"Existing properties on a missing node can be freely modified in code, "
"regardless of the type they are intended to be."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/MissingNode.xml
msgid ""
"The name of the class this node was supposed to be (see [method "
"Object.get_class])."
msgstr ""
"O nome da classe que este nó deveria ser (consulte [method "
"Object.get_class])."

#: doc/classes/MissingNode.xml
msgid "Returns the path of the scene this node was instance of originally."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o caminho da cena da qual este nó foi originalmente instanciado."

#: doc/classes/MissingNode.xml
msgid ""
"If [code]true[/code], allows new properties to be set along with existing "
"ones. If [code]false[/code], only existing properties' values can be set, "
"and new properties cannot be added."
msgstr ""
"Se [code]true[/code], permite que novas propriedades sejam definidas junto "
"com as existentes. Se [code]false[/code], apenas os valores das propriedades "
"existentes podem ser definidos, e novas propriedades não podem ser "
"adicionadas."

#: doc/classes/MissingNode.xml
msgid ""
"If [code]true[/code], allows new signals to be connected to along with "
"existing ones. If [code]false[/code], only existing signals can be connected "
"to, and new signals cannot be added."
msgstr ""
"Se [code]true[/code], permite que novos sinais sejam conectados junto com os "
"existentes. Se [code]false[/code], apenas os sinais existentes podem ser "
"conectados, e novos sinais não podem ser adicionados."

#: doc/classes/MissingResource.xml
msgid ""
"An internal editor class intended for keeping the data of unrecognized "
"resources."
msgstr ""
"Uma classe de editor interna destinada a manter os dados de recursos não "
"reconhecidos."

#: doc/classes/MissingResource.xml
msgid ""
"This is an internal editor class intended for keeping data of resources of "
"unknown type (most likely this type was supplied by an extension that is no "
"longer loaded). It can't be manually instantiated or placed in a scene.\n"
"[b]Warning:[/b] Ignore missing resources unless you know what you are doing. "
"Existing properties on a missing resource can be freely modified in code, "
"regardless of the type they are intended to be."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/MissingResource.xml
msgid ""
"The name of the class this resource was supposed to be (see [method "
"Object.get_class])."
msgstr ""
"O nome da classe que este recurso deveria ser (consulte [method "
"Object.get_class])."

#: doc/classes/MissingResource.xml
msgid ""
"If set to [code]true[/code], allows new properties to be added on top of the "
"existing ones with [method Object.set]."
msgstr ""
"Se definido como [code]true[/code], permite que novas propriedades sejam "
"adicionadas sobre as existentes com [method Object.set]."

#: modules/mobile_vr/doc_classes/MobileVRInterface.xml
msgid "Generic mobile VR implementation."
msgstr "Implementação genérica de RV móvel."

#: modules/mobile_vr/doc_classes/MobileVRInterface.xml
msgid ""
"This is a generic mobile VR implementation where you need to provide details "
"about the phone and HMD used. It does not rely on any existing framework. "
"This is the most basic interface we have. For the best effect, you need a "
"mobile phone with a gyroscope and accelerometer.\n"
"Note that even though there is no positional tracking, the camera will "
"assume the headset is at a height of 1.85 meters. You can change this by "
"setting [member eye_height].\n"
"You can initialize this interface as follows:\n"
"[codeblock]\n"
"var interface = XRServer.find_interface(\"Native mobile\")\n"
"if interface and interface.initialize():\n"
"\tget_viewport().use_xr = true\n"
"[/codeblock]\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] For Android, [member ProjectSettings.input_devices/sensors/"
"enable_accelerometer], [member ProjectSettings.input_devices/sensors/"
"enable_gravity], [member ProjectSettings.input_devices/sensors/"
"enable_gyroscope] and [member ProjectSettings.input_devices/sensors/"
"enable_magnetometer] must be enabled."
msgstr ""

#: modules/mobile_vr/doc_classes/MobileVRInterface.xml
msgid ""
"The distance between the display and the lenses inside of the device in "
"centimeters."
msgstr ""
"A distância entre o visor e as lentes dentro do dispositivo em centímetros."

#: modules/mobile_vr/doc_classes/MobileVRInterface.xml
msgid "The width of the display in centimeters."
msgstr "A largura do visor em centímetros."

#: modules/mobile_vr/doc_classes/MobileVRInterface.xml
msgid ""
"The height at which the camera is placed in relation to the ground (i.e. "
"[XROrigin3D] node)."
msgstr ""
"A altura em que a câmera é colocada em relação ao solo (ou seja, nó "
"[XROrigin3D])."

#: modules/mobile_vr/doc_classes/MobileVRInterface.xml
msgid ""
"The interocular distance, also known as the interpupillary distance. The "
"distance between the pupils of the left and right eye."
msgstr ""
"A distância interocular, também conhecida como distância interpupilar. A "
"distância entre as pupilas do olho esquerdo e direito."

#: modules/mobile_vr/doc_classes/MobileVRInterface.xml
msgid ""
"The k1 lens factor is one of the two constants that define the strength of "
"the lens used and directly influences the lens distortion effect."
msgstr ""
"O fator de lente k1 é uma das duas constantes que definem a força da lente "
"usada e influencia diretamente o efeito de distorção da lente."

#: modules/mobile_vr/doc_classes/MobileVRInterface.xml
msgid "The k2 lens factor, see k1."
msgstr "O fator de lente k2, veja k1."

#: modules/mobile_vr/doc_classes/MobileVRInterface.xml
msgid ""
"Set the offset rect relative to the area being rendered. A length of 1 "
"represents the whole rendering area on that axis."
msgstr ""
"Define o retângulo de deslocamento em relação à área que está sendo "
"renderizada. Um comprimento de 1 representa toda a área de renderização "
"nesse eixo."

#: modules/mobile_vr/doc_classes/MobileVRInterface.xml
msgid ""
"The oversample setting. Because of the lens distortion we have to render our "
"buffers at a higher resolution then the screen can natively handle. A value "
"between 1.5 and 2.0 often provides good results but at the cost of "
"performance."
msgstr ""
"A configuração de oversampling. Devido à distorção da lente, temos que "
"renderizar nossos buffers em uma resolução maior do que a tela pode "
"manipular nativamente. Um valor entre 1.5 e 2.0 geralmente fornece bons "
"resultados, mas ao custo de desempenho."

#: modules/mobile_vr/doc_classes/MobileVRInterface.xml
#: modules/openxr/doc_classes/OpenXRInterface.xml
msgid ""
"The minimum radius around the focal point where full quality is guaranteed "
"if VRS is used as a percentage of screen size.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Mobile and Forward+ renderers only. Requires [member "
"Viewport.vrs_mode] to be set to [constant Viewport.VRS_XR]."
msgstr ""

#: modules/mobile_vr/doc_classes/MobileVRInterface.xml
#: modules/openxr/doc_classes/OpenXRInterface.xml
msgid ""
"The strength used to calculate the VRS density map. The greater this value, "
"the more noticeable VRS is. This improves performance at the cost of "
"quality.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Mobile and Forward+ renderers only. Requires [member "
"Viewport.vrs_mode] to be set to [constant Viewport.VRS_XR]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/ModifierBoneTarget3D.xml
msgid ""
"А node that dynamically copies the 3D transform of a bone in its parent "
"[Skeleton3D]."
msgstr ""
"Um nó que copia dinamicamente a transformação 3D de um osso em seu "
"[Skeleton3D] pai."

#: doc/classes/ModifierBoneTarget3D.xml
msgid ""
"This node selects a bone in a [Skeleton3D] and attaches to it. This means "
"that the [ModifierBoneTarget3D] node will dynamically copy the 3D transform "
"of the selected bone.\n"
"The functionality is similar to [BoneAttachment3D], but this node adopts the "
"[SkeletonModifier3D] cycle and is intended to be used as another "
"[SkeletonModifier3D]'s target."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/MovieWriter.xml
msgid "Abstract class for non-real-time video recording encoders."
msgstr ""
"Classe abstrata para codificadores de gravação de vídeo em tempo não real."

#: doc/classes/MovieWriter.xml
msgid ""
"Godot can record videos with non-real-time simulation. Like the [code]--"
"fixed-fps[/code] [url=$DOCS_URL/tutorials/editor/"
"command_line_tutorial.html]command line argument[/url], this forces the "
"reported [code]delta[/code] in [method Node._process] functions to be "
"identical across frames, regardless of how long it actually took to render "
"the frame. This can be used to record high-quality videos with perfect frame "
"pacing regardless of your hardware's capabilities.\n"
"Godot has 3 built-in [MovieWriter]s:\n"
"- OGV container with Theora for video and Vorbis for audio ([code].ogv[/"
"code] file extension). Lossy compression, medium file sizes, fast encoding. "
"The lossy compression quality can be adjusted by changing [member "
"ProjectSettings.editor/movie_writer/video_quality] and [member "
"ProjectSettings.editor/movie_writer/ogv/audio_quality]. The resulting file "
"can be viewed in Godot with [VideoStreamPlayer] and most video players, but "
"not web browsers as they don't support Theora.\n"
"- AVI container with MJPEG for video and uncompressed audio ([code].avi[/"
"code] file extension). Lossy compression, medium file sizes, fast encoding. "
"The lossy compression quality can be adjusted by changing [member "
"ProjectSettings.editor/movie_writer/video_quality]. The resulting file can "
"be viewed in most video players, but it must be converted to another format "
"for viewing on the web or by Godot with [VideoStreamPlayer]. MJPEG does not "
"support transparency. AVI output is currently limited to a file of 4 GB in "
"size at most.\n"
"- PNG image sequence for video and WAV for audio ([code].png[/code] file "
"extension). Lossless compression, large file sizes, slow encoding. Designed "
"to be encoded to a video file with another tool such as [url=https://"
"ffmpeg.org/]FFmpeg[/url] after recording. Transparency is currently not "
"supported, even if the root viewport is set to be transparent.\n"
"If you need to encode to a different format or pipe a stream through third-"
"party software, you can extend the [MovieWriter] class to create your own "
"movie writers. This should typically be done using GDExtension for "
"performance reasons.\n"
"[b]Editor usage:[/b] A default movie file path can be specified in [member "
"ProjectSettings.editor/movie_writer/movie_file]. Alternatively, for running "
"single scenes, a [code]movie_file[/code] metadata can be added to the root "
"node, specifying the path to a movie file that will be used when recording "
"that scene. Once a path is set, click the video reel icon in the top-right "
"corner of the editor to enable Movie Maker mode, then run any scene as "
"usual. The engine will start recording as soon as the splash screen is "
"finished, and it will only stop recording when the engine quits. Click the "
"video reel icon again to disable Movie Maker mode. Note that toggling Movie "
"Maker mode does not affect project instances that are already running.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] MovieWriter is available for use in both the editor and "
"exported projects, but it is [i]not[/i] designed for use by end users to "
"record videos while playing. Players wishing to record gameplay videos "
"should install tools such as [url=https://obsproject.com/]OBS Studio[/url] "
"or [url=https://www.maartenbaert.be/"
"simplescreenrecorder/]SimpleScreenRecorder[/url] instead.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] MJPEG support ([code].avi[/code] file extension) depends on the "
"[code]jpg[/code] module being enabled at compile time (default behavior).\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] OGV support ([code].ogv[/code] file extension) depends on the "
"[code]theora[/code] module being enabled at compile time (default behavior). "
"Theora compression is only available in editor binaries."
msgstr ""
"O Godot pode gravar vídeos com simulação em tempo não real. Assim como o "
"[url=$DOCS_URL/tutorials/editor/command_line_tutorial.html]argumento de "
"linha de comando[/url] [code]--fixed-fps[/code], isso força o [code]delta[/"
"code] relatado nas funções [method Node._process] a ser idêntico entre os "
"quadros, independentemente de quanto tempo realmente levou para renderizar o "
"quadro. Isso pode ser usado para gravar vídeos de alta qualidade com "
"cadência de quadros perfeita, independentemente das capacidades do seu "
"hardware.\n"
"O Godot possui 3 [MovieWriter]s integrados:\n"
"- Contêiner OGV com Theora para vídeo e Vorbis para áudio (extensão de "
"arquivo [code].ogv[/code]). Compressão com perdas, tamanhos de arquivo "
"médios, codificação rápida. A qualidade da compressão com perdas pode ser "
"ajustada alterando [member ProjectSettings.editor/movie_writer/"
"video_quality] e [member ProjectSettings.editor/movie_writer/ogv/"
"audio_quality]. O arquivo resultante pode ser visualizado no Godot com "
"[VideoStreamPlayer] e na maioria dos reprodutores de vídeo, mas não em "
"navegadores web, pois eles não suportam Theora.\n"
"- Contêiner AVI com MJPEG para vídeo e áudio não compactado (extensão de "
"arquivo [code].avi[/code]). Compressão com perdas, tamanhos de arquivo "
"médios, codificação rápida. A qualidade da compressão com perdas pode ser "
"ajustada alterando [member ProjectSettings.editor/movie_writer/"
"video_quality]. O arquivo resultante pode ser visualizado na maioria dos "
"reprodutores de vídeo, mas deve ser convertido para outro formato para ser "
"visualizado na web ou pelo Godot com [VideoStreamPlayer]. O MJPEG não "
"suporta transparência. A saída AVI é atualmente limitada a um arquivo de no "
"máximo 4 GB de tamanho.\n"
"- Sequência de imagens PNG para vídeo e WAV para áudio (extensão de arquivo "
"[code].png[/code]). Compressão sem perdas, arquivos grandes, codificação "
"lenta. Projetado para ser codificado em um arquivo de vídeo com outra "
"ferramenta, como o [url=https://ffmpeg.org/]FFmpeg[/url], após a gravação. A "
"transparência atualmente não é suportada, mesmo que a viewport raiz esteja "
"configurada para ser transparente.\n"
"Se precisar codificar para um formato diferente ou direcionar um fluxo por "
"meio de software de terceiros, você pode estender a classe [MovieWriter] "
"para criar seus próprios gravadores de filme. Isso normalmente deve ser "
"feito usando o GDExtension por motivos de desempenho.\n"
"[b]Uso no editor:[/b] Um caminho de arquivo de filme padrão pode ser "
"especificado em [member ProjectSettings.editor/movie_writer/movie_file]. "
"Como alternativa, para executar cenas individuais, metadados "
"[code]movie_file[/code] podem ser adicionados ao nó raiz, especificando o "
"caminho para um arquivo de filme que será usado ao gravar essa cena. Assim "
"que um caminho for definido, clique no ícone de rolo de filme no canto "
"superior direito do editor para ativar o modo Movie Maker e, em seguida, "
"execute qualquer cena normalmente. O motor começará a gravar assim que a "
"tela de apresentação terminar e só parará de gravar quando o motor for "
"fechado. Clique no ícone de rolo de filme novamente para desativar o modo "
"Movie Maker. Observe que alternar o modo Movie Maker não afeta instâncias de "
"projeto que já estão em execução.\n"
"[b]Nota:[/b] O MovieWriter está disponível para uso tanto no editor quanto "
"em projetos exportados, mas [i]não[/i] foi projetado para ser usado por "
"usuários finais para gravar vídeos enquanto jogam. Jogadores que desejam "
"gravar vídeos de gameplay devem instalar ferramentas como [url=https://"
"obsproject.com/]OBS Studio[/url] ou [url=https://www.maartenbaert.be/"
"simplescreenrecorder/]SimpleScreenRecorder[/url].\n"
"[b]Nota:[/b] O suporte a MJPEG (extensão de arquivo [code].avi[/code]) "
"depende de o módulo [code]jpg[/code] estar ativado em tempo de compilação "
"(comportamento padrão).\n"
"[b]Nota:[/b] O suporte a OGV (extensão de arquivo [code].ogv[/code]) depende "
"de o módulo [code]theora[/code] estar ativado em tempo de compilação "
"(comportamento padrão). A compressão Theora está disponível apenas em "
"binários do editor."

#: doc/classes/MovieWriter.xml
msgid ""
"Called when the audio sample rate used for recording the audio is requested "
"by the engine. The value returned must be specified in Hz. Defaults to 48000 "
"Hz if [method _get_audio_mix_rate] is not overridden."
msgstr ""
"Chamado quando a taxa de amostragem de áudio usada para gravar o áudio é "
"solicitada pelo motor. O valor retornado deve ser especificado em Hz. O "
"padrão é 48000 Hz se [method _get_audio_mix_rate] não for substituído."

#: doc/classes/MovieWriter.xml
msgid ""
"Called when the audio speaker mode used for recording the audio is requested "
"by the engine. This can affect the number of output channels in the "
"resulting audio file/stream. Defaults to [constant "
"AudioServer.SPEAKER_MODE_STEREO] if [method _get_audio_speaker_mode] is not "
"overridden."
msgstr ""
"Chamado quando o modo de alto-falante de áudio usado para gravar o áudio é "
"solicitado pelo engine. Isso pode afetar o número de canais de saída no "
"arquivo/fluxo de áudio resultante. O padrão é [constant "
"AudioServer.SPEAKER_MODE_STEREO] se [method _get_audio_speaker_mode] não for "
"substituído."

#: doc/classes/MovieWriter.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the list of supported filename extensions for movies written with "
"this [MovieWriter]."
msgstr ""
"Retorna a lista de extensões de nome de arquivo suportadas para vídeos "
"gravados com este [MovieWriter]."

#: doc/classes/MovieWriter.xml
msgid ""
"Called when the engine determines whether this [MovieWriter] is able to "
"handle the file at [param path]. Must return [code]true[/code] if this "
"[MovieWriter] is able to handle the given file path, [code]false[/code] "
"otherwise. Typically, [method _handles_file] is overridden as follows to "
"allow the user to record a file at any path with a given file extension:\n"
"[codeblock]\n"
"func _handles_file(path):\n"
"\t# Allows specifying an output file with a `.mkv` file extension (case-"
"insensitive),\n"
"\t# either in the Project Settings or with the `--write-movie <path>` "
"command line argument.\n"
"\treturn path.get_extension().to_lower() == \"mkv\"\n"
"[/codeblock]"
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/MovieWriter.xml
msgid ""
"Called once before the engine starts writing video and audio data. [param "
"movie_size] is the width and height of the video to save. [param fps] is the "
"number of frames per second specified in the project settings or using the "
"[code]--fixed-fps <fps>[/code] [url=$DOCS_URL/tutorials/editor/"
"command_line_tutorial.html]command line argument[/url]."
msgstr ""
"Chamado uma vez antes de o motor começar a gravar dados de vídeo e áudio. "
"[param movie_size] é a largura e a altura do vídeo a ser salvo. [param fps] "
"é o número de quadros por segundo especificado nas configurações do projeto "
"ou usando o [url=$DOCS_URL/tutorials/editor/"
"command_line_tutorial.html]argumento de linha de comando[/url] [code]--fixed-"
"fps <fps>[/code]."

#: doc/classes/MovieWriter.xml
msgid ""
"Called when the engine finishes writing. This occurs when the engine quits "
"by pressing the window manager's close button, or when [method "
"SceneTree.quit] is called.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Pressing [kbd]Ctrl + C[/kbd] on the terminal running the editor/"
"project does [i]not[/i] result in [method _write_end] being called."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/MovieWriter.xml
msgid ""
"Called at the end of every rendered frame. The [param frame_image] and "
"[param audio_frame_block] function arguments should be written to."
msgstr ""
"Chamado no final de cada quadro renderizado. Os argumentos de função [param "
"frame_image] e [param audio_frame_block] devem ser gravados."

#: doc/classes/MovieWriter.xml
msgid ""
"Adds a writer to be usable by the engine. The supported file extensions can "
"be set by overriding [method _handles_file].\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] [method add_writer] must be called early enough in the engine "
"initialization to work, as movie writing is designed to start at the same "
"time as the rest of the engine."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/MultiMesh.xml
msgid ""
"Provides high-performance drawing of a mesh multiple times using GPU "
"instancing."
msgstr ""
"Fornece desenho de alto desempenho de uma malha várias vezes usando "
"instanciamento de GPU."

#: doc/classes/MultiMesh.xml
msgid ""
"MultiMesh provides low-level mesh instancing. Drawing thousands of "
"[MeshInstance3D] nodes can be slow, since each object is submitted to the "
"GPU then drawn individually.\n"
"MultiMesh is much faster as it can draw thousands of instances with a single "
"draw call, resulting in less API overhead.\n"
"As a drawback, if the instances are too far away from each other, "
"performance may be reduced as every single instance will always render (they "
"are spatially indexed as one, for the whole object).\n"
"Since instances may have any behavior, the AABB used for visibility must be "
"provided by the user.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] A MultiMesh is a single object, therefore the same maximum "
"lights per object restriction applies. This means, that once the maximum "
"lights are consumed by one or more instances, the rest of the MultiMesh "
"instances will [b]not[/b] receive any lighting.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Blend Shapes will be ignored if used in a MultiMesh."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/MultiMesh.xml doc/classes/MultiMeshInstance3D.xml
msgid "Using MultiMeshInstance"
msgstr "Usando MultiMeshInstance"

#: doc/classes/MultiMesh.xml doc/classes/MultiMeshInstance3D.xml
msgid "Optimization using MultiMeshes"
msgstr "Otimização usando MultiMeshes"

#: doc/classes/MultiMesh.xml doc/classes/MultiMeshInstance3D.xml
msgid "Animating thousands of fish with MultiMeshInstance"
msgstr "Animando milhares de peixes com o MultiMeshInstance"

#: doc/classes/MultiMesh.xml
msgid "Returns the visibility axis-aligned bounding box in local space."
msgstr ""
"Retorna a caixa delimitadora alinhada aos eixos de visibilidade em espaço "
"local."

#: doc/classes/MultiMesh.xml
msgid "Gets a specific instance's color multiplier."
msgstr "Obtém o multiplicador de cor de uma instância específica."

#: doc/classes/MultiMesh.xml
msgid "Returns the custom data that has been set for a specific instance."
msgstr ""
"Retorna os dados personalizados que foram definidos para uma instância "
"específica."

#: doc/classes/MultiMesh.xml
msgid "Returns the [Transform3D] of a specific instance."
msgstr "Retorna o [Transform3D] de uma instância específica."

#: doc/classes/MultiMesh.xml
msgid "Returns the [Transform2D] of a specific instance."
msgstr "Retorna o [Transform2D] de uma instância específica."

#: doc/classes/MultiMesh.xml
msgid ""
"When using [i]physics interpolation[/i], this function allows you to prevent "
"interpolation on an instance in the current physics tick.\n"
"This allows you to move instances instantaneously, and should usually be "
"used when initially placing an instance such as a bullet to prevent "
"graphical glitches."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/MultiMesh.xml
msgid ""
"When using [i]physics interpolation[/i], this function allows you to prevent "
"interpolation for all instances in the current physics tick.\n"
"This allows you to move all instances instantaneously, and should usually be "
"used when initially placing instances to prevent graphical glitches."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/MultiMesh.xml
msgid ""
"An alternative to setting the [member buffer] property, which can be used "
"with [i]physics interpolation[/i]. This method takes two arrays, and can set "
"the data for the current and previous tick in one go. The renderer will "
"automatically interpolate the data at each frame.\n"
"This is useful for situations where the order of instances may change from "
"physics tick to tick, such as particle systems.\n"
"When the order of instances is coherent, the simpler alternative of setting "
"[member buffer] can still be used with interpolation."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/MultiMesh.xml
msgid ""
"Sets the color of a specific instance by [i]multiplying[/i] the mesh's "
"existing vertex colors. This allows for different color tinting per "
"instance.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Each component is stored in 32 bits in the Forward+ and Mobile "
"rendering methods, but is packed into 16 bits in the Compatibility rendering "
"method.\n"
"For the color to take effect, ensure that [member use_colors] is [code]true[/"
"code] on the [MultiMesh] and [member "
"BaseMaterial3D.vertex_color_use_as_albedo] is [code]true[/code] on the "
"material. If you intend to set an absolute color instead of tinting, make "
"sure the material's albedo color is set to pure white ([code]Color(1, 1, 1)[/"
"code])."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/MultiMesh.xml
msgid ""
"Sets custom data for a specific instance. [param custom_data] is a [Color] "
"type only to contain 4 floating-point numbers.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Each number is stored in 32 bits in the Forward+ and Mobile "
"rendering methods, but is packed into 16 bits in the Compatibility rendering "
"method.\n"
"For the custom data to be used, ensure that [member use_custom_data] is "
"[code]true[/code].\n"
"This custom instance data has to be manually accessed in your custom shader "
"using [code]INSTANCE_CUSTOM[/code]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/MultiMesh.xml
msgid "Sets the [Transform3D] for a specific instance."
msgstr "Define o [Transform3D] para uma instância específica."

#: doc/classes/MultiMesh.xml
msgid "Sets the [Transform2D] for a specific instance."
msgstr "Define o [Transform2D] para uma instância específica."

#: doc/classes/MultiMesh.xml
msgid ""
"Accessing this property is very slow. Use [method set_instance_color] and "
"[method get_instance_color] instead."
msgstr ""
"O acesso a esta propriedade é muito lento. Use [method set_instance_color] e "
"[method get_instance_color] em vez disso."

#: doc/classes/MultiMesh.xml
msgid "Array containing each [Color] used by all instances of this mesh."
msgstr ""
"Matriz contendo cada [Color] usada por todas as instâncias desta malha."

#: doc/classes/MultiMesh.xml
msgid ""
"Custom AABB for this MultiMesh resource. Setting this manually prevents "
"costly runtime AABB recalculations."
msgstr ""
"AABB personalizado para este recurso MultiMesh. Definir isso manualmente "
"evita recálculos custosos de AABB em tempo de execução."

#: doc/classes/MultiMesh.xml
msgid ""
"Accessing this property is very slow. Use [method set_instance_custom_data] "
"and [method get_instance_custom_data] instead."
msgstr ""
"Acessar esta propriedade é muito lento. Use [method "
"set_instance_custom_data] e [method get_instance_custom_data] em vez disso."

#: doc/classes/MultiMesh.xml
msgid ""
"Array containing each custom data value used by all instances of this mesh, "
"as a [PackedColorArray]."
msgstr ""
"Array contendo cada valor de dado personalizado usado por todas as "
"instâncias desta malha, como um [PackedColorArray]."

#: doc/classes/MultiMesh.xml
msgid ""
"Number of instances that will get drawn. This clears and (re)sizes the "
"buffers. Setting data format or flags afterwards will have no effect.\n"
"By default, all instances are drawn but you can limit this with [member "
"visible_instance_count]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/MultiMesh.xml
msgid ""
"[Mesh] resource to be instanced.\n"
"The looks of the individual instances can be modified using [method "
"set_instance_color] and [method set_instance_custom_data]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/MultiMesh.xml
msgid ""
"Choose whether to use an interpolation method that favors speed or quality.\n"
"When using low physics tick rates (typically below 20) or high rates of "
"object rotation, you may get better results from the high quality setting.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Fast quality does not equate to low quality. Except in the "
"special cases mentioned above, the quality should be comparable to high "
"quality."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/MultiMesh.xml
msgid ""
"Accessing this property is very slow. Use [method set_instance_transform_2d] "
"and [method get_instance_transform_2d] instead."
msgstr ""
"Acessar esta propriedade é muito lento. Use [method "
"set_instance_transform_2d] e [method get_instance_transform_2d] em vez disso."

#: doc/classes/MultiMesh.xml
msgid ""
"Array containing each [Transform2D] value used by all instances of this "
"mesh, as a [PackedVector2Array]. Each transform is divided into 3 [Vector2] "
"values corresponding to the transforms' [code]x[/code], [code]y[/code], and "
"[code]origin[/code]."
msgstr ""
"Matriz contendo cada valor [Transform2D] usado por todas as instâncias desta "
"malha, como um [PackedVector2Array]. Cada transformação é dividida em 3 "
"valores [Vector2] correspondentes a [code]x[/code], [code]y[/code] e "
"[code]origin[/code] das transformações."

#: doc/classes/MultiMesh.xml
msgid ""
"Accessing this property is very slow. Use [method set_instance_transform] "
"and [method get_instance_transform] instead."
msgstr ""
"Acessar esta propriedade é muito lento. Use [method set_instance_transform] "
"e [method get_instance_transform] em vez disso."

#: doc/classes/MultiMesh.xml
msgid ""
"Array containing each [Transform3D] value used by all instances of this "
"mesh, as a [PackedVector3Array]. Each transform is divided into 4 [Vector3] "
"values corresponding to the transforms' [code]x[/code], [code]y[/code], "
"[code]z[/code], and [code]origin[/code]."
msgstr ""
"Matriz contendo cada valor [Transform3D] usado por todas as instâncias desta "
"malha, como um [PackedVector3Array]. Cada transformação é dividida em 4 "
"valores [Vector3] correspondentes a [code]x[/code], [code]y[/code], [code]z[/"
"code] e [code]origin[/code] das transformações."

#: doc/classes/MultiMesh.xml
msgid "Format of transform used to transform mesh, either 2D or 3D."
msgstr ""
"Formato de transformação usado para transformar a malha, seja 2D ou 3D."

#: doc/classes/MultiMesh.xml
msgid ""
"If [code]true[/code], the [MultiMesh] will use color data (see [method "
"set_instance_color]). Can only be set when [member instance_count] is "
"[code]0[/code] or less. This means that you need to call this method before "
"setting the instance count, or temporarily reset it to [code]0[/code]."
msgstr ""
"Se [code]true[/code], o [MultiMesh] usará dados de cor (veja [method "
"set_instance_color]). Só pode ser definido quando [member instance_count] "
"for [code]0[/code] ou menos. Isso significa que você precisa chamar este "
"método antes de definir a contagem de instâncias, ou redefini-la "
"temporariamente para [code]0[/code]."

#: doc/classes/MultiMesh.xml
msgid ""
"If [code]true[/code], the [MultiMesh] will use custom data (see [method "
"set_instance_custom_data]). Can only be set when [member instance_count] is "
"[code]0[/code] or less. This means that you need to call this method before "
"setting the instance count, or temporarily reset it to [code]0[/code]."
msgstr ""
"Se [code]true[/code], o [MultiMesh] usará dados personalizados (veja [method "
"set_instance_custom_data]). Só pode ser definido quando [member "
"instance_count] for [code]0[/code] ou menos. Isso significa que você precisa "
"chamar este método antes de definir a contagem de instâncias, ou redefini-la "
"temporariamente para [code]0[/code]."

#: doc/classes/MultiMesh.xml
msgid ""
"Limits the number of instances drawn, -1 draws all instances. Changing this "
"does not change the sizes of the buffers."
msgstr ""
"Limita o número de instâncias desenhadas; -1 desenha todas as instâncias. "
"Alterar isso não altera os tamanhos dos buffers."

#: doc/classes/MultiMesh.xml
msgid "Use this when using 2D transforms."
msgstr "Use isto ao usar transformações 2D."

#: doc/classes/MultiMesh.xml
msgid "Use this when using 3D transforms."
msgstr "Use isto ao usar transformações 3D."

#: doc/classes/MultiMesh.xml
msgid ""
"Always interpolate using Basis lerping, which can produce warping artifacts "
"in some situations."
msgstr ""
"Sempre interpola usando lerp de Basis, o que pode produzir artefatos de "
"deformação em algumas situações."

#: doc/classes/MultiMesh.xml
msgid ""
"Attempt to interpolate using Basis slerping (spherical linear interpolation) "
"where possible, otherwise fall back to lerping."
msgstr ""
"Tenta interpolar usando slerp de Basis (interpolação linear esférica) sempre "
"que possível, caso contrário, recorre a lerp."

#: doc/classes/MultiMeshInstance2D.xml
msgid "Node that instances a [MultiMesh] in 2D."
msgstr "Nó que instancia um [MultiMesh] em 2D."

#: doc/classes/MultiMeshInstance2D.xml
msgid ""
"[MultiMeshInstance2D] is a specialized node to instance a [MultiMesh] "
"resource in 2D. This can be faster to render compared to displaying many "
"[Sprite2D] nodes with large transparent areas, especially if the nodes take "
"up a lot of space on screen at high viewport resolutions. This is because "
"using a mesh designed to fit the sprites' opaque areas will reduce GPU fill "
"rate utilization (at the cost of increased vertex processing utilization).\n"
"Usage is the same as [MultiMeshInstance3D]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/MultiMeshInstance2D.xml
msgid "The [MultiMesh] that will be drawn by the [MultiMeshInstance2D]."
msgstr "O [MultiMesh] que será desenhado pelo [MultiMeshInstance2D]."

#: doc/classes/MultiMeshInstance3D.xml
msgid "Node that instances a [MultiMesh]."
msgstr "Nó que instancia um [MultiMesh]."

#: doc/classes/MultiMeshInstance3D.xml
msgid ""
"[MultiMeshInstance3D] is a specialized node to instance "
"[GeometryInstance3D]s based on a [MultiMesh] resource.\n"
"This is useful to optimize the rendering of a high number of instances of a "
"given mesh (for example trees in a forest or grass strands)."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/MultiMeshInstance3D.xml
msgid ""
"The [MultiMesh] resource that will be used and shared among all instances of "
"the [MultiMeshInstance3D]."
msgstr ""
"O recurso [MultiMesh] que será usado e compartilhado entre todas as "
"instâncias do [MultiMeshInstance3D]."

#: doc/classes/MultiplayerAPI.xml
msgid "High-level multiplayer API interface."
msgstr "Interface de API multiplayer de alto nível."

#: doc/classes/MultiplayerAPI.xml
msgid ""
"Base class for high-level multiplayer API implementations. See also "
"[MultiplayerPeer].\n"
"By default, [SceneTree] has a reference to an implementation of this class "
"and uses it to provide multiplayer capabilities (i.e. RPCs) across the whole "
"scene.\n"
"It is possible to override the MultiplayerAPI instance used by specific tree "
"branches by calling the [method SceneTree.set_multiplayer] method, "
"effectively allowing to run both client and server in the same scene.\n"
"It is also possible to extend or replace the default implementation via "
"scripting or native extensions. See [MultiplayerAPIExtension] for details "
"about extensions, [SceneMultiplayer] for the details about the default "
"implementation."
msgstr ""
"Classe base para implementações de API multijogador de alto nível. Veja "
"também [Multiplayer Peer].\n"
"Por padrão, [SceneTree] tem uma referência a uma implementação dessa classe "
"e a usa para fornecer recursos multijogador (ou seja, RPCs) em toda a cena.\n"
"É possível substituir a instância MultiplayerAPI usada por ramificações de "
"árvore específicas chamando o método [method SceneTree.set_multiplayer], "
"permitindo efetivamente executar o cliente e o servidor na mesma cena.\n"
"Também é possível estender ou substituir a implementação padrão por meio de "
"scripts ou extensões nativas. Consulte [MultiplayerAPIExtension] para obter "
"detalhes sobre extensões, [SceneMultiplayer] para obter detalhes sobre a "
"implementação padrão."

#: doc/classes/MultiplayerAPI.xml
msgid "Returns a new instance of the default MultiplayerAPI."
msgstr "Retorna uma nova instância da MultiplayerAPI padrão."

#: doc/classes/MultiplayerAPI.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the default MultiplayerAPI implementation class name. This is "
"usually [code]\"SceneMultiplayer\"[/code] when [SceneMultiplayer] is "
"available. See [method set_default_interface]."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o nome da classe de implementação MultiplayerAPI padrão. Geralmente "
"é [code]\"SceneMultiplayer\"[/code] quando [SceneMultiplayer] está "
"disponível. Consulte [method set_default_interface]."

#: doc/classes/MultiplayerAPI.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the peer IDs of all connected peers of this MultiplayerAPI's [member "
"multiplayer_peer]."
msgstr ""
"Retorna os IDs de peer de todos os peers conectados do [member "
"multiplayer_peer] desta MultiplayerAPI."

#: doc/classes/MultiplayerAPI.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the sender's peer ID for the RPC currently being executed.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] This method returns [code]0[/code] when called outside of an "
"RPC. As such, the original peer ID may be lost when code execution is "
"delayed (such as with GDScript's [code]await[/code] keyword)."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/MultiplayerAPI.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the unique peer ID of this MultiplayerAPI's [member "
"multiplayer_peer]."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o ID de par exclusivo do [member multiplayer_peer] deste "
"MultiplayerAPI."

#: doc/classes/MultiplayerAPI.xml
msgid "Returns [code]true[/code] if there is a [member multiplayer_peer] set."
msgstr ""
"Retorna [code]true[/code] se houver um [member multiplayer_peer] definido."

#: doc/classes/MultiplayerAPI.xml
msgid ""
"Returns [code]true[/code] if this MultiplayerAPI's [member multiplayer_peer] "
"is valid and in server mode (listening for connections)."
msgstr ""
"Retorna [code]true[/code] se o [member multiplayer_peer] desta "
"MultiplayerAPI for válido e estiver no modo de servidor (ouvindo conexões)."

#: doc/classes/MultiplayerAPI.xml
msgid ""
"Notifies the MultiplayerAPI of a new [param configuration] for the given "
"[param object]. This method is used internally by [SceneTree] to configure "
"the root path for this MultiplayerAPI (passing [code]null[/code] and a valid "
"[NodePath] as [param configuration]). This method can be further used by "
"MultiplayerAPI implementations to provide additional features, refer to "
"specific implementation (e.g. [SceneMultiplayer]) for details on how they "
"use it.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] This method is mostly relevant when extending or overriding the "
"MultiplayerAPI behavior via [MultiplayerAPIExtension]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/MultiplayerAPI.xml
msgid ""
"Notifies the MultiplayerAPI to remove a [param configuration] for the given "
"[param object]. This method is used internally by [SceneTree] to configure "
"the root path for this MultiplayerAPI (passing [code]null[/code] and an "
"empty [NodePath] as [param configuration]). This method can be further used "
"by MultiplayerAPI implementations to provide additional features, refer to "
"specific implementation (e.g. [SceneMultiplayer]) for details on how they "
"use it.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] This method is mostly relevant when extending or overriding the "
"MultiplayerAPI behavior via [MultiplayerAPIExtension]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/MultiplayerAPI.xml
msgid ""
"Method used for polling the MultiplayerAPI. You only need to worry about "
"this if you set [member SceneTree.multiplayer_poll] to [code]false[/code]. "
"By default, [SceneTree] will poll its MultiplayerAPI(s) for you.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] This method results in RPCs being called, so they will be "
"executed in the same context of this function (e.g. [code]_process[/code], "
"[code]physics[/code], [Thread])."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/MultiplayerAPI.xml
msgid ""
"Sends an RPC to the target [param peer]. The given [param method] will be "
"called on the remote [param object] with the provided [param arguments]. The "
"RPC may also be called locally depending on the implementation and RPC "
"configuration. See [method Node.rpc] and [method Node.rpc_config].\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Prefer using [method Node.rpc], [method Node.rpc_id], or "
"[code]my_method.rpc(peer, arg1, arg2, ...)[/code] (in GDScript), since they "
"are faster. This method is mostly useful in conjunction with "
"[MultiplayerAPIExtension] when extending or replacing the multiplayer "
"capabilities."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/MultiplayerAPI.xml
msgid ""
"Sets the default MultiplayerAPI implementation class. This method can be "
"used by modules and extensions to configure which implementation will be "
"used by [SceneTree] when the engine starts."
msgstr ""
"Define a classe de implementação MultiplayerAPI padrão. Este método pode ser "
"usado por módulos e extensões para configurar qual implementação será usada "
"pelo [SceneTree] quando o motor for iniciado."

#: doc/classes/MultiplayerAPI.xml
msgid ""
"The peer object to handle the RPC system (effectively enabling networking "
"when set). Depending on the peer itself, the MultiplayerAPI will become a "
"network server (check with [method is_server]) and will set root node's "
"network mode to authority, or it will become a regular client peer. All "
"child nodes are set to inherit the network mode by default. Handling of "
"networking-related events (connection, disconnection, new clients) is done "
"by connecting to MultiplayerAPI's signals."
msgstr ""
"O objeto par para lidar com o sistema RPC (efetivamente habilitando rede "
"quando definido). Dependendo do próprio par, o MultiplayerAPI se tornará um "
"servidor de rede (verifique com [method is_server]) e definirá o modo de "
"rede do nó raiz como autoridade, ou se tornará um par cliente regular. Todos "
"os nós filhos são configurados para herdar o modo de rede por padrão. O "
"tratamento de eventos relacionados à rede (conexão, desconexão, novos "
"clientes) é feito conectando-se aos sinais da MultiplayerAPI."

#: doc/classes/MultiplayerAPI.xml
msgid ""
"Emitted when this MultiplayerAPI's [member multiplayer_peer] successfully "
"connected to a server. Only emitted on clients."
msgstr ""
"Emitido quando o [member multiplayer_peer] desta MultiplayerAPI se conecta "
"com sucesso a um servidor. Emitido apenas em clientes."

#: doc/classes/MultiplayerAPI.xml
msgid ""
"Emitted when this MultiplayerAPI's [member multiplayer_peer] fails to "
"establish a connection to a server. Only emitted on clients."
msgstr ""
"Emitido quando o [member multiplayer_peer] desta MultiplayerAPI falha ao "
"estabelecer uma conexão com um servidor. Emitido apenas em clientes."

#: doc/classes/MultiplayerAPI.xml
msgid ""
"Emitted when this MultiplayerAPI's [member multiplayer_peer] connects with a "
"new peer. ID is the peer ID of the new peer. Clients get notified when other "
"clients connect to the same server. Upon connecting to a server, a client "
"also receives this signal for the server (with ID being 1)."
msgstr ""
"Emitido quando o [member multiplayer_peer] deste MultiplayerAPI se conecta "
"com um novo par. ID é o ID de par do novo par. Os clientes são notificados "
"quando outros clientes se conectam ao mesmo servidor. Ao se conectar a um "
"servidor, um cliente também recebe este sinal para o servidor (com o ID "
"sendo 1)."

#: doc/classes/MultiplayerAPI.xml
msgid ""
"Emitted when this MultiplayerAPI's [member multiplayer_peer] disconnects "
"from a peer. Clients get notified when other clients disconnect from the "
"same server."
msgstr ""
"Emitido quando o [member multiplayer_peer] deste MultiplayerAPI se "
"desconecta de um par. Os clientes são notificados quando outros clientes se "
"desconectam do mesmo servidor."

#: doc/classes/MultiplayerAPI.xml
msgid ""
"Emitted when this MultiplayerAPI's [member multiplayer_peer] disconnects "
"from server. Only emitted on clients."
msgstr ""
"Emitido quando o [member multiplayer_peer] desta MultiplayerAPI se "
"desconecta do servidor. Emitido apenas em clientes."

#: doc/classes/MultiplayerAPI.xml
msgid ""
"Used with [method Node.rpc_config] to disable a method or property for all "
"RPC calls, making it unavailable. Default for all methods."
msgstr ""
"Usado com [method Node.rpc_config] para desativar um método ou propriedade "
"para todas as chamadas RPC, tornando-o indisponível. Padrão para todos os "
"métodos."

#: doc/classes/MultiplayerAPI.xml
msgid ""
"Used with [method Node.rpc_config] to set a method to be callable remotely "
"by any peer. Analogous to the [code]@rpc(\"any_peer\")[/code] annotation. "
"Calls are accepted from all remote peers, no matter if they are node's "
"authority or not."
msgstr ""
"Usado com [method Node.rpc_config] para definir um método como chamável "
"remotamente por qualquer par. Análogo à anotação [code]@rpc(\"any_peer\")[/"
"code]. As chamadas são aceitas de todos os pares remotos, independentemente "
"de serem a autoridade do nó ou não."

#: doc/classes/MultiplayerAPI.xml
msgid ""
"Used with [method Node.rpc_config] to set a method to be callable remotely "
"only by the current multiplayer authority (which is the server by default). "
"Analogous to the [code]@rpc(\"authority\")[/code] annotation. See [method "
"Node.set_multiplayer_authority]."
msgstr ""
"Usado com [method Node.rpc_config] para definir que um método seja chamável "
"remotamente apenas pela autoridade multiplayer atual (que é o servidor por "
"padrão). Análogo à anotação [code]@rpc(\"authority\")[/code]. Veja [method "
"Node.set_multiplayer_authority]."

#: doc/classes/MultiplayerAPIExtension.xml
msgid "Base class used for extending the [MultiplayerAPI]."
msgstr "Classe base usada para estender o [MultiplayerAPI]."

#: doc/classes/MultiplayerAPIExtension.xml
msgid ""
"This class can be used to extend or replace the default [MultiplayerAPI] "
"implementation via script or extensions.\n"
"The following example extend the default implementation ([SceneMultiplayer]) "
"by logging every RPC being made, and every object being configured for "
"replication.\n"
"[codeblocks]\n"
"[gdscript]\n"
"extends MultiplayerAPIExtension\n"
"class_name LogMultiplayer\n"
"\n"
"# We want to extend the default SceneMultiplayer.\n"
"var base_multiplayer = SceneMultiplayer.new()\n"
"\n"
"func _init():\n"
"\t# Just passthrough base signals (copied to var to avoid cyclic reference)\n"
"\tvar cts = connected_to_server\n"
"\tvar cf = connection_failed\n"
"\tvar sd = server_disconnected\n"
"\tvar pc = peer_connected\n"
"\tvar pd = peer_disconnected\n"
"\tbase_multiplayer.connected_to_server.connect(func(): cts.emit())\n"
"\tbase_multiplayer.connection_failed.connect(func(): cf.emit())\n"
"\tbase_multiplayer.server_disconnected.connect(func(): sd.emit())\n"
"\tbase_multiplayer.peer_connected.connect(func(id): pc.emit(id))\n"
"\tbase_multiplayer.peer_disconnected.connect(func(id): pd.emit(id))\n"
"\n"
"func _poll():\n"
"\treturn base_multiplayer.poll()\n"
"\n"
"# Log RPC being made and forward it to the default multiplayer.\n"
"func _rpc(peer: int, object: Object, method: StringName, args: Array) -> "
"Error:\n"
"\tprint(\"Got RPC for %d: %s::%s(%s)\" % [peer, object, method, args])\n"
"\treturn base_multiplayer.rpc(peer, object, method, args)\n"
"\n"
"# Log configuration add. E.g. root path (nullptr, NodePath), replication "
"(Node, Spawner|Synchronizer), custom.\n"
"func _object_configuration_add(object, config: Variant) -> Error:\n"
"\tif config is MultiplayerSynchronizer:\n"
"\t\tprint(\"Adding synchronization configuration for %s. Synchronizer: %s\" "
"% [object, config])\n"
"\telif config is MultiplayerSpawner:\n"
"\t\tprint(\"Adding node %s to the spawn list. Spawner: %s\" % [object, "
"config])\n"
"\treturn base_multiplayer.object_configuration_add(object, config)\n"
"\n"
"# Log configuration remove. E.g. root path (nullptr, NodePath), replication "
"(Node, Spawner|Synchronizer), custom.\n"
"func _object_configuration_remove(object, config: Variant) -> Error:\n"
"\tif config is MultiplayerSynchronizer:\n"
"\t\tprint(\"Removing synchronization configuration for %s. Synchronizer: "
"%s\" % [object, config])\n"
"\telif config is MultiplayerSpawner:\n"
"\t\tprint(\"Removing node %s from the spawn list. Spawner: %s\" % [object, "
"config])\n"
"\treturn base_multiplayer.object_configuration_remove(object, config)\n"
"\n"
"# These can be optional, but in our case we want to extend SceneMultiplayer, "
"so forward everything.\n"
"func _set_multiplayer_peer(p_peer: MultiplayerPeer):\n"
"\tbase_multiplayer.multiplayer_peer = p_peer\n"
"\n"
"func _get_multiplayer_peer() -> MultiplayerPeer:\n"
"\treturn base_multiplayer.multiplayer_peer\n"
"\n"
"func _get_unique_id() -> int:\n"
"\treturn base_multiplayer.get_unique_id()\n"
"\n"
"func _get_remote_sender_id() -> int:\n"
"\treturn base_multiplayer.get_remote_sender_id()\n"
"\n"
"func _get_peer_ids() -> PackedInt32Array:\n"
"\treturn base_multiplayer.get_peers()\n"
"[/gdscript]\n"
"[/codeblocks]\n"
"Then in your main scene or in an autoload call [method "
"SceneTree.set_multiplayer] to start using your custom [MultiplayerAPI]:\n"
"[codeblocks]\n"
"[gdscript]\n"
"# autoload.gd\n"
"func _enter_tree():\n"
"\t# Sets our custom multiplayer as the main one in SceneTree.\n"
"\tget_tree().set_multiplayer(LogMultiplayer.new())\n"
"[/gdscript]\n"
"[/codeblocks]\n"
"Native extensions can alternatively use the [method "
"MultiplayerAPI.set_default_interface] method during initialization to "
"configure themselves as the default implementation."
msgstr ""
"Esta classe pode ser usada para estender ou substituir a implementação "
"padrão de [MultiplayerAPI] por meio de script ou extensões.\n"
"O exemplo a seguir estende a implementação padrão ([SceneMultiplayer]) "
"registrando cada RPC sendo feito e cada objeto sendo configurado para "
"replicação.\n"
"[codeblocks]\n"
"[gdscript]\n"
"extends MultiplayerAPIExtension\n"
"class_name LogMultiplayer\n"
"\n"
"# Queremos estender o SceneMultiplayer padrão.\n"
"var base_multiplayer = SceneMultiplayer.new()\n"
"\n"
"func _init():\n"
"\t# Apenas encaminha os sinais base (copiados para variáveis para evitar "
"referência cíclica)\n"
"\tvar cts = connected_to_server\n"
"\tvar cf = connection_failed\n"
"\tvar sd = server_disconnected\n"
"\tvar pc = peer_connected\n"
"\tvar pd = peer_disconnected\n"
"\tbase_multiplayer.connected_to_server.connect(func(): cts.emit())\n"
"\tbase_multiplayer.connection_failed.connect(func(): cf.emit())\n"
"\tbase_multiplayer.server_disconnected.connect(func(): sd.emit())\n"
"\tbase_multiplayer.peer_connected.connect(func(id): pc.emit(id))\n"
"\tbase_multiplayer.peer_disconnected.connect(func(id): pd.emit(id))\n"
"\n"
"func _poll():\n"
"\treturn base_multiplayer.poll()\n"
"\n"
"# Registra o RPC sendo feito e o encaminha para o multiplayer padrão.\n"
"func _rpc(peer: int, object: Object, method: StringName, args: Array) -> "
"Error:\n"
"\tprint(\"Got RPC for %d: %s::%s(%s)\" % [peer, object, method, args])\n"
"\treturn base_multiplayer.rpc(peer, object, method, args)\n"
"\n"
"# Registra a adição de configuração. Ex.: caminho raiz (nullptr, NodePath), "
"replicação (Node, Spawner|Synchronizer), personalizado.\n"
"func _object_configuration_add(object, config: Variant) -> Error:\n"
"\tif config is MultiplayerSynchronizer:\n"
"\t\tprint(\"Adding synchronization configuration for %s. Synchronizer: %s\" "
"% [object, config])\n"
"\telif config is MultiplayerSpawner:\n"
"\t\tprint(\"Adding node %s to the spawn list. Spawner: %s\" % [object, "
"config])\n"
"\treturn base_multiplayer.object_configuration_add(object, config)\n"
"\n"
"# Registra a remoção de configuração. Ex.: caminho raiz (nullptr, NodePath), "
"replicação (Node, Spawner|Synchronizer), personalizado.\n"
"func _object_configuration_remove(object, config: Variant) -> Error:\n"
"\tif config is MultiplayerSynchronizer:\n"
"\t\tprint(\"Removing synchronization configuration for %s. Synchronizer: "
"%s\" % [object, config])\n"
"\telif config is MultiplayerSpawner:\n"
"\t\tprint(\"Removing node %s from the spawn list. Spawner: %s\" % [object, "
"config])\n"
"\treturn base_multiplayer.object_configuration_remove(object, config)\n"
"\n"
"# Estes podem ser opcionais, mas neste caso queremos estender o "
"SceneMultiplayer, então encaminhamos tudo.\n"
"func _set_multiplayer_peer(p_peer: MultiplayerPeer):\n"
"\tbase_multiplayer.multiplayer_peer = p_peer\n"
"\n"
"func _get_multiplayer_peer() -> MultiplayerPeer:\n"
"\treturn base_multiplayer.multiplayer_peer\n"
"\n"
"func _get_unique_id() -> int:\n"
"\treturn base_multiplayer.get_unique_id()\n"
"\n"
"func _get_remote_sender_id() -> int:\n"
"\treturn base_multiplayer.get_remote_sender_id()\n"
"\n"
"func _get_peer_ids() -> PackedInt32Array:\n"
"\treturn base_multiplayer.get_peers()\n"
"[/gdscript]\n"
"[/codeblocks]\n"
"Então, na sua cena principal ou em um autoload, chame [method "
"SceneTree.set_multiplayer] para começar a usar sua [MultiplayerAPI] "
"personalizada:\n"
"[codeblocks]\n"
"[gdscript]\n"
"# autoload.gd\n"
"func _enter_tree():\n"
"\t# Define nosso multiplayer personalizado como o principal no SceneTree.\n"
"\tget_tree().set_multiplayer(LogMultiplayer.new())\n"
"[/gdscript]\n"
"[/codeblocks]\n"
"Extensões nativas também podem usar alternativamente o método [method "
"MultiplayerAPI.set_default_interface] durante a inicialização para se "
"configurarem como a implementação padrão."

