#: doc/classes/MultiplayerPeer.xml
msgid ""
"Abstract class for specialized [PacketPeer]s used by the [MultiplayerAPI]."
msgstr ""
"Classe abstrata para [PacketPeer]s especializados usados pelo "
"[MultiplayerAPI]."

#: doc/classes/MultiplayerPeer.xml
msgid ""
"Manages the connection with one or more remote peers acting as server or "
"client and assigning unique IDs to each of them. See also [MultiplayerAPI].\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] The [MultiplayerAPI] protocol is an implementation detail and "
"isn't meant to be used by non-Godot servers. It may change without notice.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] When exporting to Android, make sure to enable the "
"[code]INTERNET[/code] permission in the Android export preset before "
"exporting the project or using one-click deploy. Otherwise, network "
"communication of any kind will be blocked by Android."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/MultiplayerPeer.xml
msgid ""
"Immediately close the multiplayer peer returning to the state [constant "
"CONNECTION_DISCONNECTED]. Connected peers will be dropped without emitting "
"[signal peer_disconnected]."
msgstr ""
"Fecha imediatamente o par multijogador retornando ao estado [constant "
"CONNECTION_DISCONNECTED]. Pares conectados serão desconectados sem emitir o "
"[signal peer_disconnected]."

#: doc/classes/MultiplayerPeer.xml
msgid ""
"Disconnects the given [param peer] from this host. If [param force] is "
"[code]true[/code] the [signal peer_disconnected] signal will not be emitted "
"for this peer."
msgstr ""
"Desconecta o [param peer] fornecido deste host. Se [param force] for "
"[code]true[/code], o sinal [signal peer_disconnected] não será emitido para "
"este peer."

#: doc/classes/MultiplayerPeer.xml
msgid ""
"Returns a randomly generated integer that can be used as a network unique ID."
msgstr ""
"Retorna um número inteiro gerado aleatoriamente que pode ser usado como um "
"ID exclusivo de rede."

#: doc/classes/MultiplayerPeer.xml
msgid "Returns the current state of the connection."
msgstr "Retorna o estado atual da conexão."

#: doc/classes/MultiplayerPeer.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the channel over which the next available packet was received. See "
"[method PacketPeer.get_available_packet_count]."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o canal sobre o qual o próximo pacote disponível foi recebido. Veja "
"também [method PacketPeer.get_available_packet_count]."

#: doc/classes/MultiplayerPeer.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the transfer mode the remote peer used to send the next available "
"packet. See [method PacketPeer.get_available_packet_count]."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o modo de transferência que o par remoto usou para enviar o próximo "
"pacote disponível. Veja [method PacketPeer.get_available_packet_count]."

#: doc/classes/MultiplayerPeer.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the ID of the [MultiplayerPeer] who sent the next available packet. "
"See [method PacketPeer.get_available_packet_count]."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o ID do [MultiplayerPeer] que enviou o próximo pacote disponível. "
"Veja [method PacketPeer.get_available_packet_count]."

#: doc/classes/MultiplayerPeer.xml
msgid "Returns the ID of this [MultiplayerPeer]."
msgstr "Retorna o ID deste [MultiplayerPeer]."

#: doc/classes/MultiplayerPeer.xml
msgid ""
"Returns [code]true[/code] if the server can act as a relay in the current "
"configuration. That is, if the higher level [MultiplayerAPI] should notify "
"connected clients of other peers, and implement a relay protocol to allow "
"communication between them."
msgstr ""
"Retorna [code]true[/code] se o servidor puder agir como um relé na "
"configuração atual. Ou seja, se o [MultiplayerAPI] de nível superior deve "
"notificar os clientes conectados de outros peers e implementar um protocolo "
"de relé para permitir a comunicação entre eles."

#: doc/classes/MultiplayerPeer.xml
msgid "Waits up to 1 second to receive a new network event."
msgstr "Aguarda até 1 segundo para receber um novo evento de rede."

#: doc/classes/MultiplayerPeer.xml
msgid ""
"Sets the peer to which packets will be sent.\n"
"The [param id] can be one of: [constant TARGET_PEER_BROADCAST] to send to "
"all connected peers, [constant TARGET_PEER_SERVER] to send to the peer "
"acting as server, a valid peer ID to send to that specific peer, a negative "
"peer ID to send to all peers except that one. By default, the target peer is "
"[constant TARGET_PEER_BROADCAST]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/MultiplayerPeer.xml
msgid "If [code]true[/code], this [MultiplayerPeer] refuses new connections."
msgstr "Se [code]true[/code], este [MultiplayerPeer] recusa novas conexões."

#: doc/classes/MultiplayerPeer.xml
msgid ""
"The channel to use to send packets. Many network APIs such as ENet and "
"WebRTC allow the creation of multiple independent channels which behaves, in "
"a way, like separate connections. This means that reliable data will only "
"block delivery of other packets on that channel, and ordering will only be "
"in respect to the channel the packet is being sent on. Using different "
"channels to send [b]different and independent[/b] state updates is a common "
"way to optimize network usage and decrease latency in fast-paced games.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] The default channel ([code]0[/code]) actually works as 3 "
"separate channels (one for each [enum TransferMode]) so that [constant "
"TRANSFER_MODE_RELIABLE] and [constant TRANSFER_MODE_UNRELIABLE_ORDERED] does "
"not interact with each other by default. Refer to the specific network API "
"documentation (e.g. ENet or WebRTC) to learn how to set up channels "
"correctly."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/MultiplayerPeer.xml
msgid ""
"The manner in which to send packets to the target peer. See the [method "
"set_target_peer] method."
msgstr ""
"A maneira de enviar pacotes para o peer de destino. Veja o método [method "
"set_target_peer]."

#: doc/classes/MultiplayerPeer.xml
msgid "Emitted when a remote peer connects."
msgstr "Emitido quando um par remoto se conecta."

#: doc/classes/MultiplayerPeer.xml
msgid "Emitted when a remote peer has disconnected."
msgstr "Emitido quando um par remoto se desconectou."

#: doc/classes/MultiplayerPeer.xml
msgid "The MultiplayerPeer is disconnected."
msgstr "O MultiplayerPeer está desconectado."

#: doc/classes/MultiplayerPeer.xml
msgid "The MultiplayerPeer is currently connecting to a server."
msgstr "O MultiplayerPeer está conectando-se a um servidor no momento."

#: doc/classes/MultiplayerPeer.xml
msgid "This MultiplayerPeer is connected."
msgstr "Este MultiplayerPeer está conectado."

#: doc/classes/MultiplayerPeer.xml
msgid "Packets are sent to all connected peers."
msgstr "Os pacotes são enviados para todos os pares conectados."

#: doc/classes/MultiplayerPeer.xml
msgid "Packets are sent to the remote peer acting as server."
msgstr "Os pacotes são enviados para o par remoto atuando como servidor."

#: doc/classes/MultiplayerPeer.xml
msgid ""
"Packets are not acknowledged, no resend attempts are made for lost packets. "
"Packets may arrive in any order. Potentially faster than [constant "
"TRANSFER_MODE_UNRELIABLE_ORDERED]. Use for non-critical data, and always "
"consider whether the order matters."
msgstr ""
"Os pacotes não são confirmados, nenhuma tentativa de reenvio é feita para "
"pacotes perdidos. Os pacotes podem chegar em qualquer ordem. Potencialmente "
"mais rápido que [constant TRANSFER_MODE_UNRELIABLE_ORDERED]. Use para dados "
"não críticos e sempre considere se a ordem importa."

#: doc/classes/MultiplayerPeer.xml
msgid ""
"Packets are not acknowledged, no resend attempts are made for lost packets. "
"Packets are received in the order they were sent in. Potentially faster than "
"[constant TRANSFER_MODE_RELIABLE]. Use for non-critical data or data that "
"would be outdated if received late due to resend attempt(s) anyway, for "
"example movement and positional data."
msgstr ""
"Os pacotes não são confirmados, nenhuma tentativa de reenvio é feita para "
"pacotes perdidos. Os pacotes são recebidos na ordem em que foram enviados. "
"Potencialmente mais rápido que [constant TRANSFER_MODE_RELIABLE]. Use para "
"dados não críticos ou dados que ficariam desatualizados se recebidos tarde "
"de qualquer maneira devido à(s) tentativa(s) de reenvio, por exemplo, dados "
"de movimento e posicionamento."

#: doc/classes/MultiplayerPeer.xml
msgid ""
"Packets must be received and resend attempts should be made until the "
"packets are acknowledged. Packets must be received in the order they were "
"sent in. Most reliable transfer mode, but potentially the slowest due to the "
"overhead. Use for critical data that must be transmitted and arrive in "
"order, for example an ability being triggered or a chat message. Consider "
"carefully if the information really is critical, and use sparingly."
msgstr ""
"Os pacotes devem ser recebidos e tentativas de reenvio devem ser feitas até "
"que os pacotes sejam confirmados. Os pacotes devem ser recebidos na ordem em "
"que foram enviados. É o modo de transferência mais confiável, mas "
"potencialmente o mais lento devido à sobrecarga (overhead). Use para dados "
"críticos que devem ser transmitidos e chegar em ordem, por exemplo, uma "
"habilidade sendo acionada ou uma mensagem de chat. Considere cuidadosamente "
"se a informação é realmente crítica e use com moderação."

#: doc/classes/MultiplayerPeerExtension.xml
msgid ""
"Class that can be inherited to implement custom multiplayer API networking "
"layers via GDExtension."
msgstr ""
"Classe que pode ser herdada para implementar camadas de API de multiplayer "
"personalizadas via GDExtension."

#: doc/classes/MultiplayerPeerExtension.xml
msgid ""
"This class is designed to be inherited from a GDExtension plugin to "
"implement custom networking layers for the multiplayer API (such as WebRTC). "
"All the methods below [b]must[/b] be implemented to have a working custom "
"multiplayer implementation. See also [MultiplayerAPI]."
msgstr ""
"Esta classe foi projetada para ser herdada de um plug-in GDExtension para "
"implementar camadas de rede personalizadas para a API multiplayer (como "
"WebRTC). Todos os métodos abaixo [b]devem[/b] ser implementados para se ter "
"uma implementação multiplayer personalizada funcional. Veja também "
"[MultiplayerAPI]."

#: doc/classes/MultiplayerPeerExtension.xml
msgid ""
"Called when the multiplayer peer should be immediately closed (see [method "
"MultiplayerPeer.close])."
msgstr ""
"Chamado quando o par multiplayer deve ser imediatamente fechado (consulte "
"[method MultiplayerPeer.close])."

#: doc/classes/MultiplayerPeerExtension.xml
msgid ""
"Called when the connected [param peer] should be forcibly disconnected (see "
"[method MultiplayerPeer.disconnect_peer])."
msgstr ""
"Chamado quando o [param peer] conectado deve ser desconectado à força (veja "
"[method MultiplayerPeer.disconnect_peer])."

#: doc/classes/MultiplayerPeerExtension.xml
msgid ""
"Called when the available packet count is internally requested by the "
"[MultiplayerAPI]."
msgstr ""
"Chamado quando a contagem de pacotes disponíveis é solicitada internamente "
"pelo [MultiplayerAPI]."

#: doc/classes/MultiplayerPeerExtension.xml
msgid ""
"Called when the connection status is requested on the [MultiplayerPeer] (see "
"[method MultiplayerPeer.get_connection_status])."
msgstr ""
"Chamado quando o status da conexão é solicitado no [MultiplayerPeer] (veja "
"[method MultiplayerPeer.get_connection_status])."

#: doc/classes/MultiplayerPeerExtension.xml
msgid ""
"Called when the maximum allowed packet size (in bytes) is requested by the "
"[MultiplayerAPI]."
msgstr ""
"Chamado quando o tamanho máximo de pacote permitido (em bytes) é solicitado "
"pelo [MultiplayerAPI]."

#: doc/classes/MultiplayerPeerExtension.xml
msgid ""
"Called when a packet needs to be received by the [MultiplayerAPI], with "
"[param r_buffer_size] being the size of the binary [param r_buffer] in bytes."
msgstr ""
"Chamado quando um pacote precisa ser recebido pelo [MultiplayerAPI], sendo "
"[param r_buffer_size] o tamanho do [param r_buffer] binário em bytes."

#: doc/classes/MultiplayerPeerExtension.xml
msgid ""
"Called to get the channel over which the next available packet was received. "
"See [method MultiplayerPeer.get_packet_channel]."
msgstr ""
"Chamado para obter o canal pelo qual o próximo pacote disponível foi "
"recebido. Veja [method MultiplayerPeer.get_packet_channel]."

#: doc/classes/MultiplayerPeerExtension.xml
msgid ""
"Called to get the transfer mode the remote peer used to send the next "
"available packet. See [method MultiplayerPeer.get_packet_mode]."
msgstr ""
"Chamado para obter o modo de transferência que o par remoto usou para enviar "
"o próximo pacote disponível. Veja [method MultiplayerPeer.get_packet_mode]."

#: doc/classes/MultiplayerPeerExtension.xml
msgid ""
"Called when the ID of the [MultiplayerPeer] who sent the most recent packet "
"is requested (see [method MultiplayerPeer.get_packet_peer])."
msgstr ""
"Chamado quando o ID do [MultiplayerPeer] que enviou o pacote mais recente é "
"solicitado (veja [method MultiplayerPeer.get_packet_peer])."

#: doc/classes/MultiplayerPeerExtension.xml
msgid ""
"Called when a packet needs to be received by the [MultiplayerAPI], if "
"[method _get_packet] isn't implemented. Use this when extending this class "
"via GDScript."
msgstr ""
"Chamado quando um pacote precisa ser recebido pelo [MultiplayerAPI], caso "
"[method _get_packet] não esteja implementado. Use isso ao estender esta "
"classe via GDScript."

#: doc/classes/MultiplayerPeerExtension.xml
msgid ""
"Called when the transfer channel to use is read on this [MultiplayerPeer] "
"(see [member MultiplayerPeer.transfer_channel])."
msgstr ""
"Chamado quando o canal de transferência a ser usado é lido neste "
"[MultiplayerPeer] (veja [member MultiplayerPeer.transfer_channel])."

#: doc/classes/MultiplayerPeerExtension.xml
msgid ""
"Called when the transfer mode to use is read on this [MultiplayerPeer] (see "
"[member MultiplayerPeer.transfer_mode])."
msgstr ""
"Chamado quando o modo de transferência a ser usado é lido neste "
"[MultiplayerPeer] (veja [member MultiplayerPeer.transfer_mode])."

#: doc/classes/MultiplayerPeerExtension.xml
msgid ""
"Called when the unique ID of this [MultiplayerPeer] is requested (see "
"[method MultiplayerPeer.get_unique_id]). The value must be between [code]1[/"
"code] and [code]2147483647[/code]."
msgstr ""
"Chamado quando o ID exclusivo deste [MultiplayerPeer] é solicitado (consulte "
"[method MultiplayerPeer.get_unique_id]). O valor deve estar entre [code]1[/"
"code] e [code]2147483647[/code]."

#: doc/classes/MultiplayerPeerExtension.xml
msgid ""
"Called when the \"refuse new connections\" status is requested on this "
"[MultiplayerPeer] (see [member MultiplayerPeer.refuse_new_connections])."
msgstr ""
"Chamado quando o status \"recusar novas conexões\" é solicitado neste "
"[MultiplayerPeer] (consulte [member MultiplayerPeer.refuse_new_connections])."

#: doc/classes/MultiplayerPeerExtension.xml
msgid ""
"Called when the \"is server\" status is requested on the [MultiplayerAPI]. "
"See [method MultiplayerAPI.is_server]."
msgstr ""
"Chamado quando o status \"é servidor\" é solicitado no [MultiplayerAPI]. "
"Veja [method MultiplayerAPI.is_server]."

#: doc/classes/MultiplayerPeerExtension.xml
msgid ""
"Called to check if the server can act as a relay in the current "
"configuration. See [method MultiplayerPeer.is_server_relay_supported]."
msgstr ""
"Chamado para verificar se o servidor pode atuar como um retransmissor na "
"configuração atual. Veja [method MultiplayerPeer.is_server_relay_supported]."

#: doc/classes/MultiplayerPeerExtension.xml
msgid ""
"Called when the [MultiplayerAPI] is polled. See [method MultiplayerAPI.poll]."
msgstr ""
"Chamado quando o [MultiplayerAPI] é pesquisado. Consulte [method "
"MultiplayerAPI.poll]."

#: doc/classes/MultiplayerPeerExtension.xml
msgid ""
"Called when a packet needs to be sent by the [MultiplayerAPI], with [param "
"buffer_size] being the size of the binary [param buffer] in bytes."
msgstr ""
"Chamado quando um pacote precisa ser enviado pelo [MultiplayerAPI], com "
"[param buffer_size] sendo o tamanho do [param buffer] binário em bytes."

#: doc/classes/MultiplayerPeerExtension.xml
msgid ""
"Called when a packet needs to be sent by the [MultiplayerAPI], if [method "
"_put_packet] isn't implemented. Use this when extending this class via "
"GDScript."
msgstr ""
"Chamado quando um pacote precisa ser enviado pelo [MultiplayerAPI], caso "
"[method _put_packet] não esteja implementado. Use isso ao estender esta "
"classe via GDScript."

#: doc/classes/MultiplayerPeerExtension.xml
msgid ""
"Called when the \"refuse new connections\" status is set on this "
"[MultiplayerPeer] (see [member MultiplayerPeer.refuse_new_connections])."
msgstr ""
"Chamado quando o status \"recusar novas conexões\" é definido neste "
"[MultiplayerPeer] (veja [member MultiplayerPeer.refuse_new_connections])."

#: doc/classes/MultiplayerPeerExtension.xml
msgid ""
"Called when the target peer to use is set for this [MultiplayerPeer] (see "
"[method MultiplayerPeer.set_target_peer])."
msgstr ""
"Chamado quando o peer de destino a ser usado é definido para este "
"[MultiplayerPeer] (veja [member MultiplayerPeer.set_target_peer])."

#: doc/classes/MultiplayerPeerExtension.xml
msgid ""
"Called when the channel to use is set for this [MultiplayerPeer] (see "
"[member MultiplayerPeer.transfer_channel])."
msgstr ""
"Chamado quando o canal a ser usado é definido para este [MultiplayerPeer] "
"(veja [member MultiplayerPeer.transfer_channel])."

#: doc/classes/MultiplayerPeerExtension.xml
msgid ""
"Called when the transfer mode is set on this [MultiplayerPeer] (see [member "
"MultiplayerPeer.transfer_mode])."
msgstr ""
"Chamado quando o modo de transferência é definido neste [MultiplayerPeer] "
"(consulte [member MultiplayerPeer.transfer_mode])."

#: modules/multiplayer/doc_classes/MultiplayerSpawner.xml
msgid ""
"Automatically replicates spawnable nodes from the authority to other "
"multiplayer peers."
msgstr ""
"Replicia automaticamente nós passíveis de spawn da autoridade para outros "
"pares multiplayer."

#: modules/multiplayer/doc_classes/MultiplayerSpawner.xml
msgid ""
"Spawnable scenes can be configured in the editor or through code (see "
"[method add_spawnable_scene]).\n"
"Also supports custom node spawns through [method spawn], calling [member "
"spawn_function] on all peers.\n"
"Internally, [MultiplayerSpawner] uses [method "
"MultiplayerAPI.object_configuration_add] to notify spawns passing the "
"spawned node as the [code]object[/code] and itself as the "
"[code]configuration[/code], and [method "
"MultiplayerAPI.object_configuration_remove] to notify despawns in a similar "
"way."
msgstr ""

#: modules/multiplayer/doc_classes/MultiplayerSpawner.xml
msgid ""
"Adds a scene path to spawnable scenes, making it automatically replicated "
"from the multiplayer authority to other peers when added as children of the "
"node pointed by [member spawn_path]."
msgstr ""
"Adiciona um caminho de cena a cenas geráveis, fazendo com que seja replicado "
"automaticamente da autoridade multiplayer para outros pares quando "
"adicionado como filho do nó apontado por [member spawn_path]."

#: modules/multiplayer/doc_classes/MultiplayerSpawner.xml
msgid ""
"Clears all spawnable scenes. Does not despawn existing instances on remote "
"peers."
msgstr ""
"Limpa todas as cenas geráveis (spawnable). Não remove instâncias existentes "
"em pares remotos."

#: modules/multiplayer/doc_classes/MultiplayerSpawner.xml
msgid "Returns the spawnable scene path by index."
msgstr "Retorna o caminho da cena gerável por índice."

#: modules/multiplayer/doc_classes/MultiplayerSpawner.xml
msgid "Returns the count of spawnable scene paths."
msgstr "Retorna a contagem de caminhos de cena geráveis."

#: modules/multiplayer/doc_classes/MultiplayerSpawner.xml
msgid ""
"Requests a custom spawn, with [param data] passed to [member spawn_function] "
"on all peers. Returns the locally spawned node instance already inside the "
"scene tree, and added as a child of the node pointed by [member "
"spawn_path].\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Spawnable scenes are spawned automatically. [method spawn] is "
"only needed for custom spawns."
msgstr ""

#: modules/multiplayer/doc_classes/MultiplayerSpawner.xml
msgid ""
"Method called on all peers when a custom [method spawn] is requested by the "
"authority. Will receive the [code]data[/code] parameter, and should return a "
"[Node] that is not in the scene tree.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] The returned node should [b]not[/b] be added to the scene with "
"[method Node.add_child]. This is done automatically."
msgstr ""

#: modules/multiplayer/doc_classes/MultiplayerSpawner.xml
msgid ""
"Maximum number of nodes allowed to be spawned by this spawner. Includes both "
"spawnable scenes and custom spawns.\n"
"When set to [code]0[/code] (the default), there is no limit."
msgstr ""

#: modules/multiplayer/doc_classes/MultiplayerSpawner.xml
msgid ""
"Path to the spawn root. Spawnable scenes that are added as direct children "
"are replicated to other peers."
msgstr ""
"Caminho para a raiz de spawn. Cenas geráveis que são adicionadas como filhos "
"diretos são replicadas para outros peers."

#: modules/multiplayer/doc_classes/MultiplayerSpawner.xml
msgid ""
"Emitted when a spawnable scene or custom spawn was despawned by the "
"multiplayer authority. Only called on remote peers."
msgstr ""
"Emitido quando uma cena gerável ou geração personalizada foi desagregada "
"pela autoridade multiplayer. Chamado apenas em peers remotos."

#: modules/multiplayer/doc_classes/MultiplayerSpawner.xml
msgid ""
"Emitted when a spawnable scene or custom spawn was spawned by the "
"multiplayer authority. Only called on remote peers."
msgstr ""
"Emitido quando uma cena gerável ou geração personalizada foi gerada pela "
"autoridade multiplayer. Chamado apenas em peers remotos."

#: modules/multiplayer/doc_classes/MultiplayerSynchronizer.xml
msgid ""
"Synchronizes properties from the multiplayer authority to the remote peers."
msgstr ""
"Sincroniza propriedades da autoridade multiplayer para os pares remotos."

#: modules/multiplayer/doc_classes/MultiplayerSynchronizer.xml
msgid ""
"By default, [MultiplayerSynchronizer] synchronizes configured properties to "
"all peers.\n"
"Visibility can be handled directly with [method set_visibility_for] or as-"
"needed with [method add_visibility_filter] and [method update_visibility].\n"
"[MultiplayerSpawner]s will handle nodes according to visibility of "
"synchronizers as long as the node at [member root_path] was spawned by one.\n"
"Internally, [MultiplayerSynchronizer] uses [method "
"MultiplayerAPI.object_configuration_add] to notify synchronization start "
"passing the [Node] at [member root_path] as the [code]object[/code] and "
"itself as the [code]configuration[/code], and uses [method "
"MultiplayerAPI.object_configuration_remove] to notify synchronization end in "
"a similar way.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Synchronization is not supported for [Object] type properties, "
"like [Resource]. Properties that are unique to each peer, like the instance "
"IDs of [Object]s (see [method Object.get_instance_id]) or [RID]s, will also "
"not work in synchronization."
msgstr ""

#: modules/multiplayer/doc_classes/MultiplayerSynchronizer.xml
msgid ""
"Adds a peer visibility filter for this synchronizer.\n"
"[param filter] should take a peer ID [int] and return a [bool]."
msgstr ""

#: modules/multiplayer/doc_classes/MultiplayerSynchronizer.xml
msgid "Queries the current visibility for peer [param peer]."
msgstr "Consulta a visibilidade atual para o par [param peer]."

#: modules/multiplayer/doc_classes/MultiplayerSynchronizer.xml
msgid "Removes a peer visibility filter from this synchronizer."
msgstr "Remove um filtro de visibilidade de pares deste sincronizador."

#: modules/multiplayer/doc_classes/MultiplayerSynchronizer.xml
msgid ""
"Sets the visibility of [param peer] to [param visible]. If [param peer] is "
"[code]0[/code], the value of [member public_visibility] will be updated "
"instead."
msgstr ""
"Define a visibilidade de [param peer] para [param visible]. Se [param peer] "
"for [code]0[/code], o valor de [member public_visibility] será atualizado em "
"vez disso."

#: modules/multiplayer/doc_classes/MultiplayerSynchronizer.xml
msgid ""
"Updates the visibility of [param for_peer] according to visibility filters. "
"If [param for_peer] is [code]0[/code] (the default), all peers' visibilties "
"are updated."
msgstr ""
"Atualiza a visibilidade de [param for_peer] de acordo com os filtros de "
"visibilidade. Se [param for_peer] for [code]0[/code] (o padrão), as "
"visibilidades de todos os peers são atualizadas."

#: modules/multiplayer/doc_classes/MultiplayerSynchronizer.xml
msgid ""
"Time interval between delta synchronizations. Used when the replication is "
"set to [constant SceneReplicationConfig.REPLICATION_MODE_ON_CHANGE]. If set "
"to [code]0.0[/code] (the default), delta synchronizations happen every "
"network process frame."
msgstr ""
"Intervalo de tempo entre sincronizações delta. Usado quando a replicação "
"está definida como [constant "
"SceneReplicationConfig.REPLICATION_MODE_ON_CHANGE]. Se definido como "
"[code]0.0[/code] (o padrão), as sincronizações delta ocorrem a cada quadro "
"de processo de rede."

#: modules/multiplayer/doc_classes/MultiplayerSynchronizer.xml
msgid ""
"Whether synchronization should be visible to all peers by default. See "
"[method set_visibility_for] and [method add_visibility_filter] for ways of "
"configuring fine-grained visibility options."
msgstr ""
"Se a sincronização deve estar visível para todos os pares por padrão. "
"Consulte [method set_visibility_for] e [method add_visibility_filter] para "
"maneiras de configurar opções de visibilidade detalhadas."

#: modules/multiplayer/doc_classes/MultiplayerSynchronizer.xml
msgid "Resource containing which properties to synchronize."
msgstr "Recurso que contém quais propriedades sincronizar."

#: modules/multiplayer/doc_classes/MultiplayerSynchronizer.xml
msgid ""
"Time interval between synchronizations. Used when the replication is set to "
"[constant SceneReplicationConfig.REPLICATION_MODE_ALWAYS]. If set to "
"[code]0.0[/code] (the default), synchronizations happen every network "
"process frame."
msgstr ""
"Intervalo de tempo entre sincronizações. Usado quando a replicação está "
"definida como [constant SceneReplicationConfig.REPLICATION_MODE_ALWAYS]. Se "
"definido como [code]0.0[/code] (o padrão), as sincronizações ocorrem a cada "
"quadro de processo de rede."

#: modules/multiplayer/doc_classes/MultiplayerSynchronizer.xml
msgid ""
"Node path that replicated properties are relative to.\n"
"If [member root_path] was spawned by a [MultiplayerSpawner], the node will "
"be also be spawned and despawned based on this synchronizer visibility "
"options."
msgstr ""

#: modules/multiplayer/doc_classes/MultiplayerSynchronizer.xml
msgid "Specifies when visibility filters are updated."
msgstr "Especifica quando os filtros de visibilidade são atualizados."

#: modules/multiplayer/doc_classes/MultiplayerSynchronizer.xml
msgid ""
"Emitted when a new delta synchronization state is received by this "
"synchronizer after the properties have been updated."
msgstr ""
"Emitido quando um novo estado de sincronização delta é recebido por este "
"sincronizador após as propriedades terem sido atualizadas."

#: modules/multiplayer/doc_classes/MultiplayerSynchronizer.xml
msgid ""
"Emitted when a new synchronization state is received by this synchronizer "
"after the properties have been updated."
msgstr ""
"Emitido quando um novo estado de sincronização é recebido por este "
"sincronizador após as propriedades terem sido atualizadas."

#: modules/multiplayer/doc_classes/MultiplayerSynchronizer.xml
msgid ""
"Emitted when visibility of [param for_peer] is updated. See [method "
"update_visibility]."
msgstr ""
"Emitido quando a visibilidade de [param for_peer] é atualizada. Veja [method "
"update_visibility]."

#: modules/multiplayer/doc_classes/MultiplayerSynchronizer.xml
msgid ""
"Visibility filters are updated during process frames (see [constant "
"Node.NOTIFICATION_INTERNAL_PROCESS])."
msgstr ""
"Os filtros de visibilidade são atualizados durante os quadros de processo "
"(consulte [constant Node.NOTIFICATION_INTERNAL_PROCESS])."

#: modules/multiplayer/doc_classes/MultiplayerSynchronizer.xml
msgid ""
"Visibility filters are updated during physics frames (see [constant "
"Node.NOTIFICATION_INTERNAL_PHYSICS_PROCESS])."
msgstr ""
"Os filtros de visibilidade são atualizados durante os quadros de física "
"(veja [constant Node.NOTIFICATION_INTERNAL_PHYSICS_PROCESS])."

#: modules/multiplayer/doc_classes/MultiplayerSynchronizer.xml
msgid ""
"Visibility filters are not updated automatically, and must be updated "
"manually by calling [method update_visibility]."
msgstr ""
"Os filtros de visibilidade não são atualizados automaticamente e devem ser "
"atualizados manualmente chamando [method update_visibility]."

#: doc/classes/Mutex.xml
msgid "A binary [Semaphore] for synchronization of multiple [Thread]s."
msgstr "Um [Semaphore] binário para sincronização de múltiplas [Thread]s."

#: doc/classes/Mutex.xml
msgid ""
"A synchronization mutex (mutual exclusion). This is used to synchronize "
"multiple [Thread]s, and is equivalent to a binary [Semaphore]. It guarantees "
"that only one thread can access a critical section at a time.\n"
"This is a reentrant mutex, meaning that it can be locked multiple times by "
"one thread, provided it also unlocks it as many times.\n"
"[b]Warning:[/b] To ensure proper cleanup without crashes or deadlocks, the "
"following conditions must be met:\n"
"- When a [Mutex]'s reference count reaches zero and it is therefore "
"destroyed, no threads (including the one on which the destruction will "
"happen) must have it locked.\n"
"- When a [Thread]'s reference count reaches zero and it is therefore "
"destroyed, it must not have any mutex locked."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Mutex.xml doc/classes/Semaphore.xml doc/classes/Thread.xml
#: doc/classes/WorkerThreadPool.xml
msgid "Using multiple threads"
msgstr "Usando múltiplos threads"

#: doc/classes/Mutex.xml doc/classes/Semaphore.xml doc/classes/Thread.xml
#: doc/classes/WorkerThreadPool.xml
msgid "Thread-safe APIs"
msgstr "APIs Thread-Safes"

#: doc/classes/Mutex.xml
msgid ""
"Locks this [Mutex], blocks until it is unlocked by the current owner.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] This function returns without blocking if the thread already "
"has ownership of the mutex."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Mutex.xml
msgid ""
"Tries locking this [Mutex], but does not block. Returns [code]true[/code] on "
"success, [code]false[/code] otherwise.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] This function returns [code]true[/code] if the thread already "
"has ownership of the mutex."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Mutex.xml
msgid ""
"Unlocks this [Mutex], leaving it to other threads.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] If a thread called [method lock] or [method try_lock] multiple "
"times while already having ownership of the mutex, it must also call [method "
"unlock] the same number of times in order to unlock it correctly.\n"
"[b]Warning:[/b] Calling [method unlock] more times than [method lock] on a "
"given thread, thus ending up trying to unlock a non-locked mutex, is wrong "
"and may causes crashes or deadlocks."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/NativeMenu.xml
msgid "A server interface for OS native menus."
msgstr "Uma interface de servidor para menus nativos do SO."

#: doc/classes/NativeMenu.xml
msgid ""
"[NativeMenu] handles low-level access to the OS native global menu bar and "
"popup menus.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] This is low-level API, consider using [MenuBar] with [member "
"MenuBar.prefer_global_menu] set to [code]true[/code], and [PopupMenu] with "
"[member PopupMenu.prefer_native_menu] set to [code]true[/code].\n"
"To create a menu, use [method create_menu], add menu items using "
"[code]add_*_item[/code] methods. To remove a menu, use [method free_menu].\n"
"[codeblock]\n"
"var menu\n"
"\n"
"func _menu_callback(item_id):\n"
"\tif item_id == \"ITEM_CUT\":\n"
"\t\tcut()\n"
"\telif item_id == \"ITEM_COPY\":\n"
"\t\tcopy()\n"
"\telif item_id == \"ITEM_PASTE\":\n"
"\t\tpaste()\n"
"\n"
"func _enter_tree():\n"
"\t# Create new menu and add items:\n"
"\tmenu = NativeMenu.create_menu()\n"
"\tNativeMenu.add_item(menu, \"Cut\", _menu_callback, Callable(), "
"\"ITEM_CUT\")\n"
"\tNativeMenu.add_item(menu, \"Copy\", _menu_callback, Callable(), "
"\"ITEM_COPY\")\n"
"\tNativeMenu.add_separator(menu)\n"
"\tNativeMenu.add_item(menu, \"Paste\", _menu_callback, Callable(), "
"\"ITEM_PASTE\")\n"
"\n"
"func _on_button_pressed():\n"
"\t# Show popup menu at mouse position:\n"
"\tNativeMenu.popup(menu, DisplayServer.mouse_get_position())\n"
"\n"
"func _exit_tree():\n"
"\t# Remove menu when it's no longer needed:\n"
"\tNativeMenu.free_menu(menu)\n"
"[/codeblock]"
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/NativeMenu.xml
msgid ""
"Adds a new checkable item with text [param label] to the global menu [param "
"rid].\n"
"Returns index of the inserted item, it's not guaranteed to be the same as "
"[param index] value.\n"
"An [param accelerator] can optionally be defined, which is a keyboard "
"shortcut that can be pressed to trigger the menu button even if it's not "
"currently open. The [param accelerator] is generally a combination of [enum "
"KeyModifierMask]s and [enum Key]s using bitwise OR such as "
"[code]KEY_MASK_CTRL | KEY_A[/code] ([kbd]Ctrl + A[/kbd]).\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] The [param callback] and [param key_callback] Callables need to "
"accept exactly one Variant parameter, the parameter passed to the Callables "
"will be the value passed to [param tag].\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] This method is implemented on macOS and Windows.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] On Windows, [param accelerator] and [param key_callback] are "
"ignored."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/NativeMenu.xml
msgid ""
