#: doc/classes/PackedVector4Array.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the slice of the [PackedVector4Array], from [param begin] "
"(inclusive) to [param end] (exclusive), as a new [PackedVector4Array].\n"
"The absolute value of [param begin] and [param end] will be clamped to the "
"array size, so the default value for [param end] makes it slice to the size "
"of the array by default (i.e. [code]arr.slice(1)[/code] is a shorthand for "
"[code]arr.slice(1, arr.size())[/code]).\n"
"If either [param begin] or [param end] are negative, they will be relative "
"to the end of the array (i.e. [code]arr.slice(0, -2)[/code] is a shorthand "
"for [code]arr.slice(0, arr.size() - 2)[/code])."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/PackedVector4Array.xml
msgid ""
"Returns a new [PackedVector4Array] with contents of [param right] added at "
"the end of this array. For better performance, consider using [method "
"append_array] instead."
msgstr ""
"Retorna um novo [PackedVector4Array] com o conteúdo de [param right] "
"adicionado ao final deste array. Para melhor desempenho, considere usar "
"[method append_array] em vez disso."

#: doc/classes/PackedVector4Array.xml
msgid ""
"Returns [code]true[/code] if contents of both arrays are the same, i.e. they "
"have all equal [Vector4]s at the corresponding indices."
msgstr ""
"Retorna [code]true[/code] se o conteúdo de ambos os arrays for o mesmo, ou "
"seja, se eles tiverem todos os [Vector4]s iguais nos índices correspondentes."

#: doc/classes/PackedVector4Array.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the [Vector4] at index [param index]. Negative indices can be used "
"to access the elements starting from the end. Using index out of array's "
"bounds will result in an error."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o [Vector4] no índice [param index]. Índices negativos podem ser "
"usados para acessar os elementos começando do fim. Usar um índice fora dos "
"limites da matriz resultará em um erro."

#: doc/classes/PacketPeer.xml
msgid "Abstraction and base class for packet-based protocols."
msgstr "Abstração e classe base para protocolos baseados em pacotes."

#: doc/classes/PacketPeer.xml
msgid ""
"PacketPeer is an abstraction and base class for packet-based protocols (such "
"as UDP). It provides an API for sending and receiving packets both as raw "
"data or variables. This makes it easy to transfer data over a protocol, "
"without having to encode data as low-level bytes or having to worry about "
"network ordering.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] When exporting to Android, make sure to enable the "
"[code]INTERNET[/code] permission in the Android export preset before "
"exporting the project or using one-click deploy. Otherwise, network "
"communication of any kind will be blocked by Android."
msgstr ""
"PacketPeer é uma abstração e classe base para protocolos baseados em pacotes "
"(como UDP). Ele fornece uma API para enviar e receber pacotes como dados "
"brutos ou variáveis. Isso facilita a transferência de dados por meio de um "
"protocolo, sem a necessidade de codificar os dados como bytes de baixo nível "
"ou de se preocupar com a ordenação da rede.\n"
"[b]Nota:[/b] Ao exportar para o Android, certifique-se de ativar a permissão "
"[code]INTERNET[/code] na predefinição de exportação do Android antes de "
"exportar o projeto ou usar a implantação com um clique. Caso contrário, "
"qualquer tipo de comunicação de rede será bloqueada pelo Android."

#: doc/classes/PacketPeer.xml
msgid "Returns the number of packets currently available in the ring-buffer."
msgstr "Retorna o número de pacotes disponíveis atualmente no buffer circular."

#: doc/classes/PacketPeer.xml
msgid "Gets a raw packet."
msgstr "Obtém um pacote bruto."

#: doc/classes/PacketPeer.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the error state of the last packet received (via [method get_packet] "
"and [method get_var])."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o estado de erro do último pacote recebido (via [method get_packet] "
"e [method get_var])."

#: doc/classes/PacketPeer.xml
msgid ""
"Gets a Variant. If [param allow_objects] is [code]true[/code], decoding "
"objects is allowed.\n"
"Internally, this uses the same decoding mechanism as the [method "
"@GlobalScope.bytes_to_var] method.\n"
"[b]Warning:[/b] Deserialized objects can contain code which gets executed. "
"Do not use this option if the serialized object comes from untrusted sources "
"to avoid potential security threats such as remote code execution."
msgstr ""
"Obtém um Variant. Se [param allow_objects] for [code]true[/code], a "
"decodificação de objetos é permitida.\n"
"Internamente, isso utiliza o mesmo mecanismo de decodificação do método "
"[method @GlobalScope.bytes_to_var].\n"
"[b]Aviso:[/b] Objetos desserializados podem conter código que é executado. "
"Não utilize esta opção se o objeto serializado provier de fontes não "
"confiáveis, para evitar possíveis ameaças à segurança, como a execução "
"remota de código."

#: doc/classes/PacketPeer.xml
msgid "Sends a raw packet."
msgstr "Envia um pacote bruto."

#: doc/classes/PacketPeer.xml
msgid ""
"Sends a [Variant] as a packet. If [param full_objects] is [code]true[/code], "
"encoding objects is allowed (and can potentially include code).\n"
"Internally, this uses the same encoding mechanism as the [method "
"@GlobalScope.var_to_bytes] method."
msgstr ""
"Envia um [Variant] como um pacote. Se [param full_objects] for [code]true[/"
"code], a codificação de objetos será permitida (e poderá incluir código "
"potencialmente).\n"
"Internamente, isso usa o mesmo mecanismo de codificação que o método [method "
"@GlobalScope.var_to_bytes]."

#: doc/classes/PacketPeer.xml
msgid ""
"Maximum buffer size allowed when encoding [Variant]s. Raise this value to "
"support heavier memory allocations.\n"
"The [method put_var] method allocates memory on the stack, and the buffer "
"used will grow automatically to the closest power of two to match the size "
"of the [Variant]. If the [Variant] is bigger than [member "
"encode_buffer_max_size], the method will error out with [constant "
"ERR_OUT_OF_MEMORY]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/PacketPeerDTLS.xml
msgid "DTLS packet peer."
msgstr "Par de pacotes DTLS."

#: doc/classes/PacketPeerDTLS.xml
msgid ""
"This class represents a DTLS peer connection. It can be used to connect to a "
"DTLS server, and is returned by [method DTLSServer.take_connection].\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] When exporting to Android, make sure to enable the "
"[code]INTERNET[/code] permission in the Android export preset before "
"exporting the project or using one-click deploy. Otherwise, network "
"communication of any kind will be blocked by Android.\n"
"[b]Warning:[/b] TLS certificate revocation and certificate pinning are "
"currently not supported. Revoked certificates are accepted as long as they "
"are otherwise valid. If this is a concern, you may want to use automatically "
"managed certificates with a short validity period."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/PacketPeerDTLS.xml
msgid ""
"Connects a [param packet_peer] beginning the DTLS handshake using the "
"underlying [PacketPeerUDP] which must be connected (see [method "
"PacketPeerUDP.connect_to_host]). You can optionally specify the [param "
"client_options] to be used while verifying the TLS connections. See [method "
"TLSOptions.client] and [method TLSOptions.client_unsafe]."
msgstr ""
"Conecta um [param packet_peer] iniciando o handshake DTLS usando o "
"[PacketPeerUDP] subjacente que deve estar conectado (consulte [method "
"PacketPeerUDP.connect_to_host]). Você pode especificar opcionalmente as "
"[param client_options] a serem usadas ao verificar as conexões TLS. Consulte "
"[method TLSOptions.client] e [method TLSOptions.client_unsafe]."

#: doc/classes/PacketPeerDTLS.xml
msgid "Disconnects this peer, terminating the DTLS session."
msgstr "Desconecta este par, terminando a sessão DTLS."

#: doc/classes/PacketPeerDTLS.xml doc/classes/StreamPeerSocket.xml
#: doc/classes/StreamPeerTLS.xml
msgid "Returns the status of the connection."
msgstr "Retorna o status da conexão."

#: doc/classes/PacketPeerDTLS.xml
msgid ""
"Poll the connection to check for incoming packets. Call this frequently to "
"update the status and keep the connection working."
msgstr ""
"Executa o polling na conexão para verificar pacotes de entrada. Chame isso "
"com frequência para atualizar o status e manter a conexão funcionando."

#: doc/classes/PacketPeerDTLS.xml
msgid "A status representing a [PacketPeerDTLS] that is disconnected."
msgstr "Um status representando um [PacketPeerDTLS] que está desconectado."

#: doc/classes/PacketPeerDTLS.xml
msgid ""
"A status representing a [PacketPeerDTLS] that is currently performing the "
"handshake with a remote peer."
msgstr ""
"Um status que representa um [PacketPeerDTLS] que está executando no momento "
"o handshake com um par remoto."

#: doc/classes/PacketPeerDTLS.xml
msgid ""
"A status representing a [PacketPeerDTLS] that is connected to a remote peer."
msgstr ""
"Um status representando um [PacketPeerDTLS] que está conectado a um par "
"remoto."

#: doc/classes/PacketPeerDTLS.xml
msgid "A status representing a [PacketPeerDTLS] in a generic error state."
msgstr ""
"Um status representando um [PacketPeerDTLS] em um estado de erro genérico."

#: doc/classes/PacketPeerDTLS.xml
msgid ""
"An error status that shows a mismatch in the DTLS certificate domain "
"presented by the host and the domain requested for validation."
msgstr ""
"Um status de erro que mostra uma incompatibilidade no domínio do certificado "
"DTLS apresentado pelo host e o domínio solicitado para validação."

#: doc/classes/PacketPeerStream.xml
msgid "Wrapper to use a PacketPeer over a StreamPeer."
msgstr "Wrapper para usar um PacketPeer sobre um StreamPeer."

#: doc/classes/PacketPeerStream.xml
msgid ""
"PacketStreamPeer provides a wrapper for working using packets over a stream. "
"This allows for using packet based code with StreamPeers. PacketPeerStream "
"implements a custom protocol over the StreamPeer, so the user should not "
"read or write to the wrapped StreamPeer directly.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] When exporting to Android, make sure to enable the "
"[code]INTERNET[/code] permission in the Android export preset before "
"exporting the project or using one-click deploy. Otherwise, network "
"communication of any kind will be blocked by Android."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/PacketPeerStream.xml
msgid "The wrapped [StreamPeer] object."
msgstr "O objeto [StreamPeer] empacotado."

#: doc/classes/PacketPeerUDP.xml
msgid "UDP packet peer."
msgstr "Par de pacotes UDP."

#: doc/classes/PacketPeerUDP.xml
msgid ""
"UDP packet peer. Can be used to send and receive raw UDP packets as well as "
"[Variant]s.\n"
"[b]Example:[/b] Send a packet:\n"
"[codeblock]\n"
"var peer = PacketPeerUDP.new()\n"
"\n"
"# Optionally, you can select the local port used to send the packet.\n"
"peer.bind(4444)\n"
"\n"
"peer.set_dest_address(\"1.1.1.1\", 4433)\n"
"peer.put_packet(\"hello\".to_utf8_buffer())\n"
"[/codeblock]\n"
"[b]Example:[/b] Listen for packets:\n"
"[codeblock]\n"
"var peer\n"
"\n"
"func _ready():\n"
"\tpeer = PacketPeerUDP.new()\n"
"\tpeer.bind(4433)\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"func _process(_delta):\n"
"\tif peer.get_available_packet_count() > 0:\n"
"\t\tvar array_bytes = peer.get_packet()\n"
"\t\tvar packet_string = array_bytes.get_string_from_ascii()\n"
"\t\tprint(\"Received message: \", packet_string)\n"
"[/codeblock]\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] When exporting to Android, make sure to enable the "
"[code]INTERNET[/code] permission in the Android export preset before "
"exporting the project or using one-click deploy. Otherwise, network "
"communication of any kind will be blocked by Android."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/PacketPeerUDP.xml
msgid ""
"Binds this [PacketPeerUDP] to the specified [param port] and [param "
"bind_address] with a buffer size [param recv_buf_size], allowing it to "
"receive incoming packets.\n"
"If [param bind_address] is set to [code]\"*\"[/code] (default), the peer "
"will be bound on all available addresses (both IPv4 and IPv6).\n"
"If [param bind_address] is set to [code]\"0.0.0.0\"[/code] (for IPv4) or "
"[code]\"::\"[/code] (for IPv6), the peer will be bound to all available "
"addresses matching that IP type.\n"
"If [param bind_address] is set to any valid address (e.g. [code]"
"\"192.168.1.101\"[/code], [code]\"::1\"[/code], etc.), the peer will only be "
"bound to the interface with that address (or fail if no interface with the "
"given address exists)."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/PacketPeerUDP.xml
msgid "Closes the [PacketPeerUDP]'s underlying UDP socket."
msgstr "Fecha o socket UDP subjacente do [PacketPeerUDP]."

#: doc/classes/PacketPeerUDP.xml
msgid ""
"Calling this method connects this UDP peer to the given [param host]/[param "
"port] pair. UDP is in reality connectionless, so this option only means that "
"incoming packets from different addresses are automatically discarded, and "
"that outgoing packets are always sent to the connected address (future calls "
"to [method set_dest_address] are not allowed). This method does not send any "
"data to the remote peer, to do that, use [method PacketPeer.put_var] or "
"[method PacketPeer.put_packet] as usual. See also [UDPServer].\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Connecting to the remote peer does not help to protect from "
"malicious attacks like IP spoofing, etc. Think about using an encryption "
"technique like TLS or DTLS if you feel like your application is transferring "
"sensitive information."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/PacketPeerUDP.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the IP of the remote peer that sent the last packet(that was "
"received with [method PacketPeer.get_packet] or [method PacketPeer.get_var])."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o IP do par remoto que enviou o último pacote (que foi recebido com "
"[method PacketPeer.get_packet] ou [method PacketPeer.get_var])."

#: doc/classes/PacketPeerUDP.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the port of the remote peer that sent the last packet(that was "
"received with [method PacketPeer.get_packet] or [method PacketPeer.get_var])."
msgstr ""
"Retorna a porta do par remoto que enviou o último pacote (que foi recebido "
"com [method PacketPeer.get_packet] ou [method PacketPeer.get_var])."

#: doc/classes/PacketPeerUDP.xml
msgid ""
"Returns whether this [PacketPeerUDP] is bound to an address and can receive "
"packets."
msgstr ""
"Retorna se este [PacketPeerUDP] está vinculado a um endereço e pode receber "
"pacotes."

#: doc/classes/PacketPeerUDP.xml
msgid ""
"Returns [code]true[/code] if the UDP socket is open and has been connected "
"to a remote address. See [method connect_to_host]."
msgstr ""
"Retorna [code]true[/code] se o socket UDP estiver aberto e conectado a um "
"endereço remoto. Veja [method connect_to_host]."

#: doc/classes/PacketPeerUDP.xml
msgid ""
"Joins the multicast group specified by [param multicast_address] using the "
"interface identified by [param interface_name].\n"
"You can join the same multicast group with multiple interfaces. Use [method "
"IP.get_local_interfaces] to know which are available.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Some Android devices might require the "
"[code]CHANGE_WIFI_MULTICAST_STATE[/code] permission for multicast to work."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/PacketPeerUDP.xml
msgid ""
"Removes the interface identified by [param interface_name] from the "
"multicast group specified by [param multicast_address]."
msgstr ""
"Remove a interface identificada por [param interface_name] do grupo "
"multicast especificado por [param multicast_address]."

#: doc/classes/PacketPeerUDP.xml
msgid ""
"Enable or disable sending of broadcast packets (e.g. "
"[code]set_dest_address(\"255.255.255.255\", 4343)[/code]. This option is "
"disabled by default.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Some Android devices might require the "
"[code]CHANGE_WIFI_MULTICAST_STATE[/code] permission and this option to be "
"enabled to receive broadcast packets too."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/PacketPeerUDP.xml
msgid ""
"Sets the destination address and port for sending packets and variables. A "
"hostname will be resolved using DNS if needed.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] [method set_broadcast_enabled] must be enabled before sending "
"packets to a broadcast address (e.g. [code]255.255.255.255[/code])."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/PacketPeerUDP.xml
msgid ""
"Waits for a packet to arrive on the bound address. See [method bind].\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] [method wait] can't be interrupted once it has been called. "
"This can be worked around by allowing the other party to send a specific "
"\"death pill\" packet like this:\n"
"[codeblocks]\n"
"[gdscript]\n"
"socket = PacketPeerUDP.new()\n"
"# Server\n"
"socket.set_dest_address(\"127.0.0.1\", 789)\n"
"socket.put_packet(\"Time to stop\".to_ascii_buffer())\n"
"\n"
"# Client\n"
"while socket.wait() == OK:\n"
"\tvar data = socket.get_packet().get_string_from_ascii()\n"
"\tif data == \"Time to stop\":\n"
"\t\treturn\n"
"[/gdscript]\n"
"[csharp]\n"
"var socket = new PacketPeerUdp();\n"
"// Server\n"
"socket.SetDestAddress(\"127.0.0.1\", 789);\n"
"socket.PutPacket(\"Time to stop\".ToAsciiBuffer());\n"
"\n"
"// Client\n"
"while (socket.Wait() == OK)\n"
"{\n"
"\tstring data = socket.GetPacket().GetStringFromASCII();\n"
"\tif (data == \"Time to stop\")\n"
"\t{\n"
"\t\treturn;\n"
"\t}\n"
"}\n"
"[/csharp]\n"
"[/codeblocks]"
msgstr ""
"Aguarda a chegada de um pacote no endereço vinculado. Consulte [method "
"bind].\n"
"[b]Nota:[/b] [method wait] não pode ser interrompido após ser chamado. Isso "
"pode ser contornado permitindo que a outra parte envie um pacote específico "
"de \"pílula de veneno\" (death pill) como este:\n"
"[codeblocks]\n"
"[gdscript]\n"
"socket = PacketPeerUDP.new()\n"
"# Servidor\n"
"socket.set_dest_address(\"127.0.0.1\", 789)\n"
"socket.put_packet(\"Time to stop\".to_ascii_buffer())\n"
"\n"
"# Cliente\n"
"while socket.wait() == OK:\n"
"\tvar data = socket.get_packet().get_string_from_ascii()\n"
"\tif data == \"Time to stop\":\n"
"\t\treturn\n"
"[/gdscript]\n"
"[csharp]\n"
"var socket = new PacketPeerUdp();\n"
"// Servidor\n"
"socket.SetDestAddress(\"127.0.0.1\", 789);\n"
"socket.PutPacket(\"Time to stop\".ToAsciiBuffer());\n"
"\n"
"// Cliente\n"
"while (socket.Wait() == OK)\n"
"{\n"
"\tstring data = socket.GetPacket().GetStringFromASCII();\n"
"\tif (data == \"Time to stop\")\n"
"\t{\n"
"\t\treturn;\n"
"\t}\n"
"}\n"
"[/csharp]\n"
"[/codeblocks]"

#: doc/classes/Panel.xml
msgid "A GUI control that displays a [StyleBox]."
msgstr "Um controle de GUI que exibe um [StyleBox]."

#: doc/classes/Panel.xml
msgid ""
"[Panel] is a GUI control that displays a [StyleBox]. See also "
"[PanelContainer]."
msgstr ""
"[Panel] é um controle de GUI que exibe um [StyleBox]. Veja também "
"[PanelContainer]."

#: doc/classes/Panel.xml
msgid "Hierarchical Finite State Machine Demo"
msgstr "Demonstração de Máquina de Estados Finitos Hierárquica"

#: doc/classes/Panel.xml
msgid "The [StyleBox] of this control."
msgstr "O [StyleBox] deste controle."

#: doc/classes/PanelContainer.xml
msgid ""
"A container that keeps its child controls within the area of a [StyleBox]."
msgstr ""
"Um contêiner que mantém seus controles filhos dentro da área de um "
"[StyleBox]."

#: doc/classes/PanelContainer.xml
msgid ""
"A container that keeps its child controls within the area of a [StyleBox]. "
"Useful for giving controls an outline."
msgstr ""
"Um contêiner que mantém seus controles filhos dentro da área de um "
"[StyleBox]. Útil para dar um contorno aos controles."

#: doc/classes/PanelContainer.xml
msgid "The style of [PanelContainer]'s background."
msgstr "O estilo do fundo de [PanelContainer]."

#: doc/classes/PanoramaSkyMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"A material that provides a special texture to a [Sky], usually an HDR "
"panorama."
msgstr ""
"Um material que fornece uma textura especial para um [Sky], geralmente um "
"panorama HDR."

#: doc/classes/PanoramaSkyMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"A resource referenced in a [Sky] that is used to draw a background. "
"[PanoramaSkyMaterial] functions similar to skyboxes in other engines, except "
"it uses an equirectangular sky map instead of a [Cubemap].\n"
"Using an HDR panorama is strongly recommended for accurate, high-quality "
"reflections. Godot supports the Radiance HDR ([code].hdr[/code]) and OpenEXR "
"([code].exr[/code]) image formats for this purpose.\n"
"You can use [url=https://danilw.github.io/GLSL-howto/cubemap_to_panorama_js/"
"cubemap_to_panorama.html]this tool[/url] to convert a cubemap to an "
"equirectangular sky map."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/PanoramaSkyMaterial.xml doc/classes/PhysicalSkyMaterial.xml
#: doc/classes/ProceduralSkyMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"The sky's overall brightness multiplier. Higher values result in a brighter "
"sky."
msgstr ""
"O multiplicador de brilho geral do céu. Valores mais altos resultam em um "
"céu mais brilhante."

#: doc/classes/PanoramaSkyMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"A boolean value to determine if the background texture should be filtered or "
"not."
msgstr ""
"Um valor booleano para determinar se a textura de fundo deve ser filtrada ou "
"não."

#: doc/classes/PanoramaSkyMaterial.xml
msgid "[Texture2D] to be applied to the [PanoramaSkyMaterial]."
msgstr "[Texture2D] a ser aplicado ao [PanoramaSkyMaterial]."

#: doc/classes/Parallax2D.xml doc/classes/ParallaxBackground.xml
msgid "A node used to create a parallax scrolling background."
msgstr "Um nó usado para criar um fundo de rolagem paralaxe."

#: doc/classes/Parallax2D.xml
msgid ""
"A [Parallax2D] is used to create a parallax effect. It can move at a "
"different speed relative to the camera movement using [member scroll_scale]. "
"This creates an illusion of depth in a 2D game. If manual scrolling is "
"desired, the [Camera2D] position can be ignored with [member "
"ignore_camera_scroll].\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Any changes to this node's position made after it enters the "
"scene tree will be overridden if [member ignore_camera_scroll] is "
"[code]false[/code] or [member screen_offset] is modified."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Parallax2D.xml
msgid "2D Parallax"
msgstr "Paralaxe 2D"

#: doc/classes/Parallax2D.xml
msgid ""
"Velocity at which the offset scrolls automatically, in pixels per second."
msgstr ""
"Velocidade na qual o deslocamento rola automaticamente, em pixels por "
"segundo."

#: doc/classes/Parallax2D.xml
msgid ""
"If [code]true[/code], this [Parallax2D] is offset by the current camera's "
"position. If the [Parallax2D] is in a [CanvasLayer] separate from the "
"current camera, it may be desired to match the value with [member "
"CanvasLayer.follow_viewport_enabled]."
msgstr ""
"Se [code]true[/code], este [Parallax2D] é deslocado pela posição da câmera "
"atual. Se o [Parallax2D] estiver em um [CanvasLayer] separado da câmera "
"atual, pode ser desejável corresponder o valor com [member "
"CanvasLayer.follow_viewport_enabled]."

#: doc/classes/Parallax2D.xml
msgid ""
"If [code]true[/code], [Parallax2D]'s position is not affected by the "
"position of the camera."
msgstr ""
"Se [code]true[/code], a posição do [Parallax2D] não é afetada pela posição "
"da câmera."

#: doc/classes/Parallax2D.xml
msgid ""
"Top-left limits for scrolling to begin. If the camera is outside of this "
"limit, the [Parallax2D] stops scrolling. Must be lower than [member "
"limit_end] minus the viewport size to work."
msgstr ""
"Limites superiores e inferiores para o início da rolagem. Se a câmera "
"estiver fora deste limite, o [Parallax2D] para de rolar. Deve ser menor que "
"[member limit_end] menos o tamanho da viewport para funcionar."

#: doc/classes/Parallax2D.xml
msgid ""
"Bottom-right limits for scrolling to end. If the camera is outside of this "
"limit, the [Parallax2D] will stop scrolling. Must be higher than [member "
"limit_begin] and the viewport size combined to work."
msgstr ""
"Limites inferiores direitos para rolagem até o fim. Se a câmera estiver fora "
"deste limite, o [Parallax2D] parará de rolar. Deve ser maior que [member "
"limit_begin] e o tamanho da viewport combinados para funcionar."

#: doc/classes/Parallax2D.xml
msgid ""
"Repeats the [Texture2D] of each of this node's children and offsets them by "
"this value. When scrolling, the node's position loops, giving the illusion "
"of an infinite scrolling background if the values are larger than the screen "
"size. If an axis is set to [code]0[/code], the [Texture2D] will not be "
"repeated."
msgstr ""
"Repete o [Texture2D] de cada um dos filhos deste nó e os desloca por este "
"valor. Ao rolar, a posição do nó faz um loop, dando a ilusão de um fundo de "
"rolagem infinita se os valores forem maiores que o tamanho da tela. Se um "
"eixo for definido como [code]0[/code], o [Texture2D] não será repetido."

#: doc/classes/Parallax2D.xml
msgid ""
"Overrides the amount of times the texture repeats. Each texture copy spreads "
"evenly from the original by [member repeat_size]. Useful for when zooming "
"out with a camera."
msgstr ""
"Sobrescreve a quantidade de vezes que a textura se repete. Cada cópia da "
"textura se espalha uniformemente a partir da original por [member "
"repeat_size]. Útil para quando se afasta o zoom com uma câmera."

#: doc/classes/Parallax2D.xml
msgid ""
"Offset used to scroll this [Parallax2D]. This value is updated automatically "
"unless [member ignore_camera_scroll] is [code]true[/code]."
msgstr ""
"Deslocamento usado para rolar este [Parallax2D]. Este valor é atualizado "
"automaticamente, a menos que [member ignore_camera_scroll] seja [code]true[/"
"code]."

#: doc/classes/Parallax2D.xml
msgid ""
"The [Parallax2D]'s offset. Similar to [member screen_offset] and [member "
"Node2D.position], but will not be overridden.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Values will loop if [member repeat_size] is set higher than "
"[code]0[/code]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Parallax2D.xml
msgid ""
"Multiplier to the final [Parallax2D]'s offset. Can be used to simulate "
"distance from the camera.\n"
"For example, a value of [code]1[/code] scrolls at the same speed as the "
"camera. A value greater than [code]1[/code] scrolls faster, making objects "
"appear closer. Less than [code]1[/code] scrolls slower, making objects "
"appear further, and a value of [code]0[/code] stops the objects completely."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/ParallaxBackground.xml doc/classes/ParallaxLayer.xml
msgid "Use the [Parallax2D] node instead."
msgstr "Use o nó [Parallax2D] em vez disso."

#: doc/classes/ParallaxBackground.xml
msgid ""
"A ParallaxBackground uses one or more [ParallaxLayer] child nodes to create "
"a parallax effect. Each [ParallaxLayer] can move at a different speed using "
"[member ParallaxLayer.motion_offset]. This creates an illusion of depth in a "
"2D game. If not used with a [Camera2D], you must manually calculate the "
"[member scroll_offset].\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Each [ParallaxBackground] is drawn on one specific [Viewport] "
"and cannot be shared between multiple [Viewport]s, see [member "
"CanvasLayer.custom_viewport]. When using multiple [Viewport]s, for example "
"in a split-screen game, you need create an individual [ParallaxBackground] "
"for each [Viewport] you want it to be drawn on."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/ParallaxBackground.xml
msgid "The base position offset for all [ParallaxLayer] children."
msgstr ""
"O deslocamento de posição base para todos os filhos de [ParallaxLayer]."

#: doc/classes/ParallaxBackground.xml
msgid "The base motion scale for all [ParallaxLayer] children."
msgstr "A escala de movimento base para todos os filhos [ParallaxLayer]."

#: doc/classes/ParallaxBackground.xml
msgid ""
"If [code]true[/code], elements in [ParallaxLayer] child aren't affected by "
"the zoom level of the camera."
msgstr ""
"Se [code]true[/code], os elementos no filho [ParallaxLayer] não são afetados "
"pelo nível de zoom da câmera."

#: doc/classes/ParallaxBackground.xml
msgid ""
"Top-left limits for scrolling to begin. If the camera is outside of this "
"limit, the background will stop scrolling. Must be lower than [member "
"scroll_limit_end] to work."
msgstr ""
"Limites superiores esquerdos para a rolagem começar. Se a câmera estiver "
"fora desse limite, o fundo parará de rolar. Deve ser menor do que [member "
"scroll_limit_end] para funcionar."

#: doc/classes/ParallaxBackground.xml
msgid ""
"Bottom-right limits for scrolling to end. If the camera is outside of this "
"limit, the background will stop scrolling. Must be higher than [member "
"scroll_limit_begin] to work."
msgstr ""
"Limites inferiores direitos para a rolagem terminar. Se a câmera estiver "
"fora desse limite, o fundo parará de rolar. Deve ser maior do que [member "
"scroll_limit_begin] para funcionar."

#: doc/classes/ParallaxBackground.xml
msgid ""
"The ParallaxBackground's scroll value. Calculated automatically when using a "
"[Camera2D], but can be used to manually manage scrolling when no camera is "
"present."
msgstr ""
"O valor de rolagem do ParallaxBackground. Calculado automaticamente ao usar "
"um [Camera2D], mas pode ser usado para gerenciar manualmente a rolagem "
"quando nenhuma câmera estiver presente."

#: doc/classes/ParallaxLayer.xml
msgid "A parallax scrolling layer to be used with [ParallaxBackground]."
msgstr "Uma camada de rolagem paralaxe a ser usada com [ParallaxBackground]."

#: doc/classes/ParallaxLayer.xml
msgid ""
"A ParallaxLayer must be the child of a [ParallaxBackground] node. Each "
"ParallaxLayer can be set to move at different speeds relative to the camera "
"movement or the [member ParallaxBackground.scroll_offset] value.\n"
"This node's children will be affected by its scroll offset.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Any changes to this node's position and scale made after it "
"enters the scene will be ignored."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/ParallaxLayer.xml
msgid ""
"The interval, in pixels, at which the [ParallaxLayer] is drawn repeatedly. "
"Useful for creating an infinitely scrolling background. If an axis is set to "
"[code]0[/code], the [ParallaxLayer] will be drawn only once along that "
"direction.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] If you want the repetition to pixel-perfect match a [Texture2D] "
"displayed by a child node, you should account for any scale applied to the "
"texture when defining this interval. For example, if you use a child "
"[Sprite2D] scaled to [code]0.5[/code] to display a 600x600 texture, and want "
"this sprite to be repeated continuously horizontally, you should set the "
"mirroring to [code]Vector2(300, 0)[/code].\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] If the length of the viewport axis is bigger than twice the "
"repeated axis size, it will not repeat infinitely, as the parallax layer "
"only draws 2 instances of the layer at any given time. The visibility window "
"is calculated from the parent [ParallaxBackground]'s position, not the "
"layer's own position. So, if you use mirroring, [b]do not[/b] change the "
"[ParallaxLayer] position relative to its parent. Instead, if you need to "
"adjust the background's position, set the [member CanvasLayer.offset] "
"property in the parent [ParallaxBackground].\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Despite the name, the layer will not be mirrored, it will only "
"be repeated."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/ParallaxLayer.xml
msgid ""
"The ParallaxLayer's offset relative to the parent ParallaxBackground's "
"[member ParallaxBackground.scroll_offset]."
msgstr ""
"O deslocamento do ParallaxLayer em relação ao [member "
"ParallaxBackground.scroll_offset] do ParallaxBackground pai."

#: doc/classes/ParallaxLayer.xml
msgid ""
"Multiplies the ParallaxLayer's motion. If an axis is set to [code]0[/code], "
"it will not scroll."
msgstr ""
"Multiplica o movimento do ParallaxLayer. Se um eixo estiver definido como "
"[code]0[/code], ele não rolará."

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"Holds a particle configuration for [GPUParticles2D] or [GPUParticles3D] "
"nodes."
msgstr ""
"Mantém uma configuração de partículas para nós [GPUParticles2D] ou "
"[GPUParticles3D]."

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"[ParticleProcessMaterial] defines particle properties and behavior. It is "
"used in the [code]process_material[/code] of the [GPUParticles2D] and "
"[GPUParticles3D] nodes. Some of this material's properties are applied to "
"each particle when emitted, while others can have a [CurveTexture] or a "
"[GradientTexture1D] applied to vary numerical or color values over the "
"lifetime of the particle."
msgstr ""
"[ParticleProcessMaterial] define as propriedades e o comportamento das "
"partículas. Ele é usado no [code]process_material[/code] dos nós "
"[GPUParticles2D] e [GPUParticles3D]. Algumas das propriedades deste material "
"são aplicadas a cada partícula quando emitida, enquanto outras podem ter um "
"[CurveTexture] ou um [GradientTexture1D] aplicado para variar valores "
"numéricos ou de cor ao longo da vida útil da partícula."

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the minimum and maximum values of the given [param param] as a "
"vector.\n"
"The [code]x[/code] component of the returned vector corresponds to minimum "
"and the [code]y[/code] component corresponds to maximum."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid "Returns the [Texture2D] used by the specified parameter."
msgstr "Retorna o [Texture2D] usado pelo parâmetro especificado."

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid "Returns [code]true[/code] if the specified particle flag is enabled."
msgstr ""
"Retorna [code]true[/code] se a flag de partícula especificada estiver "
"ativada."

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"Sets the minimum and maximum values of the given [param param].\n"
"The [code]x[/code] component of the argument vector corresponds to minimum "
"and the [code]y[/code] component corresponds to maximum."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid "Sets the maximum value range for the given parameter."
msgstr "Define o intervalo de valores máximo para o parâmetro fornecido."

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid "Sets the minimum value range for the given parameter."
msgstr "Define o intervalo de valores mínimo para o parâmetro fornecido."

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid "Sets the [Texture2D] for the specified [enum Parameter]."
msgstr "Define o [Texture2D] para o [enum Parameter] especificado."

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid "Sets the [param particle_flag] to [param enable]."
msgstr "Define o [param particle_flag] para [param enable]."

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"The alpha value of each particle's color will be multiplied by this "
"[CurveTexture] over its lifetime.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] [member alpha_curve] multiplies the particle mesh's vertex "
"colors. To have a visible effect on a [BaseMaterial3D], [member "
"BaseMaterial3D.vertex_color_use_as_albedo] [i]must[/i] be [code]true[/code]. "
"For a [ShaderMaterial], [code]ALPHA *= COLOR.a;[/code] must be inserted in "
"the shader's [code]fragment()[/code] function. Otherwise, [member "
"alpha_curve] will have no visible effect."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid "Each particle's rotation will be animated along this [CurveTexture]."
msgstr ""
"A rotação de cada partícula será animada ao longo deste [CurveTexture]."

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"Maximum initial rotation applied to each particle, in degrees.\n"
"Only applied when [member particle_flag_disable_z] or [member "
"particle_flag_rotate_y] are [code]true[/code] or the [BaseMaterial3D] being "
"used to draw the particle is using [constant "
"BaseMaterial3D.BILLBOARD_PARTICLES]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"Each particle's angular velocity (rotation speed) will vary along this "
"[CurveTexture] over its lifetime."
msgstr ""
"A velocidade angular (velocidade de rotação) de cada partícula varia ao "
"longo deste [CurveTexture] durante seu tempo de vida."

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"Maximum initial angular velocity (rotation speed) applied to each particle "
"in [i]degrees[/i] per second.\n"
"Only applied when [member particle_flag_disable_z] or [member "
"particle_flag_rotate_y] are [code]true[/code] or the [BaseMaterial3D] being "
"used to draw the particle is using [constant "
"BaseMaterial3D.BILLBOARD_PARTICLES]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid "Each particle's animation offset will vary along this [CurveTexture]."
msgstr ""
"O deslocamento de animação de cada partícula variará ao longo deste "
"[CurveTexture]."

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid "Each particle's animation speed will vary along this [CurveTexture]."
msgstr ""
"A velocidade de animação de cada partícula variará ao longo deste "
"[CurveTexture]."

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"If [code]true[/code], interaction with particle attractors is enabled. In "
"3D, attraction only occurs within the area defined by the [GPUParticles3D] "
"node's [member GPUParticles3D.visibility_aabb]."
msgstr ""
"Se [code]true[/code], a interação com atratores de partículas estará "
"ativada. Em 3D, a atração ocorre apenas dentro da área definida pelo "
"[visibility_aabb] do nó [GPUParticles3D] [member "
"GPUParticles3D.visibility_aabb]."

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"The particles' bounciness. Values range from [code]0[/code] (no bounce) to "
"[code]1[/code] (full bounciness). Only effective if [member collision_mode] "
"is [constant COLLISION_RIGID]."
msgstr ""
"A elasticidade das partículas. Os valores variam de [code]0[/code] (sem "
"elasticidade) a [code]1[/code] (elasticidade total). Só tem efeito se "
"[member collision_mode] for [constant COLLISION_RIGID]."

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"The particles' friction. Values range from [code]0[/code] (frictionless) to "
"[code]1[/code] (maximum friction). Only effective if [member collision_mode] "
"is [constant COLLISION_RIGID]."
msgstr ""
"O atrito das partículas. Os valores variam de [code]0[/code] (sem atrito) a "
"[code]1[/code] (atrito máximo). Só é eficaz se [member collision_mode] for "
"[constant COLLISION_RIGID]."

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"The particles' collision mode.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] 3D Particles can only collide with [GPUParticlesCollision3D] "
"nodes, not [PhysicsBody3D] nodes. To make particles collide with various "
"objects, you can add [GPUParticlesCollision3D] nodes as children of "
"[PhysicsBody3D] nodes. In 3D, collisions only occur within the area defined "
"by the [GPUParticles3D] node's [member GPUParticles3D.visibility_aabb].\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] 2D Particles can only collide with [LightOccluder2D] nodes, not "
"[PhysicsBody2D] nodes."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"If [code]true[/code], [member GPUParticles3D.collision_base_size] is "
"multiplied by the particle's effective scale (see [member scale_min], "
"[member scale_max], [member scale_curve], and [member "
"scale_over_velocity_curve])."
msgstr ""
"Se [code]true[/code], o [member GPUParticles3D.collision_base_size] é "
"multiplicado pela escala efetiva da partícula (veja [member scale_min], "
"[member scale_max], [member scale_curve] e [member "
"scale_over_velocity_curve])."

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"Each particle's initial color. If the [GPUParticles2D]'s [code]texture[/"
"code] is defined, it will be multiplied by this color.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] [member color] multiplies the particle mesh's vertex colors. To "
"have a visible effect on a [BaseMaterial3D], [member "
"BaseMaterial3D.vertex_color_use_as_albedo] [i]must[/i] be [code]true[/code]. "
"For a [ShaderMaterial], [code]ALBEDO *= COLOR.rgb;[/code] must be inserted "
"in the shader's [code]fragment()[/code] function. Otherwise, [member color] "
"will have no visible effect."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"Each particle's initial color will vary along this [GradientTexture1D] "
"(multiplied with [member color]).\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] [member color_initial_ramp] multiplies the particle mesh's "
"vertex colors. To have a visible effect on a [BaseMaterial3D], [member "
"BaseMaterial3D.vertex_color_use_as_albedo] [i]must[/i] be [code]true[/code]. "
"For a [ShaderMaterial], [code]ALBEDO *= COLOR.rgb;[/code] must be inserted "
"in the shader's [code]fragment()[/code] function. Otherwise, [member "
"color_initial_ramp] will have no visible effect."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"Each particle's color will vary along this [GradientTexture1D] over its "
"lifetime (multiplied with [member color]).\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] [member color_ramp] multiplies the particle mesh's vertex "
"colors. To have a visible effect on a [BaseMaterial3D], [member "
"BaseMaterial3D.vertex_color_use_as_albedo] [i]must[/i] be [code]true[/code]. "
"For a [ShaderMaterial], [code]ALBEDO *= COLOR.rgb;[/code] must be inserted "
"in the shader's [code]fragment()[/code] function. Otherwise, [member "
"color_ramp] will have no visible effect."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid "Damping will vary along this [CurveTexture]."
msgstr "O amortecimento variará ao longo deste [CurveTexture]."

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"A curve that specifies the velocity along each of the axes of the particle "
"system along its lifetime.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Animated velocities will not be affected by damping, use "
"[member velocity_limit_curve] instead."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"Maximum directional velocity value, which is multiplied by [member "
"directional_velocity_curve].\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Animated velocities will not be affected by damping, use "
"[member velocity_limit_curve] instead."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"Minimum directional velocity value, which is multiplied by [member "
"directional_velocity_curve].\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Animated velocities will not be affected by damping, use "
"[member velocity_limit_curve] instead."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"The box's extents if [member emission_shape] is set to [constant "
"EMISSION_SHAPE_BOX].\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] [member emission_box_extents] starts from the center point and "
"applies the X, Y, and Z values in both directions. The size is twice the "
"area of the extents."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"Particle color will be modulated by color determined by sampling this "
"texture at the same point as the [member emission_point_texture].\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] [member emission_color_texture] multiplies the particle mesh's "
"vertex colors. To have a visible effect on a [BaseMaterial3D], [member "
"BaseMaterial3D.vertex_color_use_as_albedo] [i]must[/i] be [code]true[/code]. "
"For a [ShaderMaterial], [code]ALBEDO *= COLOR.rgb;[/code] must be inserted "
"in the shader's [code]fragment()[/code] function. Otherwise, [member "
"emission_color_texture] will have no visible effect."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"Each particle's color will be multiplied by this [CurveTexture] over its "
"lifetime.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] [member emission_curve] multiplies the particle mesh's vertex "
"colors. To have a visible effect on a [BaseMaterial3D], [member "
"BaseMaterial3D.vertex_color_use_as_albedo] [i]must[/i] be [code]true[/code]. "
"For a [ShaderMaterial], [code]ALBEDO *= COLOR.rgb;[/code] must be inserted "
"in the shader's [code]fragment()[/code] function. Otherwise, [member "
"emission_curve] will have no visible effect."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"Particle velocity and rotation will be set by sampling this texture at the "
"same point as the [member emission_point_texture]. Used only in [constant "
"EMISSION_SHAPE_DIRECTED_POINTS]. Can be created automatically from mesh or "
"node by selecting \"Create Emission Points from Mesh/Node\" under the "
"\"Particles\" tool in the toolbar."
msgstr ""
"A velocidade e a rotação das partículas serão definidas amostrando esta "
"textura no mesmo ponto que o [member emission_point_texture]. Usado apenas "
"em [constant EMISSION_SHAPE_DIRECTED_POINTS]. Pode ser criado "
"automaticamente a partir de uma malha ou nó selecionando \"Criar pontos de "
"emissão a partir da malha/nó\" sob a ferramenta \"Partículas\" na barra de "
"ferramentas."

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"The number of emission points if [member emission_shape] is set to [constant "
"EMISSION_SHAPE_POINTS] or [constant EMISSION_SHAPE_DIRECTED_POINTS]."
msgstr ""
"O número de pontos de emissão se [member emission_shape] estiver definido "
"como [constant EMISSION_SHAPE_POINTS] ou [constant "
"EMISSION_SHAPE_DIRECTED_POINTS]."

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"Particles will be emitted at positions determined by sampling this texture "
"at a random position. Used with [constant EMISSION_SHAPE_POINTS] and "
"[constant EMISSION_SHAPE_DIRECTED_POINTS]. Can be created automatically from "
"mesh or node by selecting \"Create Emission Points from Mesh/Node\" under "
"the \"Particles\" tool in the toolbar."
msgstr ""
"As partículas serão emitidas em posições determinadas pela amostragem desta "
"textura em uma posição aleatória. Usado com [constant EMISSION_SHAPE_POINTS] "
"e [constant EMISSION_SHAPE_DIRECTED_POINTS]. Pode ser criado automaticamente "
"a partir de uma malha ou nó selecionando \"Criar pontos de emissão a partir "
"da malha/nó\" sob a ferramenta \"Partículas\" na barra de ferramentas."

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid "The offset for the [member emission_shape], in local space."
msgstr "O deslocamento para o [member emission_shape], em espaço local."

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid "The scale of the [member emission_shape], in local space."
msgstr "A escala do [member emission_shape], em espaço local."

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid "Amount of [member spread] along the Y axis."
msgstr "Quantidade de [member spread] ao longo do eixo Y."

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid "Each particle's hue will vary along this [CurveTexture]."
msgstr "O matiz de cada partícula variará ao longo deste [CurveTexture]."

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"Percentage of the velocity of the respective [GPUParticles2D] or "
"[GPUParticles3D] inherited by each particle when spawning."
msgstr ""
"Porcentagem da velocidade do respectivo [GPUParticles2D] ou [GPUParticles3D] "
"herdada por cada partícula ao gerar."

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"Particle lifetime randomness ratio. The equation for the lifetime of a "
"particle is [code]lifetime * (1.0 - randf() * lifetime_randomness)[/code]. "
"For example, a [member lifetime_randomness] of [code]0.4[/code] scales the "
"lifetime between [code]0.6[/code] to [code]1.0[/code] of its original value."
msgstr ""
"Proporção de aleatoriedade do tempo de vida da partícula. A equação para o "
"tempo de vida de uma partícula é [code]lifetime * (1.0 - randf() * "
"lifetime_randomness)[/code]. Por exemplo, um [member lifetime_randomness] de "
"[code]0.4[/code] escala o tempo de vida entre [code]0.6[/code] e [code]1.0[/"
"code] do seu valor original."

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"Each particle's linear acceleration will vary along this [CurveTexture]."
msgstr ""
"A aceleração linear de cada partícula vai variar ao longo deste "
"[CurveTexture]."

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"Each particle's orbital velocity will vary along this [CurveTexture].\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] For 3D orbital velocity, use a [CurveXYZTexture].\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Animated velocities will not be affected by damping, use "
"[member velocity_limit_curve] instead."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"Maximum orbital velocity applied to each particle. Makes the particles "
"circle around origin. Specified in number of full rotations around origin "
"per second.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Animated velocities will not be affected by damping, use "
"[member velocity_limit_curve] instead."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"Minimum equivalent of [member orbit_velocity_max].\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Animated velocities will not be affected by damping, use "
"[member velocity_limit_curve] instead."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"Changes the behavior of the damping properties from a linear deceleration to "
"a deceleration based on speed percentage."
msgstr ""
"Altera o comportamento das propriedades de amortecimento de uma "
"desaceleração linear para uma desaceleração baseada na porcentagem de "
"velocidade."

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid "If [code]true[/code], particles will not move on the z axis."
msgstr "Se [code]true[/code], as partículas não se moverão no eixo Z."

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"If [code]true[/code], particles will inherit the scale of the emitter.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] This has no effect when [member GPUParticles3D.local_coords] is "
"[code]true[/code], since particles in local space are already affected by "
"the emitter's scale."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"Each particle's radial acceleration will vary along this [CurveTexture]."
msgstr ""
"A aceleração radial de cada partícula vai variar ao longo deste "
"[CurveTexture]."

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"A [CurveTexture] that defines the velocity over the particle's lifetime away "
"(or toward) the [member velocity_pivot].\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Animated velocities will not be affected by damping, use "
"[member velocity_limit_curve] instead."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"Maximum radial velocity applied to each particle. Makes particles move away "
"from the [member velocity_pivot], or toward it if negative.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Animated velocities will not be affected by damping, use "
"[member velocity_limit_curve] instead."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"Minimum radial velocity applied to each particle. Makes particles move away "
"from the [member velocity_pivot], or toward it if negative.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Animated velocities will not be affected by damping, use "
"[member velocity_limit_curve] instead."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"The maximum 3D orientation, in degrees. Works only in 3D and if [member "
"use_rotation_3d] is enabled."
msgstr ""
"A orientação 3D máxima, em graus. Funciona apenas em 3D e se [member "
"use_rotation_3d] estiver ativado."

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"The minimum 3D orientation, in degrees. Works only in 3D and if [member "
"use_rotation_3d] is enabled."
msgstr ""
"A orientação 3D mínima, em graus. Funciona apenas em 3D e se [member "
"use_rotation_3d] estiver ativado."

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"Rotation velocity curve over lifetime, per-axis. Enable [member "
"use_rotation_velocity_3d] to use this."
msgstr ""
"Curva de velocidade de rotação ao longo do tempo de vida, por eixo. Ative "
"[member use_rotation_velocity_3d] para usar isto."

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"Maximum 3D rotation velocity on the particle's local axis. Enable [member "
"use_rotation_velocity_3d] to use this."
msgstr ""
"Velocidade máxima de rotação 3D no eixo local da partícula. Ative [member "
"use_rotation_velocity_3d] para usar isso."

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"Minimum 3D rotation velocity on the particle's local axis. Enable [member "
"use_rotation_velocity_3d] to use this."
msgstr ""
"Velocidade mínima de rotação 3D no eixo local da partícula. Ative [member "
"use_rotation_velocity_3d] para usar isso."

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"The maximum value of the random scale vector for each particle.\n"
"Works only if [member use_scale_3d] is enabled."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"The minimum value of the random scale vector for each particle.\n"
"Works only if [member use_scale_3d] is enabled."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"Each particle's scale will vary along this [CurveTexture] over its lifetime. "
"If a [CurveXYZTexture] is supplied instead, the scale will be separated per-"
"axis."
msgstr ""
"A escala de cada partícula variará ao longo desta [CurveTexture] durante seu "
"tempo de vida. Se um [CurveXYZTexture] for fornecido em vez disso, a escala "
"será separada por eixo."

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid "Minimum equivalent of [member scale_max]."
msgstr "Equivalente mínimo de [member scale_max]."

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"Either a [CurveTexture] or a [CurveXYZTexture] that scales each particle "
"based on its velocity."
msgstr ""
"Um [CurveTexture] ou um [CurveXYZTexture] que dimensiona cada partícula com "
"base em sua velocidade."

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"Maximum velocity value reference for [member scale_over_velocity_curve].\n"
"[member scale_over_velocity_curve] will be interpolated between [member "
"scale_over_velocity_min] and [member scale_over_velocity_max]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"Minimum velocity value reference for [member scale_over_velocity_curve].\n"
"[member scale_over_velocity_curve] will be interpolated between [member "
"scale_over_velocity_min] and [member scale_over_velocity_max]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"The amount of particles to spawn from the subemitter node when a collision "
"occurs. When combined with [constant COLLISION_HIDE_ON_CONTACT] on the main "
"particles material, this can be used to achieve effects such as raindrops "
"hitting the ground.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] This value shouldn't exceed [member GPUParticles2D.amount] or "
"[member GPUParticles3D.amount] defined on the [i]subemitter node[/i] (not "
"the main node), relative to the subemitter's particle lifetime. If the "
"number of particles is exceeded, no new particles will spawn from the "
"subemitter until enough particles have expired."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"The amount of particles to spawn from the subemitter node when the particle "
"expires.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] This value shouldn't exceed [member GPUParticles2D.amount] or "
"[member GPUParticles3D.amount] defined on the [i]subemitter node[/i] (not "
"the main node), relative to the subemitter's particle lifetime. If the "
"number of particles is exceeded, no new particles will spawn from the "
"subemitter until enough particles have expired."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"The amount of particles to spawn from the subemitter node when the particle "
"spawns.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] This value shouldn't exceed [member GPUParticles2D.amount] or "
"[member GPUParticles3D.amount] defined on the [i]subemitter node[/i] (not "
"the main node), relative to the subemitter's particle lifetime. If the "
"number of particles is exceeded, no new particles will spawn from the "
"subemitter until enough particles have expired."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"The frequency at which particles should be emitted from the subemitter node. "
"One particle will be spawned every [member sub_emitter_frequency] seconds.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] This value shouldn't exceed [member GPUParticles2D.amount] or "
"[member GPUParticles3D.amount] defined on the [i]subemitter node[/i] (not "
"the main node), relative to the subemitter's particle lifetime. If the "
"number of particles is exceeded, no new particles will spawn from the "
"subemitter until enough particles have expired."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"If [code]true[/code], the subemitter inherits the parent particle's velocity "
"when it spawns."
msgstr ""
"Se [code]true[/code], o subemissores herda a velocidade da partícula pai "
"quando ela é gerada."

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"The particle subemitter mode (see [member GPUParticles2D.sub_emitter] and "
"[member GPUParticles3D.sub_emitter])."
msgstr ""
"O modo de subemissor de partículas (veja [member GPUParticles2D.sub_emitter] "
"e [member GPUParticles3D.sub_emitter])."

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"Each particle's tangential acceleration will vary along this [CurveTexture]."
msgstr ""
"A aceleração tangencial de cada partícula vai variar ao longo deste "
"[CurveTexture]."

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"If [code]true[/code], enables turbulence for the particle system. Turbulence "
"can be used to vary particle movement according to its position (based on a "
"3D noise pattern). In 3D, [GPUParticlesAttractorVectorField3D] with "
"[NoiseTexture3D] can be used as an alternative to turbulence that works in "
"world space and with multiple particle systems reacting in the same way.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Enabling turbulence has a high performance cost on the GPU. "
"Only enable turbulence on a few particle systems at once at most, and "
"consider disabling it when targeting mobile/web platforms."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"Maximum turbulence influence on each particle.\n"
"The actual amount of turbulence influence on each particle is calculated as "
"a random value between [member turbulence_influence_min] and [member "
"turbulence_influence_max] and multiplied by the amount of turbulence "
"influence from [member turbulence_influence_over_life]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"Minimum turbulence influence on each particle.\n"
"The actual amount of turbulence influence on each particle is calculated as "
"a random value between [member turbulence_influence_min] and [member "
"turbulence_influence_max] and multiplied by the amount of turbulence "
"influence from [member turbulence_influence_over_life]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"Each particle's amount of turbulence will be influenced along this "
"[CurveTexture] over its life time."
msgstr ""
"A quantidade de turbulência de cada partícula será influenciada ao longo "
"deste [CurveTexture] durante seu tempo de vida."

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"Maximum displacement of each particle's spawn position by the turbulence.\n"
"The actual amount of displacement will be a factor of the underlying "
"turbulence multiplied by a random value between [member "
"turbulence_initial_displacement_min] and [member "
"turbulence_initial_displacement_max]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"Minimum displacement of each particle's spawn position by the turbulence.\n"
"The actual amount of displacement will be a factor of the underlying "
"turbulence multiplied by a random value between [member "
"turbulence_initial_displacement_min] and [member "
"turbulence_initial_displacement_max]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"This value controls the overall scale/frequency of the turbulence noise "
"pattern.\n"
"A small scale will result in smaller features with more detail while a high "
"scale will result in smoother noise with larger features."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"A scrolling velocity for the turbulence field. This sets a directional trend "
"for the pattern to move in over time.\n"
"The default value of [code]Vector3(0, 0, 0)[/code] turns off the scrolling."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"The in-place rate of change of the turbulence field. This defines how "
"quickly the noise pattern varies over time.\n"
"A value of 0.0 will result in a fixed pattern."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"The turbulence noise strength. Increasing this will result in a stronger, "
"more contrasting, flow pattern."
msgstr ""
"A força do ruído de turbulência. Aumentar isso resultará em um padrão de "
"fluxo mais forte e contrastante."

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"Enable the usage of [member rotation_3d_min] and [member rotation_3d_max]."
msgstr "Ativa o uso de [member rotation_3d_min] e [member rotation_3d_max]."

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid "Enable 3D rotation velocity."
msgstr "Ativa a velocidade de rotação 3D."

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid "Enable the usage of [member scale_3d_min] and [member scale_3d_max]."
msgstr "Habilita o uso de [member scale_3d_min] e [member scale_3d_max]."

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"A [CurveTexture] that defines the maximum velocity of a particle during its "
"lifetime."
msgstr ""
"Um [CurveTexture] que define a velocidade máxima de uma partícula durante "
"sua vida útil."

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"A pivot point used to calculate radial and orbital velocity of particles."
msgstr ""
"Um ponto pivô usado para calcular a velocidade radial e orbital das "
"partículas."

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"Emitted when this material's emission shape is changed in any way. This "
"includes changes to [member emission_shape], [member emission_shape_scale], "
"or [member emission_sphere_radius], and any other property that affects the "
"emission shape's offset, size, scale, or orientation.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] This signal is only emitted inside the editor for performance "
"reasons."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"Use with [method set_param_min], [method set_param_max], and [method "
"set_param_texture] to set initial velocity properties."
msgstr ""
"Use com [method set_param_min], [method set_param_max] e [method "
"set_param_texture] para definir propriedades de velocidade inicial."

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"Use with [method set_param_min], [method set_param_max], and [method "
"set_param_texture] to set angular velocity properties."
msgstr ""
"Use com [method set_param_min], [method set_param_max] e [method "
"set_param_texture] para definir propriedades de velocidade angular."

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"Use with [method set_param_min], [method set_param_max], and [method "
"set_param_texture] to set orbital velocity properties."
msgstr ""
"Use com [method set_param_min], [method set_param_max] e [method "
"set_param_texture] para definir propriedades de velocidade orbital."

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"Use with [method set_param_min], [method set_param_max], and [method "
"set_param_texture] to set linear acceleration properties."
msgstr ""
"Use com [method set_param_min], [method set_param_max] e [method "
"set_param_texture] para definir propriedades de aceleração linear."

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"Use with [method set_param_min], [method set_param_max], and [method "
"set_param_texture] to set radial acceleration properties."
msgstr ""
"Use com [method set_param_min], [method set_param_max] e [method "
"set_param_texture] para definir propriedades de aceleração radial."

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"Use with [method set_param_min], [method set_param_max], and [method "
"set_param_texture] to set tangential acceleration properties."
msgstr ""
"Use com [method set_param_min], [method set_param_max] e [method "
"set_param_texture] para definir propriedades de aceleração tangencial."

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"Use with [method set_param_min], [method set_param_max], and [method "
"set_param_texture] to set damping properties."
msgstr ""
"Use com [method set_param_min], [method set_param_max] e [method "
"set_param_texture] para definir as propriedades de amortecimento."

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"Use with [method set_param_min], [method set_param_max], and [method "
"set_param_texture] to set angle properties."
msgstr ""
"Use com [method set_param_min], [method set_param_max] e [method "
"set_param_texture] para definir as propriedades de ângulo."

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"Use with [method set_param_min], [method set_param_max], and [method "
"set_param_texture] to set scale properties."
msgstr ""
"Use com [method set_param_min], [method set_param_max] e [method "
"set_param_texture] para definir as propriedades de escala."

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"Use with [method set_param_min], [method set_param_max], and [method "
"set_param_texture] to set hue variation properties."
msgstr ""
"Use com [method set_param_min], [method set_param_max] e [method "
"set_param_texture] para definir propriedades de variação de tonalidade."

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"Use with [method set_param_min], [method set_param_max], and [method "
"set_param_texture] to set animation speed properties."
msgstr ""
"Use com [method set_param_min], [method set_param_max] e [method "
"set_param_texture] para definir propriedades de velocidade de animação."

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"Use with [method set_param_min], [method set_param_max], and [method "
"set_param_texture] to set animation offset properties."
msgstr ""
"Use com [method set_param_min], [method set_param_max] e [method "
"set_param_texture] para definir propriedades de deslocamento de animação."

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"Use with [method set_param_min], [method set_param_max], and [method "
"set_param_texture] to set radial velocity properties."
msgstr ""
"Use com [method set_param_min], [method set_param_max] e [method "
"set_param_texture] para definir propriedades de velocidade radial."

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"Use with [method set_param_min], [method set_param_max], and [method "
"set_param_texture] to set directional velocity properties."
msgstr ""
"Use com [method set_param_min], [method set_param_max] e [method "
"set_param_texture] para definir propriedades de velocidade direcional."

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"Use with [method set_param_min], [method set_param_max], and [method "
"set_param_texture] to set scale over velocity properties."
msgstr ""
"Use com [method set_param_min], [method set_param_max] e [method "
"set_param_texture] para definir propriedades de escala sobre a velocidade."

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"Particles will be emitted at a position determined by sampling a random "
"point on the [member emission_point_texture]. Particle color will be "
"modulated by [member emission_color_texture]."
msgstr ""
"As partículas serão emitidas em uma posição determinada pela amostragem de "
"um ponto aleatório no [member emission_point_texture]. A cor da partícula "
"será modulada por [member emission_color_texture]."

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"Particles will be emitted at a position determined by sampling a random "
"point on the [member emission_point_texture]. Particle velocity and rotation "
"will be set based on [member emission_normal_texture]. Particle color will "
"be modulated by [member emission_color_texture]."
msgstr ""
"As partículas serão emitidas em uma posição determinada pela amostragem de "
"um ponto aleatório em [member emission_point_texture]. A velocidade e a "
"rotação da partícula serão definidas com base em [member "
"emission_normal_texture]. A cor da partícula será modulada por [member "
"emission_color_texture]."

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"Use with [method set_param_min] and [method set_param_max] to set the "
"turbulence minimum und maximum influence on each particles velocity."
msgstr ""
"Use com [method set_param_min] e [method set_param_max] para definir a "
"influência mínima e máxima da turbulência na velocidade de cada partícula."

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"Use with [method set_param_min] and [method set_param_max] to set the "
"turbulence minimum and maximum displacement of the particles spawn position."
msgstr ""
"Use com [method set_param_min] e [method set_param_max] para definir o "
"deslocamento mínimo e máximo da turbulência da posição de surgimento das "
"partículas."

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"Use with [method set_param_texture] to set the turbulence influence over the "
"particles life time."
msgstr ""
"Use com [method set_param_texture] para definir a influência da turbulência "
"ao longo do tempo de vida das partículas."

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid "The subemitter is disabled."
msgstr "O subemissor está desativado."

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"The submitter is emitted on the constant interval defined by [member "
"sub_emitter_frequency]."
msgstr ""
"O subemissor é emitido no intervalo constante definido por [member "
"sub_emitter_frequency]."

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid "The subemitter is emitted at the end of the particle's lifetime."
msgstr "O subemissor é emitido no final do tempo de vida da partícula."

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid "The subemitter is emitted when the particle collides."
msgstr "O subemissor é emitido quando a partícula colide."

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid "The subemitter is emitted when the particle spawns."
msgstr "O subemissor é emitido quando a partícula gera."

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid "Represents the size of the [enum SubEmitterMode] enum."
msgstr "Representa o tamanho da enumeração [enum SubEmitterMode]."

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"No collision for particles. Particles will go through "
"[GPUParticlesCollision3D] nodes."
msgstr ""
"Sem colisão para partículas. As partículas passarão pelos nós "
"[GPUParticlesCollision3D]."

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"[RigidBody3D]-style collision for particles using [GPUParticlesCollision3D] "
"nodes."
msgstr ""
"Colisão no estilo [RigidBody3D] para partículas usando nós "
"[GPUParticlesCollision3D]."

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"Hide particles instantly when colliding with a [GPUParticlesCollision3D] "
"node. This can be combined with a subemitter that uses the [constant "
"COLLISION_RIGID] collision mode to \"replace\" the parent particle with the "
"subemitter on impact."
msgstr ""
"Oculta partículas instantaneamente ao colidir com um nó "
"[GPUParticlesCollision3D]. Isso pode ser combinado com um subemissor que usa "
"o modo de colisão [constant COLLISION_RIGID] para \"substituir\" a partícula "
"pai pelo subemissor no impacto."

#: doc/classes/ParticleProcessMaterial.xml
msgid "Represents the size of the [enum CollisionMode] enum."
msgstr "Representa o tamanho da enumeração [enum CollisionMode]."

#: doc/classes/Path2D.xml
msgid "Contains a [Curve2D] path for [PathFollow2D] nodes to follow."
msgstr "Contém um caminho [Curve2D] para nós [PathFollow2D] seguirem."

#: doc/classes/Path2D.xml
msgid ""
"Can have [PathFollow2D] child nodes moving along the [Curve2D]. See "
"[PathFollow2D] for more information on usage.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] The path is considered as relative to the moved nodes (children "
"of [PathFollow2D]). As such, the curve should usually start with a zero "
"vector ([code](0, 0)[/code])."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Path2D.xml
msgid "A [Curve2D] describing the path."
msgstr "Uma [Curve2D] que descreve o caminho."

#: doc/classes/Path3D.xml
msgid "Contains a [Curve3D] path for [PathFollow3D] nodes to follow."
msgstr "Contém um caminho [Curve3D] para nós [PathFollow3D] seguirem."

#: doc/classes/Path3D.xml
msgid ""
"Can have [PathFollow3D] child nodes moving along the [Curve3D]. See "
"[PathFollow3D] for more information on the usage.\n"
"Note that the path is considered as relative to the moved nodes (children of "
"[PathFollow3D]). As such, the curve should usually start with a zero vector "
"[code](0, 0, 0)[/code]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Path3D.xml
msgid "A [Curve3D] describing the path."
msgstr "Uma [Curve3D] que descreve o caminho."

#: doc/classes/Path3D.xml
msgid ""
"The custom color used to draw the path in the editor. If set to [constant "
"Color.BLACK] (as by default), the color set in [member ProjectSettings.debug/"
"shapes/paths/geometry_color] is used."
msgstr ""
"A cor personalizada usada para desenhar o caminho no editor. Se definido "
"como [constant Color.BLACK] (como por padrão), a cor definida em [member "
"ProjectSettings.debug/shapes/paths/geometry_color] é usada."

#: doc/classes/Path3D.xml
msgid "Emitted when the [member curve] changes."
msgstr "Emitido quando a [member curve] muda."

#: doc/classes/Path3D.xml
msgid "Emitted when the [member debug_custom_color] changes."
msgstr "Emitido quando o [member debug_custom_color] muda."

#: doc/classes/PathFollow2D.xml
msgid "Point sampler for a [Path2D]."
msgstr "Amostrador de pontos para um [Path2D]."

#: doc/classes/PathFollow2D.xml
msgid ""
"This node takes its parent [Path2D], and returns the coordinates of a point "
"within it, given a distance from the first vertex.\n"
"It is useful for making other nodes follow a path, without coding the "
"movement pattern. For that, the nodes must be children of this node. The "
"descendant nodes will then move accordingly when setting the [member "
"progress] in this node."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/PathFollow2D.xml
msgid ""
"If [code]true[/code], the position between two cached points is interpolated "
"cubically, and linearly otherwise.\n"
"The points along the [Curve2D] of the [Path2D] are precomputed before use, "
"for faster calculations. The point at the requested offset is then "
"calculated interpolating between two adjacent cached points. This may "
"present a problem if the curve makes sharp turns, as the cached points may "
"not follow the curve closely enough.\n"
"There are two answers to this problem: either increase the number of cached "
"points and increase memory consumption, or make a cubic interpolation "
"between two points at the cost of (slightly) slower calculations."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/PathFollow2D.xml doc/classes/PathFollow3D.xml
msgid "The node's offset along the curve."
msgstr "O deslocamento do nó ao longo da curva."

#: doc/classes/PathFollow2D.xml doc/classes/PathFollow3D.xml
msgid ""
"If [code]true[/code], any offset outside the path's length will wrap around, "
"instead of stopping at the ends. Use it for cyclic paths."
msgstr ""
"Se [code]true[/code], qualquer deslocamento fora do comprimento do caminho "
"dará a volta (wrap around), em vez de parar nas extremidades. Use para "
"caminhos cíclicos."

#: doc/classes/PathFollow2D.xml
msgid ""
"The distance along the path, in pixels. Changing this value sets this node's "
"position to a point within the path."
msgstr ""
"A distância ao longo do caminho, em pixels. Alterar este valor define a "
"posição deste nó para um ponto dentro do caminho."

#: doc/classes/PathFollow2D.xml
msgid ""
"The distance along the path as a number in the range 0.0 (for the first "
"vertex) to 1.0 (for the last). This is just another way of expressing the "
"progress within the path, as the offset supplied is multiplied internally by "
"the path's length.\n"
"It can be set or get only if the [PathFollow2D] is the child of a [Path2D] "
"which is part of the scene tree, and that this [Path2D] has a [Curve2D] with "
"a non-zero length. Otherwise, trying to set this field will print an error, "
"and getting this field will return [code]0.0[/code]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/PathFollow2D.xml
msgid ""
"If [code]true[/code], this node rotates to follow the path, with the +X "
"direction facing forward on the path."
msgstr ""
"Se [code]true[/code], este nó rotaciona para seguir o caminho, com a direção "
"+X voltada para a frente no caminho."

#: doc/classes/PathFollow2D.xml doc/classes/PathFollow3D.xml
msgid "The node's offset perpendicular to the curve."
msgstr "O deslocamento do nó perpendicular à curva."

#: doc/classes/PathFollow3D.xml
msgid "Point sampler for a [Path3D]."
msgstr "Amostrador de pontos para um [Path3D]."

#: doc/classes/PathFollow3D.xml
msgid ""
"This node takes its parent [Path3D], and returns the coordinates of a point "
"within it, given a distance from the first vertex.\n"
"It is useful for making other nodes follow a path, without coding the "
"movement pattern. For that, the nodes must be children of this node. The "
"descendant nodes will then move accordingly when setting the [member "
"progress] in this node."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/PathFollow3D.xml
msgid ""
"Correct the [param transform]. [param rotation_mode] implicitly specifies "
"how posture (forward, up and sideway direction) is calculated."
msgstr ""
"Corrige o [param transform]. [param rotation_mode] especifica implicitamente "
"como a postura (direção para frente, para cima e para o lado) é calculada."

#: doc/classes/PathFollow3D.xml
msgid ""
"If [code]true[/code], the position between two cached points is interpolated "
"cubically, and linearly otherwise.\n"
"The points along the [Curve3D] of the [Path3D] are precomputed before use, "
"for faster calculations. The point at the requested offset is then "
"calculated interpolating between two adjacent cached points. This may "
"present a problem if the curve makes sharp turns, as the cached points may "
"not follow the curve closely enough.\n"
"There are two answers to this problem: either increase the number of cached "
"points and increase memory consumption, or make a cubic interpolation "
"between two points at the cost of (slightly) slower calculations."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/PathFollow3D.xml
msgid ""
"The distance from the first vertex, measured in 3D units along the path. "
"Changing this value sets this node's position to a point within the path."
msgstr ""
"A distância do primeiro vértice, medida em unidades 3D ao longo do caminho. "
"Alterar este valor define a posição deste nó para um ponto dentro do caminho."

#: doc/classes/PathFollow3D.xml
msgid ""
"The distance from the first vertex, considering 0.0 as the first vertex and "
"1.0 as the last. This is just another way of expressing the progress within "
"the path, as the progress supplied is multiplied internally by the path's "
"length.\n"
"It can be set or get only if the [PathFollow3D] is the child of a [Path3D] "
"which is part of the scene tree, and that this [Path3D] has a [Curve3D] with "
"a non-zero length. Otherwise, trying to set this field will print an error, "
"and getting this field will return [code]0.0[/code]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/PathFollow3D.xml
msgid ""
"Allows or forbids rotation on one or more axes, depending on the [enum "
"RotationMode] constants being used."
msgstr ""
"Permite ou proíbe a rotação em um ou mais eixos, dependendo das constantes "
"[enum RotationMode] usadas."

#: doc/classes/PathFollow3D.xml
msgid "If [code]true[/code], the tilt property of [Curve3D] takes effect."
msgstr ""
"Se [code]true[/code], a propriedade de inclinação de [Curve3D] entra em "
"vigor."

#: doc/classes/PathFollow3D.xml
msgid ""
"If [code]true[/code], the node moves on the travel path with orienting the "
"+Z axis as forward. See also [constant Vector3.FORWARD] and [constant "
"Vector3.MODEL_FRONT]."
msgstr ""
"Se [code]true[/code], o nó se move no caminho de percurso orientando o eixo "
"+Z como frente. Veja também [constant Vector3.FORWARD] e [constant "
"Vector3.MODEL_FRONT]."

#: doc/classes/PathFollow3D.xml
msgid "Forbids the PathFollow3D to rotate."
msgstr "Proíbe o PathFollow3D de girar."

#: doc/classes/PathFollow3D.xml
msgid "Allows the PathFollow3D to rotate in the Y axis only."
msgstr "Permite que o PathFollow3D rotacione apenas no eixo Y."

#: doc/classes/PathFollow3D.xml
msgid "Allows the PathFollow3D to rotate in both the X, and Y axes."
msgstr "Permite que o PathFollow3D rotacione em ambos os eixos X e Y."

#: doc/classes/PathFollow3D.xml
msgid "Allows the PathFollow3D to rotate in any axis."
msgstr "Permite que o PathFollow3D rotacione em qualquer eixo."

#: doc/classes/PathFollow3D.xml
msgid ""
"Uses the up vector information in a [Curve3D] to enforce orientation. This "
"rotation mode requires the [Path3D]'s [member Curve3D.up_vector_enabled] "
"property to be set to [code]true[/code]."
msgstr ""
"Usa a informação do vetor \"up\" em um [Curve3D] para impor orientação. Este "
"modo de rotação requer que a propriedade [member Curve3D.up_vector_enabled] "
"do [Path3D] esteja definida como [code]true[/code]."

#: doc/classes/PCKPacker.xml
msgid "Creates packages that can be loaded into a running project."
msgstr "Cria pacotes que podem ser carregados em um projeto em execução."

#: doc/classes/PCKPacker.xml
msgid ""
"The [PCKPacker] is used to create packages that can be loaded into a running "
"project using [method ProjectSettings.load_resource_pack].\n"
"[codeblocks]\n"
"[gdscript]\n"
"var packer = PCKPacker.new()\n"
"packer.pck_start(\"test.pck\")\n"
"packer.add_file(\"res://text.txt\", \"text.txt\")\n"
"packer.flush()\n"
"[/gdscript]\n"
"[csharp]\n"
"var packer = new PckPacker();\n"
"packer.PckStart(\"test.pck\");\n"
"packer.AddFile(\"res://text.txt\", \"text.txt\");\n"
"packer.Flush();\n"
"[/csharp]\n"
"[/codeblocks]\n"
"The above [PCKPacker] creates package [code]test.pck[/code], then adds a "
"file named [code]text.txt[/code] at the root of the package.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] PCK is Godot's own pack file format. To create ZIP archives "
"that can be read by any program, use [ZIPPacker] instead."
msgstr ""
"O [PCKPacker] é usado para criar pacotes que podem ser carregados em um "
"projeto em execução usando [method ProjectSettings.load_resource_pack].\n"
"[codeblocks]\n"
"[gdscript]\n"
"var packer = PCKPacker.new()\n"
"packer.pck_start(\"test.pck\")\n"
"packer.add_file(\"res://text.txt\", \"text.txt\")\n"
"packer.flush()\n"
"[/gdscript]\n"
"[csharp]\n"
"var packer = new PckPacker();\n"
"packer.PckStart(\"test.pck\");\n"
"packer.AddFile(\"res://text.txt\", \"text.txt\");\n"
"packer.Flush();\n"
"[/csharp]\n"
"[/codeblocks]\n"
"O [PCKPacker] acima cria o pacote [code]test.pck[/code] e, em seguida, "
"adiciona um arquivo chamado [code]text.txt[/code] na raiz do pacote.\n"
"[b]Nota:[/b] PCK é o formato de arquivo de pacote próprio do Godot. Para "
"criar arquivos ZIP que possam ser lidos por qualquer programa, use "
"[ZIPPacker] em vez disso."

#: doc/classes/PCKPacker.xml
msgid ""
"Adds the [param source_path] file to the current PCK package at the [param "
"target_path] internal path. The [code]res://[/code] prefix for [param "
"target_path] is optional and stripped internally. File content is "
"immediately written to the PCK."
msgstr ""
"Adiciona o arquivo [param source_path] ao pacote PCK atual no caminho "
"interno [param target_path]. O prefixo [code]res://[/code] para [param "
"target_path] é opcional e removido internamente. O conteúdo do arquivo é "
"gravado imediatamente no PCK."

#: doc/classes/PCKPacker.xml
msgid ""
"Adds the [param data] to the current PCK package at the [param target_path] "
"internal path. The [code]res://[/code] prefix for [param target_path] is "
"optional and stripped internally. File content is immediately written to the "
"PCK."
msgstr ""
"Adiciona os [param data] ao pacote PCK atual no caminho interno [param "
"target_path]. O prefixo [code]res://[/code] para [param target_path] é "
"opcional e removido internamente. O conteúdo do arquivo é gravado "
"imediatamente no PCK."

#: doc/classes/PCKPacker.xml
msgid ""
"Registers a file removal of the [param target_path] internal path to the "
"PCK. This is mainly used for patches. If the file at this path has been "
"loaded from a previous PCK, it will be removed. The [code]res://[/code] "
"prefix for [param target_path] is optional and stripped internally."
msgstr ""
"Registra a remoção de arquivo do caminho interno [param target_path] para o "
"PCK. Isso é usado principalmente para patches. Se o arquivo neste caminho "
"tiver sido carregado de um PCK anterior, ele será removido. O prefixo "
"[code]res://[/code] para [param target_path] é opcional e removido "
"internamente."

#: doc/classes/PCKPacker.xml
msgid ""
"Writes the file directory and closes the PCK. If [param verbose] is "
"[code]true[/code], a list of files added will be printed to the console for "
"easier debugging.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] [PCKPacker] will automatically flush when it's freed, which "
"happens when it goes out of scope or when it gets assigned with [code]null[/"
"code]. In C# the reference must be disposed after use, either with the "
"[code]using[/code] statement or by calling the [code]Dispose[/code] method "
"directly."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/PCKPacker.xml
msgid ""
"Creates a new PCK file at the file path [param pck_path]. The [code].pck[/"
"code] file extension isn't added automatically, so it should be part of "
"[param pck_path] (even though it's not required)."
msgstr ""
"Cria um novo arquivo PCK no caminho de arquivo [param pck_path]. A extensão "
"de arquivo [code].pck[/code] não é adicionada automaticamente, portanto, "
"deve fazer parte de [param pck_path] (mesmo que não seja obrigatório)."

#: doc/classes/Performance.xml
msgid "Exposes performance-related data."
msgstr "Expõe dados relacionados ao desempenho."

#: doc/classes/Performance.xml
msgid ""
"This class provides access to a number of different monitors related to "
"performance, such as memory usage, draw calls, and FPS. These are the same "
"as the values displayed in the [b]Monitor[/b] tab in the editor's "
"[b]Debugger[/b] panel. By using the [method get_monitor] method of this "
"class, you can access this data from your code.\n"
"You can add custom monitors using the [method add_custom_monitor] method. "
"Custom monitors are available in [b]Monitor[/b] tab in the editor's "
"[b]Debugger[/b] panel together with built-in monitors.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Some of the built-in monitors are only available in debug mode "
"and will always return [code]0[/code] when used in a project exported in "
"release mode.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Some of the built-in monitors are not updated in real-time for "
"performance reasons, so there may be a delay of up to 1 second between "
"changes.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Custom monitors do not support negative values. Negative values "
"are clamped to 0."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Performance.xml
msgid ""
"Adds a custom monitor with the name [param id]. You can specify the category "
"of the monitor using slash delimiters in [param id] (for example: [code]"
"\"Game/NumberOfNPCs\"[/code]). If there is more than one slash delimiter, "
"then the default category is used. The default category is [code]\"Custom\"[/"
"code]. Prints an error if given [param id] is already present.\n"
"[codeblocks]\n"
"[gdscript]\n"
"func _ready():\n"
"\tvar monitor_value = Callable(self, \"get_monitor_value\")\n"
"\n"
"\t# Adds monitor with name \"MyName\" to category \"MyCategory\".\n"
"\tPerformance.add_custom_monitor(\"MyCategory/MyMonitor\", monitor_value)\n"
"\n"
"\t# Adds monitor with name \"MyName\" to category \"Custom\".\n"
"\t# Note: \"MyCategory/MyMonitor\" and \"MyMonitor\" have same name but "
"different IDs, so the code is valid.\n"
"\tPerformance.add_custom_monitor(\"MyMonitor\", monitor_value)\n"
"\n"
"\t# Adds monitor with name \"MyName\" to category \"Custom\".\n"
"\t# Note: \"MyMonitor\" and \"Custom/MyMonitor\" have same name and same "
"category but different IDs, so the code is valid.\n"
"\tPerformance.add_custom_monitor(\"Custom/MyMonitor\", monitor_value)\n"
"\n"
"\t# Adds monitor with name \"MyCategoryOne/MyCategoryTwo/MyMonitor\" to "
"category \"Custom\".\n"
"\tPerformance.add_custom_monitor(\"MyCategoryOne/MyCategoryTwo/MyMonitor\", "
"monitor_value)\n"
"\n"
"func get_monitor_value():\n"
"\treturn randi() % 25\n"
"[/gdscript]\n"
"[csharp]\n"
"public override void _Ready()\n"
"{\n"
"\tvar monitorValue = new Callable(this, MethodName.GetMonitorValue);\n"
"\n"
"\t// Adds monitor with name \"MyName\" to category \"MyCategory\".\n"
"\tPerformance.AddCustomMonitor(\"MyCategory/MyMonitor\", monitorValue);\n"
"\t// Adds monitor with name \"MyName\" to category \"Custom\".\n"
"\t// Note: \"MyCategory/MyMonitor\" and \"MyMonitor\" have same name but "
"different ids so the code is valid.\n"
"\tPerformance.AddCustomMonitor(\"MyMonitor\", monitorValue);\n"
"\n"
"\t// Adds monitor with name \"MyName\" to category \"Custom\".\n"
"\t// Note: \"MyMonitor\" and \"Custom/MyMonitor\" have same name and same "
"category but different ids so the code is valid.\n"
"\tPerformance.AddCustomMonitor(\"Custom/MyMonitor\", monitorValue);\n"
"\n"
"\t// Adds monitor with name \"MyCategoryOne/MyCategoryTwo/MyMonitor\" to "
"category \"Custom\".\n"
"\tPerformance.AddCustomMonitor(\"MyCategoryOne/MyCategoryTwo/MyMonitor\", "
"monitorValue);\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"public int GetMonitorValue()\n"
"{\n"
"\treturn GD.Randi() % 25;\n"
"}\n"
"[/csharp]\n"
"[/codeblocks]\n"
"The debugger calls the callable to get the value of custom monitor. The "
"callable must return a zero or positive integer or floating-point number.\n"
"Callables are called with arguments supplied in argument array."
msgstr ""
"Adiciona um monitor personalizado com o nome [param id]. Você pode "
"especificar a categoria do monitor usando delimitadores de barra em [param "
"id] (por exemplo: [code]\"Game/NumberOfNPCs\"[/code]). Se houver mais de um "
"delimitador de barra, a categoria padrão será usada. A categoria padrão é "
"[code]\"Custom\"[/code]. Imprime um erro se o [param id] fornecido já "
"estiver presente.\n"
"[codeblocks]\n"
"[gdscript]\n"
"func _ready():\n"
"\tvar monitor_value = Callable(self, \"get_monitor_value\")\n"
"\n"
"\t# Adiciona um monitor com o nome \"MyName\" à categoria \"MyCategory\".\n"
"\tPerformance.add_custom_monitor(\"MyCategory/MyMonitor\", monitor_value)\n"
"\n"
"\t# Adiciona um monitor com o nome \"MyName\" à categoria \"Custom\".\n"
"\t# Nota: \"MyCategory/MyMonitor\" e \"MyMonitor\" têm o mesmo nome, mas IDs "
"diferentes, portanto o código é válido.\n"
"\tPerformance.add_custom_monitor(\"MyMonitor\", monitor_value)\n"
"\n"
"\t# Adiciona um monitor com o nome \"MyName\" à categoria \"Custom\".\n"
"\t# Nota: \"MyMonitor\" e \"Custom/MyMonitor\" têm o mesmo nome e a mesma "
"categoria, mas IDs diferentes, portanto o código é válido.\n"
"\tPerformance.add_custom_monitor(\"Custom/MyMonitor\", monitor_value)\n"
"\n"
"\t# Adiciona um monitor com o nome \"MyCategoryOne/MyCategoryTwo/MyMonitor\" "
"à categoria \"Custom\".\n"
"\tPerformance.add_custom_monitor(\"MyCategoryOne/MyCategoryTwo/MyMonitor\", "
"monitor_value)\n"
"\n"
"func get_monitor_value():\n"
"\treturn randi() % 25\n"
"[/gdscript]\n"
"[csharp]\n"
"public override void _Ready()\n"
"{\n"
"\tvar monitorValue = new Callable(this, MethodName.GetMonitorValue);\n"
"\n"
"\t// Adiciona um monitor com o nome \"MyName\" à categoria \"MyCategory\".\n"
"\tPerformance.AddCustomMonitor(\"MyCategory/MyMonitor\", monitorValue);\n"
"\t// Adiciona um monitor com o nome \"MyName\" à categoria \"Custom\".\n"
"\t// Nota: \"MyCategory/MyMonitor\" e \"MyMonitor\" têm o mesmo nome, mas "
"IDs diferentes, portanto o código é válido.\n"
"\tPerformance.AddCustomMonitor(\"MyMonitor\", monitorValue);\n"
"\n"
"\t// Adiciona um monitor com o nome \"MyName\" à categoria \"Custom\".\n"
"\t// Nota: \"MyMonitor\" e \"Custom/MyMonitor\" têm o mesmo nome e a mesma "
"categoria, mas IDs diferentes, portanto o código é válido.\n"
"\tPerformance.AddCustomMonitor(\"Custom/MyMonitor\", monitorValue);\n"
"\n"
"\t// Adiciona um monitor com o nome \"MyCategoryOne/MyCategoryTwo/"
"MyMonitor\" à categoria \"Custom\".\n"
"\tPerformance.AddCustomMonitor(\"MyCategoryOne/MyCategoryTwo/MyMonitor\", "
"monitorValue);\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"public int GetMonitorValue()\n"
"{\n"
"\treturn GD.Randi() % 25;\n"
"}\n"
"[/csharp]\n"
"[/codeblocks]\n"
"O depurador chama o callable para obter o valor do monitor personalizado. O "
"callable deve retornar um número inteiro ou de ponto flutuante zero ou "
"positivo.\n"
"Os callables são chamados com argumentos fornecidos no array de argumentos."

#: doc/classes/Performance.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the value of custom monitor with given [param id]. The callable is "
"called to get the value of custom monitor. See also [method "
"has_custom_monitor]. Prints an error if the given [param id] is absent."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o valor do monitor personalizado com o [param id] fornecido. O "
"callable é chamado para obter o valor do monitor personalizado. Consulte "
"também [method has_custom_monitor]. Imprime um erro se o [param id] "
"fornecido estiver ausente."

#: doc/classes/Performance.xml
msgid "Returns the names of active custom monitors in an [Array]."
msgstr "Retorna os nomes dos monitores personalizados ativos em um [Array]."

#: doc/classes/Performance.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the [enum MonitorType] values of active custom monitors in an "
"[Array]."
msgstr ""
"Retorna os valores [enum MonitorType] de monitores personalizados ativos em "
"um [Array]."

#: doc/classes/Performance.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the value of one of the available built-in monitors. You should "
"provide one of the [enum Monitor] constants as the argument, like this:\n"
"[codeblocks]\n"
"[gdscript]\n"
"print(Performance.get_monitor(Performance.TIME_FPS)) # Prints the FPS to the "
"console.\n"
"[/gdscript]\n"
"[csharp]\n"
"GD.Print(Performance.GetMonitor(Performance.Monitor.TimeFps)); // Prints the "
"FPS to the console.\n"
"[/csharp]\n"
"[/codeblocks]\n"
"See [method get_custom_monitor] to query custom performance monitors' values."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o valor de um dos monitores embutidos disponíveis. Você deve "
"fornecer uma das constantes de [enum Monitor] como argumento, desta forma:\n"
"[codeblocks]\n"
"[gdscript]\n"
"print(Performance.get_monitor(Performance.TIME_FPS)) # Imprime o FPS no "
"console.\n"
"[/gdscript]\n"
"[csharp]\n"
"GD.Print(Performance.GetMonitor(Performance.Monitor.TimeFps)); // Imprime o "
"FPS no console.\n"
"[/csharp]\n"
"[/codeblocks]\n"
"Consulte [method get_custom_monitor] para consultar os valores de monitores "
"de desempenho personalizados."

#: doc/classes/Performance.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the last tick in which custom monitor was added/removed (in "
"microseconds since the engine started). This is set to [method "
"Time.get_ticks_usec] when the monitor is updated."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o último tique em que o monitor personalizado foi adicionado/"
"removido (em microssegundos desde que o motor foi iniciado). Isso é definido "
"como [method Time.get_ticks_usec] quando o monitor é atualizado."

#: doc/classes/Performance.xml
msgid ""
"Returns [code]true[/code] if custom monitor with the given [param id] is "
"present, [code]false[/code] otherwise."
msgstr ""
"Retorna [code]true[/code] se o monitor personalizado com o [param id] "
"fornecido estiver presente, [code]false[/code] caso contrário."

#: doc/classes/Performance.xml
msgid ""
"Removes the custom monitor with given [param id]. Prints an error if the "
"given [param id] is already absent."
msgstr ""
"Remove o monitor personalizado com o [param id] fornecido. Exibe um erro se "
"o [param id] fornecido já estiver ausente."

#: doc/classes/Performance.xml
msgid ""
"The number of frames rendered in the last second. This metric is only "
"updated once per second, even if queried more often. [i]Higher is better.[/i]"
msgstr ""
"O número de quadros renderizados no último segundo. Essa métrica é "
"atualizada apenas uma vez por segundo, mesmo se consultada com mais "
"frequência. [i]Quanto maior, melhor.[/i]"

#: doc/classes/Performance.xml
msgid "Time it took to complete one frame, in seconds. [i]Lower is better.[/i]"
msgstr ""
"Tempo que levou para concluir um quadro, em segundos. [i]Quanto menor, "
"melhor.[/i]"

#: doc/classes/Performance.xml
msgid ""
"Time it took to complete one physics frame, in seconds. [i]Lower is better.[/"
"i]"
msgstr ""
"Tempo necessário para concluir um quadro de física, em segundos. [i]Menor é "
"melhor.[/i]"

#: doc/classes/Performance.xml
msgid ""
"Time it took to complete one navigation step, in seconds. This includes "
"navigation map updates as well as agent avoidance calculations. [i]Lower is "
"better.[/i]"
msgstr ""
"O tempo necessário para concluir uma etapa de navegação, em segundos. Isso "
"inclui atualizações do mapa de navegação, bem como cálculos de desvio de "
"agentes. [i]Menor é melhor.[/i]"

#: doc/classes/Performance.xml
msgid ""
"Static memory currently used, in bytes. Not available in release builds. "
"[i]Lower is better.[/i]"
msgstr ""
"Memória estática atualmente usada, em bytes. Não disponível em builds de "
"lançamento. [i]Quanto menor, melhor.[/i]"

#: doc/classes/Performance.xml
msgid ""
"Available static memory. Not available in release builds. [i]Lower is better."
"[/i]"
msgstr ""
"Memória estática disponível. Não disponível em builds de lançamento. "
"[i]Menor é melhor.[/i]"

#: doc/classes/Performance.xml
msgid ""
"Largest amount of memory the message queue buffer has used, in bytes. The "
"message queue is used for deferred functions calls and notifications. "
"[i]Lower is better.[/i]"
msgstr ""
"A maior quantidade de memória que o buffer da fila de mensagens utilizou, em "
"bytes. A fila de mensagens é usada para chamadas de funções adiadas e "
"notificações. [i]Menor é melhor.[/i]"

#: doc/classes/Performance.xml
msgid ""
"Number of objects currently instantiated (including nodes). [i]Lower is "
"better.[/i]"
msgstr ""
"Número de objetos instanciados atualmente (incluindo nós). [i]Quanto menor, "
"melhor.[/i]"

#: doc/classes/Performance.xml
msgid "Number of resources currently used. [i]Lower is better.[/i]"
msgstr "Número de recursos usados atualmente. [i]Menor é melhor.[/i]"

#: doc/classes/Performance.xml
msgid ""
"Number of nodes currently instantiated in the scene tree. This also includes "
"the root node. [i]Lower is better.[/i]"
msgstr ""
"Número de nós instanciados atualmente na árvore de cena. Isso também inclui "
"o nó raiz. [i]Menor é melhor.[/i]"

#: doc/classes/Performance.xml
msgid ""
"Number of orphan nodes, i.e. nodes which are not parented to a node of the "
"scene tree. [i]Lower is better.[/i]\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] This is only available in debug mode and will always return "
"[code]0[/code] when used in a project exported in release mode."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Performance.xml
msgid ""
"The total number of objects in the last rendered frame. This metric doesn't "
"include culled objects (either via hiding nodes, frustum culling or "
"occlusion culling). [i]Lower is better.[/i]"
msgstr ""
"O número total de objetos no último quadro renderizado. Esta métrica não "
"inclui objetos descartados (seja ocultando nós, por corte de frustum ou "
"corte de oclusão). [i]Menor é melhor.[/i]"

#: doc/classes/Performance.xml
msgid ""
"The total number of vertices or indices rendered in the last rendered frame. "
"This metric doesn't include primitives from culled objects (either via "
"hiding nodes, frustum culling or occlusion culling). Due to the depth "
"prepass and shadow passes, the number of primitives is always higher than "
"the actual number of vertices in the scene (typically double or triple the "
"original vertex count). [i]Lower is better.[/i]"
msgstr ""
"O número total de vértices ou índices renderizados no último quadro "
"renderizado. Esta métrica não inclui primitivas de objetos descartados (seja "
"por ocultação de nós, descarte de tronco de visão ou descarte de oclusão). "
"Devido à pré-passagem de profundidade e passagens de sombra, o número de "
"primitivas é sempre maior que o número real de vértices na cena (tipicamente "
"o dobro ou o triplo da contagem de vértices original). [i]Quanto menor, "
"melhor.[/i]"

#: doc/classes/Performance.xml
msgid ""
"The total number of draw calls performed in the last rendered frame. This "
"metric doesn't include culled objects (either via hiding nodes, frustum "
"culling or occlusion culling), since they do not result in draw calls. "
"[i]Lower is better.[/i]"
msgstr ""
"O número total de chamadas de desenho realizadas no último quadro "
"renderizado. Esta métrica não inclui objetos eliminados (seja por ocultação "
"de nós, eliminação de frustum ou eliminação de oclusão), pois eles não "
"resultam em chamadas de desenho. [i]Menor é melhor.[/i]"

#: doc/classes/Performance.xml
msgid ""
"The amount of video memory used (texture and vertex memory combined, in "
"bytes). Since this metric also includes miscellaneous allocations, this "
"value is always greater than the sum of [constant RENDER_TEXTURE_MEM_USED] "
"and [constant RENDER_BUFFER_MEM_USED]. [i]Lower is better.[/i]"
msgstr ""
"A quantidade de memória de vídeo usada (memória de textura e de vértices "
"combinadas, em bytes). Como esta métrica também inclui alocações diversas, "
"este valor é sempre maior do que a soma de [constant "
"RENDER_TEXTURE_MEM_USED] e [constant RENDER_BUFFER_MEM_USED]. [i]Quanto "
"menor, melhor.[/i]"

#: doc/classes/Performance.xml
msgid "The amount of texture memory used (in bytes). [i]Lower is better.[/i]"
msgstr ""
"A quantidade de memória de textura usada (em bytes). [i]Menor é melhor.[/i]"

#: doc/classes/Performance.xml
msgid ""
"The amount of render buffer memory used (in bytes). [i]Lower is better.[/i]"
msgstr ""
"A quantidade de memória de buffer de renderização usada (em bytes). "
"[i]Quanto menor, melhor.[/i]"

#: doc/classes/Performance.xml
msgid ""
"Number of active [RigidBody2D] nodes in the game. [i]Lower is better.[/i]"
msgstr ""
"Número de nós [RigidBody2D] ativos no jogo. [i]Quanto menor, melhor.[/i]"

#: doc/classes/Performance.xml
msgid ""
"Number of collision pairs in the 2D physics engine. [i]Lower is better.[/i]"
msgstr ""
"Número de pares de colisão no motor de física 2D. [i]Quanto menor, melhor.[/"
"i]"

#: doc/classes/Performance.xml
msgid "Number of islands in the 2D physics engine. [i]Lower is better.[/i]"
msgstr "Número de ilhas no motor de física 2D. [i]Menor é melhor.[/i]"

#: doc/classes/Performance.xml
msgid ""
"Number of active [RigidBody3D] and [VehicleBody3D] nodes in the game. "
"[i]Lower is better.[/i]"
msgstr ""
"Número de nós [RigidBody3D] e [VehicleBody3D] ativos no jogo. [i]Quanto "
"menor, melhor.[/i]"

#: doc/classes/Performance.xml
msgid ""
"Number of collision pairs in the 3D physics engine. [i]Lower is better.[/i]"
msgstr ""
"Número de pares de colisão no motor de física 3D. [i]Quanto menor, melhor.[/"
"i]"

#: doc/classes/Performance.xml
msgid "Number of islands in the 3D physics engine. [i]Lower is better.[/i]"
msgstr "Número de ilhas no motor de física 3D. [i]Menor é melhor.[/i]"

#: doc/classes/Performance.xml
msgid ""
"Output latency of the [AudioServer]. Equivalent to calling [method "
"AudioServer.get_output_latency], it is not recommended to call this every "
"frame."
msgstr ""
"Latência de saída do [AudioServer]. Equivalente a chamar [method "
"AudioServer.get_output_latency], não é recomendado chamar isso a cada quadro."

#: doc/classes/Performance.xml
msgid ""
"Number of active navigation maps in [NavigationServer2D] and "
"[NavigationServer3D]. This also includes the empty default navigation maps "
"created by [World2D] and [World3D] instances."
msgstr ""
"Número de mapas de navegação ativos em [NavigationServer2D] e "
"[NavigationServer3D]. Isso também inclui os mapas de navegação padrão vazios "
"criados pelas instâncias de [World2D] e [World3D]."

#: doc/classes/Performance.xml
msgid ""
"Number of active navigation regions in [NavigationServer2D] and "
"[NavigationServer3D]."
msgstr ""
"Número de regiões de navegação ativas no [NavigationServer2D] e no "
"[NavigationServer3D]."

#: doc/classes/Performance.xml
msgid ""
"Number of active navigation agents processing avoidance in "
"[NavigationServer2D] and [NavigationServer3D]."
msgstr ""
"Número de agentes de navegação ativos processando evasão em "
"[NavigationServer2D] e [NavigationServer3D]."

#: doc/classes/Performance.xml
msgid ""
"Number of active navigation links in [NavigationServer2D] and "
"[NavigationServer3D]."
msgstr ""
"Número de links de navegação ativos no [NavigationServer2D] e no "
"[NavigationServer3D]."

#: doc/classes/Performance.xml
msgid ""
"Number of navigation mesh polygons in [NavigationServer2D] and "
"[NavigationServer3D]."
msgstr ""
"Número de polígonos de malha de navegação no [NavigationServer2D] e no "
"[NavigationServer3D]."

#: doc/classes/Performance.xml
msgid ""
"Number of navigation mesh polygon edges in [NavigationServer2D] and "
"[NavigationServer3D]."
msgstr ""
"Número de arestas de polígono de malha de navegação no [NavigationServer2D] "
"e [NavigationServer3D]."

#: doc/classes/Performance.xml
msgid ""
"Number of navigation mesh polygon edges that were merged due to edge key "
"overlap in [NavigationServer2D] and [NavigationServer3D]."
msgstr ""
"Número de arestas de polígonos de malha de navegação que foram mescladas "
"devido à sobreposição de chaves de aresta em [NavigationServer2D] e "
"[NavigationServer3D]."

#: doc/classes/Performance.xml
msgid ""
"Number of polygon edges that are considered connected by edge proximity "
"[NavigationServer2D] and [NavigationServer3D]."
msgstr ""
"Número de arestas de polígono consideradas conectadas por proximidade de "
"arestas [NavigationServer2D] e [NavigationServer3D]."

#: doc/classes/Performance.xml
msgid ""
"Number of navigation mesh polygon edges that could not be merged in "
"[NavigationServer2D] and [NavigationServer3D]. The edges still may be "
"connected by edge proximity or with links."
msgstr ""
"Número de arestas de polígono de malha de navegação que não puderam ser "
"mescladas em [NavigationServer2D] e [NavigationServer3D]. As arestas ainda "
"podem estar conectadas por proximidade de arestas ou com links."

#: doc/classes/Performance.xml
msgid ""
"Number of active navigation obstacles in the [NavigationServer2D] and "
"[NavigationServer3D]."
msgstr ""
"Número de obstáculos de navegação ativos no [NavigationServer2D] e no "
"[NavigationServer3D]."

#: doc/classes/Performance.xml doc/classes/RenderingServer.xml
msgid ""
"Number of pipeline compilations that were triggered by the 2D canvas "
"renderer."
msgstr ""
"Número de compilações de pipeline que foram acionadas pelo renderizador de "
"canvas 2D."

#: doc/classes/Performance.xml doc/classes/RenderingServer.xml
msgid ""
"Number of pipeline compilations that were triggered by loading meshes. These "
"compilations will show up as longer loading times the first time a user runs "
"the game and the pipeline is required."
msgstr ""
"Número de compilações de pipeline que foram disparadas pelo carregamento de "
"malhas. Essas compilações aparecerão como tempos de carregamento mais longos "
"na primeira vez que um usuário executar o jogo e o pipeline for necessário."

#: doc/classes/Performance.xml doc/classes/RenderingServer.xml
msgid ""
"Number of pipeline compilations that were triggered by building the surface "
"cache before rendering the scene. These compilations will show up as a "
"stutter when loading a scene the first time a user runs the game and the "
"pipeline is required."
msgstr ""
"Número de compilações de pipeline que foram acionadas pela construção do "
"cache de superfície antes de renderizar a cena. Essas compilações aparecerão "
"como um engasgo ao carregar uma cena pela primeira vez em que um usuário "
"executa o jogo e o pipeline é necessário."

#: doc/classes/Performance.xml doc/classes/RenderingServer.xml
msgid ""
"Number of pipeline compilations that were triggered while drawing the scene. "
"These compilations will show up as stutters during gameplay the first time a "
"user runs the game and the pipeline is required."
msgstr ""
"Número de compilações de pipeline que foram acionadas ao desenhar a cena. "
"Essas compilações aparecerão como engasgos (stutters) durante a jogabilidade "
"na primeira vez que um usuário executar o jogo e o pipeline for necessário."

#: doc/classes/Performance.xml doc/classes/RenderingServer.xml
msgid ""
"Number of pipeline compilations that were triggered to optimize the current "
"scene. These compilations are done in the background and should not cause "
"any stutters whatsoever."
msgstr ""
"Número de compilações de pipeline que foram disparadas para otimizar a cena "
"atual. Essas compilações são feitas em segundo plano e não devem causar "
"nenhum engasgo."

#: doc/classes/Performance.xml
msgid ""
"Number of active navigation maps in the [NavigationServer2D]. This also "
"includes the empty default navigation maps created by [World2D] instances."
msgstr ""
"Número de mapas de navegação ativos no [NavigationServer2D]. Isso também "
"inclui os mapas de navegação padrão vazios criados por instâncias de "
"[World2D]."

#: doc/classes/Performance.xml
msgid "Number of active navigation regions in the [NavigationServer2D]."
msgstr "Número de regiões de navegação ativas no [NavigationServer2D]."

#: doc/classes/Performance.xml
msgid ""
"Number of active navigation agents processing avoidance in the "
"[NavigationServer2D]."
msgstr ""
"Número de agentes de navegação ativos processando evasão no "
"[NavigationServer2D]."

#: doc/classes/Performance.xml
msgid "Number of active navigation links in the [NavigationServer2D]."
msgstr "Número de links de navegação ativos no [NavigationServer2D]."

#: doc/classes/Performance.xml
msgid "Number of navigation mesh polygons in the [NavigationServer2D]."
msgstr "Número de polígonos de malha de navegação no [NavigationServer2D]."

#: doc/classes/Performance.xml
msgid "Number of navigation mesh polygon edges in the [NavigationServer2D]."
msgstr ""
"Número de arestas de polígonos de malha de navegação no [NavigationServer2D]."

#: doc/classes/Performance.xml
msgid ""
"Number of navigation mesh polygon edges that were merged due to edge key "
"overlap in the [NavigationServer2D]."
msgstr ""
"Número de arestas de polígonos de malha de navegação que foram mescladas "
"devido à sobreposição de chaves de aresta no [NavigationServer2D]."

#: doc/classes/Performance.xml
msgid ""
"Number of polygon edges that are considered connected by edge proximity "
"[NavigationServer2D]."
msgstr ""
"Número de arestas de polígono consideradas conectadas por proximidade de "
"aresta [NavigationServer2D]."

#: doc/classes/Performance.xml
msgid ""
"Number of navigation mesh polygon edges that could not be merged in the "
"[NavigationServer2D]. The edges still may be connected by edge proximity or "
"with links."
msgstr ""
"Número de arestas de polígono de malha de navegação que não puderam ser "
"mescladas no [NavigationServer2D]. As arestas ainda podem ser conectadas por "
"proximidade de arestas ou com links."

#: doc/classes/Performance.xml
msgid "Number of active navigation obstacles in the [NavigationServer2D]."
msgstr "Número de obstáculos de navegação ativos no [NavigationServer2D]."

#: doc/classes/Performance.xml
msgid ""
"Number of active navigation maps in the [NavigationServer3D]. This also "
"includes the empty default navigation maps created by [World3D] instances."
msgstr ""
"Número de mapas de navegação ativos no [NavigationServer3D]. Isso também "
"inclui os mapas de navegação padrão vazios criados por instâncias de "
"[World3D]."

#: doc/classes/Performance.xml
msgid "Number of active navigation regions in the [NavigationServer3D]."
msgstr "Número de regiões de navegação ativas no [NavigationServer3D]."

#: doc/classes/Performance.xml
msgid ""
"Number of active navigation agents processing avoidance in the "
"[NavigationServer3D]."
msgstr ""
"Número de agentes de navegação ativos processando evasão no "
"[NavigationServer3D]."

#: doc/classes/Performance.xml
msgid "Number of active navigation links in the [NavigationServer3D]."
msgstr "Número de links de navegação ativos no [NavigationServer3D]."

#: doc/classes/Performance.xml
msgid "Number of navigation mesh polygons in the [NavigationServer3D]."
msgstr "Número de polígonos de malha de navegação no [NavigationServer3D]."

#: doc/classes/Performance.xml
msgid "Number of navigation mesh polygon edges in the [NavigationServer3D]."
msgstr ""
"Número de arestas de polígonos de malha de navegação no [NavigationServer3D]."

#: doc/classes/Performance.xml
msgid ""
"Number of navigation mesh polygon edges that were merged due to edge key "
"overlap in the [NavigationServer3D]."
msgstr ""
"Número de arestas de polígono de malha de navegação que foram mescladas "
"devido à sobreposição de chaves de aresta no [NavigationServer3D]."

#: doc/classes/Performance.xml
msgid ""
"Number of polygon edges that are considered connected by edge proximity "
"[NavigationServer3D]."
msgstr ""
"Número de arestas de polígono consideradas conectadas por proximidade de "
"arestas [NavigationServer3D]."

#: doc/classes/Performance.xml
msgid ""
"Number of navigation mesh polygon edges that could not be merged in the "
"[NavigationServer3D]. The edges still may be connected by edge proximity or "
"with links."
msgstr ""
"Número de arestas de polígono de malha de navegação que não puderam ser "
"mescladas no [NavigationServer3D]. As arestas ainda podem ser conectadas por "
"proximidade de arestas ou com links."

#: doc/classes/Performance.xml
msgid "Number of active navigation obstacles in the [NavigationServer3D]."
msgstr "Número de obstáculos de navegação ativos no [NavigationServer3D]."

#: doc/classes/Performance.xml
msgid "Represents the size of the [enum Monitor] enum."
msgstr "Representa o tamanho da enumeração [enum Monitor]."

#: doc/classes/Performance.xml
msgid "Monitor output is formatted as an integer value."
msgstr "A saída do monitor é formatada como um valor inteiro."

#: doc/classes/Performance.xml
msgid ""
"Monitor output is formatted as computer memory. Submitted values should "
"represent a number of bytes."
msgstr ""
"A saída do monitor é formatada como memória de computador. Os valores "
"enviados devem representar um número de bytes."

#: doc/classes/Performance.xml
msgid ""
"Monitor output is formatted as time in milliseconds. Submitted values should "
"represent a time in seconds (not milliseconds)."
msgstr ""
"A saída do monitor é formatada como tempo em milissegundos. Os valores "
"enviados devem representar um tempo em segundos (não milissegundos)."

#: doc/classes/Performance.xml
msgid ""
"Monitor output is formatted as a percentage. Submitted values should "
"represent a fractional value rather than the percentage directly, e.g. "
"[code]0.5[/code] for [code]50.00%[/code]."
msgstr ""
"A saída do monitor é formatada como uma porcentagem. Os valores enviados "
"devem representar um valor fracionário em vez da porcentagem diretamente, "
"ex: [code]0.5[/code] para [code]50.00%[/code]."

#: doc/classes/PhysicalBone2D.xml
msgid ""
"A [RigidBody2D]-derived node used to make [Bone2D]s in a [Skeleton2D] react "
"to physics."
msgstr ""
"Um nó derivado de [RigidBody2D] usado para fazer [Bone2D]s em um "
"[Skeleton2D] reagirem à física."

#: doc/classes/PhysicalBone2D.xml
msgid ""
"The [PhysicalBone2D] node is a [RigidBody2D]-based node that can be used to "
"make [Bone2D]s in a [Skeleton2D] react to physics.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] To make the [Bone2D]s visually follow the [PhysicalBone2D] "
"node, use a [SkeletonModification2DPhysicalBones] modification on the "
"[Skeleton2D] parent.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] The [PhysicalBone2D] node does not automatically create a "
"[Joint2D] node to keep [PhysicalBone2D] nodes together. They must be created "
"manually. For most cases, you want to use a [PinJoint2D] node. The "
"[PhysicalBone2D] node will automatically configure the [Joint2D] node once "
"it's been added as a child node."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/PhysicalBone2D.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the first [Joint2D] child node, if one exists. This is mainly a "
"helper function to make it easier to get the [Joint2D] that the "
"[PhysicalBone2D] is autoconfiguring."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o primeiro nó filho [Joint2D], se existir um. Esta é principalmente "
"uma função auxiliar para facilitar a obtenção da [Joint2D] que o "
"[PhysicalBone2D] está autoconfigurando."

#: doc/classes/PhysicalBone2D.xml
msgid ""
"Returns a boolean that indicates whether the [PhysicalBone2D] is running and "
"simulating using the Godot 2D physics engine. When [code]true[/code], the "
"PhysicalBone2D node is using physics."
msgstr ""
"Retorna um booleano que indica se o [PhysicalBone2D] está executando e "
"simulando usando o motor de física 2D do Godot. Quando [code]true[/code], o "
"nó PhysicalBone2D está usando física."

#: doc/classes/PhysicalBone2D.xml
msgid ""
"If [code]true[/code], the [PhysicalBone2D] will automatically configure the "
"first [Joint2D] child node. The automatic configuration is limited to "
"setting up the node properties and positioning the [Joint2D]."
msgstr ""
"Se [code]true[/code], o [PhysicalBone2D] configurará automaticamente o "
"primeiro nó filho [Joint2D]. A configuração automática é limitada a definir "
"as propriedades do nó e posicionar o [Joint2D]."

#: doc/classes/PhysicalBone2D.xml
msgid "The index of the [Bone2D] that this [PhysicalBone2D] should simulate."
msgstr "O índice do [Bone2D] que este [PhysicalBone3D] deve simular."

#: doc/classes/PhysicalBone2D.xml
msgid ""
"The [NodePath] to the [Bone2D] that this [PhysicalBone2D] should simulate."
msgstr "O [NodePath] para o [Bone2D] que este [PhysicalBone2D] deve simular."

#: doc/classes/PhysicalBone2D.xml
msgid ""
"If [code]true[/code], the [PhysicalBone2D] will keep the transform of the "
"bone it is bound to when simulating physics."
msgstr ""
"Se [code]true[/code], o [PhysicalBone2D] manterá a transformação do osso ao "
"qual está vinculado ao simular física."

#: doc/classes/PhysicalBone2D.xml
msgid ""
"If [code]true[/code], the [PhysicalBone2D] will start simulating using "
"physics. If [code]false[/code], the [PhysicalBone2D] will follow the "
"transform of the [Bone2D] node.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] To have the [Bone2D]s visually follow the [PhysicalBone2D], use "
"a [SkeletonModification2DPhysicalBones] modification on the [Skeleton2D] "
"node with the [Bone2D] nodes."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/PhysicalBone3D.xml
msgid "A physics body used to make bones in a [Skeleton3D] react to physics."
msgstr ""
"Um corpo de física usado para fazer os ossos em um [Skeleton3D] reagirem à "
"física."

#: doc/classes/PhysicalBone3D.xml
msgid ""
"The [PhysicalBone3D] node is a physics body that can be used to make bones "
"in a [Skeleton3D] react to physics.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] In order to detect physical bones with raycasts, the [member "
"SkeletonModifier3D.active] property of the parent [PhysicalBoneSimulator3D] "
"must be [code]true[/code] and the [Skeleton3D]'s bone must be assigned to "
"[PhysicalBone3D] correctly; it means that [method get_bone_id] should return "
"a valid id ([code]>= 0[/code])."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/PhysicalBone3D.xml
msgid "Ragdoll System"
msgstr "Sistema de Boneca de Trapo"

#: doc/classes/PhysicalBone3D.xml doc/classes/RigidBody2D.xml
#: doc/classes/RigidBody3D.xml
msgid ""
"Called during physics processing, allowing you to read and safely modify the "
"simulation state for the object. By default, it is called before the "
"standard force integration, but the [member custom_integrator] property "
"allows you to disable the standard force integration and do fully custom "
"force integration for a body."
msgstr ""
"Chamado durante o processamento de física, permitindo que você leia e "
"modifique com segurança o estado da simulação para o objeto. Por padrão, é "
"chamado antes da integração de força padrão, mas a propriedade [member "
"custom_integrator] permite que você desative a integração de força padrão e "
"faça uma integração de força totalmente personalizada para um corpo."

#: doc/classes/PhysicalBone3D.xml
msgid ""
"Applies a directional impulse without affecting rotation.\n"
"An impulse is time-independent! Applying an impulse every frame would result "
"in a framerate-dependent force. For this reason, it should only be used when "
"simulating one-time impacts (use the \"_integrate_forces\" functions "
"otherwise).\n"
"This is equivalent to using [method apply_impulse] at the body's center of "
"mass."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/PhysicalBone3D.xml
msgid ""
"Applies a positioned impulse to the PhysicsBone3D.\n"
"An impulse is time-independent! Applying an impulse every frame would result "
"in a framerate-dependent force. For this reason, it should only be used when "
"simulating one-time impacts (use the \"_integrate_forces\" functions "
"otherwise).\n"
"[param position] is the offset from the PhysicsBone3D origin in global "
"coordinates."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/PhysicalBone3D.xml
msgid "Returns the unique identifier of the PhysicsBone3D."
msgstr "Retorna o identificador exclusivo do PhysicsBone3D."

#: doc/classes/PhysicalBone3D.xml
msgid ""
"Returns [code]true[/code] if the PhysicsBone3D is allowed to simulate "
"physics."
msgstr ""
"Retorna [code]true[/code] se o PhysicsBone3D tiver permissão para simular "
"física."

#: doc/classes/PhysicalBone3D.xml
msgid ""
"Returns [code]true[/code] if the PhysicsBone3D is currently simulating "
"physics."
msgstr ""
"Retorna [code]true[/code] se o PhysicsBone3D estiver simulando física no "
"momento."

#: doc/classes/PhysicalBone3D.xml doc/classes/RigidBody3D.xml
msgid ""
"Damps the body's rotation. By default, the body will use the [member "
"ProjectSettings.physics/3d/default_angular_damp] project setting or any "
"value override set by an [Area3D] the body is in. Depending on [member "
"angular_damp_mode], you can set [member angular_damp] to be added to or to "
"replace the body's damping value.\n"
"See [member ProjectSettings.physics/3d/default_angular_damp] for more "
"details about damping."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/PhysicalBone3D.xml doc/classes/RigidBody2D.xml
#: doc/classes/RigidBody3D.xml
msgid "Defines how [member angular_damp] is applied."
msgstr "Define como [member angular_damp] é aplicado."

#: doc/classes/PhysicalBone3D.xml
msgid "The PhysicalBone3D's rotational velocity in [i]radians[/i] per second."
msgstr ""
"A velocidade rotacional do PhysicalBone3D em [i]radians[/i] por segundo."

#: doc/classes/PhysicalBone3D.xml
msgid "Sets the body's transform."
msgstr "Define a transformação do corpo."

#: doc/classes/PhysicalBone3D.xml
msgid ""
"The body's bounciness. Values range from [code]0[/code] (no bounce) to "
"[code]1[/code] (full bounciness).\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Even with [member bounce] set to [code]1.0[/code], some energy "
"will be lost over time due to linear and angular damping. To have a "
"[PhysicalBone3D] that preserves all its energy over time, set [member "
"bounce] to [code]1.0[/code], [member linear_damp_mode] to [constant "
"DAMP_MODE_REPLACE], [member linear_damp] to [code]0.0[/code], [member "
"angular_damp_mode] to [constant DAMP_MODE_REPLACE], and [member "
"angular_damp] to [code]0.0[/code]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/PhysicalBone3D.xml
msgid ""
"If [code]true[/code], the body is deactivated when there is no movement, so "
"it will not take part in the simulation until it is awakened by an external "
"force."
msgstr ""
"Se [code]true[/code], o corpo é desativado quando não há movimento, para que "
"não participe da simulação até ser acordado por uma força externa."

#: doc/classes/PhysicalBone3D.xml doc/classes/RigidBody3D.xml
msgid ""
"If [code]true[/code], the standard force integration (like gravity or "
"damping) will be disabled for this body. Other than collision response, the "
"body will only move as determined by the [method _integrate_forces] method, "
"if that virtual method is overridden.\n"
"Setting this property will call the method [method "
"PhysicsServer3D.body_set_omit_force_integration] internally."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/PhysicalBone3D.xml
msgid ""
"The body's friction, from [code]0[/code] (frictionless) to [code]1[/code] "
"(max friction)."
msgstr ""
"O atrito do corpo, de [code]0[/code] (sem atrito) a [code]1[/code] (atrito "
"máximo)."

#: doc/classes/PhysicalBone3D.xml doc/classes/RigidBody3D.xml
msgid ""
"This is multiplied by [member ProjectSettings.physics/3d/default_gravity] to "
"produce this body's gravity. For example, a value of [code]1.0[/code] will "
"apply normal gravity, [code]2.0[/code] will apply double the gravity, and "
"[code]0.5[/code] will apply half the gravity to this body."
msgstr ""
"Isso é multiplicado por [member ProjectSettings.physics/3d/default_gravity] "
"para produzir a gravidade deste corpo. Por exemplo, um valor de [code]1.0[/"
"code] aplicará gravidade normal, [code]2.0[/code] aplicará o dobro da "
"gravidade e [code]0.5[/code] aplicará metade da gravidade a este corpo."

#: doc/classes/PhysicalBone3D.xml
msgid "Sets the joint's transform."
msgstr "Define a transformação da articulação."

#: doc/classes/PhysicalBone3D.xml
msgid "Sets the joint's rotation in radians."
msgstr "Define a rotação da articulação em radianos."

#: doc/classes/PhysicalBone3D.xml
msgid "Sets the joint type."
msgstr "Define o tipo de articulação."

#: doc/classes/PhysicalBone3D.xml
msgid ""
"Damps the body's movement. By default, the body will use [member "
"ProjectSettings.physics/3d/default_linear_damp] or any value override set by "
"an [Area3D] the body is in. Depending on [member linear_damp_mode], [member "
"linear_damp] may be added to or replace the body's damping value.\n"
"See [member ProjectSettings.physics/3d/default_linear_damp] for more details "
"about damping."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/PhysicalBone3D.xml doc/classes/RigidBody2D.xml
#: doc/classes/RigidBody3D.xml
msgid "Defines how [member linear_damp] is applied."
msgstr "Define como [member linear_damp] é aplicado."

#: doc/classes/PhysicalBone3D.xml doc/classes/RigidBody3D.xml
msgid ""
"The body's linear velocity in units per second. Can be used sporadically, "
"but [b]don't set this every frame[/b], because physics may run in another "
"thread and runs at a different granularity. Use [method _integrate_forces] "
"as your process loop for precise control of the body state."
msgstr ""
"A velocidade linear do corpo em unidades por segundo. Pode ser usada "
"esporadicamente, mas [b]não defina isso a cada quadro[/b], porque a física "
"pode ser executada em outra thread e roda em uma granularidade diferente. "
"Use [method _integrate_forces] como seu loop de processo para controle "
"preciso do estado do corpo."

#: doc/classes/PhysicalBone3D.xml doc/classes/RigidBody2D.xml
#: doc/classes/RigidBody3D.xml
msgid "The body's mass."
msgstr "A massa do corpo."

#: doc/classes/PhysicalBone3D.xml doc/classes/RigidBody2D.xml
#: doc/classes/RigidBody3D.xml
msgid ""
"In this mode, the body's damping value is added to any value set in areas or "
"the default value."
msgstr ""
"Neste modo, o valor de amortecimento do corpo é adicionado a qualquer valor "
"definido em áreas ou ao valor padrão."

#: doc/classes/PhysicalBone3D.xml doc/classes/RigidBody2D.xml
#: doc/classes/RigidBody3D.xml
msgid ""
"In this mode, the body's damping value replaces any value set in areas or "
"the default value."
msgstr ""
"Neste modo, o valor de amortecimento do corpo substitui qualquer valor "
"definido em áreas ou o valor padrão."

#: doc/classes/PhysicalBone3D.xml
msgid "No joint is applied to the PhysicsBone3D."
msgstr "Nenhuma junta é aplicada ao PhysicsBone3D."

#: doc/classes/PhysicalBone3D.xml
msgid "A pin joint is applied to the PhysicsBone3D."
msgstr "Uma junta de pino é aplicada ao PhysicsBone3D."

#: doc/classes/PhysicalBone3D.xml
msgid "A cone joint is applied to the PhysicsBone3D."
msgstr "Uma junta cônica é aplicada ao PhysicsBone3D."

#: doc/classes/PhysicalBone3D.xml
msgid "A hinge joint is applied to the PhysicsBone3D."
msgstr "Uma junta de dobradiça é aplicada ao PhysicsBone3D."

#: doc/classes/PhysicalBone3D.xml
msgid "A slider joint is applied to the PhysicsBone3D."
msgstr "Uma junta deslizante é aplicada ao PhysicsBone3D."

#: doc/classes/PhysicalBone3D.xml
msgid "A 6 degrees of freedom joint is applied to the PhysicsBone3D."
msgstr "Uma junta de 6 graus de liberdade é aplicada ao PhysicsBone3D."

#: doc/classes/PhysicalBoneSimulator3D.xml
msgid ""
"Node that can be the parent of [PhysicalBone3D] and can apply the simulation "
"results to [Skeleton3D]."
msgstr ""
"Nó que pode ser o pai de [PhysicalBone3D] e pode aplicar os resultados da "
"simulação ao [Skeleton3D]."

#: doc/classes/PhysicalBoneSimulator3D.xml
msgid ""
"Returns a boolean that indicates whether the [PhysicalBoneSimulator3D] is "
"running and simulating."
msgstr ""
"Retorna um booleano que indica se o [PhysicalBoneSimulator3D] está em "
"execução e simulando."

#: doc/classes/PhysicalBoneSimulator3D.xml doc/classes/Skeleton3D.xml
msgid ""
"Adds a collision exception to the physical bone.\n"
"Works just like the [RigidBody3D] node."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/PhysicalBoneSimulator3D.xml doc/classes/Skeleton3D.xml
msgid ""
"Removes a collision exception to the physical bone.\n"
"Works just like the [RigidBody3D] node."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/PhysicalBoneSimulator3D.xml doc/classes/Skeleton3D.xml
msgid ""
"Tells the [PhysicalBone3D] nodes in the Skeleton to start simulating and "
"reacting to the physics world.\n"
"Optionally, a list of bone names can be passed-in, allowing only the passed-"
"in bones to be simulated."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/PhysicalBoneSimulator3D.xml doc/classes/Skeleton3D.xml
msgid "Tells the [PhysicalBone3D] nodes in the Skeleton to stop simulating."
msgstr "Diz aos nós [PhysicalBone3D] no Skeleton para parar de simular."

#: doc/classes/PhysicalSkyMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"A material that defines a sky for a [Sky] resource by a set of physical "
"properties."
msgstr ""
"Um material que define um céu para um recurso [Sky] por meio de um conjunto "
"de propriedades físicas."

#: doc/classes/PhysicalSkyMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"The [PhysicalSkyMaterial] uses the Preetham analytic daylight model to draw "
"a sky based on physical properties. This results in a substantially more "
"realistic sky than the [ProceduralSkyMaterial], but it is slightly slower "
"and less flexible.\n"
"The [PhysicalSkyMaterial] only supports one sun. The color, energy, and "
"direction of the sun are taken from the first [DirectionalLight3D] in the "
"scene tree."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/PhysicalSkyMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"Modulates the [Color] on the bottom half of the sky to represent the ground."
msgstr "Modula o [Color] na metade inferior do céu para representar o solo."

#: doc/classes/PhysicalSkyMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"Controls the strength of [url=https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/"
"Mie_scattering]Mie scattering[/url] for the sky. Mie scattering results from "
"light colliding with larger particles (like water). On earth, Mie scattering "
"results in a whitish color around the sun and horizon."
msgstr ""
"Controla a força do [url=https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/"
"Mie_scattering]espalhamento de Mie[/url] para o céu. O espalhamento de Mie "
"resulta da colisão da luz com partículas maiores (como água). Na Terra, o "
"espalhamento de Mie resulta em uma cor esbranquiçada ao redor do sol e do "
"horizonte."

#: doc/classes/PhysicalSkyMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"Controls the [Color] of the [url=https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/"
"Mie_scattering]Mie scattering[/url] effect. While not physically accurate, "
"this allows for the creation of alien-looking planets."
msgstr ""
"Controla o [Color] do efeito [url=https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/"
"Mie_scattering]dispersão de Mie[/url]. Embora não seja fisicamente preciso, "
"isso permite a criação de planetas com aparência alienígena."

#: doc/classes/PhysicalSkyMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"Controls the direction of the [url=https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/"
"Mie_scattering]Mie scattering[/url]. A value of [code]1[/code] means that "
"when light hits a particle it's passing through straight forward. A value of "
"[code]-1[/code] means that all light is scatter backwards."
msgstr ""
"Controla a direção do [url=https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/"
"Mie_scattering]espalhamento de Mie[/url]. Um valor de [code]1[/code] "
"significa que, quando a luz atinge uma partícula, ela passa direto. Um valor "
"de [code]-1[/code] significa que toda a luz é espalhada para trás."

#: doc/classes/PhysicalSkyMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"[Texture2D] for the night sky. This is added to the sky, so if it is bright "
"enough, it may be visible during the day."
msgstr ""
"[Texture2D] para o céu noturno. Isso é adicionado ao céu, portanto, se for "
"brilhante o suficiente, pode ficar visível durante o dia."

#: doc/classes/PhysicalSkyMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"Controls the strength of the [url=https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/"
"Rayleigh_scattering]Rayleigh scattering[/url]. Rayleigh scattering results "
"from light colliding with small particles. It is responsible for the blue "
"color of the sky."
msgstr ""
"Controla a força do [url=https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/"
"Rayleigh_scattering]espalhamento de Rayleigh[/url]. O espalhamento de "
"Rayleigh resulta da colisão da luz com pequenas partículas. Ele é "
"responsável pela cor azul do céu."

#: doc/classes/PhysicalSkyMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"Controls the [Color] of the [url=https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/"
"Rayleigh_scattering]Rayleigh scattering[/url]. While not physically "
"accurate, this allows for the creation of alien-looking planets. For "
"example, setting this to a red [Color] results in a Mars-looking atmosphere "
"with a corresponding blue sunset."
msgstr ""
"Controla a [Color] do espalhamento de [url=https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/"
"Rayleigh_scattering]Rayleigh[/url]. Embora não seja fisicamente preciso, "
"isso permite a criação de planetas com aparência alienígena. Por exemplo, "
"definir isso para uma [Color] vermelha resulta em uma atmosfera com "
"aparência de Marte com um pôr do sol azul correspondente."

#: doc/classes/PhysicalSkyMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"Sets the size of the sun disk. Default value is based on Sol's perceived "
"size from Earth."
msgstr ""
"Define o tamanho do disco solar. O valor padrão é baseado no tamanho "
"percebido do Sol a partir da Terra."

#: doc/classes/PhysicalSkyMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"Sets the thickness of the atmosphere. High turbidity creates a foggy-looking "
"atmosphere, while a low turbidity results in a clearer atmosphere."
msgstr ""
"Define a espessura da atmosfera. Alta turbidez cria uma atmosfera com "
"aparência nebulosa, enquanto baixa turbidez resulta em uma atmosfera mais "
"clara."

#: doc/classes/PhysicalSkyMaterial.xml doc/classes/ProceduralSkyMaterial.xml
msgid ""
"If [code]true[/code], enables debanding. Debanding adds a small amount of "
"noise which helps reduce banding that appears from the smooth changes in "
"color in the sky."
msgstr ""
"Se [code]true[/code], ativa o debanding. O debanding adiciona uma pequena "
"quantidade de ruído que ajuda a reduzir o banding que aparece nas mudanças "
"suaves de cor no céu."

#: doc/classes/PhysicsBody2D.xml
msgid "Abstract base class for 2D game objects affected by physics."
msgstr "Classe base abstrata para objetos de jogo 2D afetados por física."

#: doc/classes/PhysicsBody2D.xml
msgid ""
"[PhysicsBody2D] is an abstract base class for 2D game objects affected by "
"physics. All 2D physics bodies inherit from it."
msgstr ""
"[PhysicsBody2D] é uma classe base abstrata para objetos de jogo 2D afetados "
"por física. Todos os corpos físicos 2D herdam dela."

#: doc/classes/PhysicsBody2D.xml doc/classes/PhysicsBody3D.xml
#: doc/classes/SoftBody3D.xml
msgid "Adds a body to the list of bodies that this body can't collide with."
msgstr ""
"Adiciona um corpo à lista de corpos com os quais este corpo não pode colidir."

#: doc/classes/PhysicsBody2D.xml doc/classes/PhysicsBody3D.xml
#: doc/classes/SoftBody3D.xml
msgid ""
"Returns an array of nodes that were added as collision exceptions for this "
"body."
msgstr ""
"Retorna um array de nós que foram adicionados como exceções de colisão para "
"este corpo."

#: doc/classes/PhysicsBody2D.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the gravity vector computed from all sources that can affect the "
"body, including all gravity overrides from [Area2D] nodes and the global "
"world gravity."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o vetor de gravidade calculado a partir de todas as fontes que podem "
"afetar o corpo, incluindo todas as substituições de gravidade de nós "
"[Area2D] e a gravidade do mundo global."

#: doc/classes/PhysicsBody2D.xml
msgid ""
"Moves the body along the vector [param motion]. In order to be frame rate "
"independent in [method Node._physics_process] or [method Node._process], "
"[param motion] should be computed using [code]delta[/code].\n"
"Returns a [KinematicCollision2D], which contains information about the "
"collision when stopped, or when touching another body along the motion.\n"
"If [param test_only] is [code]true[/code], the body does not move but the "
"would-be collision information is given.\n"
"[param safe_margin] is the extra margin used for collision recovery (see "
"[member CharacterBody2D.safe_margin] for more details).\n"
"If [param recovery_as_collision] is [code]true[/code], any depenetration "
"from the recovery phase is also reported as a collision; this is used e.g. "
"by [CharacterBody2D] for improving floor detection during floor snapping."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/PhysicsBody2D.xml doc/classes/PhysicsBody3D.xml
#: doc/classes/SoftBody3D.xml
msgid ""
"Removes a body from the list of bodies that this body can't collide with."
msgstr ""
"Remove um corpo da lista de corpos com os quais este corpo não pode colidir."

#: doc/classes/PhysicsBody2D.xml
msgid ""
"Checks for collisions without moving the body. In order to be frame rate "
"independent in [method Node._physics_process] or [method Node._process], "
"[param motion] should be computed using [code]delta[/code].\n"
"Virtually sets the node's position, scale and rotation to that of the given "
"[Transform2D], then tries to move the body along the vector [param motion]. "
"Returns [code]true[/code] if a collision would stop the body from moving "
"along the whole path.\n"
"[param collision] is an optional object of type [KinematicCollision2D], "
"which contains additional information about the collision when stopped, or "
"when touching another body along the motion.\n"
"[param safe_margin] is the extra margin used for collision recovery (see "
"[member CharacterBody2D.safe_margin] for more details).\n"
"If [param recovery_as_collision] is [code]true[/code], any depenetration "
"from the recovery phase is also reported as a collision; this is useful for "
"checking whether the body would [i]touch[/i] any other bodies."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/PhysicsBody3D.xml
msgid "Abstract base class for 3D game objects affected by physics."
msgstr "Classe base abstrata para objetos de jogo 3D afetados por física."

#: doc/classes/PhysicsBody3D.xml
msgid ""
"[PhysicsBody3D] is an abstract base class for 3D game objects affected by "
"physics. All 3D physics bodies inherit from it.\n"
"[b]Warning:[/b] With a non-uniform scale, this node will likely not behave "
"as expected. It is advised to keep its scale the same on all axes and adjust "
"its collision shape(s) instead."
msgstr ""
"[PhysicsBody3D] é uma classe base abstrata para objetos de jogo 3D afetados "
"pela física. Todos os corpos físicos 3D herdam dela.\n"
"[b]Aviso:[/b] Com uma escala não uniforme, este nó provavelmente não se "
"comportará conforme o esperado. É aconselhável manter sua escala igual em "
"todos os eixos e ajustar sua(s) forma(s) de colisão em vez disso."

#: doc/classes/PhysicsBody3D.xml
msgid ""
"Returns [code]true[/code] if the specified linear or rotational [param axis] "
"is locked."
msgstr ""
"Retorna [code]true[/code] se o [param axis] linear ou rotacional "
"especificado estiver bloqueado."

#: doc/classes/PhysicsBody3D.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the gravity vector computed from all sources that can affect the "
"body, including all gravity overrides from [Area3D] nodes and the global "
"world gravity."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o vetor de gravidade calculado a partir de todas as fontes que podem "
"afetar o corpo, incluindo todas as substituições de gravidade de nós "
"[Area3D] e a gravidade do mundo global."

#: doc/classes/PhysicsBody3D.xml
msgid ""
"Moves the body along the vector [param motion]. In order to be frame rate "
"independent in [method Node._physics_process] or [method Node._process], "
"[param motion] should be computed using [code]delta[/code].\n"
"The body will stop if it collides. Returns a [KinematicCollision3D], which "
"contains information about the collision when stopped, or when touching "
"another body along the motion.\n"
"If [param test_only] is [code]true[/code], the body does not move but the "
"would-be collision information is given.\n"
"[param safe_margin] is the extra margin used for collision recovery (see "
"[member CharacterBody3D.safe_margin] for more details).\n"
"If [param recovery_as_collision] is [code]true[/code], any depenetration "
"from the recovery phase is also reported as a collision; this is used e.g. "
"by [CharacterBody3D] for improving floor detection during floor snapping.\n"
"[param max_collisions] allows to retrieve more than one collision result."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/PhysicsBody3D.xml
msgid ""
"Locks or unlocks the specified linear or rotational [param axis] depending "
"on the value of [param lock]."
msgstr ""
"Bloqueia ou desbloqueia o [param axis] linear ou rotacional especificado "
"dependendo do valor de [param lock]."

#: doc/classes/PhysicsBody3D.xml
msgid ""
"Checks for collisions without moving the body. In order to be frame rate "
"independent in [method Node._physics_process] or [method Node._process], "
"[param motion] should be computed using [code]delta[/code].\n"
"Virtually sets the node's position, scale and rotation to that of the given "
"[Transform3D], then tries to move the body along the vector [param motion]. "
"Returns [code]true[/code] if a collision would stop the body from moving "
"along the whole path.\n"
"[param collision] is an optional object of type [KinematicCollision3D], "
"which contains additional information about the collision when stopped, or "
"when touching another body along the motion.\n"
"[param safe_margin] is the extra margin used for collision recovery (see "
"[member CharacterBody3D.safe_margin] for more details).\n"
"If [param recovery_as_collision] is [code]true[/code], any depenetration "
"from the recovery phase is also reported as a collision; this is useful for "
"checking whether the body would [i]touch[/i] any other bodies.\n"
"[param max_collisions] allows to retrieve more than one collision result."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/PhysicsBody3D.xml
msgid "Lock the body's rotation in the X axis."
msgstr "Trava a rotação do corpo no eixo X."

#: doc/classes/PhysicsBody3D.xml
msgid "Lock the body's rotation in the Y axis."
msgstr "Trava a rotação do corpo no eixo Y."

#: doc/classes/PhysicsBody3D.xml
msgid "Lock the body's rotation in the Z axis."
msgstr "Trava a rotação do corpo no eixo Z."

#: doc/classes/PhysicsBody3D.xml
msgid "Lock the body's linear movement in the X axis."
msgstr "Trava o movimento linear do corpo no eixo X."

#: doc/classes/PhysicsBody3D.xml
msgid "Lock the body's linear movement in the Y axis."
msgstr "Trava o movimento linear do corpo no eixo Y."

#: doc/classes/PhysicsBody3D.xml
msgid "Lock the body's linear movement in the Z axis."
msgstr "Trava o movimento linear do corpo no eixo Z."

#: doc/classes/PhysicsDirectBodyState2D.xml
msgid "Provides direct access to a physics body in the [PhysicsServer2D]."
msgstr "Fornece acesso direto a um corpo de física no [PhysicsServer2D]."

#: doc/classes/PhysicsDirectBodyState2D.xml
msgid ""
"Provides direct access to a physics body in the [PhysicsServer2D], allowing "
"safe changes to physics properties. This object is passed via the direct "
"state callback of [RigidBody2D], and is intended for changing the direct "
"state of that body. See [method RigidBody2D._integrate_forces]."
msgstr ""
"Fornece acesso direto a um corpo físico no [PhysicsServer2D], permitindo "
"alterações seguras nas propriedades de física. Este objeto é passado por "
"meio do retorno de chamada de estado direto de [RigidBody2D] e destina-se a "
"alterar o estado direto desse corpo. Veja [method "
"RigidBody2D._integrate_forces]."

#: doc/classes/PhysicsDirectBodyState2D.xml
#: doc/classes/PhysicsDirectBodyState3D.xml
#: doc/classes/PhysicsDirectSpaceState2D.xml
#: doc/classes/PhysicsDirectSpaceState3D.xml doc/classes/RayCast2D.xml
#: doc/classes/RayCast3D.xml doc/classes/World2D.xml doc/classes/World3D.xml
msgid "Ray-casting"
msgstr "Ray-casting"

#: doc/classes/PhysicsDirectBodyState2D.xml doc/classes/RigidBody2D.xml
msgid ""
"Adds a constant directional force without affecting rotation that keeps "
"being applied over time until cleared with [code]constant_force = Vector2(0, "
"0)[/code].\n"
"This is equivalent to using [method add_constant_force] at the body's center "
"of mass."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/PhysicsDirectBodyState2D.xml doc/classes/RigidBody2D.xml
msgid ""
"Adds a constant positioned force to the body that keeps being applied over "
"time until cleared with [code]constant_force = Vector2(0, 0)[/code].\n"
"[param position] is the offset from the body origin in global coordinates."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/PhysicsDirectBodyState2D.xml doc/classes/RigidBody2D.xml
msgid ""
"Adds a constant rotational force without affecting position that keeps being "
"applied over time until cleared with [code]constant_torque = 0[/code]."
msgstr ""
"Adiciona uma força rotacional constante sem afetar a posição que continua "
"sendo aplicada ao longo do tempo até ser limpa com [code]constant_torque = "
"0[/code]."

#: doc/classes/PhysicsDirectBodyState2D.xml
#: doc/classes/PhysicsDirectBodyState3D.xml doc/classes/RigidBody2D.xml
#: doc/classes/RigidBody3D.xml
msgid ""
"Applies a directional force without affecting rotation. A force is time "
"dependent and meant to be applied every physics update.\n"
"This is equivalent to using [method apply_force] at the body's center of "
"mass."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/PhysicsDirectBodyState2D.xml
#: doc/classes/PhysicsDirectBodyState3D.xml doc/classes/RigidBody2D.xml
#: doc/classes/RigidBody3D.xml
msgid ""
"Applies a directional impulse without affecting rotation.\n"
"An impulse is time-independent! Applying an impulse every frame would result "
"in a framerate-dependent force. For this reason, it should only be used when "
"simulating one-time impacts (use the \"_force\" functions otherwise).\n"
"This is equivalent to using [method apply_impulse] at the body's center of "
"mass."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/PhysicsDirectBodyState2D.xml
#: doc/classes/PhysicsDirectBodyState3D.xml doc/classes/PhysicsServer3D.xml
#: doc/classes/RigidBody2D.xml doc/classes/RigidBody3D.xml
msgid ""
"Applies a positioned force to the body. A force is time dependent and meant "
"to be applied every physics update.\n"
"[param position] is the offset from the body origin in global coordinates."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/PhysicsDirectBodyState2D.xml
#: doc/classes/PhysicsDirectBodyState3D.xml doc/classes/PhysicsServer3D.xml
#: doc/classes/RigidBody2D.xml doc/classes/RigidBody3D.xml
msgid ""
"Applies a positioned impulse to the body.\n"
"An impulse is time-independent! Applying an impulse every frame would result "
"in a framerate-dependent force. For this reason, it should only be used when "
"simulating one-time impacts (use the \"_force\" functions otherwise).\n"
"[param position] is the offset from the body origin in global coordinates."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/PhysicsDirectBodyState2D.xml
msgid ""
"Applies a rotational force without affecting position. A force is time "
"dependent and meant to be applied every physics update.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] [member inverse_inertia] is required for this to work. To have "
"[member inverse_inertia], an active [CollisionShape2D] must be a child of "
"the node, or you can manually set [member inverse_inertia]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/PhysicsDirectBodyState2D.xml
msgid ""
"Applies a rotational impulse to the body without affecting the position.\n"
"An impulse is time-independent! Applying an impulse every frame would result "
"in a framerate-dependent force. For this reason, it should only be used when "
"simulating one-time impacts (use the \"_force\" functions otherwise).\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] [member inverse_inertia] is required for this to work. To have "
"[member inverse_inertia], an active [CollisionShape2D] must be a child of "
"the node, or you can manually set [member inverse_inertia]."
