#: doc/classes/Variant.xml
msgid "The most important data type in Godot."
msgstr "O tipo de dado mais importante no Godot."

#: doc/classes/Variant.xml
msgid ""
"In computer programming, a Variant class is a class that is designed to "
"store a variety of other types. Dynamic programming languages like PHP, Lua, "
"JavaScript and GDScript like to use them to store variables' data on the "
"backend. With these Variants, properties are able to change value types "
"freely.\n"
"[codeblocks]\n"
"[gdscript]\n"
"var foo = 2 # foo is dynamically an integer\n"
"foo = \"Now foo is a string!\"\n"
"foo = RefCounted.new() # foo is an Object\n"
"var bar: int = 2 # bar is a statically typed integer.\n"
"# bar = \"Uh oh! I can't make statically typed variables become a different "
"type!\"\n"
"[/gdscript]\n"
"[csharp]\n"
"// C# is statically typed. Once a variable has a type it cannot be changed. "
"You can use the `var` keyword to let the compiler infer the type "
"automatically.\n"
"var foo = 2; // Foo is a 32-bit integer (int). Be cautious, integers in "
"GDScript are 64-bit and the direct C# equivalent is `long`.\n"
"// foo = \"foo was and will always be an integer. It cannot be turned into a "
"string!\";\n"
"var boo = \"Boo is a string!\";\n"
"var ref = new RefCounted(); // var is especially useful when used together "
"with a constructor.\n"
"\n"
"// Godot also provides a Variant type that works like a union of all the "
"Variant-compatible types.\n"
"Variant fooVar = 2; // fooVar is dynamically an integer (stored as a `long` "
"in the Variant type).\n"
"fooVar = \"Now fooVar is a string!\";\n"
"fooVar = new RefCounted(); // fooVar is a GodotObject.\n"
"[/csharp]\n"
"[/codeblocks]\n"
"Godot tracks all scripting API variables within Variants. Without even "
"realizing it, you use Variants all the time. When a particular language "
"enforces its own rules for keeping data typed, then that language is "
"applying its own custom logic over the base Variant scripting API.\n"
"- GDScript automatically wrap values in them. It keeps all data in plain "
"Variants by default and then optionally enforces custom static typing rules "
"on variable types.\n"
"- C# is statically typed, but uses its own implementation of the Variant "
"type in place of Godot's [Variant] class when it needs to represent a "
"dynamic value. C# Variant can be assigned any compatible type implicitly but "
"converting requires an explicit cast.\n"
"The global [method @GlobalScope.typeof] function returns the enumerated "
"value of the Variant type stored in the current variable (see [enum "
"Variant.Type]).\n"
"[codeblocks]\n"
"[gdscript]\n"
"var foo = 2\n"
"match typeof(foo):\n"
"\tTYPE_NIL:\n"
"\t\tprint(\"foo is null\")\n"
"\tTYPE_INT:\n"
"\t\tprint(\"foo is an integer\")\n"
"\tTYPE_OBJECT:\n"
"\t\t# Note that Objects are their own special category.\n"
"\t\t# To get the name of the underlying Object type, you need the "
"`get_class()` method.\n"
"\t\tprint(\"foo is a(n) %s\" % foo.get_class()) # inject the class name into "
"a formatted string.\n"
"\t\t# Note that this does not get the script's `class_name` global "
"identifier.\n"
"\t\t# If the `class_name` is needed, use "
"`foo.get_script().get_global_name()` instead.\n"
"[/gdscript]\n"
"[csharp]\n"
"Variant foo = 2;\n"
"switch (foo.VariantType)\n"
"{\n"
"\tcase Variant.Type.Nil:\n"
"\t\tGD.Print(\"foo is null\");\n"
"\t\tbreak;\n"
"\tcase Variant.Type.Int:\n"
"\t\tGD.Print(\"foo is an integer\");\n"
"\t\tbreak;\n"
"\tcase Variant.Type.Object:\n"
"\t\t// Note that Objects are their own special category.\n"
"\t\t// You can convert a Variant to a GodotObject and use reflection to get "
"its name.\n"
"\t\tGD.Print($\"foo is a(n) {foo.AsGodotObject().GetType().Name}\");\n"
"\t\tbreak;\n"
"}\n"
"[/csharp]\n"
"[/codeblocks]\n"
"A Variant takes up only 20 bytes and can store almost any engine datatype "
"inside of it. Variants are rarely used to hold information for long periods "
"of time. Instead, they are used mainly for communication, editing, "
"serialization and moving data around.\n"
"Godot has specifically invested in making its Variant class as flexible as "
"possible; so much so that it is used for a multitude of operations to "
"facilitate communication between all of Godot's systems.\n"
"A Variant:\n"
"- Can store almost any datatype.\n"
"- Can perform operations between many variants. GDScript uses Variant as its "
"atomic/native datatype.\n"
"- Can be hashed, so it can be compared quickly to other variants.\n"
"- Can be used to convert safely between datatypes.\n"
"- Can be used to abstract calling methods and their arguments. Godot exports "
"all its functions through variants.\n"
"- Can be used to defer calls or move data between threads.\n"
"- Can be serialized as binary and stored to disk, or transferred via "
"network.\n"
"- Can be serialized to text and use it for printing values and editable "
"settings.\n"
"- Can work as an exported property, so the editor can edit it universally.\n"
"- Can be used for dictionaries, arrays, parsers, etc.\n"
"[b]Containers (Array and Dictionary):[/b] Both are implemented using "
"variants. A [Dictionary] can match any datatype used as key to any other "
"datatype. An [Array] just holds an array of Variants. Of course, a Variant "
"can also hold a [Dictionary] and an [Array] inside, making it even more "
"flexible.\n"
"Modifications to a container will modify all references to it. A [Mutex] "
"should be created to lock it if multi-threaded access is desired."
msgstr ""
"Em programação, uma classe Variant é uma classe projetada para armazenar uma "
"variedade de outros tipos. Linguagens de programação dinâmicas como PHP, "
"Lua, JavaScript e GDScript utilizam-nas para armazenar dados de variáveis no "
"backend. Com essas Variants, as propriedades podem alterar os tipos de "
"valores livremente.\n"
"[codeblocks]\n"
"[gdscript]\n"
"var foo = 2 # foo é dinamicamente um inteiro\n"
"foo = \"Agora foo é uma string!\"\n"
"foo = RefCounted.new() # foo é um Objeto\n"
"var bar: int = 2 # bar é um inteiro estaticamente tipado.\n"
"# bar = \"Oh não! Não posso fazer variáveis estaticamente tipadas mudarem de "
"tipo!\"\n"
"[/gdscript]\n"
"[csharp]\n"
"// C# é estaticamente tipado. Uma vez que uma variável possui um tipo, ele "
"não pode ser alterado. Você pode usar a palavra-chave `var` para deixar o "
"compilador inferir o tipo automaticamente.\n"
"var foo = 2; // Foo é um inteiro de 32 bits (int). Seja cauteloso, inteiros "
"em GDScript são de 64 bits e o equivalente direto em C# é `long`.\n"
"// foo = \"foo era e sempre será um inteiro. Ele não pode ser transformado "
"em uma string!\";\n"
"var boo = \"Boo é uma string!\";\n"
"var ref = new RefCounted(); // var é especialmente útil quando usado junto "
"com um construtor.\n"
"\n"
"// Godot também fornece um tipo Variant que funciona como uma união de todos "
"os tipos compatíveis com Variant.\n"
"Variant fooVar = 2; // fooVar é dinamicamente um inteiro (armazenado como um "
"`long` no tipo Variant).\n"
"fooVar = \"Agora fooVar é uma string!\";\n"
"fooVar = new RefCounted(); // fooVar é um GodotObject.\n"
"[/csharp]\n"
"[/codeblocks]\n"
"O Godot rastreia todas as variáveis da API de script dentro de Variants. Sem "
"nem perceber, você usa Variants o tempo todo. Quando uma linguagem "
"específica impõe suas próprias regras para manter os dados tipados, essa "
"linguagem está aplicando sua própria lógica personalizada sobre a API de "
"script base Variant.\n"
"- GDScript envolve valores automaticamente nelas. Ele mantém todos os dados "
"em Variants simples por padrão e, opcionalmente, impõe regras de tipagem "
"estática personalizadas nos tipos de variáveis.\n"
"- C# é estaticamente tipado, mas usa sua própria implementação do tipo "
"Variant no lugar da classe [Variant] do Godot quando precisa representar um "
"valor dinâmico. O Variant em C# pode ser atribuído a qualquer tipo "
"compatível implicitamente, mas a conversão requer uma conversão explícita "
"(cast).\n"
"A função global [method @GlobalScope.typeof] retorna o valor enumerado do "
"tipo Variant armazenado na variável atual (veja [enum Variant.Type]).\n"
"[codeblocks]\n"
"[gdscript]\n"
"var foo = 2\n"
"match typeof(foo):\n"
"\tTYPE_NIL:\n"
"\t\tprint(\"foo é nulo\")\n"
"\tTYPE_INT:\n"
"\t\tprint(\"foo é um inteiro\")\n"
"\tTYPE_OBJECT:\n"
"\t\t# Note que Objetos são sua própria categoria especial.\n"
"\t\t# Para obter o nome do tipo de Objeto subjacente, você precisa do método "
"`get_class()`.\n"
"\t\tprint(\"foo é um(a) %s\" % foo.get_class()) # injeta o nome da classe em "
"uma string formatada.\n"
"\t\t# Note que isso não obtém o identificador global `class_name` do "
"script.\n"
"\t\t# Se o `class_name` for necessário, use "
"`foo.get_script().get_global_name()` em vez disso.\n"
"[/gdscript]\n"
"[csharp]\n"
"Variant foo = 2;\n"
"switch (foo.VariantType)\n"
"{\n"
"\tcase Variant.Type.Nil:\n"
"\t\tGD.Print(\"foo é nulo\");\n"
"\t\tbreak;\n"
"\tcase Variant.Type.Int:\n"
"\t\tGD.Print(\"foo é um inteiro\");\n"
"\t\tbreak;\n"
"\tcase Variant.Type.Object:\n"
"\t\t// Note que Objetos são sua própria categoria especial.\n"
"\t\t// Você pode converter um Variant para um GodotObject e usar reflexão "
"para obter seu nome.\n"
"\t\tGD.Print($\"foo é um(a) {foo.AsGodotObject().GetType().Name}\");\n"
"\t\tbreak;\n"
"}\n"
"[/csharp]\n"
"[/codeblocks]\n"
"Um Variant ocupa apenas 20 bytes e pode armazenar quase qualquer tipo de "
"dado da engine dentro dele. Variants raramente são usados para manter "
"informações por longos períodos de tempo. Em vez disso, são usados "
"principalmente para comunicação, edição, serialização e movimentação de "
"dados.\n"
"O Godot investiu especificamente em tornar sua classe Variant o mais "
"flexível possível; tanto que é usada para uma infinidade de operações para "
"facilitar a comunicação entre todos os sistemas do Godot.\n"
"Um Variant:\n"
"- Pode armazenar quase qualquer tipo de dado.\n"
"- Pode realizar operações entre muitos variants. GDScript usa Variant como "
"seu tipo de dado atômico/nativo.\n"
"- Pode ser hashed (gerar hash), para que possa ser comparado rapidamente com "
"outros variants.\n"
"- Pode ser usado para converter com segurança entre tipos de dados.\n"
"- Pode ser usado para abstrair chamadas de métodos e seus argumentos. O "
"Godot exporta todas as suas funções através de variants.\n"
"- Pode ser usado para adiar chamadas ou mover dados entre threads.\n"
"- Pode ser serializado como binário e armazenado em disco, ou transferido "
"via rede.\n"
"- Pode ser serializado para texto e usado para imprimir valores e "
"configurações editáveis.\n"
"- Pode funcionar como uma propriedade exportada, para que o editor possa "
"editá-la universalmente.\n"
"- Pode ser usado para dicionários, arrays, parsers, etc.\n"
"[b]Containers (Array e Dictionary):[/b] Ambos são implementados usando "
"variants. Um [Dictionary] pode combinar qualquer tipo de dado usado como "
"chave para qualquer outro tipo de dado. Um [Array] apenas contém uma matriz "
"de Variants. Claro, um Variant também pode conter um [Dictionary] e um "
"[Array] dentro dele, tornando-o ainda mais flexível.\n"
"Modificações em um container modificarão todas as referências a ele. Um "
"[Mutex] deve ser criado para travá-lo se for desejado acesso multi-thread."

#: doc/classes/Variant.xml
msgid "Variant class introduction"
msgstr "Introdução à classe Variant"

#: doc/classes/VBoxContainer.xml
msgid "A container that arranges its child controls vertically."
msgstr "Um contêiner que organiza seus controles filhos verticalmente."

#: doc/classes/VBoxContainer.xml
msgid ""
"A variant of [BoxContainer] that can only arrange its child controls "
"vertically. Child controls are rearranged automatically when their minimum "
"size changes."
msgstr ""
"Uma variante de [BoxContainer] que só pode organizar seus controles filhos "
"verticalmente. Os controles filhos são reorganizados automaticamente quando "
"seu tamanho mínimo muda."

#: doc/classes/Vector2.xml
msgid "A 2D vector using floating-point coordinates."
msgstr "Um vetor 2D usando coordenadas de ponto flutuante."

#: doc/classes/Vector2.xml
msgid ""
"A 2-element structure that can be used to represent 2D coordinates or any "
"other pair of numeric values.\n"
"It uses floating-point coordinates. By default, these floating-point values "
"use 32-bit precision, unlike [float] which is always 64-bit. If double "
"precision is needed, compile the engine with the option "
"[code]precision=double[/code].\n"
"See [Vector2i] for its integer counterpart.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] In a boolean context, a Vector2 will evaluate to [code]false[/"
"code] if it's equal to [code]Vector2(0, 0)[/code]. Otherwise, a Vector2 will "
"always evaluate to [code]true[/code]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Vector2.xml doc/classes/Vector2i.xml doc/classes/Vector3.xml
#: doc/classes/Vector3i.xml
msgid "3Blue1Brown Essence of Linear Algebra"
msgstr "3Blue1Brown Essência da Álgebra Linear"

#: doc/classes/Vector2.xml
msgid ""
"Constructs a default-initialized [Vector2] with all components set to "
"[code]0[/code]."
msgstr ""
"Constrói um [Vector2] inicializado por padrão com todos os componentes "
"definidos como [code]0[/code]."

#: doc/classes/Vector2.xml
msgid "Constructs a [Vector2] as a copy of the given [Vector2]."
msgstr "Constrói um [Vector2] como uma cópia do [Vector2] fornecido."

#: doc/classes/Vector2.xml
msgid "Constructs a new [Vector2] from [Vector2i]."
msgstr "Constrói um novo [Vector2] a partir de [Vector2i]."

#: doc/classes/Vector2.xml
msgid "Constructs a new [Vector2] from the given [param x] and [param y]."
msgstr ""
"Constrói um novo [Vector2] a partir de [param x] e [param y] fornecidos."

#: doc/classes/Vector2.xml doc/classes/Vector2i.xml doc/classes/Vector3.xml
#: doc/classes/Vector3i.xml doc/classes/Vector4.xml doc/classes/Vector4i.xml
msgid ""
"Returns a new vector with all components in absolute values (i.e. positive)."
msgstr ""
"Retorna um novo vetor com todos os componentes em valores absolutos (ou "
"seja, positivos)."

#: doc/classes/Vector2.xml
msgid ""
"Returns this vector's angle with respect to the positive X axis, or [code]"
"(1, 0)[/code] vector, in radians.\n"
"For example, [code]Vector2.RIGHT.angle()[/code] will return zero, "
"[code]Vector2.DOWN.angle()[/code] will return [code]PI / 2[/code] (a quarter "
"turn, or 90 degrees), and [code]Vector2(1, -1).angle()[/code] will return "
"[code]-PI / 4[/code] (a negative eighth turn, or -45 degrees).\n"
"This is equivalent to calling [method @GlobalScope.atan2] with [member y] "
"and [member x].\n"
"[url=https://raw.githubusercontent.com/godotengine/godot-docs/master/img/"
"vector2_angle.png]Illustration of the returned angle.[/url]"
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Vector2.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the signed angle to the given vector, in radians. The result ranges "
"from [code]-PI[/code] to [code]PI[/code] (inclusive).\n"
"[url=https://raw.githubusercontent.com/godotengine/godot-docs/master/img/"
"vector2_angle_to.png]Illustration of the returned angle.[/url]"
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Vector2.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the signed angle between the X axis and the line from this vector to "
"point [param to], in radians. The result ranges from [code]-PI[/code] to "
"[code]PI[/code] (inclusive).\n"
"[code]a.angle_to_point(b)[/code] is equivalent to [code](b - a).angle()[/"
"code]. See also [method angle].\n"
"[url=https://raw.githubusercontent.com/godotengine/godot-docs/master/img/"
"vector2_angle_to_point.png]Illustration of the returned angle.[/url]"
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Vector2.xml
msgid ""
"Returns this vector's aspect ratio, which is [member x] divided by [member "
"y]."
msgstr ""
"Retorna a proporção de aspecto deste vetor, que é [member x] dividido por "
"[member y]."

#: doc/classes/Vector2.xml doc/classes/Vector3.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the derivative at the given [param t] on the [url=https://"
"en.wikipedia.org/wiki/B%C3%A9zier_curve]Bézier curve[/url] defined by this "
"vector and the given [param control_1], [param control_2], and [param end] "
"points."
msgstr ""
"Retorna a derivada no [param t] fornecido na [url=https://en.wikipedia.org/"
"wiki/B%C3%A9zier_curve]curva de Bézier[/url] definida por este vetor e pelos "
"pontos [param control_1], [param control_2] e [param end] fornecidos."

#: doc/classes/Vector2.xml doc/classes/Vector3.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the point at the given [param t] on the [url=https://"
"en.wikipedia.org/wiki/B%C3%A9zier_curve]Bézier curve[/url] defined by this "
"vector and the given [param control_1], [param control_2], and [param end] "
"points."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o ponto no [param t] fornecido na [url=https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/"
"B%C3%A9zier_curve]curva de Bézier[/url] definida por este vetor e pelos "
"pontos [param control_1], [param control_2] e [param end] fornecidos."

#: doc/classes/Vector2.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the vector \"bounced off\" from a line defined by the given normal "
"[param n] perpendicular to the line.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] [method bounce] performs the operation that most engines and "
"frameworks call [code skip-lint]reflect()[/code]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Vector2.xml doc/classes/Vector3.xml doc/classes/Vector4.xml
msgid ""
"Returns a new vector with all components rounded up (towards positive "
"infinity)."
msgstr ""
"Retorna um novo vetor com todos os componentes arredondados para cima (rumo "
"ao infinito positivo)."

#: doc/classes/Vector2.xml doc/classes/Vector2i.xml doc/classes/Vector3.xml
#: doc/classes/Vector3i.xml doc/classes/Vector4.xml doc/classes/Vector4i.xml
msgid ""
"Returns a new vector with all components clamped between the components of "
"[param min] and [param max], by running [method @GlobalScope.clamp] on each "
"component."
msgstr ""
"Retorna um novo vetor com todos os componentes limitados entre os "
"componentes de [param min] e [param max], executando [method "
"@GlobalScope.clamp] em cada componente."

#: doc/classes/Vector2.xml doc/classes/Vector2i.xml doc/classes/Vector3.xml
#: doc/classes/Vector3i.xml doc/classes/Vector4.xml doc/classes/Vector4i.xml
msgid ""
"Returns a new vector with all components clamped between [param min] and "
"[param max], by running [method @GlobalScope.clamp] on each component."
msgstr ""
"Retorna um novo vetor com todos os componentes limitados (clamped) entre "
"[param min] e [param max], executando [method @GlobalScope.clamp] em cada "
"componente."

#: doc/classes/Vector2.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the 2D analog of the cross product for this vector and [param "
"with].\n"
"This is the signed area of the parallelogram formed by the two vectors. If "
"the second vector is clockwise from the first vector, then the cross product "
"is the positive area. If counter-clockwise, the cross product is the "
"negative area. If the two vectors are parallel this returns zero, making it "
"useful for testing if two vectors are parallel.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Cross product is not defined in 2D mathematically. This method "
"embeds the 2D vectors in the XY plane of 3D space and uses their cross "
"product's Z component as the analog."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Vector2.xml doc/classes/Vector3.xml doc/classes/Vector4.xml
msgid ""
"Performs a cubic interpolation between this vector and [param b] using "
"[param pre_a] and [param post_b] as handles, and returns the result at "
"position [param weight]. [param weight] is on the range of 0.0 to 1.0, "
"representing the amount of interpolation."
msgstr ""
"Executa uma interpolação cúbica entre este vetor e [param b] usando [param "
"pre_a] e [param post_b] como alças, e retorna o resultado na posição [param "
"weight]. [param weight] está no intervalo de 0,0 a 1,0, representando a "
"quantidade de interpolação."

#: doc/classes/Vector2.xml doc/classes/Vector3.xml doc/classes/Vector4.xml
msgid ""
"Performs a cubic interpolation between this vector and [param b] using "
"[param pre_a] and [param post_b] as handles, and returns the result at "
"position [param weight]. [param weight] is on the range of 0.0 to 1.0, "
"representing the amount of interpolation.\n"
"It can perform smoother interpolation than [method cubic_interpolate] by the "
"time values."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Vector2.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the normalized vector pointing from this vector to [param to].\n"
"[code]a.direction_to(b)[/code] is equivalent to [code](b - a).normalized()[/"
"code]. See also [method normalized]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Vector2.xml doc/classes/Vector2i.xml doc/classes/Vector3.xml
#: doc/classes/Vector3i.xml doc/classes/Vector4.xml doc/classes/Vector4i.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the squared [url=https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/"
"Euclidean_distance]Euclidean distance[/url] between this vector and [param "
"to].\n"
"This method runs faster than [method distance_to], so prefer it if you need "
"to compare vectors or need the squared distance for some formula."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Vector2.xml doc/classes/Vector2i.xml doc/classes/Vector3.xml
#: doc/classes/Vector3i.xml doc/classes/Vector4.xml doc/classes/Vector4i.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the [url=https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Euclidean_distance]Euclidean "
"distance[/url] between this vector and [param to]."
msgstr ""
"Retorna a [url=https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Euclidean_distance]distância "
"euclidiana[/url] entre este vetor e [param to]."

#: doc/classes/Vector2.xml doc/classes/Vector3.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the dot product of this vector and [param with]. This can be used to "
"compare the angle between two vectors. For example, this can be used to "
"determine whether an enemy is facing the player.\n"
"The dot product will be [code]0[/code] for a right angle (90 degrees), "
"greater than 0 for angles narrower than 90 degrees and lower than 0 for "
"angles wider than 90 degrees.\n"
"When using unit (normalized) vectors, the result will always be between "
"[code]-1.0[/code] (180 degree angle) when the vectors are facing opposite "
"directions, and [code]1.0[/code] (0 degree angle) when the vectors are "
"aligned.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] [code]a.dot(b)[/code] is equivalent to [code]b.dot(a)[/code]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Vector2.xml doc/classes/Vector3.xml doc/classes/Vector4.xml
msgid ""
"Returns a new vector with all components rounded down (towards negative "
"infinity)."
msgstr ""
"Retorna um novo vetor com todos os componentes arredondados para baixo (em "
"direção ao infinito negativo)."

#: doc/classes/Vector2.xml
msgid ""
"Creates a [Vector2] rotated to the given [param angle] in radians. This is "
"equivalent to doing [code]Vector2(cos(angle), sin(angle))[/code] or "
"[code]Vector2.RIGHT.rotated(angle)[/code].\n"
"[codeblock]\n"
"print(Vector2.from_angle(0)) # Prints (1.0, 0.0)\n"
"print(Vector2(1, 0).angle()) # Prints 0.0, which is the angle used above.\n"
"print(Vector2.from_angle(PI / 2)) # Prints (0.0, 1.0)\n"
"[/codeblock]\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] The length of the returned [Vector2] is [i]approximately[/i] "
"[code]1.0[/code], but is is not guaranteed to be exactly [code]1.0[/code] "
"due to floating-point precision issues. Call [method normalized] on the "
"returned [Vector2] if you require a unit vector."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Vector2.xml doc/classes/Vector3.xml doc/classes/Vector4.xml
msgid ""
"Returns [code]true[/code] if this vector and [param to] are approximately "
"equal, by running [method @GlobalScope.is_equal_approx] on each component."
msgstr ""
"Retorna [code]true[/code] se este vetor e [param to] forem aproximadamente "
"iguais, executando [method @GlobalScope.is_equal_approx] em cada componente."

#: doc/classes/Vector2.xml doc/classes/Vector3.xml doc/classes/Vector4.xml
msgid ""
"Returns [code]true[/code] if this vector is finite, by calling [method "
"@GlobalScope.is_finite] on each component."
msgstr ""
"Retorna [code]true[/code] se este vetor for finito, chamando [method "
"@GlobalScope.is_finite] em cada componente."

#: doc/classes/Vector2.xml doc/classes/Vector3.xml doc/classes/Vector4.xml
msgid ""
"Returns [code]true[/code] if the vector is normalized, i.e. its length is "
"approximately equal to 1."
msgstr ""
"Retorna [code]true[/code] se o vetor estiver normalizado, ou seja, seu "
"comprimento for aproximadamente igual a 1."

#: doc/classes/Vector2.xml doc/classes/Vector3.xml doc/classes/Vector4.xml
msgid ""
"Returns [code]true[/code] if this vector's values are approximately zero, by "
"running [method @GlobalScope.is_zero_approx] on each component.\n"
"This method is faster than using [method is_equal_approx] with one value as "
"a zero vector."
msgstr ""
"Retorna [code]true[/code] se os valores deste vetor forem aproximadamente "
"zero, executando [method @GlobalScope.is_zero_approx] em cada componente.\n"
"Este método é mais rápido do que usar [method is_equal_approx] com um dos "
"valores sendo um vetor zero."

#: doc/classes/Vector2.xml doc/classes/Vector2i.xml doc/classes/Vector3.xml
#: doc/classes/Vector3i.xml doc/classes/Vector4.xml doc/classes/Vector4i.xml
msgid "Returns the length (magnitude) of this vector."
msgstr "Retorna o comprimento (magnitude) deste vetor."

#: doc/classes/Vector2.xml doc/classes/Vector2i.xml doc/classes/Vector3.xml
#: doc/classes/Vector3i.xml doc/classes/Vector4.xml doc/classes/Vector4i.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the squared length (squared magnitude) of this vector.\n"
"This method runs faster than [method length], so prefer it if you need to "
"compare vectors or need the squared distance for some formula."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Vector2.xml doc/classes/Vector3.xml doc/classes/Vector4.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the result of the linear interpolation between this vector and "
"[param to] by amount [param weight]. [param weight] is on the range of "
"[code]0.0[/code] to [code]1.0[/code], representing the amount of "
"interpolation."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o resultado da interpolação linear entre este vetor e [param to] "
"pela quantidade [param weight]. [param weight] está no intervalo de "
"[code]0.0[/code] a [code]1.0[/code], representando a quantidade de "
"interpolação."

#: doc/classes/Vector2.xml doc/classes/Vector3.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the vector with a maximum length by limiting its length to [param "
"length]. If the vector is non-finite, the result is undefined."
msgstr ""
"Retornar o vetor com comprimento máximo, limitando seu comprimento a [param "
"length]. Se o vetor for não finito, o resultado é indefinido."

#: doc/classes/Vector2.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the component-wise maximum of this and [param with], equivalent to "
"[code]Vector2(maxf(x, with.x), maxf(y, with.y))[/code]."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o máximo componente a componente disto e [param with], equivalente a "
"[code]Vector2(maxf(x, with.x), maxf(y, with.y))[/code]."

#: doc/classes/Vector2.xml doc/classes/Vector2i.xml doc/classes/Vector3.xml
#: doc/classes/Vector3i.xml doc/classes/Vector4.xml doc/classes/Vector4i.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the axis of the vector's highest value. See [code]AXIS_*[/code] "
"constants. If all components are equal, this method returns [constant "
"AXIS_X]."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o eixo do maior valor do vetor. Consulte as constantes [code]AXIS_*[/"
"code]. Se todos os componentes forem iguais, este método retorna [constant "
"AXIS_X]."

#: doc/classes/Vector2.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the component-wise maximum of this and [param with], equivalent to "
"[code]Vector2(maxf(x, with), maxf(y, with))[/code]."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o máximo componente a componente disto e [param with], equivalente a "
"[code]Vector2(maxf(x, with), maxf(y, with))[/code]."

#: doc/classes/Vector2.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the component-wise minimum of this and [param with], equivalent to "
"[code]Vector2(minf(x, with.x), minf(y, with.y))[/code]."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o mínimo componente a componente disto e [param with], equivalente a "
"[code]Vector2(minf(x, with.x), minf(y, with.y))[/code]."

#: doc/classes/Vector2.xml doc/classes/Vector2i.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the axis of the vector's lowest value. See [code]AXIS_*[/code] "
"constants. If all components are equal, this method returns [constant "
"AXIS_Y]."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o eixo do menor valor do vetor. Consulte as constantes [code]AXIS_*[/"
"code]. Se todos os componentes forem iguais, este método retorna [constant "
"AXIS_Y]."

#: doc/classes/Vector2.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the component-wise minimum of this and [param with], equivalent to "
"[code]Vector2(minf(x, with), minf(y, with))[/code]."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o mínimo componente a componente disto e [param with], equivalente a "
"[code]Vector2(minf(x, with), minf(y, with))[/code]."

#: doc/classes/Vector2.xml doc/classes/Vector3.xml
msgid ""
"Returns a new vector moved toward [param to] by the fixed [param delta] "
"amount. Will not go past the final value."
msgstr ""
"Retorna um novo vetor movido em direção a [param to] pela quantidade fixa "
"[param delta]. Não passará do valor final."

#: doc/classes/Vector2.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the result of scaling the vector to unit length. Equivalent to "
"[code]v / v.length()[/code]. Returns [code](0, 0)[/code] if [code]v.length() "
"== 0[/code]. See also [method is_normalized].\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] This function may return incorrect values if the input vector "
"length is near zero."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Vector2.xml
msgid ""
"Returns a perpendicular vector rotated 90 degrees counter-clockwise compared "
"to the original, with the same length."
msgstr ""
"Retorna um vetor perpendicular rotacionado 90 graus no sentido anti-horário "
"em comparação com o original, com o mesmo comprimento."

#: doc/classes/Vector2.xml doc/classes/Vector3.xml doc/classes/Vector4.xml
msgid ""
"Returns a vector composed of the [method @GlobalScope.fposmod] of this "
"vector's components and [param mod]."
msgstr ""
"Retorna um vetor composto pelo [method @GlobalScope.fposmod] dos componentes "
"deste vetor e [param mod]."

#: doc/classes/Vector2.xml doc/classes/Vector3.xml doc/classes/Vector4.xml
msgid ""
"Returns a vector composed of the [method @GlobalScope.fposmod] of this "
"vector's components and [param modv]'s components."
msgstr ""
"Retorna um vetor composto pelo [method @GlobalScope.fposmod] dos componentes "
"deste vetor e dos componentes de [param modv]."

#: doc/classes/Vector2.xml doc/classes/Vector3.xml
msgid ""
"Returns a new vector resulting from projecting this vector onto the given "
"vector [param b]. The resulting new vector is parallel to [param b]. See "
"also [method slide].\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] If the vector [param b] is a zero vector, the components of the "
"resulting new vector will be [constant @GDScript.NAN]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Vector2.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the result of reflecting the vector from a line defined by the given "
"direction vector [param line].\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] [method reflect] differs from what other engines and frameworks "
"call [code skip-lint]reflect()[/code]. In other engines, [code skip-"
"lint]reflect()[/code] takes a normal direction which is a direction "
"perpendicular to the line. In Godot, you specify the direction of the line "
"directly. See also [method bounce] which does what most engines call [code "
"skip-lint]reflect()[/code]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Vector2.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the result of rotating this vector by [param angle] (in radians). "
"See also [method @GlobalScope.deg_to_rad]."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o resultado de rotacionar este vetor por [param angle] (em "
"radianos). Veja também [method @GlobalScope.deg_to_rad]."

#: doc/classes/Vector2.xml doc/classes/Vector3.xml doc/classes/Vector4.xml
msgid ""
"Returns a new vector with all components rounded to the nearest integer, "
"with halfway cases rounded away from zero."
msgstr ""
"Retorna um novo vetor com todos os componentes arredondados para o inteiro "
"mais próximo, com casos intermediários arredondados para longe de zero."

#: doc/classes/Vector2.xml doc/classes/Vector3.xml doc/classes/Vector4.xml
msgid ""
"Returns a new vector with each component set to [code]1.0[/code] if it's "
"positive, [code]-1.0[/code] if it's negative, and [code]0.0[/code] if it's "
"zero. The result is identical to calling [method @GlobalScope.sign] on each "
"component."
msgstr ""
"Retorna um novo vetor com cada componente definido como [code]1.0[/code] se "
"for positivo, [code]-1.0[/code] se for negativo e [code]0.0[/code] se for "
"zero. O resultado é idêntico a chamar [method @GlobalScope.sign] em cada "
"componente."

#: doc/classes/Vector2.xml doc/classes/Vector3.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the result of spherical linear interpolation between this vector and "
"[param to], by amount [param weight]. [param weight] is on the range of 0.0 "
"to 1.0, representing the amount of interpolation.\n"
"This method also handles interpolating the lengths if the input vectors have "
"different lengths. For the special case of one or both input vectors having "
"zero length, this method behaves like [method lerp]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Vector2.xml
msgid ""
"Returns a new vector resulting from sliding this vector along a line with "
"normal [param n]. The resulting new vector is perpendicular to [param n], "
"and is equivalent to this vector minus its projection on [param n]. See also "
"[method project].\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] The vector [param n] must be normalized. See also [method "
"normalized]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Vector2.xml doc/classes/Vector3.xml doc/classes/Vector4.xml
msgid ""
"Returns a new vector with each component snapped to the nearest multiple of "
"the corresponding component in [param step]. This can also be used to round "
"the components to an arbitrary number of decimals."
msgstr ""
"Retorna um novo vetor com cada componente ajustado para o múltiplo mais "
"próximo do componente correspondente em [param step]. Isso também pode ser "
"usado para arredondar os componentes para um número arbitrário de decimais."

#: doc/classes/Vector2.xml doc/classes/Vector3.xml doc/classes/Vector4.xml
msgid ""
"Returns a new vector with each component snapped to the nearest multiple of "
"[param step]. This can also be used to round the components to an arbitrary "
"number of decimals."
msgstr ""
"Retorna um novo vetor com cada componente ajustado para o múltiplo mais "
"próximo de [param step]. Isso também pode ser usado para arredondar os "
"componentes para um número arbitrário de decimais."

#: doc/classes/Vector2.xml doc/classes/Vector2i.xml doc/classes/Vector3.xml
#: doc/classes/Vector3i.xml doc/classes/Vector4.xml doc/classes/Vector4i.xml
msgid ""
"The vector's X component. Also accessible by using the index position [code]"
"[0][/code]."
msgstr ""
"O componente X do vetor. Também acessível usando a posição de índice [code]"
"[0][/code]."

#: doc/classes/Vector2.xml doc/classes/Vector2i.xml doc/classes/Vector3.xml
#: doc/classes/Vector3i.xml doc/classes/Vector4.xml doc/classes/Vector4i.xml
msgid ""
"The vector's Y component. Also accessible by using the index position [code]"
"[1][/code]."
msgstr ""
"O componente Y do vetor. Também acessível usando a posição de índice [code]"
"[1][/code]."

#: doc/classes/Vector2.xml doc/classes/Vector2i.xml doc/classes/Vector3.xml
#: doc/classes/Vector3i.xml doc/classes/Vector4.xml doc/classes/Vector4i.xml
msgid ""
"Enumerated value for the X axis. Returned by [method max_axis_index] and "
"[method min_axis_index]."
msgstr ""
"Valor enumerado para o eixo X. Retornado por [method max_axis_index] e "
"[method min_axis_index]."

#: doc/classes/Vector2.xml doc/classes/Vector2i.xml doc/classes/Vector3.xml
#: doc/classes/Vector3i.xml doc/classes/Vector4.xml doc/classes/Vector4i.xml
msgid ""
"Enumerated value for the Y axis. Returned by [method max_axis_index] and "
"[method min_axis_index]."
msgstr ""
"Valor enumerado para o eixo Y. Retornado por [method max_axis_index] e "
"[method min_axis_index]."

#: doc/classes/Vector2.xml doc/classes/Vector2i.xml doc/classes/Vector3.xml
#: doc/classes/Vector3i.xml doc/classes/Vector4.xml doc/classes/Vector4i.xml
msgid "Zero vector, a vector with all components set to [code]0[/code]."
msgstr ""
"Vetor zero, um vetor com todos os componentes definidos como [code]0[/code]."

#: doc/classes/Vector2.xml doc/classes/Vector2i.xml doc/classes/Vector3.xml
#: doc/classes/Vector3i.xml doc/classes/Vector4.xml doc/classes/Vector4i.xml
msgid "One vector, a vector with all components set to [code]1[/code]."
msgstr ""
"Um vetor, um vetor com todos os componentes definidos como [code]1[/code]."

#: doc/classes/Vector2.xml doc/classes/Vector3.xml doc/classes/Vector4.xml
msgid ""
"Infinity vector, a vector with all components set to [constant "
"@GDScript.INF]."
msgstr ""
"Vetor de infinito, um vetor com todos os componentes definidos como "
"[constant @GDScript.INF]."

#: doc/classes/Vector2.xml doc/classes/Vector2i.xml
msgid "Left unit vector. Represents the direction of left."
msgstr "Vetor unitário esquerdo. Representa a direção da esquerda."

#: doc/classes/Vector2.xml doc/classes/Vector2i.xml
msgid "Right unit vector. Represents the direction of right."
msgstr "Vetor unitário direito. Representa a direção da direita."

#: doc/classes/Vector2.xml doc/classes/Vector2i.xml
msgid "Up unit vector. Y is down in 2D, so this vector points -Y."
msgstr ""
"Vetor unitário para cima. O Y é para baixo em 2D, então este vetor aponta "
"para -Y."

#: doc/classes/Vector2.xml doc/classes/Vector2i.xml
msgid "Down unit vector. Y is down in 2D, so this vector points +Y."
msgstr ""
"Vetor unitário para baixo. O Y é para baixo em 2D, então este vetor aponta "
"para +Y."

#: doc/classes/Vector2.xml doc/classes/Vector3.xml doc/classes/Vector4.xml
msgid ""
"Returns [code]true[/code] if the vectors are not equal.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Due to floating-point precision errors, consider using [method "
"is_equal_approx] instead, which is more reliable.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Vectors with [constant @GDScript.NAN] elements don't behave the "
"same as other vectors. Therefore, the results from this operator may not be "
"accurate if NaNs are included."
msgstr ""
"Retorna [code]true[/code] se os vetores não forem iguais.\n"
"[b]Nota:[/b] Devido a erros de precisão de ponto flutuante, considere usar "
"[method is_equal_approx], que é mais confiável.\n"
"[b]Nota:[/b] Vetores com elementos [constant @GDScript.NAN] não se comportam "
"da mesma forma que outros vetores. Portanto, os resultados deste operador "
"podem não ser precisos se contiverem valores NaN."

#: doc/classes/Vector2.xml
msgid ""
"Inversely transforms (multiplies) the [Vector2] by the given [Transform2D] "
"transformation matrix, under the assumption that the transformation basis is "
"orthonormal (i.e. rotation/reflection is fine, scaling/skew is not).\n"
"[code]vector * transform[/code] is equivalent to [code]transform.inverse() * "
"vector[/code]. See [method Transform2D.inverse].\n"
"For transforming by inverse of an affine transformation (e.g. with scaling) "
"[code]transform.affine_inverse() * vector[/code] can be used instead. See "
"[method Transform2D.affine_inverse]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Vector2.xml
msgid ""
"Multiplies each component of the [Vector2] by the components of the given "
"[Vector2].\n"
"[codeblock]\n"
"print(Vector2(10, 20) * Vector2(3, 4)) # Prints (30.0, 80.0)\n"
"[/codeblock]"
msgstr ""
"Multiplica cada componente do [Vector2] pelos componentes do [Vector2] "
"fornecido.\n"
"[codeblock]\n"
"print(Vector2(10, 20) * Vector2(3, 4)) # Imprime (30.0, 80.0)\n"
"[/codeblock]"

#: doc/classes/Vector2.xml
msgid "Multiplies each component of the [Vector2] by the given [float]."
msgstr "Multiplica cada componente do [Vector2] pelo [float] fornecido."

#: doc/classes/Vector2.xml
msgid "Multiplies each component of the [Vector2] by the given [int]."
msgstr "Multiplica cada componente do [Vector2] pelo [int] fornecido."

#: doc/classes/Vector2.xml
msgid ""
"Adds each component of the [Vector2] by the components of the given "
"[Vector2].\n"
"[codeblock]\n"
"print(Vector2(10, 20) + Vector2(3, 4)) # Prints (13.0, 24.0)\n"
"[/codeblock]"
msgstr ""
"Adiciona cada componente do [Vector2] aos componentes do [Vector2] "
"fornecido.\n"
"[codeblock]\n"
"print(Vector2(10, 20) + Vector2(3, 4)) # Imprime (13.0, 24.0)\n"
"[/codeblock]"

#: doc/classes/Vector2.xml
msgid ""
"Subtracts each component of the [Vector2] by the components of the given "
"[Vector2].\n"
"[codeblock]\n"
"print(Vector2(10, 20) - Vector2(3, 4)) # Prints (7.0, 16.0)\n"
"[/codeblock]"
msgstr ""
"Subtrai de cada componente do [Vector2] os componentes do [Vector2] "
"fornecido.\n"
"[codeblock]\n"
"print(Vector2(10, 20) - Vector2(3, 4)) # Imprime (7.0, 16.0)\n"
"[/codeblock]"

#: doc/classes/Vector2.xml
msgid ""
"Divides each component of the [Vector2] by the components of the given "
"[Vector2].\n"
"[codeblock]\n"
"print(Vector2(10, 20) / Vector2(2, 5)) # Prints (5.0, 4.0)\n"
"[/codeblock]"
msgstr ""
"Divide cada componente do [Vector2] pelos componentes do [Vector2] "
"fornecido.\n"
"[codeblock]\n"
"print(Vector2(10, 20) / Vector2(2, 5)) # Imprime (5.0, 4.0)\n"
"[/codeblock]"

#: doc/classes/Vector2.xml
msgid "Divides each component of the [Vector2] by the given [float]."
msgstr "Divide cada componente do [Vector2] pelo [float] fornecido."

#: doc/classes/Vector2.xml
msgid "Divides each component of the [Vector2] by the given [int]."
msgstr "Divide cada componente do [Vector2] pelo [int] fornecido."

#: doc/classes/Vector2.xml
msgid ""
"Compares two [Vector2] vectors by first checking if the X value of the left "
"vector is less than the X value of the [param right] vector. If the X values "
"are exactly equal, then it repeats this check with the Y values of the two "
"vectors. This operator is useful for sorting vectors.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Vectors with [constant @GDScript.NAN] elements don't behave the "
"same as other vectors. Therefore, the results from this operator may not be "
"accurate if NaNs are included."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Vector2.xml
msgid ""
"Compares two [Vector2] vectors by first checking if the X value of the left "
"vector is less than or equal to the X value of the [param right] vector. If "
"the X values are exactly equal, then it repeats this check with the Y values "
"of the two vectors. This operator is useful for sorting vectors.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Vectors with [constant @GDScript.NAN] elements don't behave the "
"same as other vectors. Therefore, the results from this operator may not be "
"accurate if NaNs are included."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Vector2.xml doc/classes/Vector3.xml doc/classes/Vector4.xml
msgid ""
"Returns [code]true[/code] if the vectors are exactly equal.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Due to floating-point precision errors, consider using [method "
"is_equal_approx] instead, which is more reliable.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Vectors with [constant @GDScript.NAN] elements don't behave the "
"same as other vectors. Therefore, the results from this operator may not be "
"accurate if NaNs are included."
msgstr ""
"Retorna [code]true[/code] se os vetores forem exatamente iguais.\n"
"[b]Nota:[/b] Devido a erros de precisão de ponto flutuante, considere usar "
"[method is_equal_approx], que é mais confiável.\n"
"[b]Nota:[/b] Vetores com elementos [constant @GDScript.NAN] não se comportam "
"da mesma forma que outros vetores. Portanto, os resultados deste operador "
"podem não ser precisos se contiverem valores NaN."

#: doc/classes/Vector2.xml
msgid ""
"Compares two [Vector2] vectors by first checking if the X value of the left "
"vector is greater than the X value of the [param right] vector. If the X "
"values are exactly equal, then it repeats this check with the Y values of "
"the two vectors. This operator is useful for sorting vectors.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Vectors with [constant @GDScript.NAN] elements don't behave the "
"same as other vectors. Therefore, the results from this operator may not be "
"accurate if NaNs are included."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Vector2.xml
msgid ""
"Compares two [Vector2] vectors by first checking if the X value of the left "
"vector is greater than or equal to the X value of the [param right] vector. "
"If the X values are exactly equal, then it repeats this check with the Y "
"values of the two vectors. This operator is useful for sorting vectors.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Vectors with [constant @GDScript.NAN] elements don't behave the "
"same as other vectors. Therefore, the results from this operator may not be "
"accurate if NaNs are included."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Vector2.xml doc/classes/Vector2i.xml
msgid ""
"Access vector components using their [param index]. [code]v[0][/code] is "
"equivalent to [code]v.x[/code], and [code]v[1][/code] is equivalent to "
"[code]v.y[/code]."
msgstr ""
"Acessa os componentes do vetor usando seu [param index]. [code]v[0][/code] é "
"equivalente a [code]v.x[/code] e [code]v[1][/code] é equivalente a "
"[code]v.y[/code]."

#: doc/classes/Vector2.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the negative value of the [Vector2]. This is the same as writing "
"[code]Vector2(-v.x, -v.y)[/code]. This operation flips the direction of the "
"vector while keeping the same magnitude. With floats, the number zero can be "
"either positive or negative."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o valor negativo do [Vector2]. Isso é o mesmo que escrever "
"[code]Vector2(-v.x, -v.y)[/code]. Esta operação inverte a direção do vetor "
"mantendo a mesma magnitude. Com floats, o número zero pode ser positivo ou "
"negativo."

#: doc/classes/Vector2i.xml
msgid "A 2D vector using integer coordinates."
msgstr "Um vetor 2D usando coordenadas inteiras."

#: doc/classes/Vector2i.xml
msgid ""
"A 2-element structure that can be used to represent 2D grid coordinates or "
"any other pair of integers.\n"
"It uses integer coordinates and is therefore preferable to [Vector2] when "
"exact precision is required. Note that the values are limited to 32 bits, "
"and unlike [Vector2] this cannot be configured with an engine build option. "
"Use [int] or [PackedInt64Array] if 64-bit values are needed.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] In a boolean context, a Vector2i will evaluate to [code]false[/"
"code] if it's equal to [code]Vector2i(0, 0)[/code]. Otherwise, a Vector2i "
"will always evaluate to [code]true[/code]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Vector2i.xml
msgid ""
"Constructs a default-initialized [Vector2i] with all components set to "
"[code]0[/code]."
msgstr ""
"Constrói um [Vector2i] inicializado por padrão com todos os componentes "
"definidos como [code]0[/code]."

#: doc/classes/Vector2i.xml
msgid "Constructs a [Vector2i] as a copy of the given [Vector2i]."
msgstr "Constrói um [Vector2i] como uma cópia do [Vector2i] fornecido."

#: doc/classes/Vector2i.xml
msgid ""
"Constructs a new [Vector2i] from the given [Vector2] by truncating "
"components' fractional parts (rounding towards zero). For a different "
"behavior consider passing the result of [method Vector2.ceil], [method "
"Vector2.floor] or [method Vector2.round] to this constructor instead."
msgstr ""
"Constrói um novo [Vector2i] a partir do [Vector2] fornecido truncando as "
"partes fracionárias dos componentes (arredondando em direção a zero). Para "
"um comportamento diferente, considere passar o resultado de [method "
"Vector2.ceil], [method Vector2.floor] ou [method Vector2.round] para este "
"construtor."

#: doc/classes/Vector2i.xml
msgid "Constructs a new [Vector2i] from the given [param x] and [param y]."
msgstr ""
"Constrói um novo [Vector2i] a partir de [param x] e [param y] fornecidos."

#: doc/classes/Vector2i.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the aspect ratio of this vector, the ratio of [member x] to [member "
"y]."
msgstr ""
"Retorna a proporção de aspecto deste vetor, a razão de [member x] para "
"[member y]."

#: doc/classes/Vector2i.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the component-wise maximum of this and [param with], equivalent to "
"[code]Vector2i(maxi(x, with.x), maxi(y, with.y))[/code]."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o máximo componente a componente disto e [param with], equivalente a "
"[code]Vector2i(maxi(x, with.x), maxi(y, with.y))[/code]."

#: doc/classes/Vector2i.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the component-wise maximum of this and [param with], equivalent to "
"[code]Vector2i(maxi(x, with), maxi(y, with))[/code]."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o máximo componente a componente disto e [param with], equivalente a "
"[code]Vector2i(maxi(x, with), maxi(y, with))[/code]."

#: doc/classes/Vector2i.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the component-wise minimum of this and [param with], equivalent to "
"[code]Vector2i(mini(x, with.x), mini(y, with.y))[/code]."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o mínimo componente a componente disto e [param with], equivalente a "
"[code]Vector2i(mini(x, with.x), mini(y, with.y))[/code]."

#: doc/classes/Vector2i.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the component-wise minimum of this and [param with], equivalent to "
"[code]Vector2i(mini(x, with), mini(y, with))[/code]."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o mínimo componente a componente disto e [param with], equivalente a "
"[code]Vector2i(mini(x, with), mini(y, with))[/code]."

#: doc/classes/Vector2i.xml doc/classes/Vector3i.xml doc/classes/Vector4i.xml
msgid ""
"Returns a new vector with each component set to [code]1[/code] if it's "
"positive, [code]-1[/code] if it's negative, and [code]0[/code] if it's zero. "
"The result is identical to calling [method @GlobalScope.sign] on each "
"component."
msgstr ""
"Retorna um novo vetor com cada componente definido como [code]1[/code] se "
"for positivo, [code]-1[/code] se for negativo e [code]0[/code] se for zero. "
"O resultado é idêntico a chamar [method @GlobalScope.sign] em cada "
"componente."

#: doc/classes/Vector2i.xml doc/classes/Vector3i.xml doc/classes/Vector4i.xml
msgid ""
"Returns a new vector with each component snapped to the closest multiple of "
"the corresponding component in [param step]."
msgstr ""
"Retorna um novo vetor com cada componente ajustado ao múltiplo mais próximo "
"do componente correspondente em [param step]."

#: doc/classes/Vector2i.xml doc/classes/Vector3i.xml doc/classes/Vector4i.xml
msgid ""
"Returns a new vector with each component snapped to the closest multiple of "
"[param step]."
msgstr ""
"Retorna um novo vetor com cada componente ajustado para o múltiplo mais "
"próximo de [param step]."

#: doc/classes/Vector2i.xml
msgid ""
"Min vector, a vector with all components equal to [code]INT32_MIN[/code]. "
"Can be used as a negative integer equivalent of [constant Vector2.INF]."
msgstr ""
"Vetor mínimo, um vetor com todos os componentes iguais a [code]INT32_MIN[/"
"code]. Pode ser usado como um equivalente inteiro negativo de [constant "
"Vector2.INF]."

#: doc/classes/Vector2i.xml
msgid ""
"Max vector, a vector with all components equal to [code]INT32_MAX[/code]. "
"Can be used as an integer equivalent of [constant Vector2.INF]."
msgstr ""
"Vetor máximo, um vetor com todos os componentes iguais a [code]INT32_MAX[/"
"code]. Pode ser usado como um equivalente inteiro de [constant Vector2.INF]."

#: doc/classes/Vector2i.xml doc/classes/Vector3i.xml doc/classes/Vector4i.xml
msgid "Returns [code]true[/code] if the vectors are not equal."
msgstr "Retorna [code]true[/code] se os vetores não forem iguais."

#: doc/classes/Vector2i.xml
msgid ""
"Gets the remainder of each component of the [Vector2i] with the components "
"of the given [Vector2i]. This operation uses truncated division, which is "
"often not desired as it does not work well with negative numbers. Consider "
"using [method @GlobalScope.posmod] instead if you want to handle negative "
"numbers.\n"
"[codeblock]\n"
"print(Vector2i(10, -20) % Vector2i(7, 8)) # Prints (3, -4)\n"
"[/codeblock]"
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Vector2i.xml
msgid ""
"Gets the remainder of each component of the [Vector2i] with the given [int]. "
"This operation uses truncated division, which is often not desired as it "
"does not work well with negative numbers. Consider using [method "
"@GlobalScope.posmod] instead if you want to handle negative numbers.\n"
"[codeblock]\n"
"print(Vector2i(10, -20) % 7) # Prints (3, -6)\n"
"[/codeblock]"
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Vector2i.xml
msgid ""
"Multiplies each component of the [Vector2i] by the components of the given "
"[Vector2i].\n"
"[codeblock]\n"
"print(Vector2i(10, 20) * Vector2i(3, 4)) # Prints (30, 80)\n"
"[/codeblock]"
msgstr ""
"Multiplica cada componente do [Vector2i] pelos componentes do [Vector2i] "
"fornecido.\n"
"[codeblock]\n"
"print(Vector2i(10, 20) * Vector2i(3, 4)) # Imprime (30, 80)\n"
"[/codeblock]"

#: doc/classes/Vector2i.xml
msgid ""
"Multiplies each component of the [Vector2i] by the given [float]. Returns a "
"[Vector2].\n"
"[codeblock]\n"
"print(Vector2i(10, 15) * 0.9) # Prints (9.0, 13.5)\n"
"[/codeblock]"
msgstr ""
"Multiplica cada componente do [Vector2i] pelo [float] fornecido. Retorna um "
"[Vector2].\n"
"[codeblock]\n"
"print(Vector2i(10, 15) * 0.9) # Imprime (9.0, 13.5)\n"
"[/codeblock]"

#: doc/classes/Vector2i.xml
msgid "Multiplies each component of the [Vector2i] by the given [int]."
msgstr "Multiplica cada componente do [Vector2i] pelo [int] fornecido."

#: doc/classes/Vector2i.xml
msgid ""
"Adds each component of the [Vector2i] by the components of the given "
"[Vector2i].\n"
"[codeblock]\n"
"print(Vector2i(10, 20) + Vector2i(3, 4)) # Prints (13, 24)\n"
"[/codeblock]"
msgstr ""
"Adiciona cada componente do [Vector2i] aos componentes do [Vector2i] "
"fornecido.\n"
"[codeblock]\n"
"print(Vector2i(10, 20) + Vector2i(3, 4)) # Imprime (13, 24)\n"
"[/codeblock]"

#: doc/classes/Vector2i.xml
msgid ""
"Subtracts each component of the [Vector2i] by the components of the given "
"[Vector2i].\n"
"[codeblock]\n"
"print(Vector2i(10, 20) - Vector2i(3, 4)) # Prints (7, 16)\n"
"[/codeblock]"
msgstr ""
"Subtrai de cada componente do [Vector2i] os componentes do [Vector2i] "
"fornecido.\n"
"[codeblock]\n"
"print(Vector2i(10, 20) - Vector2i(3, 4)) # Imprime (7, 16)\n"
"[/codeblock]"

#: doc/classes/Vector2i.xml
msgid ""
"Divides each component of the [Vector2i] by the components of the given "
"[Vector2i].\n"
"[codeblock]\n"
"print(Vector2i(10, 20) / Vector2i(2, 5)) # Prints (5, 4)\n"
"[/codeblock]"
msgstr ""
"Divide cada componente do [Vector2i] pelos componentes do [Vector2i] "
"fornecido.\n"
"[codeblock]\n"
"print(Vector2i(10, 20) / Vector2i(2, 5)) # Imprime (5, 4)\n"
"[/codeblock]"

#: doc/classes/Vector2i.xml
msgid ""
"Divides each component of the [Vector2i] by the given [float]. Returns a "
"[Vector2].\n"
"[codeblock]\n"
"print(Vector2i(1, 2) / 2.5) # Prints (0.4, 0.8)\n"
"[/codeblock]"
msgstr ""
"Divide cada componente do [Vector2i] pelo [float] fornecido. Retorna um "
"[Vector2].\n"
"[codeblock]\n"
"print(Vector2i(1, 2) / 2.5) # Imprime (0.4, 0.8)\n"
"[/codeblock]"

#: doc/classes/Vector2i.xml
msgid "Divides each component of the [Vector2i] by the given [int]."
msgstr "Divide cada componente do [Vector2i] pelo [int] fornecido."

#: doc/classes/Vector2i.xml
msgid ""
"Compares two [Vector2i] vectors by first checking if the X value of the left "
"vector is less than the X value of the [param right] vector. If the X values "
"are exactly equal, then it repeats this check with the Y values of the two "
"vectors. This operator is useful for sorting vectors."
msgstr ""
"Compara dois vetores [Vector2i] verificando primeiro se o valor X do vetor "
"esquerdo é menor que o valor X do vetor [param right]. Se os valores X forem "
"exatamente iguais, ele repete essa verificação com os valores Y dos dois "
"vetores. Este operador é útil para ordenar vetores."

#: doc/classes/Vector2i.xml
msgid ""
"Compares two [Vector2i] vectors by first checking if the X value of the left "
"vector is less than or equal to the X value of the [param right] vector. If "
"the X values are exactly equal, then it repeats this check with the Y values "
"of the two vectors. This operator is useful for sorting vectors."
msgstr ""
"Compara dois vetores [Vector2i] verificando primeiro se o valor X do vetor "
"esquerdo é menor ou igual ao valor X do vetor [param right]. Se os valores X "
"forem exatamente iguais, ele repete essa verificação com os valores Y dos "
"dois vetores. Este operador é útil para ordenar vetores."

#: doc/classes/Vector2i.xml doc/classes/Vector3i.xml
msgid "Returns [code]true[/code] if the vectors are equal."
msgstr "Retorna [code]true[/code] se os vetores forem iguais."

#: doc/classes/Vector2i.xml
msgid ""
"Compares two [Vector2i] vectors by first checking if the X value of the left "
"vector is greater than the X value of the [param right] vector. If the X "
"values are exactly equal, then it repeats this check with the Y values of "
"the two vectors. This operator is useful for sorting vectors."
msgstr ""
"Compara dois vetores [Vector2i] verificando primeiro se o valor X do vetor "
"esquerdo é maior que o valor X do vetor [param right]. Se os valores X forem "
"exatamente iguais, ele repete essa verificação com os valores Y dos dois "
"vetores. Este operador é útil para ordenar vetores."

#: doc/classes/Vector2i.xml
msgid ""
"Compares two [Vector2i] vectors by first checking if the X value of the left "
"vector is greater than or equal to the X value of the [param right] vector. "
"If the X values are exactly equal, then it repeats this check with the Y "
"values of the two vectors. This operator is useful for sorting vectors."
msgstr ""
"Compara dois vetores [Vector2i] verificando primeiro se o valor X do vetor "
"esquerdo é maior ou igual ao valor X do vetor [param right]. Se os valores X "
"forem exatamente iguais, ele repete essa verificação com os valores Y dos "
"dois vetores. Este operador é útil para ordenar vetores."

#: doc/classes/Vector2i.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the negative value of the [Vector2i]. This is the same as writing "
"[code]Vector2i(-v.x, -v.y)[/code]. This operation flips the direction of the "
"vector while keeping the same magnitude."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o valor negativo do [Vector2i]. Isso é o mesmo que escrever "
"[code]Vector2i(-v.x, -v.y)[/code]. Esta operação inverte a direção do vetor "
"mantendo a mesma magnitude."

#: doc/classes/Vector3.xml
msgid "A 3D vector using floating-point coordinates."
msgstr "Um vetor 3D usando coordenadas de ponto flutuante."

#: doc/classes/Vector3.xml
msgid ""
"A 3-element structure that can be used to represent 3D coordinates or any "
"other triplet of numeric values.\n"
"It uses floating-point coordinates. By default, these floating-point values "
"use 32-bit precision, unlike [float] which is always 64-bit. If double "
"precision is needed, compile the engine with the option "
"[code]precision=double[/code].\n"
"See [Vector3i] for its integer counterpart.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] In a boolean context, a Vector3 will evaluate to [code]false[/"
"code] if it's equal to [code]Vector3(0, 0, 0)[/code]. Otherwise, a Vector3 "
"will always evaluate to [code]true[/code]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Vector3.xml
msgid ""
"Constructs a default-initialized [Vector3] with all components set to "
"[code]0[/code]."
msgstr ""
"Constrói um [Vector3] inicializado por padrão com todos os componentes "
"definidos como [code]0[/code]."

#: doc/classes/Vector3.xml
msgid "Constructs a [Vector3] as a copy of the given [Vector3]."
msgstr "Constrói um [Vector3] como uma cópia do [Vector3] fornecido."

#: doc/classes/Vector3.xml
msgid "Constructs a new [Vector3] from [Vector3i]."
msgstr "Constrói um novo [Vector3] a partir de [Vector3i]."

#: doc/classes/Vector3.xml
msgid "Returns a [Vector3] with the given components."
msgstr "Retorna um [Vector3] com os componentes fornecidos."

#: doc/classes/Vector3.xml
msgid "Returns the unsigned minimum angle to the given vector, in radians."
msgstr "Retorna o ângulo mínimo sem sinal para o vetor fornecido, em radianos."

#: doc/classes/Vector3.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the vector \"bounced off\" from a plane defined by the given normal "
"[param n].\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] [method bounce] performs the operation that most engines and "
"frameworks call [code skip-lint]reflect()[/code]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Vector3.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the cross product of this vector and [param with].\n"
"This returns a vector perpendicular to both this and [param with], which "
"would be the normal vector of the plane defined by the two vectors. As there "
"are two such vectors, in opposite directions, this method returns the vector "
"defined by a right-handed coordinate system. If the two vectors are parallel "
"this returns an empty vector, making it useful for testing if two vectors "
"are parallel."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Vector3.xml doc/classes/Vector4.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the normalized vector pointing from this vector to [param to]. This "
"is equivalent to using [code](b - a).normalized()[/code]."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o vetor normalizado apontando deste vetor para [param to]. Isso é "
"equivalente a usar [code](b - a).normalized()[/code]."

#: doc/classes/Vector3.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the inverse of the vector. This is the same as [code]Vector3(1.0 / "
"v.x, 1.0 / v.y, 1.0 / v.z)[/code]."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o inverso do vetor. Isto é o mesmo que [code]Vector3(1.0 / v.x, "
"1.0 / v.y, 1.0 / v.z)[/code]."

#: doc/classes/Vector3.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the component-wise maximum of this and [param with], equivalent to "
"[code]Vector3(maxf(x, with.x), maxf(y, with.y), maxf(z, with.z))[/code]."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o máximo componente a componente deste e de [param with], "
"equivalente a [code]Vector3(maxf(x, with.x), maxf(y, with.y), maxf(z, "
"with.z))[/code]."

#: doc/classes/Vector3.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the component-wise maximum of this and [param with], equivalent to "
"[code]Vector3(maxf(x, with), maxf(y, with), maxf(z, with))[/code]."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o máximo componente a componente deste objeto e de [param with], "
"equivalente a [code]Vector3(maxf(x, with), maxf(y, with), maxf(z, with))[/"
"code]."

#: doc/classes/Vector3.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the component-wise minimum of this and [param with], equivalent to "
"[code]Vector3(minf(x, with.x), minf(y, with.y), minf(z, with.z))[/code]."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o mínimo componente a componente deste e de [param with], "
"equivalente a [code]Vector3(minf(x, with.x), minf(y, with.y), minf(z, "
"with.z))[/code]."

#: doc/classes/Vector3.xml doc/classes/Vector3i.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the axis of the vector's lowest value. See [code]AXIS_*[/code] "
"constants. If all components are equal, this method returns [constant "
"AXIS_Z]."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o eixo do menor valor do vetor. Consulte as constantes [code]AXIS_*[/"
"code]. Se todos os componentes forem iguais, este método retorna [constant "
"AXIS_Z]."

#: doc/classes/Vector3.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the component-wise minimum of this and [param with], equivalent to "
"[code]Vector3(minf(x, with), minf(y, with), minf(z, with))[/code]."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o mínimo componente a componente deste objeto e de [param with], "
"equivalente a [code]Vector3(minf(x, with), minf(y, with), minf(z, with))[/"
"code]."

#: doc/classes/Vector3.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the result of scaling the vector to unit length. Equivalent to "
"[code]v / v.length()[/code]. Returns [code](0, 0, 0)[/code] if "
"[code]v.length() == 0[/code]. See also [method is_normalized].\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] This function may return incorrect values if the input vector "
"length is near zero."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Vector3.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the [Vector3] from an octahedral-compressed form created using "
"[method octahedron_encode] (stored as a [Vector2])."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o [Vector3] a partir de uma forma compactada octaédrica criada "
"usando [method octahedron_encode] (armazenada como [Vector2])."

#: doc/classes/Vector3.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the octahedral-encoded (oct32) form of this [Vector3] as a "
"[Vector2]. Since a [Vector2] occupies 1/3 less memory compared to [Vector3], "
"this form of compression can be used to pass greater amounts of [method "
"normalized] [Vector3]s without increasing storage or memory requirements. "
"See also [method octahedron_decode].\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] [method octahedron_encode] can only be used for [method "
"normalized] vectors. [method octahedron_encode] does [i]not[/i] check "
"whether this [Vector3] is normalized, and will return a value that does not "
"decompress to the original value if the [Vector3] is not normalized.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Octahedral compression is [i]lossy[/i], although visual "
"differences are rarely perceptible in real world scenarios."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Vector3.xml
msgid "Returns the outer product with [param with]."
msgstr "Retorna o produto externo com [param with]."

#: doc/classes/Vector3.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the result of reflecting the vector through a plane defined by the "
"given normal vector [param n].\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] [method reflect] differs from what other engines and frameworks "
"call [code skip-lint]reflect()[/code]. In other engines, [code skip-"
"lint]reflect()[/code] returns the result of the vector reflected by the "
"given plane. The reflection thus passes through the given normal. While in "
"Godot the reflection passes through the plane and can be thought of as "
"bouncing off the normal. See also [method bounce] which does what most "
"engines call [code skip-lint]reflect()[/code]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Vector3.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the result of rotating this vector around a given axis by [param "
"angle] (in radians). The axis must be a normalized vector. See also [method "
"@GlobalScope.deg_to_rad]."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o resultado de rotacionar este vetor em torno de um dado eixo por "
"[param angle] (em radianos). O eixo deve ser um vetor normalizado. Veja "
"também [method @GlobalScope.deg_to_rad]."

#: doc/classes/Vector3.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the signed angle to the given vector, in radians. The sign of the "
"angle is positive in a counter-clockwise direction and negative in a "
"clockwise direction when viewed from the side specified by the [param axis]."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o ângulo sinalizado para o vetor fornecido, em radianos. O sinal do "
"ângulo é positivo no sentido anti-horário e negativo no sentido horário "
"quando visto do lado especificado pelo [param axis]."

#: doc/classes/Vector3.xml
msgid ""
"Returns a new vector resulting from sliding this vector along a plane with "
"normal [param n]. The resulting new vector is perpendicular to [param n], "
"and is equivalent to this vector minus its projection on [param n]. See also "
"[method project].\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] The vector [param n] must be normalized. See also [method "
"normalized]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Vector3.xml doc/classes/Vector3i.xml doc/classes/Vector4.xml
#: doc/classes/Vector4i.xml
msgid ""
"The vector's Z component. Also accessible by using the index position [code]"
"[2][/code]."
msgstr ""
"O componente Z do vetor. Também acessível usando a posição de índice [code]"
"[2][/code]."

#: doc/classes/Vector3.xml doc/classes/Vector3i.xml doc/classes/Vector4.xml
#: doc/classes/Vector4i.xml
msgid ""
"Enumerated value for the Z axis. Returned by [method max_axis_index] and "
"[method min_axis_index]."
msgstr ""
"Valor enumerado para o eixo Z. Retornado por [method max_axis_index] e "
"[method min_axis_index]."

#: doc/classes/Vector3.xml doc/classes/Vector3i.xml
msgid ""
"Left unit vector. Represents the local direction of left, and the global "
"direction of west."
msgstr ""
"Vetor unitário esquerdo. Representa a direção local da esquerda e a direção "
"global do oeste."

#: doc/classes/Vector3.xml doc/classes/Vector3i.xml
msgid ""
"Right unit vector. Represents the local direction of right, and the global "
"direction of east."
msgstr ""
"Vetor unitário direito. Representa a direção local da direita e a direção "
"global do leste."

#: doc/classes/Vector3.xml doc/classes/Vector3i.xml
msgid "Up unit vector."
msgstr "Vetor unitário para cima."

#: doc/classes/Vector3.xml doc/classes/Vector3i.xml
msgid "Down unit vector."
msgstr "Vetor unitário para baixo."

#: doc/classes/Vector3.xml
msgid ""
"Forward unit vector. Represents the local direction of forward, and the "
"global direction of north. Keep in mind that the forward direction for "
"lights, cameras, etc is different from 3D assets like characters, which face "
"towards the camera by convention. Use [constant Vector3.MODEL_FRONT] and "
"similar constants when working in 3D asset space."
msgstr ""
"Vetor unitário para a frente. Representa a direção local para a frente e a "
"direção global para o norte. Tenha em mente que a direção para a frente para "
"luzes, câmeras, etc., é diferente de ativos 3D como personagens, que ficam "
"virados para a câmera por convenção. Use [constant Vector3.MODEL_FRONT] e "
"constantes semelhantes ao trabalhar no espaço de ativos 3D."

#: doc/classes/Vector3.xml doc/classes/Vector3i.xml
msgid ""
"Back unit vector. Represents the local direction of back, and the global "
"direction of south."
msgstr ""
"Vetor unitário traseiro. Representa a direção local de trás e a direção "
"global do sul."

#: doc/classes/Vector3.xml
msgid "Unit vector pointing towards the left side of imported 3D assets."
msgstr "Vetor unitário apontando para o lado esquerdo de ativos 3D importados."

#: doc/classes/Vector3.xml
msgid "Unit vector pointing towards the right side of imported 3D assets."
msgstr "Vetor unitário apontando para o lado direito de ativos 3D importados."

#: doc/classes/Vector3.xml
msgid "Unit vector pointing towards the top side (up) of imported 3D assets."
msgstr ""
"Vetor unitário apontando para o lado superior (acima) de ativos 3D "
"importados."

#: doc/classes/Vector3.xml
msgid ""
"Unit vector pointing towards the bottom side (down) of imported 3D assets."
msgstr ""
"Vetor unitário apontando para o lado inferior (baixo) de ativos 3D "
"importados."

#: doc/classes/Vector3.xml
msgid ""
"Unit vector pointing towards the front side (facing forward) of imported 3D "
"assets."
msgstr ""
"Vetor unitário apontando para o lado frontal (virado para frente) de ativos "
"3D importados."

#: doc/classes/Vector3.xml
msgid ""
"Unit vector pointing towards the rear side (back) of imported 3D assets."
msgstr ""
"Vetor unitário apontando para o lado traseiro (costas) de ativos 3D "
"importados."

#: doc/classes/Vector3.xml
msgid ""
"Inversely transforms (multiplies) the [Vector3] by the given [Basis] matrix, "
"under the assumption that the basis is orthonormal (i.e. rotation/reflection "
"is fine, scaling/skew is not).\n"
"[code]vector * basis[/code] is equivalent to [code]basis.transposed() * "
"vector[/code]. See [method Basis.transposed].\n"
"For transforming by inverse of a non-orthonormal basis (e.g. with scaling) "
"[code]basis.inverse() * vector[/code] can be used instead. See [method "
"Basis.inverse]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Vector3.xml
msgid ""
"Inversely transforms (multiplies) the [Vector3] by the given [Quaternion].\n"
"[code]vector * quaternion[/code] is equivalent to [code]quaternion.inverse() "
"* vector[/code]. See [method Quaternion.inverse]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Vector3.xml
msgid ""
"Inversely transforms (multiplies) the [Vector3] by the given [Transform3D] "
"transformation matrix, under the assumption that the transformation basis is "
"orthonormal (i.e. rotation/reflection is fine, scaling/skew is not).\n"
"[code]vector * transform[/code] is equivalent to [code]transform.inverse() * "
"vector[/code]. See [method Transform3D.inverse].\n"
"For transforming by inverse of an affine transformation (e.g. with scaling) "
"[code]transform.affine_inverse() * vector[/code] can be used instead. See "
"[method Transform3D.affine_inverse]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Vector3.xml
msgid ""
"Multiplies each component of the [Vector3] by the components of the given "
"[Vector3].\n"
"[codeblock]\n"
"print(Vector3(10, 20, 30) * Vector3(3, 4, 5)) # Prints (30.0, 80.0, 150.0)\n"
"[/codeblock]"
msgstr ""
"Multiplica cada componente do [Vector3] pelos componentes do [Vector3] "
"fornecido.\n"
"[codeblock]\n"
"print(Vector3(10, 20, 30) * Vector3(3, 4, 5)) # Imprime (30.0, 80.0, 150.0)\n"
"[/codeblock]"

#: doc/classes/Vector3.xml
msgid "Multiplies each component of the [Vector3] by the given [int]."
msgstr "Multiplica cada componente do [Vector3] pelo [int] fornecido."

#: doc/classes/Vector3.xml
msgid ""
"Adds each component of the [Vector3] by the components of the given "
"[Vector3].\n"
"[codeblock]\n"
"print(Vector3(10, 20, 30) + Vector3(3, 4, 5)) # Prints (13.0, 24.0, 35.0)\n"
"[/codeblock]"
msgstr ""
"Adiciona cada componente do [Vector3] aos componentes do [Vector3] "
"fornecido.\n"
"[codeblock]\n"
"print(Vector3(10, 20, 30) + Vector3(3, 4, 5)) # Imprime (13.0, 24.0, 35.0)\n"
"[/codeblock]"

#: doc/classes/Vector3.xml
msgid ""
"Subtracts each component of the [Vector3] by the components of the given "
"[Vector3].\n"
"[codeblock]\n"
"print(Vector3(10, 20, 30) - Vector3(3, 4, 5)) # Prints (7.0, 16.0, 25.0)\n"
"[/codeblock]"
msgstr ""
"Subtrai de cada componente do [Vector3] os componentes do [Vector3] "
"fornecido.\n"
"[codeblock]\n"
"print(Vector3(10, 20, 30) - Vector3(3, 4, 5)) # Imprime (7.0, 16.0, 25.0)\n"
"[/codeblock]"

#: doc/classes/Vector3.xml
msgid ""
"Divides each component of the [Vector3] by the components of the given "
"[Vector3].\n"
"[codeblock]\n"
"print(Vector3(10, 20, 30) / Vector3(2, 5, 3)) # Prints (5.0, 4.0, 10.0)\n"
"[/codeblock]"
msgstr ""
"Divide cada componente do [Vector3] pelos componentes do [Vector3] "
"fornecido.\n"
"[codeblock]\n"
"print(Vector3(10, 20, 30) / Vector3(2, 5, 3)) # Imprime (5.0, 4.0, 10.0)\n"
"[/codeblock]"

#: doc/classes/Vector3.xml
msgid "Divides each component of the [Vector3] by the given [float]."
msgstr "Divide cada componente do [Vector3] pelo [float] fornecido."

#: doc/classes/Vector3.xml
msgid "Divides each component of the [Vector3] by the given [int]."
msgstr "Divide cada componente do [Vector3] pelo [int] fornecido."

#: doc/classes/Vector3.xml
msgid ""
"Compares two [Vector3] vectors by first checking if the X value of the left "
"vector is less than the X value of the [param right] vector. If the X values "
"are exactly equal, then it repeats this check with the Y values of the two "
"vectors, and then with the Z values. This operator is useful for sorting "
"vectors.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Vectors with [constant @GDScript.NAN] elements don't behave the "
"same as other vectors. Therefore, the results from this operator may not be "
"accurate if NaNs are included."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Vector3.xml
msgid ""
"Compares two [Vector3] vectors by first checking if the X value of the left "
"vector is less than or equal to the X value of the [param right] vector. If "
"the X values are exactly equal, then it repeats this check with the Y values "
"of the two vectors, and then with the Z values. This operator is useful for "
"sorting vectors.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Vectors with [constant @GDScript.NAN] elements don't behave the "
"same as other vectors. Therefore, the results from this operator may not be "
"accurate if NaNs are included."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Vector3.xml
msgid ""
"Compares two [Vector3] vectors by first checking if the X value of the left "
"vector is greater than the X value of the [param right] vector. If the X "
"values are exactly equal, then it repeats this check with the Y values of "
"the two vectors, and then with the Z values. This operator is useful for "
"sorting vectors.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Vectors with [constant @GDScript.NAN] elements don't behave the "
"same as other vectors. Therefore, the results from this operator may not be "
"accurate if NaNs are included."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Vector3.xml
msgid ""
"Compares two [Vector3] vectors by first checking if the X value of the left "
"vector is greater than or equal to the X value of the [param right] vector. "
"If the X values are exactly equal, then it repeats this check with the Y "
"values of the two vectors, and then with the Z values. This operator is "
"useful for sorting vectors.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Vectors with [constant @GDScript.NAN] elements don't behave the "
"same as other vectors. Therefore, the results from this operator may not be "
"accurate if NaNs are included."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Vector3.xml doc/classes/Vector3i.xml
msgid ""
"Access vector components using their [param index]. [code]v[0][/code] is "
"equivalent to [code]v.x[/code], [code]v[1][/code] is equivalent to "
"[code]v.y[/code], and [code]v[2][/code] is equivalent to [code]v.z[/code]."
msgstr ""
"Acessa os componentes do vetor usando seu [param index]. [code]v[0][/code] é "
"equivalente a [code]v.x[/code], [code]v[1][/code] é equivalente a [code]v.y[/"
"code] e [code]v[2][/code] é equivalente a [code]v.z[/code]."

#: doc/classes/Vector3.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the negative value of the [Vector3]. This is the same as writing "
"[code]Vector3(-v.x, -v.y, -v.z)[/code]. This operation flips the direction "
"of the vector while keeping the same magnitude. With floats, the number zero "
"can be either positive or negative."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o valor negativo do [Vector3]. Isso é o mesmo que escrever "
"[code]Vector3(-v.x, -v.y, -v.z)[/code]. Esta operação inverte a direção do "
"vetor mantendo a mesma magnitude. Com ponto flutuante, o número zero pode "
"ser positivo ou negativo."

#: doc/classes/Vector3i.xml
msgid "A 3D vector using integer coordinates."
msgstr "Um vetor 3D usando coordenadas inteiras."

#: doc/classes/Vector3i.xml
msgid ""
"A 3-element structure that can be used to represent 3D grid coordinates or "
"any other triplet of integers.\n"
"It uses integer coordinates and is therefore preferable to [Vector3] when "
"exact precision is required. Note that the values are limited to 32 bits, "
"and unlike [Vector3] this cannot be configured with an engine build option. "
"Use [int] or [PackedInt64Array] if 64-bit values are needed.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] In a boolean context, a Vector3i will evaluate to [code]false[/"
"code] if it's equal to [code]Vector3i(0, 0, 0)[/code]. Otherwise, a Vector3i "
"will always evaluate to [code]true[/code]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Vector3i.xml
msgid ""
"Constructs a default-initialized [Vector3i] with all components set to "
"[code]0[/code]."
msgstr ""
"Constrói um [Vector3i] inicializado por padrão com todos os componentes "
"definidos como [code]0[/code]."

#: doc/classes/Vector3i.xml
msgid "Constructs a [Vector3i] as a copy of the given [Vector3i]."
msgstr "Cria um [Vector3i] como uma cópia do [Vector3i] fornecido."

#: doc/classes/Vector3i.xml
msgid ""
"Constructs a new [Vector3i] from the given [Vector3] by truncating "
"components' fractional parts (rounding towards zero). For a different "
"behavior consider passing the result of [method Vector3.ceil], [method "
"Vector3.floor] or [method Vector3.round] to this constructor instead."
msgstr ""
"Constrói um novo [Vector3i] a partir do [Vector3] fornecido truncando as "
"partes fracionárias dos componentes (arredondando em direção a zero). Para "
"um comportamento diferente, considere passar o resultado de [method "
"Vector3.ceil], [method Vector3.floor] ou [method Vector3.round] para este "
"construtor."

#: doc/classes/Vector3i.xml
msgid "Returns a [Vector3i] with the given components."
msgstr "Retorna um [Vector3i] com os componentes fornecidos."

#: doc/classes/Vector3i.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the component-wise maximum of this and [param with], equivalent to "
"[code]Vector3i(maxi(x, with.x), maxi(y, with.y), maxi(z, with.z))[/code]."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o máximo componente a componente deste e de [param with], "
"equivalente a [code]Vector3i(maxi(x, with.x), maxi(y, with.y), maxi(z, "
"with.z))[/code]."

#: doc/classes/Vector3i.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the component-wise maximum of this and [param with], equivalent to "
"[code]Vector3i(maxi(x, with), maxi(y, with), maxi(z, with))[/code]."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o máximo componente a componente deste objeto e de [param with], "
"equivalente a [code]Vector3i(maxi(x, with), maxi(y, with), maxi(z, with))[/"
"code]."

#: doc/classes/Vector3i.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the component-wise minimum of this and [param with], equivalent to "
"[code]Vector3i(mini(x, with.x), mini(y, with.y), mini(z, with.z))[/code]."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o mínimo componente a componente deste e de [param with], "
"equivalente a [code]Vector3i(mini(x, with.x), mini(y, with.y), mini(z, "
"with.z))[/code]."

#: doc/classes/Vector3i.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the component-wise minimum of this and [param with], equivalent to "
"[code]Vector3i(mini(x, with), mini(y, with), mini(z, with))[/code]."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o mínimo componente a componente deste objeto e de [param with], "
"equivalente a [code]Vector3i(mini(x, with), mini(y, with), mini(z, with))[/"
"code]."

#: doc/classes/Vector3i.xml
msgid ""
"Min vector, a vector with all components equal to [code]INT32_MIN[/code]. "
"Can be used as a negative integer equivalent of [constant Vector3.INF]."
msgstr ""
"Vetor mínimo, um vetor com todos os componentes iguais a [code]INT32_MIN[/"
"code]. Pode ser usado como um equivalente inteiro negativo de [constant "
"Vector3.INF]."

#: doc/classes/Vector3i.xml
msgid ""
"Max vector, a vector with all components equal to [code]INT32_MAX[/code]. "
"Can be used as an integer equivalent of [constant Vector3.INF]."
msgstr ""
"Vetor máximo, um vetor com todos os componentes iguais a [code]INT32_MAX[/"
"code]. Pode ser usado como um equivalente inteiro de [constant Vector3.INF]."

#: doc/classes/Vector3i.xml
msgid ""
"Forward unit vector. Represents the local direction of forward, and the "
"global direction of north."
msgstr ""
"Vetor unitário frontal. Representa a direção local de frente e a direção "
"global do norte."

#: doc/classes/Vector3i.xml
msgid ""
"Gets the remainder of each component of the [Vector3i] with the components "
"of the given [Vector3i]. This operation uses truncated division, which is "
"often not desired as it does not work well with negative numbers. Consider "
"using [method @GlobalScope.posmod] instead if you want to handle negative "
"numbers.\n"
"[codeblock]\n"
"print(Vector3i(10, -20, 30) % Vector3i(7, 8, 9)) # Prints (3, -4, 3)\n"
"[/codeblock]"
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Vector3i.xml
msgid ""
"Gets the remainder of each component of the [Vector3i] with the given [int]. "
"This operation uses truncated division, which is often not desired as it "
"does not work well with negative numbers. Consider using [method "
"@GlobalScope.posmod] instead if you want to handle negative numbers.\n"
"[codeblock]\n"
"print(Vector3i(10, -20, 30) % 7) # Prints (3, -6, 2)\n"
"[/codeblock]"
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Vector3i.xml
msgid ""
"Multiplies each component of the [Vector3i] by the components of the given "
"[Vector3i].\n"
"[codeblock]\n"
"print(Vector3i(10, 20, 30) * Vector3i(3, 4, 5)) # Prints (30, 80, 150)\n"
"[/codeblock]"
msgstr ""
"Multiplica cada componente do [Vector3i] pelos componentes do [Vector3i] "
"fornecido.\n"
"[codeblock]\n"
"print(Vector3i(10, 20, 30) * Vector3i(3, 4, 5)) # Imprime (30, 80, 150)\n"
"[/codeblock]"

#: doc/classes/Vector3i.xml
msgid ""
"Multiplies each component of the [Vector3i] by the given [float]. Returns a "
"[Vector3].\n"
"[codeblock]\n"
"print(Vector3i(10, 15, 20) * 0.9) # Prints (9.0, 13.5, 18.0)\n"
"[/codeblock]"
msgstr ""
"Multiplica cada componente do [Vector3i] pelo [float] fornecido. Retorna um "
"[Vector3].\n"
"[codeblock]\n"
"print(Vector3i(10, 15, 20) * 0.9) # Imprime (9.0, 13.5, 18.0)\n"
"[/codeblock]"

#: doc/classes/Vector3i.xml
msgid "Multiplies each component of the [Vector3i] by the given [int]."
msgstr "Multiplica cada componente do [Vector3i] pelo [int] fornecido."

#: doc/classes/Vector3i.xml
msgid ""
"Adds each component of the [Vector3i] by the components of the given "
"[Vector3i].\n"
"[codeblock]\n"
"print(Vector3i(10, 20, 30) + Vector3i(3, 4, 5)) # Prints (13, 24, 35)\n"
"[/codeblock]"
msgstr ""
"Adiciona cada componente do [Vector3i] aos componentes do [Vector3i] "
"fornecido.\n"
"[codeblock]\n"
"print(Vector3i(10, 20, 30) + Vector3i(3, 4, 5)) # Imprime (13, 24, 35)\n"
"[/codeblock]"

#: doc/classes/Vector3i.xml
msgid ""
"Subtracts each component of the [Vector3i] by the components of the given "
"[Vector3i].\n"
"[codeblock]\n"
"print(Vector3i(10, 20, 30) - Vector3i(3, 4, 5)) # Prints (7, 16, 25)\n"
"[/codeblock]"
msgstr ""
"Subtrai de cada componente do [Vector3i] os componentes do [Vector3i] "
"fornecido.\n"
"[codeblock]\n"
"print(Vector3i(10, 20, 30) - Vector3i(3, 4, 5)) # Imprime (7, 16, 25)\n"
"[/codeblock]"

#: doc/classes/Vector3i.xml
msgid ""
"Divides each component of the [Vector3i] by the components of the given "
"[Vector3i].\n"
"[codeblock]\n"
"print(Vector3i(10, 20, 30) / Vector3i(2, 5, 3)) # Prints (5, 4, 10)\n"
"[/codeblock]"
msgstr ""
"Divide cada componente do [Vector3i] pelos componentes do [Vector3i] "
"fornecido.\n"
"[codeblock]\n"
"print(Vector3i(10, 20, 30) / Vector3i(2, 5, 3)) # Imprime (5, 4, 10)\n"
"[/codeblock]"

#: doc/classes/Vector3i.xml
msgid ""
"Divides each component of the [Vector3i] by the given [float]. Returns a "
"[Vector3].\n"
"[codeblock]\n"
"print(Vector3i(1, 2, 3) / 2.5) # Prints (0.4, 0.8, 1.2)\n"
"[/codeblock]"
msgstr ""
"Divide cada componente do [Vector3i] pelo [float] fornecido. Retorna um "
"[Vector3].\n"
"[codeblock]\n"
"print(Vector3i(1, 2, 3) / 2.5) # Imprime (0.4, 0.8, 1.2)\n"
"[/codeblock]"

#: doc/classes/Vector3i.xml
msgid "Divides each component of the [Vector3i] by the given [int]."
msgstr "Divide cada componente do [Vector3i] pelo [int] fornecido."

#: doc/classes/Vector3i.xml
msgid ""
"Compares two [Vector3i] vectors by first checking if the X value of the left "
"vector is less than the X value of the [param right] vector. If the X values "
"are exactly equal, then it repeats this check with the Y values of the two "
"vectors, and then with the Z values. This operator is useful for sorting "
"vectors."
msgstr ""
"Compara dois vetores [Vector3i] verificando primeiro se o valor X do vetor "
"esquerdo é menor que o valor X do vetor [param right]. Se os valores X forem "
"exatamente iguais, ele repete essa verificação com os valores Y dos dois "
"vetores e, em seguida, com os valores Z. Este operador é útil para ordenar "
"vetores."

#: doc/classes/Vector3i.xml
msgid ""
"Compares two [Vector3i] vectors by first checking if the X value of the left "
"vector is less than or equal to the X value of the [param right] vector. If "
"the X values are exactly equal, then it repeats this check with the Y values "
"of the two vectors, and then with the Z values. This operator is useful for "
"sorting vectors."
msgstr ""
"Compara dois vetores [Vector3i] verificando primeiro se o valor X do vetor "
"esquerdo é menor ou igual ao valor X do vetor [param right]. Se os valores X "
"forem exatamente iguais, ele repete esta verificação com os valores Y dos "
"dois vetores e, em seguida, com os valores Z. Este operador é útil para "
"ordenar vetores."

#: doc/classes/Vector3i.xml
msgid ""
"Compares two [Vector3i] vectors by first checking if the X value of the left "
"vector is greater than the X value of the [param right] vector. If the X "
"values are exactly equal, then it repeats this check with the Y values of "
"the two vectors, and then with the Z values. This operator is useful for "
"sorting vectors."
msgstr ""
"Compara dois vetores [Vector3i] verificando primeiro se o valor X do vetor "
"esquerdo é maior que o valor X do vetor [param right]. Se os valores X forem "
"exatamente iguais, ele repete essa verificação com os valores Y dos dois "
"vetores e, em seguida, com os valores Z. Este operador é útil para ordenar "
"vetores."

#: doc/classes/Vector3i.xml
msgid ""
"Compares two [Vector3i] vectors by first checking if the X value of the left "
"vector is greater than or equal to the X value of the [param right] vector. "
"If the X values are exactly equal, then it repeats this check with the Y "
"values of the two vectors, and then with the Z values. This operator is "
"useful for sorting vectors."
msgstr ""
"Compara dois vetores [Vector3i] verificando primeiro se o valor X do vetor "
"esquerdo é maior ou igual ao valor X do vetor [param right]. Se os valores X "
"forem exatamente iguais, ele repete esta verificação com os valores Y dos "
"dois vetores e, em seguida, com os valores Z. Este operador é útil para "
"ordenar vetores."

#: doc/classes/Vector3i.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the negative value of the [Vector3i]. This is the same as writing "
"[code]Vector3i(-v.x, -v.y, -v.z)[/code]. This operation flips the direction "
"of the vector while keeping the same magnitude."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o valor negativo do [Vector3i]. Isso é o mesmo que escrever "
"[code]Vector3i(-v.x, -v.y, -v.z)[/code]. Esta operação inverte a direção do "
"vetor mantendo a mesma magnitude."

#: doc/classes/Vector4.xml
msgid "A 4D vector using floating-point coordinates."
msgstr "Um vetor 4D usando coordenadas de ponto flutuante."

#: doc/classes/Vector4.xml
msgid ""
"A 4-element structure that can be used to represent 4D coordinates or any "
"other quadruplet of numeric values.\n"
"It uses floating-point coordinates. By default, these floating-point values "
"use 32-bit precision, unlike [float] which is always 64-bit. If double "
"precision is needed, compile the engine with the option "
"[code]precision=double[/code].\n"
"See [Vector4i] for its integer counterpart.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] In a boolean context, a Vector4 will evaluate to [code]false[/"
"code] if it's equal to [code]Vector4(0, 0, 0, 0)[/code]. Otherwise, a "
"Vector4 will always evaluate to [code]true[/code]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Vector4.xml
msgid ""
"Constructs a default-initialized [Vector4] with all components set to "
"[code]0[/code]."
msgstr ""
"Constrói um [Vector4] inicializado por padrão com todos os componentes "
"definidos como [code]0[/code]."

#: doc/classes/Vector4.xml
msgid "Constructs a [Vector4] as a copy of the given [Vector4]."
msgstr "Constrói um [Vector4] como uma cópia do [Vector4] fornecido."

#: doc/classes/Vector4.xml
msgid "Constructs a new [Vector4] from the given [Vector4i]."
msgstr "Constrói um novo [Vector4] a partir do [Vector4i] fornecido."

#: doc/classes/Vector4.xml
msgid "Returns a [Vector4] with the given components."
msgstr "Retorna um [Vector4] com os componentes fornecidos."

#: doc/classes/Vector4.xml
msgid "Returns the dot product of this vector and [param with]."
msgstr "Retorna o produto escalar (dot product) deste vetor e [param with]."

#: doc/classes/Vector4.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the inverse of the vector. This is the same as [code]Vector4(1.0 / "
"v.x, 1.0 / v.y, 1.0 / v.z, 1.0 / v.w)[/code]."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o inverso do vetor. Isso é o mesmo que [code]Vector4(1.0 / v.x, "
"1.0 / v.y, 1.0 / v.z, 1.0 / v.w)[/code]."

#: doc/classes/Vector4.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the component-wise maximum of this and [param with], equivalent to "
"[code]Vector4(maxf(x, with.x), maxf(y, with.y), maxf(z, with.z), maxf(w, "
"with.w))[/code]."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o máximo componente a componente deste e de [param with], "
"equivalente a [code]Vector4(maxf(x, with.x), maxf(y, with.y), maxf(z, "
"with.z), maxf(w, with.w))[/code]."

#: doc/classes/Vector4.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the component-wise maximum of this and [param with], equivalent to "
"[code]Vector4(maxf(x, with), maxf(y, with), maxf(z, with), maxf(w, with))[/"
"code]."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o máximo componente a componente deste e de [param with], "
"equivalente a [code]Vector4(maxf(x, with), maxf(y, with), maxf(z, with), "
"maxf(w, with))[/code]."

#: doc/classes/Vector4.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the component-wise minimum of this and [param with], equivalent to "
"[code]Vector4(minf(x, with.x), minf(y, with.y), minf(z, with.z), minf(w, "
"with.w))[/code]."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o mínimo componente a componente deste e de [param with], "
"equivalente a [code]Vector4(minf(x, with.x), minf(y, with.y), minf(z, "
"with.z), minf(w, with.w))[/code]."

#: doc/classes/Vector4.xml doc/classes/Vector4i.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the axis of the vector's lowest value. See [code]AXIS_*[/code] "
"constants. If all components are equal, this method returns [constant "
"AXIS_W]."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o eixo do menor valor do vetor. Consulte as constantes [code]AXIS_*[/"
"code]. Se todos os componentes forem iguais, este método retorna [constant "
"AXIS_W]."

#: doc/classes/Vector4.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the component-wise minimum of this and [param with], equivalent to "
"[code]Vector4(minf(x, with), minf(y, with), minf(z, with), minf(w, with))[/"
"code]."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o mínimo componente a componente deste e de [param with], "
"equivalente a [code]Vector4(minf(x, with), minf(y, with), minf(z, with), "
"minf(w, with))[/code]."

#: doc/classes/Vector4.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the result of scaling the vector to unit length. Equivalent to "
"[code]v / v.length()[/code]. Returns [code](0, 0, 0, 0)[/code] if "
"[code]v.length() == 0[/code]. See also [method is_normalized].\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] This function may return incorrect values if the input vector "
"length is near zero."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Vector4.xml doc/classes/Vector4i.xml
msgid ""
"The vector's W component. Also accessible by using the index position [code]"
"[3][/code]."
msgstr ""
"O componente W do vetor. Também acessível usando a posição de índice [code]"
"[3][/code]."

#: doc/classes/Vector4.xml doc/classes/Vector4i.xml
msgid ""
"Enumerated value for the W axis. Returned by [method max_axis_index] and "
"[method min_axis_index]."
msgstr ""
"Valor enumerado para o eixo W. Retornado por [method max_axis_index] e "
"[method min_axis_index]."

#: doc/classes/Vector4.xml
msgid ""
"Transforms (multiplies) the [Vector4] by the transpose of the given "
"[Projection] matrix.\n"
"For transforming by inverse of a projection [code]projection.inverse() * "
"vector[/code] can be used instead. See [method Projection.inverse]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Vector4.xml
msgid ""
"Multiplies each component of the [Vector4] by the components of the given "
"[Vector4].\n"
"[codeblock]\n"
"print(Vector4(10, 20, 30, 40) * Vector4(3, 4, 5, 6)) # Prints (30.0, 80.0, "
"150.0, 240.0)\n"
"[/codeblock]"
msgstr ""
"Multiplica cada componente do [Vector4] pelos componentes do [Vector4] "
"fornecido.\n"
"[codeblock]\n"
"print(Vector4(10, 20, 30, 40) * Vector4(3, 4, 5, 6)) # Imprime (30.0, 80.0, "
"150.0, 240.0)\n"
"[/codeblock]"

#: doc/classes/Vector4.xml
msgid ""
"Multiplies each component of the [Vector4] by the given [float].\n"
"[codeblock]\n"
"print(Vector4(10, 20, 30, 40) * 2) # Prints (20.0, 40.0, 60.0, 80.0)\n"
"[/codeblock]"
msgstr ""
"Multiplica cada componente do [Vector4] pelo [float] fornecido.\n"
"[codeblock]\n"
"print(Vector4(10, 20, 30, 40) * 2) # Imprime (20.0, 40.0, 60.0, 80.0)\n"
"[/codeblock]"

#: doc/classes/Vector4.xml
msgid "Multiplies each component of the [Vector4] by the given [int]."
msgstr "Multiplica cada componente do [Vector4] pelo [int] fornecido."

#: doc/classes/Vector4.xml
msgid ""
"Adds each component of the [Vector4] by the components of the given "
"[Vector4].\n"
"[codeblock]\n"
"print(Vector4(10, 20, 30, 40) + Vector4(3, 4, 5, 6)) # Prints (13.0, 24.0, "
"35.0, 46.0)\n"
"[/codeblock]"
msgstr ""
"Adiciona cada componente do [Vector4] aos componentes do [Vector4] "
"fornecido.\n"
"[codeblock]\n"
"print(Vector4(10, 20, 30, 40) + Vector4(3, 4, 5, 6)) # Imprime (13.0, 24.0, "
"35.0, 46.0)\n"
"[/codeblock]"

#: doc/classes/Vector4.xml
msgid ""
"Subtracts each component of the [Vector4] by the components of the given "
"[Vector4].\n"
"[codeblock]\n"
"print(Vector4(10, 20, 30, 40) - Vector4(3, 4, 5, 6)) # Prints (7.0, 16.0, "
"25.0, 34.0)\n"
"[/codeblock]"
msgstr ""
"Subtrai de cada componente do [Vector4] os componentes do [Vector4] "
"fornecido.\n"
"[codeblock]\n"
"print(Vector4(10, 20, 30, 40) - Vector4(3, 4, 5, 6)) # Imprime (7.0, 16.0, "
"25.0, 34.0)\n"
"[/codeblock]"

#: doc/classes/Vector4.xml
msgid ""
"Divides each component of the [Vector4] by the components of the given "
"[Vector4].\n"
"[codeblock]\n"
"print(Vector4(10, 20, 30, 40) / Vector4(2, 5, 3, 4)) # Prints (5.0, 4.0, "
"10.0, 10.0)\n"
"[/codeblock]"
msgstr ""
"Divide cada componente do [Vector4] pelos componentes do [Vector4] "
"fornecido.\n"
"[codeblock]\n"
"print(Vector4(10, 20, 30, 40) / Vector4(2, 5, 3, 4)) # Imprime (5.0, 4.0, "
"10.0, 10.0)\n"
"[/codeblock]"

#: doc/classes/Vector4.xml
msgid ""
"Divides each component of the [Vector4] by the given [float].\n"
"[codeblock]\n"
"print(Vector4(10, 20, 30, 40) / 2) # Prints (5.0, 10.0, 15.0, 20.0)\n"
"[/codeblock]"
msgstr ""
"Divide cada componente do [Vector4] pelo [float] fornecido.\n"
"[codeblock]\n"
"print(Vector4(10, 20, 30, 40) / 2) # Imprime (5.0, 10.0, 15.0, 20.0)\n"
"[/codeblock]"

#: doc/classes/Vector4.xml
msgid "Divides each component of the [Vector4] by the given [int]."
msgstr "Divide cada componente do [Vector4] pelo [int] fornecido."

#: doc/classes/Vector4.xml
msgid ""
"Compares two [Vector4] vectors by first checking if the X value of the left "
"vector is less than the X value of the [param right] vector. If the X values "
"are exactly equal, then it repeats this check with the Y values of the two "
"vectors, Z values of the two vectors, and then with the W values. This "
"operator is useful for sorting vectors.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Vectors with [constant @GDScript.NAN] elements don't behave the "
"same as other vectors. Therefore, the results from this operator may not be "
"accurate if NaNs are included."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Vector4.xml
msgid ""
"Compares two [Vector4] vectors by first checking if the X value of the left "
"vector is less than or equal to the X value of the [param right] vector. If "
"the X values are exactly equal, then it repeats this check with the Y values "
"of the two vectors, Z values of the two vectors, and then with the W values. "
"This operator is useful for sorting vectors.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Vectors with [constant @GDScript.NAN] elements don't behave the "
"same as other vectors. Therefore, the results from this operator may not be "
"accurate if NaNs are included."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Vector4.xml
msgid ""
"Compares two [Vector4] vectors by first checking if the X value of the left "
"vector is greater than the X value of the [param right] vector. If the X "
"values are exactly equal, then it repeats this check with the Y values of "
"the two vectors, Z values of the two vectors, and then with the W values. "
"This operator is useful for sorting vectors.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Vectors with [constant @GDScript.NAN] elements don't behave the "
"same as other vectors. Therefore, the results from this operator may not be "
"accurate if NaNs are included."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Vector4.xml
msgid ""
"Compares two [Vector4] vectors by first checking if the X value of the left "
"vector is greater than or equal to the X value of the [param right] vector. "
"If the X values are exactly equal, then it repeats this check with the Y "
"values of the two vectors, Z values of the two vectors, and then with the W "
"values. This operator is useful for sorting vectors.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Vectors with [constant @GDScript.NAN] elements don't behave the "
"same as other vectors. Therefore, the results from this operator may not be "
"accurate if NaNs are included."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Vector4.xml doc/classes/Vector4i.xml
msgid ""
"Access vector components using their [param index]. [code]v[0][/code] is "
"equivalent to [code]v.x[/code], [code]v[1][/code] is equivalent to "
"[code]v.y[/code], [code]v[2][/code] is equivalent to [code]v.z[/code], and "
"[code]v[3][/code] is equivalent to [code]v.w[/code]."
msgstr ""
"Acesse os componentes do vetor usando seu [param index]. [code]v[0][/code] é "
"equivalente a [code]v.x[/code], [code]v[1][/code] é equivalente a [code]v.y[/"
"code], [code]v[2][/code] é equivalente a [code]v.z[/code] e [code]v[3][/"
"code] é equivalente a [code]v.w[/code]."

#: doc/classes/Vector4.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the negative value of the [Vector4]. This is the same as writing "
"[code]Vector4(-v.x, -v.y, -v.z, -v.w)[/code]. This operation flips the "
"direction of the vector while keeping the same magnitude. With floats, the "
"number zero can be either positive or negative."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o valor negativo do [Vector4]. Isso é o mesmo que escrever "
"[code]Vector4(-v.x, -v.y, -v.z, -v.w)[/code]. Esta operação inverte a "
"direção do vetor mantendo a mesma magnitude. Com ponto flutuante, o número "
"zero pode ser positivo ou negativo."

#: doc/classes/Vector4i.xml
msgid "A 4D vector using integer coordinates."
msgstr "Um vetor 4D usando coordenadas inteiras."

#: doc/classes/Vector4i.xml
msgid ""
"A 4-element structure that can be used to represent 4D grid coordinates or "
"any other quadruplet of integers.\n"
"It uses integer coordinates and is therefore preferable to [Vector4] when "
"exact precision is required. Note that the values are limited to 32 bits, "
"and unlike [Vector4] this cannot be configured with an engine build option. "
"Use [int] or [PackedInt64Array] if 64-bit values are needed.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] In a boolean context, a Vector4i will evaluate to [code]false[/"
"code] if it's equal to [code]Vector4i(0, 0, 0, 0)[/code]. Otherwise, a "
"Vector4i will always evaluate to [code]true[/code]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Vector4i.xml
msgid ""
"Constructs a default-initialized [Vector4i] with all components set to "
"[code]0[/code]."
msgstr ""
"Constrói um [Vector4i] inicializado por padrão com todos os componentes "
"definidos como [code]0[/code]."

#: doc/classes/Vector4i.xml
msgid "Constructs a [Vector4i] as a copy of the given [Vector4i]."
msgstr "Constrói um [Vector4i] como uma cópia do [Vector4i] fornecido."

#: doc/classes/Vector4i.xml
msgid ""
"Constructs a new [Vector4i] from the given [Vector4] by truncating "
"components' fractional parts (rounding towards zero). For a different "
"behavior consider passing the result of [method Vector4.ceil], [method "
"Vector4.floor] or [method Vector4.round] to this constructor instead."
msgstr ""
"Constrói um novo [Vector4i] a partir do [Vector4] fornecido truncando as "
"partes fracionárias dos componentes (arredondando em direção a zero). Para "
"um comportamento diferente, considere passar o resultado de [method "
"Vector4.ceil], [method Vector4.floor] ou [method Vector4.round] para este "
"construtor."

#: doc/classes/Vector4i.xml
msgid "Returns a [Vector4i] with the given components."
msgstr "Retorna um [Vector4i] com os componentes fornecidos."

#: doc/classes/Vector4i.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the component-wise maximum of this and [param with], equivalent to "
"[code]Vector4i(maxi(x, with.x), maxi(y, with.y), maxi(z, with.z), maxi(w, "
"with.w))[/code]."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o máximo componente a componente deste e de [param with], "
"equivalente a [code]Vector4i(maxi(x, with.x), maxi(y, with.y), maxi(z, "
"with.z), maxi(w, with.w))[/code]."

#: doc/classes/Vector4i.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the component-wise maximum of this and [param with], equivalent to "
"[code]Vector4i(maxi(x, with), maxi(y, with), maxi(z, with), maxi(w, with))[/"
"code]."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o máximo componente a componente deste e de [param with], "
"equivalente a [code]Vector4i(maxi(x, with), maxi(y, with), maxi(z, with), "
"maxi(w, with))[/code]."

#: doc/classes/Vector4i.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the component-wise minimum of this and [param with], equivalent to "
"[code]Vector4i(mini(x, with.x), mini(y, with.y), mini(z, with.z), mini(w, "
"with.w))[/code]."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o mínimo componente a componente deste e de [param with], "
"equivalente a [code]Vector4i(mini(x, with.x), mini(y, with.y), mini(z, "
"with.z), mini(w, with.w))[/code]."

#: doc/classes/Vector4i.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the component-wise minimum of this and [param with], equivalent to "
"[code]Vector4i(mini(x, with), mini(y, with), mini(z, with), mini(w, with))[/"
"code]."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o mínimo componente a componente deste e de [param with], "
"equivalente a [code]Vector4i(mini(x, with), mini(y, with), mini(z, with), "
"mini(w, with))[/code]."

#: doc/classes/Vector4i.xml
msgid ""
"Min vector, a vector with all components equal to [code]INT32_MIN[/code]. "
"Can be used as a negative integer equivalent of [constant Vector4.INF]."
msgstr ""
"Vetor mínimo, um vetor com todos os componentes iguais a [code]INT32_MIN[/"
"code]. Pode ser usado como um equivalente inteiro negativo de [constant "
"Vector4.INF]."

#: doc/classes/Vector4i.xml
msgid ""
"Max vector, a vector with all components equal to [code]INT32_MAX[/code]. "
"Can be used as an integer equivalent of [constant Vector4.INF]."
msgstr ""
"Vetor máximo, um vetor com todos os componentes iguais a [code]INT32_MAX[/"
"code]. Pode ser usado como um equivalente inteiro de [constant Vector4.INF]."

#: doc/classes/Vector4i.xml
msgid ""
"Gets the remainder of each component of the [Vector4i] with the components "
"of the given [Vector4i]. This operation uses truncated division, which is "
"often not desired as it does not work well with negative numbers. Consider "
"using [method @GlobalScope.posmod] instead if you want to handle negative "
"numbers.\n"
"[codeblock]\n"
"print(Vector4i(10, -20, 30, -40) % Vector4i(7, 8, 9, 10)) # Prints (3, -4, "
"3, 0)\n"
"[/codeblock]"
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Vector4i.xml
msgid ""
"Gets the remainder of each component of the [Vector4i] with the given [int]. "
"This operation uses truncated division, which is often not desired as it "
"does not work well with negative numbers. Consider using [method "
"@GlobalScope.posmod] instead if you want to handle negative numbers.\n"
"[codeblock]\n"
"print(Vector4i(10, -20, 30, -40) % 7) # Prints (3, -6, 2, -5)\n"
"[/codeblock]"
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Vector4i.xml
msgid ""
"Multiplies each component of the [Vector4i] by the components of the given "
"[Vector4i].\n"
"[codeblock]\n"
"print(Vector4i(10, 20, 30, 40) * Vector4i(3, 4, 5, 6)) # Prints (30, 80, "
"150, 240)\n"
"[/codeblock]"
msgstr ""
"Multiplica cada componente do [Vector4i] pelos componentes do [Vector4i] "
"fornecido.\n"
"[codeblock]\n"
"print(Vector4i(10, 20, 30, 40) * Vector4i(3, 4, 5, 6)) # Imprime (30, 80, "
"150, 240)\n"
"[/codeblock]"

#: doc/classes/Vector4i.xml
msgid ""
"Multiplies each component of the [Vector4i] by the given [float].\n"
"Returns a Vector4 value due to floating-point operations.\n"
"[codeblock]\n"
"print(Vector4i(10, 20, 30, 40) * 2) # Prints (20.0, 40.0, 60.0, 80.0)\n"
"[/codeblock]"
msgstr ""
"Multiplica cada componente do [Vector4i] pelo [float] fornecido.\n"
"Retorna um valor [Vector4] devido às operações de ponto flutuante.\n"
"[codeblock]\n"
"print(Vector4i(10, 20, 30, 40) * 2) # Imprime (20.0, 40.0, 60.0, 80.0)\n"
"[/codeblock]"

#: doc/classes/Vector4i.xml
msgid "Multiplies each component of the [Vector4i] by the given [int]."
msgstr "Multiplica cada componente do [Vector4i] pelo [int] fornecido."

#: doc/classes/Vector4i.xml
msgid ""
"Adds each component of the [Vector4i] by the components of the given "
"[Vector4i].\n"
"[codeblock]\n"
"print(Vector4i(10, 20, 30, 40) + Vector4i(3, 4, 5, 6)) # Prints (13, 24, 35, "
"46)\n"
"[/codeblock]"
msgstr ""
"Soma cada componente do [Vector4i] aos componentes do [Vector4i] fornecido.\n"
"[codeblock]\n"
"print(Vector4i(10, 20, 30, 40) + Vector4i(3, 4, 5, 6)) # Exibe (13, 24, 35, "
"46)\n"
"[/codeblock]"

#: doc/classes/Vector4i.xml
msgid ""
"Subtracts each component of the [Vector4i] by the components of the given "
"[Vector4i].\n"
"[codeblock]\n"
"print(Vector4i(10, 20, 30, 40) - Vector4i(3, 4, 5, 6)) # Prints (7, 16, 25, "
"34)\n"
"[/codeblock]"
msgstr ""
"Subtrai de cada componente do [Vector4i] os componentes do [Vector4i] "
"fornecido.\n"
"[codeblock]\n"
"print(Vector4i(10, 20, 30, 40) - Vector4i(3, 4, 5, 6)) # Exibe (7, 16, 25, "
"34)\n"
"[/codeblock]"

#: doc/classes/Vector4i.xml
msgid ""
"Divides each component of the [Vector4i] by the components of the given "
"[Vector4i].\n"
"[codeblock]\n"
"print(Vector4i(10, 20, 30, 40) / Vector4i(2, 5, 3, 4)) # Prints (5, 4, 10, "
"10)\n"
"[/codeblock]"
msgstr ""
"Divide cada componente do [Vector4i] pelos componentes do [Vector4i] "
"fornecido.\n"
"[codeblock]\n"
"print(Vector4i(10, 20, 30, 40) / Vector4i(2, 5, 3, 4)) # Exibe (5, 4, 10, "
"10)\n"
"[/codeblock]"

#: doc/classes/Vector4i.xml
msgid ""
"Divides each component of the [Vector4i] by the given [float].\n"
"Returns a Vector4 value due to floating-point operations.\n"
"[codeblock]\n"
"print(Vector4i(1, 2, 3, 4) / 2.5) # Prints (0.4, 0.8, 1.2, 1.6)\n"
"[/codeblock]"
msgstr ""
"Divide cada componente do [Vector4i] pelo [float] fornecido.\n"
"Retorna um valor [Vector4] devido às operações de ponto flutuante.\n"
"[codeblock]\n"
"print(Vector4i(1, 2, 3, 4) / 2.5) # Exibe (0.4, 0.8, 1.2, 1.6)\n"
"[/codeblock]"

#: doc/classes/Vector4i.xml
msgid "Divides each component of the [Vector4i] by the given [int]."
msgstr "Divide cada componente do [Vector4i] pelo [int] fornecido."

#: doc/classes/Vector4i.xml
msgid ""
"Compares two [Vector4i] vectors by first checking if the X value of the left "
"vector is less than the X value of the [param right] vector. If the X values "
"are exactly equal, then it repeats this check with the Y values of the two "
"vectors, Z values of the two vectors, and then with the W values. This "
"operator is useful for sorting vectors."
msgstr ""
"Compara dois vetores [Vector4i] verificando primeiro se o valor X do vetor "
"esquerdo é menor que o valor X do vetor [param right]. Se os valores X forem "
"exatamente iguais, ele repete esta verificação com os valores Y dos dois "
"vetores, valores Z dos dois vetores e, em seguida, com os valores W. Este "
"operador é útil para ordenar vetores."

#: doc/classes/Vector4i.xml
msgid ""
"Compares two [Vector4i] vectors by first checking if the X value of the left "
"vector is less than or equal to the X value of the [param right] vector. If "
"the X values are exactly equal, then it repeats this check with the Y values "
"of the two vectors, Z values of the two vectors, and then with the W values. "
"This operator is useful for sorting vectors."
msgstr ""
"Compara dois vetores [Vector4i] verificando primeiro se o valor X do vetor "
"da esquerda é menor ou igual ao valor X do vetor [param right]. Se os "
"valores X forem exatamente iguais, ele repete esta verificação com os "
"valores Y dos dois vetores, os valores Z dos dois vetores e, em seguida, com "
"os valores W. Este operador é útil para ordenar vetores."

#: doc/classes/Vector4i.xml
msgid "Returns [code]true[/code] if the vectors are exactly equal."
msgstr "Retorna [code]true[/code] se os vetores forem exatamente iguais."

#: doc/classes/Vector4i.xml
msgid ""
"Compares two [Vector4i] vectors by first checking if the X value of the left "
"vector is greater than the X value of the [param right] vector. If the X "
"values are exactly equal, then it repeats this check with the Y values of "
"the two vectors, Z values of the two vectors, and then with the W values. "
"This operator is useful for sorting vectors."
msgstr ""
"Compara dois vetores [Vector4i] verificando primeiro se o valor X do vetor "
"da esquerda é maior que o valor X do vetor [param right]. Se os valores X "
"forem exatamente iguais, ele repete esta verificação com os valores Y dos "
"dois vetores, os valores Z dos dois vetores e, em seguida, com os valores W. "
"Este operador é útil para ordenar vetores."

#: doc/classes/Vector4i.xml
msgid ""
"Compares two [Vector4i] vectors by first checking if the X value of the left "
"vector is greater than or equal to the X value of the [param right] vector. "
"If the X values are exactly equal, then it repeats this check with the Y "
"values of the two vectors, Z values of the two vectors, and then with the W "
"values. This operator is useful for sorting vectors."
msgstr ""
"Compara dois vetores [Vector4i] verificando primeiro se o valor X do vetor "
"da esquerda é maior ou igual ao valor X do vetor [param right]. Se os "
"valores X forem exatamente iguais, ele repete esta verificação com os "
"valores Y dos dois vetores, os valores Z dos dois vetores e, em seguida, com "
"os valores W. Este operador é útil para ordenar vetores."

#: doc/classes/Vector4i.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the negative value of the [Vector4i]. This is the same as writing "
"[code]Vector4i(-v.x, -v.y, -v.z, -v.w)[/code]. This operation flips the "
"direction of the vector while keeping the same magnitude."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o valor negativo do [Vector4i]. Isso é o mesmo que escrever "
"[code]Vector4i(-v.x, -v.y, -v.z, -v.w)[/code]. Esta operação inverte a "
"direção do vetor mantendo a mesma magnitude."

#: doc/classes/VehicleBody3D.xml
msgid "A 3D physics body that simulates the behavior of a car."
msgstr "Um corpo de física 3D que simula o comportamento de um carro."

#: doc/classes/VehicleBody3D.xml
msgid ""
"This physics body implements all the physics logic needed to simulate a car. "
"It is based on the raycast vehicle system commonly found in physics engines. "
"Aside from a [CollisionShape3D] for the main body of the vehicle, you must "
"also add a [VehicleWheel3D] node for each wheel. You should also add a "
"[MeshInstance3D] to this node for the 3D model of the vehicle, but this "
"model should generally not include meshes for the wheels. You can control "
"the vehicle by using the [member brake], [member engine_force], and [member "
"steering] properties. The position or orientation of this node shouldn't be "
"changed directly.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] The local forward for this node is [constant "
"Vector3.MODEL_FRONT].\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] The origin point of your VehicleBody3D will determine the "
"center of gravity of your vehicle. To make the vehicle more grounded, the "
"origin point is usually kept low, moving the [CollisionShape3D] and "
"[MeshInstance3D] upwards.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] This class has known issues and isn't designed to provide "
"realistic 3D vehicle physics. If you want advanced vehicle physics, you may "
"have to write your own physics integration using [CharacterBody3D] or "
"[RigidBody3D]."
msgstr ""
"Este corpo de física implementa toda a lógica de física necessária para "
"simular um carro. Ele é baseado no sistema de veículo por raycast comumente "
"encontrado em motores de física. Além de um [CollisionShape3D] para o corpo "
"principal do veículo, você também deve adicionar um nó [VehicleWheel3D] para "
"cada roda. Você também deve adicionar um [MeshInstance3D] a este nó para o "
"modelo 3D do veículo, mas este modelo geralmente não deve incluir malhas "
"para as rodas. Você pode controlar o veículo usando as propriedades [member "
"brake], [member engine_force] e [member steering]. A posição ou orientação "
"deste nó não deve ser alterada diretamente.\n"
"[b]Nota:[/b] A frente local para este nó é [constant Vector3.MODEL_FRONT].\n"
"[b]Nota:[/b] O ponto de origem do seu VehicleBody3D determinará o centro de "
"gravidade do seu veículo. Para tornar o veículo mais estável no chão, o "
"ponto de origem geralmente é mantido baixo, movendo o [CollisionShape3D] e o "
"[MeshInstance3D] para cima.\n"
"[b]Nota:[/b] Esta classe possui problemas conhecidos e não foi projetada "
"para fornecer física de veículos 3D realista. Se você quiser física de "
"veículos avançada, talvez precise escrever sua própria integração de física "
"usando [CharacterBody3D] ou [RigidBody3D]."

#: doc/classes/VehicleBody3D.xml
msgid ""
"Slows down the vehicle by applying a braking force. The vehicle is only "
"slowed down if the wheels are in contact with a surface. The force you need "
"to apply to adequately slow down your vehicle depends on the [member "
"RigidBody3D.mass] of the vehicle. For a vehicle with a mass set to 1000, try "
"a value in the 25 - 30 range for hard braking."
msgstr ""
"Desacelera o veículo aplicando uma força de frenagem. O veículo só é "
"desacelerado se as rodas estiverem em contato com uma superfície. A força "
"que você precisa aplicar para desacelerar adequadamente o seu veículo "
"depende do [member RigidBody3D.mass] do veículo. Para um veículo com uma "
"massa definida como 1000, tente um valor na faixa de 25 a 30 para uma "
"frenagem brusca."

#: doc/classes/VehicleBody3D.xml
msgid ""
"Accelerates the vehicle by applying an engine force. The vehicle is only "
"sped up if the wheels that have [member VehicleWheel3D.use_as_traction] set "
"to [code]true[/code] and are in contact with a surface. The [member "
"RigidBody3D.mass] of the vehicle has an effect on the acceleration of the "
"vehicle. For a vehicle with a mass set to 1000, try a value in the 25 - 50 "
"range for acceleration.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] The simulation does not take the effect of gears into account, "
"you will need to add logic for this if you wish to simulate gears.\n"
"A negative value will result in the vehicle reversing."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/VehicleBody3D.xml
msgid ""
"The steering angle for the vehicle. Setting this to a non-zero value will "
"result in the vehicle turning when it's moving. Wheels that have [member "
"VehicleWheel3D.use_as_steering] set to [code]true[/code] will automatically "
"be rotated.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] This property is edited in the inspector in degrees. In code "
"the property is set in radians."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/VehicleWheel3D.xml
msgid ""
"A 3D physics body for a [VehicleBody3D] that simulates the behavior of a "
"wheel."
msgstr ""
"Um corpo físico 3D para um [VehicleBody3D] que simula o comportamento de uma "
"roda."

#: doc/classes/VehicleWheel3D.xml
msgid ""
"A node used as a child of a [VehicleBody3D] parent to simulate the behavior "
"of one of its wheels. This node also acts as a collider to detect if the "
"wheel is touching a surface.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] This class has known issues and isn't designed to provide "
"realistic 3D vehicle physics. If you want advanced vehicle physics, you may "
"need to write your own physics integration using another [PhysicsBody3D] "
"class."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/VehicleWheel3D.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the contacting body node if valid in the tree, as [Node3D]. At the "
"moment, [GridMap] is not supported so the node will be always of type "
"[PhysicsBody3D].\n"
"Returns [code]null[/code] if the wheel is not in contact with a surface, or "
"the contact body is not a [PhysicsBody3D]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/VehicleWheel3D.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the normal of the suspension's collision in world space if the wheel "
"is in contact. If the wheel isn't in contact with anything, returns a vector "
"pointing directly along the suspension axis toward the vehicle in world "
"space."
msgstr ""
"Retorna a normal da colisão da suspensão no espaço global se a roda estiver "
"em contato. Se a roda não estiver em contato com nada, retorna um vetor "
"apontando diretamente ao longo do eixo da suspensão em direção ao veículo no "
"espaço global."

#: doc/classes/VehicleWheel3D.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the point of the suspension's collision in world space if the wheel "
"is in contact. If the wheel isn't in contact with anything, returns the "
"maximum point of the wheel's ray cast in world space, which is defined by "
"[code]wheel_rest_length + wheel_radius[/code]."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o ponto de colisão da suspensão no espaço mundial se a roda estiver "
"em contato. Se a roda não estiver em contato com nada, retorna o ponto "
"máximo do ray cast da roda no espaço mundial, que é definido por "
"[code]wheel_rest_length + wheel_radius[/code]."

#: doc/classes/VehicleWheel3D.xml
msgid "Returns the rotational speed of the wheel in revolutions per minute."
msgstr "Retorna a velocidade de rotação da roda em rotações por minuto."

#: doc/classes/VehicleWheel3D.xml
msgid ""
"Returns a value between 0.0 and 1.0 that indicates whether this wheel is "
"skidding. 0.0 is skidding (the wheel has lost grip, e.g. icy terrain), 1.0 "
"means not skidding (the wheel has full grip, e.g. dry asphalt road)."
msgstr ""
"Retorna um valor entre 0.0 e 1.0 que indica se esta roda está derrapando. "
"0.0 significa derrapando (a roda perdeu aderência, ex.: terreno congelado), "
"1.0 significa sem derrapagem (a roda tem aderência total, ex.: estrada de "
"asfalto seco)."

#: doc/classes/VehicleWheel3D.xml
msgid "Returns [code]true[/code] if this wheel is in contact with a surface."
msgstr ""
"Retorna [code]true[/code] se esta roda estiver em contato com uma superfície."

#: doc/classes/VehicleWheel3D.xml
msgid ""
"Slows down the wheel by applying a braking force. The wheel is only slowed "
"down if it is in contact with a surface. The force you need to apply to "
"adequately slow down your vehicle depends on the [member RigidBody3D.mass] "
"of the vehicle. For a vehicle with a mass set to 1000, try a value in the 25 "
"- 30 range for hard braking."
msgstr ""
"Desacelera a roda aplicando uma força de frenagem. A roda só é desacelerada "
"se estiver em contato com uma superfície. A força que você precisa aplicar "
"para desacelerar adequadamente o seu veículo depende da [member "
"RigidBody3D.mass] do veículo. Para um veículo com massa definida como 1000, "
"tente um valor na faixa de 25 a 30 para uma frenagem brusca."

#: doc/classes/VehicleWheel3D.xml
msgid ""
"The damping applied to the suspension spring when being compressed, meaning "
"when the wheel is moving up relative to the vehicle. It is measured in "
"Newton-seconds per millimeter (N⋅s/mm), or megagrams per second (Mg/s). This "
"value should be between 0.0 (no damping) and 1.0, but may be more. A value "
"of 0.0 means the car will keep bouncing as the spring keeps its energy. A "
"good value for this is around 0.3 for a normal car, 0.5 for a race car."
msgstr ""
"O amortecimento aplicado à mola da suspensão ao ser comprimida, ou seja, "
"quando a roda está se movendo para cima em relação ao veículo. É medido em "
"Newton-segundos por milímetro (N⋅s/mm) ou megagramas por segundo (Mg/s). "
"Este valor deve estar entre 0.0 (sem amortecimento) e 1.0, mas pode ser "
"maior. Um valor de 0.0 significa que o carro continuará quicando enquanto a "
"mola mantiver sua energia. Um bom valor para isso é cerca de 0.3 para um "
"carro normal, 0.5 para um carro de corrida."

#: doc/classes/VehicleWheel3D.xml
msgid ""
"The damping applied to the suspension spring when rebounding or extending, "
"meaning when the wheel is moving down relative to the vehicle. It is "
"measured in Newton-seconds per millimeter (N⋅s/mm), or megagrams per second "
"(Mg/s). This value should be between 0.0 (no damping) and 1.0, but may be "
"more. This value should always be slightly higher than the [member "
"damping_compression] property. For a [member damping_compression] value of "
"0.3, try a relaxation value of 0.5."
msgstr ""
"O amortecimento aplicado à mola da suspensão ao retornar ou estender, ou "
"seja, quando a roda está se movendo para baixo em relação ao veículo. É "
"medido em Newton-segundos por milímetro (N⋅s/mm) ou megagramas por segundo "
"(Mg/s). Este valor deve estar entre 0.0 (sem amortecimento) e 1.0, mas pode "
"ser maior. Este valor deve ser sempre ligeiramente superior à propriedade "
"[member damping_compression]. Para um valor de [member damping_compression] "
"de 0.3, tente um valor de relaxamento de 0.5."

#: doc/classes/VehicleWheel3D.xml
msgid ""
"Accelerates the wheel by applying an engine force. The wheel is only sped up "
"if it is in contact with a surface. The [member RigidBody3D.mass] of the "
"vehicle has an effect on the acceleration of the vehicle. For a vehicle with "
"a mass set to 1000, try a value in the 25 - 50 range for acceleration.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] The simulation does not take the effect of gears into account, "
"you will need to add logic for this if you wish to simulate gears.\n"
"A negative value will result in the wheel reversing."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/VehicleWheel3D.xml
msgid ""
"The steering angle for the wheel, in radians. Setting this to a non-zero "
"value will result in the vehicle turning when it's moving."
msgstr ""
"O ângulo de direção (steering angle) para a roda, em radianos. Definir isso "
"como um valor diferente de zero fará com que o veículo faça curvas quando "
"estiver em movimento."

#: doc/classes/VehicleWheel3D.xml
msgid ""
"The maximum force the spring can resist. This value should be higher than a "
"quarter of the [member RigidBody3D.mass] of the [VehicleBody3D] or the "
"spring will not carry the weight of the vehicle. Good results are often "
"obtained by a value that is about 3× to 4× this number."
msgstr ""
"A força máxima que a mola pode resistir. Este valor deve ser maior que um "
"quarto da [member RigidBody3D.mass] do [VehicleBody3D] ou a mola não "
"suportará o peso do veículo. Bons resultados são frequentemente obtidos por "
"um valor que seja cerca de 3× a 4× este número."

#: doc/classes/VehicleWheel3D.xml
msgid ""
"The stiffness of the suspension, measured in Newtons per millimeter (N/mm), "
"or megagrams per second squared (Mg/s²). Use a value lower than 50 for an "
"off-road car, a value between 50 and 100 for a race car and try something "
"around 200 for something like a Formula 1 car."
msgstr ""
"A rigidez da suspensão, medida em Newtons por milímetro (N/mm) ou megagramas "
"por segundo ao quadrado (Mg/s²). Use um valor inferior a 50 para um carro "
"off-road, um valor entre 50 e 100 para um carro de corrida e tente algo em "
"torno de 200 para algo como um carro de Fórmula 1."

#: doc/classes/VehicleWheel3D.xml
msgid ""
"This is the distance the suspension can travel. As Godot units are "
"equivalent to meters, keep this setting relatively low. Try a value between "
"0.1 and 0.3 depending on the type of car."
msgstr ""
"Esta é a distância que a suspensão pode percorrer. Como as unidades do Godot "
"são equivalentes a metros, mantenha essa configuração relativamente baixa. "
"Tente um valor entre 0,1 e 0,3 dependendo do tipo de carro."

#: doc/classes/VehicleWheel3D.xml
msgid ""
"If [code]true[/code], this wheel will be turned when the car steers. This "
"value is used in conjunction with [member VehicleBody3D.steering] and "
"ignored if you are using the per-wheel [member steering] value instead."
msgstr ""
"Se [code]true[/code], esta roda será esterçada quando o carro virar. Este "
"valor é usado em conjunto com [member VehicleBody3D.steering] e ignorado se "
"você estiver usando o valor de [member steering] por roda."

#: doc/classes/VehicleWheel3D.xml
msgid ""
"If [code]true[/code], this wheel transfers engine force to the ground to "
"propel the vehicle forward. This value is used in conjunction with [member "
"VehicleBody3D.engine_force] and ignored if you are using the per-wheel "
"[member engine_force] value instead."
msgstr ""
"Se [code]true[/code], esta roda transfere força do motor para o solo para "
"impulsionar o veículo para frente. Este valor é usado em conjunto com "
"[member VehicleBody3D.engine_force] e é ignorado se você estiver usando o "
"valor de [member engine_force] por roda."

#: doc/classes/VehicleWheel3D.xml
msgid ""
"This determines how much grip this wheel has. It is combined with the "
"friction setting of the surface the wheel is in contact with. 0.0 means no "
"grip, 1.0 is normal grip. For a drift car setup, try setting the grip of the "
"rear wheels slightly lower than the front wheels, or use a lower value to "
"simulate tire wear.\n"
"It's best to set this to 1.0 when starting out."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/VehicleWheel3D.xml
msgid "The radius of the wheel in meters."
msgstr "O raio da roda em metros."

#: doc/classes/VehicleWheel3D.xml
msgid ""
"This is the distance in meters the wheel is lowered from its origin point. "
"Don't set this to 0.0 and move the wheel into position, instead move the "
"origin point of your wheel (the gizmo in Godot) to the position the wheel "
"will take when bottoming out, then use the rest length to move the wheel "
"down to the position it should be in when the car is in rest."
msgstr ""
"Esta é a distância em metros que a roda é abaixada a partir de seu ponto de "
"origem. Não defina isso como 0.0 e mova a roda para a posição; em vez disso, "
"mova o ponto de origem da sua roda (o gizmo no Godot) para a posição que a "
"roda assumirá quando atingir o limite máximo, e então use o comprimento de "
"repouso para abaixar a roda para a posição em que ela deve estar quando o "
"carro estiver em repouso."

#: doc/classes/VehicleWheel3D.xml
msgid ""
"This value affects the roll of your vehicle. If set to 1.0 for all wheels, "
"your vehicle will resist body roll, while a value of 0.0 will be prone to "
"rolling over."
msgstr ""
"Este valor afeta a rolagem do seu veículo. Se definido como 1.0 para todas "
"as rodas, seu veículo resistirá à rolagem da carroceria, enquanto um valor "
"de 0.0 será propenso a capotar."

#: doc/classes/VFlowContainer.xml
msgid ""
"A container that arranges its child controls vertically and wraps them "
"around at the borders."
msgstr ""
"Um contêiner que organiza seus controles filhos verticalmente e os quebra "
"nas bordas."

#: doc/classes/VFlowContainer.xml
msgid ""
"A variant of [FlowContainer] that can only arrange its child controls "
"vertically, wrapping them around at the borders. This is similar to how text "
"in a book wraps around when no more words can fit on a line, except "
"vertically."
msgstr ""
"Uma variante de [FlowContainer] que só pode organizar seus controles filhos "
"verticalmente, quebrando-os nas bordas. Isso é semelhante a como o texto em "
"um livro se ajusta quando não cabem mais palavras em uma linha, exceto que "
"verticalmente."

#: doc/classes/VideoStream.xml
msgid "Base resource for video streams."
msgstr "Recurso base para fluxos de vídeo."

#: doc/classes/VideoStream.xml
msgid ""
"Base resource type for all video streams. Classes that derive from "
"[VideoStream] can all be used as resource types to play back videos in "
"[VideoStreamPlayer]."
msgstr ""
"Tipo de recurso base para todos os fluxos de vídeo. Todas as classes "
"derivadas de [VideoStream] podem ser usadas como tipos de recursos para "
"reproduzir vídeos em [VideoStreamPlayer]."

#: doc/classes/VideoStream.xml doc/classes/VideoStreamPlayer.xml
msgid "Playing videos"
msgstr "Reproduzindo videos"

#: doc/classes/VideoStream.xml
msgid ""
"Called when the video starts playing, to initialize and return a subclass of "
"[VideoStreamPlayback]."
msgstr ""
"Chamado quando o vídeo começa a ser reproduzido, para inicializar e retornar "
"uma subclasse de [VideoStreamPlayback]."

#: doc/classes/VideoStream.xml
msgid ""
"The video file path or URI that this [VideoStream] resource handles.\n"
"For [VideoStreamTheora], this filename should be an Ogg Theora video file "
"with the [code].ogv[/code] extension."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/VideoStreamPlayback.xml
msgid ""
"Internal class used by [VideoStream] to manage playback state when played "
"from a [VideoStreamPlayer]."
msgstr ""
"Classe interna usada por [VideoStream] para gerenciar o estado de reprodução "
"quando reproduzido a partir de um [VideoStreamPlayer]."

#: doc/classes/VideoStreamPlayback.xml
msgid ""
"This class is intended to be overridden by video decoder extensions with "
"custom implementations of [VideoStream]."
msgstr ""
"Esta classe destina-se a ser substituída por extensões de decodificador de "
"vídeo com implementações personalizadas de [VideoStream]."

#: doc/classes/VideoStreamPlayback.xml
msgid "Returns the number of audio channels."
msgstr "Retorna o número de canais de áudio."

#: doc/classes/VideoStreamPlayback.xml
msgid "Returns the video duration in seconds, if known, or 0 if unknown."
msgstr ""
"Retorna a duração do vídeo em segundos, se conhecida, ou 0 se desconhecida."

#: doc/classes/VideoStreamPlayback.xml
msgid "Returns the audio sample rate used for mixing."
msgstr "Retorna a taxa de amostragem de áudio usada para a mixagem."

#: doc/classes/VideoStreamPlayback.xml
msgid ""
"Return the current playback timestamp. Called in response to the [member "
"VideoStreamPlayer.stream_position] getter."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o carimbo de tempo atual de reprodução. Chamado em resposta ao "
"getter de [member VideoStreamPlayer.stream_position]."

#: doc/classes/VideoStreamPlayback.xml
msgid "Allocates a [Texture2D] in which decoded video frames will be drawn."
msgstr ""
"Aloca um [Texture2D] no qual os quadros de vídeo decodificados serão "
"desenhados."

#: doc/classes/VideoStreamPlayback.xml
msgid "Returns the paused status, as set by [method _set_paused]."
msgstr "Retorna o status de pausa, conforme definido por [method _set_paused]."

#: doc/classes/VideoStreamPlayback.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the playback state, as determined by calls to [method _play] and "
"[method _stop]."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o estado de reprodução, conforme determinado por chamadas a [method "
"_play] e [method _stop]."

#: doc/classes/VideoStreamPlayback.xml
msgid ""
"Called in response to [member VideoStreamPlayer.autoplay] or [method "
"VideoStreamPlayer.play]. Note that manual playback may also invoke [method "
"_stop] multiple times before this method is called. [method _is_playing] "
"should return [code]true[/code] once playing."
msgstr ""
"Chamado em resposta a [member VideoStreamPlayer.autoplay] ou [method "
"VideoStreamPlayer.play]. Observe que a reprodução manual também pode invocar "
"[method _stop] várias vezes antes que este método seja chamado. [method "
"_is_playing] deve retornar [code]true[/code] assim que estiver reproduzindo."

#: doc/classes/VideoStreamPlayback.xml
msgid ""
"Seeks to [param time] seconds. Called in response to the [member "
"VideoStreamPlayer.stream_position] setter."
msgstr ""
"Move para [param time] segundos. Chamado em resposta ao setter de [member "
"VideoStreamPlayer.stream_position]."

#: doc/classes/VideoStreamPlayback.xml
msgid ""
"Select the audio track [param idx]. Called when playback starts, and in "
"response to the [member VideoStreamPlayer.audio_track] setter."
msgstr ""
"Seleciona a faixa de áudio [param idx]. Chamado quando a reprodução começa e "
"em resposta ao método de configuração (setter) de [member "
"VideoStreamPlayer.audio_track]."

#: doc/classes/VideoStreamPlayback.xml
msgid ""
"Set the paused status of video playback. [method _is_paused] must return "
"[param paused]. Called in response to the [member VideoStreamPlayer.paused] "
"setter."
msgstr ""
"Define o status de pausa da reprodução de vídeo. [method _is_paused] deve "
"retornar [param paused]. Chamado em resposta ao setter [member "
"VideoStreamPlayer.paused]."

#: doc/classes/VideoStreamPlayback.xml
msgid ""
"Stops playback. May be called multiple times before [method _play], or in "
"response to [method VideoStreamPlayer.stop]. [method _is_playing] should "
"return [code]false[/code] once stopped."
msgstr ""
"Interrompe a reprodução. Pode ser chamado várias vezes antes de [method "
"_play], ou em resposta a [method VideoStreamPlayer.stop]. [method "
"_is_playing] deve retornar [code]false[/code] uma vez interrompido."

#: doc/classes/VideoStreamPlayback.xml
msgid ""
"Ticks video playback for [param delta] seconds. Called every frame as long "
"as both [method _is_paused] and [method _is_playing] return [code]true[/"
"code]."
msgstr ""
"Executa o tick da reprodução de vídeo por [param delta] segundos. Chamado a "
"cada quadro, desde que [method _is_paused] e [method _is_playing] retornem "
"[code]true[/code]."

#: doc/classes/VideoStreamPlayback.xml
msgid ""
"Render [param num_frames] audio frames (of [method _get_channels] floats "
"each) from [param buffer], starting from index [param offset] in the array. "
"Returns the number of audio frames rendered, or -1 on error."
msgstr ""
"Renderiza [param num_frames] quadros de áudio (de [method _get_channels] "
"floats cada) a partir do [param buffer], começando no índice [param offset] "
"no array. Retorna o número de quadros de áudio renderizados ou -1 em caso de "
"erro."

#: doc/classes/VideoStreamPlayer.xml
msgid "A control used for video playback."
msgstr "Um controle usado para reprodução de vídeo."

#: doc/classes/VideoStreamPlayer.xml
msgid ""
"A control used for playback of [VideoStream] resources.\n"
"Supported video formats are [url=https://www.theora.org/]Ogg Theora[/url] "
"([code].ogv[/code], [VideoStreamTheora]) and any format exposed via a "
"GDExtension plugin.\n"
"[b]Warning:[/b] On Web, video playback [i]will[/i] perform poorly due to "
"missing architecture-specific assembly optimizations."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/VideoStreamPlayer.xml
msgid "The length of the current stream, in seconds."
msgstr "A duração do fluxo atual, em segundos."

#: doc/classes/VideoStreamPlayer.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the video stream's name, or [code]\"<No Stream>\"[/code] if no video "
"stream is assigned."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o nome do fluxo de vídeo ou [code]\"<No Stream>\"[/code] se nenhum "
"fluxo de vídeo estiver atribuído."

#: doc/classes/VideoStreamPlayer.xml
msgid "Returns the current frame as a [Texture2D]."
msgstr "Retorna o quadro atual como um [Texture2D]."

#: doc/classes/VideoStreamPlayer.xml
msgid ""
"Returns [code]true[/code] if the video is playing.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] The video is still considered playing if paused during playback."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/VideoStreamPlayer.xml
msgid ""
"Starts the video playback from the beginning. If the video is paused, this "
"will not unpause the video."
msgstr ""
"Inicia a reprodução do vídeo do início. Se o vídeo estiver pausado, isso não "
"despausará o vídeo."

#: doc/classes/VideoStreamPlayer.xml
msgid ""
"Stops the video playback and sets the stream position to 0.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Although the stream position will be set to 0, the first frame "
"of the video stream won't become the current frame."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/VideoStreamPlayer.xml
msgid "The embedded audio track to play."
msgstr "A faixa de áudio embutida a ser reproduzida."

#: doc/classes/VideoStreamPlayer.xml
msgid "If [code]true[/code], playback starts when the scene loads."
msgstr "Se [code]true[/code], a reprodução começa quando a cena é carregada."

#: doc/classes/VideoStreamPlayer.xml
msgid "Amount of time in milliseconds to store in buffer while playing."
msgstr ""
"Quantidade de tempo em milissegundos para armazenar no buffer durante a "
"reprodução."

#: doc/classes/VideoStreamPlayer.xml
msgid "Audio bus to use for sound playback."
msgstr "Barramento de áudio a ser usado para reprodução de som."

#: doc/classes/VideoStreamPlayer.xml
msgid ""
"If [code]true[/code], the video scales to the control size. Otherwise, the "
"control minimum size will be automatically adjusted to match the video "
"stream's dimensions."
msgstr ""
"Se [code]true[/code], o vídeo é dimensionado para o tamanho do controle. "
"Caso contrário, o tamanho mínimo do controle será ajustado automaticamente "
"para corresponder às dimensões do fluxo de vídeo."

#: doc/classes/VideoStreamPlayer.xml
msgid "If [code]true[/code], the video restarts when it reaches its end."
msgstr "Se [code]true[/code], o vídeo reinicia quando chega ao fim."

#: doc/classes/VideoStreamPlayer.xml
msgid "If [code]true[/code], the video is paused."
msgstr "Se [code]true[/code], o vídeo está pausado."

#: doc/classes/VideoStreamPlayer.xml
msgid ""
"The stream's current speed scale. [code]1.0[/code] is the normal speed, "
"while [code]2.0[/code] is double speed and [code]0.5[/code] is half speed. A "
"speed scale of [code]0.0[/code] pauses the video, similar to setting [member "
"paused] to [code]true[/code]."
msgstr ""
"A escala de velocidade atual do fluxo. [code]1.0[/code] é a velocidade "
"normal, enquanto [code]2.0[/code] é o dobro da velocidade e [code]0.5[/code] "
"é metade da velocidade. Uma escala de velocidade de [code]0.0[/code] pausa o "
"vídeo, de forma semelhante a definir [member paused] como [code]true[/code]."

#: doc/classes/VideoStreamPlayer.xml
msgid "The assigned video stream. See description for supported formats."
msgstr ""
"O fluxo de vídeo atribuído. Consulte a descrição para os formatos suportados."

#: doc/classes/VideoStreamPlayer.xml
msgid "The current position of the stream, in seconds."
msgstr "A posição atual do fluxo, em segundos."

#: doc/classes/VideoStreamPlayer.xml
msgid "Audio volume as a linear value."
msgstr "Volume do áudio como um valor linear."

#: doc/classes/VideoStreamPlayer.xml
msgid "Audio volume in dB."
msgstr "Volume do áudio em dB."

#: doc/classes/VideoStreamPlayer.xml
msgid "Emitted when playback is finished."
msgstr "Emitido quando a reprodução termina."

#: modules/theora/doc_classes/VideoStreamTheora.xml
msgid "[VideoStream] resource for Ogg Theora videos."
msgstr "Recurso [VideoStream] para vídeos Ogg Theora."

#: modules/theora/doc_classes/VideoStreamTheora.xml
msgid ""
"[VideoStream] resource handling the [url=https://www.theora.org/]Ogg Theora[/"
"url] video format with [code].ogv[/code] extension. The Theora codec is "
"decoded on the CPU.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] While Ogg Theora videos can also have a [code].ogg[/code] "
"extension, you will have to rename the extension to [code].ogv[/code] to use "
"those videos within Godot."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"Abstract base class for viewports. Encapsulates drawing and interaction with "
"a game world."
msgstr ""
"Classe base abstrata para viewports. Encapsula o desenho e a interação com "
"um mundo de jogo."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"A [Viewport] creates a different view into the screen, or a sub-view inside "
"another viewport. Child 2D nodes will display on it, and child Camera3D 3D "
"nodes will render on it too.\n"
"Optionally, a viewport can have its own 2D or 3D world, so it doesn't share "
"what it draws with other viewports.\n"
"Viewports can also choose to be audio listeners, so they generate positional "
"audio depending on a 2D or 3D camera child of it.\n"
"Also, viewports can be assigned to different screens in case the devices "
"have multiple screens.\n"
"Finally, viewports can also behave as render targets, in which case they "
"will not be visible unless the associated texture is used to draw."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the first valid [World2D] for this viewport, searching the [member "
"world_2d] property of itself and any Viewport ancestor."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o primeiro [World2D] válido para este viewport, pesquisando a "
"propriedade [member world_2d] de si mesmo e de qualquer ancestral Viewport."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the first valid [World3D] for this viewport, searching the [member "
"world_3d] property of itself and any Viewport ancestor."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o primeiro [World3D] válido para este viewport, pesquisando a "
"propriedade [member world_3d] de si mesmo e de qualquer ancestral Viewport."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the currently active 2D audio listener. Returns [code]null[/code] if "
"there are no active 2D audio listeners, in which case the active 2D camera "
"will be treated as listener."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o ouvinte de áudio 2D atualmente ativo. Retorna [code]null[/code] se "
"não houver ouvintes de áudio 2D ativos, caso em que a câmera 2D ativa será "
"tratada como ouvinte."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the currently active 3D audio listener. Returns [code]null[/code] if "
"there are no active 3D audio listeners, in which case the active 3D camera "
"will be treated as listener."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o ouvinte de áudio 3D atualmente ativo. Retorna [code]null[/code] se "
"não houver ouvintes de áudio 3D ativos, caso em que a câmera 3D ativa será "
"tratada como ouvinte."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the currently active 2D camera. Returns [code]null[/code] if there "
"are no active cameras.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] If called while the [i]Camera Override[/i] system is active in "
"editor, this will return the internally managed override camera. It is "
"therefore advised to avoid caching the return value, or to check that the "
"cached value is still a valid instance and is the current camera before use. "
"See [method @GlobalScope.is_instance_valid] and [method Camera2D.is_current]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the currently active 3D camera. Returns [code]null[/code] if there "
"are no active cameras.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] If called while the [i]Camera Override[/i] system is active in "
"editor, this will return the internally managed override camera. It is "
"therefore advised to avoid caching the return value, or to check that the "
"cached value is a valid instance and is the current camera before use. See "
"[method @GlobalScope.is_instance_valid] and [member Camera3D.current]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid "Returns an individual bit on the rendering layer mask."
msgstr "Retorna um bit individual na máscara da camada de renderização."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"Returns a list of the visible embedded [Window]s inside the viewport.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] [Window]s inside other viewports will not be listed."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the transform from the viewport's coordinate system to the "
"embedder's coordinate system."
msgstr ""
"Retorna a transformação do sistema de coordenadas do viewport para o sistema "
"de coordenadas do incorporador."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the mouse's position in this [Viewport] using the coordinate system "
"of this [Viewport]."
msgstr ""
"Retorna a posição do mouse nesta [Viewport] usando o sistema de coordenadas "
"desta [Viewport]."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid "Returns viewport oversampling factor."
msgstr "Retorna o fator de sobreamostragem da janela de visualização."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the positional shadow atlas quadrant subdivision of the specified "
"quadrant."
msgstr ""
"Retorna a subdivisão do quadrante do atlas de sombras posicional do "
"quadrante especificado."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid "Returns rendering statistics of the given type."
msgstr "Retorna estatísticas de renderização do tipo fornecido."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the transform from the Viewport's coordinates to the screen "
"coordinates of the containing window manager window."
msgstr ""
"Retorna a transformação das coordenadas do Viewport para as coordenadas de "
"tela da janela do gerenciador de janelas contenedora."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the automatically computed 2D stretch transform, taking the "
"[Viewport]'s stretch settings into account. The final value is multiplied by "
"[member Window.content_scale_factor], but only for the root viewport. If "
"this method is called on a [SubViewport] (e.g., in a scene tree with "
"[SubViewportContainer] and [SubViewport]), the scale factor of the root "
"window will not be applied. Using [method Transform2D.get_scale] on the "
"returned value, this can be used to compensate for scaling when zooming a "
"[Camera2D] node, or to scale down a [TextureRect] to be pixel-perfect "
"regardless of the automatically computed scale factor.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Due to how pixel scaling works, the returned transform's X and "
"Y scale may differ slightly, even when [member Window.content_scale_aspect] "
"is set to a mode that preserves the pixels' aspect ratio. If [member "
"Window.content_scale_aspect] is [constant "
"Window.CONTENT_SCALE_ASPECT_IGNORE], the X and Y scale may differ "
"[i]significantly[/i]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the viewport's texture.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] When trying to store the current texture (e.g. in a file), it "
"might be completely black or outdated if used too early, especially when "
"used in e.g. [method Node._ready]. To make sure the texture you get is "
"correct, you can await [signal RenderingServer.frame_post_draw] signal.\n"
"[codeblocks]\n"
"[gdscript]\n"
"func _ready():\n"
"    await RenderingServer.frame_post_draw\n"
"    $Viewport.get_texture().get_image().save_png(\"user://Screenshot.png\")\n"
"[/gdscript]\n"
"[csharp]\n"
"public async override void _Ready()\n"
"{\n"
"    await ToSignal(RenderingServer.Singleton, "
"RenderingServer.SignalName.FramePostDraw);\n"
"    var viewport = GetNode<Viewport>(\"Viewport\");\n"
"    viewport.GetTexture().GetImage().SavePng(\"user://Screenshot.png\");\n"
"}\n"
"[/csharp]\n"
"[/codeblocks]\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] When [member use_hdr_2d] is [code]true[/code] the returned "
"texture will be an HDR image using linear encoding."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid "Returns the viewport's RID from the [RenderingServer]."
msgstr "Retorna o RID da viewport do [RenderingServer]."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid "Returns the visible rectangle in global screen coordinates."
msgstr "Retorna o retângulo visível em coordenadas globais de tela."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"Cancels the drag operation that was previously started through [method "
"Control._get_drag_data] or forced with [method Control.force_drag]."
msgstr ""
"Cancela a operação de arrastar que foi iniciada anteriormente através de "
"[method Control._get_drag_data] ou forçada com [method Control.force_drag]."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the drag data from the GUI, that was previously returned by [method "
"Control._get_drag_data]."
msgstr ""
"Retorna os dados de arrastar da GUI, que foram retornados anteriormente por "
"[method Control._get_drag_data]."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the human-readable description of the drag data, used for assistive "
"apps."
msgstr ""
"Retorna a descrição legível por humanos dos dados de arrastar, usada por "
"aplicativos assistivos."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the currently focused [Control] within this viewport. If no "
"[Control] is focused, returns [code]null[/code]."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o [Control] atualmente focado dentro deste viewport. Se nenhum "
"[Control] estiver focado, retorna [code]null[/code]."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the [Control] that the mouse is currently hovering over in this "
"viewport. If no [Control] has the cursor, returns [code]null[/code].\n"
"Typically the leaf [Control] node or deepest level of the subtree which "
"claims hover. This is very useful when used together with [method "
"Node.is_ancestor_of] to find if the mouse is within a control tree."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid "Returns [code]true[/code] if the drag operation is successful."
msgstr "Retorna [code]true[/code] se a operação de arrastar for bem-sucedida."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"Returns [code]true[/code] if a drag operation is currently ongoing and where "
"the drop action could happen in this viewport.\n"
"Alternative to [constant Node.NOTIFICATION_DRAG_BEGIN] and [constant "
"Node.NOTIFICATION_DRAG_END] when you prefer polling the value."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"Removes the focus from the currently focused [Control] within this viewport. "
"If no [Control] has the focus, does nothing."
msgstr ""
"Remove o foco do [Control] atualmente focado dentro deste viewport. Se "
"nenhum [Control] tiver o foco, não faz nada."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"Sets the human-readable description of the drag data to [param description], "
"used for assistive apps."
msgstr ""
"Define a descrição legível por humanos dos dados de arrastar para [param "
"description], usada por aplicativos assistivos."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"Returns whether the current [InputEvent] has been handled. Input events are "
"not handled until [method set_input_as_handled] has been called during the "
"lifetime of an [InputEvent].\n"
"This is usually done as part of input handling methods like [method "
"Node._input], [method Control._gui_input] or others, as well as in "
"corresponding signal handlers.\n"
"If [member handle_input_locally] is set to [code]false[/code], this method "
"will try finding the first parent viewport that is set to handle input "
"locally, and return its value for [method is_input_handled] instead."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"Inform the Viewport that the mouse has entered its area. Use this function "
"before sending an [InputEventMouseButton] or [InputEventMouseMotion] to the "
"[Viewport] with [method Viewport.push_input]. See also [method "
"notify_mouse_exited].\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] In most cases, it is not necessary to call this function "
"because [SubViewport] nodes that are children of [SubViewportContainer] are "
"notified automatically. This is only necessary when interacting with "
"viewports in non-default ways, for example as textures in [TextureRect] or "
"with an [Area3D] that forwards input events."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"Inform the Viewport that the mouse has left its area. Use this function when "
"the node that displays the viewport notices the mouse has left the area of "
"the displayed viewport. See also [method notify_mouse_entered].\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] In most cases, it is not necessary to call this function "
"because [SubViewport] nodes that are children of [SubViewportContainer] are "
"notified automatically. This is only necessary when interacting with "
"viewports in non-default ways, for example as textures in [TextureRect] or "
"with an [Area3D] that forwards input events."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"Triggers the given [param event] in this [Viewport]. This can be used to "
"pass an [InputEvent] between viewports, or to locally apply inputs that were "
"sent over the network or saved to a file.\n"
"If [param in_local_coords] is [code]false[/code], the event's position is in "
"the embedder's coordinates and will be converted to viewport coordinates. If "
"[param in_local_coords] is [code]true[/code], the event's position is in "
"viewport coordinates.\n"
"While this method serves a similar purpose as [method "
"Input.parse_input_event], it does not remap the specified [param event] "
"based on project settings like [member ProjectSettings.input_devices/"
"pointing/emulate_touch_from_mouse].\n"
"Calling this method will propagate calls to child nodes for following "
"methods in the given order:\n"
"- [method Node._input]\n"
"- [method Control._gui_input] for [Control] nodes\n"
"- [method Node._shortcut_input]\n"
"- [method Node._unhandled_key_input]\n"
"- [method Node._unhandled_input]\n"
"If an earlier method marks the input as handled via [method "
"set_input_as_handled], any later method in this list will not be called.\n"
"If none of the methods handle the event and [member physics_object_picking] "
"is [code]true[/code], the event is used for physics object picking."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"Helper method which calls the [code]set_text()[/code] method on the "
"currently focused [Control], provided that it is defined (e.g. if the "
"focused Control is [Button] or [LineEdit])."
msgstr ""
"Método auxiliar que chama o método [code]set_text()[/code] no [Control] "
"atualmente em foco, desde que esteja definido (por exemplo, se o Control em "
"foco for [Button] ou [LineEdit])."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid "Use [method push_input] instead."
msgstr "Use [method push_input] em vez disso."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"Triggers the given [param event] in this [Viewport]. This can be used to "
"pass an [InputEvent] between viewports, or to locally apply inputs that were "
"sent over the network or saved to a file.\n"
"If [param in_local_coords] is [code]false[/code], the event's position is in "
"the embedder's coordinates and will be converted to viewport coordinates. If "
"[param in_local_coords] is [code]true[/code], the event's position is in "
"viewport coordinates.\n"
"Calling this method will propagate calls to child nodes for following "
"methods in the given order:\n"
"- [method Node._shortcut_input]\n"
"- [method Node._unhandled_key_input]\n"
"- [method Node._unhandled_input]\n"
"If an earlier method marks the input as handled via [method "
"set_input_as_handled], any later method in this list will not be called.\n"
"If none of the methods handle the event and [member physics_object_picking] "
"is [code]true[/code], the event is used for physics object picking.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] This method doesn't propagate input events to embedded "
"[Window]s or [SubViewport]s."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"Set/clear individual bits on the rendering layer mask. This simplifies "
"editing this [Viewport]'s layers."
msgstr ""
"Defina/limpe os bits individuais na máscara da camada de renderização. Isso "
"simplifica a edição desta camada [Viewport]."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"Stops the input from propagating further up the [SceneTree].\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] This does not affect the methods in [Input], only the way "
"events are propagated."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"Sets the number of subdivisions to use in the specified quadrant. A higher "
"number of subdivisions allows you to have more shadows in the scene at once, "
"but reduces the quality of the shadows. A good practice is to have quadrants "
"with a varying number of subdivisions and to have as few subdivisions as "
"possible."
msgstr ""
"Define o número de subdivisões a serem usadas no quadrante especificado. Um "
"número maior de subdivisões permite ter mais sombras na cena ao mesmo tempo, "
"mas reduz a qualidade das sombras. Uma boa prática é ter quadrantes com um "
"número variável de subdivisões e ter o mínimo de subdivisões possível."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"Force instantly updating the display based on the current mouse cursor "
"position. This includes updating the mouse cursor shape and sending "
"necessary [signal Control.mouse_entered], [signal "
"CollisionObject2D.mouse_entered], [signal CollisionObject3D.mouse_entered] "
"and [signal Window.mouse_entered] signals and their respective "
"[code]mouse_exited[/code] counterparts."
msgstr ""
"Força a atualização instantânea da exibição com base na posição atual do "
"cursor do mouse. Isso inclui atualizar a forma do cursor do mouse e enviar "
"os sinais necessários [signal Control.mouse_entered], [signal "
"CollisionObject2D.mouse_entered], [signal CollisionObject3D.mouse_entered] e "
"[signal Window.mouse_entered] e suas respectivas contrapartes "
"[code]mouse_exited[/code]."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"Moves the mouse pointer to the specified position in this [Viewport] using "
"the coordinate system of this [Viewport].\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] [method warp_mouse] is only supported on Windows, macOS and "
"Linux. It has no effect on Android, iOS and Web."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid "If [code]true[/code], the viewport will process 2D audio streams."
msgstr "Se [code]true[/code], a viewport processará fluxos de áudio 2D."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid "If [code]true[/code], the viewport will process 3D audio streams."
msgstr "Se [code]true[/code], a viewport processará fluxos de áudio 3D."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"The rendering layers in which this [Viewport] renders [CanvasItem] nodes.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] A [CanvasItem] does not inherit its parents' visibility layers. "
"See [member CanvasItem.visibility_layer]'s description for details."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid "The default filter mode used by [CanvasItem] nodes in this viewport."
msgstr "O modo de filtro padrão usado por nós [CanvasItem] nesta viewport."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid "The default repeat mode used by [CanvasItem] nodes in this viewport."
msgstr "O modo de repetição padrão usado por nós [CanvasItem] nesta viewport."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"The canvas transform of the viewport, useful for changing the on-screen "
"positions of all child [CanvasItem]s. This is relative to the global canvas "
"transform of the viewport."
msgstr ""
"A transformação de canvas da viewport, útil para alterar as posições na tela "
"de todos os [CanvasItem]s filhos. Isso é relativo à transformação de canvas "
"global da viewport."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid "The overlay mode for test rendered geometry in debug purposes."
msgstr ""
"O modo de sobreposição para geometria de teste renderizada para fins de "
"depuração."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid "Disable 3D rendering (but keep 2D rendering)."
msgstr "Desativa a renderização 3D (mas mantém a renderização 2D)."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"Determines how sharp the upscaled image will be when using the FSR upscaling "
"mode. Sharpness halves with every whole number. Values go from 0.0 "
"(sharpest) to 2.0. Values above 2.0 won't make a visible difference.\n"
"To control this property on the root viewport, set the [member "
"ProjectSettings.rendering/scaling_3d/fsr_sharpness] project setting."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"The global canvas transform of the viewport. The canvas transform is "
"relative to this."
msgstr ""
"A transformação de canvas global do viewport. A transformação de canvas é "
"relativa a isso."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid "If [code]true[/code], the viewport will not receive input events."
msgstr "Se [code]true[/code], a viewport não receberá eventos de entrada."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"The minimum distance the mouse cursor must move while pressed before a drag "
"operation begins."
msgstr ""
"A distância mínima que o cursor do mouse deve se mover enquanto pressionado "
"antes que uma operação de arrastar comece."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"If [code]true[/code], sub-windows (popups and dialogs) will be embedded "
"inside application window as control-like nodes. If [code]false[/code], they "
"will appear as separate windows handled by the operating system."
msgstr ""
"Se [code]true[/code], as subjanelas (pop-ups e diálogos) serão incorporadas "
"dentro da janela do aplicativo como nós semelhantes a controles. Se "
"[code]false[/code], elas aparecerão como janelas separadas gerenciadas pelo "
"sistema operacional."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"If [code]true[/code], the GUI controls on the viewport will lay pixel "
"perfectly."
msgstr ""
"Se [code]true[/code], os controles de GUI na viewport serão posicionados com "
"precisão de pixels (pixel perfectly)."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"If [code]true[/code], this viewport will mark incoming input events as "
"handled by itself. If [code]false[/code], this is instead done by the first "
"parent viewport that is set to handle input locally.\n"
"A [SubViewportContainer] will automatically set this property to "
"[code]false[/code] for the [Viewport] contained inside of it.\n"
"See also [method set_input_as_handled] and [method is_input_handled]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"The automatic LOD bias to use for meshes rendered within the [Viewport] "
"(this is analogous to [member ReflectionProbe.mesh_lod_threshold]). Higher "
"values will use less detailed versions of meshes that have LOD variations "
"generated. If set to [code]0.0[/code], automatic LOD is disabled. Increase "
"[member mesh_lod_threshold] to improve performance at the cost of geometry "
"detail.\n"
"To control this property on the root viewport, set the [member "
"ProjectSettings.rendering/mesh_lod/lod_change/threshold_pixels] project "
"setting.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Depending on the mesh's attributes (vertex colors, blend "
"shapes, ...), a mesh may have fewer levels of LOD generated to avoid visible "
"distortion of the mesh once it is affected by vertex colors or blend shapes. "
"Meshes with a very low vertex count will also not have any LODs generated, "
"which means this setting will not affect them at all. In general, this "
"setting makes the largest impact on static meshes with a high vertex count.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] [member mesh_lod_threshold] does not affect "
"[GeometryInstance3D] visibility ranges (also known as \"manual\" LOD or "
"hierarchical LOD)."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"The multisample antialiasing mode for 2D/Canvas rendering. A higher number "
"results in smoother edges at the cost of significantly worse performance. A "
"value of [constant Viewport.MSAA_2X] or [constant Viewport.MSAA_4X] is best "
"unless targeting very high-end systems. This has no effect on shader-induced "
"aliasing or texture aliasing.\n"
"See also [member ProjectSettings.rendering/anti_aliasing/quality/msaa_2d] "
"and [method RenderingServer.viewport_set_msaa_2d]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"The multisample antialiasing mode for 3D rendering. A higher number results "
"in smoother edges at the cost of significantly worse performance. A value of "
"[constant Viewport.MSAA_2X] or [constant Viewport.MSAA_4X] is best unless "
"targeting very high-end systems. See also bilinear scaling 3D [member "
"scaling_3d_mode] for supersampling, which provides higher quality but is "
"much more expensive. This has no effect on shader-induced aliasing or "
"texture aliasing.\n"
"See also [member ProjectSettings.rendering/anti_aliasing/quality/msaa_3d] "
"and [method RenderingServer.viewport_set_msaa_3d]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"If [code]true[/code] and one of the following conditions are true: [member "
"SubViewport.size_2d_override_stretch] and [member "
"SubViewport.size_2d_override] are set, [member Window.content_scale_factor] "
"is set and scaling is enabled, [member oversampling_override] is set, font "
"and [DPITexture] oversampling are enabled."
msgstr ""
"Se [code]true[/code] e uma das seguintes condições forem verdadeiras: "
"[member SubViewport.size_2d_override_stretch] e [member "
"SubViewport.size_2d_override] estão definidos, [member "
"Window.content_scale_factor] está definido e o dimensionamento está ativado, "
"[member oversampling_override] está definido, o oversampling de fonte e "
"[DPITexture] estão ativados."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"If greater than zero, this value is used as the font oversampling factor, "
"otherwise oversampling is equal to viewport scale."
msgstr ""
"Se for maior que zero, este valor é usado como o fator de oversampling da "
"fonte; caso contrário, o oversampling é igual à escala do viewport."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"If [code]true[/code], the viewport will use a unique copy of the [World3D] "
"defined in [member world_3d]."
msgstr ""
"Se [code]true[/code], a viewport usará uma cópia exclusiva do [World3D] "
"definido em [member world_3d]."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"If [code]true[/code], the objects rendered by viewport become subjects of "
"mouse picking process.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] The number of simultaneously pickable objects is limited to 64 "
"and they are selected in a non-deterministic order, which can be different "
"in each picking process."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"If [code]true[/code], the input_event signal will only be sent to one "
"physics object in the mouse picking process. If you want to get the top "
"object only, you must also enable [member physics_object_picking_sort].\n"
"If [code]false[/code], an input_event signal will be sent to all physics "
"objects in the mouse picking process.\n"
"This applies to 2D CanvasItem object picking only."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"If [code]true[/code], objects receive mouse picking events sorted primarily "
"by their [member CanvasItem.z_index] and secondarily by their position in "
"the scene tree. If [code]false[/code], the order is undetermined.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] This setting is disabled by default because of its potential "
"expensive computational cost.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Sorting happens after selecting the pickable objects. Because "
"of the limitation of 64 simultaneously pickable objects, it is not "
"guaranteed that the object with the highest [member CanvasItem.z_index] "
"receives the picking event."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid "The subdivision amount of the first quadrant on the shadow atlas."
msgstr "A quantidade de subdivisão do primeiro quadrante no atlas de sombras."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid "The subdivision amount of the second quadrant on the shadow atlas."
msgstr "A quantidade de subdivisão do segundo quadrante no atlas de sombras."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid "The subdivision amount of the third quadrant on the shadow atlas."
msgstr "A quantidade de subdivisão do terceiro quadrante no atlas de sombras."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid "The subdivision amount of the fourth quadrant on the shadow atlas."
msgstr "A quantidade de subdivisão do quarto quadrante no atlas de sombras."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"The shadow atlas' resolution (used for omni and spot lights). The value is "
"rounded up to the nearest power of 2.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] If this is set to [code]0[/code], no positional shadows will be "
"visible at all. This can improve performance significantly on low-end "
"systems by reducing both the CPU and GPU load (as fewer draw calls are "
"needed to draw the scene without shadows)."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"Sets scaling 3D mode. Bilinear scaling renders at different resolution to "
"either undersample or supersample the viewport. FidelityFX Super Resolution "
"1.0, abbreviated to FSR, is an upscaling technology that produces high "
"quality images at fast framerates by using a spatially aware upscaling "
"algorithm. FSR is slightly more expensive than bilinear, but it produces "
"significantly higher image quality. FSR should be used where possible.\n"
"To control this property on the root viewport, set the [member "
"ProjectSettings.rendering/scaling_3d/mode] project setting."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"Scales the 3D render buffer based on the viewport size uses an image filter "
"specified in [member ProjectSettings.rendering/scaling_3d/mode] to scale the "
"output image to the full viewport size. Values lower than [code]1.0[/code] "
"can be used to speed up 3D rendering at the cost of quality (undersampling). "
"Values greater than [code]1.0[/code] are only valid for bilinear mode and "
"can be used to improve 3D rendering quality at a high performance cost "
"(supersampling). See also [member ProjectSettings.rendering/anti_aliasing/"
"quality/msaa_3d] for multi-sample antialiasing, which is significantly "
"cheaper but only smooths the edges of polygons.\n"
"When using FSR upscaling, AMD recommends exposing the following values as "
"preset options to users \"Ultra Quality: 0.77\", \"Quality: 0.67\", "
"\"Balanced: 0.59\", \"Performance: 0.5\" instead of exposing the entire "
"scale.\n"
"To control this property on the root viewport, set the [member "
"ProjectSettings.rendering/scaling_3d/scale] project setting."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"Sets the screen-space antialiasing method used. Screen-space antialiasing "
"works by selectively blurring edges in a post-process shader. It differs "
"from MSAA which takes multiple coverage samples while rendering objects. "
"Screen-space AA methods are typically faster than MSAA and will smooth out "
"specular aliasing, but tend to make scenes appear blurry.\n"
"See also [member ProjectSettings.rendering/anti_aliasing/quality/"
"screen_space_aa] and [method RenderingServer.viewport_set_screen_space_aa]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"Controls how much of the original viewport's size should be covered by the "
"2D signed distance field. This SDF can be sampled in [CanvasItem] shaders "
"and is also used for [GPUParticles2D] collision. Higher values allow "
"portions of occluders located outside the viewport to still be taken into "
"account in the generated signed distance field, at the cost of performance. "
"If you notice particles falling through [LightOccluder2D]s as the occluders "
"leave the viewport, increase this setting.\n"
"The percentage is added on each axis and on both sides. For example, with "
"the default [constant SDF_OVERSIZE_120_PERCENT], the signed distance field "
"will cover 20% of the viewport's size outside the viewport on each side "
"(top, right, bottom, left)."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"The resolution scale to use for the 2D signed distance field. Higher values "
"lead to a more precise and more stable signed distance field as the camera "
"moves, at the cost of performance."
msgstr ""
"A escala de resolução a ser usada para o campo de distância assinado 2D. "
"Valores mais altos levam a um campo de distância assinado mais preciso e "
"estável conforme a câmera se move, ao custo de desempenho."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"If [code]true[/code], [CanvasItem] nodes will internally snap to full "
"pixels. Their position can still be sub-pixel, but the decimals will not "
"have effect. This can lead to a crisper appearance at the cost of less "
"smooth movement, especially when [Camera2D] smoothing is enabled."
msgstr ""
"Se [code]true[/code], os nós [CanvasItem] irão se ajustar internamente a "
"pixels inteiros. A posição deles ainda pode ser subpixel, mas os decimais "
"não terão efeito. Isso pode levar a uma aparência mais nítida ao custo de um "
"movimento menos suave, especialmente quando a suavização da [Camera2D] "
"estiver ativada."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"If [code]true[/code], vertices of [CanvasItem] nodes will snap to full "
"pixels. Only affects the final vertex positions, not the transforms. This "
"can lead to a crisper appearance at the cost of less smooth movement, "
"especially when [Camera2D] smoothing is enabled."
msgstr ""
"Se [code]true[/code], os vértices dos nós [CanvasItem] se encaixarão em "
"pixels inteiros. Afeta apenas as posições finais dos vértices, não as "
"transformações. Isso pode levar a uma aparência mais nítida ao custo de um "
"movimento menos suave, especialmente quando a suavização do [Camera2D] está "
"ativada."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"Affects the final texture sharpness by reading from a lower or higher mipmap "
"(also called \"texture LOD bias\"). Negative values make mipmapped textures "
"sharper but grainier when viewed at a distance, while positive values make "
"mipmapped textures blurrier (even when up close).\n"
"Enabling temporal antialiasing ([member use_taa]) will automatically apply a "
"[code]-0.5[/code] offset to this value, while enabling FXAA ([member "
"screen_space_aa]) will automatically apply a [code]-0.25[/code] offset to "
"this value. If both TAA and FXAA are enabled at the same time, an offset of "
"[code]-0.75[/code] is applied to this value.\n"
"To control this property on the root viewport, set the [member "
"ProjectSettings.rendering/textures/default_filters/texture_mipmap_bias] "
"project setting.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] If [member scaling_3d_scale] is lower than [code]1.0[/code] "
"(exclusive), [member texture_mipmap_bias] is used to adjust the automatic "
"mipmap bias which is calculated internally based on the scale factor. The "
"formula for this is [code]log2(scaling_3d_scale) + mipmap_bias[/code].\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] This property is only supported in the Forward+ and Mobile "
"renderers, not Compatibility. In Compatibility, this property is always "
"treated as if it was set to [code]0.0[/code]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"If [code]true[/code], the viewport should render its background as "
"transparent.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Due to technical limitations, certain rendering features are "
"disabled when a viewport has a transparent background. This currently "
"applies to screen-space reflections, subsurface scattering, and depth of "
"field."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"When using the Mobile or Forward+ renderers, set [member use_debanding] to "
"enable or disable the debanding feature of this [Viewport]. If [member "
"use_hdr_2d] is [code]false[/code], 2D rendering is [i]not[/i] affected by "
"debanding unless the [member Environment.background_mode] is [constant "
"Environment.BG_CANVAS]. If [member use_hdr_2d] is [code]true[/code], "
"debanding will only be applied if this is the root [Viewport] and will "
"affect all 2D and 3D rendering, including canvas items.\n"
"[member use_debanding] has no effect when using the Compatibility rendering "
"method. The Mobile renderer can also use material debanding, which can be "
"set with [method RenderingServer.material_set_use_debanding] or configured "
"with [member ProjectSettings.rendering/anti_aliasing/quality/"
"use_debanding].\n"
"See also [member ProjectSettings.rendering/anti_aliasing/quality/"
"use_debanding], [method RenderingServer.material_set_use_debanding], and "
"[method RenderingServer.viewport_set_use_debanding]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"If [code]true[/code], 2D rendering will use a high dynamic range (HDR) "
"[code]RGBA16[/code] format framebuffer. Additionally, 2D rendering will be "
"performed on linear values and will be converted using the appropriate "
"transfer function immediately before blitting to the screen (if the Viewport "
"is attached to the screen).\n"
"Practically speaking, this means that the end result of the Viewport will "
"not be clamped to the [code]0-1[/code] range and can be used in 3D rendering "
"without color encoding adjustments. This allows 2D rendering to take "
"advantage of effects requiring high dynamic range (e.g. 2D glow) as well as "
"substantially improves the appearance of effects requiring highly detailed "
"gradients."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"If [code]true[/code], [OccluderInstance3D] nodes will be usable for "
"occlusion culling in 3D for this viewport. For the root viewport, [member "
"ProjectSettings.rendering/occlusion_culling/use_occlusion_culling] must be "
"set to [code]true[/code] instead.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Enabling occlusion culling has a cost on the CPU. Only enable "
"occlusion culling if you actually plan to use it, and think whether your "
"scene can actually benefit from occlusion culling. Large, open scenes with "
"few or no objects blocking the view will generally not benefit much from "
"occlusion culling. Large open scenes generally benefit more from mesh LOD "
"and visibility ranges ([member GeometryInstance3D.visibility_range_begin] "
"and [member GeometryInstance3D.visibility_range_end]) compared to occlusion "
"culling.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Due to memory constraints, occlusion culling is not supported "
"by default in Web export templates. It can be enabled by compiling custom "
"Web export templates with [code]module_raycast_enabled=yes[/code]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"Enables temporal antialiasing for this viewport. TAA works by jittering the "
"camera and accumulating the images of the last rendered frames, motion "
"vector rendering is used to account for camera and object motion.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] The implementation is not complete yet, some visual instances "
"such as particles and skinned meshes may show artifacts.\n"
"See also [member ProjectSettings.rendering/anti_aliasing/quality/use_taa] "
"and [method RenderingServer.viewport_set_use_taa]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"If [code]true[/code], the viewport will use the primary XR interface to "
"render XR output. When applicable this can result in a stereoscopic image "
"and the resulting render being output to a headset."
msgstr ""
"Se [code]true[/code], a viewport usará a interface XR principal para "
"renderizar a saída XR. Quando aplicável, isso pode resultar em uma imagem "
"estereoscópica e a renderização resultante ser emitida para um headset."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"The Variable Rate Shading (VRS) mode that is used for this viewport. Note, "
"if hardware does not support VRS this property is ignored."
msgstr ""
"O modo Variable Rate Shading (VRS) usado para este viewport. Observe que, se "
"o hardware não suportar VRS, esta propriedade será ignorada."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"Texture to use when [member vrs_mode] is set to [constant "
"Viewport.VRS_TEXTURE].\n"
"The texture [i]must[/i] use a lossless compression format so that colors can "
"be matched precisely. The following VRS densities are mapped to various "
"colors, with brighter colors representing a lower level of shading "
"precision:\n"
"[codeblock lang=text]\n"
"- 1×1 = rgb(0, 0, 0)     - #000000\n"
"- 1×2 = rgb(0, 85, 0)    - #005500\n"
"- 2×1 = rgb(85, 0, 0)    - #550000\n"
"- 2×2 = rgb(85, 85, 0)   - #555500\n"
"- 2×4 = rgb(85, 170, 0)  - #55aa00\n"
"- 4×2 = rgb(170, 85, 0)  - #aa5500\n"
"- 4×4 = rgb(170, 170, 0) - #aaaa00\n"
"- 4×8 = rgb(170, 255, 0) - #aaff00 - Not supported on most hardware\n"
"- 8×4 = rgb(255, 170, 0) - #ffaa00 - Not supported on most hardware\n"
"- 8×8 = rgb(255, 255, 0) - #ffff00 - Not supported on most hardware\n"
"[/codeblock]"
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"Sets the update mode for Variable Rate Shading (VRS) for the viewport. VRS "
"requires the input texture to be converted to the format usable by the VRS "
"method supported by the hardware. The update mode defines how often this "
"happens. If the GPU does not support VRS, or VRS is not enabled, this "
"property is ignored."
msgstr ""
"Define o modo de atualização para Variable Rate Shading (VRS) para a "
"viewport. O VRS exige que a textura de entrada seja convertida para o "
"formato utilizável pelo método VRS suportado pelo hardware. O modo de "
"atualização define com que frequência isso acontece. Se a GPU não suportar "
"VRS, ou se o VRS não estiver ativado, esta propriedade será ignorada."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid "The custom [World2D] which can be used as 2D environment source."
msgstr ""
"O [World2D] personalizado que pode ser usado como fonte de ambiente 2D."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid "The custom [World3D] which can be used as 3D environment source."
msgstr ""
"O [World3D] personalizado que pode ser usado como fonte de ambiente 3D."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"Emitted when a Control node grabs keyboard focus.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] A Control node losing focus doesn't cause this signal to be "
"emitted."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"Emitted when the size of the viewport is changed, whether by resizing of "
"window, or some other means."
msgstr ""
"Emitido quando o tamanho do viewport é alterado, seja pelo redimensionamento "
"da janela ou por algum outro meio."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid "This quadrant will not be used."
msgstr "Este quadrante não será usado."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid "This quadrant will only be used by one shadow map."
msgstr "Este quadrante será usado apenas por um mapa de sombras."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid "This quadrant will be split in 4 and used by up to 4 shadow maps."
msgstr "Este quadrante será dividido em 4 e usado por até 4 mapas de sombra."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid "This quadrant will be split 16 ways and used by up to 16 shadow maps."
msgstr ""
"Este quadrante será dividido em 16 partes e usado por até 16 mapas de sombra."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid "This quadrant will be split 64 ways and used by up to 64 shadow maps."
msgstr ""
"Este quadrante será dividido em 64 partes e usado por até 64 mapas de sombra."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"This quadrant will be split 256 ways and used by up to 256 shadow maps. "
"Unless the [member positional_shadow_atlas_size] is very high, the shadows "
"in this quadrant will be very low resolution."
msgstr ""
"Este quadrante será dividido em 256 partes e usado por até 256 mapas de "
"sombra. A menos que o [member positional_shadow_atlas_size] seja muito alto, "
"as sombras neste quadrante terão resolução muito baixa."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"This quadrant will be split 1024 ways and used by up to 1024 shadow maps. "
"Unless the [member positional_shadow_atlas_size] is very high, the shadows "
"in this quadrant will be very low resolution."
msgstr ""
"Este quadrante será dividido em 1024 partes e usado por até 1024 mapas de "
"sombra. A menos que o [member positional_shadow_atlas_size] seja muito alto, "
"as sombras neste quadrante terão resolução muito baixa."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"Represents the size of the [enum PositionalShadowAtlasQuadrantSubdiv] enum."
msgstr ""
"Representa o tamanho da enumeração [enum "
"PositionalShadowAtlasQuadrantSubdiv]."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"Use bilinear scaling for the viewport's 3D buffer. The amount of scaling can "
"be set using [member scaling_3d_scale]. Values less than [code]1.0[/code] "
"will result in undersampling while values greater than [code]1.0[/code] will "
"result in supersampling. A value of [code]1.0[/code] disables scaling."
msgstr ""
"Usa escala bilinear para o buffer 3D da viewport. A quantidade de escala "
"pode ser definida usando [member scaling_3d_scale]. Valores menores que "
"[code]1.0[/code] resultarão em subamostragem, enquanto valores maiores que "
"[code]1.0[/code] resultarão em superamostragem. Um valor de [code]1.0[/code] "
"desativa a escala."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"Use AMD FidelityFX Super Resolution 1.0 upscaling for the viewport's 3D "
"buffer. The amount of scaling can be set using [member scaling_3d_scale]. "
"Values less than [code]1.0[/code] will result in the viewport being upscaled "
"using FSR. Values greater than [code]1.0[/code] are not supported and "
"bilinear downsampling will be used instead. A value of [code]1.0[/code] "
"disables scaling."
msgstr ""
"Use o upscaling do AMD FidelityFX Super Resolution 1.0 para o buffer 3D do "
"viewport. A quantidade de escala pode ser definida usando [member "
"scaling_3d_scale]. Valores menores que [code]1.0[/code] farão com que o "
"viewport seja redimensionado usando FSR. Valores maiores que [code]1.0[/"
"code] não são suportados e a subamostragem bilinear será usada em vez disso. "
"Um valor de [code]1.0[/code] desativa o redimensionamento."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"Use the [url=https://developer.apple.com/documentation/metalfx/"
"mtlfxspatialscaler#overview]MetalFX spatial upscaler[/url] for the "
"viewport's 3D buffer.\n"
"The amount of scaling can be set using [member scaling_3d_scale].\n"
"Values less than [code]1.0[/code] will result in the viewport being upscaled "
"using MetalFX. Values greater than [code]1.0[/code] are not supported and "
"bilinear downsampling will be used instead. A value of [code]1.0[/code] "
"disables scaling.\n"
"More information: [url=https://developer.apple.com/documentation/"
"metalfx]MetalFX[/url].\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Only supported when the Metal rendering driver is in use, which "
"limits this scaling mode to macOS and iOS."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"Use the [url=https://developer.apple.com/documentation/metalfx/"
"mtlfxtemporalscaler#overview]MetalFX temporal upscaler[/url] for the "
"viewport's 3D buffer.\n"
"The amount of scaling can be set using [member scaling_3d_scale]. To "
"determine the minimum input scale, use the [method "
"RenderingDevice.limit_get] method with [constant "
"RenderingDevice.LIMIT_METALFX_TEMPORAL_SCALER_MIN_SCALE].\n"
"Values less than [code]1.0[/code] will result in the viewport being upscaled "
"using MetalFX. Values greater than [code]1.0[/code] are not supported and "
"bilinear downsampling will be used instead. A value of [code]1.0[/code] will "
"use MetalFX at native resolution as a TAA solution.\n"
"More information: [url=https://developer.apple.com/documentation/"
"metalfx]MetalFX[/url].\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Only supported when the Metal rendering driver is in use, which "
"limits this scaling mode to macOS and iOS."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"Use nearest-neighbor filtering for the viewport's 3D buffer. This looks "
"crisper than [constant SCALING_3D_MODE_BILINEAR] and has no additional "
"rendering cost. The amount of scaling can be set using [member "
"scaling_3d_scale]. Values greater than [code]1.0[/code] are not supported "
"and bilinear downsampling will be used instead. A value of [code]1.0[/code] "
"disables scaling.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] When using the [b]Nearest[/b] scaling mode, to avoid uneven "
"pixel scaling, it's highly recommended to use a value equal to an integer "
"divisor with a dividend of [code]1[/code]. For example, it's best to use a "
"scale of [code]0.5[/code] (1/2), [code]0.3333[/code] (1/3), [code]0.25[/"
"code] (1/4), [code]0.2[/code] (1/5), and so on."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid "Represents the size of the [enum Scaling3DMode] enum."
msgstr "Representa o tamanho da enumeração [enum Scaling3DMode]."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"Multisample antialiasing mode disabled. This is the default value, and is "
"also the fastest setting."
msgstr ""
"Modo de anti-aliasing multisample desativado. Este é o valor padrão e também "
"a configuração mais rápida."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"Use 2× Multisample Antialiasing. This has a moderate performance cost. It "
"helps reduce aliasing noticeably, but 4× MSAA still looks substantially "
"better."
msgstr ""
"Usa Antialiasing de Multiamostragem 2×. Isso tem um custo moderado de "
"desempenho. Ajuda a reduzir o serrilhado visivelmente, mas o MSAA 4× ainda "
"parece substancialmente melhor."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"Use 4× Multisample Antialiasing. This has a significant performance cost, "
"and is generally a good compromise between performance and quality."
msgstr ""
"Usa Antialiasing Multiamostragem 4×. Isso tem um custo de desempenho "
"significativo e geralmente é um bom compromisso entre desempenho e qualidade."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"Use 8× Multisample Antialiasing. This has a very high performance cost. The "
"difference between 4× and 8× MSAA may not always be visible in real gameplay "
"conditions. Likely unsupported on low-end and older hardware."
msgstr ""
"Use o Antialiasing Multiamostragem 8×. Isso tem um custo de desempenho muito "
"alto. A diferença entre o MSAA 4× e 8× pode nem sempre ser visível em "
"condições reais de jogo. Provavelmente sem suporte em hardware de baixo "
"desempenho e mais antigo."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid "Represents the size of the [enum MSAA] enum."
msgstr "Representa o tamanho da enumeração [enum MSAA]."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid "Represents the size of the [enum AnisotropicFiltering] enum."
msgstr "Representa o tamanho da enumeração [enum AnisotropicFiltering]."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid "Represents the size of the [enum ScreenSpaceAA] enum."
msgstr "Representa o tamanho da enumeração [enum ScreenSpaceAA]."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid "Amount of objects in frame."
msgstr "Quantidade de objetos no quadro."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid "Amount of vertices in frame."
msgstr "Quantidade de vértices no quadro."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid "Amount of draw calls in frame."
msgstr "Quantidade de chamadas de desenho no quadro."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid "Represents the size of the [enum RenderInfo] enum."
msgstr "Representa o tamanho do enum [enum RenderInfo]."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid "Represents the size of the [enum RenderInfoType] enum."
msgstr "Representa o tamanho da enumeração [enum RenderInfoType]."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid "Objects are displayed normally."
msgstr "Objetos são exibidos normalmente."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"Objects are displayed without textures and only with lighting information.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] When using this debug draw mode, custom shaders are ignored "
"since all materials in the scene temporarily use a debug material. This "
"means the result from custom shader functions (such as vertex displacement) "
"won't be visible anymore when using this debug draw mode."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"Objects are displayed semi-transparent with additive blending so you can see "
"where they are drawing over top of one another. A higher overdraw means you "
"are wasting performance on drawing pixels that are being hidden behind "
"others.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] When using this debug draw mode, custom shaders are ignored "
"since all materials in the scene temporarily use a debug material. This "
"means the result from custom shader functions (such as vertex displacement) "
"won't be visible anymore when using this debug draw mode."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"Objects are displayed as wireframe models.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] [method RenderingServer.set_debug_generate_wireframes] must be "
"called before loading any meshes for wireframes to be visible when using the "
"Compatibility renderer.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] In the Compatibility renderer, backfaces are always visible "
"when using wireframe rendering. In the Forward+ and Mobile renderers, "
"wireframes follow the material's backface culling properties instead."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"Objects are displayed without lighting information and their textures "
"replaced by normal mapping.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Only supported when using the Forward+ rendering method."
msgstr ""
"Objetos são exibidos sem informações de iluminação e suas texturas "
"substituídas por normal mapping.\n"
"[b]Nota:[/b] Apenas suportado ao usar o método de renderização Forward+."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"Draws the shadow atlas that stores shadows from [DirectionalLight3D]s in the "
"upper left quadrant of the [Viewport]."
msgstr ""
"Desenha o atlas de sombras que armazena sombras de [DirectionalLight3D]s no "
"quadrante superior esquerdo do [Viewport]."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"Draws the scene luminance buffer (if available) in the upper left quadrant "
"of the [Viewport].\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Only supported when using the Forward+ or Mobile rendering "
"methods."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"Draws the screen-space ambient occlusion texture instead of the scene so "
"that you can clearly see how it is affecting objects. In order for this "
"display mode to work, you must have [member Environment.ssao_enabled] set in "
"your [WorldEnvironment].\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Only supported when using the Forward+ rendering method."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"Draws the screen-space indirect lighting texture instead of the scene so "
"that you can clearly see how it is affecting objects. In order for this "
"display mode to work, you must have [member Environment.ssil_enabled] set in "
"your [WorldEnvironment].\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Only supported when using the Forward+ rendering method."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"Draws the decal atlas used by [Decal]s and light projector textures in the "
"upper left quadrant of the [Viewport].\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Only supported when using the Forward+ or Mobile rendering "
"methods."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"Draws the cascades used to render signed distance field global illumination "
"(SDFGI).\n"
"Does nothing if the current environment's [member Environment.sdfgi_enabled] "
"is [code]false[/code].\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Only supported when using the Forward+ rendering method."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"Draws the probes used for signed distance field global illumination "
"(SDFGI).\n"
"When in the editor, left-clicking a probe will display additional bright "
"dots that show its occlusion information. A white dot means the light is not "
"occluded at all at the dot's position, while a red dot means the light is "
"fully occluded. Intermediate values are possible.\n"
"Does nothing if the current environment's [member Environment.sdfgi_enabled] "
"is [code]false[/code].\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Only supported when using the Forward+ rendering method."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"Draws the buffer used for global illumination from [VoxelGI] or SDFGI. "
"Requires [VoxelGI] (at least one visible baked VoxelGI node) or SDFGI "
"([member Environment.sdfgi_enabled]) to be enabled to have a visible "
"effect.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Only supported when using the Forward+ rendering method."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"Draws all of the objects at their highest polycount regardless of their "
"distance from the camera. No low level of detail (LOD) is applied."
msgstr ""
"Desenha todos os objetos com sua contagem de polígonos mais alta, "
"independentemente da distância da câmera. Nenhum nível de detalhe (LOD) é "
"aplicado."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"Draws the cluster used by [OmniLight3D] nodes to optimize light rendering.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Only supported when using the Forward+ rendering method."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"Draws the cluster used by [SpotLight3D] nodes to optimize light rendering.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Only supported when using the Forward+ rendering method."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"Draws the cluster used by [Decal] nodes to optimize decal rendering.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Only supported when using the Forward+ rendering method."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"Draws the cluster used by [ReflectionProbe] nodes to optimize reflection "
"probes.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Only supported when using the Forward+ rendering method."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"Draws the buffer used for occlusion culling.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Only supported when using the Forward+ or Mobile rendering "
"methods."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"Draws vector lines over the viewport to indicate the movement of pixels "
"between frames.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Only supported when using the Forward+ rendering method."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"Draws the internal resolution buffer of the scene in linear colorspace "
"before tonemapping or post-processing is applied.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Only supported when using the Forward+ or Mobile rendering "
"methods."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"Draws the cluster used by [AreaLight3D] nodes to optimize light rendering.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Only supported when using the Forward+ rendering method."
msgstr ""
"Desenha o cluster usado pelos nós [AreaLight3D] para otimizar a renderização "
"da iluminação.\n"
"[b]Nota:[/b] Compatível apenas ao usar o método de renderização Forward+."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"Draws the atlas used by [AreaLight3D] nodes in the upper left quadrant of "
"the [Viewport].\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Only supported when using the Forward+ or Mobile rendering "
"method."
msgstr ""
"Desenha o atlas usado pelos nós [AreaLight3D] no quadrante superior esquerdo "
"do [Viewport].\n"
"[b]Nota:[/b] Compatível apenas ao usar o método de renderização Forward+ ou "
"Mobile."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"The [Viewport] will inherit the filter from its parent [CanvasItem] or "
"[Viewport]."
msgstr "O [Viewport] herdará o filtro de seu [CanvasItem] ou [Viewport] pai."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid "Represents the size of the [enum DefaultCanvasItemTextureFilter] enum."
msgstr ""
"Representa o tamanho da enumeração [enum DefaultCanvasItemTextureFilter]."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"The [Viewport] will inherit the repeat mode from its parent [CanvasItem] or "
"[Viewport]."
msgstr ""
"O [Viewport] herdará o modo de repetição de seu [CanvasItem] ou [Viewport] "
"pai."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid "Represents the size of the [enum DefaultCanvasItemTextureRepeat] enum."
msgstr ""
"Representa o tamanho da enumeração [enum DefaultCanvasItemTextureRepeat]."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid "The signed distance field only covers the viewport's own rectangle."
msgstr ""
"O campo de distância assinada abrange apenas o retângulo da própria viewport."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"The signed distance field is expanded to cover 20% of the viewport's size "
"around the borders."
msgstr ""
"O campo de distância sinalizada é expandido para cobrir 20% do tamanho do "
"viewport ao redor das bordas."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"The signed distance field is expanded to cover 50% of the viewport's size "
"around the borders."
msgstr ""
"O campo de distância sinalizada é expandido para cobrir 50% do tamanho do "
"viewport ao redor das bordas."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"The signed distance field is expanded to cover 100% (double) of the "
"viewport's size around the borders."
msgstr ""
"O campo de distância com sinal é expandido para cobrir 100% (o dobro) do "
"tamanho do viewport ao redor das bordas."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid "Represents the size of the [enum SDFOversize] enum."
msgstr "Representa o tamanho da enumeração [enum SDFOversize]."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid "The signed distance field is rendered at full resolution."
msgstr "O campo de distância assinada é renderizado na resolução máxima."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"The signed distance field is rendered at half the resolution of this "
"viewport."
msgstr ""
"O campo de distância sinalizada é renderizado à metade da resolução desta "
"viewport."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"The signed distance field is rendered at a quarter the resolution of this "
"viewport."
msgstr ""
"O campo de distância com sinal é renderizado a um quarto da resolução deste "
"viewport."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid "Represents the size of the [enum SDFScale] enum."
msgstr "Representa o tamanho da enumeração [enum SDFScale]."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid "Variable Rate Shading is disabled."
msgstr "O sombreamento de taxa variável está desativado."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"Variable Rate Shading uses a texture. Note, for stereoscopic use a texture "
"atlas with a texture for each view."
msgstr ""
"O Sombreamento de Taxa Variável usa uma textura. Nota: para uso "
"estereoscópico, use um atlas de textura com uma textura para cada vista."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid ""
"Variable Rate Shading's texture is supplied by the primary [XRInterface]."
msgstr ""
"A textura do Variable Rate Shading é fornecida pelo [XRInterface] primário."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid "Represents the size of the [enum VRSMode] enum."
msgstr "Representa o tamanho da enumeração [enum VRSMode]."

#: doc/classes/Viewport.xml
msgid "Represents the size of the [enum VRSUpdateMode] enum."
msgstr "Representa o tamanho da enumeração [enum VRSUpdateMode]."

#: doc/classes/ViewportTexture.xml
msgid "Provides the content of a [Viewport] as a dynamic texture."
msgstr "Fornece o conteúdo de um [Viewport] como uma textura dinâmica."

#: doc/classes/ViewportTexture.xml
msgid ""
"A [ViewportTexture] provides the content of a [Viewport] as a dynamic "
"[Texture2D]. This can be used to combine the rendering of [Control], "
"[Node2D] and [Node3D] nodes. For example, you can use this texture to "
"display a 3D scene inside a [TextureRect], or a 2D overlay in a [Sprite3D].\n"
"To get a [ViewportTexture] in code, use the [method Viewport.get_texture] "
"method on the target viewport.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] A [ViewportTexture] is always local to its scene (see [member "
"Resource.resource_local_to_scene]). If the scene root is not ready, it may "
"return incorrect data (see [signal Node.ready]).\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Instantiating scenes containing a high-resolution "
"[ViewportTexture] may cause noticeable stutter.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] When using a [Viewport] with [member Viewport.use_hdr_2d] set "
"to [code]true[/code], the returned texture will be an HDR image that uses "
"linear encoding. This may look darker than normal when displayed directly on "
"screen. To convert to nonlinear sRGB encoding, you can do the following:\n"
"[codeblock]\n"
"img.convert(Image.FORMAT_RGBA8)\n"
"img.linear_to_srgb()\n"
"[/codeblock]\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Some nodes such as [Decal], [Light3D], and [PointLight2D] do "
"not support using [ViewportTexture] directly. To use texture data from a "
"[ViewportTexture] in these nodes, you need to create an [ImageTexture] by "
"calling [method Texture2D.get_image] on the [ViewportTexture] and passing "
"the result to [method ImageTexture.create_from_image]. This conversion is a "
"slow operation, so it should not be performed every frame."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/ViewportTexture.xml
msgid ""
"The path to the [Viewport] node to display. This is relative to the local "
"scene root (see [method Resource.get_local_scene]), [b]not[/b] to the nodes "
"that use this texture.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] In the editor, this path is automatically updated when the "
"target viewport or one of its ancestors is renamed or moved. At runtime, "
"this path may not automatically update if the scene root cannot be found."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/VirtualJoystick.xml
msgid "A virtual joystick control for touchscreen devices."
msgstr ""
"Um controle de joystick virtual para dispositivos de tela sensível ao toque."

#: doc/classes/VirtualJoystick.xml
msgid ""
"A customizable on-screen joystick control designed for touchscreen devices. "
"It allows users to provide directional input by dragging a virtual tip "
"within a defined circular area.\n"
"This control can simulate directional actions (see [member action_up], "
"[member action_down], [member action_left], and [member action_right]), "
"which are triggered when the joystick is moved in the corresponding "
"directions."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/VirtualJoystick.xml
msgid "The action to trigger when the joystick is moved down."
msgstr "A ação a ser disparada quando o joystick é movido para baixo."

#: doc/classes/VirtualJoystick.xml
msgid "The action to trigger when the joystick is moved left."
msgstr "A ação a ser disparada quando o joystick é movido para a esquerda."

#: doc/classes/VirtualJoystick.xml
msgid "The action to trigger when the joystick is moved right."
msgstr "A ação a ser acionada quando o joystick é movido para a direita."

#: doc/classes/VirtualJoystick.xml
msgid "The action to trigger when the joystick is moved up."
msgstr "A ação a ser disparada quando o joystick for movido para cima."

#: doc/classes/VirtualJoystick.xml
msgid ""
"The multiplier applied to the joystick's radius that defines the clamp "
"zone.\n"
"This zone limits how far the joystick tip can move from its center before "
"being clamped.\n"
"A value of [code]1.0[/code] means the tip can move up to the edge of the "
"joystick's visual size.\n"
"In [constant JOYSTICK_FOLLOWING] mode, this radius also determines how far "
"the finger can move before the joystick base starts following the touch "
"input."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/VirtualJoystick.xml
msgid ""
"The ratio of the joystick size that defines the joystick deadzone. The "
"joystick tip must move beyond this ratio before being considered active.\n"
"This deadzone is applied before triggering input actions and affects the "
"joystick's input vector and all related signals.\n"
"Note that input actions may also define their own deadzones in the InputMap. "
"If both are set, the joystick deadzone is applied first, followed by the "
"action's deadzone.\n"
"By default, this value is [code]0.0[/code], meaning the joystick does not "
"apply its own deadzone and relies entirely on the InputMap action deadzones."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/VirtualJoystick.xml
msgid ""
"The initial position of the joystick as a ratio of the control's size. [code]"
"(0, 0)[/code] is top-left and [code](1, 1)[/code] is bottom-right."
msgstr ""
"A posição inicial do joystick como uma proporção do tamanho do controle. "
"[code](0, 0)[/code] é o canto superior esquerdo e [code](1, 1)[/code] é o "
"canto inferior direito."

#: doc/classes/VirtualJoystick.xml
msgid "The joystick mode to use."
msgstr "O modo de joystick a ser usado."

#: doc/classes/VirtualJoystick.xml
msgid "The size of the joystick in pixels."
msgstr "O tamanho do joystick em pixels."

#: doc/classes/VirtualJoystick.xml
msgid "The size of the joystick tip in pixels."
msgstr "O tamanho da ponta do joystick em pixels."

#: doc/classes/VirtualJoystick.xml
msgid "The visibility mode to use."
msgstr "O modo de visibilidade a ser usado."

#: doc/classes/VirtualJoystick.xml
msgid "Emitted when the tip enters the deadzone after being outside of it."
msgstr "Emitido quando a ponta entra na zona morta após estar fora dela."

#: doc/classes/VirtualJoystick.xml
msgid ""
"Emitted when the tip moved outside the deadzone and the joystick is "
"released. The [param input_vector] contains the last input direction and "
"strength before release. Its length is between [code]0.0[/code] and "
"[code]1.0[/code]."
msgstr ""
"Emitido quando a ponta se move para fora da zona morta e o joystick é solto. "
"O [param input_vector] contém a última direção de entrada e força antes de "
"ser solto. Seu comprimento está entre [code]0.0[/code] e [code]1.0[/code]."

#: doc/classes/VirtualJoystick.xml
msgid "Emitted when the joystick is pressed."
msgstr "Emitido quando o joystick é pressionado."

#: doc/classes/VirtualJoystick.xml
msgid ""
"Emitted when the joystick is released. The [param input_vector] is the final "
"input direction and strength, with a length between [code]0.0[/code] and "
"[code]1.0[/code]."
msgstr ""
"Emitido quando o joystick é solto. O [param input_vector] é a direção e a "
"força de entrada finais, com um comprimento entre [code]0.0[/code] e "
"[code]1.0[/code]."

#: doc/classes/VirtualJoystick.xml
msgid "Emitted when the joystick is released without moving the tip."
msgstr "Emitido quando o joystick é solto sem mover a ponta."

#: doc/classes/VirtualJoystick.xml
msgid "The joystick doesn't move."
msgstr "O joystick não se move."

#: doc/classes/VirtualJoystick.xml
msgid ""
"The joystick is moved to the initial touch position as long as it's within "
"the joystick's bounds. It moves back to its original position when released."
msgstr ""
"O joystick é movido para a posição inicial de toque, desde que esteja dentro "
"dos limites do joystick. Ele retorna à sua posição original quando solto."

#: doc/classes/VirtualJoystick.xml
msgid ""
"The joystick is moved to the initial touch position as long as it's within "
"the joystick's bounds. It will follow the touch input if it goes outside the "
"joystick's range. It moves back to its original position when released."
msgstr ""
"O joystick é movido para a posição de toque inicial, desde que esteja dentro "
"dos limites do joystick. Ele seguirá a entrada de toque se sair do intervalo "
"do joystick. Ele retorna à sua posição original quando solto."

#: doc/classes/VirtualJoystick.xml
msgid "The joystick is always visible."
msgstr "O joystick está sempre visível."

#: doc/classes/VirtualJoystick.xml
msgid "The joystick is only visible when being touched."
msgstr "O joystick só fica visível ao ser tocado."

#: doc/classes/VirtualJoystick.xml
msgid "Base joystick [StyleBox]."
msgstr "[StyleBox] do joystick base."

#: doc/classes/VirtualJoystick.xml
msgid "Tip joystick [StyleBox]."
msgstr "[StyleBox] do joystick de ponta."

#: doc/classes/VirtualJoystick.xml
msgid "Base joystick [StyleBox] when pressed."
msgstr "[StyleBox] do joystick base quando pressionado."

#: doc/classes/VirtualJoystick.xml
msgid "Tip joystick [StyleBox] when pressed."
msgstr "[StyleBox] do joystick de ponta quando pressionado."

#: doc/classes/VisibleOnScreenEnabler2D.xml
msgid ""
"A rectangular region of 2D space that, when visible on screen, enables a "
"target node."
msgstr ""
"Uma região retangular de espaço 2D que, quando visível na tela, habilita um "
"nó de destino."

#: doc/classes/VisibleOnScreenEnabler2D.xml
msgid ""
"[VisibleOnScreenEnabler2D] contains a rectangular region of 2D space and a "
"target node. The target node will be automatically enabled (via its [member "
"Node.process_mode] property) when any part of this region becomes visible on "
"the screen, and automatically disabled otherwise. This can for example be "
"used to activate enemies only when the player approaches them.\n"
"See [VisibleOnScreenNotifier2D] if you only want to be notified when the "
"region is visible on screen.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] [VisibleOnScreenEnabler2D] uses the render culling code to "
"determine whether it's visible on screen, so it won't function unless "
"[member CanvasItem.visible] is set to [code]true[/code]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/VisibleOnScreenEnabler2D.xml
#: doc/classes/VisibleOnScreenEnabler3D.xml
msgid ""
"Determines how the target node is enabled. Corresponds to [enum "
"Node.ProcessMode]. When the node is disabled, it always uses [constant "
"Node.PROCESS_MODE_DISABLED]."
msgstr ""
"Determina como o nó de destino é ativado. Corresponde a [enum "
"Node.ProcessMode]. Quando o nó está desativado, ele sempre usa [constant "
"Node.PROCESS_MODE_DISABLED]."

#: doc/classes/VisibleOnScreenEnabler2D.xml
msgid ""
"The path to the target node, relative to the [VisibleOnScreenEnabler2D]. The "
"target node is cached; it's only assigned when setting this property (if the "
"[VisibleOnScreenEnabler2D] is inside the scene tree) and every time the "
"[VisibleOnScreenEnabler2D] enters the scene tree. If the path is empty, no "
"node will be affected. If the path is invalid, an error is also generated."
msgstr ""
"O caminho para o nó de destino, relativo ao [VisibleOnScreenEnabler2D]. O nó "
"de destino é armazenado em cache; ele é atribuído apenas ao definir esta "
"propriedade (se o [VisibleOnScreenEnabler2D] estiver dentro da árvore de "
"cena) e toda vez que o [VisibleOnScreenEnabler2D] entrar na árvore de cena. "
"Se o caminho estiver vazio, nenhum nó será afetado. Se o caminho for "
"inválido, um erro também será gerado."

#: doc/classes/VisibleOnScreenEnabler2D.xml
#: doc/classes/VisibleOnScreenEnabler3D.xml
msgid "Corresponds to [constant Node.PROCESS_MODE_INHERIT]."
msgstr "Corresponde a [constant Node.PROCESS_MODE_INHERIT]."

#: doc/classes/VisibleOnScreenEnabler2D.xml
#: doc/classes/VisibleOnScreenEnabler3D.xml
msgid "Corresponds to [constant Node.PROCESS_MODE_ALWAYS]."
msgstr "Corresponde a [constant Node.PROCESS_MODE_ALWAYS]."

#: doc/classes/VisibleOnScreenEnabler2D.xml
#: doc/classes/VisibleOnScreenEnabler3D.xml
msgid "Corresponds to [constant Node.PROCESS_MODE_WHEN_PAUSED]."
msgstr "Corresponde a [constant Node.PROCESS_MODE_WHEN_PAUSED]."

#: doc/classes/VisibleOnScreenEnabler3D.xml
msgid ""
"A box-shaped region of 3D space that, when visible on screen, enables a "
"target node."
msgstr ""
"Uma região em formato de caixa de espaço 3D que, quando visível na tela, "
"habilita um nó de destino."

#: doc/classes/VisibleOnScreenEnabler3D.xml
msgid ""
"[VisibleOnScreenEnabler3D] contains a box-shaped region of 3D space and a "
"target node. The target node will be automatically enabled (via its [member "
"Node.process_mode] property) when any part of this region becomes visible on "
"the screen, and automatically disabled otherwise. This can for example be "
"used to activate enemies only when the player approaches them.\n"
"See [VisibleOnScreenNotifier3D] if you only want to be notified when the "
"region is visible on screen.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] [VisibleOnScreenEnabler3D] uses an approximate heuristic that "
"doesn't take walls and other occlusion into account, unless occlusion "
"culling is used. It also won't function unless [member Node3D.visible] is "
"set to [code]true[/code]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/VisibleOnScreenEnabler3D.xml
msgid ""
"The path to the target node, relative to the [VisibleOnScreenEnabler3D]. The "
"target node is cached; it's only assigned when setting this property (if the "
"[VisibleOnScreenEnabler3D] is inside the scene tree) and every time the "
"[VisibleOnScreenEnabler3D] enters the scene tree. If the path is empty, no "
"node will be affected. If the path is invalid, an error is also generated."
msgstr ""
"O caminho para o nó de destino, relativo ao [VisibleOnScreenEnabler3D]. O nó "
"de destino é armazenado em cache; ele é atribuído apenas ao definir esta "
"propriedade (se o [VisibleOnScreenEnabler3D] estiver dentro da árvore de "
"cena) e toda vez que o [VisibleOnScreenEnabler3D] entrar na árvore de cena. "
"Se o caminho estiver vazio, nenhum nó será afetado. Se o caminho for "
"inválido, um erro também será gerado."

#: doc/classes/VisibleOnScreenNotifier2D.xml
msgid ""
"A rectangular region of 2D space that detects whether it is visible on "
"screen."
msgstr ""
"Uma região retangular de espaço 2D que detecta se está visível na tela."

#: doc/classes/VisibleOnScreenNotifier2D.xml
msgid ""
"[VisibleOnScreenNotifier2D] represents a rectangular region of 2D space. "
"When any part of this region becomes visible on screen or in a viewport, it "
"will emit a [signal screen_entered] signal, and likewise it will emit a "
"[signal screen_exited] signal when no part of it remains visible.\n"
"If you want a node to be enabled automatically when this region is visible "
"on screen, use [VisibleOnScreenEnabler2D].\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] [VisibleOnScreenNotifier2D] uses the render culling code to "
"determine whether it's visible on screen, so it won't function unless "
"[member CanvasItem.visible] is set to [code]true[/code]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/VisibleOnScreenNotifier2D.xml
msgid ""
"If [code]true[/code], the bounding rectangle is on the screen.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] It takes one frame for the [VisibleOnScreenNotifier2D]'s "
"visibility to be determined once added to the scene tree, so this method "
"will always return [code]false[/code] right after it is instantiated, before "
"the draw pass."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/VisibleOnScreenNotifier2D.xml
msgid "The VisibleOnScreenNotifier2D's bounding rectangle."
msgstr "O retângulo delimitador do VisibleOnScreenNotifier2D."

#: doc/classes/VisibleOnScreenNotifier2D.xml
msgid ""
"If [code]true[/code], shows the rectangle area of [member rect] in the "
"editor with a translucent magenta fill. Unlike changing the visibility of "
"the VisibleOnScreenNotifier2D, this does not affect the screen culling "
"detection."
msgstr ""
"Se [code]true[/code], exibe a área retangular de [member rect] no editor com "
"um preenchimento magenta translúcido. Ao contrário de alterar a visibilidade "
"do VisibleOnScreenNotifier2D, isso não afeta a detecção de culling de tela."

#: doc/classes/VisibleOnScreenNotifier2D.xml
msgid "Emitted when the VisibleOnScreenNotifier2D enters the screen."
msgstr "Emitido quando o VisibleOnScreenNotifier2D entra na tela."

#: doc/classes/VisibleOnScreenNotifier2D.xml
msgid "Emitted when the VisibleOnScreenNotifier2D exits the screen."
msgstr "Emitido quando o VisibleOnScreenNotifier2D sai da tela."

#: doc/classes/VisibleOnScreenNotifier3D.xml
msgid ""
"A box-shaped region of 3D space that detects whether it is visible on screen."
msgstr ""
"Uma região em formato de caixa de espaço 3D que detecta se está visível na "
"tela."

#: doc/classes/VisibleOnScreenNotifier3D.xml
msgid ""
"[VisibleOnScreenNotifier3D] represents a box-shaped region of 3D space. When "
"any part of this region becomes visible on screen or in a [Camera3D]'s view, "
"it will emit a [signal screen_entered] signal, and likewise it will emit a "
"[signal screen_exited] signal when no part of it remains visible.\n"
"If you want a node to be enabled automatically when this region is visible "
"on screen, use [VisibleOnScreenEnabler3D].\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] [VisibleOnScreenNotifier3D] uses an approximate heuristic that "
"doesn't take walls and other occlusion into account, unless occlusion "
"culling is used. It also won't function unless [member Node3D.visible] is "
"set to [code]true[/code]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/VisibleOnScreenNotifier3D.xml
msgid ""
"Returns [code]true[/code] if the bounding box is on the screen.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] It takes one frame for the [VisibleOnScreenNotifier3D]'s "
"visibility to be assessed once added to the scene tree, so this method will "
"always return [code]false[/code] right after it is instantiated."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/VisibleOnScreenNotifier3D.xml
msgid "The [VisibleOnScreenNotifier3D]'s bounding box."
msgstr "A caixa delimitadora do [VisibleOnScreenNotifier3D]."

#: doc/classes/VisibleOnScreenNotifier3D.xml
msgid "Emitted when the [VisibleOnScreenNotifier3D] enters the screen."
msgstr "Emitido quando o [VisibleOnScreenNotifier3D] entra na tela."

#: doc/classes/VisibleOnScreenNotifier3D.xml
msgid "Emitted when the [VisibleOnScreenNotifier3D] exits the screen."
msgstr "Emitido quando o [VisibleOnScreenNotifier3D] sai da tela."

#: doc/classes/VisualInstance3D.xml
msgid "Parent of all visual 3D nodes."
msgstr "Pai de todos os nós 3D visuais."

#: doc/classes/VisualInstance3D.xml
msgid ""
"The [VisualInstance3D] is used to connect a resource to a visual "
"representation. All visual 3D nodes inherit from the [VisualInstance3D]. In "
"general, you should not access the [VisualInstance3D] properties directly as "
"they are accessed and managed by the nodes that inherit from "
"[VisualInstance3D]. [VisualInstance3D] is the node representation of the "
"[RenderingServer] instance."
msgstr ""
"O [VisualInstance3D] é usado para conectar um recurso a uma representação "
"visual. Todos os nós 3D visuais herdam de [VisualInstance3D]. Em geral, você "
"não deve acessar as propriedades de [VisualInstance3D] diretamente, pois "
"elas são acessadas e gerenciadas pelos nós que herdam de [VisualInstance3D]. "
"O [VisualInstance3D] é a representação em nó da instância de "
"[RenderingServer]."

#: doc/classes/VisualInstance3D.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the [AABB] (also known as the bounding box) for this "
"[VisualInstance3D]."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o [AABB] (também conhecido como caixa delimitadora) para este "
"[VisualInstance3D]."

#: doc/classes/VisualInstance3D.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the RID of the resource associated with this [VisualInstance3D]. For "
"example, if the Node is a [MeshInstance3D], this will return the RID of the "
"associated [Mesh]."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o RID do recurso associado a este [VisualInstance3D]. Por exemplo, "
"se o nó for um [MeshInstance3D], isso retornará o RID da [Mesh] associada."

#: doc/classes/VisualInstance3D.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the RID of this instance. This RID is the same as the RID returned "
"by [method RenderingServer.instance_create]. This RID is needed if you want "
"to call [RenderingServer] functions directly on this [VisualInstance3D]."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o RID desta instância. Este RID é o mesmo que o RID retornado por "
"[method RenderingServer.instance_create]. Este RID é necessário se você "
"quiser chamar funções do [RenderingServer] diretamente neste "
"[VisualInstance3D]."

#: doc/classes/VisualInstance3D.xml
msgid ""
"Returns whether or not the specified layer of the [member layers] is "
"enabled, given a [param layer_number] between 1 and 20."
msgstr ""
"Retorna se a camada especificada da [member layers] está ativada, dado um "
"[param layer_number] entre 1 e 20."

#: doc/classes/VisualInstance3D.xml
msgid ""
"Sets the resource that is instantiated by this [VisualInstance3D], which "
"changes how the engine handles the [VisualInstance3D] under the hood. "
"Equivalent to [method RenderingServer.instance_set_base]."
msgstr ""
"Define o recurso instanciado por este [VisualInstance3D], o que altera a "
"forma como o motor lida com o [VisualInstance3D] internamente. Equivalente a "
"[method RenderingServer.instance_set_base]."

#: doc/classes/VisualInstance3D.xml
msgid ""
"Based on [param value], enables or disables the specified layer in the "
"[member layers], given a [param layer_number] between 1 and 20."
msgstr ""
"Com base em [param value], ativa ou desativa a camada especificada em "
"[member layers], dado um [param layer_number] entre 1 e 20."

#: doc/classes/VisualInstance3D.xml
msgid ""
"The render layer(s) this [VisualInstance3D] is drawn on.\n"
"This object will only be visible for [Camera3D]s whose cull mask includes "
"any of the render layers this [VisualInstance3D] is set to.\n"
"For [Light3D]s, this can be used to control which [VisualInstance3D]s are "
"affected by a specific light. For [GPUParticles3D], this can be used to "
"control which particles are effected by a specific attractor. For [Decal]s, "
"this can be used to control which [VisualInstance3D]s are affected by a "
"specific decal.\n"
"To adjust [member layers] more easily using a script, use [method "
"get_layer_mask_value] and [method set_layer_mask_value].\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] [VoxelGI], SDFGI and [LightmapGI] will always take all layers "
"into account to determine what contributes to global illumination. If this "
"is an issue, set [member GeometryInstance3D.gi_mode] to [constant "
"GeometryInstance3D.GI_MODE_DISABLED] for meshes and [member "
"Light3D.light_bake_mode] to [constant Light3D.BAKE_DISABLED] for lights to "
"exclude them from global illumination."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/VisualInstance3D.xml
msgid ""
"The amount by which the depth of this [VisualInstance3D] will be adjusted "
"when sorting by depth. Uses the same units as the engine (which are "
"typically meters). Adjusting it to a higher value will make the "
"[VisualInstance3D] reliably draw on top of other [VisualInstance3D]s that "
"are otherwise positioned at the same spot. To ensure it always draws on top "
"of other objects around it (not positioned at the same spot), set the value "
"to be greater than the distance between this [VisualInstance3D] and the "
"other nearby [VisualInstance3D]s."
msgstr ""
"A quantidade pela qual a profundidade deste [VisualInstance3D] será ajustada "
"ao ordenar por profundidade. Usa as mesmas unidades do motor (que "
"normalmente são metros). Ajustá-lo para um valor mais alto fará com que o "
"[VisualInstance3D] seja desenhado de forma confiável em cima de outros "
"[VisualInstance3D]s que de outra forma estariam posicionados no mesmo local. "
"Para garantir que ele sempre seja desenhado em cima de outros objetos ao seu "
"redor (não posicionados no mesmo local), defina o valor para ser maior do "
"que a distância entre este [VisualInstance3D] e os outros "
"[VisualInstance3D]s próximos."

#: doc/classes/VisualInstance3D.xml
msgid ""
"If [code]true[/code], the object is sorted based on the [AABB] center. The "
"object will be sorted based on the global position otherwise.\n"
"The [AABB] center based sorting is generally more accurate for 3D models. "
"The position based sorting instead allows to better control the drawing "
"order when working with [GPUParticles3D] and [CPUParticles3D]."
msgstr ""

#: modules/visual_shader/doc_classes/VisualShader.xml
msgid "A custom shader program with a visual editor."
msgstr "Um programa de shader personalizado com um editor visual."

#: modules/visual_shader/doc_classes/VisualShader.xml
msgid ""
"This class provides a graph-like visual editor for creating a [Shader]. "
"Although [VisualShader]s do not require coding, they share the same logic "
"with script shaders. They use [VisualShaderNode]s that can be connected to "
"each other to control the flow of the shader. The visual shader graph is "
"converted to a script shader behind the scenes."
msgstr ""
"Esta classe fornece um editor visual semelhante a um gráfico para criar um "
"[Shader]. Embora os [VisualShader]s não exijam codificação, eles "
"compartilham a mesma lógica com os shaders de script. Eles usam "
"[VisualShaderNode]s que podem ser conectados entre si para controlar o fluxo "
"do shader. O gráfico do shader visual é convertido em um shader de script "
"por trás dos panos."

#: modules/visual_shader/doc_classes/VisualShader.xml
#: modules/visual_shader/doc_classes/VisualShaderNode.xml
msgid "Using VisualShaders"
msgstr "Usando VisualShaders"

#: modules/visual_shader/doc_classes/VisualShader.xml
msgid "Adds the specified [param node] to the shader."
msgstr "Adiciona o [param node] especificado ao shader."

#: modules/visual_shader/doc_classes/VisualShader.xml
msgid "Adds a new varying value node to the shader."
msgstr "Adiciona um novo nó de valor de variação ao shader."

#: modules/visual_shader/doc_classes/VisualShader.xml
msgid "Attaches the given node to the given frame."
msgstr "Anexa o nó fornecido ao quadro fornecido."

#: modules/visual_shader/doc_classes/VisualShader.xml
msgid ""
"Returns [code]true[/code] if the specified nodes and ports can be connected "
"together."
msgstr ""
"Retorna [code]true[/code] se os nós e portas especificados puderem ser "
"conectados juntos."

#: modules/visual_shader/doc_classes/VisualShader.xml
msgid "Connects the specified nodes and ports."
msgstr "Conecta os nós e portas especificados."

#: modules/visual_shader/doc_classes/VisualShader.xml
msgid ""
"Connects the specified nodes and ports, even if they can't be connected. "
"Such connection is invalid and will not function properly."
msgstr ""
"Conecta os nós e portas especificados, mesmo que não possam ser conectados. "
"Tal conexão é inválida e não funcionará corretamente."

#: modules/visual_shader/doc_classes/VisualShader.xml
msgid "Detaches the given node from the frame it is attached to."
msgstr "Desconecta o nó fornecido do quadro ao qual está anexado."

#: modules/visual_shader/doc_classes/VisualShader.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the shader node instance with specified [param type] and [param id]."
msgstr ""
"Retorna a instância do nó de shader com o [param type] e o [param id] "
"especificados."

#: modules/visual_shader/doc_classes/VisualShader.xml
msgid "Returns the list of connected nodes with the specified type."
msgstr "Retorna a lista de nós conectados com o tipo especificado."

#: modules/visual_shader/doc_classes/VisualShader.xml
msgid "Returns the list of all nodes in the shader with the specified type."
msgstr "Retorna a lista de todos os nós no shader com o tipo especificado."

#: modules/visual_shader/doc_classes/VisualShader.xml
msgid "Returns the position of the specified node within the shader graph."
msgstr "Retorna a posição do nó especificado dentro do gráfico de shader."

#: modules/visual_shader/doc_classes/VisualShader.xml
msgid "Returns next valid node ID that can be added to the shader graph."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o próximo ID de nó válido que pode ser adicionado ao gráfico de "
"shader."

#: modules/visual_shader/doc_classes/VisualShader.xml
msgid ""
"Returns [code]true[/code] if the shader has a varying with the given [param "
"name]."
msgstr ""
"Retorna [code]true[/code] se o shader tiver uma variável varying com o "
"[param name] fornecido."

#: modules/visual_shader/doc_classes/VisualShader.xml
msgid ""
"Returns [code]true[/code] if the specified node and port connection exist."
msgstr ""
"Retorna [code]true[/code] se o nó e a conexão de porta especificados "
"existirem."

#: modules/visual_shader/doc_classes/VisualShader.xml
msgid "Removes the specified node from the shader."
msgstr "Remove o nó especificado do shader."

#: modules/visual_shader/doc_classes/VisualShader.xml
msgid ""
"Removes a varying value node with the given [param name]. Prints an error if "
"a node with this name is not found."
msgstr ""
"Remove um nó de valor varying com o [param name] dado. Imprime um erro se um "
"nó com esse nome não for encontrado."

#: modules/visual_shader/doc_classes/VisualShader.xml
msgid "Replaces the specified node with a node of new class type."
msgstr "Substitui o nó especificado por um nó de um novo tipo de classe."

#: modules/visual_shader/doc_classes/VisualShader.xml
msgid "Sets the mode of this shader."
msgstr "Define o modo deste shader."

#: modules/visual_shader/doc_classes/VisualShader.xml
msgid "Sets the position of the specified node."
msgstr "Define a posição do nó especificado."

#: modules/visual_shader/doc_classes/VisualShader.xml
msgid "This property does nothing and always equals to zero."
msgstr "Esta propriedade não faz nada e é sempre igual a zero."

#: modules/visual_shader/doc_classes/VisualShader.xml
msgid "Deprecated."
msgstr "Obsoleto."

#: modules/visual_shader/doc_classes/VisualShader.xml
msgid "A vertex shader, operating on vertices."
msgstr "Um shader de vértices, operando em vértices."

#: modules/visual_shader/doc_classes/VisualShader.xml
msgid "A fragment shader, operating on fragments (pixels)."
msgstr "Um shader de fragmento, operando em fragmentos (píxeis)."

#: modules/visual_shader/doc_classes/VisualShader.xml
msgid "A shader for light calculations."
msgstr "Um shader para cálculos de luz."

#: modules/visual_shader/doc_classes/VisualShader.xml
msgid "A function for the \"start\" stage of particle shader."
msgstr "Uma função para o estágio \"start\" do shader de partículas."

#: modules/visual_shader/doc_classes/VisualShader.xml
msgid "A function for the \"process\" stage of particle shader."
msgstr "Uma função para o estágio \"process\" do shader de partículas."

#: modules/visual_shader/doc_classes/VisualShader.xml
msgid ""
"A function for the \"collide\" stage (particle collision handler) of "
"particle shader."
msgstr ""
"Uma função para o estágio \"collide\" (manipulador de colisão de partículas) "
"do shader de partículas."

#: modules/visual_shader/doc_classes/VisualShader.xml
msgid ""
"A function for the \"start\" stage of particle shader, with customized "
"output."
msgstr ""
"Uma função para o estágio \"start\" de shader de partícula, com saída "
"personalizada."

#: modules/visual_shader/doc_classes/VisualShader.xml
msgid ""
"A function for the \"process\" stage of particle shader, with customized "
"output."
msgstr ""
"Uma função para o estágio \"process\" de shader de partícula, com saída "
"personalizada."

#: modules/visual_shader/doc_classes/VisualShader.xml
msgid "A shader for 3D environment's sky."
msgstr "Um shader para o céu de ambiente 3D."

#: modules/visual_shader/doc_classes/VisualShader.xml
msgid "A compute shader that runs for each froxel of the volumetric fog map."
msgstr ""
"Um shader de computação executado para cada froxel do mapa de névoa "
"volumétrica."

#: modules/visual_shader/doc_classes/VisualShader.xml
msgid "A shader used to process blit calls to a DrawableTexture."
msgstr ""
"Um shader usado para processar chamadas de blit para um DrawableTexture."

#: modules/visual_shader/doc_classes/VisualShader.xml
msgid "Represents the size of the [enum Type] enum."
msgstr "Representa o tamanho da enumeração [enum Type]."

#: modules/visual_shader/doc_classes/VisualShader.xml
msgid ""
"Varying is passed from [code]Vertex[/code] function to [code]Fragment[/code] "
"and [code]Light[/code] functions."
msgstr ""
"O Varying é passado da função [code]Vertex[/code] para as funções "
"[code]Fragment[/code] e [code]Light[/code]."

#: modules/visual_shader/doc_classes/VisualShader.xml
msgid ""
"Varying is passed from [code]Fragment[/code] function to [code]Light[/code] "
"function."
msgstr ""
"O varying é passado da função [code]Fragment[/code] para a função "
"[code]Light[/code]."

#: modules/visual_shader/doc_classes/VisualShader.xml
msgid "Represents the size of the [enum VaryingMode] enum."
msgstr "Representa o tamanho da enumeração [enum VaryingMode]."

#: modules/visual_shader/doc_classes/VisualShader.xml
msgid "Varying is of type [float]."
msgstr "A variação é do tipo [float]."

#: modules/visual_shader/doc_classes/VisualShader.xml
msgid "Varying is of type [int]."
msgstr "A variação é do tipo [int]."

#: modules/visual_shader/doc_classes/VisualShader.xml
msgid "Varying is of type unsigned [int]."
msgstr "A variação é do tipo [int] sem sinal."

#: modules/visual_shader/doc_classes/VisualShader.xml
msgid "Varying is of type [Vector2]."
msgstr "A variação é do tipo [Vector2]."

#: modules/visual_shader/doc_classes/VisualShader.xml
msgid "Varying is of type [Vector3]."
msgstr "A variação é do tipo [Vector3]."

#: modules/visual_shader/doc_classes/VisualShader.xml
msgid "Varying is of type [Vector4]."
msgstr "A variação é do tipo [Vector4]."

#: modules/visual_shader/doc_classes/VisualShader.xml
msgid "Varying is of type [bool]."
msgstr "A variação é do tipo [bool]."

#: modules/visual_shader/doc_classes/VisualShader.xml
msgid "Varying is of type [Transform3D]."
msgstr "A variação é do tipo [Transform3D]."

#: modules/visual_shader/doc_classes/VisualShader.xml
msgid "Represents the size of the [enum VaryingType] enum."
msgstr "Representa o tamanho da enumeração [enum VaryingType]."

#: modules/visual_shader/doc_classes/VisualShader.xml
msgid "Indicates an invalid [VisualShader] node."
msgstr "Indica um nó [VisualShader] inválido."

#: modules/visual_shader/doc_classes/VisualShader.xml
msgid "Indicates an output node of [VisualShader]."
msgstr "Indica um nó de saída de [VisualShader]."

#: modules/visual_shader/doc_classes/VisualShaderNode.xml
msgid "Base class for [VisualShader] nodes. Not related to scene nodes."
msgstr ""
"Classe base para nós [VisualShader]. Não está relacionada a nós de cena."

#: modules/visual_shader/doc_classes/VisualShaderNode.xml
msgid ""
"Visual shader graphs consist of various nodes. Each node in the graph is a "
"separate object and they are represented as a rectangular boxes with title "
"and a set of properties. Each node also has connection ports that allow to "
"connect it to another nodes and control the flow of the shader."
msgstr ""
"Gráficos de shaders visuais consistem em vários nós. Cada nó no gráfico é um "
"objeto separado e eles são representados como caixas retangulares com um "
"título e um conjunto de propriedades. Cada nó também possui portas de "
"conexão que permitem conectá-lo a outros nós e controlar o fluxo do shader."

#: modules/visual_shader/doc_classes/VisualShaderNode.xml
msgid "Clears the default input ports value."
msgstr "Limpa o valor padrão das portas de entrada."

#: modules/visual_shader/doc_classes/VisualShaderNode.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the input port which should be connected by default when this node "
"is created as a result of dragging a connection from an existing node to the "
"empty space on the graph."
msgstr ""
"Retorna a porta de entrada que deve ser conectada por padrão quando este nó "
"é criado como resultado de arrastar uma conexão de um nó existente para o "
"espaço vazio no gráfico."

#: modules/visual_shader/doc_classes/VisualShaderNode.xml
msgid ""
"Returns an [Array] containing default values for all of the input ports of "
"the node in the form [code][index0, value0, index1, value1, ...][/code]."
msgstr ""
"Retorna um [Array] contendo valores padrão para todas as portas de entrada "
"do nó no formato [code][index0, value0, index1, value1, ...][/code]."

#: modules/visual_shader/doc_classes/VisualShaderNode.xml
msgid "Returns the default value of the input [param port]."
msgstr "Retorna o valor padrão da [param port] de entrada."

#: modules/visual_shader/doc_classes/VisualShaderNode.xml
msgid "Removes the default value of the input [param port]."
msgstr "Remove o valor padrão da [param port] de entrada."

#: modules/visual_shader/doc_classes/VisualShaderNode.xml
msgid ""
"Sets the default input ports values using an [Array] of the form [code]"
"[index0, value0, index1, value1, ...][/code]. For example: [code][0, "
"Vector3(0, 0, 0), 1, Vector3(0, 0, 0)][/code]."
msgstr ""
"Define os valores das portas de entrada padrão usando um [Array] da forma "
"[code][index0, value0, index1, value1, ...][/code]. Por exemplo: [code][0, "
"Vector3(0, 0, 0), 1, Vector3(0, 0, 0)][/code]."

#: modules/visual_shader/doc_classes/VisualShaderNode.xml
msgid "Sets the default [param value] for the selected input [param port]."
msgstr ""
"Define o [param value] padrão para a [param port] de entrada selecionada."

#: modules/visual_shader/doc_classes/VisualShaderNode.xml
msgid ""
"Represents the index of the frame this node is linked to. If set to "
"[code]-1[/code] the node is not linked to any frame."
msgstr ""
"Representa o índice do quadro ao qual este nó está vinculado. Se definido "
"como [code]-1[/code], o nó não está vinculado a nenhum quadro."

#: modules/visual_shader/doc_classes/VisualShaderNode.xml
msgid ""
"Sets the output port index which will be showed for preview. If set to "
"[code]-1[/code] no port will be open for preview."
msgstr ""
"Define o índice da porta de saída que será exibido para visualização. Se "
"definido como [code]-1[/code], nenhuma porta estará aberta para visualização."

#: modules/visual_shader/doc_classes/VisualShaderNode.xml
msgid ""
"Floating-point scalar. Translated to [code skip-lint]float[/code] type in "
"shader code."
msgstr ""
"Escalar de ponto flutuante. Traduzido para o tipo [code skip-lint]float[/"
"code] no código do shader."

#: modules/visual_shader/doc_classes/VisualShaderNode.xml
msgid ""
"Integer scalar. Translated to [code skip-lint]int[/code] type in shader code."
msgstr ""
"Escalar inteiro. Traduzido para o tipo [code skip-lint]int[/code] no código "
"do shader."

#: modules/visual_shader/doc_classes/VisualShaderNode.xml
msgid ""
"Unsigned integer scalar. Translated to [code skip-lint]uint[/code] type in "
"shader code."
msgstr ""
"Escalar inteiro sem sinal. Traduzido para o tipo [code skip-lint]uint[/code] "
"no código do shader."

#: modules/visual_shader/doc_classes/VisualShaderNode.xml
msgid ""
"2D vector of floating-point values. Translated to [code skip-lint]vec2[/"
"code] type in shader code."
msgstr ""
"Vetor 2D de valores de ponto flutuante. Traduzido para o tipo [code skip-"
"lint]vec2[/code] no código do shader."

#: modules/visual_shader/doc_classes/VisualShaderNode.xml
msgid ""
"3D vector of floating-point values. Translated to [code skip-lint]vec3[/"
"code] type in shader code."
msgstr ""
"Vetor 3D de valores de ponto flutuante. Traduzido para o tipo [code skip-"
"lint]vec3[/code] no código do shader."

#: modules/visual_shader/doc_classes/VisualShaderNode.xml
msgid ""
"4D vector of floating-point values. Translated to [code skip-lint]vec4[/"
"code] type in shader code."
msgstr ""
"Vetor 4D de valores de ponto flutuante. Traduzido para o tipo [code skip-"
"lint]vec4[/code] no código do shader."

#: modules/visual_shader/doc_classes/VisualShaderNode.xml
msgid ""
"Boolean type. Translated to [code skip-lint]bool[/code] type in shader code."
msgstr ""
"Tipo booleano. Traduzido para o tipo [code skip-lint]bool[/code] no código "
"do shader."

#: modules/visual_shader/doc_classes/VisualShaderNode.xml
msgid ""
"Transform type. Translated to [code skip-lint]mat4[/code] type in shader "
"code."
msgstr ""
"Tipo de transformação (Transform). Traduzido para o tipo [code skip-"
"lint]mat4[/code] no código do shader."

#: modules/visual_shader/doc_classes/VisualShaderNode.xml
msgid ""
"Sampler type. Translated to reference of sampler uniform in shader code. Can "
"only be used for input ports in non-uniform nodes."
msgstr ""
"Tipo de amostrador. Traduzido para a referência de sampler uniform no código "
"do shader. Só pode ser usado para portas de entrada em nós não uniformes."

#: modules/visual_shader/doc_classes/VisualShaderNode.xml
msgid "Represents the size of the [enum PortType] enum."
msgstr "Representa o tamanho do enum [enum PortType]."

#: modules/visual_shader/doc_classes/VisualShaderNodeBillboard.xml
msgid ""
"A node that controls how the object faces the camera to be used within the "
"visual shader graph."
msgstr ""
"Um nó que controla como o objeto fica voltado para a câmera a ser usado "
"dentro do grafo de shader visual."

#: modules/visual_shader/doc_classes/VisualShaderNodeBillboard.xml
msgid ""
"The output port of this node needs to be connected to [code]Model View "
"Matrix[/code] port of [VisualShaderNodeOutput]."
msgstr ""
"A porta de saída deste nó precisa ser conectada à porta [code]Model View "
"Matrix[/code] de [VisualShaderNodeOutput]."

#: modules/visual_shader/doc_classes/VisualShaderNodeBillboard.xml
msgid "Controls how the object faces the camera."
msgstr "Controla como o objeto está voltado para a câmera."

#: modules/visual_shader/doc_classes/VisualShaderNodeBillboard.xml
msgid ""
"If [code]true[/code], the shader will keep the scale set for the mesh. "
"Otherwise, the scale is lost when billboarding."
msgstr ""
"Se [code]true[/code], o shader manterá a escala definida para a malha. Caso "
"contrário, a escala será perdida ao usar o billboard."

#: modules/visual_shader/doc_classes/VisualShaderNodeBillboard.xml
msgid "Billboarding is disabled and the node does nothing."
msgstr "O billboarding é desativado e o nó não faz nada."

#: modules/visual_shader/doc_classes/VisualShaderNodeBillboard.xml
msgid "A standard billboarding algorithm is enabled."
msgstr "Um algoritmo de billboarding padrão está ativado."

#: modules/visual_shader/doc_classes/VisualShaderNodeBillboard.xml
msgid "A billboarding algorithm to rotate around Y-axis is enabled."
msgstr ""
"Um algoritmo de billboard para rotacionar em torno do eixo Y está ativado."

#: modules/visual_shader/doc_classes/VisualShaderNodeBillboard.xml
msgid "A billboarding algorithm designed to use on particles is enabled."
msgstr ""
"Um algoritmo de billboarding projetado para ser usado em partículas está "
"ativado."

#: modules/visual_shader/doc_classes/VisualShaderNodeBillboard.xml
msgid "Represents the size of the [enum BillboardType] enum."
msgstr "Representa o tamanho da enumeração [enum BillboardType]."

#: modules/visual_shader/doc_classes/VisualShaderNodeBooleanConstant.xml
msgid "A boolean constant to be used within the visual shader graph."
msgstr "Uma constante booleana a ser usada dentro do gráfico de shader visual."

#: modules/visual_shader/doc_classes/VisualShaderNodeBooleanConstant.xml
msgid ""
"Has only one output port and no inputs.\n"
