msgstr "Retorna a direção do layout e a direção da escrita do texto."

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the maximum value for linear color components that can be displayed "
"in this window, regardless of SDR or HDR output. Returns [code]1.0[/code] if "
"HDR is not enabled or not supported. The [signal "
"output_max_linear_value_changed] signal will be emitted whenever this value "
"changes.\n"
"This value is used by tonemapping and other [Environment] effects to ensure "
"that bright colors are presented in the range that can be displayed by this "
"window. When using this maximum linear value in your project, it should only "
"be used to present colors directly to the screen without tonemapping and "
"without influencing lighting, post-processing effects, or surrounding color. "
"The following is an example that produces the brightest purple color that "
"the screen can produce:\n"
"[codeblocks]\n"
"[gdscript]\n"
"func _process(_delta):\n"
"\t# output_max_linear_value may change often, so do this every frame.\n"
"\tvar max_linear_value = get_window().get_output_max_linear_value()\n"
"\t# Replace this with your color:\n"
"\tvar original_color = Color.PURPLE\n"
"\t# Normalize to max_linear_value to produce the brightest color possible,\n"
"\t# regardless of SDR or HDR output:\n"
"\tvar bright_color = normalize_color(original_color, max_linear_value)\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"func normalize_color(srgb_color, max_linear_value = 1.0):\n"
"\t# Color must be linear-encoded to use math operations.\n"
"\tvar linear_color = srgb_color.srgb_to_linear()\n"
"\tvar max_rgb_value = maxf(linear_color.r, maxf(linear_color.g, "
"linear_color.b))\n"
"\tvar brightness_scale = max_linear_value / max_rgb_value\n"
"\tlinear_color *= brightness_scale\n"
"\t# Undo changes to the alpha channel, which should not be modified.\n"
"\tlinear_color.a = srgb_color.a\n"
"\t# Convert back to nonlinear sRGB encoding, which is required for Color in\n"
"\t# Godot unless stated otherwise.\n"
"\treturn linear_color.linear_to_srgb()\n"
"[/gdscript]\n"
"[/codeblocks]\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] You will need to convert sRGB colors to linear before "
"multiplying by this value to get correct results."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o valor máximo para os componentes de cor linear que podem ser "
"exibidos nesta janela, independentemente da saída SDR ou HDR. Retorna "
"[code]1.0[/code] se o HDR não estiver ativado ou não for suportado. O sinal "
"[signal output_max_linear_value_changed] será emitido sempre que este valor "
"mudar.\n"
"Este valor é usado pelo mapeamento de tons e outros efeitos de [Environment] "
"para garantir que cores brilhantes sejam apresentadas no intervalo que pode "
"ser exibido por esta janela. Ao usar este valor linear máximo no seu "
"projeto, ele deve ser usado apenas para apresentar cores diretamente na tela "
"sem mapeamento de tons e sem influenciar a iluminação, efeitos de pós-"
"processamento ou a cor ao redor. O exemplo a seguir produz a cor roxa mais "
"brilhante que a tela pode produzir:\n"
"[codeblocks]\n"
"[gdscript]\n"
"func _process(_delta):\n"
"\t# output_max_linear_value pode mudar com frequência, então faça isso a "
"cada quadro.\n"
"\tvar max_linear_value = get_window().get_output_max_linear_value()\n"
"\t# Substitua isto pela sua cor:\n"
"\tvar original_color = Color.PURPLE\n"
"\t# Normaliza para max_linear_value para produzir a cor mais brilhante "
"possível,\n"
"\t# independentemente da saída SDR ou HDR:\n"
"\tvar bright_color = normalize_color(original_color, max_linear_value)\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"func normalize_color(srgb_color, max_linear_value = 1.0):\n"
"\t# A cor deve estar codificada em linear para usar operações matemáticas.\n"
"\tvar linear_color = srgb_color.srgb_to_linear()\n"
"\tvar max_rgb_value = maxf(linear_color.r, maxf(linear_color.g, "
"linear_color.b))\n"
"\tvar brightness_scale = max_linear_value / max_rgb_value\n"
"\tlinear_color *= brightness_scale\n"
"\t# Desfaz alterações no canal alfa, que não deve ser modificado.\n"
"\tlinear_color.a = srgb_color.a\n"
"\t# Converte de volta para a codificação sRGB não linear, que é necessária "
"para Color no\n"
"\t# Godot, a menos que indicado o contrário.\n"
"\treturn linear_color.linear_to_srgb()\n"
"[/gdscript]\n"
"[/codeblocks]\n"
"[b]Nota:[/b] Você precisará converter cores sRGB para linear antes de "
"multiplicar por este valor para obter resultados corretos."

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the window's position including its border.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] If [member visible] is [code]false[/code], this method returns "
"the same value as [member position]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the window's size including its border.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] If [member visible] is [code]false[/code], this method returns "
"the same value as [member size]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"Returns a [Color] from the first matching [Theme] in the tree if that "
"[Theme] has a color item with the specified [param name] and [param "
"theme_type].\n"
"See [method Control.get_theme_color] for more details."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"Returns a constant from the first matching [Theme] in the tree if that "
"[Theme] has a constant item with the specified [param name] and [param "
"theme_type].\n"
"See [method Control.get_theme_color] for more details."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the default base scale value from the first matching [Theme] in the "
"tree if that [Theme] has a valid [member Theme.default_base_scale] value.\n"
"See [method Control.get_theme_color] for details."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the default font from the first matching [Theme] in the tree if that "
"[Theme] has a valid [member Theme.default_font] value.\n"
"See [method Control.get_theme_color] for details."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the default font size value from the first matching [Theme] in the "
"tree if that [Theme] has a valid [member Theme.default_font_size] value.\n"
"See [method Control.get_theme_color] for details."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"Returns a [Font] from the first matching [Theme] in the tree if that [Theme] "
"has a font item with the specified [param name] and [param theme_type].\n"
"See [method Control.get_theme_color] for details."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"Returns a font size from the first matching [Theme] in the tree if that "
"[Theme] has a font size item with the specified [param name] and [param "
"theme_type].\n"
"See [method Control.get_theme_color] for details."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"Returns an icon from the first matching [Theme] in the tree if that [Theme] "
"has an icon item with the specified [param name] and [param theme_type].\n"
"See [method Control.get_theme_color] for details."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"Returns a [StyleBox] from the first matching [Theme] in the tree if that "
"[Theme] has a stylebox item with the specified [param name] and [param "
"theme_type].\n"
"See [method Control.get_theme_color] for details."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid "Returns the ID of the window."
msgstr "Retorna o ID da janela."

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid "Causes the window to grab focus, allowing it to receive user input."
msgstr ""
"Faz com que a janela capture o foco, permitindo que ela receba entrada do "
"usuário."

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid "Returns [code]true[/code] if the window is focused."
msgstr "Retorna [code]true[/code] se a janela estiver focada."

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"Returns [code]true[/code] if there is a matching [Theme] in the tree that "
"has a color item with the specified [param name] and [param theme_type].\n"
"See [method Control.get_theme_color] for details."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"Returns [code]true[/code] if there is a matching [Theme] in the tree that "
"has a constant item with the specified [param name] and [param theme_type].\n"
"See [method Control.get_theme_color] for details."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"Returns [code]true[/code] if there is a matching [Theme] in the tree that "
"has a font item with the specified [param name] and [param theme_type].\n"
"See [method Control.get_theme_color] for details."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"Returns [code]true[/code] if there is a matching [Theme] in the tree that "
"has a font size item with the specified [param name] and [param "
"theme_type].\n"
"See [method Control.get_theme_color] for details."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"Returns [code]true[/code] if there is a matching [Theme] in the tree that "
"has an icon item with the specified [param name] and [param theme_type].\n"
"See [method Control.get_theme_color] for details."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"Returns [code]true[/code] if there is a matching [Theme] in the tree that "
"has a stylebox item with the specified [param name] and [param theme_type].\n"
"See [method Control.get_theme_color] for details."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"Hides the window. This is not the same as minimized state. Hidden window "
"can't be interacted with and needs to be made visible with [method show]."
msgstr ""
"Oculta a janela. Isso não é o mesmo que o estado minimizado. Uma janela "
"oculta não pode ser interagida e precisa ser tornada visível com [method "
"show]."

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"Returns [code]true[/code] if the window is currently embedded in another "
"window."
msgstr ""
"Retorna [code]true[/code] se a janela estiver atualmente embutida em outra "
"janela."

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid "Returns [code]true[/code] if the layout is right-to-left."
msgstr "Retorna [code]true[/code] se o layout for da direita para a esquerda."

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"Returns [code]true[/code] if the window can be maximized (the maximize "
"button is enabled)."
msgstr ""
"Retorna [code]true[/code] se a janela puder ser maximizada (o botão de "
"maximizar está ativado)."

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"Returns [code]true[/code] if font oversampling is enabled. See [method "
"set_use_font_oversampling]."
msgstr ""
"Retorna [code]true[/code] se o oversampling de fonte estiver ativado. Veja "
"[method set_use_font_oversampling]."

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"Centers the window in the current screen. If the window is embedded, it is "
"centered in the embedder [Viewport] instead."
msgstr ""
"Centraliza a janela na tela atual. Se a janela estiver embutida, ela é "
"centralizada no [Viewport] embutidor."

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid "Use [method Window.grab_focus] instead."
msgstr "Use [method Window.grab_focus] em vez disso."

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"Shows the [Window] and makes it transient (see [member transient]). If "
"[param rect] is provided, it will be set as the [Window]'s size. Fails if "
"called on the main window.\n"
"If [member ProjectSettings.display/window/subwindows/embed_subwindows] is "
"[code]true[/code] (single-window mode), [param rect]'s coordinates are "
"global and relative to the main window's top-left corner (excluding window "
"decorations). If [param rect]'s position coordinates are negative, the "
"window will be located outside the main window and may not be visible as a "
"result.\n"
"If [member ProjectSettings.display/window/subwindows/embed_subwindows] is "
"[code]false[/code] (multi-window mode), [param rect]'s coordinates are "
"global and relative to the top-left corner of the leftmost screen. If [param "
"rect]'s position coordinates are negative, the window will be placed at the "
"top-left corner of the screen.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] [param rect] must be in global coordinates if specified."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"Popups the [Window] at the center of the current screen, with optionally "
"given minimum size. If the [Window] is embedded, it will be centered in the "
"parent [Viewport] instead.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Calling it with the default value of [param minsize] is "
"equivalent to calling it with [member size]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"Popups the [Window] centered inside its parent [Window]. [param "
"fallback_ratio] determines the maximum size of the [Window], in relation to "
"its parent.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Calling it with the default value of [param minsize] is "
"equivalent to calling it with [member size]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"If [Window] is embedded, popups the [Window] centered inside its embedder "
"and sets its size as a [param ratio] of embedder's size.\n"
"If [Window] is a native window, popups the [Window] centered inside the "
"screen of its parent [Window] and sets its size as a [param ratio] of the "
"screen size."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"Attempts to parent this dialog to the last exclusive window relative to "
"[param from_node], and then calls [method Window.popup] on it. The dialog "
"must have no current parent, otherwise the method fails.\n"
"See also [method set_unparent_when_invisible] and [method "
"Node.get_last_exclusive_window]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"Attempts to parent this dialog to the last exclusive window relative to "
"[param from_node], and then calls [method Window.popup_centered] on it. The "
"dialog must have no current parent, otherwise the method fails.\n"
"See also [method set_unparent_when_invisible] and [method "
"Node.get_last_exclusive_window]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"Attempts to parent this dialog to the last exclusive window relative to "
"[param from_node], and then calls [method Window.popup_centered_clamped] on "
"it. The dialog must have no current parent, otherwise the method fails.\n"
"See also [method set_unparent_when_invisible] and [method "
"Node.get_last_exclusive_window]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"Attempts to parent this dialog to the last exclusive window relative to "
"[param from_node], and then calls [method Window.popup_centered_ratio] on "
"it. The dialog must have no current parent, otherwise the method fails.\n"
"See also [method set_unparent_when_invisible] and [method "
"Node.get_last_exclusive_window]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"Attempts to parent this dialog to the last exclusive window relative to "
"[param from_node], and then calls [method Window.popup_on_parent] on it. The "
"dialog must have no current parent, otherwise the method fails.\n"
"See also [method set_unparent_when_invisible] and [method "
"Node.get_last_exclusive_window]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"Popups the [Window] with a position shifted by parent [Window]'s position. "
"If the [Window] is embedded, has the same effect as [method popup]."
msgstr ""
"Abre o pop-up da [Window] com uma posição deslocada pela posição da [Window] "
"pai. Se a [Window] estiver embutida, terá o mesmo efeito que [method popup]."

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"Tells the OS that the [Window] needs an attention. This makes the window "
"stand out in some way depending on the system, e.g. it might blink on the "
"task bar."
msgstr ""
"Informa ao SO que a [Window] precisa de atenção. Isso faz com que a janela "
"se destaque de alguma forma, dependendo do sistema; por exemplo, ela pode "
"piscar na barra de tarefas."

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"Resets the size to the minimum size, which is the max of [member min_size] "
"and (if [member wrap_controls] is enabled) [method "
"get_contents_minimum_size]. This is equivalent to calling "
"[code]set_size(Vector2i())[/code] (or any size below the minimum)."
msgstr ""
"Redefine o tamanho para o tamanho mínimo, que é o máximo entre [member "
"min_size] e (se [member wrap_controls] estiver ativado) [method "
"get_contents_minimum_size]. Isso é equivalente a chamar "
"[code]set_size(Vector2i())[/code] (ou qualquer tamanho abaixo do mínimo)."

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid "Sets a specified window flag."
msgstr "Define um sinalizador de janela especificado."

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"If [param active] is [code]true[/code], enables system's native IME (Input "
"Method Editor)."
msgstr ""
"Se [param active] for [code]true[/code], ativa o IME (Editor de Método de "
"Entrada) nativo do sistema."

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid "Moves IME to the given position."
msgstr "Move o IME para a posição fornecida."

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"Sets layout direction and text writing direction. Right-to-left layouts are "
"necessary for certain languages (e.g. Arabic and Hebrew)."
msgstr ""
"Define a direção do layout e a direção da escrita do texto. Layouts da "
"direita para a esquerda são necessários para determinados idiomas (por "
"exemplo, árabe e hebraico)."

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"Sets the type and state of the progress bar on the taskbar/dock icon of the "
"[Window]. See [enum DisplayServer.ProgressState] for possible values and how "
"each mode behaves.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] This method is implemented only on Windows and macOS."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"Creates a progress bar on the taskbar/dock icon of the [Window] if it does "
"not exist, sets the progress of the icon.\n"
"[param value] acts as a relative percentage value, ranges from [code]0.0[/"
"code] (lowest) to [code]1.0[/code] (highest).\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] This method is implemented only on Windows and macOS."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"If [param unparent] is [code]true[/code], the window is automatically "
"unparented when going invisible.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Make sure to keep a reference to the node, otherwise it will be "
"orphaned. You also need to manually call [method Node.queue_free] to free "
"the window if it's not parented."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"Enables font oversampling. This makes fonts look better when they are scaled "
"up."
msgstr ""
"Ativa a sobreamostragem de fontes. Isso faz com que as fontes fiquem "
"melhores quando redimensionadas para cima."

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"Makes the [Window] appear. This enables interactions with the [Window] and "
"doesn't change any of its property other than visibility (unlike e.g. "
"[method popup])."
msgstr ""
"Faz a [Window] aparecer. Isso ativa interações com a [Window] e não altera "
"nenhuma de suas propriedades além da visibilidade (ao contrário, por "
"exemplo, de [method popup])."

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"Starts an interactive drag operation on the window, using the current mouse "
"position. Call this method when handling a mouse button being pressed to "
"simulate a pressed event on the window's title bar. Using this method allows "
"the window to participate in space switching, tiling, and other system "
"features."
msgstr ""
"Inicia uma operação de arrastamento interativo na janela, usando a posição "
"atual do mouse. Chame este método ao manipular um botão do mouse sendo "
"pressionado para simular um evento pressionado na barra de título da janela. "
"O uso deste método permite que a janela participe da troca de espaços, "
"tiling e outros recursos do sistema."

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"Starts an interactive resize operation on the window, using the current "
"mouse position. Call this method when handling a mouse button being pressed "
"to simulate a pressed event on the window's edge."
msgstr ""
"Inicia uma operação de redimensionamento interativa na janela, usando a "
"posição atual do mouse. Chame este método ao manipular um botão do mouse "
"sendo pressionado para simular um evento de pressão na borda da janela."

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"If [code]true[/code], the window will be on top of all other windows. Does "
"not work if [member transient] is enabled."
msgstr ""
"Se [code]true[/code], a janela ficará acima de todas as outras janelas. Não "
"funciona se [member transient] estiver ativado."

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid "If [code]true[/code], the window will have no borders."
msgstr "Se [code]true[/code], a janela não terá bordas."

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"Specifies how the content's aspect behaves when the [Window] is resized. The "
"base aspect is determined by [member content_scale_size]."
msgstr ""
"Especifica como o aspecto do conteúdo se comporta quando a [Window] é "
"redimensionada. O aspecto base é determinado por [member content_scale_size]."

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"Specifies the base scale of [Window]'s content when its [member size] is "
"equal to [member content_scale_size]. See also [method "
"Viewport.get_stretch_transform]."
msgstr ""
"Especifica a escala base do conteúdo da [Window] quando seu [member size] "
"for igual a [member content_scale_size]. Veja também [method "
"Viewport.get_stretch_transform]."

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid "Specifies how the content is scaled when the [Window] is resized."
msgstr ""
"Especifica como o conteúdo é escalado quando a [Window] é redimensionada."

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"The content's base size in \"virtual\" pixels. Not to be confused with "
"[member size], which sets the actual window's physical size in pixels. If "
"set to a value greater than [code]0[/code] and [member content_scale_mode] "
"is set to a value other than [constant CONTENT_SCALE_MODE_DISABLED], the "
"[Window]'s content will be scaled when the window is resized to a different "
"size. Higher values will make the content appear [i]smaller[/i], as it will "
"be able to fit more of the project in view. On the root [Window], this is "
"set to match [member ProjectSettings.display/window/size/viewport_width] and "
"[member ProjectSettings.display/window/size/viewport_height] by default.\n"
"For example, when using [constant CONTENT_SCALE_MODE_CANVAS_ITEMS] and "
"[member content_scale_size] set to [code]Vector2i(1280, 720)[/code], using a "
"window size of [code]2560×1440[/code] will make 2D elements appear at double "
"their original size, as the content is scaled by a factor of [code]2.0[/"
"code] ([code]2560.0 / 1280.0 = 2.0[/code], [code]1440.0 / 720.0 = 2.0[/"
"code]).\n"
"See [url=$DOCS_URL/tutorials/rendering/multiple_resolutions.html#base-"
"size]the Base size section of the Multiple resolutions documentation[/url] "
"for details."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"The policy to use to determine the final scale factor for 2D elements. This "
"affects how [member content_scale_factor] is applied, in addition to the "
"automatic scale factor determined by [member content_scale_size]."
msgstr ""
"A política a ser usada para determinar o fator de escala final para "
"elementos 2D. Isso afeta como [member content_scale_factor] é aplicado, além "
"do fator de escala automático determinado por [member content_scale_size]."

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid "The screen the window is currently on."
msgstr "A tela em que a janela está atualmente."

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"If [code]true[/code], the [Window] is excluded from screenshots taken by "
"[method DisplayServer.screen_get_image], [method "
"DisplayServer.screen_get_image_rect], and [method "
"DisplayServer.screen_get_pixel].\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] This property is implemented on macOS and Windows.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Enabling this setting will prevent standard screenshot methods "
"from capturing a window image, but does [b]NOT[/b] guarantee that other apps "
"won't be able to capture an image. It should not be used as a DRM or "
"security measure."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"If [code]true[/code], the [Window] will be in exclusive mode. Exclusive "
"windows are always on top of their parent and will block all input going to "
"the parent [Window].\n"
"Needs [member transient] enabled to work."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"If [code]true[/code], the [Window] contents is expanded to the full size of "
"the window, window title bar is transparent.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] This property is implemented only on macOS.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] This property only works with native windows."
msgstr ""
"Se [code]true[/code], o conteúdo da [Window] é expandido para ocupar todo o "
"tamanho da janela, e a barra de título da janela se torna transparente.\n"
"[b]Nota:[/b] Esta propriedade é implementada apenas no macOS.\n"
"[b]Nota:[/b] Esta propriedade funciona apenas com janelas nativas."

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"If [code]true[/code], native window will be used regardless of parent "
"viewport and project settings."
msgstr ""
"Se [code]true[/code], a janela nativa será usada independentemente da "
"viewport pai e das configurações do projeto."

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"If [code]true[/code], requests HDR output for the [Window], falling back to "
"SDR if not supported, and automatically switching between HDR and SDR as the "
"window moves between screens, screen capabilities change, or system settings "
"are modified. This will internally force [member Viewport.use_hdr_2d] to be "
"enabled on the main [Viewport]. All other [SubViewport] of this [Window] "
"must have their [member Viewport.use_hdr_2d] property enabled to produce HDR "
"output."
msgstr ""
"Se [code]true[/code], solicita saída HDR para a [Window], recorrendo a SDR "
"se não for suportado e alternando automaticamente entre HDR e SDR conforme a "
"janela se move entre telas, as capacidades da tela mudam ou as configurações "
"do sistema são modificadas. Isso forçará internamente [member "
"Viewport.use_hdr_2d] a ser habilitado no [Viewport] principal. Todos os "
"outros [SubViewport] desta [Window] devem ter sua propriedade [member "
"Viewport.use_hdr_2d] habilitada para produzir saída HDR."

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid "Specifies the initial type of position for the [Window]."
msgstr "Especifica o tipo inicial de posição para a [Window]."

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"If [code]true[/code], the [Window] width is expanded to keep the title bar "
"text fully visible."
msgstr ""
"Se [code]true[/code], a largura do [Window] é expandida para manter o texto "
"da barra de título totalmente visível."

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"If non-zero, the [Window] can't be resized to be bigger than this size.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] This property will be ignored if the value is lower than "
"[member min_size]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"If [code]true[/code], the [Window]'s maximize button is disabled.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] If both minimize and maximize buttons are disabled, buttons are "
"fully hidden, and only close button is visible.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] This property is implemented only on macOS and Windows."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"If non-zero, the [Window] can't be resized to be smaller than this size.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] This property will be ignored in favor of [method "
"get_contents_minimum_size] if [member wrap_controls] is enabled and if its "
"size is bigger."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"If [code]true[/code], the [Window]'s minimize button is disabled.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] If both minimize and maximize buttons are disabled, buttons are "
"fully hidden, and only close button is visible.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] This property is implemented only on macOS and Windows."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"Set's the window's current mode.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Fullscreen mode is not exclusive full screen on Windows and "
"Linux.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] This method only works with native windows, i.e. the main "
"window and [Window]-derived nodes when [member "
"Viewport.gui_embed_subwindows] is disabled in the main viewport."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"If [code]true[/code], all mouse events will be passed to the underlying "
"window of the same application. See also [member "
"mouse_passthrough_polygon].\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] This property is implemented on Linux (X11), macOS and "
"Windows.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] This property only works with native windows."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"Sets a polygonal region of the window which accepts mouse events. Mouse "
"events outside the region will be passed through.\n"
"Passing an empty array will disable passthrough support (all mouse events "
"will be intercepted by the window, which is the default behavior).\n"
"[codeblocks]\n"
"[gdscript]\n"
"# Set region, using Path2D node.\n"
"$Window.mouse_passthrough_polygon = $Path2D.curve.get_baked_points()\n"
"\n"
"# Set region, using Polygon2D node.\n"
"$Window.mouse_passthrough_polygon = $Polygon2D.polygon\n"
"\n"
"# Reset region to default.\n"
"$Window.mouse_passthrough_polygon = []\n"
"[/gdscript]\n"
"[csharp]\n"
"// Set region, using Path2D node.\n"
"GetNode<Window>(\"Window\").MousePassthroughPolygon = "
"GetNode<Path2D>(\"Path2D\").Curve.GetBakedPoints();\n"
"\n"
"// Set region, using Polygon2D node.\n"
"GetNode<Window>(\"Window\").MousePassthroughPolygon = "
"GetNode<Polygon2D>(\"Polygon2D\").Polygon;\n"
"\n"
"// Reset region to default.\n"
"GetNode<Window>(\"Window\").MousePassthroughPolygon = [];\n"
"[/csharp]\n"
"[/codeblocks]\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] This property is ignored if [member mouse_passthrough] is set "
"to [code]true[/code].\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] On Windows, the portion of a window that lies outside the "
"region is not drawn, while on Linux (X11) and macOS it is.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] This property is implemented on Linux (X11), macOS and Windows."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"If set, defines the window's custom decoration area which will receive mouse "
"input, even if normal input to the window is blocked (such as when it has an "
"exclusive child opened). See also [signal nonclient_window_input]."
msgstr ""
"Se definido, define a área de decoração personalizada da janela que receberá "
"entrada do mouse, mesmo se a entrada normal para a janela estiver bloqueada "
"(como quando ela tem um filho exclusivo aberto). Veja também [signal "
"nonclient_window_input]."

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"If [code]true[/code], the [Window] will be considered a popup. Popups are "
"sub-windows that don't show as separate windows in system's window manager's "
"window list and will send close request when anything is clicked outside of "
"them (unless [member exclusive] is enabled)."
msgstr ""
"Se [code]true[/code], a [Window] será considerada um pop-up. Pop-ups são "
"subjanelas que não aparecem como janelas separadas na lista de janelas do "
"gerenciador de janelas do sistema e enviarão uma solicitação de fechamento "
"quando algo for clicado fora delas (a menos que [member exclusive] esteja "
"ativado)."

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"If [code]true[/code], the [Window] will signal to the window manager that it "
"is supposed to be an implementation-defined \"popup\" (usually a floating, "
"borderless, untileable and immovable child window)."
msgstr ""
"Se [code]true[/code], a [Window] sinalizará para o gerenciador de janelas "
"que deve ser um \"popup\" definido pela implementação (geralmente uma janela "
"filha flutuante, sem bordas, impossível de reorganizar em mosaico e "
"inamovível)."

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"The window's position in pixels.\n"
"If [member ProjectSettings.display/window/subwindows/embed_subwindows] is "
"[code]false[/code], the position is in absolute screen coordinates. This "
"typically applies to editor plugins. If the setting is [code]true[/code], "
"the window's position is in the coordinates of its parent [Viewport].\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] This property only works if [member initial_position] is set to "
"[constant WINDOW_INITIAL_POSITION_ABSOLUTE]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"If [code]true[/code], the [Window] will override the OS window style to "
"display sharp corners.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] This property is implemented only on Windows (11).\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] This property only works with native windows."
msgstr ""
"Se [code]true[/code], a [Window] substituirá o estilo de janela do sistema "
"operacional para exibir cantos nítidos.\n"
"[b]Nota:[/b] Esta propriedade é implementada apenas no Windows (11).\n"
"[b]Nota:[/b] Esta propriedade funciona apenas com janelas nativas."

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"The window's size in pixels. See also [member content_scale_size], which "
"doesn't set the window's physical size but affects how scaling works "
"relative to the current [member content_scale_mode]."
msgstr ""
"O tamanho da janela em pixels. Consulte também [member content_scale_size], "
"que não define o tamanho físico da janela, mas afeta como o "
"redimensionamento funciona em relação ao [member content_scale_mode] atual."

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"The name of a theme type variation used by this [Window] to look up its own "
"theme items. See [member Control.theme_type_variation] for more details."
msgstr ""
"O nome de uma variação de tipo de tema usada por esta [Window] para procurar "
"seus próprios itens de tema. Consulte [member Control.theme_type_variation] "
"para obter mais detalhes."

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"The window's title. If the [Window] is native, title styles set in [Theme] "
"will have no effect."
msgstr ""
"O título da janela. Se a [Window] for nativa, os estilos de título definidos "
"em [Theme] não terão efeito."

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"If [code]true[/code], the [Window] is transient, i.e. it's considered a "
"child of another [Window]. The transient window will be destroyed with its "
"transient parent and will return focus to their parent when closed. The "
"transient window is displayed on top of a non-exclusive full-screen parent "
"window. Transient windows can't enter full-screen mode.\n"
"Note that behavior might be different depending on the platform."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"If [code]true[/code], and the [Window] is [member transient], this window "
"will (at the time of becoming visible) become transient to the currently "
"focused window instead of the immediate parent window in the hierarchy. Note "
"that the transient parent is assigned at the time this window becomes "
"visible, so changing it afterwards has no effect until re-shown."
msgstr ""
"Se [code]true[/code], e a [Window] for [member transient], esta janela se "
"tornará (no momento em que se tornar visível) transiente para a janela "
"atualmente em foco, em vez da janela pai imediata na hierarquia. Observe que "
"o pai transiente é atribuído no momento em que esta janela se torna visível, "
"portanto, alterá-lo posteriormente não terá efeito até que seja exibida "
"novamente."

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"If [code]true[/code], the [Window]'s background can be transparent. This is "
"best used with embedded windows.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Transparency support is implemented on Linux, macOS and "
"Windows, but availability might vary depending on GPU driver, display "
"manager, and compositor capabilities.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] This property has no effect if [member ProjectSettings.display/"
"window/per_pixel_transparency/allowed] is set to [code]false[/code]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"If [code]true[/code], the [Window] can't be focused nor interacted with. It "
"can still be visible."
msgstr ""
"Se [code]true[/code], o [Window] não pode receber foco nem interagir com "
"ele. Ele ainda pode ficar visível."

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid "If [code]true[/code], the window can't be resized."
msgstr "Se [code]true[/code], a janela não pode ser redimensionada."

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid "If [code]true[/code], the window is visible."
msgstr "Se [code]true[/code], a janela está visível."

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"If [code]true[/code], the window's size will automatically update when a "
"child node is added or removed, ignoring [member min_size] if the new size "
"is bigger.\n"
"If [code]false[/code], you need to call [method child_controls_changed] "
"manually."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"Emitted right after [method popup] call, before the [Window] appears or does "
"anything."
msgstr ""
"Emitido logo após a chamada de [method popup], antes que o [Window] apareça "
"ou faça qualquer coisa."

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"Emitted when the [Window]'s close button is pressed or when [member "
"popup_window] is enabled and user clicks outside the window.\n"
"This signal can be used to handle window closing, e.g. by connecting it to "
"[method hide]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"Emitted when the [Window]'s DPI changes as a result of OS-level changes "
"(e.g. moving the window from a Retina display to a lower resolution one).\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Only implemented on macOS and Linux (Wayland)."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"Emitted when files are dragged from the OS file manager and dropped in the "
"game window. The argument is a list of file paths.\n"
"[codeblock]\n"
"func _ready():\n"
"\tget_window().files_dropped.connect(on_files_dropped)\n"
"\n"
"func on_files_dropped(files):\n"
"\tprint(files)\n"
"[/codeblock]\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] This signal only works with native windows, i.e. the main "
"window and [Window]-derived nodes when [member "
"Viewport.gui_embed_subwindows] is disabled in the main viewport."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid "Emitted when the [Window] gains focus."
msgstr "Emitido quando o [Window] ganha foco."

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid "Emitted when the [Window] loses its focus."
msgstr "Emitido quando a [Window] perde o foco."

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"Emitted when a go back request is sent (e.g. pressing the \"Back\" button on "
"Android), right after [constant Node.NOTIFICATION_WM_GO_BACK_REQUEST]."
msgstr ""
"Emitido quando uma solicitação de retorno é enviada (por exemplo, "
"pressionando o botão \"Voltar\" no Android), logo após [constant "
"Node.NOTIFICATION_WM_GO_BACK_REQUEST]."

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"Emitted when the mouse cursor enters the [Window]'s visible area, that is "
"not occluded behind other [Control]s or windows, provided its [member "
"Viewport.gui_disable_input] is [code]false[/code] and regardless if it's "
"currently focused or not."
msgstr ""
"Emitido quando o ponteiro do mouse entra na área visível da [Window], que "
"não está ocluída por trás de outros [Control]s ou janelas, desde que seu "
"[member Viewport.gui_disable_input] seja [code]false[/code] e "
"independentemente de estar focada no momento ou não."

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"Emitted when the mouse cursor leaves the [Window]'s visible area, that is "
"not occluded behind other [Control]s or windows, provided its [member "
"Viewport.gui_disable_input] is [code]false[/code] and regardless if it's "
"currently focused or not."
msgstr ""
"Emitido quando o ponteiro do mouse deixa a área visível da [Window], que não "
"está ocluída por trás de outros [Control]s ou janelas, desde que seu [member "
"Viewport.gui_disable_input] seja [code]false[/code] e independentemente de "
"estar focada no momento ou não."

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"Emitted when the mouse event is received by the custom decoration area "
"defined by [member nonclient_area], and normal input to the window is "
"blocked (such as when it has an exclusive child opened). [param event]'s "
"position is in the embedder's coordinate system."
msgstr ""
"Emitido quando o evento do mouse é recebido pela área de decoração "
"personalizada definida por [member nonclient_area], e a entrada normal para "
"a janela é bloqueada (como quando há um filho exclusivo aberto). A posição "
"de [param event] está no sistema de coordenadas do embutidor."

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"Emitted when the output max linear value returned by [method "
"Window.get_output_max_linear_value] has changed. This occurs when HDR output "
"is enabled or disabled and when any HDR output luminance values of the "
"window have changed, such as when the player adjusts their screen brightness "
"setting or moves the window to a different screen. [param "
"output_max_linear_value] is the new value."
msgstr ""
"Emitido quando o valor linear máximo de saída retornado por [method "
"Window.get_output_max_linear_value] é alterado. Isso ocorre quando a saída "
"HDR é ativada ou desativada e quando quaisquer valores de luminância de "
"saída HDR da janela são alterados, como quando o jogador ajusta a "
"configuração de brilho da tela ou move a janela para uma tela diferente. "
"[param output_max_linear_value] é o novo valor."

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid "Emitted when window title bar text is changed."
msgstr "Emitido quando o texto da barra de título da janela é alterado."

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"Emitted when window title bar decorations are changed, e.g. macOS window "
"enter/exit full screen mode, or extend-to-title flag is changed."
msgstr ""
"Emitido quando as decorações da barra de título da janela são alteradas, por "
"exemplo, o modo de tela cheia de entrada/saída da janela do macOS ou a flag "
"extend-to-title é alterada."

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid "Emitted when [Window] is made visible or disappears."
msgstr "Emitido quando a [Window] se torna visível ou desaparece."

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"Emitted when the [Window] is currently focused and receives any input, "
"passing the received event as an argument. The event's position, if present, "
"is in the embedder's coordinate system."
msgstr ""
"Emitido quando a [Window] está atualmente focada e recebe qualquer entrada, "
"passando o evento recebido como um argumento. A posição do evento, se "
"presente, está no sistema de coordenadas do embutidor."

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"Emitted when [Window]'s visibility changes, right before [signal "
"visibility_changed]."
msgstr ""
"Emitido quando a visibilidade de [Window] muda, logo antes de [signal "
"visibility_changed]."

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"Sent when the node needs to refresh its theme items. This happens in one of "
"the following cases:\n"
"- The [member theme] property is changed on this node or any of its "
"ancestors.\n"
"- The [member theme_type_variation] property is changed on this node.\n"
"- The node enters the scene tree.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] As an optimization, this notification won't be sent from "
"changes that occur while this node is outside of the scene tree. Instead, "
"all of the theme item updates can be applied at once when the node enters "
"the scene tree."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"A single window full screen mode. This mode has less overhead, but only one "
"window can be open on a given screen at a time (opening a child window or "
"application switching will trigger a full screen transition).\n"
"Full screen window covers the entire display area of a screen and has no "
"border or decorations. The display's video mode is not changed.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] This mode might not work with screen recording software.\n"
"[b]On Android:[/b] This enables immersive mode.\n"
"[b]On Windows:[/b] Depending on video driver, full screen transition might "
"cause screens to go black for a moment.\n"
"[b]On macOS:[/b] A new desktop is used to display the running project. "
"Exclusive full screen mode prevents Dock and Menu from showing up when the "
"mouse pointer is hovering the edge of the screen.\n"
"[b]On Linux (X11):[/b] Exclusive full screen mode bypasses compositor.\n"
"[b]On Linux (Wayland):[/b] Equivalent to [constant MODE_FULLSCREEN].\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Regardless of the platform, enabling full screen will change "
"the window size to match the monitor's size. Therefore, make sure your "
"project supports [url=$DOCS_URL/tutorials/rendering/"
"multiple_resolutions.html]multiple resolutions[/url] when enabling full "
"screen mode."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"The window can't be resized by dragging its resize grip. It's still possible "
"to resize the window using [member size]. This flag is ignored for full "
"screen windows. Set with [member unresizable].\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] This flag is implemented on Linux (X11), macOS, Windows, and "
"embedded windows."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"The window do not have native title bar and other decorations. This flag is "
"ignored for full-screen windows. Set with [member borderless].\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] This flag is implemented on Linux (X11/Wayland), macOS, "
"Windows, and embedded windows."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"The window is floating on top of all other windows. This flag is ignored for "
"full-screen windows. Set with [member always_on_top].\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] This flag is implemented on Linux (X11), macOS, Windows, and "
"embedded windows."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"The window background can be transparent. Set with [member transparent].\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] This flag has no effect if either [member "
"ProjectSettings.display/window/per_pixel_transparency/allowed], or the "
"window's [member Viewport.transparent_bg] is set to [code]false[/code].\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Transparency support is implemented on Linux (X11/Wayland), "
"macOS, Windows, and embedded windows."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"The window can't be focused. No-focus window will ignore all input, except "
"mouse clicks. Set with [member unfocusable].\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] This flag is implemented on Linux (X11), macOS, Windows, and "
"embedded windows."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"Window is part of menu or [OptionButton] dropdown. This flag can't be "
"changed when the window is visible. An active popup window will exclusively "
"receive all input, without stealing focus from its parent. Popup windows are "
"automatically closed when uses click outside it, or when an application is "
"switched. Popup window must have transient parent set (see [member "
"transient]).\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] This flag is implemented on Linux (X11/Wayland), macOS, "
"Windows, and embedded [Popup] windows."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"Window content is expanded to the full size of the window. Unlike borderless "
"window, the frame is left intact and can be used to resize the window, title "
"bar is transparent, but have minimize/maximize/close buttons. Set with "
"[member extend_to_title].\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] This flag has no effect in embedded windows.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] This flag is implemented only on macOS."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"All mouse events are passed to the underlying window of the same "
"application.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] This flag has no effect in embedded windows.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] This flag is implemented on Linux (X11), macOS, Windows."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"Window style is overridden, forcing sharp corners.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] This flag has no effect in embedded windows.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] This flag is implemented only on Windows (11)."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"Windows is excluded from screenshots taken by [method "
"DisplayServer.screen_get_image], [method "
"DisplayServer.screen_get_image_rect], and [method "
"DisplayServer.screen_get_pixel].\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] This flag has no effect in embedded windows.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] This flag is implemented on macOS and Windows (10, 20H1).\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Setting this flag will prevent standard screenshot methods from "
"capturing a window image, but does [b]NOT[/b] guarantee that other apps "
"won't be able to capture an image. It should not be used as a DRM or "
"security measure."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"Signals the window manager that this window is supposed to be an "
"implementation-defined \"popup\" (usually a floating, borderless, untileable "
"and immovable child window).\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] This flag has no effect in embedded windows.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] This flag is implemented on Linux (Wayland)."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"Window minimize button is disabled.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] This flag has no effect in embedded windows.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] This flag is implemented on Linux (X11), macOS, and Windows."
msgstr ""
"O botão de minimizar da janela está desabilitado.\n"
"[b]Nota:[/b] Este sinalizador não tem efeito em janelas incorporadas.\n"
"[b]Nota:[/b] Este sinalizador é implementado no Linux (X11), macOS e Windows."

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"Window maximize button is disabled.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] This flag has no effect in embedded windows.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] This flag is implemented on Linux (X11), macOS, and Windows."
msgstr ""
"O botão de maximizar da janela está desabilitado.\n"
"[b]Nota:[/b] Este sinalizador não tem efeito em janelas incorporadas.\n"
"[b]Nota:[/b] Este sinalizador é implementado no Linux (X11), macOS e Windows."

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid "Max value of the [enum Flags]."
msgstr "Valor máximo do [enum Flags]."

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"The content will not be scaled to match the [Window]'s size ([member "
"content_scale_size] is ignored)."
msgstr ""
"O conteúdo não será dimensionado para corresponder ao tamanho do [Window] "
"([member content_scale_size] é ignorado)."

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"The content will be rendered at the target size. This is more performance-"
"expensive than [constant CONTENT_SCALE_MODE_VIEWPORT], but provides better "
"results."
msgstr ""
"O conteúdo será renderizado no tamanho de alvo. Isso consome mais desempenho "
"do que [constant CONTENT_SCALE_MODE_VIEWPORT], mas oferece melhores "
"resultados."

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"The content will be rendered at the base size and then scaled to the target "
"size. More performant than [constant CONTENT_SCALE_MODE_CANVAS_ITEMS], but "
"results in pixelated image."
msgstr ""
"O conteúdo será renderizado no tamanho base e depois dimensionado para o "
"tamanho de destino. Mais performático que [constant "
"CONTENT_SCALE_MODE_CANVAS_ITEMS], mas resulta em imagem pixelada."

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"The aspect will be ignored. Scaling will simply stretch the content to fit "
"the target size."
msgstr ""
"O aspecto será ignorado. A escala simplesmente esticará o conteúdo para "
"caber no tamanho de destino."

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"The content's aspect will be preserved. If the target size has different "
"aspect from the base one, the image will be centered and black bars will "
"appear on left and right sides."
msgstr ""
"A proporção do conteúdo será preservada. Se o tamanho de destino tiver uma "
"proporção diferente da base, a imagem será centralizada e barras pretas "
"aparecerão nos lados esquerdo e direito."

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"The content can be expanded vertically. Scaling horizontally will result in "
"keeping the width ratio and then black bars on left and right sides."
msgstr ""
"O conteúdo pode ser expandido verticalmente. O dimensionamento horizontal "
"resultará na manutenção da proporção de largura e, em seguida, barras pretas "
"nos lados esquerdo e direito."

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"The content can be expanded horizontally. Scaling vertically will result in "
"keeping the height ratio and then black bars on top and bottom sides."
msgstr ""
"O conteúdo pode ser expandido horizontalmente. O dimensionamento vertical "
"resultará na manutenção da proporção de altura e, em seguida, barras pretas "
"nas partes superior e inferior."

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"The content's aspect will be preserved. If the target size has different "
"aspect from the base one, the content will stay in the top-left corner and "
"add an extra visible area in the stretched space."
msgstr ""
"A proporção do conteúdo será preservada. Se o tamanho de destino tiver uma "
"proporção diferente da base, o conteúdo permanecerá no canto superior "
"esquerdo e adicionará uma área visível extra no espaço esticado."

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"The content will be stretched according to a fractional factor. This fills "
"all the space available in the window, but allows \"pixel wobble\" to occur "
"due to uneven pixel scaling."
msgstr ""
"O conteúdo será esticado de acordo com um fator fracionário. Isso preenche "
"todo o espaço disponível na janela, mas permite que ocorra oscilação de "
"pixels devido ao dimensionamento desigual de pixels."

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"The content will be stretched only according to an integer factor, "
"preserving sharp pixels. This may leave a black background visible on the "
"window's edges depending on the window size."
msgstr ""
"O conteúdo será esticado apenas de acordo com um fator inteiro, preservando "
"pixels nítidos. Isso pode deixar um fundo preto visível nas bordas da "
"janela, dependendo do tamanho dela."

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"Automatic layout direction, determined from the parent window layout "
"direction."
msgstr ""
"Direção de layout automática, determinada a partir da direção de layout da "
"janela pai."

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid "Automatic layout direction, determined from the current locale."
msgstr ""
"Direção de layout automática, determinada a partir da localidade atual."

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid "Automatic layout direction, determined from the system locale."
msgstr ""
"Direção de layout automática, determinada a partir da localidade do sistema."

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid "Initial window position is determined by [member position]."
msgstr "A posição inicial da janela é determinada por [member position]."

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid "Initial window position is the center of the primary screen."
msgstr "A posição inicial da janela é o centro da tela principal."

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid "Initial window position is the center of the main window screen."
msgstr "A posição inicial da janela é o centro da tela da janela principal."

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"Initial window position is the center of [member current_screen] screen."
msgstr ""
"A posição inicial da janela é o centro da tela [member current_screen]."

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"Initial window position is the center of the screen containing the mouse "
"pointer."
msgstr ""
"A posição inicial da janela é o centro da tela que contém o ponteiro do "
"mouse."

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"Initial window position is the center of the screen containing the window "
"with the keyboard focus."
msgstr ""
"A posição inicial da janela é o centro da tela que contém a janela com o "
"foco do teclado."

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid "The color of the title's text."
msgstr "A cor do texto do título."

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid "The color of the title's text outline."
msgstr "A cor do contorno do texto do título."

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"Horizontal position offset of the close button, relative to the end of the "
"title bar, towards the beginning of the title bar."
msgstr ""
"Deslocamento de posição horizontal do botão de fechar, relativo ao final da "
"barra de título, em direção ao início da barra de título."

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"Vertical position offset of the close button, relative to the bottom of the "
"title bar, towards the top of the title bar."
msgstr ""
"Deslocamento de posição vertical do botão de fechar, relativo à parte "
"inferior da barra de título, em direção à parte superior da barra de título."

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"Defines the outside margin at which the window border can be grabbed with "
"mouse and resized."
msgstr ""
"Define a margem externa na qual a borda da janela pode ser agarrada com o "
"mouse e redimensionada."

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid "Height of the title bar."
msgstr "Altura da barra de título."

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid "The size of the title outline."
msgstr "O tamanho do contorno do título."

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid "The font used to draw the title."
msgstr "A fonte usada para desenhar o título."

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid "The size of the title font."
msgstr "O tamanho da fonte do título."

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid "The icon for the close button."
msgstr "O ícone para o botão de fechar."

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid "The icon for the close button when it's being pressed."
msgstr "O ícone para o botão de fechar quando ele está sendo pressionado."

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid ""
"The background style used when the [Window] is embedded. Note that this is "
"drawn only under the window's content, excluding the title. For proper "
"borders and title bar style, you can use [code]expand_margin_*[/code] "
"properties of [StyleBoxFlat].\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] The content background will not be visible unless [member "
"transparent] is enabled."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/Window.xml
msgid "The background style used when the [Window] is embedded and unfocused."
msgstr "O estilo de fundo usado quando a [Window] está embutida e sem foco."

#: doc/classes/WorkerThreadPool.xml
msgid ""
"A singleton that allocates some [Thread]s on startup, used to offload tasks "
"to these threads."
msgstr ""
"Um singleton que aloca alguns [Thread]s na inicialização, usado para "
"descarregar tarefas para essas threads."

#: doc/classes/WorkerThreadPool.xml
msgid ""
"The [WorkerThreadPool] singleton allocates a set of [Thread]s (called worker "
"threads) on project startup and provides methods for offloading tasks to "
"them. This can be used for simple multithreading without having to create "
"[Thread]s.\n"
"Tasks hold the [Callable] to be run by the threads. [WorkerThreadPool] can "
"be used to create regular tasks, which will be taken by one worker thread, "
"or group tasks, which can be distributed between multiple worker threads. "
"Group tasks execute the [Callable] multiple times, which makes them useful "
"for iterating over a lot of elements, such as the enemies in an arena.\n"
"Here's a sample on how to offload an expensive function to worker threads:\n"
"[codeblocks]\n"
"[gdscript]\n"
"var enemies = [] # An array to be filled with enemies.\n"
"\n"
"func process_enemy_ai(enemy_index):\n"
"\tvar processed_enemy = enemies[enemy_index]\n"
"\t# Expensive logic...\n"
"\n"
"func _process(delta):\n"
"\tvar task_id = WorkerThreadPool.add_group_task(process_enemy_ai, "
"enemies.size())\n"
"\t# Other code...\n"
"\tWorkerThreadPool.wait_for_group_task_completion(task_id)\n"
"\t# Other code that depends on the enemy AI already being processed.\n"
"[/gdscript]\n"
"[csharp]\n"
"private List<Node> _enemies = new List<Node>(); // A list to be filled with "
"enemies.\n"
"\n"
"private void ProcessEnemyAI(int enemyIndex)\n"
"{\n"
"\tNode processedEnemy = _enemies[enemyIndex];\n"
"\t// Expensive logic here.\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"public override void _Process(double delta)\n"
"{\n"
"\tlong taskId = "
"WorkerThreadPool.AddGroupTask(Callable.From<int>(ProcessEnemyAI), "
"_enemies.Count);\n"
"\t// Other code...\n"
"\tWorkerThreadPool.WaitForGroupTaskCompletion(taskId);\n"
"\t// Other code that depends on the enemy AI already being processed.\n"
"}\n"
"[/csharp]\n"
"[/codeblocks]\n"
"The above code relies on the number of elements in the [code]enemies[/code] "
"array remaining constant during the multithreaded part.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Using this singleton could affect performance negatively if the "
"task being distributed between threads is not computationally expensive."
msgstr ""
"O singleton [WorkerThreadPool] aloca um conjunto de [Thread]s (chamadas de "
"threads de trabalho) na inicialização do projeto e fornece métodos para "
"descarregar tarefas para elas. Isso pode ser usado para multithreading "
"simples sem a necessidade de criar [Thread]s.\n"
"As tarefas mantêm o [Callable] a ser executado pelas threads. O "
"[WorkerThreadPool] pode ser usado para criar tarefas regulares, que serão "
"assumidas por uma thread de trabalho, ou tarefas em grupo, que podem ser "
"distribuídas entre várias threads de trabalho. Tarefas em grupo executam o "
"[Callable] várias vezes, o que as torna úteis para iterar sobre muitos "
"elementos, como os inimigos em uma arena.\n"
"Aqui está um exemplo de como descarregar uma função custosa para as threads "
"de trabalho:\n"
"[codeblocks]\n"
"[gdscript]\n"
"var enemies = [] # Uma matriz a ser preenchida com inimigos.\n"
"\n"
"func process_enemy_ai(enemy_index):\n"
"\tvar processed_enemy = enemies[enemy_index]\n"
"\t# Lógica custosa...\n"
"\n"
"func _process(delta):\n"
"\tvar task_id = WorkerThreadPool.add_group_task(process_enemy_ai, "
"enemies.size())\n"
"\t# Outro código...\n"
"\tWorkerThreadPool.wait_for_group_task_completion(task_id)\n"
"\t# Outro código que depende da IA do inimigo já estar sendo processada.\n"
"[/gdscript]\n"
"[csharp]\n"
"private List<Node> _enemies = new List<Node>(); // Uma lista a ser "
"preenchida com inimigos.\n"
"\n"
"private void ProcessEnemyAI(int enemyIndex)\n"
"{\n"
"\tNode processedEnemy = _enemies[enemyIndex];\n"
"\t// Lógica custosa aqui.\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"public override void _Process(double delta)\n"
"{\n"
"\tlong taskId = "
"WorkerThreadPool.AddGroupTask(Callable.From<int>(ProcessEnemyAI), "
"_enemies.Count);\n"
"\t// Outro código...\n"
"\tWorkerThreadPool.WaitForGroupTaskCompletion(taskId);\n"
"\t// Outro código que depende da IA do inimigo já estar sendo processada.\n"
"}\n"
"[/csharp]\n"
"[/codeblocks]\n"
"O código acima depende de que o número de elementos na matriz [code]enemies[/"
"code] permaneça constante durante a parte multithreaded.\n"
"[b]Nota:[/b] O uso deste singleton pode afetar o desempenho negativamente se "
"a tarefa distribuída entre as threads não for computacionalmente custosa."

#: doc/classes/WorkerThreadPool.xml
msgid ""
"Adds [param action] as a group task to be executed by the worker threads. "
"The [Callable] will be called a number of times based on [param elements], "
"with the first thread calling it with the value [code]0[/code] as a "
"parameter, and each consecutive execution incrementing this value by 1 until "
"it reaches [code]element - 1[/code].\n"
"The number of threads the task is distributed to is defined by [param "
"tasks_needed], where the default value [code]-1[/code] means it is "
"distributed to all worker threads. [param high_priority] determines if the "
"task has a high priority or a low priority (default). You can optionally "
"provide a [param description] to help with debugging.\n"
"Returns a group task ID that can be used by other methods.\n"
"[b]Warning:[/b] Every task must be waited for completion using [method "
"wait_for_task_completion] or [method wait_for_group_task_completion] at some "
"point so that any allocated resources inside the task can be cleaned up."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/WorkerThreadPool.xml
msgid ""
"Adds [param action] as a task to be executed by a worker thread. [param "
"high_priority] determines if the task has a high priority or a low priority "
"(default). You can optionally provide a [param description] to help with "
"debugging.\n"
"Returns a task ID that can be used by other methods.\n"
"[b]Warning:[/b] Every task must be waited for completion using [method "
"wait_for_task_completion] or [method wait_for_group_task_completion] at some "
"point so that any allocated resources inside the task can be cleaned up."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/WorkerThreadPool.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the task group ID of the current thread calling this method, or "
"[code]-1[/code] if invalid or the current thread is not part of a task group."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o ID do grupo de tarefas da thread atual que chama este método, ou "
"[code]-1[/code] se for inválido ou se a thread atual não fizer parte de um "
"grupo de tarefas."

#: doc/classes/WorkerThreadPool.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the task ID of the current thread calling this method, or [code]-1[/"
"code] if the task is a group task, invalid or the current thread is not part "
"of the thread pool (e.g. the main thread).\n"
"Can be used by a task to get its own task ID, or to determine whether the "
"current code is running inside the worker thread pool.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Group tasks have their own IDs, so this method will return "
"[code]-1[/code] for group tasks."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/WorkerThreadPool.xml
msgid ""
"Returns how many times the [Callable] of the group task with the given ID "
"has already been executed by the worker threads.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] If a thread has started executing the [Callable] but is yet to "
"finish, it won't be counted."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/WorkerThreadPool.xml
msgid ""
"Returns [code]true[/code] if the group task with the given ID is completed.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] You should only call this method between adding the group task "
"and awaiting its completion."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/WorkerThreadPool.xml
msgid ""
"Returns [code]true[/code] if the task with the given ID is completed.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] You should only call this method between adding the task and "
"awaiting its completion."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/WorkerThreadPool.xml
msgid ""
"Pauses the thread that calls this method until the group task with the given "
"ID is completed."
msgstr ""
"Pausa a thread que chama este método até que a tarefa em grupo com o ID "
"fornecido seja concluída."

#: doc/classes/WorkerThreadPool.xml
msgid ""
"Pauses the thread that calls this method until the task with the given ID is "
"completed.\n"
"Returns [constant @GlobalScope.OK] if the task could be successfully "
"awaited.\n"
"Returns [constant @GlobalScope.ERR_INVALID_PARAMETER] if a task with the "
"passed ID does not exist (maybe because it was already awaited and disposed "
"of).\n"
"Returns [constant @GlobalScope.ERR_BUSY] if the call is made from another "
"running task and, due to task scheduling, there's potential for deadlocking "
"(e.g., the task to await may be at a lower level in the call stack and "
"therefore can't progress). This is an advanced situation that should only "
"matter when some tasks depend on others (in the current implementation, the "
"tricky case is a task trying to wait on an older one)."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/World2D.xml
msgid ""
"A resource that holds all components of a 2D world, such as a canvas and a "
"physics space."
msgstr ""
"Um recurso que contém todos os componentes de um mundo 2D, como um canvas e "
"um espaço físico."

#: doc/classes/World2D.xml
msgid ""
"Class that has everything pertaining to a 2D world: A physics space, a "
"canvas, and a sound space. 2D nodes register their resources into the "
"current 2D world."
msgstr ""
"Classe que tem tudo referente a um mundo 2D: Um espaço de física, um canvas "
"e um espaço de som. Nós 2D registram seus recursos no mundo 2D atual."

#: doc/classes/World2D.xml
msgid ""
"The [RID] of this world's canvas resource. Used by the [RenderingServer] for "
"2D drawing."
msgstr ""
"O [RID] do recurso de canvas deste mundo. Usado pelo [RenderingServer] para "
"desenho 2D."

#: doc/classes/World2D.xml
msgid ""
"Direct access to the world's physics 2D space state. Used for querying "
"current and potential collisions. When using multi-threaded physics, access "
"is limited to [method Node._physics_process] in the main thread."
msgstr ""
"Acesso direto ao estado do espaço de física 2D do mundo. Usado para "
"consultar colisões atuais e potenciais. Ao usar física multithread, o acesso "
"é limitado a [method Node._physics_process] na thread principal."

#: doc/classes/World2D.xml
msgid ""
"The [RID] of this world's navigation map. Used by the [NavigationServer2D]."
msgstr ""
"O [RID] do mapa de navegação deste mundo. Usado pelo [NavigationServer2D]."

#: doc/classes/World2D.xml
msgid ""
"The [RID] of this world's physics space resource. Used by the "
"[PhysicsServer2D] for 2D physics, treating it as both a space and an area."
msgstr ""
"O [RID] do recurso de espaço de física deste mundo. Usado pelo "
"[PhysicsServer2D] para física 2D, tratando-o como um espaço e uma área."

#: doc/classes/World3D.xml
msgid ""
"A resource that holds all components of a 3D world, such as a visual "
"scenario and a physics space."
msgstr ""
"Um recurso que contém todos os componentes de um mundo 3D, como um cenário "
"visual e um espaço físico."

#: doc/classes/World3D.xml
msgid ""
"Class that has everything pertaining to a world: A physics space, a visual "
"scenario, and a sound space. 3D nodes register their resources into the "
"current 3D world."
msgstr ""
"Classe que tem tudo referente a um mundo: Um espaço de física, um cenário "
"visual e um som espaço. Nós 3D registram seus recursos no mundo 3D atual."

#: doc/classes/World3D.xml doc/classes/WorldEnvironment.xml
msgid ""
"The default [CameraAttributes] resource to use if none set on the [Camera3D]."
msgstr ""
"O recurso [CameraAttributes] padrão a ser usado se nenhum for definido na "
"[Camera3D]."

#: doc/classes/World3D.xml
msgid ""
"Direct access to the world's physics 3D space state. Used for querying "
"current and potential collisions. When using multi-threaded physics, access "
"is limited to [method Node._physics_process] in the main thread."
msgstr ""
"Acesso direto ao estado do espaço de física 3D do mundo. Usado para "
"consultar colisões atuais e potenciais. Ao usar física multithread, o acesso "
"é limitado a [method Node._physics_process] na thread principal."

#: doc/classes/World3D.xml
msgid "The World3D's [Environment]."
msgstr "O [Environment] do World3D."

#: doc/classes/World3D.xml
msgid ""
"The World3D's fallback environment will be used if [member environment] "
"fails or is missing."
msgstr ""
"O ambiente de fallback do World3D será usado se [member environment] falhar "
"ou estiver ausente."

#: doc/classes/World3D.xml
msgid ""
"The [RID] of this world's navigation map. Used by the [NavigationServer3D]."
msgstr ""
"O [RID] do mapa de navegação deste mundo. Usado pelo [NavigationServer3D]."

#: doc/classes/World3D.xml
msgid "The World3D's visual scenario."
msgstr "O cenário visual do World3D."

#: doc/classes/World3D.xml
msgid "The World3D's physics space."
msgstr "O espaço físico do World3D."

#: doc/classes/WorldBoundaryShape2D.xml
msgid "A 2D world boundary (half-plane) shape used for physics collision."
msgstr ""
"Uma forma de limite de mundo 2D (meio plano) usada para colisão física."

#: doc/classes/WorldBoundaryShape2D.xml
msgid ""
"A 2D world boundary shape, intended for use in physics. "
"[WorldBoundaryShape2D] works like an infinite straight line that forces all "
"physics bodies to stay above it. The line's normal determines which "
"direction is considered as \"above\" and in the editor, the smaller line "
"over it represents this direction. It can for example be used for endless "
"flat floors."
msgstr ""
"Uma forma de limite de mundo 2D, destinada ao uso em física. "
"[WorldBoundaryShape2D] funciona como uma linha reta infinita que força todos "
"os corpos físicos a permanecerem acima dela. A normal da linha determina "
"qual direção é considerada \"acima\" e, no editor, a linha menor sobre ela "
"representa essa direção. Ela pode, por exemplo, ser usada para pisos planos "
"intermináveis."

#: doc/classes/WorldBoundaryShape2D.xml
msgid ""
"The distance from the origin to the line, expressed in terms of [member "
"normal] (according to its direction and magnitude). Actual absolute distance "
"from the origin to the line can be calculated as [code]abs(distance) / "
"normal.length()[/code].\n"
"In the scalar equation of the line [code]ax + by = d[/code], this is "
"[code]d[/code], while the [code](a, b)[/code] coordinates are represented by "
"the [member normal] property."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/WorldBoundaryShape2D.xml
msgid ""
"The line's normal, typically a unit vector. Its direction indicates the non-"
"colliding half-plane. Can be of any length but zero. Defaults to [constant "
"Vector2.UP]."
msgstr ""
"A normal da linha, tipicamente um vetor unitário. Sua direção indica o "
"semiplano sem colisão. Pode ter qualquer comprimento, exceto zero. O padrão "
"é [constant Vector2.UP]."

#: doc/classes/WorldBoundaryShape3D.xml
msgid "A 3D world boundary (half-space) shape used for physics collision."
msgstr ""
"Uma forma de limite de mundo 3D (meio espaço) usada para colisão física."

#: doc/classes/WorldBoundaryShape3D.xml
msgid ""
"A 3D world boundary shape, intended for use in physics. "
"[WorldBoundaryShape3D] works like an infinite plane that forces all physics "
"bodies to stay above it. The [member plane]'s normal determines which "
"direction is considered as \"above\" and in the editor, the line over the "
"plane represents this direction. It can for example be used for endless flat "
"floors.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] When the physics engine is set to [b]Jolt Physics[/b] in the "
"project settings ([member ProjectSettings.physics/3d/physics_engine]), "
"[WorldBoundaryShape3D] has a finite size (centered at the shape's origin). "
"It can be adjusted by changing [member ProjectSettings.physics/"
"jolt_physics_3d/limits/world_boundary_shape_size]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/WorldBoundaryShape3D.xml
msgid "The [Plane] used by the [WorldBoundaryShape3D] for collision."
msgstr "O [Plane] usado pelo [WorldBoundaryShape3D] para colisão."

#: doc/classes/WorldEnvironment.xml
msgid ""
"Default environment properties for the entire scene (post-processing "
"effects, lighting and background settings)."
msgstr ""
"Propriedades de ambiente padrão para toda a cena (efeitos de pós-"
"processamento, iluminação e configurações de fundo)."

#: doc/classes/WorldEnvironment.xml
msgid ""
"The [WorldEnvironment] node is used to configure the default [Environment] "
"for the scene.\n"
"The parameters defined in the [WorldEnvironment] can be overridden by an "
"[Environment] node set on the current [Camera3D]. Additionally, only one "
"[WorldEnvironment] may be instantiated in a given scene at a time.\n"
"The [WorldEnvironment] allows the user to specify default lighting "
"parameters (e.g. ambient lighting), various post-processing effects (e.g. "
"SSAO, DOF, Tonemapping), and how to draw the background (e.g. solid color, "
"skybox). Usually, these are added in order to improve the realism/color "
"balance of the scene."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/WorldEnvironment.xml
msgid "The default [Compositor] resource to use if none set on the [Camera3D]."
msgstr ""
"O recurso [Compositor] padrão a ser usado se nenhum for definido na "
"[Camera3D]."

#: doc/classes/WorldEnvironment.xml
msgid ""
"The [Environment] resource used by this [WorldEnvironment], defining the "
"default properties."
msgstr ""
"O recurso [Environment] usado por este [WorldEnvironment], definindo as "
"propriedades padrão."

#: doc/classes/X509Certificate.xml
msgid "An X509 certificate (e.g. for TLS)."
msgstr "Um certificado X509 (por exemplo, para TLS)."

#: doc/classes/X509Certificate.xml
msgid ""
"The X509Certificate class represents an X509 certificate. Certificates can "
"be loaded and saved like any other [Resource].\n"
"They can be used as the server certificate in [method "
"StreamPeerTLS.accept_stream] (along with the proper [CryptoKey]), and to "
"specify the only certificate that should be accepted when connecting to a "
"TLS server via [method StreamPeerTLS.connect_to_stream]."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/X509Certificate.xml
msgid "Loads a certificate from [param path] (\"*.crt\" file)."
msgstr "Carrega um certificado de [param path] (arquivo \"*.crt\")."

#: doc/classes/X509Certificate.xml
msgid "Loads a certificate from the given [param string]."
msgstr "Carrega um certificado a partir da [param string] fornecida."

#: doc/classes/X509Certificate.xml
msgid ""
"Saves a certificate to the given [param path] (should be a \"*.crt\" file)."
msgstr ""
"Salva um certificado no [param path] fornecido (deve ser um arquivo "
"\"*.crt\")."

#: doc/classes/X509Certificate.xml
msgid ""
"Returns a string representation of the certificate, or an empty string if "
"the certificate is invalid."
msgstr ""
"Retorna uma representação em string do certificado, ou uma string vazia se o "
"certificado for inválido."

#: doc/classes/XMLParser.xml
msgid "Provides a low-level interface for creating parsers for XML files."
msgstr ""
"Fornece uma interface de baixo nível para criar analisadores para arquivos "
"XML."

#: doc/classes/XMLParser.xml
msgid ""
"Provides a low-level interface for creating parsers for [url=https://"
"en.wikipedia.org/wiki/XML]XML[/url] files. This class can serve as base to "
"make custom XML parsers.\n"
"To parse XML, you must open a file with the [method open] method or a buffer "
"with the [method open_buffer] method. Then, the [method read] method must be "
"called to parse the next nodes. Most of the methods take into consideration "
"the currently parsed node.\n"
"Here is an example of using [XMLParser] to parse an SVG file (which is based "
"on XML), printing each element and its attributes as a dictionary:\n"
"[codeblocks]\n"
"[gdscript]\n"
"var parser = XMLParser.new()\n"
"parser.open(\"path/to/file.svg\")\n"
"while parser.read() != ERR_FILE_EOF:\n"
"\tif parser.get_node_type() == XMLParser.NODE_ELEMENT:\n"
"\t\tvar node_name = parser.get_node_name()\n"
"\t\tvar attributes_dict = {}\n"
"\t\tfor idx in range(parser.get_attribute_count()):\n"
"\t\t\tattributes_dict[parser.get_attribute_name(idx)] = "
"parser.get_attribute_value(idx)\n"
"\t\tprint(\"The \", node_name, \" element has the following attributes: \", "
"attributes_dict)\n"
"[/gdscript]\n"
"[csharp]\n"
"var parser = new XmlParser();\n"
"parser.Open(\"path/to/file.svg\");\n"
"while (parser.Read() != Error.FileEof)\n"
"{\n"
"\tif (parser.GetNodeType() == XmlParser.NodeType.Element)\n"
"\t{\n"
"\t\tvar nodeName = parser.GetNodeName();\n"
"\t\tvar attributesDict = new Godot.Collections.Dictionary();\n"
"\t\tfor (int idx = 0; idx < parser.GetAttributeCount(); idx++)\n"
"\t\t{\n"
"\t\t\tattributesDict[parser.GetAttributeName(idx)] = "
"parser.GetAttributeValue(idx);\n"
"\t\t}\n"
"\t\tGD.Print($\"The {nodeName} element has the following attributes: "
"{attributesDict}\");\n"
"\t}\n"
"}\n"
"[/csharp]\n"
"[/codeblocks]"
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/XMLParser.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the number of attributes in the currently parsed element.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] If this method is used while the currently parsed node is not "
"[constant NODE_ELEMENT] or [constant NODE_ELEMENT_END], this count will not "
"be updated and will still reflect the last element."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/XMLParser.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the name of an attribute of the currently parsed element, specified "
"by the [param idx] index."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o nome de um atributo do elemento atualmente analisado, especificado "
"pelo índice [param idx]."

#: doc/classes/XMLParser.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the value of an attribute of the currently parsed element, specified "
"by the [param idx] index."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o valor de um atributo do elemento atualmente analisado, "
"especificado pelo índice [param idx]."

#: doc/classes/XMLParser.xml
msgid "Returns the current line in the parsed file, counting from 0."
msgstr "Retorna a linha atual no arquivo analisado, contando a partir de 0."

#: doc/classes/XMLParser.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the value of an attribute of the currently parsed element, specified "
"by its [param name]. This method will raise an error if the element has no "
"such attribute."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o valor de um atributo do elemento analisado no momento, "
"especificado pelo seu [param name]. Este método gerará um erro se o elemento "
"não tiver tal atributo."

#: doc/classes/XMLParser.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the value of an attribute of the currently parsed element, specified "
"by its [param name]. This method will return an empty string if the element "
"has no such attribute."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o valor de um atributo do elemento analisado no momento, "
"especificado pelo seu [param name]. Este método retornará uma string vazia "
"se o elemento não possuir tal atributo."

#: doc/classes/XMLParser.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the contents of a text node. This method will raise an error if the "
"current parsed node is of any other type."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o conteúdo de um nó de texto. Este método gerará um erro se o nó "
"analisado atual for de qualquer outro tipo."

#: doc/classes/XMLParser.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the name of a node. This method will raise an error if the currently "
"parsed node is a text node.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] The content of a [constant NODE_CDATA] node and the comment "
"string of a [constant NODE_COMMENT] node are also considered names."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/XMLParser.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the byte offset of the currently parsed node since the beginning of "
"the file or buffer. This is usually equivalent to the number of characters "
"before the read position."
msgstr ""
"Retorna o deslocamento de bytes do nó analisado atualmente desde o início do "
"arquivo ou buffer. Isso geralmente é equivalente ao número de caracteres "
"antes da posição de leitura."

#: doc/classes/XMLParser.xml
msgid ""
"Returns the type of the current node. Compare with [enum NodeType] constants."
msgstr "Retorna o tipo do nó atual. Compare com as constantes [enum NodeType]."

#: doc/classes/XMLParser.xml
msgid ""
"Returns [code]true[/code] if the currently parsed element has an attribute "
"with the [param name]."
msgstr ""
"Retorna [code]true[/code] se o elemento analisado atualmente tiver um "
"atributo com o [param name]."

#: doc/classes/XMLParser.xml
msgid ""
"Returns [code]true[/code] if the currently parsed element is empty, e.g. "
"[code]<element />[/code]."
msgstr ""
"Retorna [code]true[/code] se o elemento atualmente analisado estiver vazio, "
"por exemplo [code]<element />[/code]."

#: doc/classes/XMLParser.xml
msgid ""
"Opens an XML [param file] for parsing. This method returns an error code."
msgstr ""
"Abre um [param file] XML para análise. Este método retorna um código de erro."

#: doc/classes/XMLParser.xml
msgid ""
"Opens an XML raw [param buffer] for parsing. This method returns an error "
"code."
msgstr ""
"Abre um [param buffer] bruto XML para análise. Este método retorna um código "
"de erro."

#: doc/classes/XMLParser.xml
msgid "Parses the next node in the file. This method returns an error code."
msgstr ""
"Analisa o próximo nó no arquivo. Este método retorna um código de erro."

#: doc/classes/XMLParser.xml
msgid ""
"Moves the buffer cursor to a certain offset (since the beginning) and reads "
"the next node there. This method returns an error code."
msgstr ""
"Move o cursor do buffer para um determinado deslocamento (desde o início) e "
"lê o próximo nó lá. Este método retorna um código de erro."

#: doc/classes/XMLParser.xml
msgid ""
"Skips the current section. If the currently parsed node contains more inner "
"nodes, they will be ignored and the cursor will go to the closing of the "
"current element."
msgstr ""
"Pula a seção atual. Se o nó analisado no momento contiver mais nós internos, "
"eles serão ignorados e o cursor irá para o fechamento do elemento atual."

#: doc/classes/XMLParser.xml
msgid "There's no node (no file or buffer opened)."
msgstr "Não há nenhum nó (nenhum arquivo ou buffer aberto)."

#: doc/classes/XMLParser.xml
msgid "An element node type, also known as a tag, e.g. [code]<title>[/code]."
msgstr ""
"Um tipo de nó de elemento, também conhecido como tag, por exemplo, "
"[code]<title>[/code]."

#: doc/classes/XMLParser.xml
msgid "An end of element node type, e.g. [code]</title>[/code]."
msgstr "Um tipo de nó de fim de elemento, por exemplo, [code]</title>[/code]."

#: doc/classes/XMLParser.xml
msgid ""
"A text node type, i.e. text that is not inside an element. This includes "
"whitespace."
msgstr ""
"Um tipo de nó de texto, ou seja, texto que não está dentro de um elemento. "
"Isso inclui espaços em branco."

#: doc/classes/XMLParser.xml
msgid "A comment node type, e.g. [code]<!--A comment-->[/code]."
msgstr ""
"Um tipo de nó de comentário, por exemplo, [code]<!--Um comentário-->[/code]."

#: doc/classes/XMLParser.xml
msgid ""
"A node type for CDATA (Character Data) sections, e.g. [code]<![CDATA[CDATA "
"section]]>[/code]."
msgstr ""
"Um tipo de nó para seções CDATA (Dados de Caracteres), por exemplo, [code]<!"
"[CDATA[CDATA section]]>[/code]."

#: doc/classes/XMLParser.xml
msgid "An unknown node type."
msgstr "Um tipo de nó desconhecido."

#: doc/classes/XRAnchor3D.xml
msgid "An anchor point in AR space."
msgstr "Um ponto de ancoragem no espaço AR."

#: doc/classes/XRAnchor3D.xml
msgid ""
"The [XRAnchor3D] point is an [XRNode3D] that maps a real world location "
"identified by the AR platform to a position within the game world. For "
"example, as long as plane detection in ARKit is on, ARKit will identify and "
"update the position of planes (tables, floors, etc.) and create anchors for "
"them.\n"
"This node is mapped to one of the anchors through its unique ID. When you "
"receive a signal that a new anchor is available, you should add this node to "
"your scene for that anchor. You can predefine nodes and set the ID; the "
"nodes will simply remain on [code](0, 0, 0)[/code] until a plane is "
"recognized.\n"
"Keep in mind that, as long as plane detection is enabled, the size, placing "
"and orientation of an anchor will be updated as the detection logic learns "
"more about the real world out there especially if only part of the surface "
"is in view."
msgstr ""

